\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 First Thing: Lockerbie bomb suspect in US custody \u8216\'20\'18abducted by warlord\u8217\'20\'19\b0\par\par\uc2 Nicola Slawson \par \uc2 1,790 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 December 2022\par 11:40 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Mohammed Abouagela Masud accused by US of preparing the bomb that destroyed \uc2 Boeing\uc2  747, killing 270 people in 1988. Plus, the oldest university student graduates\par \par \uc2 Good morning.\par \par \uc2 A former Libyan intelligence operative accused of preparing the bomb that brought down Pan Am flight 103 over Lockerbie, Scotland, in 1988 was taken into US custody after being abducted from his home by a notorious warlord and then detained by armed militia for two weeks, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2022/dec/12/lockerbie-bomb-suspect-masud-us-custody"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Guardian has been told}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Mohammed Abouagela Masud appeared briefly in court in Washington DC on Monday, accused of having set the timer for the bomb that destroyed the \uc2 Boeing\uc2  747, killing 270 people in the most deadly terrorist attack to have taken place on British soil.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US Department of Justice\uc2  announced it had custody of Masud at the weekend, but gave no details of how he had arrived in the US.\par \par \uc2 Officials with knowledge of the case in Libya told the Guardian that Masud was seized at his home in the capital\u8217\'20\'19s Abu Salem neighbourhood by forces loyal to Abdel Ghani al-Kikili, known as \u8220\'20\'1CGheniwa\u8221\'20\'1D, who commands the Stability Support Authority (SSA) of the Tripoli-based Government of National Unity.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What have the White House said? Jake Sullivan, the US national security adviser, told reporters: \u8220\'20\'1CToday is a good day because Masud will be facing justice for his alleged role in the 1988 Lockerbie bombing. I will say that this was done in a lawful manner according to established procedures. For more specifics on how it happened I would refer you to the justice department because they\u8217\'20\'19re best positioned to be able to speak to that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What did the justice department say? In a statement, Michael H Glasheen, the acting assistant director in charge of the FBI Washington field office, said: \u8220\'20\'1CThe lawful arrest and presentment in court of the alleged bombmaker \u8230\'20\'26 is the product of hard work and partnerships across the globe.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Onslaught of new \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions looms in reddest of states\par \par \uc2 In Nebraska, a total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban could be on the horizon. In Florida, the gestational limit for abortions could drop from 15 weeks to 12. Elsewhere, lawmakers have \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills in their sights, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/dec/13/abortion-restrictions-us-state-legislatures"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 writes Poppy Noor}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 When Roe v Wade fell, most states were no longer in legislative session, meaning the term during which they usually write and pass bills had ended. In January, state legislatures will reconvene in an entirely new reality, one where conservative lawmakers are no longer constrained by the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  once assured by Roe.\par \par \uc2 The midterm elections brought victories for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in a number of states. But in others, politics are on the side of anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  advocates. In those reddest of states, the new state legislative sessions are likely to bring a fresh onslaught of efforts to restrict, penalize or altogether ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Katie Glenn, the state policy director at Susan B Anthony Pro-Life America, confirms the group\u8217\'20\'19s top priority in 2023 will be reducing the gestational age for legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , alongside bringing new outright bans. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  is currently banned in 13 states.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 How restrictive will those bans be? It remains to be seen. Conservatives across the country embroiled in conflicts over which exceptions \u8211\'20\'13 if any \u8211\'20\'13 should be allowed for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CExceptions in the case of rape and incest, we realise, are sometimes a necessary political reality. And we would not block a bill or oppose a bill that would prevent 95% of abortions,\u8221\'20\'1D explains Glenn.\par \par \uc2 Sam Bankman-Fried arrested in the Bahamas as criminal charges loom\par \par \uc2 The Bahamas police have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/dec/12/former-ftx-ceo-sam-bankman-fried-arrested-in-the-bahamas-local-authorities-say"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 arrested former FTX CEO Sam Bankman-Fried}}}\uc2 , the country\u8217\'20\'19s attorney general said in a statement on Monday, adding that the Bahamas has received formal notification from the US of criminal charges against him.\par \par \uc2 Bankman-Fried is expected to be extradited to the US, the attorney general\u8217\'20\'19s office for the Bahamas told Reuters, but declined to comment on what the charges were.\par \par \uc2 In a statement released on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , \uc2 Damian Williams\uc2 , the US attorney for the southern district of New York, confirmed Bankman-Fried\u8217\'20\'19s arrest and said the related indictment would be unsealed on Tuesday morning. \u8220\'20\'1C[We] will have more to say at that time,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 The former CEO had been expected to make his first public appearance today since FTX\u8217\'20\'19s collapse by testifying before \uc2 US Congress\uc2 . Bankman-Fried, who has been vocal throughout the collapse of FTX on his \uc2 Twitter\uc2  account and in public media appearances, was tweeting just hours before his arrest.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What happened with FTX? The company filed for US bankruptcy protection last month and Bankman-Fried resigned as chief executive, triggering a wave of public demands for greater regulation of the cryptocurrency industry.\par \par \uc2 In other news \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Researchers have reportedly made a breakthrough in the quest to unlock a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2022/dec/12/breakthrough-in-nuclear-fusion-could-mean-near-limitless-energy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cnear-limitless, safe, clean\u8221\'20\'1D source of energy}}}\uc2  : they have got more energy out of a nuclear fusion reaction than they put in. Researchers managed to release a positive gain known as ignition.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Twitter\uc2  abruptly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2022/dec/12/elon-musk-booed-dave-chappelle-san-francisco-show"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dissolved its Trust and Safety Council}}}\uc2  last night,\par \par \uc2 moments before it was scheduled to meet with company representatives. Meanwhile, the billionaire was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2022/dec/12/elon-musk-booed-dave-chappelle-san-francisco-show"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 booed for 10 minutes}}}\uc2  while appearing on stage on Sunday with comedian Dave Chappelle.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A young protester has been\par \par \uc2 detained in southern China for nine days after taking part in rallies against Covid restrictions, her mother has said, expressing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/dec/13/mother-fears-chinese-anti-lockdown-protester-covid-yang-zijing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fear and anguish over her daughter\u8217\'20\'19s safety}}}\uc2 . China last week effectively ended its harsh zero-Covid policy, after public discontent.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 New York City is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/dec/12/new-york-city-central-park-five-wrongful-conviction-gate-of-exonerated"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 naming a gate in Central Park}}}\uc2  in honor of the five men who, as teenagers, were wrongfully convicted of the 1989 rape of a jogger and spent years in prison before being exonerated. The city\u8217\'20\'19s public design commission unanimously approved the project yesterday.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The US has shipped the first part of its power equipment aid to Ukraine, officials said yesterday, as Washington works to support the country\u8217\'20\'19s energy infrastructure against intensifying attacks from Russia. The first tranche was power equipment worth about $13m, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/dec/13/russia-ukraine-war-live-us-sends-first-power-equipment-to-ukraine-eu-breaks-hungary-stalemate-to-approve-18bn-aid-plan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 one of the officials said}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 World Cup 2022: Semi-finals kick off\par \par \uc2 The first semi-final kicks off at 2pm ET today. Lionel Messi, one of the greatest players in history, is on the hunt for one of the few trophies to elude him: the World Cup. In his way are Croatia, who reached the final in 2018, an incredible feat for a country with a population of 4 million. As the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/football/2022/dec/12/croatias-success-story-built-on-family-values-and-a-sprinkling-of-stardust"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s Nick Ames tells us}}}\uc2 , Croatia\u8217\'20\'19s success story is built on family values and a sprinkling of stardust. You can follow the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/football/world-cup-2022"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 latest action here from 1pm ET}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere at the World Cup\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The US were knocked out more than a week ago, but one of their storylines rumbles on. Reports over the weekend suggested that one of their young stars, Gio Reyna, was nearly sent home because of a perceived lack of effort. Reyna {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/football/2022/dec/12/gio-reyna-world-cup-2022-gregg-berhalter-usmnt-soccer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hit back on Instagram on Monday}}}\uc2 , calling parts of the coverage \u8220\'20\'1Chighly fictionalized versions of events\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Bono (not that one) has emerged as one of the stars of the tournament. The Morocco goalkeeper has been instrumental in his team becoming the first African side in history to reach the World Cup semi-finals. But, as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/football/2022/dec/12/sliding-doors-moment-has-taken-bono-to-the-brink-of-world-cup-immortality"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sid Lowe tells us}}}\uc2 , his career could have taken a very different trajectory.\par \par \uc2 Stat of the day: Emma Tucker to become first female editor-in-chief of the Wall Street Journal in its 133-year history\par \par \uc2 Emma Tucker, the British editor of the UK Sunday Times, was named on Monday as the new editor-in-chief of the Wall Street Journal, and will become the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2022/dec/12/emma-tucker-first-female-editor-in-chief-wall-street-journal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 first woman to lead the 133-year-old business title}}}\uc2 . The move, announced by Rupert Murdoch\u8217\'20\'19s News Corp, will happen in February next year when Tucker, who will also run Dow Jones Newswires, will succeed \uc2 Matt Murray\uc2 , who will depart after a four-year tenure. Tucker was named editor of the \uc2 Sunday Times\uc2  in 2020, and in published interviews talked about building digital growth and working to broaden the publication\u8217\'20\'19s audience beyond its core older, affluent and middle-class readers.\par \par \uc2 Don\u8217\'20\'19t miss this: \u8216\'20\'18It\u8217\'20\'19s been very dark for all of us\u8217\'20\'19\u8211\'20\'13 film-maker Alexandra Pelosi on a family on America\u8217\'20\'19s political frontline\par \par \uc2 While her father \uc2 Paul Pelosi\uc2 , 82, is undergoing a slow and painful recovery from a hammer attack in late October by a home intruder and her mother \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 , also 82, last month announced her retirement as Democratic leader in the House of Representatives, assured of a place in history as the first female speaker,\par \par \uc2 filmmaker Alexandra Pelosi is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/2022/dec/13/alexandra-pelosi-nancy-paul-hbo-documentary-interview"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 promoting her latest documentary Pelosi in the House}}}\uc2 , which shows her mother resisting the January 6 insurrection. She talks to David Smith about her dad\u8217\'20\'19s attack, her mum\u8217\'20\'19s long goodbye to politics and what happened when the Capitol was stormed.\par \par \uc2 Climate check: Tanzania\u8217\'20\'19s booming charcoal trade drives unchecked deforestation\par \par \uc2 Large swathes of Ruhoi forest reserve in eastern Tanzania now lay bare, the ground in some sections dry and scorched, covered with stumps and brittle and fallen trees, writes Caroline Kimeu. The forest is being cut down at an alarming rate to meet the growing demand for charcoal in the nearby city of Dar es Salaam. As a result of high gas prices, about 90% of Tanzanian households now use charcoal or firewood to cook, which is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2022/dec/13/tanzania-charcoal-trade-deforestation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fuelling rapid deforestation across the country}}}\uc2 . Between 2015 and 2020, the country lost almost 470,000 hectares (1.16m acres) of forest a year, according to the \uc2 UN Food and Agriculture Organization\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Last Thing:\par \par \uc2 ninety-year-old woman is oldest person to graduate from Illinois university\par \par \uc2 Joyce DeFauw of Illinois has given a whole new meaning to the term super senior, used for students who take longer than the usual four years to get their undergraduate degrees. On Sunday, the 90-year-old received a bachelor\u8217\'20\'19s of general studies from \uc2 Northern Illinois University\uc2  more than seven decades after she first stepped on campus, becoming what officials believe to be the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/dec/13/northern-illinois-university-90-year-old-woman-graduates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 eldest person to graduate from the school}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19d never dreamed I\u8217\'20\'19d be around at this time, but here I am,\u8221\'20\'1D DeFauw said about her academic journey. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve learned that I can do things I never thought I could do, with the help of others. You can never quit learning.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Sign up\par \par \uc2 First Thing is delivered to thousands of inboxes every weekday. If you\u8217\'20\'19re not already signed up, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/info/2018/sep/17/guardian-us-morning-briefing-sign-up-to-stay-informed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 subscribe now}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Get in touch\par \par \uc2 If you have any questions or comments about any of our newsletters please email {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:newsletters@theguardian.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 newsletters@theguardian.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020221213eicd001s3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
