\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Democrats beating expectations as \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2  wins crucial \uc2 US Senate\uc2  race \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Martin Belam (now); Maanvi Singh and Chris Stein (earlier) in Washington \par \uc2 18,219 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 November 2022\par 12:59 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This live blog has now closed. You can find all the latest results and reaction in our new US midterms live blog\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.12am GMT\par \par \uc2 Thank you for reading. We will shortly be closing this live blog, and we\u8217\'20\'19ve started a new one, so please follow our continuing coverage over {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/nov/09/midterm-elections-2022-results-senate-house-us-democrats-republicans-live-updates-latest-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/nov/09/midterm-elections-2022-results-senate-house-us-democrats-republicans-live-updates-latest-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Midterm elections 2022: \u8216\'20\'18Red wave\u8217\'20\'19 fails to materialise as Fetterman clinches crucial Senate seat for Democrats \u8211\'20\'13 live}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.30am GMT\par \par \uc2 Our Politics Weekly America team have been working through the night in the US to produce a special edition of the podcast looking at the early results. Jonathan Freedland is joined by Joan E Greve, columnist Richard Wolffe, and Chris Scott of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.democracyforamerica.com/about"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democracy for America}}}\uc2 , to look at what we know so far. You can listen to it {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/audio/2022/nov/09/no-sign-of-the-red-wave-yet-politics-weekly-america-midterms-special"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/audio/2022/nov/09/no-sign-of-the-red-wave-yet-politics-weekly-america-midterms-special"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 No sign of the red wave \u8211\'20\'13 yet: Politics Weekly America midterms special }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.24am GMT\par \par \uc2 Six-term Republican representative Mark Amodei has defeated Elizabeth Mercedes Krause, as expected, in Nevada \u8217\'20\'19s rural northern district where no Democrat has ever won, the AP reports.\par \par \uc2 The second congressional district was considered the only safe seat for either party among the four in the western battleground of Nevada, where three incumbent Democrats faced stiff challenges on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.38am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.11am GMT\par \par \uc2 It may be a while until we know which party will win control of the House and Senate. But so far, the 8 November midterm has been full of surprises. Democrats have showed surprising strength in key races, defying what was broadly expected to be a Republican sweep amid high inflation and low approval rating for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Two of three Virginia Democrats in districts considered bellwethers for the national mood {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/nov/08/midterm-elections-2022-polls-results-senate-house-us-midterm-voting-republicans-democrats-live-updates-latest-news?page=with:block-636b220b8f0850c5a4cd4866#block-636b220b8f0850c5a4cd4866"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have won reelection}}}\uc2 , in what was an early sign of good news for Democrats.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Democrat \uc2 Josh Shapiro\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/nov/08/midterm-elections-2022-polls-results-senate-house-us-midterm-voting-republicans-democrats-live-updates-latest-news?page=with:block-636b37f68f082d3d26930bbe#block-636b37f68f082d3d26930bbe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bested}}}\uc2  2020 election denier \uc2 Doug Mastriano\uc2  in Pennsylvania\u8217\'20\'19s governorship race.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Democrat \uc2 John Fetterman\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/nov/08/midterm-elections-2022-polls-results-senate-house-us-midterm-voting-republicans-democrats-live-updates-latest-news?page=with:block-636b43168f083f3e45283adb#block-636b43168f083f3e45283adb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 declared victory}}}\uc2  in his race for Pennsylvania\u8217\'20\'19s Senate seat. Maryland elected {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/nov/08/midterm-elections-2022-polls-results-senate-house-us-midterm-voting-republicans-democrats-live-updates-latest-news?page=with:block-636afccb8f083f3e45283905#block-636afccb8f083f3e45283905"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the first Black governor in its history}}}\uc2 , Democrat Wes Moore.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Florida\u8217\'20\'19s voters tilted\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/nov/08/midterm-elections-2022-polls-results-senate-house-us-midterm-voting-republicans-democrats-live-updates-latest-news?page=with:block-636b00878f0850c5a4cd4782#block-636b00878f0850c5a4cd4782"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 further towards Republicans}}}\uc2 , reelecting firebrand governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  and senator \uc2 Marco Rubio\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 From Washington to New York, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/nov/08/midterm-elections-2022-polls-results-senate-house-us-midterm-voting-republicans-democrats-live-updates-latest-news?page=with:block-636b2dfc8f083f3e45283a4c#block-636b2dfc8f083f3e45283a4c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats defied}}}\uc2  Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 rosy predictions that they\u8217\'20\'19d fall apart this year, even in their traditional strongholds.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 JD Vance\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/nov/08/midterm-elections-2022-polls-results-senate-house-us-midterm-voting-republicans-democrats-live-updates-latest-news?page=with:block-636b2a898f082d3d26930b72#block-636b2a898f082d3d26930b72"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 won the Republican Senate race}}}\uc2  in Ohio, dashing Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 hopes of picking up another seat in the chamber.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Michigan voters\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/nov/08/midterm-elections-2022-polls-results-senate-house-us-midterm-voting-republicans-democrats-live-updates-latest-news?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-636b47358f083f3e45283aeb#block-636b47358f083f3e45283aeb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reelected}}}\uc2  Democratic governor \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2 , and Democratic {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/nov/08/midterm-elections-2022-polls-results-senate-house-us-midterm-voting-republicans-democrats-live-updates-latest-news?page=with:block-636b64108f0850c5a4cd4a2e#block-636b64108f0850c5a4cd4a2e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 representative}}}\uc2 Elissa Slotkin in a hard-fought race. They also backed a ballot measure enshrining reproductive freedom.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Voters in Vermont and California also backed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/08/recreational-drugs-abortion-climate-crisis-down-ballot-midterm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights measures}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Maryland\u8217\'20\'19s Wes Moore will be the state\u8217\'20\'19s first Black governor, and in Massachusetts \uc2 Maura Healey\uc2  will be the first out lesbian governor in US history.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.06am GMT\par \par \uc2 Earlier, Democrat Wes Moore made history by becoming the first Black governor of Maryland. He replaces Republican \uc2 Larry Hogan\uc2 , a moderate who managed to twice win election in what is otherwise a solidly blue state.\par \par \uc2 The newly elected official assured the electorate \u8220\'20\'1CI hear you\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cthis is our time\u8221\'20\'1D in his victory speech. Referencing his time in the army, Moore promised to \u8220\'20\'1Cleave no one behind\u8221\'20\'1D. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  had joined Moore in a pre-election rally in Maryland the evening before election day. Here is the video clip.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.18am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.52am GMT\par \par \uc2 Michigan voters favor \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights\par \par \uc2 Michigan voters enshrined protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, the AP projects.\par \par \uc2 Voters approved a ballot measure affirming the right to make personal reproductive decisions without interference, and negating a 1931 ban on abortions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CToday, the people of Michigan voted to restore the reproductive rights they\u8217\'20\'19ve had for 50 years,\u8221\'20\'1D said Darci McConnell, a spokesperson for Reproductive Freedom for All, which put forth the ballot measure. The measure marks a \u8220\'20\'1Chistoric victory for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in our state and in our country \u8211\'20\'13 and Michigan has paved the way for future efforts to restore the rights and protections of Roe v Wade nationwide,\u8221\'20\'1D McConnell said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.19am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.39am GMT\par \par \uc2 California resoundingly votes no on sports betting, \uc2 Guardian\uc2  tech reporter Kari Paul reports.\par \par \uc2 Voters in California voted overwhelmingly to reject two gambling initiatives on Tuesday, marking a decisive end to the most expensive ballot proposition battle in US history.\par \par \uc2 The two propositions would have expanded gambling access in the state in different ways: Proposition 27 aimed to legalize online and mobile sports betting while Proposition 26 would have allowed casinos and the state\u8217\'20\'19s four horse tracks to offer sports betting in person.\par \par \uc2 The online sports betting initiative was put on the ballot by sports betting companies including \uc2 DraftKings\uc2  and \uc2 FanDuel\uc2 , while Proposition 26 was funded by a coalition for Native American tribes.\par \par \uc2 Nearly $600m was spent advocating for the propositions, more than double the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/business-california-837ebb151c7aa65596537b4a5f7a2f9d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 record amount spent}}}\uc2  by gig economy firms such as Uber and \uc2 Lyft\uc2  in 2020 to classify their workers as contractors and block them from benefits and protections.\par \par \uc2 Californians overwhelmingly rejected both propositions, with 84% voting no on Prop 27 and 70% voting no on Prop 26.\par \par \uc2 State Democrats had opposed Proposition 27, but were neutral on Proposition 26. Democratic governor \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  was neutral on both proposals. The California Republican party opposed both proposals.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.50am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.38am GMT\par \par \uc2 Democratic representative \uc2 Elissa Slotkin\uc2  has won reelection in a hard-fought Michigan race against Republican Tom Barrett.\par \par \uc2 In 2018, Slotkin flipped a seat that was held by a Republican and won again in 2020 in a district that backed \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . She was seen as vulnerable once again this year, and the race was one of the top two most expensive races nationally, with both parties spending tens of millions on TV ads and mailers.\par \par \uc2 Slotkin, a moderate who previously worked as an intelligence and defense department official who worked for both Democratic and Republican presidential administrations, was supported by Republican senator and Trump critic \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.51am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.21am GMT\par \par \uc2 California voters have rejected a ballot measure that would have levied a wealth tax to fund the transition to electric vehicles.\par \par \uc2 The measure, Prop 30, failed after California governor \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  heavily {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/14/california-proposition-30-gavin-newsom-electric-vehicles"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 campaigned against it}}}\uc2 , siding with Republicans over his fellow Democrats, environmental groups, firefighters and labor unions. In misleading ads against Prop 30, Newsom claimed it was a corporate carve-out for \uc2 Lyft\uc2 , the ride-hailing company that has backed the measure and helped fund its campaign.\par \par \uc2 The environmental and public advocacy groups that developed the measure cried afoul. The measure had no provisions to specifically benefit rideshare companies, and \uc2 Lyft\uc2  only joined the effort to promote Prop 30 only after local groups developed the bulk of it.\par \par \uc2 Among the biggest donors to the \u8220\'20\'1CNo on 30\u8221\'20\'1D campaign were wealthy Californians who had also propped the governor\u8217\'20\'19s campaign.\par \par \uc2 Newsom this year issued an executive order banning the sale of new gas-powered vehicles by 2035, and allocated $10bn to the effort to subsidize electric vehicle purchases and build out charging infrastructure, but environmental groups said the funding will quickly fall short.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.52am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.02am GMT\par \par \uc2 Josh Green, a Democrat and Hawaii\u8217\'20\'19s lieutenant governor, has won the race to be the state\u8217\'20\'19s next governor, the AP projects.\par \par \uc2 Green defeated Duke Aiona, a Republican and former lieutenant governor, by what appeared to be a wide margin. Aiona had run for the office twice before.\par \par \uc2 At his election night party, Green told supporters, \u8220\'20\'1CTonight is the first day of that new era where our leaders must start doing more to listen, to care and to work on issues that matter to all of us, that matter to you.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 On the campaign trail, Green said he would address the housing shortage in the state by advocating for building 10,000 new units and cracking down on vacation rentals. He also pledged to fight for reproductive rights, noting his opponent\u8217\'20\'19s opposition to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections.\par \par \uc2 enltrBREAKING: Crowds cheering at Democratic HQ as it\u8217\'20\'19s official \u8212\'20\'14 Josh Green beats Duke Aiona in landslide on first printout with 66% of the Hawaii vote {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/HIGov?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #HIGov}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/ElectionNight?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #ElectionNight}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KITV4?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @KITV4}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/6Lh2hCS2Vq"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/6Lh2hCS2Vq}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Tom George (@TheTomGeorge) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TheTomGeorge/status/1590228778600759297?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.01am GMT\par \par \uc2 Kevin McCarthy, the House Republican leader, addressed supporters after an hours-long delay.\par \par \uc2 The California congressman projected confidence that Republicans would take the House despite several dozen seats still undecided. \u8220\'20\'1CWhen you wake up tomorrow, we will be in the majority and \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  will be in the minority,\u8221\'20\'1D he told supporters in Washington.\par \par \uc2 After a few key Democratic wins dashed expectations of an easy Republican sweep, McCarthy pointed to GOP wins in contested races in Texas and Virginia. Democrats have also kept seats in key Virginia districts, as well as contested seats in Kansas and Rhode Island.\par \par \uc2 Kevin McCarthy was confident Republicans would take the house, telling supporters, \u8216\'20\'18We will be in the majority.\u8217\'20\'19 Photograph: Brendan Smialowski/AFP/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.20am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.44am GMT\par \par \uc2 In Nevada, tight races might not be known for days, officials said. Dani {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/dani-anguiano"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Anguiano}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 Supporters of Senator \uc2 Catherine Cortez Masto\uc2 , react as she speaks during an election night party in Las Vegas. Photograph: Gregory Bull/AP\par \par \uc2 Nevada Democrats and Republicans have urged patience as residents await to hear the outcome of several razor-thin elections, including the Senate race, one of the tightest in the country.\par \par \uc2 Full results will not come in tonight, officials have said, and may not be known for several days. By 11:30pm PST, returns showed incumbent \uc2 Catherine Cortez Masto\uc2  ahead with about 51.2% of the votes to Republican \uc2 Adam Laxalt\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 46% with 47% of precincts reporting, a lead expected to shrink.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am confident in the campaign that we have built to win,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Cortez Masto\uc2  said. \u8220\'20\'1CI am so grateful to every Nevadan who knocked down doors, who made phone calls and stood up and fought for our state.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrThe votes are still being counted. We know this will take time and we won\u8217\'20\'19t have more election results for several days.\par \par \uc2 I am confident in this team. I'm confident in the campaign that we've built to win. \u161\'00\'A1La lucha sigue!\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Catherine Cortez Masto\uc2  (@CortezMasto) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CortezMasto/status/1590220602518175745?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Laxalt, Nevada\u8217\'20\'19s former attorney general who unsuccessfully ran for governor in 2018, said \u8220\'20\'1Cwe are exactly where we want to be in this race.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen we win this race, I\u8217\'20\'19m gonna support our police and fight to make our streets safe again. I will not rest until we\u8217\'20\'19ve secured our southern border,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re in for a long night and even a few days but we\u8217\'20\'19re confident we\u8217\'20\'19re gonna win this race and take back Nevada and take back America.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.47am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.42am GMT\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/sam-levine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sam Levine}}}\uc2  in Detroit reports:\par \par \uc2 We don\u8217\'20\'19t have all of the results yet, but election day did not appear to go particularly well for election deniers in competitive races.\par \par \uc2 In Pennsylvania, \uc2 Doug Mastriano\uc2 , who played a key role in \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s efforts to overturn the 2020 election, lost his re-election bid to \uc2 Josh Shapiro\uc2 , a Democrat who put defending democracy at the start of his campaign. \uc2 Jocelyn Benson\uc2 , Michigan\u8217\'20\'19s secretary of state who staunchly defended the 2020 election results also defeated Kristina Karamo, who rose to prominence after she spread false claims about fraud after ballots were counted in Detroit in 2020.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWell, well, well, democracy has prevailed,\u8221\'20\'1D Benson said as she took the stage at a Democratic victory party in downtown Detroit around midnight Wednesday. \u8220\'20\'1CToday Michigan voters showed the world that they will vote for truth over lies, facts over conspiracy theories, real results over empty promises.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Election deniers also lost races to be the top election official in New Mexico and Minnesota. Votes were still being counted in Nevada early Wednesday morning, where there is also a closely-watched secretary of state race.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.42am GMT\par \par \uc2 Democrat \uc2 Tony Evers\uc2  has won reelection for governor in Wisconsin, the AP has projected.\par \par \uc2 CNN had previously called the race in a crucial battleground state. Evers defeated Trump-backed construction executive \uc2 Tim Michels\uc2 , and will be a key counterbalance against the state Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 efforts to take control of the election system. Michels had said he would try to decertify the 2020 presidential results in Wisconsin, despite there being no legal mechanism to do so.\par \par \uc2 Evers has been a key veto against Republican legislators\u8217\'20\'19 efforts to disrupt election systems. That veto power may not hold if Republicans win a supermajority in the legislature, but it\u8217\'20\'19s unclear if they will.\par \par \uc2 Evers campaign was boosted in its final days by a visit from \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSome people call it boring, but as it turns out, Wisconsin, boring wins,\u8221\'20\'1D he said in his victory speech.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.48am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.24am GMT\par \par \uc2 The AP has called a few more House races in favor of Democrats.\par \par \uc2 In a fiercely contested race in New York, Democratic representative Joseph Morelle fended off a challenge from Republican former police chief La\u8217\'20\'19Ron Singletary.\par \par \uc2 In Michigan, Hillary Scholten defeated former Trump administration housing official and far-right election denier John Gibbs. And in Ohio, Republican representative \uc2 Steve Chabot\uc2  lost his seat to Democrat Greg Landsman.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.15am GMT\par \par \uc2 New Mexico\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic governor \uc2 Michelle Lujan Grisham\uc2  has won reelection, defeating Republican challenger Mark Ronchetti.\par \par \uc2 Lujan Grisham\uc2  honed in on the issue of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access. \u8220\'20\'1CTonight New Mexico said \u8216\'20\'18no\u8217\'20\'19 to a political crusade that wants to turn women into second-class citizens,\u8221\'20\'1D she said in a victory speech.\par \par \uc2 A former member of Congress and state health secretary, she was favored to win. Ronchetti, a former television meteorologist who never held elected office, had sought to distance himself from his party\u8217\'20\'19s far-right policies, but fell short.\par \par \uc2 Michelle Lujan Grisham\uc2  speaks to supporters during the celebration party in Albuquerque, New Mexico. Photograph: Andres Leighton/AP\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.36am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.06am GMT\par \par \uc2 Organizers claimed victory after Michigan voters appeared well on their way to approving a constitutional amendment that would significantly expand voting access and make it much harder for anyone to try and overturn the results of an election.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/sam-levine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sam Levine}}}\uc2  in Detroit reports:\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/07/michigan-proposal-2-voting-access-overturning-elections"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The measure}}}\uc2 , Proposal 2, establishes a fundamental right to vote in the Michigan constitution requires at least nine days of voting access and drop boxes, and allows voters to sign an affidavit if they lack photo ID, among other measures. And most significantly, it prevents officials from certifying an election based on anything other than the vote tally. That\u8217\'20\'19s a huge deal in Michigan, where boards of canvassers nearly refused to certify the vote in 2020 at the county and statewide level without solid evidence.\par \par \uc2 With 62% of the vote in early Wednesday, yes votes for the measure led 57.7% to 42.3%\par \par \uc2 The measure\u8217\'20\'19s passage marks the latest victory in a significantly growing grassroots voting rights movement in Michigan. In 2018, voters approved a constitutional amendment creating an independent redistricting commission and allowing for automatic and same-day registration.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMichigan voters clearly support ensuring every voice is heard and every vote is counted in every election no matter what political party or candidate we support, where we live or what we look like,\u8221\'20\'1D Micheal Davis, executive director for Promote the Vote, the coalition behind the amendment, said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.22am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.54am GMT\par \par \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  has issued a statement hailing an unexpectedly good performance by Democrats, even as votes are still being counted:\par \par \uc2 While many races remain too close to call, it is clear that House Democratic members and candidates are strongly outperforming expectations across the country.\par \par \uc2 As states continue to tabulate the final results, every vote must be counted as cast.\par \par \uc2 Many thanks to our grassroots volunteers for enabling every voter to have their say in our Democracy.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.53am GMT\par \par \uc2 Democrat Fetterman wins Pennsylvania Senate race\par \par \uc2 Democrat \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2  has won the Pennsylvania Senate race, the Associated Press confirms, giving \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s party another seat in Congress\u8217\'20\'19 upper chamber and increasing their chances of holding it for another two years.\par \par \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2  has secured the Pennsylvania Senate race. Photograph: Angela Weiss/AFP/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.06am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.49am GMT\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press reports Republican senator \uc2 Mike Lee\uc2  has won reelection in Utah.\par \par \uc2 He was up against independent Evan McMullin, who has cast himself as a foe of Trump. While polls generally showed Lee ahead, he had pled for aid on the campaign trail, including from his fellow senator \uc2 Mitt Romney\uc2 , who endorsed neither candidate, saying he considered both friends.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.48am GMT\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/erum-salam"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Erum Salam}}}\uc2  reflects on a highly polarized election, with varied results, in Texas:\par \par \uc2 In a predictable but still disappointing loss for Democrats in Texas, Republican incumbent Greg Abbott defeated his Democratic rival, \uc2 Beto O\u8217\'20\'19Rourke\uc2 , to win a third term as governor.\par \par \uc2 Attorney general \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2 , who denied the result of the 2020 presidential election, pushed false conspiracy theories about widespread voter fraud, and remains embroiled in legal trouble, also won a third term, defeating Democrat Rochelle Garza.\par \par \uc2 Another tight race in south Texas\u8217\'20\'19s newly drawn congressional district 15, where Latino voters are key, seems likely to lean Republican. While not officially called yet, progressive Michelle Vallejo seems poised to lose to Trump-backed Monica De La Cruz.\par \par \uc2 But Democrats can count victories in other races across the state.\par \par \uc2 Progressive Greg Casar, who earned an endorsement from Senator \uc2 Bernie Sanders\uc2 , won his House race in district 35, which stretches from eastern San Antonio to Austin.\par \par \uc2 Conservative Democrat Henry Cuellar will be holding onto his house seat in south Texas\u8217\'20\'19s district 28.\par \par \uc2 District 34 is back to being blue after far-right conspiracy theorist Mayra Flores, who made her mark as the first female Mexican-born member of the House, lost the seat she won in a June special election.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEarly voting came in already. Election day numbers are also coming in as well. We\u8217\'20\'19re still pending thousands of votes, but it doesn\u8217\'20\'19t look our way,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 On \uc2 Twitter\uc2  she chastised Republican and independent voters she believed stayed home.\par \par \uc2 enltrThe RED WAVE did not happen. Republicans and Independents stayed home. DO NOT COMPLAIN ABOUT THE RESULTS IF YOU DID NOT DO YOUR PART!\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Mayra Flores (@MayraFlores2022) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MayraFlores2022/status/1590214537051242502?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Some votes are still being counted,particularly in the heavily populated Harris county, where polls opened late.\par \par \uc2 A district judge ordered all 800 voting locations in the county to stay open for one more hour until 8pm CT, but the order was blocked by the state\u8217\'20\'19s highest civil court. It remains unclear if the provisional ballots cast in that extra hour will be thrown out.\par \par \uc2 Perhaps the greatest loss tonight in Texas are voting rights.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.07am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.47am GMT\par \par \uc2 In another victory Tuesday for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights advocates, campaigners declared victory on proposal three - the ballot initiative looking to enshrine a constitutional right to the procedure in Michigan.\par \par \uc2 It follows similar, earlier victories for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights measures in California and Vermont.\par \par \uc2 A win means Michiganders will now escape a 1931 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban that was on the books, although votes are still being counted.\par \par \uc2 If proposal three does pass, Michigan will become the first to fight off a pre-existing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban with a ballot proposal, creating a roadmap for campaigners across the country, during an election cycle in which voters seem to be coming out in full force for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CProposal 3\u8217\'20\'19s passage marks an historic victory for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in our state and in our country - and Michigan has paved the way for future efforts to restore the rights and protections of Roe v Wade nationwide,\u8221\'20\'1D Darci McConnell, communication director for Reproductive Freedom For All, wrote in a statement, announcing the news after it was called by locally ABC and NBC.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.44am GMT\par \par \uc2 New York\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic governor Kathy Hochul has won her election for a full term in office, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 A former lieutenant governor, Hochul took over leadership of the state last year after Andrew Cuomo resigned following accusations of sexual misconduct. She defeated Republican Lee Zeldin in the battle for a full term.\par \par \uc2 Kathy Hochul has secured a full term as New York\u8217\'20\'19s governor. Photograph: Timothy A Clary/AFP/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.49am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.39am GMT\par \par \uc2 Things appear to be breaking Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 direction in Wisconsin, a deeply polarized state that\u8217\'20\'19s among the most crucial of battlegrounds in presidential elections.\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press has not called the race yet, but CNN projects that Democratic governor \uc2 Tony Evers\uc2  has won a second term in office:\par \par \uc2 enltrTony Evers, the incumbent Dem gov in Wisconsin, wins, CNN projects. Dem gov candidates in AZ, MI, NV and Kansas are currently leading their races\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Manu Raju (@mkraju) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju/status/1590229846440951808?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Republicans dominate the state legislature but have seen many of their proposals vetoed by Evers. They had hoped to achieve a supermajority in yesterday\u8217\'20\'19s elections that would allow them to blunt his powers, but the Wisconsin State Journal reports {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://madison.com/news/local/govt-and-politics/elections/republicans-appear-short-of-winning-legislative-supermajority-in-wisconsin-legislature/article_dfd64dcb-d3e0-5138-91fe-01568f182707.html?utm_medium=social&utm_source=twitter&utm_campaign=user-share"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 that may not happen}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.33am GMT\par \par \uc2 From Dani Anguiano in Las Vegas, Nevada:\par \par \uc2 A judge in Nevada ruled against a request from Senator \uc2 Catherine Cortez Masto\uc2  to keep some polls open later after some locations ran out of paper leading to long lines and other delays.\par \par \uc2 Cortez Masto\uc2 , who is facing a tough re-election bid against Republican \uc2 Adam Laxalt\uc2 , and the Democratic senatorial campaign committee, had asked that some sites stay open until 9pm PT.\par \par \uc2 Polling places closed at 7pm local time with the exception of voters already in line.\par \par \uc2 enltrHere's more from the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CortezMasto?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @CortezMasto}}}\uc2  and DSCC lawsuit to keep polls open in Clark County.\par \par \uc2 Cites delays, long lines and at least 8 polling locations running out of paper, something that takes "up to two hours" to replace {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/3jUthAaJjZ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/3jUthAaJjZ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jacob Solis (@jacobsolisnv) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/jacobsolisnv/status/1590199081003286528?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.29am GMT\par \par \uc2 House speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 , and Kevin McCarthy, the Republican minority leader keen to seize the gavel from her, have both been re-elected to Congress from California, the Associated Press projects.\par \par \uc2 From the same state, Democratic representatives including Adam Schiff, Ted Lieu, Maxine Waters and Barbara Lee have also won re-election.\par \par \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 . Photograph: Kevin Lamarque/Reuters\par \par \uc2 McCarthy is likely to become speaker if Republicans, as expected, go on to win control of the chamber after Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s results are tallied.\par \par \uc2 Pelosi, 82, who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/07/nancy-pelosi-police-husband-attack"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 spoke emotionally on Monday}}}\uc2  about the violent attack on her husband Paul at their California home last month, said the incident would affect her decision about whether to retire if Democrats lose the House.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.28am GMT\par \par \uc2 Fetterman: Victory 'for every community across Pennsylvania'\par \par \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2  has given a victory speech to supporters gathered in Pittsburgh.\par \par \uc2 The newly elected Democratic senator for Pennsylvania, who is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/12/john-fetterman-stroke-interview-oz-senate-race"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recovering from a stroke}}}\uc2 , thanked his family and campaign team.\par \par \uc2 He declared his victory was \u8220\'20\'1Cfor everyone who\u8217\'20\'19s ever been gotten knocked down that ever got back up; for the future of every community all across Pennsylvania; for every small town, or person that ever felt left behind\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrWiping away tears, Senator-elect \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2  (D-PA) takes the stage at his victory speech to \u8220\'20\'1CBack in Black.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/raVlahIHL8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/raVlahIHL8}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1590229356601016322?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Fetterman was emotional as he spoke, his supporters chanting their approval of his downing of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s hand-picked Republican opponent, celebrity TV doctor Mehmet Oz, to flip the seat for his party.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m proud of what we ran on. Protecting a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to choose; raising our minimum wage; fighting [for] the union way of life. Healthcare is a fundamental human right. It saved my life, and it should all be there for you\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.37am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.26am GMT\par \par \uc2 Democrat Whitmer wins reelection in Michigan governor's race\par \par \uc2 Democrat \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2  has won reelection as Michigan\u8217\'20\'19s governor, the Associated Press reports, beating Republican challenger Tudor Dixon.\par \par \uc2 Whitmer was the target of intense Republican attacks for her enforcement of regulations intended to curb Covid-19 after it broke out in 2020, and the GOP hoped to oust her from office in the perennial battleground state.\par \par \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2  has won reelection as governor of Michigan. Photograph: Carlos Osorio/AP\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.30am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.18am GMT\par \par \uc2 CNN has declared \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2  the victor in Pennsylvania\u8217\'20\'19s Senate race:\par \par \uc2 enltrCNN projection: \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2  wins PA. A Dem pickup. Now GOP has to win Nevada and Georgia \u8212\'20\'14 which looks likely to go to a December runoff \u8212\'20\'14 to take back majority. In Arizona, Mark Kelly is up by 17 points with 52 percent reporting\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Manu Raju (@mkraju) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju/status/1590226125262917632?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 So has Fox News:\par \par \uc2 enltrAnd now Fox News calls Pennsylvania for Lt. Gov. \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2 : {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/cHQI5LL43o"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/cHQI5LL43o}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1590225279351676928?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press, whose race calls \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  considers definitive, still has not weighed in.\par \par \uc2 NBC was the first network to call the contest in the Democratic candidate\u8217\'20\'19s favor. Here was the scene when the crowd at Fetterman\u8217\'20\'19s election night party heard the news, as recorded by \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Oliver Laughland:\par \par \uc2 enltrThe crowd at \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s election night party in Pittsburgh erupts after MSNBC names him the projected winner: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/vl0p0d7JTq"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/vl0p0d7JTq}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Oliver Laughland (@oliverlaughland) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/oliverlaughland/status/1590225428731801600?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.10am GMT\par \par \uc2 Midterms 2022: What we know so far\par \par \uc2 Only one word is fit to sum up the results from the Senate, House and governorship races that have come in thus far: surprise. The 8 November midterm elections were expected to be rough for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s allies, potentially costing them control of one or both chambers of Congress. Instead, Democrats are showing surprising strength, holding on to Senate seats and beating back Republican challengers in several crucial House races. Full results are not in yet, and when the dust settles, the GOP may well have eked out the majorities they were expected to have. But it\u8217\'20\'19s plain tonight has not gone as expected for many Republicans across the country \u8211\'20\'13 and may end up defying the historical trend of voters using the midterm elections to punish the party in the White House:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Two of three Virginia Democrats in districts considered bellwethers for the national mood {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/nov/08/midterm-elections-2022-polls-results-senate-house-us-midterm-voting-republicans-democrats-live-updates-latest-news?page=with:block-636b220b8f0850c5a4cd4866#block-636b220b8f0850c5a4cd4866"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have won reelection}}}\uc2 , in what was an early sign of good news for Democrats.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Democrat Josh Shapiro{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/nov/08/midterm-elections-2022-polls-results-senate-house-us-midterm-voting-republicans-democrats-live-updates-latest-news?page=with:block-636b37f68f082d3d26930bbe#block-636b37f68f082d3d26930bbe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bested}}}\uc2  2020 election denier \uc2 Doug Mastriano\uc2  in Pennsylvania\u8217\'20\'19s governorship race.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 John Fetterman{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/nov/08/midterm-elections-2022-polls-results-senate-house-us-midterm-voting-republicans-democrats-live-updates-latest-news?page=with:block-636b43168f083f3e45283adb#block-636b43168f083f3e45283adb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 declared victory}}}\uc2  in his race for Pennsylvania\u8217\'20\'19s Senate seat. The Associated Press has not yet called the race.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Maryland elected {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/nov/08/midterm-elections-2022-polls-results-senate-house-us-midterm-voting-republicans-democrats-live-updates-latest-news?page=with:block-636afccb8f083f3e45283905#block-636afccb8f083f3e45283905"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the first Black governor in its history}}}\uc2 , Democrat Wes Moore.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Florida\u8217\'20\'19s voters tilted{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/nov/08/midterm-elections-2022-polls-results-senate-house-us-midterm-voting-republicans-democrats-live-updates-latest-news?page=with:block-636b00878f0850c5a4cd4782#block-636b00878f0850c5a4cd4782"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 further towards Republicans}}}\uc2 , reelecting firebrand governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  and senator \uc2 Marco Rubio\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 From Washington to New York, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/nov/08/midterm-elections-2022-polls-results-senate-house-us-midterm-voting-republicans-democrats-live-updates-latest-news?page=with:block-636b2dfc8f083f3e45283a4c#block-636b2dfc8f083f3e45283a4c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats defied}}}\uc2  Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 rosy predictions that they\u8217\'20\'19d fall apart this year, even in their traditional strongholds.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 JD Vance{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/nov/08/midterm-elections-2022-polls-results-senate-house-us-midterm-voting-republicans-democrats-live-updates-latest-news?page=with:block-636b2a898f082d3d26930b72#block-636b2a898f082d3d26930b72"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 won the Republican Senate race}}}\uc2  in Ohio, dashing Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 hopes of picking up another seat in the chamber.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.12am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.05am GMT\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press still has not called the Pennsylvania Senate race. But Democratic candidate \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2  has declared victory:\par \par \uc2 enltrIt's official. I will be the next U.S. Senator from Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 We bet on the people of Pennsylvania - and you didn\u8217\'20\'19t let us down\par \par \uc2 And I won\u8217\'20\'19t let you down. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2  (@JohnFetterman) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JohnFetterman/status/1590221958536646657?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.57am GMT\par \par \uc2 From Rachel Leingang in Phoenix, Arizona:\par \par \uc2 A heavy police presence surrounded the central tabulation building in Phoenix on Tuesday night to deter the kinds of activity seen outside the center in 2020, when \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  supporters protested outside and threatened election workers.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday night, deputies from the Maricopa county sheriff\u8217\'20\'19s office dotted the building\u8217\'20\'19s parking lot and perimeter. Some officers rode horses around the barriers.\par \par \uc2 enltrOutside the Maricopa County Tabulation Center where ballots are being processed. Horses in protest gear, about six protesters outside, lots of press {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/TCBJEbxf4S"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/TCBJEbxf4S}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Tess Owen (@misstessowen) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/misstessowen/status/1590194521056612356?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Since 2020, election workers in Maricopa county have faced threats for doing their jobs. In response, the county has taken precautions to protect them. The tabulation center now has a permanent fence around its core, and a temporary fence lining the surrounding parking lot.\par \par \uc2 In 2020, the site became the hub of conspiracy theorists including Alex Jones, who came to town {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.azmirror.com/2020/11/05/conspiracy-monger-alex-jones-shows-up-at-conspiracy-fueled-elections-protest/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 as votes were being counted}}}\uc2 , yelling through a megaphone to stop the count, and chanting to count the votes at other times.\par \par \uc2 enltrDeputies on horses trot by the Maricopa County central tabulation site in downtown Phoenix. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/dzI9uJ6QZ8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/dzI9uJ6QZ8}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rachel Leingang (@rachelleingang) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/rachelleingang/status/1590164840022421504?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Shortly after the polls closed on Tuesday, however, there were few signs of protest and only a small number of onlookers outside the fences.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.15am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.57am GMT\par \par \uc2 NBC News projects that Democrat \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2  has won the race for Pennsylvania\u8217\'20\'19s open Senate seat, giving the party their first pick up of the evening in that chamber:\par \par \uc2 enltrBREAKING: Democrat \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2  wins \uc2 U.S. Senate\uc2  race in Pennsylvania, NBC News projects. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/NqjTEpNhkv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/NqjTEpNhkv}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/34lAQYk4KR"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/34lAQYk4KR}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 NBC News (@NBCNews) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NBCNews/status/1590220564093886464?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press has not called the race. If confirmed, it could add to the Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 majority in the Senate, where the party currently has the bare minimum of 50 seats needed for control. It could also offset losses the Democrats may suffer elsewhere, if incumbent senators in states like Nevada or Arizona lose reelection.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.25am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.51am GMT\par \par \uc2 Georgia's Republican governor Kemp wins second term over Abrams\par \par \uc2 Voters in Georgia reelected Republican \uc2 Brian Kemp\uc2  to serve as governor, the Associated Press reports, handing a victory to a leader who defied \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s attempts to meddle in his state\u8217\'20\'19s election results two years ago.\par \par \uc2 His Democratic opponent \uc2 Stacey Abrams\uc2  conceded earlier tonight:\par \par \uc2 enltrDemocratic challenger \uc2 Stacey Abrams\uc2  conceded to Georgia Gov. \uc2 Brian Kemp\uc2  on Tuesday in a rematch of their 2018 race.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI may no longer be seeking the office of governor, but I will never stop doing everything in my power to ensure the people of Georgia have a voice,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/nzS1TnWZzE"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/nzS1TnWZzE}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Associated Press (@AP) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AP/status/1590217942804766720?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 This year\u8217\'20\'19s race was a rematch of 2018, when Kemp beat Abrams and won his first term in office.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.47am GMT\par \par \uc2 From {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/gabrielle-canon"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gabrielle Canon}}}\uc2  in Oakland:\par \par \uc2 California voters were on track to overwhelmingly pass a measure to enshrine the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and contraception into the state\u8217\'20\'19s constitution, making it the second state to do so on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Proposition 1 was positioned as a direct response to the \uc2 US Supreme Court\uc2  decision issued earlier this year to reverse the 1973 Roe v Wade precedent and overturn decades of established access.\par \par \uc2 Californians are clearly committed to ensuring the same can\u8217\'20\'19t happen in their home state and that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  won\u8217\'20\'19t be impacted even if the legislative tides shift. Their decisiveness on the issue will also help secure the state\u8217\'20\'19s reputation as a haven for reproductive care just as restrictions \u8211\'20\'13 and political divisions \u8211\'20\'13 deepen across the country.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights supporters protest the \uc2 US Supreme Court\uc2  decision ending federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in Los Angeles, California, on 27 June. Photograph: Mario Tama/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 Governor \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 , who won reelection with a large majority in a race called just minutes after California polls closed, joined in the celebrations at a Prop 1 rally.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CGovernor Newsom made it clear that he wants California to be visible as a haven for people seeking reproductive healthcare and Proposition 1 is part of that,\u8221\'20\'1D said constitutional law professor Cary Franklin, faculty director of the Center on Reproductive Health, Law, and Policy at the \uc2 University of California Los Angeles\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt will get media attention and people will be made more aware that California is a place they can go. People who are desperate and in need can come here and get the care they need.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrGavin Newsom speaking now at Proposition 1 rally, which is poised to pass by a huge margin to enshrine right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in California constitution:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe affirmed we are a true freedom state.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ashley Zavala (@ZavalaA) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ZavalaA/status/1590204867989340161?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 The measure had been expected to easily pass, and analysts said support for reproductive rights could draw even more women and young people to the polls, which could play positively for Democrats in California\u8217\'20\'19s conservative pockets.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C There is no \u8216\'20\'18no\u8217\'20\'19 campaign. I assume that\u8217\'20\'19s because the folks who might have financed it decided it would be a terrible waste of money and they\u8217\'20\'19d rather put their money elsewhere,\u8221\'20\'1D Bob Shrum, director of the Center for the Political Future at the \uc2 University of Southern California\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 Earlier on Tuesday, voters in Vermont voted to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the state\u8217\'20\'19s constitution.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.44am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.38am GMT\par \par \uc2 In one of the most important contests in Ohio, conservative Republicans have once again got a grip on the state\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court after winning the chief justice post and two other seats.\par \par \uc2 The victories come at a crucial time, as the court is expected to decide whether to uphold a law barring abortions beyond about six weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Republicans technically already control the court, holding four of the seven seats. But the outgoing chief justice, Maureen O\u8217\'20\'19Connor, has sided with Democrats in some politically sensitive cases, including over gerrymandering.\par \par \uc2 O\u8217\'20\'19Conner will be replaced by Sharon Kennedy, who already sits on the court but won election to the chief justice post. Kennedy made clear her commitment to conservative positions during the campaign.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is morning again at the Ohio supreme court,\u8221\'20\'1D she said in her victory speech, echoing \uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2  when he won the White House.\par \par \uc2 Ohio voters handed the state\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court to conservative Republicans once again. Photograph: Jintak Han/ZUMA Press Wire/REX/\uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 The new state supreme court is expected to decide whether to let stand the state\u8217\'20\'19s ban on most abortions which came into effect after Roe v Wade was overturned by the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 . A lower state court blocked the measure last month. Like the other Republican judges on the Ohio supreme court, Kennedy has said there is no right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Two other Republican judges were reelected. But because Kennedy has been elevated to chief justice, Ohio\u8217\'20\'19s Republican governor gets to appoint a judge to replace her.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.47am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.33am GMT\par \par \uc2 From {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/maanvi-singh"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Maanvi Singh}}}\uc2  in Oakland, California:\par \par \uc2 Democrat \uc2 Alex Padilla\uc2  has become the first Latino elected to represent California in the \uc2 US Senate\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press called the race just minutes after polls closed, with Padilla heavily favored to win. He was appointed to the post in 2021, to fill the seat formerly held by \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Alex Padilla\uc2 . Photograph: Alex Brandon/AP\par \par \uc2 Voters have chosen Padilla, 49, to complete Harris\u8217\'20\'19 term through January, and to serve a subsequent six-year term. With votes still being tallied, he is expected to lead Republican Mark Meuser by a sizable margin.\par \par \uc2 Padilla was favored to win to such an extent that he didn\u8217\'20\'19t run any campaign ads. He has said he\u8217\'20\'19ll prioritize climate action, immigration reform and reproductive freedom.\par \par \uc2 He is the first Latino senator to represent a state in which 40% of residents are of that ethnicity.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.37am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.29am GMT\par \par \uc2 In Detroit, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s Sam Levine reports the Democratic secretary of state has claimed a reelection victory against a challenger who denied the 2020 election:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWell, well, well democracy has prevailed,\u8221\'20\'1D Michigan secretary of state \uc2 Jocelyn Benson\uc2  said as she took the stage here at the Democratic election night party. She declared victory in her race to serve a second-term as Michigan\u8217\'20\'19s top election official over Kristina Karamo, a community college professor who rose to prominence by questioning the 2020 election results.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CToday Michigan voters showed the world that they will vote for truth over lies, facts over conspiracy theories, real results over empty promises,\u8221\'20\'1D Benson said.\par \par \uc2 The race was closely watched because it will determine who oversees voting in Michigan, a key battleground state. Karamo has \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s backing, while Benson vigorously defended the election results.\par \par \uc2 Secretaries of state, long overlooked as inconsequential races, have increasingly become closely-watched since \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s efforts to overturn the 2020 election. In many places, secretaries of state are the key election official, charged with overseeing how votes are cast and counted.\par \par \uc2 Election deniers are not having a good night so far. \uc2 Doug Mastriano\uc2 , another far-right candidate who sought to overturn the 2020 election results, lost his bid to be Pennsylvania\u8217\'20\'19s governor.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.34am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.19am GMT\par \par \uc2 Democrat \uc2 Josh Shapiro\uc2  beats \uc2 Doug Mastriano\uc2  in Pennsylvania governor race\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press has called Pennsylvania\u8217\'20\'19s governor\u8217\'20\'19s race for Democrat \uc2 Josh Shapiro\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 He defeats Republican \uc2 Doug Mastriano\uc2 , a strident denier of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s election victory in 2020 who has said he supports banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , without exceptions.\par \par \uc2 Josh Shapiro\uc2  gives a victory speech to supporters in Oaks, Pennsylvania, after winning the governor\u8217\'20\'19s race. Photograph: Mark Makela/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.30am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.16am GMT\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press confirms that Democratic senator \uc2 Patty Murray\uc2  of Washington has won reelection.\par \par \uc2 She will serve a sixth term representing the traditionally Democratic state, after voters rejected her challenger Tiffany Smiley. The GOP hoped \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s low approval rating and voters\u8217\'20\'19 frustration with inflation would lead to a surprise loss for Murray, but most analysts viewed that as unlikely.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.12am GMT\par \par \uc2 Democratic 'squad' members elected back to Congress\par \par \uc2 Prominent members of the so-called Democratic \u8220\'20\'1Csquad\u8221\'20\'1D have won reelection to Congress.\par \par \uc2 We reported earlier that \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2  had won her race in New York. The Associated Press has also called contests in Minnesota for \uc2 Ilhan Omar\uc2  ; in Massachusetts for \uc2 Ayanna Pressley\uc2  ; in Michigan for \uc2 Rashida Tlaib\uc2  ; and in Missouri for \uc2 Cori Bush\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Clockwise from top right: \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2 , \uc2 Ilhan Omar\uc2 , \uc2 Ayanna Pressley\uc2  and \uc2 Rashida Tlaib\uc2 . Photograph: REX/\uc2 Shutterstock\uc2 /\uc2 EPA\uc2 /AFP/Getty\par \par \uc2 The group of progressive legislators {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2019/jul/17/the-squad-name-origins-aoc-ilhan-omar-ayanna-pressley-rashida-tlaib"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gave themselves the \u8220\'20\'1Csquad\u8221\'20\'1D nickname}}}\uc2  for their disruptive style, but insisted they were about building an equitable society.\par \par \uc2 Nonetheless, their tactics have sometimes {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2021/apr/17/nancy-pelosi-the-squad-alexandria-ocasio-cortez"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 jarred with the Democratic party\u8217\'20\'19s mainstream}}}\uc2 . \uc2 Pramila Jayapal\uc2 , chair of the progressive Democratic House caucus of which the others are vocal members, made a humiliating U-turn last month when she was forced to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/25/democrats-joe-biden-ukraine-war-russia-letter"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 withdraw a letter}}}\uc2  urging \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to engage in talks with Russia to end the war in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.15am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.03am GMT\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/kari-paul"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kari Paul}}}\uc2  reports on apparent cyberattacks in Mississippi and elsewhere that briefly knocked official websites offline:\par \par \uc2 Government and voter information websites in Mississippi were temporarily knocked offline on Tuesday in an apparent cyber attack, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://therecord.media/mississippi-election-websites-knocked-out-by-ddos-attack/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 officials have confirmed}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Several state websites experienced distributed denial-of-service (DDoS) attacks, in which hackers flood the servers of a website with traffic and render it non-functional.\par \par \uc2 A senior official with the cybersecurity and infrastructure security agency (\uc2 CISA\uc2 ) said the agency is tracking a \u8220\'20\'1Chandful\u8221\'20\'1D of similar incidents in other states. Officials said the attacks were not carried out on any voting infrastructure and that no data was compromised.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have been chatting with them for the last several hours working with some of the vendors to put the mitigations in place,\u8221\'20\'1D the official said.\par \par \uc2 A pro-Russian hacking group {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ericgeller/status/1590112243382992896"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 claimed responsibility}}}\uc2  for the attacks, but officials said they had not yet confirmed the origins.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhile attribution is inherently difficult, we\u8217\'20\'19ve not seen any evidence to suggest that these are part of a widespread coordinated campaign,\u8221\'20\'1D the official said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.55am GMT\par \par \uc2 Republican \uc2 Ted Budd\uc2  has won the race for North Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s open Senate seat, defeating Democrat Cheri Beasley, the Associated Press says.\par \par \uc2 The victory denies Democrats an opportunity to increase their majority in the chamber from its current 50-50 split, where vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  breaks ties. It also gives the party fewer opportunities to keep the chamber if incumbent candidates locked in close races in states such as Georgia and Arizona end up losing.\par \par \uc2 Ted Budd\uc2  has won the race for North Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s Senate seat. Photograph: Jonathan Drake/Reuters\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.04am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.51am GMT\par \par \uc2 Historic House win for Vermont's Balint\par \par \uc2 Democrat {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://streaklinks.com/BRXXFD7SElm6OGllnAHDUAv3/https%3A%2F%2Fwww.washingtonpost.com%2Fnation%2F2022%2F10%2F27%2Fbecca-balint-vermont-woman-congress%2F"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Becca Balint}}}\uc2  made history by winning Vermont\u8217\'20\'19s only House seat, becoming the first woman and first out LGBTQ+ person to represent the state in Congress.\par \par \uc2 Balint, a lesbian, won the race with about 60% of the votes thus far, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://streaklinks.com/BRXXFD_q6omwLsMM5QTGOQEy/https%3A%2F%2Fvtdigger.org%2F2022%2F11%2F08%2Fbecca-balint-leads-liam-madden-in-vermonts-us-house-race%2F"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to VTDigger}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Balint\u8217\'20\'19s victory means that Vermont will now be in keeping with other US congressional delegations. Prior to Balint\u8217\'20\'19s victory, Vermont was the sole US state that had never elected a woman to Congress.\par \par \uc2 Becca Balint delivers a victory speech on Tuesday. Photograph: Lisa Rathke/AP\par \par \uc2 Balint replaces Vermont Democratic congressman Peter Welch, who decided to run for \uc2 US Senate\uc2  after Democratic senator \uc2 Patrick Leahy\uc2  said he would retire when his term ends in January. Welch {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://streaklinks.com/BRXXFD7TEzuOQ96RogKlnfKb/https%3A%2F%2Fvtdigger.org%2F2022%2F11%2F08%2Fpeter-welch-emerges-victorious-in-vermonts-us-senate-election%2F"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 won Leahy\u8217\'20\'19s senate seat}}}\uc2  in the election.\par \par \uc2 Annise Parker, the LGBTQ Victory Fund\u8217\'20\'19s president and CEO, celebrated Balint\u8217\'20\'19s win. \u8220\'20\'1CTonight voters made their voices heard loud and clear: they are excited about Becca and her compelling vision for Vermont and our country, one founded in courage and kindness.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor nearly a decade, Becca has worked tirelessly to enact meaningful legislation to increase fairness and equity in her community,\u8221\'20\'1D Parker said in a statement {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://streaklinks.com/BRXXFD_EBHdVSQFZqgaAyC2U/https%3A%2F%2Fwww.advocate.com%2Fpolitics%2F2022%2F8%2F10%2Fvermont-poised-send-lesbian-becca-balint-congress"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported by The Advocate}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNow, she is ready to do the same in Congress. With legislation currently moving through Congress to enshrine LGBTQ rights and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights into federal law, the urgency of this election could not be more clear.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur community and allies cannot afford to wait \u8211\'20\'13 or sit on the sidelines \u8211\'20\'13 when the rights of millions of Americans are on the line. We are confident Becca will continue to be a fierce pro-equality, pro-choice champion for all Americans,\u8221\'20\'1D Parker said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.53am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.45am GMT\par \par \uc2 Democrat Hassan wins New Hampshire Senate race\par \par \uc2 Democratic Senator \uc2 Maggie Hassan\uc2  has won reelection in New Hampshire, dealing a blow to Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 chances of retaking the majority in the chamber.\par \par \uc2 She beat Don Bolduc in a state that has been known to veer between parties but has been trending towards Democrats in recent elections.\par \par \uc2 Maggie Hassan\uc2  has won reelection in New Hampshire, holding on to her Senate seat. Photograph: Charles Krupa/AP\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.07am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.42am GMT\par \par \uc2 In the weeks leading up to today\u8217\'20\'19s election, Republicans believed Democrats were so weak that they could oust incumbent lawmakers even in traditionally blue states, like Washington.\par \par \uc2 That optimism appears to be misguided.\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press has not called the race yet, but several networks project \uc2 Patty Murray\uc2  will win reelection to represent Washington in the Senate. It will be the Democrat\u8217\'20\'19s sixth term in the chamber.\par \par \uc2 The GOP also hoped that its candidate Lee Zeldin would become the next governor of New York. Nope: multiple networks say Democratic incumbent Kathy Hochul has won a full term. Again, the AP has not called the race.\par \par \uc2 Democrats may even have picked up seats in the House. Reports are emerging that Democrat Greg Landsman managed to oust Republican House representative \uc2 Steve Chabot\uc2  in Cincinnati. The AP has yet to weigh in here.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has been hopping on the phone to congratulate his Democratic winners tonight.\par \par \uc2 enltrJust got off the phone with some of tonight\u8217\'20\'19s winners \u8212\'20\'14 including some folks I saw on the road this year.\par \par \uc2 If you\u8217\'20\'19re in line to vote, remember to stay in line! {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/43CF4rSFrP"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/43CF4rSFrP}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 President Biden (@POTUS) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS/status/1590186537961914368?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.49am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.34am GMT\par \par \uc2 Bestselling author JD Vance won the \uc2 US Senate\uc2  race in Ohio by a wider margin than opinion polls predicted, but with a narrower victory than Republicans running in other statewide races. The Democratic candidate, congressman \uc2 Tim Ryan\uc2  has conceded.\par \par \uc2 Vance\u8217\'20\'19s victory retains the seat for the Republicans.\par \par \uc2 Ohio Senate candidate JD Vance meets with supporters after casting his ballot at a polling location in Cincinnati. Photograph: Jeff Dean/AP\par \par \uc2 The Trump-backed venture capitalist, who has never won a general election before, faced a competitive challenge from Ryan, who at times appeared to be running against his own party\u8217\'20\'19s leadership as much as against Vance. Ryan {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/07/tim-ryan-ohio-senate-midterms-jd-vance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 focused his campaign}}}\uc2  on promises to support working-class communities hit by deindustrialization and the export of their jobs, which he blamed on the policies of governments of both major parties.\par \par \uc2 Congressman \uc2 Tim Ryan\uc2 , who campaigned on promises to support working-class communities, has conceded his race. Photograph: Shannon Stapleton/Reuters\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s support proved crucial in Vance winning the Republican primary but it is not clear whether it was a help or a drag with the broader electorate. Vance faced accusations of insincerity after criticising Trump as unfit for office when he was president but then embracing him when he needed his endorsement to win the primary.\par \par \uc2 In the end, Vance may have been saved by widespread disillusionment in Ohio, as elsewhere, over the state of the economy and polls showing that a majority of voters believe President Biden\u8217\'20\'19s policies are making the problem worse.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.51am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.27am GMT\par \par \uc2 A similar dynamic {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/nov/08/midterm-elections-2022-polls-results-senate-house-us-midterm-voting-republicans-democrats-live-updates-latest-news?page=with:block-636b2a898f082d3d26930b72#block-636b2a898f082d3d26930b72"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to the situation in Ohio}}}\uc2  appears to be playing out in North Carolina, where Republican \uc2 Ted Budd\uc2  may have taken the state\u8217\'20\'19s open Senate seat.\par \par \uc2 As in Ohio, Democrats had hoped a win by Cheri Beasley would allow them to pad their slim majority in the Senate. NBC and Decision Desk HQ are among those saying Budd won the race. The Associated Press has not called it.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.29am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.26am GMT\par \par \uc2 Newsom reelected as California governor\par \par \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 , who has been touted as a possible Democratic candidate for the 2024 presidential election, has won reelection as governor of California.\par \par \uc2 The race was called by the Associated Press shortly after polls closed, and his victory in a heavily Democratic state was never in doubt.\par \par \uc2 Newsom, who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/15/gavin-newsom-california-recall-victory"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 survived a recall effort}}}\uc2  a year ago, defeated Brian Dahle, the Republican challenger and a state senator.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.33am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.22am GMT\par \par \uc2 Republican Vance wins Ohio Senate race\par \par \uc2 GOP candidate JD Vance has won the race for Ohio\u8217\'20\'19s open Senate seat, the Associated Press reports, denying the Democrats an opportunity to add to their majority in Congress\u8217\'20\'19s upper chamber.\par \par \uc2 Vance defeated Democratic candidate \uc2 Tim Ryan\uc2 , who put up a stiffer-than-expected challenge in the state, which has increasingly trended towards Republicans in recent elections.\par \par \uc2 Betty Jean Bahmer, a supporter of Democratic U.S. Senate candidate, Rep. \uc2 Tim Ryan\uc2  (D-OH), reacts as the television networks call the race for Republican opponent JD Vance during an election-night event at Mr. Anthony's Banquet Center on November 8, 2022 in Boardman, Ohio. Photograph: Drew Angerer/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.31am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.18am GMT\par \par \uc2 Victory for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights activists in Vermont\par \par \uc2 Voters in Vermont have voted to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the states\u8217\'20\'19 constitution, shoring up already-existing rights in the state.\par \par \uc2 That makes it the first state to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the state constitution. For those having a \u8216\'20\'18but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/12/how-abortion-rights-won-kansas-strategies"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 what about Kansas}}}\uc2  ??\u8217\'20\'19 moment: that vote was slightly different, as anti-choice campaigners were asking people to confirm there were no protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the state constitution.\par \par \uc2 That initiative was always expected to pass - in a state so pro-choice even the Republican governor was in supports of it. But the margins speak for themselves: with 62% of votes counted, the yes campaign led 77-23%.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://vtdigger.org/2022/11/08/measure-to-enshrine-abortion-rights-in-vermont-constitution-poised-to-pass/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Local news reported a jubilant atmosphere}}}\uc2 , with many campaigners congratulating themselves for making history. Full votes will be in on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 A pick up truck drives by campaign signs opposing and supporting a proposed amendment to the Vermont constitution that would guarantee access to reproductive rights, including \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , by the side of the road in Middlesex, Vt. Photograph: Wilson Ring/AP\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.37am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.11am GMT\par \par \uc2 Democrat \uc2 Stacey Abrams\uc2  has conceded the Georgia governor\u8217\'20\'19s race to Republican incumbent \uc2 Brian Kemp\uc2 , the Atlanta Journal-Constitution reports:\par \par \uc2 enltrJust in: \uc2 Stacey Abrams\uc2  has called Kemp to concede {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/gapol?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #gapol}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Greg Bluestein (@bluestein) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/bluestein/status/1590193189973118976?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press has not yet called the race.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.07am GMT\par \par \uc2 Greg Abbott wins re-election in Texas\par \par \uc2 Greg Abbott has won a third term as Texas governor after overcoming a challenge from Democrat \uc2 Beto O\u8217\'20\'19Rourke\uc2 , the Associated Press projects.\par \par \uc2 Republicans spent more than $200m to fend off a strong challenge from the progressive O\u8217\'20\'19Rourke, who was heavily critical of the governor\u8217\'20\'19s response to the Uvalde school shooting, the state\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, and the failure of the Texas electricity grid during storms last winter.\par \par \uc2 Beto O\u8217\'20\'19Rourke\uc2 , left, has failed in his bid to unseat Greg Abbott in the Texas governor\u8217\'20\'19s race. Photograph: Eric Gay/AP\par \par \uc2 Abbott seized on crime, the economy, and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s perceived immigration failures at the southern border as key campaign issues.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.17am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.04am GMT\par \par \uc2 Polls close in California and Washington\par \par \uc2 Voting wrapped up in California and Washington as well as the rest of Oregon and Idaho at 11pm eastern time.\par \par \uc2 California is a Democratic stronghold in presidential election years, but home to several close House races in today\u8217\'20\'19s election. The dynamic is much the same in Washington, though Republicans hold long-shot hopes of ousting Democratic senator \uc2 Patty Murray\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Idaho is a Republican bastion where few surprises are expected tonight. In Oregon, the GOP thinks it has a shot at taking the governor\u8217\'20\'19s mansion amid a backlash over homelessness and crime, as well as an independent candidate\u8217\'20\'19s presence in the race.\par \par \uc2 A poll worker directs people to voting machines at Crenshaw High School in Los Angeles. Photograph: Patrick T Fallon/AFP/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.16am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.59am GMT\par \par \uc2 Virginia results indicate better-than-expected night for Democrats\par \par \uc2 The outcomes of two closely watched races in Virginia indicate Democrats are on course to lose their majority in the House of Representatives, but not by a huge margin.\par \par \uc2 Virginia is home to several House races viewed as bellwethers for the wider national mood, and results thus far indicate the \u8220\'20\'1Cred wave\u8221\'20\'1D Democrats feared would push them decisively into the majority in Congress\u8217\'20\'19s lower chamber isn\u8217\'20\'19t coming this year. Rather, Democrats appear set to lose their slim grip on the House, but not by a huge amount.\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press has just declared that Jennifer Wexton has held on to her seat in the exurbs of Washington, DC and has said that Abigail Spanberger won re-election in another district outside the nation\u8217\'20\'19s capital.\par \par \uc2 Jennifer Wexton talks with a policeman in Middleburg, Virginia last December 4. Photograph: Andrew Caballero-Reynolds/AFP/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 Voters in that area supported \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in the 2020 election, then Republican governor Glenn Youngkin the following year. If Spanberger lost, analysts believed it would have been a sign that Democrats nationally were in for a bad night. If Wexton, whose district has trended more Democratic in recent years, had fallen, that would have been a sign of a really bad night for Biden\u8217\'20\'19s allies.\par \par \uc2 Abigail Spanberger speaks to the media after visiting an early voting location along with US Senator Tim Kaine last month. Photograph: Steve Helber/AP\par \par \uc2 That said, Democrats are experiencing the rejection the party holding the White House typically does in their first midterm.\par \par \uc2 While the AP hasn\u8217\'20\'19t called the race yet, it\u8217\'20\'19s believed that Elaine Luria lost her reelection bid. She served on the January 6 committee, but has been down in the polls in a district the Cook Political Report considers the most evenly divided in the country\par \par \uc2 Elaine Luria on the trail last month. Photograph: Mike Caudill/AP\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.12am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.51am GMT\par \par \uc2 Maryland votes to legalize recreational marijuana\par \par \uc2 Maryland voters green-lighted a constitutional amendment to legalize recreational marijuana for adults over 21.\par \par \uc2 The vote puts Maryland among the 19 states, and District of Columbia, that have legalized adult-use cannabis, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://streaklinks.com/BRXKDHnGhq5YljBc7wHrR0Ct/https%3A%2F%2Fwww.baltimoresun.com%2Fpolitics%2Felections%2Fbs-md-pol-recreational-cannabis-legalization-question-20221108-gdf5yjmpwvfbzcdgmtdfxvbo6a-story.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to The Baltimore Sun}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Voters in four other states \u8211\'20\'13 including conservative strongholds such as Arkansas, Missouri, North Dakota and South Dakota \u8211\'20\'13 are considering {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://streaklinks.com/BRXKDHfkZIY5a5J0nQ4VzhD5/https%3A%2F%2Fwww.theguardian.com%2Fus-news%2F2022%2Fnov%2F08%2Fstate-ballot-initiatives-us-midterm-elections"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ballot measures}}}\uc2  that would legalize adult-use marijuana during Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s midterm election.\par \par \uc2 enltrMaryland has voted to legalize recreational marijuana use {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ZgA3ocstAR"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/ZgA3ocstAR}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 philip lewis (@Phil_Lewis_) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Phil_Lewis_/status/1590175292907134976?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 The constitutional amendment in Maryland does not mean that adults can simply go into a shop and lawfully buy marijuana. This measure effectively means that Maryland\u8217\'20\'19s state legislators can now establish the legal marijuana industry in this state.\par \par \uc2 The industry could start \u8220\'20\'1Cas soon as\u8221\'20\'1D 1 July, according to the newspaper. The vote favoring adult-use cannabis will also put into effect some legislation that was approved during the 2022 state legislative session.\par \par \uc2 Under this legislation, penalties for cannabis possession will be lowered; for possession of up to 2.5oz of marijuana, the penalty is now a civil citation rather than a criminal charge. And, the legislative change sets up a process through which people can expunge prior marijuana possession convictions.\par \par \uc2 The vote also means that adults 21 and over can legally raise up to two marijuana plants at their homes starting 1 July. Each household can have a maximum of four plants, \u8220\'20\'1Cwhich must be grown securely and out of public view,\u8221\'20\'1D the Sun reported.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.54am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.42am GMT\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press hasn\u8217\'20\'19t called Pennsylvania\u8217\'20\'19s governorship race yet, but NBC believes Democrat \uc2 Josh Shapiro\uc2  has won:\par \par \uc2 enltrBREAKING: Democrat \uc2 Josh Shapiro\uc2  wins Pennsylvania governor's race, NBC News projects. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/IAT1oNcXPg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/IAT1oNcXPg}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/osRepr5Vr0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/osRepr5Vr0}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 NBC News (@NBCNews) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NBCNews/status/1590185040427864064?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.37am GMT\par \par \uc2 Election tracker Decision Desk HQ has called New Hampshire\u8217\'20\'19s Senate race for the Democratic incumbent \uc2 Maggie Hassan\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 enltrDecision Desk HQ projects \uc2 Maggie Hassan\uc2  (D) wins re-election to the \uc2 U.S. Senate\uc2  in New Hampshire. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/DecisionMade?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #DecisionMade}}}\uc2  : 10:30pm EST\par \par \uc2 Follow more results here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ogd3AkeoyM"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/ogd3AkeoyM}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ZCnFzUSspD"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ZCnFzUSspD}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Decision Desk HQ (@DecisionDeskHQ) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DecisionDeskHQ/status/1590185198477791234?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 The GOP was hoping that their candidate Don Bolduc could oust Hassan and put them on the path to take control of the chamber. However, the Associated Press, whose race calls \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  follows, has not made a determination in New Hampshire. The northeastern state is considered a swing state, though has trended Democratic in recent years.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.31am GMT\par \par \uc2 Poppy Noor has news from Kentucky\u8217\'20\'19s referendum on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights:\par \par \uc2 Residents of Kentucky have been voting on a referendum to state there is no right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the state\u8217\'20\'19s constitution. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  advocates worried about the vote, because although voters in deep red Kansas voted no when given the same option earlier this year, Kentuckians skew slightly more conservative on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But the early signs are hopeful for pro-choice advocates. With 50% of the vote in, the no campaign has a 12% lead, which it has maintained steadily over the last few hours.\par \par \uc2 Protesters gather at the Kentucky state Capitol in Frankfort earlier this year. Photograph: Ryan C Hermens/AP\par \par \uc2 Earlier, Madeline Dyer from the EMW Surgical Center, one of two \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics that remain in Kentucky, said that voters see the ballot proposal as too extreme.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m really hopeful,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. Talking about an outreach campaign that she has been working on with \uc2 University of Kentucky\uc2  students, she added: \u8220\'20\'1CPeople find it so extreme, the idea of having no exceptions for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . These topics are very sensitive, and the majority of people understand there are situations where people should have access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Kentucky\u8217\'20\'19s state supreme court is set to review its current \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban on 15 November. A no vote on Tuesday can\u8217\'20\'19t predict how judges will vote, but a win for the yes campaign would certainly be viewed as a huge obstacle for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 In state supreme court elections, one judge seeking election is Joe Fischer, a former Republican congressman who was the key sponsor of the state\u8217\'20\'19s trigger ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 He also authored the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  referendum that\u8217\'20\'19s being put to Kentucky voters tonight.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.47am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.24am GMT\par \par \uc2 From Carlisa Johnson in Atlanta:\par \par \uc2 Election watch parties are under way in Georgia, although it looks like it could be a long night. At Democratic senator Raphael Warnock \u8217\'20\'19s event in Atlanta, Bryce Berry, president of the Young Democrats of Georgia and a Morehouse student, spoke with the audience about the legacy that Georgians stand in.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy hero, the late Congressman John Lewis, in 1965 stood on the Edmund Pettus Bridge,\u8221\'20\'1D said Berry. \u8220\'20\'1CHe didn\u8217\'20\'19t see the state troopers standing in front of him, he saw what was possible, and he pressed forward. He saw what was possible when we vote, and that\u8217\'20\'19s Georgia, that\u8217\'20\'19s America \u8211\'20\'13 the courage to press forward.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A supporter cheers with the Georgia flag in the background during the election night party for Raphael Warnock. Photograph: John Amis/\uc2 EPA\par \par \uc2 Illustrating the diversity of Warnock\u8217\'20\'19s supporters, Alma Young also took the stage to speak to the audience. \u8220\'20\'1CI stand here, the embodiment of the American Dream,\u8221\'20\'1D said Young, who arrived in Georgia at 16 as a migrant farm worker.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI know that Senator Warnock is the son of sharecroppers. For us, this means the world because farmworkers live in the shadows. But we get a glimmer of light because we know Senator Warnock understands, and stands for us.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s Senate race between Warnock and controversial Republican challenger Herschel Walker is expected to be close and could go to a run-off next month.\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 This post was amended on 21 November 2022 to remove the suggestion that Alma Young was attending the rally as a member of the United Farm Workers Foundation.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.59pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.15am GMT\par \par \uc2 From Sam Levine in Detroit, Michigan:\par \par \uc2 The mood is festive here at what Democrats hope will be an election night celebration for Michigan governor \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2  and other state party candidates at the MotorCity Casino in Detroit.\par \par \uc2 enltrMood is really celebratory here in Detroit at an election night party for Michigan Democrats {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Q5mxtJPyo2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Q5mxtJPyo2}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Sam Levine (@srl) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/srl/status/1590168538127355905?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 People are were dancing when I walked in, and cheers went up when MSNBC, playing on the big screens, showed Whitmer with a lead over her opponent, Republican Tudor Dixon.\par \par \uc2 Michigan could potentially be a bright spot for Democrats. In addition to winning the governor\u8217\'20\'19s mansion, they have a chance to hold on to the attorney general and secretary of state\u8217\'20\'19s office. They could also flip the state senate.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.10am GMT\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, at the White House, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  can\u8217\'20\'19t do much but watch \u8230\'20\'26 and work the phones.\par \par \uc2 The president has made congratulatory calls to a number of Democrats who won their races tonight, the White House announced. These include Massachusetts governor-elect \uc2 Maura Healey\uc2 , Colorado governor Jared Polis, Senate majority leader Chuck Schumer and House representative Abigail Spanberger, whose Virginia district was seen as a bellwether for how strong the Republican resurgence tonight will be.\par \par \uc2 While several outlets have called Spanberger\u8217\'20\'19s reelection win, the Associated Press has not done so.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.40am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.00am GMT\par \par \uc2 From Adam Gabbatt in Pittsburgh:\par \par \uc2 People have begun arriving at \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s election night event in Pittsburgh, as Democratic supporters nervously await news about the Pennsylvania US Senate race.\par \par \uc2 Fetterman isn\u8217\'20\'19t expected until much later, but hundreds are already in Stage AE, normally a gig space but in use tonight for political purposes.\par \par \uc2 At the crowded bar area, Bill Beardsley was drinking a beer made by Iron City, Pittsburgh\u8217\'20\'19s local brewery. The retired union official at the Pittsburgh Steam Fitters union, described himself as a \u8220\'20\'1Clabor Democrat\u8221\'20\'1D. He was confident of a Fetterman win, despite polls showing the race between Fetterman and Mehmet Oz, a Republican celebrity doctor, tightening in recent weeks.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat the polling doesn\u8217\'20\'19t reflect are the newly registered voters, most of which are women pissed off over Roe v Wade,\u8221\'20\'1D Beardsley said.\par \par \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2  supporters in Pittsburgh on Tuesday night. Photograph: Jim Lo Scalzo/\uc2 EPA\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe polls narrowing \u8211\'20\'13 it\u8217\'20\'19s bound to happen. Most elections they do narrow, it\u8217\'20\'19s not surprising in the least. Plus Oz\u8217\'20\'19s campaign ran a brutal amounts of false ads, all of them were negative, so it was bound to happen.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEvery election, a bad guy lies his way into the picture.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Oz has closed a once significant gap on Fetterman, and with the restrictive laws on when Pennsylvania can begin counting his votes, the race may not be decided tonight. Beardsley said he was not a fan of Oz, who has said he moved to Pennsylvania from New Jersey in October 2020, but has been accused of still living across the border.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s a stone goof. He\u8217\'20\'19s a fraud, he\u8217\'20\'19s a charlatan, he\u8217\'20\'19s a snake oil salesman. And he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t even live in Pennsylvania.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.05am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.00am GMT\par \par \uc2 A longshot Democratic candidate in Louisiana challenging the Republican party\u8217\'20\'19s US House whip Steve Scalise in Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s midterms will not be able to force him into a runoff, according to a New Orleans TV news station known for its accurate political projections.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wwltv.com/watch"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 WWL-TV}}}\uc2  called Scalise\u8217\'20\'19s re-election outright about 15 minutes after the polls closed at 8pm local time in his district, which mostly encompasses suburban New Orleans.\par \par \uc2 Veteran station political analysts Clancy DuBos and pollster Ron Faucheux made the call in favor of Scalise, 57, as he took 72% of a sample of votes across his district, which they projected would be too large of a margin for two challengers to overcome even as the rest of the ballots came in and were counted.\par \par \uc2 The Democratic party\u8217\'20\'19s nominee for the race, Katie Darling, captured 26% of that voting results sample, and Libertarian hopeful Howard Kearney took 2%.\par \par \uc2 Darling was hoping to finish ahead of Kearney while keeping Scalise under 50% to force him into a runoff that would have been held on 10 December.\par \par \uc2 Scalise, from the New Orleans suburb of Jefferson, has been the US House representative for Louisiana\u8217\'20\'19s 1st congressional district since 2008 and is getting set for a ninth term in that post.\par \par \uc2 Steve Scalise, in this photo from 2019. Photograph: Erin Scott/Reuters\par \par \uc2 He was the House Republican whip \u8211\'20\'13 or the party\u8217\'20\'19s number two in the chamber \u8211\'20\'13 heading into his re-election campaign. If the Republicans capture enough seats after Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s midterms to retake a majority in the House, he would be in line to become the party leader ranking just behind the chamber\u8217\'20\'19s speaker, his hometown newspaper the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nola.com/news/politics/article_cdc4450c-5492-11ed-a310-4bd879f0bba0.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Times-Picayune newspaper}}}\uc2  reported.\par \par \uc2 In that case, he would also become the highest-ranking Louisiana congressmember since the powerful New Orleans Democrat Hale Boggs, the US House majority party leader when he and his plane disappeared over Alaska during a trip in 1972.\par \par \uc2 Scalise\u8217\'20\'19s ascent to that high-ranking spot would be just over five years after he survived being shot in an attack on a congressional baseball game practice in 2017.\par \par \uc2 Fox News White House correspondent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JacquiHeinrich"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jacqui Heinrich}}}\uc2  late in the night tweeted that a Republican source told her Scalise could even be in line for the House Speaker spot if the GOP took a majority in the chamber that the party considered underwhelming and rebuked California\u8217\'20\'19s Kevin McCarthy for the role. McCarthy entered the night as the House\u8217\'20\'19s Republican leader.\par \par \uc2 Scalise appeared at a post-campaign celebration with his wife, Jennifer, and two children late Tuesday and predicted the Republican party would recapture a majority in the House. Scalise pledged to work to lower prices at stores and gasoline stations, to push to increase domestic oil production, and to send more federal funding to law enforcement, all of which were Republican talking points during this midterm cycle.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe need to make Washington work for people again, and that\u8217\'20\'19s what the focus will be,\u8221\'20\'1D Scalise told supporters at the event at the popular restaurant Drago\u8217\'20\'19s in the New Orleans suburb of Metairie.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Darling\u8217\'20\'19s campaign did capture some national attention at one point after an ad showed her pregnant and calling out the extremely restrictive Louisiana \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws which took effect after the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  in June voted to eliminate the nationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights that had been established by the landmark 1973 Roe v Wade case.\par \par \uc2 The ad features Darling going to a hospital in a wheelchair as she is about to give birth.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe should be putting pregnant women at ease, not putting their lives at risk,\u8221\'20\'1D she said in the political spot, which went viral on social media.\par \par \uc2 Then, while holding her infant baby, she looked at the camera and declared, \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m running for Congress \u8230\'20\'26 for you \u8230\'20\'26 and for him.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In other prominent congressional races in Scalise\u8217\'20\'19s region of Louisiana, WWL-TV was projecting Troy Carter \u8211\'20\'13 the Democratic incumbent in the state\u8217\'20\'19s 2nd congressional district, based mostly in New Orleans \u8211\'20\'13 to win re-election outright and avoid a runoff against Republican Dan Lux.\par \par \uc2 Louisiana\u8217\'20\'19s Republican US Senator John Neely Kennedy was also projected by the station to win outright over a large field of challengers that was arguably headlined by Democrats Luke Mixon and Gary Chambers.\par \par \uc2 None of Louisiana\u8217\'20\'19s congressional races were expected to produce surprise outcomes, with incumbent candidates or their parties predicted to retain contested seats.\par \par \uc2 Most of the country\u8217\'20\'19s congressional races during Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s midterms featured two-candidate runoffs. But in Louisiana, Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s midterms were so-called jungle primaries where the top two vote-getters would advance to a 10 December runoff regardless of party \u8211\'20\'13 unless any one candidate captured a majority of the ballots cast and won outright.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.16am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.58am GMT\par \par \uc2 Fresh off his reelection win in the South Carolina Senate race, Republican Tim Scott hinted at running for president:\par \par \uc2 enltrSen. Tim Scott (R-SC) hints at a presidential run during his victory speech. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/kGyehlGrEx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/kGyehlGrEx}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1590176056665079808?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 He would have to square off against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who is expected to announce another run for the White House, perhaps in the days after the midterms.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.54am GMT\par \par \uc2 Voting wraps up in too-close-to-call Nevada\par \par \uc2 Voting has just finished in Nevada, where its Democratic governor and senator are standing for re-election in races pollsters see as among the closest in the country.\par \par \uc2 Senator \uc2 Catherine Cortez Masto\uc2  is considered one of the most vulnerable Democrats up for another term in office, and is facing a stiff challenge from Republican \uc2 Adam Laxalt\uc2 , Nevada\u8217\'20\'19s former attorney general. \uc2 Steve Sisolak\uc2 , a Democrat, is standing for a second term against the GOP nominee Joe Lombardo, sheriff of Clark county, the state\u8217\'20\'19s most populous.\par \par \uc2 Voting also wrapped up at 10pm eastern time in Montana and Utah, as well as parts of Idaho and Oregon.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.58am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.49am GMT\par \par \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2  and \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  win re-election\par \par \uc2 Two firebrand congress members of the outside edges their parties have won reelection, \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2  in New York for the Democrats, and extremist Republican \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  in Georgia, the Associated Press projects.\par \par \uc2 Progressive Ocasio-Cortez\u8217\'20\'19s margin over Tina Forte is almost two votes to one, the agency says, although less than half the votes have so far been tallied.\par \par \uc2 AOC campaigns with Kathy Hochul, the New York state governor, on Tuesday. Photograph: David Dee Delgado/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 Election denier Taylor Greene\u8217\'20\'19s victory was called almost as soon as ballots closed in Georgia. If Republicans go on to secure control of the House of Representatives, she will be among those calling loudly for the impeachment of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.57am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.32am GMT\par \par \uc2 Dani Anguiano reports from Las Vegas:\par \par \uc2 With time running out for Nevadans to cast their ballots, candidates in the state\u8217\'20\'19s tossup Senate race are still fighting to edge each other out with TV ads and outreach to voters.\par \par \uc2 Ads for \uc2 Adam Laxalt\uc2 , the Republican former state attorney general who is trying to unseat incumbent \uc2 Catherine Cortez Masto\uc2 , were running throughout Tuesday afternoon. Meanwhile, Democratic organizers in the state have dialed up efforts to contact voters.\par \par \uc2 Catherine Cortez Masto\uc2 . Photograph: Gregory Bull/AP\par \par \uc2 Volunteers with the state\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic party have made over 55,000 phone calls, sent more than a million text messages and knocked on roughly 5,500 doors. The local culinary union, which is backing Democratic candidates up and down the ballot, has knocked on more than one million doors in the state of 3m people.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CStatewide numbers are just razor thin right now. This comes down to getting as many of those voters to turn out in Nevada. When we turn out it goes blue,\u8221\'20\'1D said Matthew Fonken, the executive director of the state\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic party.\par \par \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2  spoke over Zoom with about 20 volunteers at the state\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic party headquarters phone banking on the eve of the election: \u8220\'20\'1CIn a race this close like it is with Nevada, it is all about souls to the polls, baby. We need to go into every grocery store, every crosswalk, every school pickup, we need to be everywhere.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNevada is a really important area in our country. I truly believe that the southwest United States holds the key to America\u8217\'20\'19s political future.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the local culinary union was out canvassing through election day, knocking on doors to connect directly with voters and encourage them to vote \u8211\'20\'13 Nevada has same-day registration.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.24am GMT\par \par \uc2 The latest dispatch from Chris McGreal in Columbus, Ohio:\par \par \uc2 There is a buoyant mood among Ohio Republicans at their election party in a downtown Columbus hotel after the Associated Press projected what looks to be an emphatic win for \uc2 Mike DeWine\uc2  in his campaign for re-election as the state\u8217\'20\'19s governor.\par \par \uc2 But the predicted victory of a man widely regarded as a bipartisan, old-school conservative is a reminder of how far the Republican party has moved to the right \u8211\'20\'13 a shift accelerated by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s presidency.\par \par \uc2 The division in the Republican party was on display at Trump\u8217\'20\'19s rally in Dayton on Monday evening. When he called DeWine on stage, many in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/08/big-announcement-donald-trump-holds-back-decision-on-2024-presidential-run"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the crowd booed}}}\uc2  at the governor who drew stinging criticism from some Republicans for following the science, and not Trump, during the early months of the Covid pandemic.\par \par \uc2 Mike DeWine\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in Dayton on Monday. Photograph: Gaelen Morse/Reuters\par \par \uc2 DeWine has maintained relatively strong approval ratings among Ohioans even if a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cleveland.com/news/2022/10/majority-of-ohioans-would-support-enshrining-abortion-rights-in-the-ohio-constitution-new-poll-says.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 majority oppose}}}\uc2  the ban on abortions beyond about six weeks of pregnancy that he signed into law.\par \par \uc2 But the real test of Republican strength in a state that twice voted for \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  before embracing Trump in his two presidential elections will be the outcome of the race for \uc2 US Senate\uc2  between the bestselling author and venture capitalist, JD Vance, and his Democratic opponent, Congressman \uc2 Tim Ryan\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The result will also be a test of the extent to which Trump\u8217\'20\'19s endorsement is a help or a hindrance for a candidate. It was crucial in delivering Vance\u8217\'20\'19s victory in the Republican primary, but may have undermined him in the general election by alienating some swing voters who were happy to vote for DeWine or in motivating Democrats to come out and vote who might otherwise have given the midterms a pass.\par \par \uc2 Ryan {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/07/tim-ryan-ohio-senate-midterms-jd-vance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has run}}}\uc2  without much direct help from the Democratic leadership, although that in itself may have been a bonus because it allowed him to distance himself from a party elite viewed with suspicion by many working class voters in Ohio.\par \par \uc2 Opinion polls put the two neck and neck.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.28am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.17am GMT\par \par \uc2 Congress has its first member from generation Z, after progressive Maxwell Alejandro Frost, a musician, Uber driver and gun-control activist, won his race in central Florida.\par \par \uc2 Democrat Frost, 25, won the seat vacated by Val Demings, who gave it up for her unsuccessful campaign to unseat \uc2 Marco Rubio\uc2  as US senator for Florida.\par \par \uc2 He campaigned on issues including \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, the climate emergency and universal healthcare, and secured almost 60% of the vote against Republican candidate Calvin Wimbish.\par \par \uc2 enltrWE WON!!!! History was made tonight. We made history for Floridians, for Gen Z, and for everyone who believes we deserve a better future. I am beyond thankful for the opportunity to represent my home in the \uc2 United States Congress\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/FL10?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #FL10}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Maxwell Alejandro Frost (@MaxwellFrostFL) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MaxwellFrostFL/status/1590152059570905089?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 But the activist turned politician, who was a director of the student-led March for Our Lives group following the 2018 massacre of 17 students and staff at a Parkland, Florida, high school, also drew controversy.\par \par \uc2 A pro-Palestinian group {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.middleeasteye.net/news/how-florida-progressive-maxwell-frost-abandoned-palestine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 accused him of abandoning them}}}\uc2  and others accused him of tempering his progressive views as the campaign continued.\par \par \uc2 Other than \uc2 Madison Cawthorn\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s election in 2020, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/11/08/us/politics/maxwell-frost-florida-house.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Washington Post reports}}}\uc2 , Frost is the first 25-year-old elected to Congress in more than 45 years.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/06/ive-always-had-these-crazy-ideas-the-25-year-old-uber-driver-bidding-to-become-the-first-gen-z-member-of-congress"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18I\u8217\'20\'19ve been Maced, I\u8217\'20\'19ve been to jail \u8230\'20\'26\u8217\'20\'19 Can 25-year-old Maxwell Frost now be the first Gen Z member of Congress?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.19am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.13am GMT\par \par \uc2 While polls have closed in Arizona, the legal wrangling over voting in its most populous county has not.\par \par \uc2 The New York Times\uc2  reports that a judge has denied a Republican motion to keep polls open for three extra hours in Maricopa county, where Phoenix is:\par \par \uc2 enltrBREAKING: An Arizona judge just DENIED a GOP motion to keep polls in Maricopa county open for 3 extra hours because of the tabulations issues today. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/cFKHH6wCch"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/cFKHH6wCch}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ken Bensinger (@kenbensinger) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kenbensinger/status/1590161742994485248?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 However, the GOP plans to continue to pursue the issue:\par \par \uc2 enltrA lawyer for the plaintiffs reserved the right to keep the matter open. In argument he said that the issue could determine the next AZ governor and the balance of the Senate \u8212\'20\'14 and it's clear the \uc2 RNC\uc2  is not dropping the issue.\par \par \uc2 Another hearing on the issue is set for Nov. 16\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ken Bensinger (@kenbensinger) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kenbensinger/status/1590164524820475904?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 The two candidates for governor, Republican Kari Lake and Democrat \uc2 Katie Hobbs\uc2 , had before polls closed tweeted messages encouraging people to remain in line:\par \par \uc2 enltrRemember: if you're in line by 7pm, you'll be able to cast your ballot! Maricopa voters: find your nearest voting location at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/hMClh8UaNW"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/hMClh8UaNW}}}\uc2 . Pima voters: visit {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/76DBlSRev8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/76DBlSRev8}}}\uc2  to find your polling location. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/TrustedInfo2022?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #TrustedInfo2022}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/QwMUfuotTB"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/QwMUfuotTB}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Secretary \uc2 Katie Hobbs\uc2  (@SecretaryHobbs) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SecretaryHobbs/status/1590153647891312642?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrYour vote matters.\par \par \uc2 GET IN LINE.\par \par \uc2 STAY IN LINE.\par \par \uc2 AND VOTE!\par \par \uc2 If you are in line by 7 pm they CANNOT stop you from voting {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/fs7hwKucnr"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/fs7hwKucnr}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kari Lake (@KariLake) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KariLake/status/1590160346379345922?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.16am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.08am GMT\par \par \uc2 The senate\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic leader Chuck Schumer has been re-elected in New York, the Associated Press confirms.\par \par \uc2 Over the past two years, Schumer has led the Democratic majority in the chamber that they control by a single vote. Today\u8217\'20\'19s election will determine whether he continues in that role, or returns to being the chamber\u8217\'20\'19s minority leader if Democrats lose control.\par \par \uc2 Chuck Schumer speaks at an election night party for New York governor Kathy Hochul. Photograph: Brendan McDermid/Reuters\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.53am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.02am GMT\par \par \uc2 Polls close in swing states Arizona and Wisconsin\par \par \uc2 Voting has just wrapped in Wisconsin and Arizona, both the site of closely watched races for governor and Senate.\par \par \uc2 Polls additionally closed in Colorado, Iowa, Louisiana, Minnesota, Nebraska, New Mexico, New York and Wyoming at 9pm eastern time. Parts of Kansas, Michigan, North Dakota, South Dakota and Texas also finished voting.\par \par \uc2 Democrats are trying to revitalize their fortunes in Wisconsin by ousting sitting Republican senator Ron Johnson, though their candidate Mandela Barnes has been behind in recent polls. They\u8217\'20\'19re also hoping voters will give Democratic governor \uc2 Tony Evers\uc2  a second term.\par \par \uc2 Republican senator Ron Johnson votes in \uc2 Oshkosh\uc2 , Wisconsin. Photograph: Tannen Maury/\uc2 EPA\par \par \uc2 Arizona has only recently started trending towards Democrats, and there, senator Mark Kelly is fighting for his seat against the GOP nominee \uc2 Blake Masters\uc2 . Democrat \uc2 Katie Hobbs\uc2  is seen as badly trailing Republican Kari Lake in the contest for governor.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.10am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.56am GMT\par \par \uc2 The Republican party has scored a victory in its quest to regain the majority in the House, with Anna Luna defeating Democratic candidate Eric Lynn in Florida, according to the Associated Press.\par \par \uc2 The district around St Petersburg on the Gulf coast was previously represented by Democrat \uc2 Charlie Crist\uc2 , who resigned to unsuccessfully run against Republican governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.59am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.45am GMT\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/sam-levine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sam Levine}}}\uc2  reports from Detroit, Michigan, on fears that polling would be disrupted, and voters intimidated across the country. The state wraps up voting in about 15 minutes:\par \par \uc2 It wasn\u8217\'20\'19t perfect, but voting seems to have unfolded without major instances of violence or disruption at the polling place.\par \par \uc2 Going into election day, there was concern there would be significant numbers of voters who would show up and find their eligibility challenged. And there was deep worry that voters would face harassment, fears that were escalated when {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/04/voter-intimidation-midterm-elections-arizona"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 citizens with guns patrolled drop boxes in Arizona}}}\uc2  during early voting and photographed people as they dropped off their ballots.\par \par \uc2 But as polls began to close on Tuesday, there were no widespread reports of intimidation or harassment. Nor were there reports of widespread issues.\par \par \uc2 There were reports of voters being harassed as they went into polling sites in Florida and Texas, said Damon Hewitt, president and executive director of \uc2 Lawyers\u8217\'20\'19 Committee for Civil Rights Under Law\uc2 , which helps run a voter protection hotline.\par \par \uc2 There were also reports of students at Texas A&M not being able to get provisional ballots. College students in Ohio also reportedly faced questions about their eligibility at the polls, said an official from the state\u8217\'20\'19s chapter of Common Cause, a government watchdog group.\par \par \uc2 In Detroit, a glitch in the electronic poll book software led to voters being told that they had already cast a mail-in ballot when they showed up to vote. The issue was quickly corrected and no voters were blocked from voting, the state said.\par \par \uc2 Voters cast their ballots at a polling station in Kissimmee, Florida. Photograph: Gregg Newton/AFP/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 That didn\u8217\'20\'19t stop \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and Kristina Karamo, the Republican nominee to be Michigan\u8217\'20\'19s top election official, from suggesting something was amiss.\par \par \uc2 In Arizona, there were issues with tabulators at nearly a third of vote centers in Maricopa county. Technicians resolved the problem by late afternoon on Tuesday. The \uc2 Republican National Committee\uc2  filed a lawsuit to keep the polls open three extra hours, until 10pm ET, and not post any results until 11pm.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.11am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.40am GMT\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a little perspective on the significance Florida\u8217\'20\'19s rightward lurch, courtesy of Politico:\par \par \uc2 enltrMassive rightward shift in Florida. Against a much stronger opponent this time around (Demings), Rubio running away with it with 56 percent of the vote and 14-point edge w 78% in.\par \par \uc2 Rubio beat Murphy 52-44 in 2016.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Burgess Everett (@burgessev) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/burgessev/status/1590153851025428488?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.34am GMT\par \par \uc2 Sarah Huckabee Sanders\uc2  elected governor of Arkansas\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press confirms it: Republican \uc2 Sarah Huckabee Sanders\uc2  has been elected governor in Arkansas, becoming the state\u8217\'20\'19s first woman to serve in the office.\par \par \uc2 She takes over from fellow Republican Asa Hutchinson.\par \par \uc2 Sarah Huckabee Sanders\uc2 , the new governor of Arkansas. Photograph: Mandel Ngan/AFP/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.40am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.31am GMT\par \par \uc2 Rubio victory confirms Republican wave in Florida\par \par \uc2 Marco Rubio\uc2  has been re-elected as senator for Florida, trouncing his Democratic challenger Val Demings and confirming a wave of Republican support in the former swing state.\par \par \uc2 With 78% of votes counted, according to the Associated Press, Rubio had recorded an insurmountable lead, 56.8% to Demings\u8217\'20\'19 42.6%.\par \par \uc2 It reflected a similar margin recorded by \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , the state\u8217\'20\'19s Republican governor re-elected to a second term of office after seeing off a challenge from Democrat \uc2 Charlie Crist\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Marco Rubio\uc2 , who has won his Senate re-election race. Photograph: Eva Marie Uzcategui/AFP/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 Notable was Rubio turning Miami-Dade county, formerly a Democratic stronghold, along with neighboring Broward and Palm Beach counties in the state\u8217\'20\'19s south east corner, red for the first time in four decades.\par \par \uc2 Republicans in Florida had been increasingly confident of securing the support of the region\u8217\'20\'19s sizeable Hispanic voting bloc.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.32am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.30am GMT\par \par \uc2 Polls have closed in Arkansas, a solidly red state where no surprises are anticipated tonight.\par \par \uc2 Republican \uc2 Sarah Huckabee Sanders\uc2  is expected to win election as the state\u8217\'20\'19s first female governor. She previously served as one of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s many White House press secretaries.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.16am GMT\par \par \uc2 Democrat Healey triumphs in Massachusetts governor's race\par \par \uc2 Democrat \uc2 Maura Healey\uc2  has won the governor\u8217\'20\'19s race in Massachusetts, the Associated Press says, taking the office from outgoing Republican \uc2 Charlie Baker\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Healey is the state\u8217\'20\'19s current attorney general, and will be the first openly lesbian governor in the country. She beat Republican \uc2 Geoff Diehl\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.31am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.13am GMT\par \par \uc2 DeSantis reelected as Florida governor\par \par \uc2 Republican \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  has won reelection as Florida governor, according to an Associated Press projection.\par \par \uc2 The ultra-conservative DeSantis handily defeated Democrat \uc2 Charlie Crist\uc2 , himself a former Republican governor of the state.\par \par \uc2 enltrFlorida Gov. \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  has won reelection to his second term in office, defeating Democrat \uc2 Charlie Crist\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19 victory will help him continue his march as a rising Republican star and could serve as a launching pad to a 2024 White House bid. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/lCA8pLaimu"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/lCA8pLaimu}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/unmSrOwZnN"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/unmSrOwZnN}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Associated Press (@AP) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AP/status/1590149564480512001?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Questions will immediately be asked if DeSantis, a rising star of the Republican party, intends to see out his new term, or use his reelection as a springboard to challenge for the 2024 presidential nomination.\par \par \uc2 Former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , his likely rival if he runs, spent time Tuesday trying to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/08/donald-trump-ron-desantis-2024-president-campaign"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dissuade DeSantis from launching a campaign}}}\uc2 , advising him to \u8220\'20\'1Cstay in Florida\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.19am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.12am GMT\par \par \uc2 Wes Moore makes history as Maryland's first Black governor\par \par \uc2 Maryland has elected Democrat Wes Moore as governor, putting an African American into the governor\u8217\'20\'19s mansion for the first time:\par \par \uc2 enltrBREAKING: Democrat Wes Moore wins election for governor in Maryland. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/APracecall?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #APracecall}}}\uc2  at 8:00 p.m. EST. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/2nlgpji7ac"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/2nlgpji7ac}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 AP Politics (@AP_Politics) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AP_Politics/status/1590147481056284673?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Moore replaces Republican \uc2 Larry Hogan\uc2 , a moderate who managed to twice win election in what is otherwise a solidly blue state.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.00am GMT\par \par \uc2 Polls close in swing-state Pennsylvania and 15 others\par \par \uc2 Polls have just closed in Pennsylvania, where Democrats are trying to keep control of its governors mansion and win its open Senate seat.\par \par \uc2 The eastern state is one of more than a dozen others to finish voting at 8pm eastern time. Voting wrapped up in Alabama, Connecticut, Delaware, Illinois, Maine, Maryland, Massachusetts, Mississippi, Missouri, New Hampshire, New Jersey, Oklahoma, Rhode Island and Tennessee. Polling also concluded in the rest of Florida as well as parts of Kansas, Michigan, North Dakota, South Dakota and Texas.\par \par \uc2 Washington DC, which does not elect senators but does have a non-voting delegate in the House, also closed its polls.\par \par \uc2 Mehmet Oz, running for Senate in Pennsylvania. Photograph: Ed Jones/AFP/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.09am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.59am GMT\par \par \uc2 Polls are closing imminently in Texas. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/erum-salam"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Erum Salam}}}\uc2  takes a look at the issues that have been central to voters.\par \par \uc2 The stakes are high in Texas, a state that recently passed one of the nation\u8217\'20\'19s most restrictive \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws, saw one of the deadliest mass shootings in history in Uvalde, and where the electrical grid faces scrutiny after it failed during the 2021 winter storm, causing widespread blackouts.\par \par \uc2 For governor, Texans are witnessing a tight race between hard-right Republican Greg Abbott and Democrat \uc2 Beto O\u8217\'20\'19Rourke\uc2 , who outraised his opponent but still trails in the polls. O\u8217\'20\'19Rourke challenged Ted Cruz for his US senate seat in 2018, but lost by less than 3%.\par \par \uc2 Other key races in the state include the seats for lieutenant governor and attorney general, positions currently held by Republicans \uc2 Dan Patrick\uc2  and \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2  respectively, both of whom denied the results of the 2020 presidential election and promote false voter fraud theories.\par \par \uc2 In recent years, South Texas, a historically Democratic bastion where Latino voters are key, has been losing ground to Republicans. Across counties in the area in 2020, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  either won against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  by lower margins compared with Hillary Clinton in 2016, or lost outright.\par \par \uc2 Three key House races in south Texas are between Latinos on opposite sides of the political spectrum, and remain close. In district 15, progressive Michelle Vallejo faces off against Trump-backed Monica De La Cruz.\par \par \uc2 District 28 has been blue since its creation in 1993, but history could change if Cassy Garcia defeats incumbent Democrat Henry Cuellar.\par \par \uc2 And in district 34, far-right conspiracy theorist and incumbent Mayra Flores faces Democratic challenger Vincente Gonzalez.\par \par \uc2 Texas voters have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.uttyler.edu/politicalscience/files/utt_lv_oct2022.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cited}}}\uc2  as top concerns securing the border, inflation and the economy, and reproductive rights.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.47am GMT\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/poppy-noor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Poppy Noor}}}\uc2  is in Detroit, Michigan, where voting closes at 8pm ET.\par \par \uc2 Poll workers at the Keiden Special education center were cheerful and chatty this evening, as a line of 10 or so voters stood waited to cast their vote.\par \par \uc2 The two precincts represented at the polling booth are usually low turnout, they said, but today turnout has been much higher, especially among young people and first time voters.\par \par \uc2 But one poll worker reported frustration from several voters, who had seen signs at the Boys and Girls club of Southeast Michigan - another polling location just around the corner - saying there was no voting today.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe heard our first complaint at 6.30am, and have since heard from three others,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, expressing dismay at what she viewed as a deterrent tactic. She said they had followed up with the department of elections.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.49am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.43am GMT\par \par \uc2 In less than 30 minutes, polls will shut in Pennsylvania, home to two closely watched races.\par \par \uc2 The first is for its Senate seat, which is being vacated by a Republican and represents an opportunity for the Democrats to pad their majority in the chamber \u8211\'20\'13 or offset a loss elsewhere. Republican Mehmet Oz is in a very close race against Democrat \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The other is for the governor\u8217\'20\'19s mansion, where Democrat \uc2 Josh Shapiro\uc2  appears to be leading his Republican challenger \uc2 Doug Mastriano\uc2 . Mastriano is regarded as a particularly vociferous denier of the facts around \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s victory in the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 CBS News has reported some exit poll data for the state, which contains good news for Democrats. The survey indicates \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is voters\u8217\'20\'19 top concern, an issue that is seen as animating Democratic turnout after the supreme court in June overturned Roe v Wade and allowed states to ban the procedure:\par \par \uc2 enltrPRELIMINARY \uc2 CBS\uc2  NEWS EXIT POLL -- PENNSYLVANIA:\par \par \uc2 Which ONE of these issues mattered most to your vote?\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  36%\par \par \uc2 Inflation 28%\par \par \uc2 Crime 11%\par \par \uc2 Gun policy 10%\par \par \uc2 Immigration 8%\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Steven Portnoy (@stevenportnoy) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/stevenportnoy/status/1590107477923622912?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 8, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrPRELIMINARY \uc2 CBS\uc2  NEWS EXIT POLL -- PENNSYLVANIA:\par \par \uc2 Which comes closest to your position? \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be...\par \par \uc2 Legal in all/most cases 64%\par \par \uc2 Illegal in all/most cases 32%\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Steven Portnoy (@stevenportnoy) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/stevenportnoy/status/1590107688368840704?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 8, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.34am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump warns DeSantis against White House run\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/hugo-lowell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hugo Lowell}}}\uc2  is at former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s election night party at his Palm Beach, Florida, mansion:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  briefly wandered into the ballroom at his Mar-a-Lago resort, the venue for the election night watch party, and appeared to warn Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 for a second time on Tuesday \u8211\'20\'13 that running for the White House in 2024 would be a mistake.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not sure he would want to run,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said of DeSantis, who is expected to coast to re-election in the gubernatorial race and is considering a presidential campaign.\par \par \uc2 Guests gather in the Mar-a-Lago ballroom in Palm Beach for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s election night party. Photograph: Ricardo Arduengo/Reuters\par \par \uc2 The former president\u8217\'20\'19s remarks doubled down on more expansive comments earlier in the day that suggested he would reveal unsavory information about DeSantis were he to challenge Trump for the Republican nomination in 2024.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf he did run, I will tell you things about him that won\u8217\'20\'19t be very flattering,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump told reporters. \u8220\'20\'1CI know more about him than anybody other than perhaps his wife, who is really running his campaign.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump endorsed DeSantis in his 2018 campaign for governor, elevating him from a relatively obscure Tea Party congressman to the most powerful politician in Florida. DeSantis only narrowly won that election but his opposition to Covid lockdowns and vaccines turned him into a Republican darling.\par \par \uc2 Trump is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/06/trump-2024-presidential-run-announcement"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expected to announce his third run for the White House}}}\uc2  potentially as soon as next week, according to people familiar with discussions, but he remained coy about who he might choose as a running mate for vice-president.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COh, I\u8217\'20\'19ll let you know very soon,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/08/donald-trump-ron-desantis-2024-president-campaign"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump warns party rival Ron DeSantis not to run for president in 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.37am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.30am GMT\par \par \uc2 Polls close in Ohio, where Democrat \uc2 Tim Ryan\uc2  aims to turn back red tide\par \par \uc2 Voting has just finished in Ohio, which was once considered a swing state but has in recent elections become dominated by the GOP. That doesn\u8217\'20\'19t mean it\u8217\'20\'19s not home to an interesting race. In the contest for its open Senate seat, surveys have shown Democrat \uc2 Tim Ryan\uc2  displaying surprising strength against Republican JD Vance. A Ryan victory would be something of an upset, and would greatly aid the Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 quest to continue holding the Senate.\par \par \uc2 Also closing their polls at 7.30pm eastern time are North Carolina and West Virginia. The latter state is solidly red, and is not viewed as having close races this year. One of North Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s Senate seats is being vacated, but Republican \uc2 Ted Budd{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/2022-election-forecast/senate/north-carolina/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is favored to win}}}\uc2  over Democrat Cheri Beasley.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.33am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.24am GMT\par \par \uc2 The Republican candidate for governor in Arizona, Kari Lake, told reporters earlier she will be their \u8220\'20\'1Cworst fricking nightmare for eight years\u8221\'20\'1D if she defeats the Democrat \uc2 Katie Hobbs\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Lake has been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/03/kari-lake-trump-arizona-maga-republicanism-midterms"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 talked up}}}\uc2  as a running mate for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in his widely expected run for the Republican presidential nomination.\par \par \uc2 Asked about the prospect on Tuesday, the former TV anchor {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mediaite.com/tv/kari-lake-delivers-ominous-warning-to-reporters-at-press-conference-im-going-to-be-your-worst-freaking-nightmare/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CWe have talked about this before. I\u8217\'20\'19ve answered this question. I am going to not only be the governor of Arizona for four years, I\u8217\'20\'19m going to do two terms.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m going to be your worst fricking nightmare for eight years, and we will reform the media as well. We are going to make you guys into journalists again, so get ready. It\u8217\'20\'19s gonna be a fun eight years. I can\u8217\'20\'19t wait to be working with you.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Kari Lake, Arizona Republican candidate for governor, speaks to the media after voting on election day, in Phoenix. Photograph: Ross D Franklin/AP\par \par \uc2 Lake has mirrored Trump in attacking the mainstream media despite having thrived within it. Before entering politics, Trump hosted 14 seasons of The Apprentice for NBC. Lake had a long career as an anchor for KSAZ-TV, a Fox affiliate in Phoenix.\par \par \uc2 On election day, Lake shared {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KariLake/status/1589958414402297856"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a campaign ad}}}\uc2  in which she smashed TVs.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s time to take a sledgehammer to the mainstream media\u8217\'20\'19s lies and propaganda,\u8221\'20\'1D said Lake, who has repeated Trump\u8217\'20\'19s propagandist lie about electoral fraud in his defeat by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in 2020.\par \par \uc2 The televisions Lake destroyed showed anchors from MSNBC and CNN.\par \par \uc2 As Arizona voted on Tuesday, Lake\u8217\'20\'19s shift from TV to politics looked likely to pay off. The Cook Political Report {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cookpolitical.com/ratings/governor-race-ratings"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rated}}}\uc2  the race a toss-up but the polling website FiveThirtyEight gave Lake {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://fivethirtyeight.com/features/final-2022-governor-election-forecast/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a 68% chance}}}\uc2 . The University of Virginia Center for Politics {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://centerforpolitics.org/crystalball/articles/final-ratings-for-the-2022-election/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  the race leaned Republican.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/03/kari-lake-trump-arizona-maga-republicanism-midterms"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18A really dangerous candidate\u8217\'20\'19: Kari Lake, the new face of Maga Republicanism}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.33am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.13am GMT\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Republican National Committee\uc2  (\uc2 RNC\uc2 ) has joined a lawsuit filed by what it says is a party \u8220\'20\'1Ccoalition\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 including candidate for governor Kari Lake \u8211\'20\'13 to extend polling hours in Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s Maricopa county, citing \u8220\'20\'1Ctabulation issues\u8221\'20\'1D with voting machines that election officials say are false.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CVoting machines in over 25% of voting locations have experienced significant issues. The widespread issues \u8211\'20\'13 in an election administered by Democrat secretary of state \uc2 Katie Hobbs\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 are completely unacceptable,\u8221\'20\'1D the \uc2 RNC\uc2  statement says, in part.\par \par \uc2 County officials say a Republican claim that the machines are not tabulating votes properly is \u8220\'20\'1Cnot true\u8221\'20\'1D. They are also challenging {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JohnKavanagh_AZ?ref_src=twsrc%5Egoogle%7Ctwcamp%5Eserp%7Ctwgr%5Eauthor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a tweet}}}\uc2  by Republican state senate candidate John Kavanagh calling on voters to take photographs as evidence.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is illegal to take pictures inside a vote center,\u8221\'20\'1D the county says.\par \par \uc2 Voting in Arizona is set to close at 9pm ET.\par \par \uc2 enltr1. This claim is not true.\par \par \uc2 2. It is illegal to take pictures inside a vote center... so do not encourage friends to do this. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/TQ07hYVWmF"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/TQ07hYVWmF}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Maricopa County (@maricopacounty) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/maricopacounty/status/1590115564084948992?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 8, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.24am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.13am GMT\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press has made its first race calls for this evening, none of which are surprises:\par \par \uc2 enltrBREAKING: Republican Harold Rogers wins reelection to \uc2 U.S. House\uc2  in Kentucky's 5th Congressional District. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/APracecall?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #APracecall}}}\uc2  at 7:07 p.m. EST. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/2nlgpji7ac"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/2nlgpji7ac}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 AP Politics (@AP_Politics) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AP_Politics/status/1590134103730524162?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrBREAKING: Democrat Peter Welch wins election to \uc2 U.S. Senate\uc2  from Vermont. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/APracecall?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #APracecall}}}\uc2  at 7:00 p.m. EST. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/2nlgpji7ac"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/2nlgpji7ac}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 AP Politics (@AP_Politics) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AP_Politics/status/1590132351614558210?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrBREAKING: Republican Tim Scott wins reelection to \uc2 U.S. Senate\uc2  from South Carolina. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/APracecall?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #APracecall}}}\uc2  at 7:00 p.m. EST. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/2nlgpjzI1K"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/2nlgpjzI1K}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 AP Politics (@AP_Politics) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AP_Politics/status/1590132346870644736?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.08am GMT\par \par \uc2 Polls won\u8217\'20\'19t close there till 10 pm eastern time, but one of the biggest races tonight is in Nevada, where Democratic senator \uc2 Catherine Cortez Masto\uc2  is fighting for another term. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/dani-anguiano"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dani Anguiano}}}\uc2  is on the ground in Las Vegas:\par \par \uc2 At the Doolittle community center on the historic westside of Las Vegas, a steady stream of voters trickled in through the day, despite winds and light rain that some feared could drive down turnout.\par \par \uc2 Jazlynn Roush, a voting outreach canvasser for Democrats, attributed it to voters casting their ballots early and via mail. Roush has spent recent weeks urging people to get out and vote, particularly in local races.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPeople don\u8217\'20\'19t think about their district as much as they do their country,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s your local elections that make the biggest difference in your life\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Some at the community center voters were greeted by congressman Steven Horsford, a Democrat running against Republican Sam Peters, a retired Air Force Major who has expressed doubt about the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 Horsford spoke with an 18-year-old who had never voted, encouraging him to register and cast his ballot. \u8220\'20\'1CBy voting you can protect our democracy,\u8221\'20\'1D he told the young man. \u8220\'20\'1CIt makes a world of difference in a race as close as mine\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrWith so many close races, Nevada Dems are trying to reach as many voters as possible in the home stretch. Outside the Doolittle community center in Las Vegas\u8217\'20\'19 Westside, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepHorsford?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @RepHorsford}}}\uc2  encouraged an 18-year-old to vote for the first time: \u8220\'20\'1CBy voting you can protect our democracy\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/GGV9vAYZgz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/GGV9vAYZgz}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Dani Anguiano (@Dani_Anguiano) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Dani_Anguiano/status/1590104681245970433?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 8, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis midterm is critical to the future,\u8221\'20\'1D Horsford told the Guardian. \u8220\'20\'1CWe just want to make sure that young men like him, and all other eligible voters get their vote in today, especially young Black men, who sometimes feel maybe disenfranchised or not reached in the way that we need to.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI talked about who I am, my roots in this community and why I\u8217\'20\'19m running and I\u8217\'20\'19m hopeful that he\u8217\'20\'19ll cast his ballot, and be proud of the fact that he got to participate in this election\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Las Vegas resident Henry Thorns said he voted for Horsford and every other Democrat because he felt the candidates would address issues including housing, homelessness and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. \u8220\'20\'1CThis election here is more important than anything,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.01am GMT\par \par \uc2 Polls close in Georgia, home to crucial Senate race\par \par \uc2 Polls have just closed in Georgia, the site of one of this year\u8217\'20\'19s closest Senate races, as well as in Virginia, South Carolina and Vermont.\par \par \uc2 In Georgia, Democratic senator Raphael Warnock is fighting for his seat against Republican challenger Herschel Walker. The Democrats have the bare minimum required for a majority in Congress\u8217\'20\'19s upper chamber, and if Warnock loses, they will need to gain a Senate seat elsewhere to maintain control.\par \par \uc2 Parts of Florida and the remainder of Indiana and Kentucky also closed their polls at 7pm eastern time.\par \par \uc2 Raphael Warnock at a campaign event in Atlanta on Tuesday. Photograph: Bob Strong/Reuters\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.05am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.47pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Earlier this week, poll guru Dave Wasserman of the Cook Political Report identified a group of vulnerable Democratic House representatives whose races could be indicative of the party\u8217\'20\'19s wider fortunes.\par \par \uc2 The Republicans are widely expected to take control of the House after today\u8217\'20\'19s elections, but the greater question is how big their majority will be. Here\u8217\'20\'19s what Wasserman had to say:\par \par \uc2 enltrHere's my rough thinking early on Election Night:\par \par \uc2 - If {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/VA02?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #VA02}}}\uc2  Luria (D) holds on, better night for Dems than expected\par \par \uc2 - If {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/IN01?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #IN01}}}\uc2  Mrvan (D) or {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/VA07?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #VA07}}}\uc2  Spanberger (D) lose, Rs likely winning 20+ seats\par \par \uc2 - If {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/NH02?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #NH02}}}\uc2  Kuster (D) or {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/VA10?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #VA10}}}\uc2  Wexton (D) lose, Rs likely winning 30+ seats {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/XNIp07Sj0y"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/XNIp07Sj0y}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Dave Wasserman (@Redistrict) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Redistrict/status/1588570060670394368?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 4, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrA word of caution, though: at least in VA, the very first results reported are likely to favor Rs. Extra caution is warranted in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/VA07?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #VA07}}}\uc2 , where Prince William Co.'s mail ballots are critical to Rep. Abigail Spanberger's (D) path to victory and could be the last to be counted.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Dave Wasserman (@Redistrict) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Redistrict/status/1588573045551423488?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 4, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.35pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/adam-gabbatt"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Adam Gabbatt}}}\uc2  is in Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania, another state with tight races for senator and governor, and has this report:\par \par \uc2 The result of the Senate election in Pennsylvania is set to be extremely tight, but a corresponding race to become the state\u8217\'20\'19s next governor has mostly gone under the radar.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s largely because Doug Mastriano, the Republican candidate, has run a strange, furtive campaign: refusing all media requests from mainstream local and national media, and only running television ads in Pennsylvania in the last couple of weeks.\par \par \uc2 Doug Mastriano. Photograph: Carolyn Kaster/AP\par \par \uc2 Mastriano, a Donald Trump -backed, far-right election denier, has never troubled Josh Shapiro, the Democratic candidate, in the polls, and currently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.realclearpolitics.com/epolls/2022/governor/pa/pennsylvania_governor_mastriano_vs_shapiro-7696.html#polls"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 trails his opponent}}}\uc2  by an average of 8.3%.\par \par \uc2 The bid by Mastriano was flawed from the start. The state senator narrowly won the Republican primary, but only after Democrats {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.latimes.com/politics/story/2022-05-19/pennsylvania-governor-mastriano-shapiro-trump-democratic-meddling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ran ads boosting Mastriano}}}\uc2 , hoping he would be easier to defeat in November.\par \par \uc2 It turns out they were probably right, as Mastriano, a Christian nationalist who has said women who violated a proposed six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.witf.org/2019/11/14/heart-beat-bill-under/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 should be charged}}}\uc2  with murder, has apparently proved too extreme for his own party. Mastriano frequently attacks trans people, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://soundcloud.com/newstalk1037fm/news-talk-1037fm-welcomes-col-doug-mastriano-12-feb-18?utm_source=clipboard&utm_medium=text&utm_campaign=social_sharing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has said}}}\uc2  gay marriage should be illegal, and that same-sex couples should not be allowed to adopt children.\par \par \uc2 The establishment GOP {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/10/11/republicans-governor-elections-2022-tv-ads-00061005"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 essentially gave up}}}\uc2  on Mastriano earlier this year, opting not to spend money advertising an ailing campaign, and even {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/pittsburgh/news/former-president-trump-makes-pittsburgh-pit-stop-for-mastriano-oz/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an appearance with Trump}}}\uc2  on Saturday seems unlikely to make a difference.\par \par \uc2 In what could be a long night for Democrats, a triumph in the governor\u8217\'20\'19s race would be some good news. As governor, Mastriano, who in 2020 introduced a bill which would have rejected certification of Pennsylvania\u8217\'20\'19s vote, would choose who certifies \u8211\'20\'13 or doesn\u8217\'20\'19t \u8211\'20\'13 the state\u8217\'20\'19s election results.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/24/doug-mastriano-pennsylvania-republicans-trump-governor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Doug Mastriano: is the Trump-backed election denier too extreme to win?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.05am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.25pm GMT\par \par \uc2 First US midterms polls close in Indiana and Kentucky\par \par \uc2 Polls have just closed in Indiana and Kentucky, both states whose races aren\u8217\'20\'19t viewed as tight or crucial to determining Senate control. The calm won\u8217\'20\'19t last for long.\par \par \uc2 At 7pm eastern time, voting will end in several states, including Georgia, home to one of this year\u8217\'20\'19s marquee senate races as Democratic incumbent Raphael Warnock attempts to fend off Republican challenger Herschel Walker. Other states where polls close include South Carolina, Virginia and Vermont, as well as the rest of Kentucky and Indiana, and part of Florida.\par \par \uc2 A slew of states shut their polling places at 8pm eastern time, including New Hampshire and Pennsylvania, both states with Senate races are seen as crucial for determining whether Democrats can hang on to their majority for another two years. Other big states wrapping up include Maryland and parts of Texas and Michigan.\par \par \uc2 A voter in Indianapolis earlier on Tuesday. Photograph: Kelly Wilkinson/AP\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.53pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.14pm GMT\par \par \uc2 No races have been called yet, but the Associated Press just released the results of a poll that reveals a sour mood among the electorate, with voters tired of high inflation and worried about the state of both America\u8217\'20\'19s economy and democracy.\par \par \uc2 The poll of 90,000 voters conducted for the AP by NORC at the University of Chicago showed half of voters say inflation was a significant factor in their vote, while 8 in 10 said they think the economy is in a poor state. Another 44% of voters said the future of American democracy was their top concern.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/2022-midterm-elections-abortion-biden-inflation-cf4dffe87a7c2fd1bdd58df0346e15dc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more from the AP}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Inflation has been a clear blow to the well-being of many Americans. A third of voters describe their families as falling behind financially. That\u8217\'20\'19s nearly double the percentage of the electorate that said the same two years ago. A similar percentage say they are not confident they can keep up with their expenses.\par \par \uc2 While inflation has shaped Republican messaging in the run-up to the midterms, voters are split over pinning the blame on Biden. About half say his policies led prices to climb, while nearly as many say the inflation is due to forces outside the president\u8217\'20\'19s control.\par \par \uc2 Democrats also tried to tap their base\u8217\'20\'19s outrage after the Supreme Court overturned the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections in Roe v. Wade, the 1973 decision enshrining the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Overall, 7 in 10 voters say the ruling was an important factor in their midterm decisions.\par \par \uc2 VoteCast also shows the reversal was broadly unpopular. About 6 in 10 say they are angry or dissatisfied by it, while about 4 in 10 were pleased. And roughly 6 in 10 say they favor a law guaranteeing access to legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide.\par \par \uc2 Crime also was an important factor for most voters, and half say the Biden administration has made the U.S. less safe from crime.\par \par \uc2 Despite concerns about democracy, about 4 in 10 voters say they are \u8220\'20\'1Cvery\u8221\'20\'1D confident that votes in the midterm elections will be counted accurately, an improvement from the percentage of the 2020 electorate that said so.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.50pm GMT\par \par \uc2 First polls about to close in midterm voting\par \par \uc2 Polling places will soon close in the first US states after millions of Americans cast ballots in an election that\u8217\'20\'19s widely viewed as a referendum on Joe Biden \u8217\'20\'19s first two years in office, and could put Donald Trump \u8217\'20\'19s Republican allies back into control of Congress.\par \par \uc2 Voting will wrap up in Kentucky and most of Indiana at 6 pm eastern time, with other states following suit in the hours ahead. Expect the outcome of several crucial races to be called today and in the wee hours of Wednesday. Other contests are so close that they are expected to be fought to the last ballot, and it could be days before the outcomes are known.\par \par \uc2 However it shakes out, follow this live blog for the latest news on this year\u8217\'20\'19s midterm elections as it happens.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/08/midterm-election-day-race-won-when-timing-deadlines"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 When will we know who won US midterm races \u8212\'20\'14 and what to expect on election day}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.05pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020221121eibl0030v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
