\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Midterm elections 2022: Republicans edge towards slim House majority as last results trickle in \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Joanna Walters in New York (now) and Chris Stein in Washington (earlier) \par \uc2 6,905 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 November 2022\par 15:21 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 slim hopes of holding on to lower chamber appear to be ebbing away as \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  expected to announce 2024 runUS midterm elections results 2022 \u8211\'20\'13 liveSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.35pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 As we close this blog, Republicans need one more seat to clinch control of the \uc2 US House of Representatives\uc2  and former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is preparing for a major announcement in Florida that most believe will be his intention to run for the White House again \u8211\'20\'13 in the 2024 election.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  is launching a brand new blog now to take you through the evening\u8217\'20\'19s news, as it happens, in the run-up to the Trump event at his Mar-a-Lago residence and resort in Palm Beach, where we have reporters stationed and also watching from afar.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s been a lively day in US political news and of course it\u8217\'20\'19s far from over.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where things stand:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has asked House speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/nov/15/us-midterm-elections-republicans-house-power-senate-trump-2024?page=with:block-637416a88f08dd2276d83abf#block-637416a88f08dd2276d83abf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stay on}}}\uc2  in Congress and continue to hold a leadership role even if, as is soon expected, Republican control of the House in the midterms means her days as speaker will be numbered, sources tell Politico and Reuters.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A federal judge has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/nov/15/us-midterm-elections-republicans-house-power-senate-trump-2024?page=with:block-6374097b8f08d41054ea8974#block-6374097b8f08d41054ea8974"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ruled}}}\uc2  that a Covid-19-era order used to expel hundreds of thousands of migrants back across the southern US border to Mexico is unlawful, threatening to upend border policy.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/nov/15/us-midterm-elections-republicans-house-power-senate-trump-2024?page=with:block-6373f23d8f08dd2276d839c1#block-6373f23d8f08dd2276d839c1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 requesting}}}\uc2  another big infusion of aid from Congress to help Ukraine weather the Russian invasion, and also to fight Covid-19.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 House Republicans have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/nov/15/us-midterm-elections-republicans-house-power-senate-trump-2024?page=with:block-6373ec418f08341844536a23#block-6373ec418f08341844536a23"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 named}}}\uc2 Kevin McCarthy their candidate for speaker, should they win a majority in the chamber, which could happen very soon, with the GOP needing just one more seat win in the midterms to clinch control.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic senatorMark Kelly{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/nov/15/us-midterm-elections-republicans-house-power-senate-trump-2024?page=with:block-6373e8668f08dd2276d83970#block-6373e8668f08dd2276d83970"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  his Republican opponent \uc2 Blake Masters\uc2  conceded in a phone call that he had lost the race in the midterm elections.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Liz Cheney{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/nov/15/us-midterm-elections-republicans-house-power-senate-trump-2024?page=with:block-6373b07f8f083418445366f8#block-6373b07f8f083418445366f8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 had the last word}}}\uc2  in a spat with Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s defeated GOP governor candidate Kari Lake, but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/nov/15/us-midterm-elections-republicans-house-power-senate-trump-2024?page=with:block-6373b67d8f0834184453674d#block-6373b67d8f0834184453674d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 warned of}}}\uc2  the continued threat to democracy posed by many Republicans in Congress.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Rupert Murdoch{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/nov/15/us-midterm-elections-republicans-house-power-senate-trump-2024?page=with:block-6373be6d8f08dd2276d8376f#block-6373be6d8f08dd2276d8376f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is reportedly sick of Trump}}}\uc2  and may switch his allegiance to Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , a development that could have big implications for the ex-president\u8217\'20\'19s new White House campaign.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Only a handful of House races{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/nov/15/us-midterm-elections-republicans-house-power-senate-trump-2024?page=with:block-6373c4e78f0834184453683c#block-6373c4e78f0834184453683c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 remain uncalled}}}\uc2 , and the GOP is one seat away from winning control of the chamber. It\u8217\'20\'19s possible one of several races in California could deliver Republicans a majority today, while more results are expected in a crucial Colorado race tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.20pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Alex Villanueva, the embattled sheriff of Los Angeles county, has conceded to Robert Luna, the former police chief of Long Beach, ending the scandal-plagued tenure of a law enforcement leader who critics had called the \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  of LA\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Villanueva conceded this afternoon, one week after the election, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.latimes.com/california/story/2022-11-15/luna-wins-la-county-sheriff-election-over-villanueva"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 saying}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CI want to wish the incoming sheriff well. The safety of the community depends on him succeeding,\u8221\'20\'1D the \uc2 Los Angeles Times\uc2  reported. His concession comes as Luna\u8217\'20\'19s lead has continued to grow, with the challenger earning 60% of the vote compared to the incumbent\u8217\'20\'19s 40%.\par \par \uc2 Retired Long Beach police chief Robert Luna and Los Angeles sheriff Alex Villanueva debate ahead of the midterms at the Skirball Cultural Center in September 2022. Photograph: Allen J Schaben/AP\par \par \uc2 Over the course of his four-year term, Villanueva repeatedly attracted national attention with a series of misconduct, abuse and corruption scandals at the department, which is the largest county sheriff\u8217\'20\'19s agency in the US.\par \par \uc2 He became known for lashing out at politicians, community leaders, journalists, whistleblowers, watchdogs and other law enforcement officials who tried exposing problems at the agency. Luna has pledged to reform the department and jail system and end the \u8220\'20\'1Cdysfunction and chaos\u8221\'20\'1D of Villanueva\u8217\'20\'19s tenure, though under Luna, the Long Beach police department also had its own {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://spectrumnews1.com/ca/la-west/politics/2022/03/14/sheriff-candidate-robert-luna-goes-back-to-his-east-la-roots"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 scandals}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 This is only the second time in more than a century that LA residents have ousted an incumbent sheriff. For more background on Villanueva, here is our {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/05/los-angeles-county-sheriff-election-alex-villanueva"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 previous story}}}\uc2  on the race.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.41pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.57pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden asking Pelosi to continue in leadership role in Congress - report\par \par \uc2 As Democrats stand on the brink of losing control of the House of Representatives to the Republicans, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has asked House Speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  to stay on in Congress and continue to hold a leadership role, Reuters reports, citing unnamed sources.\par \par \uc2 Reverse ferret? Pelosi receives the gavel from House Republican leader Kevin McCarthy during the start of Congress in Washington DC. Photograph: Kevin Lamarque/Reuters\par \par \uc2 This news is just emerging. But of course if the GOP grabs the House, that will mean Pelosi handing the speaker\u8217\'20\'19s gavel to whomever the Republicans vote to be the speaker when they take control in January.\par \par \uc2 Kevin McCarthy will continue leading the Republicans in the House and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/nov/15/us-midterm-elections-republicans-house-power-senate-trump-2024?page=with:block-6373ec418f08341844536a23#block-6373ec418f08341844536a23"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was nominated}}}\uc2  to become Speaker in the event the GOP win the House, but that doesn\u8217\'20\'19t yet mean he\u8217\'20\'19ll win the necessary 218 votes in the expected January 3 floor vote ascend to the role of Speaker, much as he would like to be.\par \par \uc2 When Pelosi was asked recently if she\u8217\'20\'19d retire if the Democrats lost control of the House, and following the vicious assault on her husband Paul Pelosi last month by an unhinged right-wing suspect who put him in the hospital in California with a broken skull, Pelosi, 82, indicated that she might consider her position in Congress, depending on how the midterm elections panned out.\par \par \uc2 Well, they panned out better than expected for Democrats, despite the imminent loss of the House. Paul Pelosi is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/03/paul-pelosi-attack-hospital-released"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 home from hospital}}}\uc2  and \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  popped up at the Cop27 climate talks in Egypt last week.\par \par \uc2 Now it appears that Biden wants to keep her influential hand on the Democratic tiller in Congress in some way, pre-empting any possible retirement.\par \par \uc2 Steny Hoyer\uc2  is currently House majority leader. Reuters adds that a Politico columnist first reported the conversation and the sources confirmed the accuracy of the account.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.14pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.44pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints\uc2  will support proposed federal legislation to codify the right to same-sex marriage.\par \par \uc2 A vote is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2022/11/14/same-sex-marriage-law-senators-deal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 due in the US Senate tomorrow}}}\uc2  on the bipartisan Respect for Marriage Act that would enshrine marriage equality into federal law with regard to same-sex and interracial marriage.\par \par \uc2 In a classic tap dance, the Utah-based Mormon faith reiterated that it considers same-sex relationships to be \u8220\'20\'1Cagainst God\u8217\'20\'19s commandments\u8221\'20\'1D but that they would support the right to marriage under certain conditions, including respect for their right of religious belief on the matter.\par \par \uc2 This is the church\u8217\'20\'19s latest step to stake out a more welcoming stance toward the LGBTQ+ community while holding firm to its belief that same-sex relationships are sinful, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 Patrick Mason, a professor of religious studies at \uc2 Utah State University\uc2 , said the church\u8217\'20\'19s position was both a departure from and continuation of its past stances respecting laws yet working to safeguard religious liberty and ensuring they won\u8217\'20\'19t be forced to perform same-sex marriages or grant them official church sanction.\par \par \uc2 In 2016, the church declared that same-sex attraction was not a sin \u8211\'20\'13 while maintaining that acting on it was.\par \par \uc2 Utah senator Derek Kitchen, the state\u8217\'20\'19s only LGBTQ+ lawmaker, speaks during a news conference at the Utah State Capitol in Salt Lake City in June. Photograph: Rick Bowmer/AP\par \par \uc2 Axios reports that Wisconsin senator \uc2 Tammy Baldwin\uc2 , who, together with Republican \uc2 Susan Collins\uc2  of Maine, is leading the legislative effort on the Democratic side, believes the bill has the 60 votes needed to break a filibuster.\par \par \uc2 The news site further reports that Baldwin, Collins, Rob Portman of Ohio, \uc2 Kyrsten Sinema\uc2  of Arizona and \uc2 Thom Tillis\uc2  of North Carolina issued a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.portman.senate.gov/index.php/newsroom/press-releases/senators-move-forward-bipartisan-respect-marriage-act-protections-religious"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2  Monday saying they reached a deal on \u8220\'20\'1Ccommonsense\u8221\'20\'1D changes to the bill to protect religious freedom. The changes were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2022/08/02/gay-marriage-senate-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 first reported by Axios}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.57pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.07pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Freshly re-elected US senator for Wisconsin, the Republican {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jan/08/senator-ron-johnson-to-seek-re-election-wisconsin-republican"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ron Johnson}}}\uc2  has indicated he will back Florida\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Rick Scott\uc2  over longtime senate leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  in tomorrow\u8217\'20\'19s leadership vote, it\u8217\'20\'19s reported tonight.\par \par \uc2 Johnson has told the conservative news site the Daily Signal about his pick to unseat McConnell in what has the potential to be an acrimonious situation.\par \par \uc2 enltrNEW: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RonJohnsonWI?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @RonJohnsonWI}}}\uc2  tells me he is nominating \uc2 Rick Scott\uc2  to unseat \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/CRHsGg70XO"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/CRHsGg70XO}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Mary Margaret Olohan (@MaryMargOlohan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MaryMargOlohan/status/1592637735868977152?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 15, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.09pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.56pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Court rules Covid-era Title 42 border expulsion policy unlawful\par \par \uc2 A federal judge on Tuesday ruled that a Covid-19-era order used to expel hundreds of thousands of migrants back across the southern {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-mexico-border"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US border}}}\uc2  to Mexico was unlawful, a ruling that could have major implications for border management, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 In a 49-page opinion, US district court judge Emmit Sullivan said the policy was \u8220\'20\'1Carbitrary and capricious\u8221\'20\'1D and violated federal regulatory law.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll have more details shortly.\par \par \uc2 Title 42 is a public health mandate utilized by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  that has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/07/migrants-us-mexico-border-title-42-covid"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 persisted}}}\uc2  in the Biden administration, barring migrants and asylum seekers from entering the country at land borders.\par \par \uc2 That means, with exceptions, that the federal authorities at the border can summarily expel most migrants without granting them access to the US legal system to make a case for being able to stay in the US.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/cities/2022/nov/06/us-mexico-border-body-bags-pile-up"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18A backlog of bodies\u8217\'20\'19: why this is the deadliest year for the US-Mexico border}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.58pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.38pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has been briefed on the situation in Poland, the White House has said, and will speak with Polish president \uc2 Andrzej Duda\uc2  soon, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 The US president, who is in Bali, Indonesia, for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/nov/15/russia-launches-new-wave-of-missile-strikes-across-ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the G20 talks}}}\uc2 , is being kept up to speed on the latest alarming developments in Russia\u8217\'20\'19s war on Ukraine since, earlier today, Poland raised its military readiness after two died in a blast within its borders following Russian strikes across Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Biden is apparently talking with the head of Poland\u8217\'20\'19s national security bureau, Jacek Siewiera, right now.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/nov/15/russia-ukraine-war-live-news-updates-kherson-victory-marks-beginning-of-end-of-russian-war-zelenskiy-says"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 blogging}}}\uc2  developments in the war, live, and you can find all that coverage {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/nov/15/russia-ukraine-war-live-news-updates-kherson-victory-marks-beginning-of-end-of-russian-war-zelenskiy-says"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.40pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.33pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Senate Republicans are holding their leadership vote tomorrow, following House Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 vote today that kept Kevin McCarthy on top.\par \par \uc2 Senate minority leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 , whose prospect of becoming majority leader next year were dashed by Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 retaining control of the upper chamber in the midterm elections, is projecting confidence.\par \par \uc2 This despite an apparent challenge {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/nov/15/us-midterm-elections-republicans-house-power-senate-trump-2024?page=with:block-6373faca8f08d41054ea88fe#block-6373faca8f08d41054ea88fe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 coming from}}}\uc2  Florida senator \uc2 Rick Scott\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CI want to repeat again, I have the votes, I will be elected.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 McConnell says issue is whether they hold elections tomorrow or not. Says they have another discussion about that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/loTCjy65MJ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/loTCjy65MJ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Heather Caygle (@heatherscope) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/heatherscope/status/1592628415257272325?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 15, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.23pm GMT\par \par \uc2 A judge overturned Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  starting around six weeks into a pregnancy, ruling today that it violated the US constitution and \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  precedent when it was enacted and was therefore void.\par \par \uc2 Fulton county superior court judge Robert McBurney \u8217\'20\'19s ruling took effect immediately statewide, though the state attorney general\u8217\'20\'19s office said it appealed it. The ban had been in effect since July, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 It prohibited most abortions once a \u8220\'20\'1Cdetectable human heartbeat\u8221\'20\'1D was present (even though that is a misnomer).\par \par \uc2 Cardiac activity can be detected by ultrasound in cells within an embryo that will eventually become the heart as early as six weeks into a pregnancy. That means most abortions in Georgia were effectively banned at a point before many people even knew they were pregnant.\par \par \uc2 McBurney\u8217\'20\'19s ruling came in a lawsuit filed in July by doctors and advocacy groups that sought to strike down the ban on multiple grounds, including that it violates the Georgia constitution\u8217\'20\'19s right to privacy and liberty by forcing pregnancy and childbirth on women in the state. McBurney did not rule on that claim.\par \par \uc2 Instead, his decision agreed with a different argument made in the lawsuit that the ban was invalid because when it was signed into law in 2019, \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  precedent allowed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  well past six weeks.\par \par \uc2 Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s law was passed by state lawmakers and signed by Governor \uc2 Brian Kemp\uc2  in 2019 but had been blocked from taking effect until the supreme court overturned Roe v Wade, which had protected the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the US for nearly 50 years.\par \par \uc2 The 11th US circuit court of appeals allowed Georgia to begin enforcing its \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law just over three weeks after the high court\u8217\'20\'19s decision in June.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics remained open, but providers said they were turning many people away because cardiac activity had been detected. They could then either travel to another state for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  or continue with their pregnancies.\par \par \uc2 In this file photo, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights protesters in Atlanta participate in nationwide demonstrations following the leaked supreme court opinion that the court wanted to overturn Roe v Wade. Photograph: Alyssa Pointer/Reuters\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.27pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , meanwhile, is exulting in the fact that Democrats have kept control of the Senate, and said \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Maga ideology is to blame for the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s struggles in last week\u8217\'20\'19s election:\par \par \uc2 enltrSen. Schumer: "I have a plea for the Republicans and advice: If you embrace MAGA, you're going to keep losing. You're going to lose more." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/IcDLt5a0XI"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/IcDLt5a0XI}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CSPAN (@cspan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cspan/status/1592601570516307969?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 15, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s US politics blog is now being handed over {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/joannawalters"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joanna Walters}}}\uc2 , who will keep you abreast of the rest of today\u8217\'20\'19s news.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.52pm GMT\par \par \uc2 CNN has obtained a letter from \uc2 Rick Scott\uc2  to other Senate Republicans, in which he makes his pitch to be their leader in the chamber:\par \par \uc2 enltrHere\u8217\'20\'19s the letter \uc2 Rick Scott\uc2  sent to his colleagues saying he would challenge \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  for GOP leader {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/BP3rk4UtXz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/BP3rk4UtXz}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Manu Raju (@mkraju) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju/status/1592615531672223744?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 15, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 While he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t attack \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  by name, it\u8217\'20\'19s clear Scott has issues with how the Kentucky senator has led the party. For instance, Scott says that \u8220\'20\'1Csome believe we should not make deals with \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D, in reference to McConnell\u8217\'20\'19s occasion bipartisan agreements with the top Senate Democrat. He also notes that \u8220\'20\'1Csome say we should work to united Republicans and not Democrats\u8221\'20\'1D, another indication that Scott could perhaps take a more hardline approach in negotiating with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s party, should he win the leadership post.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.34pm GMT\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s rancor among Senate Republicans after they failed to win a majority in last week\u8217\'20\'19s midterm elections, with Florida senator \uc2 Rick Scott\uc2  announcing a challenge to \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  to lead the party in Congress\u8217\'20\'19s upper chamber, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/11/15/mcconnell-leadership-challenges-midterms-2022-00066984"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 McConnell is the Senate\u8217\'20\'19s current minority leader and Scott is chair of the National Republican Senatorial Committee, which is in charge of election efforts. The two men have been at odds over the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s poor results in last Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s election, and Politico reports Scott was encouraged to challenge McConnell by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The challenge is the first McConnell has faced in his 15 years leading Senate Republicans, but the Kentucky lawmaker believes he has enough votes to beat Scott, Politico says. McConnell and Trump have a bad relationship, even though the senator has overseen some of the party\u8217\'20\'19s biggest victories in the Senate, including installing the three conservative supreme court justices appointed by the former president who were pivotal in overturning Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.14pm GMT\par \par \uc2 White House asks Congress for $37bn in new Ukraine aid\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration is requesting another big infusion of aid from Congress to help Ukraine weather the Russian invasion, and also to fight Covid-19, NBC News reports:\par \par \uc2 enltrJUST IN: White House seeking $37.7 billion in supplemental aid for Ukraine, for continued military, intelligence support. Also seeks another $10 billion to fund ongoing fight against COVID-19 and other infectious diseases.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ed O'Keefe (@edokeefe) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/edokeefe/status/1592609297028247552?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 15, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Lawmakers have reconvened this week for the first time since the midterm elections, which appear to have delivered control of the House to Republicans. They\u8217\'20\'19re expected to tackle a number of Democatic priorities before Congress\u8217\'20\'19s mandates expires at the end of the year.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.29pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.53pm GMT\par \par \uc2 House Republicans nominate McCarthy for speaker\par \par \uc2 House Republicans have named Kevin McCarthy their candidate for speaker, should they win a majority in the chamber, Punchbowl News reports:\par \par \uc2 enltr?? MCCARTHY WINS\par \par \uc2 Kevin McCarthy of California beat Andy Biggs to become the GOP nominee for speaker of the House.\par \par \uc2 He now has to spend the next seven weeks working to get 218 supporters to win the floor vote. That will be Jan. 3.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jake Sherman (@JakeSherman) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JakeSherman/status/1592596926326784008?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 15, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrMcCarthy won 188-31 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/XQ2MrPAQHc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/XQ2MrPAQHc}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jake Sherman (@JakeSherman) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JakeSherman/status/1592597104454766594?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 15, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 The Californian would take over from Democrat \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  if the GOP gains enough seats to win a majority. While all the ballots from last Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s midterm election have not been counted, the Republicans appear to be on course to do that.\par \par \uc2 McCarthy won despite a challenge from Andy Biggs, an Arizona lawmaker running to his right.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.38pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Arizona Republican Masters concedes in Senate race, Kelly says\par \par \uc2 Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic senator Mark Kelly says his Republican opponent \uc2 Blake Masters\uc2  conceded in a phone call, Politico reports:\par \par \uc2 enltrSen. Mark Kelly says he talked to \uc2 Blake Masters\uc2  today and Masters conceded the Arizona Senate race. Kelly says it was a \u8220\'20\'1Cgood conversation\u8221\'20\'1D and Masters told him \u8220\'20\'1Ccongratulations\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Burgess Everett (@burgessev) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/burgessev/status/1592599434898341890?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 15, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press called the race for Kelly last week. The seat was considered crucial to Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 goal of keeping control of Congress\u8217\'20\'19s upper chamber for another two years.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.20pm GMT\par \par \uc2 If Democrats lose the majority in the House, \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  will have to make a decision.\par \par \uc2 Pelosi has been a fixture in American politics for nearly two decades, becoming the first woman to lead either chamber of Congress and to serve as speaker of the house. But she\u8217\'20\'19s 82, and unless something big happens, the GOP appears to be course to take control of the House once all the ballots from last week\u8217\'20\'19s election are counted.\par \par \uc2 Representing deep-blue San Francisco, it\u8217\'20\'19s unlikely Pelosi will ever lose re-election, but her days controling the chamber appear to be numbered. That leaves her with a number of options. She could stay in the game as House minority leader, a position she previously held from 2011 to 2019, when Democrats were in the minority. She could begin laying the groundwork for her successor, perhaps by announcing her intention to retire.\par \par \uc2 Then there\u8217\'20\'19s a third option, which {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/11/15/us/politics/nancy-pelosi-congress.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the New York Times reports}}}\uc2  in a piece examining the issue Pelosi may be leaning towards:\par \par \uc2 Now the question of will she stay or will she go has given way to a potential third option that some people close to Ms. Pelosi, 82, argue is a serious possibility for her: stepping down from leadership but remaining in Congress in a sort of emeritus role that would allow her to offer counsel to her colleagues and support the agenda of President Biden, 79, whom she has urged to run for re-election in 2024.\par \par \uc2 Such an arrangement would allow Ms. Pelosi to manage her own exit from the political scene while passing the torch to a new generation of leaders that many Democrats have argued for years was long overdue to take over from the three octogenarians currently running the House. She has hinted at just such a possibility.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.33pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.02pm GMT\par \par \uc2 David DePape, who is accused of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/28/paul-pelosi-nancy-pelosi-attack-san-francisco-home"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 attacking Democratic House speaker Nancy Pelosi\u8217\'20\'19s husband, Paul, last month}}}\uc2 , pleaded not guilty to federal charges today, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kron4.com/news/depape-facing-federal-charges-in-pelosi-beating-tuesday/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 KRON reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 He faces a charge of \u8220\'20\'1Cassault on an immediate family member of a United States official with intent to retaliate against the official on account of their performance of official duties\u8221\'20\'1D, which carries a maximum sentence of 30 years in prison and a $250,000 fine.\par \par \uc2 DePape is also charged with \u8220\'20\'1Cone count of attempted kidnapping of a US official\u8221\'20\'1D, for which he faces a maximum sentence of 20 years in prison and a $250,000 fine.\par \par \uc2 DePape previously pleaded not guilty to state charges over the attack in the Pelosis\u8217\'20\'19 San Francisco residence.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.16pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.42pm GMT\par \par \uc2 In a move that won\u8217\'20\'19t surprise those who never believed her to be a true Democrat anyway, the former congresswoman and 2020 presidential hopeful \uc2 Tulsi Gabbard\uc2  has signed up to work as a paid contributor forthe Republican-friendly Fox News network, just weeks after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/11/tulsi-gabbard-quits-democratic-party"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announcing her departure}}}\uc2  from the Democratic party.\par \par \uc2 Fox on Tuesday confirmed Gabbard\u8217\'20\'19s hiring for multiple media outlets after it was first reported on by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.latimes.com/entertainment-arts/business/story/2022-11-14/tulsi-gabbard-signs-as-a-contributor-for-fox-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Los Angeles Times}}}\uc2 . Gabbard, a vocal critic of numerous progressive causes despite her prior political alignment, is scheduled to begin appearing on the network\u8217\'20\'19s programs next week, the reports about her hiring at \uc2 Fox\uc2  added.\par \par \uc2 Tulsi Gabbard\uc2  in November 2022. Photograph: Jeenah Moon/Reuters\par \par \uc2 After winning her \uc2 US House of Representatives\uc2  seat in 2012, Gabbard became the first Samoan-American voting member and Hindu elected to Congress. But her views often clashed with the Democratic party\u8217\'20\'19s. And in 2016, she announced she was leaving the party\u8217\'20\'19s national committee to endorse \uc2 Bernie Sanders\uc2  for president instead of \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 , who of course won the nomination at stake before losing to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and the Republican forces backing him.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Gabbard\u8217\'20\'19s attitudes on foreign policy have often favored authoritarian figures disavowed by the Democrats.\par \par \uc2 On 11 October, she formally resigned from the party and called Democrats an \u8220\'20\'1Celitist cabal of warmongers\u8221\'20\'1D. She later appeared at a campaign rally supporting Republican congressman \uc2 Lee Zeldin\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s unsuccessful run to unseat New York\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic gubernatorial incumbent \uc2 Kathy Hochul\uc2  during the 8 November midterms.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.21pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.18pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The Republican party of Harris county, Texas, which includes the city of Houston, has reportedly filed a lawsuit against local elections administrators over alleged voting issues that occurred on polling day for the 8 November congressional midterms.\par \par \uc2 County Democratic party chairperson Odus Evbagharu has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.harrisdemocrats.org/harris-county-democrats-decry-gov-abbotts-call-election-investigation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 issued a statement}}}\uc2  dismissing the suit as \u8220\'20\'1Cpolitical theater,\u8221\'20\'1D the Houston Chronicle reported Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 According to the Chronicle, the Harris county Republican party\u8217\'20\'19s attorney, Andy Taylor, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/HarrisCountyRP/status/1592278552766185473?s=20&t=9v5Mzi7ycql4t05EQ0UaSg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 alleged}}}\uc2  that double voting may have occurred and provisional ballots weren\u8217\'20\'19t properly segregated when cast after 7pm in accordance with a court order that extended voting hours until 8pm.\par \par \uc2 The Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 gubernatorial incumbent candidate, Greg Abbott, won re-election during the midterms. But ballots cast in Harris county favored Abbott\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic challenger, \uc2 Beto O\u8217\'20\'19Rourke\uc2 , by a margin of about 104,000, before the latest Republican attempt to cast doubt about the integrity of voting in a jurisdiction that did not support their candidate.\par \par \uc2 The Harris county government\u8217\'20\'19s judge \u8211\'20\'13 or top executive \u8211\'20\'13 Lena Hidalgo is a Democrat.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.42pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  may announce {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/nov/15/us-midterm-elections-republicans-house-power-senate-trump-2024?page=with:block-6373a6f18f08d41054ea8508#block-6373a6f18f08d41054ea8508"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 another presidential run tonight}}}\uc2 , but not everybody is happy about it. The former president\u8217\'20\'19s brand {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/nov/15/us-midterm-elections-republicans-house-power-senate-trump-2024?page=with:block-6373a8fa8f08d41054ea8520#block-6373a8fa8f08d41054ea8520"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appears to have suffered}}}\uc2  after his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/nov/15/us-midterm-elections-republicans-house-power-senate-trump-2024?page=with:block-6373ace78f083418445366ca#block-6373ace78f083418445366ca"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 handpicked candidates performed poorly}}}\uc2  in last week\u8217\'20\'19s midterm elections, though {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/nov/15/us-midterm-elections-republicans-house-power-senate-trump-2024?page=with:block-63739d658f08dd2276d83552#block-63739d658f08dd2276d83552"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a poll indicates}}}\uc2  he still remains the most popular person in the Republican party.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has happened today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Liz Cheney{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/nov/15/us-midterm-elections-republicans-house-power-senate-trump-2024?page=with:block-6373b07f8f083418445366f8#block-6373b07f8f083418445366f8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 had the last word}}}\uc2  in a spat with Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s defeated GOP governor candidate Kari Lake, but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/nov/15/us-midterm-elections-republicans-house-power-senate-trump-2024?page=with:block-6373b67d8f0834184453674d#block-6373b67d8f0834184453674d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 warned of}}}\uc2  the continued threat to democracy posed by many Republicans in Congress.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Rupert Murdoch{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/nov/15/us-midterm-elections-republicans-house-power-senate-trump-2024?page=with:block-6373be6d8f08dd2276d8376f#block-6373be6d8f08dd2276d8376f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is reportedly sick of Trump}}}\uc2  and may switch his allegiance to Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , a development that could have big implications for the ex-president\u8217\'20\'19s new White House campaign.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Only a handful of House races{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/nov/15/us-midterm-elections-republicans-house-power-senate-trump-2024?page=with:block-6373c4e78f0834184453683c#block-6373c4e78f0834184453683c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 remain uncalled}}}\uc2 , and the GOP is one seat away from winning control of the chamber. It\u8217\'20\'19s possible one of several races in California could deliver Republicans a majority today, while more results are expected in a crucial Colorado race tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.24pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Back to \uc2 Lauren Boebert\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s race for a moment. While the firebrand conservative Republican appears on track to win another term in the House, it\u8217\'20\'19s going to be a narrow one, and few saw that coming.\par \par \uc2 Her western Colorado district has tended to vote Republican, and analysts viewed a victory by Democrat Adam Frisch as unlikely. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/in-lauren-boeberts-colorado-district-some-voters-grow-tired-of-trump-style-politics-11668434401"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Wall Street Journal went to her district}}}\uc2  to figure out what was behind his unexpectedly stiff challenge. Here\u8217\'20\'19s what they found:\par \par \uc2 Several supporters of Mr. Frisch, including voters registered unaffiliated and Republican, said that Mr. Frisch had won them over with his measured message, and that he has been more present than Ms. Boebert within the district. Some said they were deeply affected by the Jan. 6 attack, in which a mob of Trump supporters disrupted the certification of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/topics/person/joe-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s presidential-election victory.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Frisch said he was fed up with extremism in politics when he began considering a run against Ms. Boebert last fall.\par \par \uc2 The former Aspen city councilman and onetime financial trader sat down and began to crunch numbers on the farthest right and farthest left politicians in the country. He discovered that Ms. Boebert, who won her 2020 race by six points, was the most vulnerable, with\u8212\'20\'14as a point of comparison\u8212\'20\'14a far narrower margin of victory than Rep. \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  (R., Ga.) or Rep. \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2  (D., N.Y.).\par \par \uc2 Mr. Frisch, 55, became convinced that it was possible for someone to build a coalition to beat Ms. Boebert, and his family urged him to get in the race.\par \par \uc2 Political analysts attributed Mr. Frisch\u8217\'20\'19s surprise momentum to Ms. Boebert\u8217\'20\'19s close alignment with Mr. Trump, her reputation for attention-getting statements and a general fatigue within her district of headlines about her. That left an opening for Mr. Frisch and grass-roots groups to cobble together an alliance of Democrats, independents and disaffected Republicans to compete.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf \uc2 Lauren Boebert\uc2  had been an ordinary Republican, this race would not be competitive,\u8221\'20\'1D said Laura Chapin, a Democratic political consultant in Denver.\par \par \uc2 Benjamin Stout, a spokesman for Ms. Boebert, said she outperformed other statewide Republicans within the district and said the majority of Republicans have stuck with her. He pointed to Mr. Frisch\u8217\'20\'19s campaign as a conservative, emphasizing support for business and energy, as proof of support for Republican principles.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe just copped her policies and ran on them,\u8221\'20\'1D Mr. Stout said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.04pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Control of the House is potentially just one race call away from being decided \u8211\'20\'13 assuming the winner is a Republican.\par \par \uc2 The GOP has won 217 of the 218 seats needed to create a majority in Congress\u8217\'20\'19 lower chamber, while Democrats have 205 seats. All it will take is one more victory for Republicans to retake the chamber for the first time since 2019. The question is: where?\par \par \uc2 An obvious choice would be Colorado\u8217\'20\'19s third district, where \uc2 Lauren Boebert\uc2 , one of the chamber\u8217\'20\'19s most controversial lawmakers, is in an unexpectedly stiff battle for re-election against Democrat Adam Frisch. There are only a few ballots left to count in this race, but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cpr.org/2022/11/14/lauren-boebert-adam-frisch-race-update-colorado-3rd-congressional-district/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to Colorado Public Radio}}}\uc2 , don\u8217\'20\'19t expect the outcome to be decided today: the next results won\u8217\'20\'19t be published until Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Based on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2022/11/10/us/elections/results-house-seats-elections-congress.html?partner=slack&smid=sl-share"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 this chart from the New York Times}}}\uc2 , that makes several uncalled races in California the best possibilities for learning today which party controls the House.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.07pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.47pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Nevada Republican Laxalt concedes Senate race\par \par \uc2 Republican \uc2 Adam Laxalt\uc2  has conceded Nevada\u8217\'20\'19s Senate race and acknowledged his loss to Democratic incumbent \uc2 Catherine Cortez Masto\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 enltrI have fought the good fight, I have finished the race, I have kept the faith. (2 Tim 4:7) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/5lUGKKTcRK"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/5lUGKKTcRK}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Adam Paul Laxalt\uc2  (@AdamLaxalt) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AdamLaxalt/status/1592552436694417410?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 15, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Cortez Masto\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s victory in the race guarantees \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s allies control of the Senate for another two years. However, election season isn\u8217\'20\'19t quite over. On 6 December, voters in Georgia will cast ballots in a run-off election to determine whether Democratic incumbent \uc2 Raphael Warnock\uc2  will return to the Senate, or be replaced by Republican \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.49pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.31pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s looming re-election bid has been hit a significant defection after the influential owner of Fox News reportedly told the former president he\u8217\'20\'19s switched allegiances to \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/marksweney"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mark Sweney}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 Rupert Murdoch\uc2  has reportedly warned \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  his media empire will not back any attempt to return to the White House, as former supporters turn to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/15/trump-v-desantis-republicans-divided-2024-presidential-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 youthful Florida governor Ron DeSantis.}}}\par \par \uc2 After the Republican party\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/13/us-midterms-democrats-retain-senate-power-house-undecided"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 disappointing performance in the US midterm elections}}}\uc2 , in particular the poor showing by candidates backed by Trump, Murdoch\u8217\'20\'19s rightwing media empire appears to be seeking a clean break from the former president\u8217\'20\'19s damaged reputation and perceived waning political power.\par \par \uc2 Last week, Murdoch\u8217\'20\'19s influential media empire, including right-leaning Fox News, his flagship paper the Wall Street Journal, and the New York Post, each rounded on Trump, calling him {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/donald-trump-is-the-gops-biggest-loser-midterm-elections-senate-house-congress-republicans-11668034869"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a loser and a flop}}}\uc2  responsible for dragging the Republicans into \u8220\'20\'1Cone political fiasco after another\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/15/murdoch-press-turns-on-donald-trump-in-favour-of-defuture-ron-desantis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Murdoch tells Trump he will not back fresh White House bid \u8211\'20\'13 report}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.32pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.14pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s another tepid endorsement of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  from a Republican senator.\par \par \uc2 This time it\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 John Cornyn\uc2  of Texas, as per NBC News:\par \par \uc2 enltrSenator Cornyn (R-TX) says he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t expect Trump to be the GOP nominee for 2024, but if he is, Cornyn says he\u8217\'20\'19ll support him\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kate Santaliz (@kate_santaliz) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kate_santaliz/status/1592534344249352193?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 15, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.59pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Speaking at a \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  event today, \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  called voters\u8217\'20\'19 rejection of candidates who deny the outcome of the 2020 election in last Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s election a victory for democracy:\par \par \uc2 enltr. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepLizCheney?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @RepLizCheney}}}\uc2  on the midterms: \u8220\'20\'1CWe prevented people from taking office who had said they wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t honor the outcomes of elections... What that really means is that in 2024, the American people will actually get to choose their president.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/PostLive?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #PostLive}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/IJg3Gx7Gfl"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/IJg3Gx7Gfl}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Washington Post Live (@PostLive) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PostLive/status/1592531250677698560?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 15, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 She also accused many of her fellow Republicans in Congress, particularly the party\u8217\'20\'19s leaders, as having their head in the sand when it comes to standing up to Trump:\par \par \uc2 enltr. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepLizCheney?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @RepLizCheney}}}\uc2  tells {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/pkcapitol?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @pkcapitol}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CThere are not enough members who fully recognize that as members of Congress... we can\u8217\'20\'19t be bystanders\u8230\'20\'26 The inclination to try to be a bystander goes to the highest levels of the Republican leadership in the Senate\u8230\'20\'26 in the House it\u8217\'20\'19s worse.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/jI1cKHtVkN"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/jI1cKHtVkN}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Washington Post Live (@PostLive) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PostLive/status/1592536661987991553?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 15, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 This appearance is in some ways an exit interview for Cheney. She lost the Republican primary for her Wyoming House seat in August, and won\u8217\'20\'19t return to Congress next year.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.37pm GMT\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s not just the House where Republicans are performing poorly.\par \par \uc2 Last night, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/14/katie-hobbs-wins-arizona-governor-midterms-democrat"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Associated Press projected}}}\uc2  that Democrat \uc2 Katie Hobbs\uc2  triumphed over Trump-endorsed Republican Kari Lake in Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s governor\u8217\'20\'19s race.\par \par \uc2 It was a moment to savor for \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2 , the conservative Republican House representative and Trump foe who ran television ads encouraging voters in Arizona to reject Lake. Last month, the Arizona Republican released a snarky letter in response to Cheney\u8217\'20\'19s ads \u8211\'20\'13 but on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , Cheney may well have had the last word:\par \par \uc2 enltrYou\u8217\'20\'19re welcome, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KariLake?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @KariLake}}}\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/5jVFIprwxS"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/5jVFIprwxS}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  (@Liz_Cheney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Liz_Cheney/status/1592340964982808576?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 15, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.22pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  endorsed an extensive number of Republicans in House elections, and while ballots are still being counted, it appears that wasn\u8217\'20\'19t always a good thing.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/opinions/2022/11/15/data-trump-weighed-down-republican-candidates/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Writing in the Washington Post,}}}\uc2  Philip Wallach, a resident scholar at the right-leaning \uc2 American Enterprise Institute\uc2 , finds Trump\u8217\'20\'19s chosen Republicans underperformed in competitive House races:\par \par \uc2 enltrIn competitive House districts, Trump-endorsed Rs ran 7 pts worse than unendorsed, relative to expectations. Trumpy candidates cost the GOP much-needed seats, most likely including NC-13, OH-9, OH-13, PA-8, and WA-3. Maybe also MI-3, NH-1. Probably AK. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/EswljxQTBM"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/EswljxQTBM}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Philip Wallach (@PhilipWallach) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PhilipWallach/status/1592527946082029569?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 15, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more of his argument:\par \par \uc2 We can put a number on it by seeing how Trump-supported candidates did relative to those Republicans he did not endorse. If we look at all 401 contests in which a single Democrat faced a single Republican, there is not much difference. Relative to baseline expectations derived from their districts\u8217\'20\'19 recent voting patterns (as calculated by the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cookpolitical.com/cook-pvi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cook Partisan Voting Index}}}\uc2  ), 144 Trump-endorsed candidates exceeded their baselines by an average of 1.52 points. In 257 races where Trump did not endorse a general-election candidate, Republicans exceeded their baseline by 1.46 points.\par \par \uc2 But that similarity is driven mainly by Trump\u8217\'20\'19s endorsements of many Republicans cruising to easy reelection in uncompetitive districts. If we focus exclusively on districts where the margin of victory was less than 15 points, such that the seat was conceivably in the balance, the picture that emerges is quite different.\par \par \uc2 In these 114 districts, candidates bearing Trump endorsements underperformed their baseline by a whopping five points, while Republicans who were without Trump\u8217\'20\'19s blessing overperformed their baseline by 2.2 points \u8212\'20\'14 a remarkable difference of more than seven points.\par \par \uc2 That said, the GOP is still on course to win a majority in the chamber \u8211\'20\'13 just not a particularly big one.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.24pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.07pm GMT\par \par \uc2 At least one Republican senator has already chosen their side in the rivalry between Trump and DeSantis.\par \par \uc2 Yesterday, Wyoming\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Cynthia Lummis\uc2  said she regarded the Florida governor as leader of the Republican party, Politico reports:\par \par \uc2 enltr!!! I asked Sen. Lummis if she will endorse Trump\par \par \uc2 "I don't think that's the right question. I think the question is who is the current leader of the Republican Party. Oh, I know who it is: \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 "\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Burgess Everett (@burgessev) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/burgessev/status/1592293213053894658?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 14, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.52pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/hugo-lowell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hugo Lowell}}}\uc2  has more on the tensions within the Republican party over \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s imminent announcement of a new campaign for the White House:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is expected to announce his 2024 presidential campaign on Tuesday night as planned, according to multiple sources close to the former US president, inserting himself into the center of national politics as he attempts to box out potential rivals seeking the Republican nomination.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump}}}\uc2  will deliver at 9pm ET a speech from the ballroom at his Mar-a-Lago resort, where he recently hosted a subdued midterm elections watch party, and detail several policy goals that aides hope could become central themes of the presidential campaign.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s remarks were being finalized late into the night with a pair of speechwriters and his political team, the sources said, with aides keen for the former president to convey a degree of seriousness as he seeks voters to elevate him to a second term in the White House.\par \par \uc2 The political team at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/mar-a-lago"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mar-a-Lago}}}\uc2  are aware nonetheless that Trump has a penchant for veering off script and delivering news as he pleases, often fixating on grievances over debunked election fraud claims that have historically done him no favors.\par \par \uc2 Still, Trump appears to know that after the disappointing Republican results in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-midterm-elections-2022"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 midterm elections}}}\uc2 , he is perhaps at his most politically vulnerable since the January 6 Capitol attack, and faces a critical moment to ensure he does not get discarded by the rest of the GOP.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/14/trump-presidential-campaign-announcement-mar-a-lago"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump to barrel ahead with campaign reveal despite Republican pushback}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.36pm GMT\par \par \uc2 After years with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  as the undisputed head of their party, many Republicans are grappling with the rise of \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  and whether to switch their support to the Florida governor. \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/chrismcgreal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Chris McGreal}}}\uc2  takes a closer look at their rivalry:\par \par \uc2 Terri Burl was an early member of Women for Trump. As chair of her local Republican party branch in northern Wisconsin, she twice campaigned vigorously for his election in the key swing state. By the time Trump left office, Burl rated him the greatest president since \uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2 . Maybe even better.\par \par \uc2 But now Burl has had enough.\par \par \uc2 She views the prospect of Trump announcing another run for the presidency \u8211\'20\'13 as he is expected to do in Florida on Tuesday evening \u8211\'20\'13 with trepidation. Burl predicts \u8220\'20\'1Ca lot of blood on the floor\u8221\'20\'1D if it comes to a fight with rightwing Florida governor {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ron-desantis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ron DeSantis}}}\uc2  for the Republican nomination, and defeat in the 2024 election if the former US president is the candidate.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/15/trump-v-desantis-republicans-divided-2024-presidential-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump v DeSantis: Republicans split over 2024 run and predict \u8216\'20\'18blood on the floor\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.20pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will at 9pm today make a \u8220\'20\'1Cbig announcement\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 probably of another presidential campaign \u8211\'20\'13 at his Mar-a-Lago resort. If you\u8217\'20\'19re a Republican, it will indeed be big.\par \par \uc2 The former president is at the center of an array of investigations by local and federal authorities and just had a number of his handpicked candidates rejected by voters in the midterms, but a poll released today shows he\u8217\'20\'19s still the most popular man in the GOP.\par \par \uc2 If the primary were held today, 47% of Republicans and independents who lean towards the party would support Trump, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/11/15/donald-trump-president-campaign-00066886"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a Politico/Morning Consult poll}}}\uc2 . Florida\u8217\'20\'19s governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , who won a resounding reelection victory on Tuesday, would get 33% support. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s former vice-president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  would get only 5% support. No other candidates came close.\par \par \uc2 The figures underscore the durability of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s appeal to Republican voters, despite all that has happened since he took over the GOP in 2016 and won the White House later that year. It also cuts into the idea that Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 struggles in Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s vote are a sign of voters souring on his brand.\par \par \uc2 That said, the survey reinforces the belief that voters see DeSantis as an increasingly palatable alternative to Trump. He\u8217\'20\'19s jumped in popularity since the most recent Morning Consult poll, when he was at 26% support. In that survey, Trump was at 48% support, just a point from where he is now.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.29pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.04pm GMT\par \par \uc2 GOP on verge of claiming House majority, Trump set to enter fray\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. As votes were being counted over the past week, Democrats have wondered if their surprising strength among voters could deal them an against-all-odds victory in the House of Representatives. We appear to be nearing the answer to that question: no. While it will surely be smaller than they hoped for, Republicans are closing in on winning a majority in Congress\u8217\'20\'19 lower chamber for the first time since 2019. Their victory could be confirmed in the hours to come. Meanwhile, at 9pm eastern time, former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is scheduled to make an announcement that will likely be the start of a new presidential campaign.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is happening today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  appears to have wrapped up his day at the G20 in Indonesia, which may weigh in on Russia\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The House and Senate are in session, with the House Homeland Security Committee holding a hearing on global terrorism threats featuring \uc2 FBI\uc2  director \uc2 Christopher Wray\uc2  and Homeland Security Secretary Alejandro Mayorkas.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Top Senate Republican \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  will speak to reporters at 10 am eastern time.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.07pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020221115eibf000v9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
