\par\par \uc2 Law\par \b \uc2 Ultra-conservative gala welcomes supreme court justices who ended Roe v Wade\b0\par\par\uc2 Guardian staff and agencies \par \uc2 538 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 November 2022\par 12:13 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Opinion author \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  gets long ovation at anniversary dinner for \uc2 Federalist Society\par \par \uc2 Four of the five \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  justices {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 who overturned}}}\uc2  the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in America showed up at the ultra-conservative \uc2 Federalist Society\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s black-tie dinner marking its 40th anniversary.\par \par \uc2 Justice {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2022/may/06/samuel-alito-profile-abortion-supreme-court-justice"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Samuel Alito}}}\uc2 , who wrote the opinion in the shock decision, got a long, loud ovation at the event on Thursday night from a crowd of 2,000 people, most in tuxedos and gowns, when another speaker praised him on the overturning of Roe v Wade in June.\par \par \uc2 Such a decision was long a target of judicial conservatives and the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement had been undermining rights across many US states for decades after the original Roe decision, in 1973, ushered in the era of federal protection for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 At a moment when opinion surveys show that Americans think the court is becoming more political and give it dismal approval ratings, the justices turned out to celebrate the group that helped \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and Senate Republicans move the American judiciary, including the supreme court, firmly to the right.\par \par \uc2 The Federalist Society\uc2  has no partisan affiliation and takes no position in election campaigns, but it is closely aligned with Republican priorities, including the drive to overturn Roe.\par \par \uc2 Justice {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/amy-coney-barrett"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Amy Coney Barrett}}}\uc2  and Alito offered brief remarks that steered well clear of the court\u8217\'20\'19s work, though Alito praised the \uc2 Federalist Society\uc2  for its success in the Trump years and hoped it would continue. \u8220\'20\'1CBoy, is your work needed today,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Barrett\u8217\'20\'19s only allusion to the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  case came when she responded to the crowd\u8217\'20\'19s roar of approval when she was introduced. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s really nice to have a lot of noise made not by protesters outside my house,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, referring to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/13/us-abortion-protests-pro-choice-marches"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the protests}}}\uc2  in the spring between the time the draft opinion of the court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/02/roe-v-wade-abortion-supreme-court-draft-opinion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was leaked}}}\uc2  and the final decision.\par \par \uc2 Amid heavy security, Justices {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/neil-gorsuch"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Neil Gorsuch}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/brett-kavanaugh"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh}}}\uc2  also were in attendance in the main hall at Washington\u8217\'20\'19s Union Station, where the silhouette of James Madison, the group\u8217\'20\'19s logo, was projected on the walls. Justice {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/clarence-thomas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Clarence Thomas}}}\uc2 , the other member of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  case majority, was not at the dinner.\par \par \uc2 Norm Eisen, an ethics expert who served in the Obama administration and helped draft the articles of impeachment against Trump for his first impeachment in 2019, said the justices had shown a brazen disregard for ethical appearances, because the organization\u8217\'20\'19s mission is to move the law in a conservative direction.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhile there is no legal obstacle to them showing up at the \uc2 Federalist Society\uc2  dinner, the appearances are awful,\u8221\'20\'1D Eisen wrote in an email.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/nov/09/vermont-abortion-vote-first-us-state-constitution"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 were on the ballot}}}\uc2  in referendum questions in a number of states during the midterm elections earlier this week.\par \par \uc2 Chief Justice \uc2 John Roberts\uc2  in June joined neither the opinion nor the dissent of the three liberal-leaning justices in the bombshell Roe decision.\par \par \uc2 After \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  filled the seat left by the death of \uc2 Ruth Bader Ginsburg\uc2  in 2020 with \uc2 Amy Coney Barrett\uc2 , the court achieved a conservative super-majority.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020221114eibe001bi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
