\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Who were the big winners and losers of the US midterm elections?\b0\par\par\uc2 Adam Gabbatt \par \uc2 966 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 November 2022\par 07:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Biden and DeSantis are on the up, but \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and some of the Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 more unhinged candidates flopped\par \par \uc2 After months of campaigning and billions of dollars spent on advertising, the message from America\u8217\'20\'19s midterm elections could essentially be boiled down to: \u8220\'20\'1CNot as bad as Democrats feared.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 There were big wins for Republicans in Florida, and the party still seems likely to take the House, but elsewhere candidates endorsed by former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  flopped, and there were key victories for supporters of reproductive rights.\par \par \uc2 As Trump licks his wounds after being compared to an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/10/rupert-murdoch-trump-desantis-ny-post"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 egg on legs}}}\uc2  by a \uc2 Rupert Murdoch\uc2 -owned newspaper, and as Democrats celebrate avoiding a predicted \u8220\'20\'1Cred wave\u8221\'20\'1D, here\u8217\'20\'19s a look at who did well, and who suffered.\par \par \uc2 WINNERS\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , US president\par \par \uc2 Much of the talk ahead of last Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s elections was about how Biden might tank the Democratic party\u8217\'20\'19s candidates. Republicans across the country ran ads tying their opponents to Biden, banking that the unloved president would turn off voters. It didn\u8217\'20\'19t work, as Democrats performed much better than expected across the board. Biden remains very unpopular \u8211\'20\'13 his approval rating dropped to 39% in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://graphics.reuters.com/USA-BIDEN/POLL/nmopagnqapa/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Reuters poll}}}\uc2  this week \u8211\'20\'13 but that doesn\u8217\'20\'19t seem to be hindering his party. The results prompted Biden, who turns 80 later this month, to repeat his recent assertions that he will {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.usnews.com/news/elections/articles/2022-11-09/confident-biden-says-he-intends-to-run-again"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 run for a second term}}}\uc2  as president in two years\u8217\'20\'19 time.\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , Republican Florida governor\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s not just that the Florida governor {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/09/ron-desantis-trump-2024-florida-midterms"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 won re-election}}}\uc2 , in what is supposed to be a swing state, by almost 20 points. In the process, DeSantis, 44, has also found himself anointed by the rightwing media as the future of the Republican party \u8211\'20\'13 in the case of the New York Post, quite literally: \u8220\'20\'1CDeFuture\u8221\'20\'1D, blasted {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nypost.com/cover/november-9-2022/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the front page of the tabloid}}}\uc2  on Wednesday morning. DeSantis, an anti-immigrant, anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , anti-LGBTQ+ rights Republican, is seen as a more palatable, less hysterical version of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . He has been cagey about whether he will run for president in 2024, but if DeSantis does want to launch a campaign, then this was a pretty good way to start.\par \par \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2 , Democrat\par \par \uc2 Senate candidate\par \par \uc2 Three years ago \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2  was mayor of Braddock, a town of fewer than 2,000 people. On Tuesday he was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/09/john-fetterman-wins-pennsylvania-senate-race"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 elected to the US Senate}}}\uc2 , and will represent 13 million Pennsylvanians. It has been a remarkable rise, made all the more astonishing by the fact Fetterman had a stroke days before the Democratic primary in May. The 6ft 8in, tattooed, permanently hoodie-clad senator-elect is still recovering \u8211\'20\'13 he relied on closed captioning to process questions in a debate in October \u8211\'20\'13 but overcame a stiff challenge from Trump-backed Mehmet Oz to win relatively easily on Tuesday. Fetterman, who has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/johnfetterman/status/1383041283556585475?lang=en"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 previously said}}}\uc2  he owns only one suit, is going to have to do some clothes shopping.\par \par \uc2 Reproductive rights\par \par \uc2 Away from the noise and intrigue about Republican and Democratic candidates and races, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bridgemi.com/michigan-government/michigan-proposal-3-supporting-abortion-rights-wins-big"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Michigan}}}\uc2  voters {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/nov/09/vermont-abortion-vote-first-us-state-constitution"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 approved a ballot measure}}}\uc2  to secure a constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , blocking the imposition of a 1931 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban in the state. In Kentucky, voters rejected a measure which would have denied constitutional protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . North Carolina Republicans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wfae.org/politics/2022-11-09/n-c-republicans-appear-to-fall-one-seat-short-of-supermajorities-in-both-chambers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 failed to secure}}}\uc2  a majority which would have enabled them to ram through restrictive \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans, and it was a similar story in Wisconsin, where the re-elected Democratic governor, \uc2 Tony Evers\uc2 , will have the power to veto \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws proposed by the state legislature.\par \par \uc2 LOSERS\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\par \par \uc2 The one-term, twice-impeached president had a shocker of an evening, as one after another, many of his endorsed candidates {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/US/trump-left-fuming-14-candidates-projected-lose-midterms/story?id=92992662"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 flopped in key races}}}\uc2  across the country. The fact that many of the Republicans Trump had backed lost isn\u8217\'20\'19t the only thing that will sting. Several of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s people underperformed in states \u8211\'20\'13 including New Hampshire and Georgia \u8211\'20\'13 where Republicans who had not been anointed by Trump triumphed. To top it all off, \uc2 Rupert Murdoch{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/10/rupert-murdoch-trump-desantis-ny-post"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 seems to have turned}}}\uc2  on Trump. On Thursday the New York Post, a Murdoch-owned tabloid, mocked up an image of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/nypost/status/1590674429524295680?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw%7Ctwcamp%5Etweetembed%7Ctwterm%5E1590674429524295680%7Ctwgr%5E5028f63cbc6315ded5b44ee514b905c5bfe0307f%7Ctwcon%5Es1_c10&ref_url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.theguardian.com%2Fus-news%2F2022%2Fnov%2F10%2Frupert-murdoch-trump-desantis-ny-post"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump as Humpty Dumpty}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CDon (who couldn\u8217\'20\'19t build a wall) had a great fall \u8211\'20\'13 can all the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s men put the party back together again?\u8221\'20\'1D read the accompanying text.\par \par \uc2 Republicans \u8211\'20\'13 outside Florida and New York\par \par \uc2 With an unpopular Democratic president, soaring inflation, high gas prices and widespread doom and gloom about the economy, this was supposed to be the night that Republicans swept through Congress in a \u8220\'20\'1Cred wave\u8221\'20\'1D. They {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/11/09/2022-election-results-analysis-and-takeaways-00065878"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 didn\u8217\'20\'19t}}}\uc2 . By Friday, with votes still being tallied in some states, the Republican party was still short of a majority in the House and the Senate, as Democrats out-performed expectations across the country. There were some exceptions. In Florida both DeSantis and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2022/11/08/us/elections/results-florida-us-senate.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Marco Rubio}}}\uc2 , the state\u8217\'20\'19s incumbent senator, cruised to victory, and Republicans flourished in state-level races too. It was, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tampabay.com/news/florida-politics/elections/2022/11/10/midterms-desantis-rubio-republican/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tampa Bay Times}}}\uc2  declared, \u8220\'20\'1Can electoral catastrophe for Democrats\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 (Some of) the unhinged candidates\par \par \uc2 In Pennsylvania \uc2 Doug Mastriano\uc2 , a Christian nationalist state senator who paid for buses to take people to what became the January 6 insurrection and tried to overturn the results of the 2020 election, was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/09/josh-shapiro-wins-election-pennsylvania-governor-democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 swept away}}}\uc2  in the governor\u8217\'20\'19s race. Matthew DePerno, a fellow election conspiracy theorist who had branded Democrats \u8220\'20\'1Cradical, cultural Marxists\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.freep.com/story/news/politics/elections/2022/11/09/dana-nessel-matthew-deperno-michigan-attorney-general-race/69625622007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lost his bid}}}\uc2  to be Michigan\u8217\'20\'19s attorney general, and his ideological counterpart Kristina Karamo {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/world/us/election-denier-michigan-loses-bid-run-2024-vote-state-2022-11-09/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 failed}}}\uc2  to become secretary of state. Tina Forte, a Republican who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cityandstateny.com/politics/2022/11/aoc-and-jan-6-insurrectionist-doesnt-have-chance-beating-her/379237/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 attended}}}\uc2  the January 6 rally and has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.snopes.com/news/2021/08/25/tina-forte-capitol-riot/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dabbled}}}\uc2  in QAnon conspiracy theories, was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://kmph.com/news/connect-to-congress/aoc-wins-reelection-to-new-york-14th-congressional-district-midterms-2022-nov-8-alexandria-ocasio-cortez"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 crushed}}}\uc2  in her attempt to defeat \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2 , the Democratic congresswoman, in New York.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020221113eibd000e2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
