\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 US midterm elections 2022: focus on Nevada after Democrat Mark Kelly wins key Senate seat \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Richard Luscombe \par \uc2 4,291 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 November 2022\par 21:37 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Balance in Senate chamber remains at 49-49, with eyes on race between Democrat \uc2 Catherine Cortez Masto\uc2  and Adam LaxaltUS midterm elections results 2022 \u8211\'20\'13 liveSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.06pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re closing our live midterm elections blog now, but look out for our news reports later for developments in Senate, House and governor\u8217\'20\'19s races in which winners have yet to be projected.\par \par \uc2 Democrats need to win only one of the two remaining Senate races, in Nevada and Georgia, to retain control of the chamber for two more years. Each party currently has 49 seats.\par \par \uc2 Republicans are narrowing in on victory in the House of Representatives, having won 211 of the 218 seats they need for a majority.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what we followed today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Republican who must win his Senate challenge in Nevada if his party is to have a chance of controlling the chamber said his path to victory was \u8220\'20\'1Cnarrowing\u8221\'20\'1D. \uc2 Adam Laxalt\uc2 , ahead by just 862 votes, conceded drop-off ballots still being tallied favored Democratic incumbent \uc2 Catherine Cortez Masto\uc2  at a greater rate than he expected.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Mark Kelly, whose win over \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  -endorsed Blake Masters in Arizona put {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats}}}\uc2  on the brink of retaining Senate control, criticized election deniers and praised Republican predecessor \uc2 John McCain\uc2  in a victory speech in Phoenix.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The atmosphere grew tense outside the Maricopa county elections office in Phoenix, where several dozen rightwing protestors hurled abuse at sheriff\u8217\'20\'19s deputies. Extremist Republican Kari Lake, an election denier, narrowly trails Democrat \uc2 Katie Hobbs\uc2  in the race for Arizona governor.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Police say no powder was found in \u8220\'20\'1Csuspicious\u8221\'20\'1D envelopes sent to Lake\u8217\'20\'19s campaign headquarters last week. The candidate had closed her office and claimed what it described as an attack was politically motivated.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The race for Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s Senate seat, which will be decided in a 6 December runoff between Democratic incumbent \uc2 Raphael Warnock\uc2  and challenger \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2 , will see Pac-funded negative attack ads questioning the Republican\u8217\'20\'19s character, CNN reports.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.36pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.45pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press, whose projections the \uc2 Guardian\uc2  uses to call election results, is explaining why it declared Mark Kelly the winner in the Senate race on Friday, but has not yet done so in the contest for governor.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAt around 10pm ET on Friday, officials in Maricopa released another batch of 75,000 votes, a tranche that provided enough information for AP to determine that Democratic Senator Kelly had won reelection against Republican Blake Masters, \u8221\'20\'1D the agency says.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut there still was not enough for AP to call a winner in the governor\u8217\'20\'19s race. The batch favored Hobbs over Lake by less than 10 percentage points.\par \par \uc2 Katie Hobbs\uc2 . Photograph: Jim Urquhart/Reuters\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAfter Friday\u8217\'20\'19s vote release, the margin in the governor\u8217\'20\'19s race [between Republican Kari Lake and Democrat \uc2 Katie Hobbs\uc2  ] sat at just over 31,000 votes, with Lake about a point and a half behind.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In all of Arizona, the AP says, officials report some 400,000 ballots left to count, including up to 275,000 in Maricopa county, meaning there are simply too many left untallied to be sure which way the race will go.\par \par \uc2 The picture could become clearer around 10pm ET Saturday, when officials in Maricopa county say they will release another batch of votes.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.07pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.03pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Tense atmosphere as protesters target Arizona elections office\par \par \uc2 Protestors have been gathering outside the Maricopa county elections office in Phoenix, Arizona, and hurling abuse at sheriff\u8217\'20\'19s deputies, according to reports.\par \par \uc2 CNN\u8217\'20\'19s Kyung Lah says \u8220\'20\'1Ca few dozen\u8221\'20\'1D demonstrators waving stars and stripes flags are calling the officers \u8220\'20\'1Cevil traitors\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Workers at the office, where \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  supporters protested non-existent election fraud after his 2020 defeat, are still counting ballots from Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s midterm vote. The winner is still unclear in a highly contentious governor\u8217\'20\'19s race between the extremist rightwing Republican {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/03/kari-lake-trump-arizona-maga-republicanism-midterms"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kari Lake}}}\uc2  and her Democratic opponent, \uc2 Katie Hobbs\uc2 , who holds a narrow lead.\par \par \uc2 Lake, an election denier, has been accused of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.msnbc.com/msnbc/watch/kari-lake-leans-into-bogus-fraud-claims-in-arizona-risks-stoking-extremist-violence-153120837941"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 potentially stoking violence}}}\uc2  by leaning into debunked conspiracy theories of election malfeasance.\par \par \uc2 County officials have thanked law enforcement for keeping the elections office secure. Workers \u8220\'20\'1Chave families and roommates and pets to go home to at the end of the night\u8221\'20\'1D, they said in a tweet.\par \par \uc2 enltrThank you {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mcsoaz?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @mcsoaz}}}\uc2  deputies. We respect protesters' 1st Amendment rights & hope they demonstrate peacefully and with consideration for the people involved in administering {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MaricopaVote?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @maricopavote}}}\uc2  elections who have families and roommates and pets to go home to at the end of the night. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/IV2pKmy6c4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/IV2pKmy6c4}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Maricopa County (@maricopacounty) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/maricopacounty/status/1591515770462560257?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 12, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Earlier today, the Democrat Mark Kelly, who is projected to retain his Senate seat, berated election deniers in a victory speech in Phoenix.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve seen the consequences that come when leaders refuse to accept the truth and focus more on conspiracies of the past than solving the challenges that we face today,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Kelly\u8217\'20\'19s beaten Republican challenger, Blake Masters, has not yet conceded the race.\par \par \uc2 He posted a tweet saying: \u8220\'20\'1CIf, at the end, Senator Kelly has more [votes] than I do, then I will congratulate him on a hard-fought victory.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 zxxltr {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/XVbq4WU4nj"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/XVbq4WU4nj}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Blake Masters (@bgmasters) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/bgmasters/status/1591475417646596109?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 12, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.14pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.29pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Buoyant Montana Republicans eye 2024 Senate upset\par \par \uc2 Republicans are emboldened by a string of electoral victories in Montana and are turning their attention to seizing the Senate seat held by three-term Democrat Jon Tester in 2024, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 A potentially bruising primary battle is possible between two Republicans who won US House seats Tuesday, former interior secretary \uc2 Ryan Zinke\uc2  and representative \uc2 Matt Rosendale\uc2 , the agency says.\par \par \uc2 Ryan Zinke\uc2 . Photograph: Thom Bridge/AP\par \par \uc2 Zinke, 61, said he considers Tester vulnerable, and he will make a decision on whether to seek the Senate seat next year.\par \par \uc2 Rosendale, 62, said Tester doesn\u8217\'20\'19t represent Montana\u8217\'20\'19s interests and should be replaced, but he declined to answer when asked if he will run.\par \par \uc2 Tester is expected to be among the most vulnerable Democrats in the Senate in the next election cycle, along with fellow moderates \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2  of West Virginia and \uc2 Kyrsten Sinema\uc2  of Arizona.\par \par \uc2 Voters in Montana and West Virginia have increasingly trended Republican, while Arizona has become a key swing state targeted by both parties.\par \par \uc2 Tester, 66, said it is not certain he will seek a fourth term. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m going to make this decision based on my effectiveness and my family,\u8221\'20\'1D he said Friday.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.59pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  called three Democratic midterm winners on Saturday to offer congratulations, CNN reports.\par \par \uc2 The president phoned Maryland congressman \uc2 David Trone\uc2 , representative Pat Ryan from New York, and the newly re-elected Arizona senator Mark Kelly, the network said.\par \par \uc2 Biden \u8220\'20\'1Cmade a congratulatory call to congressman \uc2 David Trone\uc2  from Phnom Penh, Cambodia at 11.39pm local time\u8221\'20\'1D, the White House said.\par \par \uc2 Biden is in Cambodia at the Association of South-east Asian Nations summit, after attending the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2022/nov/11/cop27-joe-biden-climate-crisis-us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cop27 climate conference}}}\uc2  in Egypt on Friday.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.16pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.38pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Interim summary\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where things stand midway through a potentially decisive day for control of the Senate, as counting continues in the midterm elections:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Republican who must win his Senate challenge in Nevada if his party is to seize control of the chamber is admitting his path to victory is \u8220\'20\'1Cnarrowing\u8221\'20\'1D. \uc2 Adam Laxalt\uc2 , who leads by just 862 votes, says mail-in ballots are favoring Democratic incumbent \uc2 Catherine Cortez Masto\uc2  at a greater rate than he expected.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Mark Kelly, whose win over \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  -endorsed Blake Masters in Arizona put Democrats on the brink of retaining Senate control, criticized election deniers and praised Republican predecessor \uc2 John McCain\uc2  in a morning victory speech in Phoenix.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The race for Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s Senate seat, which will be decided in a 6 December runoff between Democratic incumbent \uc2 Raphael Warnock\uc2  and challenger \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2 , will see Pac-funded negative attack ads questioning the Republican\u8217\'20\'19s character, CNN reports.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Police in Phoenix say no powder was found in \u8220\'20\'1Csuspicious\u8221\'20\'1D envelopes sent to the headquarters of extremist Republican governor candidate Kari Lake \u8217\'20\'19s campaign last week. Lake continues to trail Democrat \uc2 Katie Hobbs\uc2  by a narrow margin.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.43pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.19pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Laxalt: Window for Nevada victory 'has narrowed'\par \par \uc2 Adam Laxalt\uc2 , who must win his Senate challenge to \uc2 Catherine Cortez Masto\uc2  in Nevada if Republicans are to have any chance of retaking control of the chamber, is acknowledging that the race could be slipping away.\par \par \uc2 In a Saturday {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AdamLaxalt/status/1591457041977311232"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  tweet}}}\uc2 , Laxalt says early ballots dropped off on election day, and currently being tallied, and which have narrowed his lead to 862 votes, are breaking for his Democratic opponent at a greater rate than he expected.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis has narrowed our victory window,\u8221\'20\'1D he wrote on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In the 2020 presidential election, ballots counted after election day largely favored Democrats.\par \par \uc2 Laxalt said the result depended on where the outstanding votes are coming from. \u8220\'20\'1CIf they are GOP precincts or slightly DEM leaning then we can still win. If they continue to trend heavy DEM then she will overtake us,\u8221\'20\'1D he wrote.\par \par \uc2 enltrHere is where we are \u8212\'20\'14 we are up only 862 votes. Multiple days in a row, the mostly mail in ballots counted continue to break in higher DEM margins than we calculated. This has narrowed our victory window. The race will come down to 20-30K Election Day Clark drop off ballots.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Adam Paul Laxalt\uc2  (@AdamLaxalt) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AdamLaxalt/status/1591457041977311232?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 12, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Earlier, the Republican candidate appeared more confident, stating in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AdamLaxalt/status/1591202411523153920"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Friday night tweet}}}\uc2  that he expected \u8220\'20\'1Cher percentages to continue to remain under what she needs\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 There is no indication yet when the race might be called, but today is the last day for Nevada mail-in ballots to arrive and be counted, as long as they were postmarked by the 8 November election day.\par \par \uc2 A Cortez Masto victory would retain Democratic control of the Senate for another two years, and lessen the importance of 6 December runoff between Democrat \uc2 Raphael Warnock\uc2  and Republican \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  in Georgia.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.49pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.48pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Kelly praises McCain in Arizona victory speech\par \par \uc2 Mark Kelly, whose {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/11/democrat-mark-kelly-arizona-senate-blake-masters"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 win in his Senate race in Arizona}}}\uc2  moved Democrats to within one seat of retaining control of the chamber, has slammed election deniers and praised his late predecessor, Republican \uc2 John McCain\uc2 , in a victory speech in Phoenix.\par \par \uc2 Kelly was speaking to jubilant supporters on Saturday morning, with his wife \uc2 Gabby Giffords\uc2 , a former Democratic congresswoman who was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/2022/jul/13/gabby-giffords-wont-back-down-documentary"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shot and badly injured}}}\uc2  in an attempted assassination 11 years ago, at his side.\par \par \uc2 Senator Mark Kelly. Photograph: Patrick T Fallon/AFP/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 Kelly also praised election workers, Republican and Democrat, who he said had done the \u8220\'20\'1Cimportant work of making sure Arizonans\u8217\'20\'19 voices are heard\u8221\'20\'1D:\par \par \uc2 After a long election it can be tempting to remain focused on the things that divide us, but we\u8217\'20\'19ve seen the consequences that come when leaders refuse to accept the truth and focus more on conspiracies of the past than solving the challenges that we face today.\par \par \uc2 And for the past two years, as we face these challenges, not a day has gone by where I have not remembered that I am sitting in the Senate seat [of] Senator \uc2 John McCain\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Senator McCain embodied everything that was to be a leader at a time when our state and our country remain divided. His legacy of building bridges and focusing on Arizona is an example of what we all should do and what we should look to.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.21pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.34pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The run-off for Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s Senate seat between incumbent Democrat \uc2 Raphael Warnock\uc2  and his Republican challenger \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  is about turn nasty, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/11/12/politics/georgia-runoff-ad-spending/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Attack advertising against the Walker campaign is set to launch Saturday, the network says, funded by a Democratic super political action committee (super Pac) that seeks to secure a victory for Warnock in the 6 December election.\par \par \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2 . Photograph: John Bazemore/AP\par \par \uc2 The ad, titled Shown Us and made by Georgia Honor, a group tied to the Senate Majority Pac, questions the character of Walker, a former football player. Walker\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2022/oct/27/herschel-walker-worst-candidate-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 troubled general election campaign}}}\uc2  saw him fending off domestic violence accusations and reports he had paid for abortions.\par \par \uc2 Walker is, the ad claims, according to CNN, \u8220\'20\'1Ca liar who has a \u8216\'20\'18long record of violence toward women\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 A narrator says: \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  has shown us who he is. \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  is unfit for office.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, a video of Walker calling America \u8220\'20\'1Cthe greatest country in the US\u8221\'20\'1D at a rally on Thursday has gone viral, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newsweek.com/video-herschel-walker-georgia-senate-greatest-country-us-viral-1759085"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Newsweek reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The gaffe has amassed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/patriottakes/status/1591228042617446401"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 half a million views on Twitter}}}\uc2 , the outlet says.\par \par \uc2 Warnock, a Black pastor who unseated the Republican Kelly Loeffler last year in a run-off following the 2020 election, leads his challenger in this year\u8217\'20\'19s race. But with neither candidate achieving 50% of the vote, a runoff is necessary under Georgia law.\par \par \uc2 Depending on the result in the only other outstanding Senate race in Nevada, the December result could determine who controls the chamber for the next two years.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.51pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.47pm GMT\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re still waiting for updates on Nevada\u8217\'20\'19s pivotal senate race, but we do know that Republican \uc2 Joe Lombardo\uc2 , a Trump-backed sheriff, will occupy the governor\u8217\'20\'19s mansion.\par \par \uc2 Lombardo\u8217\'20\'19s contest with incumbent \uc2 Steve Sisolak\uc2  was called by the Associated Press late on Friday, restoring his party to state governorship after a single term of office for the beaten Democrat.\par \par \uc2 Joe Lombardo\uc2 . Photograph: Caroline Brehman/\uc2 EPA\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt appears we will fall a percentage point or so short of winning,\u8221\'20\'1D Sisolak said in a statement conceding the race to Lombardo shortly after a batch of vote results was reported in Clark county on Friday night.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat is why I reached out to the sheriff to wish him success.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The count of ballots in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/nevada"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nevada}}}\uc2  took several days partly due to a provision of a broad mail voting law passed by the state legislature in 2020. It requires counties to accept ballots postmarked by election day if they arrive up to four days later.\par \par \uc2 Counting in the close Senate race between Democrat \uc2 Catherine Cortez Masto\uc2  and her Republican challenger \uc2 Adam Laxalt\uc2  continues.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/11/joe-lombardo-wins-nevada-governor-race"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Lombardo, Trump-backed Republican sheriff, wins Nevada governor race }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.40pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.06pm GMT\par \par \uc2 From deep dives into voter demographics and algorithms predicting results, to analysis of mail-in versus in-person balloting, there is no disputing the rise of the importance of data in any modern election cycle.\par \par \uc2 In an impressive study of critical information for the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2 , reporter {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/people/maria-luisa-paul/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mar\u237\'00\'EDa Luisa Pa\u250\'00\'FAl}}}\uc2  has found that 10% of the new \uc2 US Senate\uc2  from January will be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/nation/2022/11/11/john-jon-senate-midterms-percent/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 men named John or Jon}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Democrat \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2 , senator-elect for Pennsylvania, will be among the most prominent after flipping the previously Republican-held seat with his victory over Mehmet Oz.\par \par \uc2 There will be 10 of them in the chamber for the 118th Congress, with or without the \u8220\'20\'1Ch\u8221\'20\'1D, Pa\u250\'00\'FAl says.\par \par \uc2 enltrJohns and Jons are about to make up 10 percent of the \uc2 U.S. Senate{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/hWAhRYvIlQ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/hWAhRYvIlQ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  (@washingtonpost) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/washingtonpost/status/1591381439198957569?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 12, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Four are Democrats: Fetterman, John Hickenlooper (Colorado), \uc2 Jon Ossoff\uc2  (Georgia) and Jon Tester (Montana).\par \par \uc2 The other six are Republicans: \uc2 John Barrasso\uc2  (Wyoming), \uc2 John Boozman\uc2  (Arkansas), \uc2 John Cornyn\uc2  (Texas), John Hoeven (North Dakota), \uc2 John Kennedy\uc2  (Louisiana) and \uc2 John Thune\uc2  (South Dakota).\par \par \uc2 The name\u8217\'20\'19s popularity in politics doesn\u8217\'20\'19t extend just to the Senate, the Post notes. Four of the 46 US presidents to date were named John: \uc2 John Adams\uc2 , \uc2 John Quincy Adams\uc2 , John Tyler, and John Fitzgerald Kennedy.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.41pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.31pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The day before your daughter\u8217\'20\'19s wedding would usually be a time to check on last minute arrangements. Have the flowers arrived? Is my suit pressed? Is my father of the bride speech ready?\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , however, was mostly busy elsewhere on Friday, the eve of Saturday\u8217\'20\'19s wedding of his youngest daughter \uc2 Tiffany Trump\uc2  to Michael Boulos at the family\u8217\'20\'19s Mar-a-Lago resort in Florida.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  at Mar-a-Lago with his daughter Tiffany and her fiance Michael Boulos on Friday, the day before their wedding. Photograph: MEGA/GC Images\par \par \uc2 As the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/hugo-lowell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hugo Lowell}}}\uc2  reports, as well as continuing to fire off {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/11/trump-ron-desantis-glenn-youngkin-republicans-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 furious social media messages}}}\uc2  following the Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 disappointing performance in the midterms, Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/11/trump-lawsuit-capitol-attack-committee-subpoena"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filed a lawsuit}}}\uc2  seeking to block the House January 6 select committee\u8217\'20\'19s subpoena demanding testimony in the investigation into Capitol attack.\par \par \uc2 The suit appears to reflect an attempt by the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 former president}}}\uc2  to delay compliance with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/21/trump-subpoena-testify-jan-6-committee"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the sprawling subpoena}}}\uc2 , in an effort that could culminate in a constitutional showdown with the House of Representatives before the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFormer President Trump turns to the courts to preserve his rights and Executive Branch independence consistently upheld by the courts and endorsed by the Department of Justice,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump\u8217\'20\'19s attorneys wrote in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://storage.courtlistener.com/recap/gov.uscourts.flsd.623513/gov.uscourts.flsd.623513.1.0_1.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 41-page submission}}}\uc2  filed in federal court in West Palm Beach, Florida.\par \par \uc2 Read the full story:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/11/trump-lawsuit-capitol-attack-committee-subpoena"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump files lawsuit to block House Capitol attack panel\u8217\'20\'19s subpoena}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.53pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.07pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Police: no powder in Lake campaign HQ envelope\par \par \uc2 Police say there was no powder in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/06/kari-lake-envelope-white-powder-office-closed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Csuspicious\u8221\'20\'1D envelope opened earlier this week }}}\uc2  at the campaign headquarters of Kari Lake, the Republican candidate for governor of Arizona.\par \par \uc2 Phoenix police spokesperson Donna Rossi said that \u8220\'20\'1Cthe state lab tested the items turned over to them,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.azcentral.com/story/news/local/arizona/2022/11/11/no-powder-found-envelope-taken-kari-lakes-campaign-office/10674690002/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Arizona Republic reported}}}\uc2 . The lab \u8220\'20\'1Cdetermined there was no substance inside.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Kari Lake. Photograph: \u201\'00\'C9tienne Laurent/\uc2 EPA\par \par \uc2 Phoenix police and fire officials said they were called to the building around 2am Sunday, on a report of an envelope containing suspicious white powder. Lake closed the office temporarily.\par \par \uc2 Police said at the time there were no reports of injuries or illness, though Lake\u8217\'20\'19s campaign had said the staff member who opened the envelope was under medical supervision, the Associated Press reported.\par \par \uc2 Democrat \uc2 Katie Hobbs\uc2  held a narrow lead over Lake, a \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  acolyte and election denier, as counting continued in the key battleground state on Saturday morning.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.24pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.50pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s June decision to strip federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights was a key election issue for many midterm voters. My colleague {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/lauren-gambino"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lauren Gambino}}}\uc2  looks at how it held back a Republican \u8220\'20\'1Cred wave\u8221\'20\'1D:\par \par \uc2 This summer, after a tectonic decision by the supreme court to overturn Roe v Wade eliminated the nearly 50-year constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  predicted American women would revolt. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans}}}\uc2 , however, saw a \u8220\'20\'1Cred wave\u8221\'20\'1D brewing, fueled by widespread economic discontent.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats}}}\uc2  defied historical expectations in the first major election of the post-Roe era, Biden effectively declared: \u8220\'20\'1CI told ya so.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWomen in America made their voices heard, man,\u8221\'20\'1D the president told a crowd of supporters at the Howard Theater in Washington on Thursday. \u8220\'20\'1CY\u8217\'20\'19all showed up and beat the hell out of them.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The 2022 midterm elections were expected to usher in staggering losses for Democrats. The party in power typically fares poorly, and with Biden\u8217\'20\'19s approval ratings mired in the low 40s, Republicans were expected to make significant gains.\par \par \uc2 That is not how the results unfolded. As the vote count continues in several key races, Republicans appear on track to win a far narrower House majority than they hoped, while Democrats may retain control of the Senate.\par \par \uc2 As a fuller portrait of the results emerges, advocates, Democrats and even some Republicans say one thing is clear: \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  proved a defining issue. Fury over the loss of federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections galvanized women and young people and delivered a string of unexpected victories for Democrats and new protections for reproductive rights.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou cannot have half of the population have their body autonomy put under threat and not expect it to be mobilizing,\u8221\'20\'1D said Heidi Sieck, the CEO and co-founder of #VoteProChoice. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd that\u8217\'20\'19s what we saw across the board with young people showing up, women showing up, newly registered women being more than two-thirds of the newly registered voters.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Exit polls conducted for news networks by Edison Research showed that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was the top issue for many Americans, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/Politics/abc-news-2022-exit-poll-analysis-night-trenches/story?id=92970521"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 especially young people}}}\uc2  under the age of 30. And about 60% of voters said they were dissatisfied or angry with the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision to overturn Roe, according to exit polls conducted by AP Votecast.\par \par \uc2 Read the full story:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/11/abortion-midterm-elections-republicans-women-voters"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 How the fall of Roe shattered Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 midterm dreams}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.55pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.27pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Ever heard a tale about a reality television star deciding to change career, mounting an unexpected run for political office, then winning?\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s happened again in Kentucky, where Republican Nick Wilson, a former champion of the Survivor game show, will sit in the state\u8217\'20\'19s House of Representatives after being elected unopposed in his district.\par \par \uc2 In parallels (kind of) to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s political career, Wilson, 32, banked $1m as the champion of Survivor\u8217\'20\'19s David v Goliath edition in 2018, outlasting a large field of fellow contestants, but wasn\u8217\'20\'19t so successful in his second attempt on a reunion show in 2020, when he was unceremoniously voted out by his tribe.\par \par \uc2 Wilson, a former assistant commonwealth attorney for Whitley county, replaces retiring Republican Regina Huff, who endorsed him.\par \par \uc2 enltrThe tribe has spoken and past "Survivor" winner Nick Wilson is in the house... Kentucky's House of Representatives, that is!!! {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/n1TnkDNyZw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/n1TnkDNyZw}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 TMZ (@TMZ) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TMZ/status/1591106789042438151?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 11, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.04pm GMT\par \par \uc2 While we were largely focused on the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/11/democrat-mark-kelly-arizona-senate-blake-masters"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US Senate race in Arizona}}}\uc2 , other contests in the state have also been closely watched.\par \par \uc2 As my colleague {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/12/arizona-secretary-of-state-election-winnner-adrian-fontes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ed Pilkington}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/12/arizona-secretary-of-state-election-winnner-adrian-fontes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  writes}}}\uc2 , the victory of \uc2 Adrian Fontes\uc2 , the Democratic candidate for secretary of state, may come to be seen as one of the most significant results of the 2022 elections in terms of the future of American democracy.\par \par \uc2 Adrian Fontes\uc2 . Photograph: Jim Urquhart/Reuters\par \par \uc2 Fontes beat Mark Finchem, a rabid election denier and member of the far-right Oath Keepers militia who was present at the US Capitol on the day of the 6 January 2021 insurrection.\par \par \uc2 Finchem has made repeated efforts to overturn \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s win in Arizona in the 2020 election, in favor of his idol \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 By frustrating Finchem\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to secure the secretary of state position, Fontes, a former Marine, has prevented both local and federal election administration in Arizona falling into the hands of an avid opponent of democratic norms.\par \par \uc2 zxxltr {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/VjYqFb7NVV"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/VjYqFb7NVV}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Adrian Fontes\uc2  (@Adrian_Fontes) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Adrian_Fontes/status/1591308646520344577?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 12, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Had Finchem come out on top, as some polls suggested he might in the final stretch of the campaign, he would have been placed to radically alter Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s handling of elections and could even have subverted the outcome of the 2024 presidential battle.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI promise always to honor and defend the ideal of fair and honest elections with the voters of Arizona and I will help reignite the flame of unity in our Republic,\u8221\'20\'1D Fontes {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Adrian_Fontes/status/1591308646520344577"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tweeted}}}\uc2  after his victory was confirmed last night.\par \par \uc2 Read the full story:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/12/arizona-secretary-of-state-election-winnner-adrian-fontes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Adrian Fontes wins highly contested secretary of state in Arizona}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.54pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Good morning US politics blog readers, and welcome to a rare weekend edition covering the ongoing midterm election!\par \par \uc2 It could be a decisive day for control of the \uc2 US Senate\uc2 , where the results in only two states \u8211\'20\'13 Nevada and Georgia \u8211\'20\'13 are still outstanding, and the balance of power in the chamber remains delicately poised at 49-49.\par \par \uc2 With the race in Georgia heading to a 6 December runoff, and Democrat Mark Kelly having been declared the victor in Arizona late on Friday, that leaves all eyes on the pivotal Nevada nailbiter between the incumbent Democrat, \uc2 Catherine Cortez Masto\uc2 , and her Republican challenger, \uc2 Adam Laxalt\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Even if we don\u8217\'20\'19t get a result today, we are expecting to see more votes tallied in a race Laxalt led by a mere 862 at breakfast time from almost a million counted.\par \par \uc2 A Cortez Masto victory would keep the Senate in Democrat hands for the next two years, as the party would have the tie-breaking vote of vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . Republicans must win both Nevada and Georgia to wrest control.\par \par \uc2 Counting also continues in various races for the House of Representatives, where Republicans are closing on a narrower victory than expected.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll bring you all the developments as they come in through the day. While we wait, here\u8217\'20\'19s a primer on the state of play in Nevada and elsewhere:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/11/nothing-final-in-house-or-senate-as-us-midterm-elections-count-continues"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 All eyes on Nevada as Senate control hangs in balance}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020221112eibc000uo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
