\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 US midterms 2022: Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 Senate hopes grow as vote count edges forward \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Sam Levin in Los Angeles (now) and Chris Stein in Washington (earlier) \par \uc2 7,929 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 November 2022\par 01:59 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Democrat Mark Kelly appears close to re-election in Arizona, with Nevada still up in the air and Georgia going to a runoff voteUS midterm elections results 2022 \u8211\'20\'13 liveSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.27am GMT\par \par \uc2 Summary\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s all the live coverage for today. Here are some key developments and links from the day:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 All eyes remain on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/11/nothing-final-in-house-or-senate-as-us-midterm-elections-count-continues"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Arizona and Nevada}}}\uc2 , where hundreds of thousands of uncounted votes held the key to control of the \uc2 US Senate\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s top political staffers at Mar-a-Lago are pressing him to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/10/trump-inner-circle-rift-2024-presidential-campaign-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 move forward with his planned 2024 presidential campaign announcement}}}\uc2  next week but a chorus of allies are suggesting delaying until after the Senate runoff in Georgia in December, according to sources familiar with the matter.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/11/trump-ron-desantis-glenn-youngkin-republicans-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lashed out at other high-profile Republicans}}}\uc2  after the failure of the predicted \u8220\'20\'1Cred wave\u8221\'20\'1D in the US midterm elections, which has chilled enthusiasm for his promotion of extremist candidates and a possible new run at the White House.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has implored countries to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2022/nov/11/cop27-joe-biden-climate-crisis-us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 do more to tackle the climate emergency}}}\uc2 , telling the Cop27 summit that world leaders \u8220\'20\'1Ccan no longer plead ignorance\u8221\'20\'1D and that time to confront the crisis is running out.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Some Republican senators have called for a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/nov/11/us-midterm-election-2022-senate-house-results-congress-democrats-republicans-politics-live-updates-latest?page=with:block-636ec7d28f08786f8dfad1e5#block-636ec7d28f08786f8dfad1e5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 delay in the party\u8217\'20\'19s leadership elections}}}\uc2  scheduled to take place next week.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/11/young-voters-us-midterms-democratic-youth"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 youth vote was the highest in almost three decades}}}\uc2 , defying conventional wisdom about 18-29 demographic.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.42am GMT\par \par \uc2 In the closely watched mayor\u8217\'20\'19s race in Los Angeles, Democratic congresswoman \uc2 Karen Bass\uc2  has pulled slightly ahead with the latest batch of votes counted:\par \par \uc2 enltr??Karen Bass has taken the LEAD in the mayoral race in Los Angeles.\par \par \uc2 She now leads Caruso 50.4% to 49.6%.\par \par \uc2 (Expect her lead to continue to grow quite a bit.)\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Taniel (@Taniel) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Taniel/status/1591224963851132929?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 12, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Bass had been trailing slightly behind her competitor, \uc2 Rick Caruso\uc2 , a billionaire real estate developer.\par \par \uc2 There are, however, many more votes to be counted, and the race might not be called for days or weeks.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.03am GMT\par \par \uc2 The Republican candidate for Oregon governor has conceded the race.\par \par \uc2 Christine Drazan, who was the GOP minority leader in the state House, lost to \uc2 Tina Kotek\uc2 , the Democratic candidate who is also Oregon\u8217\'20\'19s longest-serving House speaker.\par \par \uc2 Drazan said the math showed that she cannot win, even with some ballots still to be counted, the AP reported. She noted in a statement that Kotek had not earned more than 50% of the vote, since an unaffiliated candidate had earned 8.6% of votes.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a unique moment in Oregon\u8217\'20\'19s history and an extraordinary opportunity for leadership that recognizes the dynamics of this race that call for moderation and inclusivity moving forward,\u8221\'20\'1D Drazan said. \u8220\'20\'1CI have spoken with \uc2 Tina Kotek\uc2  and hope for the best for our state as she steps into this role.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The race had been unusually close for the typically blue western state. In the final stretch of the race, in a sign of the Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 concerns they could lose the governorship, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  came to Oregon and campaigned for Kotek. Democrats had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/abortion-2022-midterm-elections-salem-liberalism-climate-and-environment-b2144651321876fdd9ba0192e4155492"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 argued}}}\uc2  that a GOP win would threaten \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and environmental protections.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.16am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.09pm GMT\par \par \uc2 In Orange county, California, incumbent Republican \uc2 Young Kim\uc2  has defeated a Democratic challenger and secured her second term, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AP_Politics/status/1590898196888240129"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according }}}\uc2  to the AP.\par \par \uc2 Kim was one of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.latimes.com/politics/story/2022-11-10/2022-california-midterm-election-young-kim-asif-mahmood-results-orange-county"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 first Korean American women elected to Congress}}}\uc2 . Democrats had hoped to flip the seat with candidate {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.latimes.com/politics/story/2022-10-20/2022-california-midterm-election-young-kim-asif-mahmood-on-abortion-inflation-immigration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dr Asif Mahmood}}}\uc2 , but some of the nearby Orange county races were more competitive and ended up receiving more attention, the LA Times reported.\par \par \uc2 The southern California district had been redrawn and became more conservative, and Kim\u8217\'20\'19s platform and messaging became further rightwing this cycle, focusing on crime and the border, the Times said.\par \par \uc2 Mahmood said in a statement today that he had conceded, noting that he and Kim \u8220\'20\'1Cboth share humble beginnings as immigrants who had big dreams and hopes for our families\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrMahmood: \u8220\'20\'1CI know this campaign did not go as we had hoped, but I wish for \uc2 Young Kim\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s success because she will represent all of us in this district.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ViyWq5K7T0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ViyWq5K7T0}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Andrew Solender (@AndrewSolender) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AndrewSolender/status/1591129457586495489?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 11, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.17pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Some Republican senators have called for a delay in the party\u8217\'20\'19s leadership elections scheduled to take place next week.\par \par \uc2 While \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 , the current minority leader, was expected to continue in his role, three GOP senators have been circulating a letter calling to postpone the vote scheduled for Wednesday morning, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/11/11/gop-senators-call-for-postponing-leadership-elections-00066532"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico reported}}}\uc2 . The letter, shared by Senators Ron Johnson, \uc2 Mike Lee\uc2  and \uc2 Rick Scott\uc2 , said:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are all disappointed that a Red Wave failed to materialize, and there are multiple reasons it did not. We need to have serious discussions within our conference as to why and what we can do to improve our chances in 2024.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Senators \uc2 Marco Rubio\uc2  and \uc2 Josh Hawley\uc2  also have supported the calls for a delay, CNN {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/politics/live-news/election-results-congress-senate-house-11-11-2022/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 enltrThe Senate GOP leadership vote next week should be postponed\par \par \uc2 First we need to make sure that those who want to lead us are genuinely committed to fighting for the priorities & values of the working Americans (of every background) who gave us big wins in states like {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Florida?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Florida}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Marco Rubio\uc2  (@marcorubio) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/marcorubio/status/1591112183945269251?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 11, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 The debate over when to hold the vote comes as the fate of the Senate is still unclear. The high-stakes Georgia race is headed to a 6 December runoff.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.52pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The closely watched Colorado congressional race between far-right congresswoman \uc2 Lauren Boebert\uc2  and the Democratic challenger Adam Frisch could potentially lead to a recount, the \uc2 New York Times{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/11/11/us/politics/lauren-boebert-recount-frisch-colorado.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 It could, however, be weeks before the race is called or before it is known whether a re-count will take place, and the process is complex. In Colorado, voters have until 16 November to fix errors or discrepancies on their ballots, and after that the secretary of state\u8217\'20\'19s office selects at least one statewide race and one race in each county to audit, the Times reported. At that point, if it\u8217\'20\'19s found that candidates are separated by less than.5%, then the secretary of state can order a re-count.\par \par \uc2 At the latest count, Boebert had 50.2% of the vote and Frisch had 49.8%. In the initial results, Frisch had the lead over Boebert, but as more votes have been counted, she earned a very narrow edge.\par \par \uc2 Boebert is known as a conspiracy theorist and election denier and is considered one of the most extreme members of her party.\par \par \uc2 Our story from yesterday:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/10/colorado-republican-lauren-boebert-tight-race-against-democrat-adam-frisch-house"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Colorado Republican Lauren Boebert locked in tight race against Democrat}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.10pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.12pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Why is the vote counting taking so long in Arizona?\par \par \uc2 The AP has a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/2022-midterm-elections-arizona-ballot-counting-d9425f8f9b0b0ea203c6453cac860016"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 helpful explainer}}}\uc2  on why its taking days for winners to be declared in Arizona, where the AP has not yet made calls in the crucial governor and Senate races.\par \par \uc2 Almost all of Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s vote happens by mail, and counting all of those ballots can take a while, particularly in a county as large as Maricopa. The state\u8217\'20\'19s largest \u8211\'20\'13 and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/elections-arizona-donald-trump-phoenix-election-2020-349ae4369102747373e65d60767f9388"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fourth-largest in the country}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 Maricopa is home to a total of 4.5 million residents, and about 2.4 million registered voters.\par \par \uc2 There were some Republican activists in Arizona who advocated that voters {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/2022-midterm-elections-health-government-and-politics-election-2020-55f4744b484919cd20d4d5e8d72e444e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 intentionally wait until Election Day}}}\uc2  to drop off their ballots. Some of this push was based on unfounded theories that fraudsters could manipulate voting systems and rig results for Democrats, once they had seen how many GOP votes had been returned early.\par \par \uc2 Experts had also warned that such a last-minute crush of ballots could end up creating delays that can ultimately be used by a bad actor to undermine confidence in the election. There were some hang ups this year. About a quarter of voting centers in Maricopa County, Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s most populous, had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/2022-midterm-elections-arizona-government-and-politics-84b7308b2c4505954a39b570eb0e833d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a printing problem}}}\uc2  Tuesday, in which marks weren\u8217\'20\'19t showing up correctly when voters showed up to print out their ballots.\par \par \uc2 Officials have assured voters that every ballot will be counted.\par \par \uc2 Some pundits have called the Senate race for Mark Kelly, saying the Democrat has defeated Blake Masters, but the AP has not yet declared a winner.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.58pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Yesterday, a newly elected House representative and the lieutenant governor of Virginia did something rare for Republican office holders: they said it was time for the party to move on from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Their comments were a sign that the uneven performance of candidates he endorsed in the midterms may have damaged the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s support for Trump.\par \par \uc2 But today, \uc2 Elise Stefanik\uc2 , the third-ranking GOP lawmaker in the House, announced Trump has her endorsement for the 2024 presidential election.\par \par \uc2 enltrI am proud to endorse my friend \uc2 Donald J. Trump\uc2  for President in 2024.\par \par \uc2 President Trump has always put America First, and I look forward to supporting him so we can save America. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/EXe6Rgz7mW"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/EXe6Rgz7mW}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Elise Stefanik\uc2  (@EliseStefanik) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/EliseStefanik/status/1591127868704141312?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 11, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 She\u8217\'20\'19s jumping the gun a little bit \u8211\'20\'13 Trump has not yet announced another campaign, but is widely expected to do so on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.04pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.41pm GMT\par \par \uc2 CBS News has more reporting indicating that Trump is not taking the loss of several of his hand-picked Republican candidates in Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s midterms particularly well:\par \par \uc2 enltrDark time in Trump's inner circle. Spoke to several longtime friends, donors, and aides in the past 24 hours. Many say he's listening to very few people, isolated, and meanspirited about his potential rivals. Several of them say they're tired of his rants and are avoiding him.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Robert Costa (@costareports) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/costareports/status/1591157532818800641?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 11, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CI have never seen him more irresponsible and chaotic then he is today. He seems to be in self-destruct mode. It is irresponsible to attack DeSantis and Youngkin, and it\u8217\'20\'19s irresponsible to announce in any time in the near future" especially before GA runoff, per a Trump adviser.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Robert Costa (@costareports) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/costareports/status/1591158172630519808?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 11, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Trump is on Tuesday expected to make what he\u8217\'20\'19s called a \u8220\'20\'1Cbig announcement\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 likely the start of his campaign to win the White House again in the 2024 election.\par \par \uc2 And with a big announcement comes big money \u8211\'20\'13 at least he hopes. An appeal email sent out by the ex-president\u8217\'20\'19s fundraising committee today offers people who contribute $45 or more the chance to win a free trip to Mar-a-Lago for the announcement.\par \par \uc2 This post has been corrected to indicate it was CBS News that reported on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s mood, not CNN.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.49pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.25pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Not all the results are in, but expect analysts to spend a lot of time debating just how Democrats pulled off their surprisingly good performance in Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s election. One theory making the rounds is that the party prevailed thanks to substantial support from young voters. \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/erum-salam"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Erum Salam}}}\uc2  takes a closer look:\par \par \uc2 The 2022 midterm election delivered surprising results, with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats}}}\uc2  maintaining more House seats than projected and a Republican \u8220\'20\'1Cred wave\u8221\'20\'1D failing to materialize. As the forces driving these come into focus, one group proved to be key: young voters.\par \par \uc2 While final figures are still pouring in, it is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://circle.tufts.edu/latest-research/millions-youth-cast-ballots-decide-key-2022-races"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 estimated}}}\uc2  that 27% of young voters aged 18-29 cast a ballot in 2022, making this the midterm election with the second highest youth voter turnout in almost three decades, after 2018. In some key battleground states, turnout was even higher, at 31%, and support for Democratic candidates was roughly over 60%, driven in large part by the fight for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights after the supreme court overturned Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 An Edison Research National Election Pool exit poll showed that 18-29s were the only age group in which a strong majority supported Democrats. Support for Democrats was even higher among Black youth at 89% and Latino youth at 68%.\par \par \uc2 It is a trend that continues from the 2018 and 2020 elections, where youth voter turnout \u8211\'20\'13 historically perceived as low \u8211\'20\'13 surged and proved to be a crucial voting bloc, particularly for Democrats. But some young voters struggled to cast their ballot \u8211\'20\'13 raising questions about the particular hurdles this group faces to have a voice in elections.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/11/young-voters-us-midterms-democratic-youth"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Young voters hailed as key to Democratic successes in midterms}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.10pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Despite many of their candidates\u8217\'20\'19 rhetoric about stolen elections and voting fraud before the midterms, Republicans who lost in Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s election don\u8217\'20\'19t seem to be flocking to the courts to challenge the results. That could change.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/11/11/republicans-redirect-hopes-for-senate-majority-on-georgia-runoff-00066517"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico reports}}}\uc2  that on a Thursday conference call, Republican senator \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2  suggested that if the party\u8217\'20\'19s Senate candidate \uc2 Adam Laxalt\uc2  loses in Nevada, it\u8217\'20\'19ll be a sign of fraud.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere is no mathematical way Laxalt loses,\u8221\'20\'1D Graham said, according to Politico. \u8220\'20\'1CIf he does, then it\u8217\'20\'19s a lie.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s unclear if Laxalt agrees with Graham, who he would join in the Senate if elected over Democratic incumbent \uc2 Catherine Cortez Masto\uc2 . On \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , Laxalt has been projecting confidence as Nevada\u8217\'20\'19s slow ballot counting process grinds on:\par \par \uc2 enltrClark County Clerk just reported there are just over 50K ballots left. This number includes Election Day drop off. We know there are rural and Washoe votes to be counted. Assuming these two at least offset, then Cortez Masto needs 63.5% to catch us. We remain very confident.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Adam Paul Laxalt\uc2  (@AdamLaxalt) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AdamLaxalt/status/1590825264912957440?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 10, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.53pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Outside New York City, House Democrat Pat Ryan has also triumphed in his re-election battle, the Associated Press says:\par \par \uc2 enltrBREAKING: Democrat Pat Ryan wins reelection to \uc2 U.S. House\uc2  in New York's 18th Congressional District. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/APracecall?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #APracecall}}}\uc2  at 12:30 p.m. EST. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/2nlgpji7ac"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/2nlgpji7ac}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 AP Politics (@AP_Politics) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AP_Politics/status/1591121455005171712?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 11, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 It was a close call for Ryan. He won 49.4% support against his Republican opponent Colin Schmitt \u8217\'20\'19s 48.6% share of the vote, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nyenr.elections.ny.gov/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to New York\u8217\'20\'19s unofficial results}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.13pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.39pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Another vulnerable House Democrat has won reelection.\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press says \uc2 David Trone\uc2  has emerged victorious in a district stretching from western Maryland to Washington\u8217\'20\'19s exurbs. Trone tweeted that his opponent, Neil Parrott, called him to concede the race:\par \par \uc2 enltrI want to thank Del. Parrott for his phone call this afternoon conceding the race. My promise to him, and to all of the people of the 6th District, is this: I\u8217\'20\'19ll continue to work across the aisle to deliver results and get things done. Thank you, Maryland! Let\u8217\'20\'19s get back to work.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 David Trone\uc2  (@davidjtrone) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/davidjtrone/status/1591148182867570688?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 11, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 The race was very close. Trone squeaked to victory with 50.5% support against Parrott\u8217\'20\'19s 49.4%, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://elections.maryland.gov/elections/2022/general_results/gen_results_2022_5.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to the state\u8217\'20\'19s unofficial results}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.50pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.22pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile in Alaska, the state\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic House representative is warning that it could be a while before voters learn whether she\u8217\'20\'19s won election to a full term:\par \par \uc2 enltrBuckle up, it\u8217\'20\'19s going to be a bit. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/9JlcJXPUig"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/9JlcJXPUig}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Mary Peltola (@MaryPeltola) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MaryPeltola/status/1591145058975506432?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 11, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Alaska\u8217\'20\'19s ranked choice voting system has made calling their elections particularly complex, and the Anchorage Daily News says don\u8217\'20\'19t expect the final results in Peltola\u8217\'20\'19s race until 23 November. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.adn.com/politics/2022/11/08/2022-alaska-general-election-preliminary-results/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Their preliminary data}}}\uc2  shows her in the lead over Republican challenger \uc2 Sarah Palin\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 yes, that \uc2 Sarah Palin\uc2 , the one-time vice-presidential nominee known for her folksy brand of conservatism.\par \par \uc2 Peltola won a special election in August to replace Alaska\u8217\'20\'19s longtime Republican House representative \uc2 Don Young\uc2 , who died in office.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.05pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden exhorts other nations to join US in climate pledges, action\par \par \uc2 Guardian US climate reporters {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/oliver-milman"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Oliver Milman}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/nina-lakhani"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nina Lakhani}}}\uc2  report from Egypt.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has implored countries to do more to tackle the climate emergency, telling the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/cop27"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cop27}}}\uc2  summit that world leaders \u8220\'20\'1Ccan no longer plead ignorance\u8221\'20\'1D and that time to confront the crisis is running out.\par \par \uc2 Biden told a large crowd of delegates at the talks, held in Egypt, that the \u8220\'20\'1Cscience is devastatingly clear \u8211\'20\'13 we have to make progress by the end of this decade.\u8221\'20\'1D The US president stated that America was taking action on cutting planet-heating emissions and that other major economies needed to \u8220\'20\'1Cstep up\u8221\'20\'1D to avoid a disastrous breach of 1.5C in global heating.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  delivers a speech during the 2022 United Nations Climate Change Conference, more commonly known as COP27, at the Sharm El Sheikh International Convention Centre, in Egypt\u8217\'20\'19s Red Sea resort. Photograph: Anadolu Agency/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLet\u8217\'20\'19s raise both our ambition and speed of our efforts,\u8221\'20\'1D he said in his speech on Friday in Sharm el-Sheikh. \u8220\'20\'1CIf we are going to win this fight, every major emitter needs to align with 1.5C. We can no longer plead ignorance of the consequences of our actions or continue to repeat our mistakes. Everyone has to keep accelerating progress throughout this decisive decade.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden, buoyed by better than expected midterm elections for Democrats this week, said that governments need to \u8220\'20\'1Cput down significant markers of progress\u8221\'20\'1D in reducing emissions. Scientists have warned that the world is heading for disastrous levels of global heating, with emissions still not falling fast enough to avoid severe heatwaves, wildfires, droughts and other impacts of the climate crisis.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s been a difficult few years; the interconnected challenges we face can seem all-consuming,\u8221\'20\'1D said Biden, who accused \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  of using \u8220\'20\'1Cenergy as a weapon\u8221\'20\'1D in Russia\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Ukraine, an action that has caused energy and food prices to soar globally. \u8220\'20\'1CAgainst this backdrop, it\u8217\'20\'19s more urgent than ever that we double down on our climate commitment.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 You can read the full report {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2022/nov/11/cop27-joe-biden-climate-crisis-us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 enltrThe climate challenges we face are great, but our capacity is greater.\par \par \uc2 The global leaders of the COP27 must reach out and take the future in our hands to make the world we wish to see and that we know we need \u8211\'20\'13 and preserve our planet for generations yet to come.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 President Biden (@POTUS) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS/status/1591143723999539200?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 11, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.10pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.30pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Four of the five {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/hub/us-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 supreme court}}}\uc2  justices who overturned the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  showed up at the conservative \uc2 Federalist Society\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s black-tie dinner marking its 40th anniversary, the Associated Press writes.\par \par \uc2 Justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  got a long, loud ovation Thursday night from a crowd of 2,000 people, most in tuxedos and gowns, when another speaker praised his opinion in June that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/abortion-supreme-court-decision-854f60302f21c2c35129e58cf8d8a7b0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturned Roe v Wade}}}\uc2 , long a target of judicial conservatives.\par \par \uc2 Justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  speaks during the \uc2 Federalist Society\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 40th anniversary dinner at Union Station in Washington. Photograph: Jos\u233\'00\'E9 Luis Maga\u241\'00\'F1a/AP\par \par \uc2 At a moment when opinion surveys show that Americans think the court is becoming more political and give it dismal approval ratings, the justices turned out to celebrate the group that helped then-president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and Senate Republicans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/joe-biden-donald-trump-judiciary-coronavirus-pandemic-us-supreme-court-c37607c9987888058d3d0650eea125cd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 move the American judiciary, including the supreme court, to the right}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Federalist Society\uc2  has no partisan affiliation and takes no position in election campaigns, but it is closely aligned with Republican priorities, including the drive to overturn Roe.\par \par \uc2 Justice \uc2 Amy Coney Barrett\uc2  and Alito offered brief remarks that steered well clear of the court\u8217\'20\'19s work, though Alito praised the \uc2 Federalist Society\uc2  for its success in the Trump years and hoped it would continue. \u8220\'20\'1CBoy, is your work needed today,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Justice \uc2 Amy Coney Barrett\uc2  speaks during the \uc2 Federalist Society\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s event. Photograph: Jos\u233\'00\'E9 Luis Maga\u241\'00\'F1a/AP\par \par \uc2 Barrett\u8217\'20\'19s only allusion to the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  case came when she responded to the crowd\u8217\'20\'19s roar of approval when she was introduced. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s really nice to have a lot of noise made not by protesters outside my house,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections were on the ballot in some states in the midterm elections earlier this week.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/nov/09/vermont-abortion-vote-first-us-state-constitution"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US states vote to protect reproductive rights in rebuke to anti-\b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  push}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.35pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.54pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 Three days after the midterm election, we\u8217\'20\'19re still awaiting {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/nov/11/us-midterm-election-2022-senate-house-results-congress-democrats-republicans-politics-live-updates-latest?page=with:block-636e5bcf8f088f91b4c6544e#block-636e5bcf8f088f91b4c6544e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the results of Arizona and Nevada\u8217\'20\'19s Senate races}}}\uc2 , which will be crucial to determining control of the chamber. The majority in the House {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/nov/11/us-midterm-election-2022-senate-house-results-congress-democrats-republicans-politics-live-updates-latest?page=with:block-636e54008f08786f8dfacbca#block-636e54008f08786f8dfacbca"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is similarly uncertain}}}\uc2 , though it looks like Republicans have a better shot than Democrats at taking the majority for the next two years. Meanwhile, \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/nov/11/us-midterm-election-2022-senate-house-results-congress-democrats-republicans-politics-live-updates-latest?page=with:block-636e62f98f088f91b4c654cf#block-636e62f98f088f91b4c654cf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appears ready to announce a new run}}}\uc2  for the White House on Tuesday, even as some in the GOP question whether he\u8217\'20\'19s the right candidate to continue leading the party.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more of what we\u8217\'20\'19ve learned so far today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump has gone after a number of Republicans on social media today, including {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/nov/11/us-midterm-election-2022-senate-house-results-congress-democrats-republicans-politics-live-updates-latest?page=with:block-636e65558f088f91b4c654f0#block-636e65558f088f91b4c654f0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Florida governor }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/nov/11/us-midterm-election-2022-senate-house-results-congress-democrats-republicans-politics-live-updates-latest?page=with:block-636e65558f088f91b4c654f0#block-636e65558f088f91b4c654f0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ron DeSantis}}}\uc2  and Virginia governor Glenn Youngkin.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Why is the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s count of Senate seats different from the AP\u8217\'20\'19s? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/nov/11/us-midterm-election-2022-senate-house-results-congress-democrats-republicans-politics-live-updates-latest?page=with:block-636e6dc38f08786f8dfacd60#block-636e6dc38f08786f8dfacd60"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 This is the reason why}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 One Democratic pollster{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/nov/11/us-midterm-election-2022-senate-house-results-congress-democrats-republicans-politics-live-updates-latest?page=with:block-636e81fb8f08786f8dfaceec#block-636e81fb8f08786f8dfaceec"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 explained}}}\uc2  why he believed his party would do well all along. Another {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/nov/11/us-midterm-election-2022-senate-house-results-congress-democrats-republicans-politics-live-updates-latest?page=with:block-636e860c8f08786f8dfacf46#block-636e860c8f08786f8dfacf46"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 explored}}}\uc2  the reasons why Democrats performed better on the issue of crime than he expected.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.12pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.34pm GMT\par \par \uc2 In the days before the election, another veteran Democratic pollster predicted a rough night for the party, in part due to frustration over crime.\par \par \uc2 Writing in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://prospect.org/politics/how-democrats-mishandled-crime/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The American Prospect}}}\uc2 , Stanley B Greenberg, who played a part in \uc2 Bill Clinton\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s successful White House campaign, argued that Democrats had failed to convince voters of their ability to stem rising crime. So bad was their handling of the issue that many voters believed the party wanted to defund the police, even though many Democrats reject the idea.\par \par \uc2 Greenberg spoke {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nymag.com/intelligencer/2022/11/2022-midterms-how-democrats-beat-back-the-gop-on-crime.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to New York Magazine in an interview}}}\uc2  published today about the reasons why Democrats ended up doing better in the midterms than his analyses predicted:\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s important not to take the wrong lessons from the fact that we were saved by late partisan polarization, which reflects the post-2016 era where we have high turnout and consolidation of both parties. A lot of moderate Democrats in our October poll said they were voting for Republicans, about twice as many Republicans who said they were voting for Democrats. But that disappeared in the intense partisan polarization at the end. And that was driven on the Democratic side by worries about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Social Security, and democracy. On Tuesday, about 3% of Democrats voted for Republicans and about 3% of Republicans voted for Democrats. A quarter of people in our survey said they made up their mind on the last day, or in the last few days before the election, which we\u8217\'20\'19ve never had before. So we were on a knife\u8217\'20\'19s edge, and it could have been and was poised to be much worse.\par \par \uc2 He also addressed why his prediction about the crime issue does not appear to have come true:\par \par \uc2 If you look at the candidates who won, they addressed the crime problem early on and spent a lot of money being clear that they were against defunding the police, and being clear that they opposed those in the party who are advocating it. Voters believe that we wanted to defund the police. And so if you didn\u8217\'20\'19t make your message almost entirely about respect for police and funding the police, you were not going to make any progress.\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m actually surprised how much voters are open to rethinking Democrats on crime, but not in the context of this election, where Democrats were mostly saying the wrong thing. They were making the issue more important, but without the right message. The national Democratic message was block grants for more police, banning assault weapons \u8212\'20\'14 a range of government programs that our data showed hurt us. If you look at what happened in New York, they led with that kind of messaging.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.36pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.16pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 success in Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s elections took many by surprise. But not Simon Rosenberg.\par \par \uc2 The veteran Democratic pollster and president of the NDN and New Policy Institute think tanks has been arguing for weeks that his party would perform better than polls indicated in the midterms, and ended up being more right than wrong.\par \par \uc2 Yesterday on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , he shared some thoughts about what propelled Democrats to their surprisingly strong showing:\par \par \uc2 enltrHappy Thursday all!\par \par \uc2 Some thoughts about the election:\par \par \uc2 - Big miss was on Dem/GOP intensity, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 - 3rd straight disappointing election for MAGA/Trump\par \par \uc2 - Rs denigration of early vote a mistake\par \par \uc2 - AZ, NV encouraging\par \par \uc2 - Please give to Warnock today! 1/ {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/vNjVzIzYFd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/vNjVzIzYFd}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Simon Rosenberg (@SimonWDC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SimonWDC/status/1590684698480893953?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 10, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrBefore I dive in, it's worth reviewing our core election arguments. Will be referencing the elements in the thread below. So take a moment to read through it. Holds up pretty well. 2/ {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/5poVsdQNKq"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/5poVsdQNKq}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Simon Rosenberg (@SimonWDC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SimonWDC/status/1590685620263071744?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 10, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrNow believe fundamental miss of the cycle was the ignoring of the signals about D and R intensity.\par \par \uc2 Ds had showed intensity all summer/fall. R's didn't. Then Ds crushed it in early vote. Rs struggled. Was a clear sign.\par \par \uc2 But somehow we got red wave. 3/\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/UjEpoMsup3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/UjEpoMsup3}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Simon Rosenberg (@SimonWDC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SimonWDC/status/1590688292772929536?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 10, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrAnd of course the thing which drove the Dem intensity was GOP extremism on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 It was really important to Rs that they erase notion \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  could drive US politics. Ideological implications of this dire for them.\par \par \uc2 It was pure gaslighting. 4/ {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/34K1cKpZ9t"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/34K1cKpZ9t}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Simon Rosenberg (@SimonWDC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SimonWDC/status/1590691137215336451?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 10, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrWill be interesting for us learn in coming days whether Rs really believed there was a red wave coming or they knew it was all bullshit.\par \par \uc2 Looking back big flood of R happy polls may be sign they knew they were having intensity issues. 5/ {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/1BEbErzFdg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/1BEbErzFdg}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Simon Rosenberg (@SimonWDC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SimonWDC/status/1590692099149926400?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 10, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrOne area we have to explore together is what a political disaster MAGA/Trump has been for Rs:\par \par \uc2 - lost Presidency/Senate/House in 18/20\par \par \uc2 - Disappointing 22\par \par \uc2 - Huge R defections across US, fractured coalition\par \par \uc2 - Attack on voting/early vote costly\par \par \uc2 - Candidates couldn't raise money 6/\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Simon Rosenberg (@SimonWDC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SimonWDC/status/1590693747997540353?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 10, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrThe GOP's crazy attack on our elections not only reminded voters every day that they'd lost their mind as a party, but it also gave Ds a huge tactical advantage as we banked huge early vote leads across US.\par \par \uc2 "Election denialism" is a disaster for Rs. 7/ {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/WJgQ5Jta12"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/WJgQ5Jta12}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Simon Rosenberg (@SimonWDC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SimonWDC/status/1590695410368405504?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 10, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrHere is the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ThePlumLineGS?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @ThePlumLineGS}}}\uc2  on what an abject failure authoritarianism has been for MAGA and the Rs.\par \par \uc2 This is a very important story. 8/ {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/nR1YQlTj1M"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/nR1YQlTj1M}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Simon Rosenberg (@SimonWDC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SimonWDC/status/1590695904566476800?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 10, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrTrendlines look very good for us in Arizona and Nevada. Am optimistic about both. 9/ {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/nR1YQlTj1M"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/nR1YQlTj1M}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Simon Rosenberg (@SimonWDC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SimonWDC/status/1590696848855269376?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 10, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.57pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Have you heard of Chase Oliver? Democratic and Republican party leaders in Georgia certainly have. The Libertarian candidate garnered 81,000 votes in the tight race for Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s Senate seat, which will now go to a run-off, in part because of his presence on the ballot. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more about the \u8220\'20\'1Carmed and gay\u8221\'20\'1D politician, from \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/andrew-lawrence"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Andrew Lawrence}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 The morning after the midterms, Chase Oliver was back at work. \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s what most other Georgians have to do after an election,\u8221\'20\'1D he tells the Guardian. \u8220\'20\'1CI have a job and have to pay rent and the bills.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Oliver, 37, has two jobs, actually \u8211\'20\'13 one as a sales account executive for a financial services company and another as an HR rep for a securities firm. And as he toggled between email replies and Zoom interviews from his north-east Atlanta home, with three cats and a dog, Delilah, underfoot, you\u8217\'20\'19d never suspect this natty, young Georgian had thrown a spanner into the cogs of American power. \u8220\'20\'1CYou are possibly the most hated man in America right now,\u8221\'20\'1D read one post to his \uc2 Facebook\uc2  page.\par \par \uc2 Oliver was the third candidate in Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 US Senate\uc2  race: a pro-gun, anti-cop, pro-choice Libertarian who proudly announces himself as the state\u8217\'20\'19s first LGBTQ+ candidate \u8211\'20\'13 \u8220\'20\'1Carmed and gay\u8221\'20\'1D, he boasts. And on Tuesday night, this surprise spoiler scored an historic upset of sorts, siphoning enough support away from the Democratic incumbent \uc2 Raphael Warnock\uc2  and his Republican challenger \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  to force the election to a 6 December runoff \u8211\'20\'13 Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s second in as many election cycles. Until then, there\u8217\'20\'19s no telling whether the Democrats will retain control of the Senate.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/11/georgia-senate-race-chase-oliver-profile"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The \u8216\'20\'18armed and gay\u8217\'20\'19 Senate hopeful who helped force Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s runoff}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.39pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Vote counting is proceeding at an agonizingly slow pace in Nevada, where Democrats are locked in tight races to keep a Senate seat and the governor\u8217\'20\'19s mansion.\par \par \uc2 For an idea as to why, take a look at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/2022-midterm-elections-nevada-congress-government-and-politics-896bf9df5d24efbdfeef92f1c10799f0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 this explainer from the Associated Press}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 The vote counting is taking days, but that\u8217\'20\'19s not abnormal for Nevada, where a chunk of votes have previously not been tallied until after election night. In the two most populous counties, officials warned up front that it would take days to process the outstanding ballots.\par \par \uc2 NEVADA\u8217\'20\'19S WAY\par \par \uc2 A few things have slowed Nevada\u8217\'20\'19s vote counting in recent elections.\par \par \uc2 First, Nevada has also had problems with long lines of voters at poll close, although Nevadans have traditionally opted to vote early. The state won\u8217\'20\'19t release vote counts until all voters who were in line at poll close have cast their vote.\par \par \uc2 Second, in 2020, Nevada greatly expanded absentee voting, sending a ballot to every registered voter. The state passed legislation to do that in future elections as well.\par \par \uc2 Also that year, nearly 15% of Nevada\u8217\'20\'19s vote was not reported until after election night \u8212\'20\'14 and it took three days for the state to report 100% of the vote.\par \par \uc2 This year, voting officials in the two most populous counties, encompassing the population centers of Las Vegas and Reno, warned it would take days to process the outstanding ballots.\par \par \uc2 County election clerks will count mail ballots received until Nov. 12 as long as they were postmarked by Election Day.\par \par \uc2 Officials have until Nov. 17 to finish the counting and submit a report to the Nevada secretary of state\u8217\'20\'19s office, according to state law.\par \par \uc2 The state has no mandatory recount law.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.24pm GMT\par \par \uc2 All eyes are on media results trackers as Arizona and Nevada\u8217\'20\'19s Senate races inch closer to official results and news on control of the House looms.\par \par \uc2 So a quick note about Alaska\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 Readers who like to pick \u8216\'20\'18n\u8217\'20\'19 mix may have noticed that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2022/nov/08/midterm-election-results-live-2022-map-us-midterms-latest-winners-seats-congress"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Guardian}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the New York Times}}}\uc2  currently have the Senate decided 48 to 48, Democrats vs Republicans in the 100-seat chamber, but CNN on screen and online {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is showing}}}\uc2  the GOP at 49 seats.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s down to Alaska, where {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/2022-midterm-elections-alaska-donald-trump-congress-2c2f7b1fe9fd1c91a74a7f7687b3a27b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ranked choice voting}}}\uc2  is used. There isn\u8217\'20\'19t a winner projected yet by the Associated Press, on which the Guardian blog, stories and tracker rely, but the AP acknowledges the race is tight and is now between two Republicans, incumbent \uc2 Lisa Murkowski\uc2  and Trump-backed challenger \uc2 Kelly Tshibaka\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Republican U.S. Senator \uc2 Lisa Murkowski\uc2  stands with supporters on U.S. election night in Anchorage. Photograph: Kerry Tasker/Reuters\par \par \uc2 AP on Thursday {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/2022-midterm-elections-alaska-donald-trump-congress-2c2f7b1fe9fd1c91a74a7f7687b3a27b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 noted}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CExactly who\u8217\'20\'19ll win Alaska\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 US Senate\uc2  contest isn\u8217\'20\'19t clear, but it will be a Republican.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 So the GOP do have 49 Senate seats nailed down, but we\u8217\'20\'19ll wait for AP to name a winner in Alaska before we recalculate our AP-driven special {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2022/nov/08/midterm-election-results-live-2022-map-us-midterms-latest-winners-seats-congress"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 live results tracker}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 What about the P-word? Mary Peltola {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.adn.com/politics/2022/11/08/peltola-leads-alaskas-us-house-race-in-early-results/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is ahead}}}\uc2  of \uc2 Sarah Palin\uc2  in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nativenewsonline.net/currents/mary-peltola-takes-lead-in-alaska-house-race"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Alaska House race}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 U.S. Rep. Mary Peltola waves a sign during the morning rush hour in Anchorage, Alaska, on Tuesday Nov. 8. Peltola, who became the first Alaska Native elected to Congress when she won a special election earlier this year, faced Republicans \uc2 Sarah Palin\uc2  and Nick Begich and Libertarian Chris Bye in the midterms general election. Final result awaited. Photograph: Mark Thiessen/AP\par \par \uc2 Remember her? Still touting \u8220\'20\'1Cdrill, baby, drill.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trailing Peltola now, here\u8217\'20\'19s former Alaska governor and former vice presidential candidate \uc2 Sarah Palin\uc2  in Anchorage on election day. Photograph: Kerry Tasker/Reuters\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.09pm GMT\par \par \uc2 If you couldn\u8217\'20\'19t tell from his social media posts, CNN confirms it: Trump is \u8220\'20\'1Ccranky\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/11/11/politics/tiffany-trump-wedding/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 this story}}}\uc2  that gets into the intra-family drama playing out ahead of Saturday\u8217\'20\'19s planned wedding of the former president\u8217\'20\'19s youngest daughter, \uc2 Tiffany Trump\uc2 . \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is, of course, expected to attend, but CNN reports he\u8217\'20\'19s distracted by his \u8220\'20\'1Cspecial announcement\u8221\'20\'1D set for Tuesday, which will likely be where he makes public a new campaign for the White House in 2024.\par \par \uc2 As for what\u8217\'20\'19s fueling Trump\u8217\'20\'19s annoyance, CNN chalks that up to the underperformance of his candidates in Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s midterms, and the handful of calls from Republicans for the ex-president to step aside.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.53pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Next up on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s hit list is Virginia governor Glenn Youngkin.\par \par \uc2 Last year, Youngkin managed to win the governor\u8217\'20\'19s office in a state that typically leans Democratic. In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump/posts/109325150085362681"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a post on this Truth social network}}}\uc2  Trump said Youngkin \u8220\'20\'1Ccouldn\u8217\'20\'19t have won without me.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI Endorsed him, did a very big Trump Rally for him telephonically, got MAGA to Vote for him - or he couldn\u8217\'20\'19t have come close to winning. But he knows that, and admits it. Besides, having a hard time with the Dems in Virginia - But he\u8217\'20\'19ll get it done!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump began his post by misspelling Youngkin\u8217\'20\'19s name as \u8220\'20\'1CYoung Kin (now that\u8217\'20\'19s an interesting take. Sounds Chinese, doesn\u8217\'20\'19t it?).\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Yesterday, Virginia\u8217\'20\'19s lieutenant-governor Winsome Sears called Trump \u8220\'20\'1Ca liability\u8221\'20\'1D for Republicans, and said if he ran in 2024, she \u8220\'20\'1Ccould not support him.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.37pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump attacks DeSantis with baseless claim of fraud, \uc2 FBI\uc2  involvement\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has spent the past hours having something of a public meltdown, and directing his ire towards various Republicans who offended him.\par \par \uc2 Last night, the target was Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 . In a statement, Trump claimed he sent federal agents to stop vote rigging during Florida\u8217\'20\'19s 2018 election, in which the Republican narrowly beat Democrat \uc2 Andrew Gillum\uc2  for the governor\u8217\'20\'19s mansion.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI was all in for Ron, and he beat Gillum, but after the Race, when votes were being stolen by the corrupt Election process in Broward County, and Ron was going down ten thousand votes a day, along with now-Senator \uc2 Rick Scott\uc2 , I sent in the \uc2 FBI\uc2  and the U.S. Attorneys, and the ballot theft immediately ended, just prior to them running out of the votes necessary to win. I stopped his Election from being stolen,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump wrote in a diatribe that called DeSantis \u8220\'20\'1CRon DeSanctimonious\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 There is no evidence of tampering with Florida\u8217\'20\'19s 2018 election. There is, however, evidence that DeSantis had a much better Tuesday evening than Trump. He was re-elected as Florida\u8217\'20\'19s governor by a big margin, on a night in which Republicans performed well statewide. Meanwhile, several of the former president\u8217\'20\'19s handpicked candidates across the country came up short, and a few Republicans have since broken the party\u8217\'20\'19s wall of support for Trump, and called for the GOP to move on.\par \par \uc2 That would be a boost to DeSantis, who is widely seen as mulling his own run for the White House in 2024. His campaign could pose the most serious challenge to Trump for the Republican nomination.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.42pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.17pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  departed Washington yesterday evening for Sharm el-Sheikh, Egypt, where he\u8217\'20\'19s minutes away from addressing the Cop27 climate summit.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/oliver-milman"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Oliver Milman}}}\uc2  is covering the event, and you can tune in to our live blog for full coverage of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s speech:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/live/2022/nov/11/cop27-egypt-joe-biden-climate-conference-decarbonisation-live-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cop27: Joe Biden about to address summit; oil and gas exec blames individuals for climate crisis - live}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.24pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.02pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s plan to announce a new presidential campaign is causing controversy among some Republicans who worry it will jeopardize their chances of winning Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s Senate runoff, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/hugo-lowell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hugo Lowell}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s top political staffers at Mar-a-Lago are pressing him to move forward with his planned 2024 presidential campaign announcement next week but a chorus of allies are suggesting delaying until after the Senate runoff in Georgia in December, according to sources familiar with the matter.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 former US president}}}\uc2  has been forced to reckon with Republican blame for underwhelming performances from rightwing candidates he endorsed in the midterm elections, with the defeat of Mehmet Oz in Pennsylvania, contributing to uncertainty over which party will control the Senate.\par \par \uc2 Trump has suggested publicly that he intends to announce his 2024 presidential campaign next week as planned. Behind the scenes at Mar-a-Lago, in a sign of concern about his standing after disappointing results in the midterms, he remains undecided on how to proceed. However, some initial invites for the \u8220\'20\'1CSpecial Announcement\u8221\'20\'1D event have been sent.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s top staffers have firmly pressed him to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/06/trump-2024-presidential-run-announcement"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announce his latest White House campaign}}}\uc2  as planned on Tuesday, the sources said, suggesting that he would appear weak and wounded by the results were he to cave to demands that he hold off until the Senate runoff early next month.\par \par \uc2 Trump also has no upside in waiting until the Senate runoff, where his handpicked Republican candidate \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  trails Democratic incumbent \uc2 Raphael Warnock\uc2 . His staffers are said to have told him: if Walker wins, he can take credit, and if Walker loses, his position would be no different.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/10/trump-inner-circle-rift-2024-presidential-campaign-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Rift in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s inner circle over 2024 presidential campaign announcement}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.05pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.47pm GMT\par \par \uc2 If Republicans win a majority in the House, Kevin McCarthy could be the man to lead it for the next two years. \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/edwardhelmore"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Edward Helmore}}}\uc2  reports on McCarthy\u8217\'20\'19s conversation with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  yesterday, and the president\u8217\'20\'19s acknowledgment that Democrats face long odds in keeping the chamber:\par \par \uc2 The eyes of the political world remained focused on Arizona and Nevada on Friday, where hundreds of thousands of uncounted votes held the key to control of the \uc2 US Senate\uc2 , three days after Americans cast their final ballots in midterm elections.\par \par \uc2 The delay in districts such as Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s Maricopa county, which includes Phoenix, is attributed to the record number of ballots cast on Tuesday. Election officials had estimated they would have a tally by Friday but now say they will count through the weekend.\par \par \uc2 In Nevada, election officials had estimated a finish by Friday but, again, the high number of ballots cast means counting will continue through next week. However, a winner could be called as soon as any candidate is judged to have passed a majority threshold.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/11/nothing-final-in-house-or-senate-as-us-midterm-elections-count-continues"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 All eyes on Nevada and Arizona as Senate control hangs in balance}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.31pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press has not called the Senate races in Nevada and Arizona, where Democratic incumbents are fighting for re-election.\par \par \uc2 But the Cook Political Report has weighed in on Arizona, saying that Democrat Mark Kelly won his race:\par \par \uc2 enltrI've seen enough: Sen. Mark Kelly (D) wins reelection in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/AZSEN?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #AZSEN}}}\uc2 , defeating Blake Masters (R).\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Dave Wasserman (@Redistrict) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Redistrict/status/1590944022939717633?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 11, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Nevada conducted its election mostly by mail, and is slowly releasing the results of ballots that have been counted. According to the Nevada Independent, the results are looking good for Democrat \uc2 Catherine Cortez Masto\uc2  in her bid for another term against Republican \uc2 Adam Laxalt\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 but it\u8217\'20\'19s not over yet:\par \par \uc2 enltrGood morning from The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/WeMatter?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #WeMatter}}}\uc2  State, and Happy Veterans Day, especially to those who served.\par \par \uc2 Here's where we are:\par \par \uc2 Laxalt leads by 9K statewide over CCM.\par \par \uc2 The news of this early AM is below, and let me tell you what it means.\par \par \uc2 1/ {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/oyNKItxqF6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/oyNKItxqF6}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jon Ralston (@RalstonReports) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RalstonReports/status/1591061666917031937?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 11, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrThis is part of the 57K mail ballots (there are actually more but wait) to be counted in Clark.\par \par \uc2 Those first 35K will put a huge dent in Laxalt's lead, and CCM, if indies are breaking to Ds as they have been, will pick up more than 6K.\par \par \uc2 2/\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jon Ralston (@RalstonReports) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RalstonReports/status/1591063499496529921?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 11, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrIf CCM continues pace of getting 60 percent and Laxalt gets 35 percent, she will pick up 9K in this batch alone.\par \par \uc2 If it's 55-40, she will add more than 5K.\par \par \uc2 The margin could be greater (65-30?).\par \par \uc2 3/\par \par \uc2 Bottom line: Unless trend suddenly shifts, this batch will help her a lot.\par \par \uc2 3/\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jon Ralston (@RalstonReports) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RalstonReports/status/1591064434562068481?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 11, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrSo what else is left?\par \par \uc2 Laxalt is still going to gain 2-4K in rurals -- super-red Douglas should post a few thousand ballots today.\par \par \uc2 There are still 20K or so to count in Clark and 20K in Washoe -- minus whatever ballots need to be cured -- and that 40K batch should help her.\par \par \uc2 4/\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jon Ralston (@RalstonReports) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RalstonReports/status/1591065729033375748?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 11, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrThe ballots needing to be cured -- mail that has signature problems, for example -- also favor Dems. Culinary, others running intense campaigns to get those voters to fix their ballots so they can be counted.\par \par \uc2 Via {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JohnRSamuelsen?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @JohnRSamuelsen}}}\uc2  : {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/X3jrPH1jm6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/X3jrPH1jm6}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jon Ralston (@RalstonReports) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RalstonReports/status/1591066584222613504?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 11, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrThere are also 5.5K provisional ballots, many of them from first-time voters, young folks. Those are thought to favor the Dems, too.\par \par \uc2 Laxalt's best chance to hang on in the face of this blizzard of mail votes is for the margins to go down and rural margins/volume to be huge.\par \par \uc2 6/7\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jon Ralston (@RalstonReports) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RalstonReports/status/1591067300332941312?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 11, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrBottom line: This first batch of 35K mail ballots shows a partisan breakdown that strongly favors CCM, and if the trend continues, she is going to win.\par \par \uc2 But miles to go before I can finally sleep, and we will know a LOT when Clark/Washoe post tonight.\par \par \uc2 Good morning!\par \par \uc2 7/7\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jon Ralston (@RalstonReports) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RalstonReports/status/1591067687798550528?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 11, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.33pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.14pm GMT\par \par \uc2 We do not know all the results of the midterms, but we do know that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will be president until January 2025. So let\u8217\'20\'19s go through a few scenarios about how the outcomes of the still-uncalled House and Senate races will affect his presidency.\par \par \uc2 Democrats seem to be on course to win the Senate again, which is a significant prize for any president. Besides passing laws, the chamber is tasked with confirming the White House\u8217\'20\'19s nominees \u8211\'20\'13 including supreme court justices, federal judges and cabinet secretaries. The last time Republicans controlled the chamber under a Democratic president, \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 , they held up nominations of judges and most famously refused to consider his nominee for a vacant supreme court seat, which ended up being filled by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . Keeping control of the chamber would be majorly helpful to Biden, even if he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t have the House.\par \par \uc2 Congress\u8217\'20\'19s lower chamber has fewer unilateral powers than the Senate, and was always seen as unlikely to remain in Democratic hands after the midterms. That does not mean the party is out of contention there. Several races remain to be called, and a return to power by Biden\u8217\'20\'19s allies is still possible \u8211\'20\'13 though as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/11/11/democrats-house-midterm-elections-00066436"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 this thorough Politico piece makes clear}}}\uc2 , it will be harder for them to pull that off than for the GOP to regain the majority.\par \par \uc2 The most likely outcome at this point appears to be a narrow Democratic majority in the Senate and a small Republican majority in the House, similar to the situation Trump faced from 2019 to 2021. If that happens, expect the House GOP to pass lots of bills that the Senate will ignore, as its Democratic leaders focus on confirming judges and whatever other nominees the White House sends them.\par \par \uc2 If Republicans take both House of Congress \u8211\'20\'13 aided by wins in Nevada and Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s still-to-be-determined Senate elections \u8211\'20\'13 then Biden will probably be using his veto pen repeatedly over the next two years against whatever legislation they manage to pass. But if Democrats somehow defy the odds and pull off a history-making victory in both chambers, Biden will get another shot at accomplishing a laundry list of priorities \u8211\'20\'13 including codifying \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections that previously were guaranteed by Roe v Wade, which the president said would be the first bill he sends to the new Congress.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.21pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.51pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Democrats edge towards Senate majority as counting continues\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. Ballots are still being counted three days after Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s midterms, and it seems like Democrats may have a shot at taking control of the Senate again. While the Associated Press hasn\u8217\'20\'19t called the race, there are signs that senator Mark Kelly has won reelection in Arizona, though the fate of Nevada\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Catherine Cortez Masto\uc2  is still up in the air. If both triumph, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s allies win control of the chamber for another two years. But if only one does, the run-off election for Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s Senate seat set for 6 December will determine control. And that\u8217\'20\'19s to say nothing of the House, where several key races are yet to be called. What a week.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a look at what\u8217\'20\'19s going on today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Democrats worried they could lose the governor\u8217\'20\'19s mansion in blue-state Oregon amid a backlash over crime, homeless and the state\u8217\'20\'19s unpopular incumbent. Their fears were allayed last night when {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AP_Politics/status/1590893483497488385"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Associated Press called }}}\uc2  the race for Democrat \uc2 Tina Kotek\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Far-right Republican Lauren Boebert{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Redistrict/status/1590925908671492096"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is edging closer to reelection}}}\uc2  despite a surprisingly strong challenge from Democrat Adam Frisch.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 In Nevada\u8217\'20\'19s Senate race, Democrat \uc2 Cortez Masto\uc2  is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/s_golonka/status/1590915709131182080?s=20&t=Ucp5xzXiqmkpgm07QnIJAw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 slowly cutting into}}}\uc2  her Republican challenger \uc2 Adam Laxalt\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s lead as mail-in ballots are counted.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020221111eibb001xm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
