\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 US states vote to protect reproductive rights in rebuke to anti- \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  push\b0\par\par\uc2 Poppy Noor in Detroit, Michigan and Gabrielle Canon in Oakland, California \par \uc2 1,242 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 November 2022\par 17:10 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 4\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Vermont, Michigan and California add protections to state constitutions while Kentucky rejects anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  measureUS midterm election results 2022: liveMidterm elections 2022 \u8211\'20\'13 latest live news and updates\par \par \uc2 Voters in multiple US states passed measures to enshrine the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  during Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s midterm elections, or knocked down attempts to further curtail such rights, in a stinging rebuke to the crackdown on reproductive freedoms taking place across the US.\par \par \uc2 In Michigan, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights campaigners declared victory on a ballot initiative looking to secure a constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , meaning the state will now escape the imposition of a 1931 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban that was on the books.\par \par \uc2 The state is the first in the US to fight off a pre-existing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban with a referendum, called Proposal 3, in a move that campaigners across the country see as a possible road map for other states.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CProposal 3\u8217\'20\'19s passage marks an historic victory for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in our state and in our country \u8211\'20\'13 and Michigan has paved the way for future efforts to restore the rights and protections of Roe v Wade nationwide,\u8221\'20\'1D Darci McConnell, the communication director for Reproductive Freedom For All, wrote in a statement, announcing the news after it was called by ABC and NBC.\par \par \uc2 The news broke as other US states too saw victories for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights initiatives.\par \par \uc2 Vermont became the first state in America to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in its state constitution just before Michigan, calling their result on Tuesday after its voters resoundingly backed a ballot initiative by a huge margin. And in California, voters were on track to overwhelmingly pass a measure to enshrine into the state\u8217\'20\'19s constitution the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and contraception.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CVermont voters made history tonight,\u8221\'20\'1D said the Vermont for Reproductive Liberty Ballot Committee, which campaigned for the amendment, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://vtdigger.org/2022/11/08/measure-to-enshrine-abortion-rights-in-vermont-constitution-poised-to-pass/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to local news}}}\uc2 . All votes had not yet been counted at 11pm ET, but the yes campaign was leading by 77% to 22%.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CVermonters support reproductive freedom in all four corners of the state \u8230\'20\'26 and they believe that our reproductive decisions are ours to make without interference from politicians,\u8221\'20\'1D the committee said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 In Vermont, the outcome was always expected, in a New England state so pro-choice that even the Republican governor backed Proposal 5. The proposal, brought by pro-choice advocates, means the constitution now determines that an \u8220\'20\'1Cindividual\u8217\'20\'19s right to personal reproductive autonomy is central to the liberty and dignity to determine one\u8217\'20\'19s own life course\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 California\u8217\'20\'19s Proposition 1, meanwhile, was positioned as a direct response to the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s decision that overturned decades of established access and thrust the country into turmoil. Voters\u8217\'20\'19 decisive support for Prop 1 will further enhance the state\u8217\'20\'19s reputation as a haven for reproductive care just as restrictions \u8211\'20\'13 and political divisions \u8211\'20\'13 deepen across the country.\par \par \uc2 The state\u8217\'20\'19s governor, \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 who won re-election on Tuesday with a large majority \u8211\'20\'13 joined in the celebrations at a Prop 1 rally.\par \par \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  speaking now at Proposition 1 rally, which is poised to pass by a huge margin to enshrine right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in California constitution:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe affirmed we are a true freedom state.\u8221\'20\'1D\u8212\'20\'14 Ashley Zavala (@ZavalaA) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ZavalaA/status/1590204867989340161?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CGovernor Newsom made it clear that he wants California to be visible as a haven for people seeking reproductive healthcare and Proposition 1 is part of that,\u8221\'20\'1D said the constitutional law professor Cary Franklin, who also serves as faculty director of the Center on Reproductive Health, Law, and Policy at the \uc2 University of California Los Angeles\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CIt will get media attention and people will be made more aware that California is a place they can go.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The measure had been expected to easily pass, and analysts said support for reproductive rights could draw even more women and young people to the polls, which could play positively for Democrats in California\u8217\'20\'19s conservative pockets.\par \par \uc2 These wins deliver more blows for Republicans who are increasingly finding that, when put to a vote, Americans frequently do not agree with a sweeping agenda to dismantle \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 So far, the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement has relied on judges, state houses and Republican lawmakers to curtail reproductive rights.\par \par \uc2 But since the supreme court dismantled the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  on 24 June, pro-choice advocates are increasingly looking to ballot initiatives as a way of shoring up rights. The anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement suffered a huge blow over the summer when Kansas \u8211\'20\'13 a usually reliably red state \u8211\'20\'13 slammed down a proposal brought by the Republicans, looking to confirm there was no right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the state constitution.\par \par \uc2 In Michigan the mood was already jubilant at the yes campaign\u8217\'20\'19s watch party before they called the result, with voters screaming loudly, banging on tables and whooping in support of local voters, doctors and speakers from the American Civil Liberties Union and Planned Parenthood.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy name is Nicholas, and I live in Ingham county,\u8221\'20\'1D one campaigner took to the stage to say. Speaking about him and his girlfriend, he added: \u8220\'20\'1CWe knocked on over 1,500 doors and walked over a hundred miles, talking to neighbors who \u8211\'20\'13 like the rest of us here \u8211\'20\'13 agree this is a fundamental right,\u8221\'20\'1D to screams and cheers.\par \par \uc2 Nicole Wells Stallworth, executive director at Planned Parenthood Advocates of Michigan later added: \u8220\'20\'1CWe are living in a time like no other. The \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  did something they have never done: They reversed Roe. They tried it. And as such, we needed a campaign like none other. This campaign turned out to be just that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The biggest surprise was in Kentucky, where voters rejected a ballot measure aimed at denying any constitutional protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . That referendum was brought by a Republican-dominated legislature expecting a win, who earlier this year imposed a near-total ban on abortions.\par \par \uc2 The key sponsor of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban and the ballot proposal, former congressman Joe Fischer, was running for a judicial seat on Kentucky\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court this election \u8211\'20\'13 which he has not won.\par \par \uc2 For the meantime, Kentucky\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban will remain in place. But Fischer\u8217\'20\'19s loss is more good news for pro-choice campaigners: as the ban is being challenged in the state supreme court on 15 November. And although judges are generally not supposed to be swayed by public opinion, the victory will certainly, in theory, make it harder for the sweeping ban to stand up in court.\par \par \uc2 Madeline Dyer, a former counselor for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  patients at one of the two remaining clinics in Kentucky, EMW Women\u8217\'20\'19s Surgical Center, which has had its doors shuttered since 24 June, said it was a relief to finally have the result over with.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a little surreal, I\u8217\'20\'19ve been so consumed by worrying about this amendment for months,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CBut I\u8217\'20\'19m elated Kentuckians used their voice and showed politicians that they don\u8217\'20\'19t want a ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . We\u8217\'20\'19re showing we care for each other. It\u8217\'20\'19s such a heart-warming reassurance \u8211\'20\'13 because when it really comes down to it, it\u8217\'20\'19s just not popular, to have an outright ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Rachel Sweet of Protect Kentucky Access said the outcome was a \u8220\'20\'1Chistoric win\u8221\'20\'1D against \u8220\'20\'1Cgovernment overreach\u8221\'20\'1D into the personal medical decisions of Kentuckians.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020221109eib9000p2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
