\par\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 American voters just sent a crystal-clear message: they believe in  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights\b0\par\par\uc2 Jill Filipovic \par \uc2 1,044 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 November 2022\par 18:41 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights voters delivered several key elections for Democrats. Now Democrats had better deliver for them\par \par \uc2 The 2022 midterm elections were not the \u8220\'20\'1Cred wave\u8221\'20\'1D of Republican dreams. They didn\u8217\'20\'19t end up being a rebuke to the Biden presidency, a message about inflation or a protest against perceived crime rates.\par \par \uc2 The only issue voters sent a clear message on? \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Voters who came out to support reproductive rights seem to be one of the chief reasons Democrats weren\u8217\'20\'19t absolutely routed. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights voters delivered several key elections for Democrats. And now, Democrats had better deliver for them.\par \par \uc2 There are still some races outstanding, including important Senate battles in Georgia, Arizona and Nevada and a smattering of House races. But early numbers tell an important and definitive story: the Democratic base {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://catalist.us/election-day-2022/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 showed up}}}\uc2  in numbers that are wildly uncommon in a midterm election, particularly from a party that already controls Congress and the White House. Turnout this year surpassed the 2018 midterms, when Democrats surged to the polls to signal their disgust with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . And exit polling suggests that these Democratic voters were overwhelmingly motivated by \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with 76% of Democrats listing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as their top issue, according to CNN {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/election/2022/exit-polls/national-results/house/0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 polling}}}\uc2 . And voters generally \u8211\'20\'13 not just Democrats \u8211\'20\'13 said that they trusted Democrats over Republicans to handle \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights supporters encouraged Democrats to prioritize \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in their campaigns, but that strategy came with its fair share of detractors. Senator Bernie Sanders wrote in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/commentisfree/2022/oct/10/democrats-midterms-victory-economy-bernie-sanders"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 these pages}}}\uc2  that focusing on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  over inflation and the economy was a mistake. (Democrats, in their defense, did overwhelmingly make their case about the economy, too; they just emphasized \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights more forcefully than at any point in my living memory.) It would appear that detractors got it wrong, and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was indeed a winning strategy.\par \par \uc2 The Democratic line has been \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is on the ballot.\u8221\'20\'1D And in four states, it literally was: voters in California, Michigan and Vermont were asked to decide whether to enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights into their state constitutions; voters in Kentucky were asked to decide whether \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights should not be protected by their state constitution.\par \par \uc2 Voters in all four states voted for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions, echoing the outcome of a ballot measure earlier this year in Kansas.\par \par \uc2 This is an unmistakable pattern: when voters are given the chance to decide whether the state should outlaw \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  or if the choice should be left to a woman and her doctor, they tell the state to butt out. Even in conservative strongholds, state legislatures appear to be far more conservative on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  than the voters they purport to represent.\par \par \uc2 These \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights voters have also cast their ballots for Democrats more broadly. Candidates in several tight races, including in Michigan and Pennsylvania, emphasized that they would protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights \u8211\'20\'13 and those candidates won, bringing down-ballot victories for state legislators with them.\par \par \uc2 In Pennsylvania, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was the number-one issue for voters, according to NBC {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2022-election/live-blog/elections-2022-live-updates-rcna55757#rcrd6769"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 exit polling}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 and 78% of voters who said \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was their main issue cast their ballots for Democrat \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2 . Democrat Josh Shapiro also won against arch-conservative \uc2 Doug Mastriano\uc2  in Pennsylvania\u8217\'20\'19s gubernatorial race. And while votes are still being tallied, Democrats seem to have done {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/StephenJ_Caruso/status/1590322078989058048"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 surprisingly well}}}\uc2  in races for seats in the Pennsylvania state legislature.\par \par \uc2 In Michigan, voters sent a resounding message that they want \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights enshrined into the state constitution. They also re-elected \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2 , who ran on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in a state that has been engulfed in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.usnews.com/news/elections/articles/2022-11-09/gretchen-whitmer-wins-michigan-governors-race-in-latest-test-for-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 legal battles}}}\uc2  over the status of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . And they {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bridgemi.com/michigan-government/huge-wins-democrats-theyre-poised-retake-michigan-legislature"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 flipped the state legislature}}}\uc2 , handing Democrats control of all three chambers for the first time in nearly four decades.\par \par \uc2 These voters are all clear: they turned out not just to put Democrats in power generally, but in support of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights specifically.\par \par \uc2 Now these voters will want results. Yes, delivering on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights may be tough with a divided House and Senate \u8211\'20\'13 especially if Republicans gain control of one or both chambers. But Democrats were never under the impression that they could achieve overwhelming victory. They still promised pro-choice voters that if they turned out, Democrats would stand up for them. Now they have to make good on that promise, even if it\u8217\'20\'19s tough.\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration has been frustratingly tepid on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, and it\u8217\'20\'19s beyond time for Democrats at all levels to get creative to secure \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights however they can. Elizabeth Warren and \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2  have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vox.com/2022/6/27/23185624/biden-abortion-rights-executive-actions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 suggested}}}\uc2 , for example, that Biden could use his executive powers to allow \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics to open on federally owned lands, including military bases.\par \par \uc2 Congress could affirm the basic rights of all Americans to travel for medical care \u8211\'20\'13 which could help to stave off conservative efforts to criminalize those who help women cross state borders for abortions \u8211\'20\'13 and pass a bill protecting women and their loved ones from prosecution for pregnancy termination. (In my ideal world, Congress would pass a bill protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights much more broadly, but that path will become impossible if Republicans gain power.) The FDA could treat \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -inducing medications like any other prescription drug and evaluate them on safety and efficacy rather than politics \u8211\'20\'13 which, frustratingly, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/11/01/health/fda-preventive-medication-abortion/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 remains the case}}}\uc2  even with a Biden administration in the White House. And if Democrats do somehow manage to maintain control of Congress, Biden and the Democratic party truly have no excuse to not pass a bill enshrining \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights into law nationwide.\par \par \uc2 The American people sent a loud message yesterday: we are a pro-choice nation, and we want the government out of our most intimate reproductive decisions. Republicans should listen, and realize that their party\u8217\'20\'19s position \u8211\'20\'13 that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be outlawed in nearly all cases \u8211\'20\'13 represents but a tiny minority of Americans; if they want to stay competitive, they should back off from their extremist positions.\par \par \uc2 And Democrats should realize that these pro-choice voters just saved many of their hides, and recently elected Democratic politicians now owe them more than pro-choice platitudes. They owe what they promised: \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Jill Filipovic is the author of OK Boomer, Let\u8217\'20\'19s Talk\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020221110eiba0038x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
