\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Oregon could see first Republican governor in 40 years as polls tilt away from Democrats\b0\par\par\uc2 Hallie Golden \par \uc2 1,045 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 November 2022\par 11:51 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Independent hopeful with bipartisan support, along with funds from state\u8217\'20\'19s richest man, could deliver victory to Christine DrazanMidterm elections 2022 \u8211\'20\'13 latest live news and updates\par \par \uc2 For the first time in more than 40 years, a Republican could win the governor\u8217\'20\'19s seat in Oregon, breaching the seemingly solid Democratic line of states running along the Pacific coastline of the US.\par \par \uc2 The tight race between the former Oregon house speaker \uc2 Tina Kotek\uc2 , a Democrat, and former Oregon house minority leader Christine Drazan, a Republican, which in the latest {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/polls/governor/2022/oregon/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 polling}}}\uc2  showed Drazan with a hairline lead, indicates a rebuff of the current term-limited liberal governor, \uc2 Kate Brown\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Brown has one of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://morningconsult.com/2022/10/11/whitmers-approval-ticks-up-in-michigan-ahead-of-midterms/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lowest approval ratings}}}\uc2  of any governor in the country amid brewing concern over how state leadership has handled everything from the pandemic to homelessness.\par \par \uc2 But it\u8217\'20\'19s a third-party candidate with support from both Republicans and Democrats, along with contributions from the richest man in the state, that has truly set a Republican on a path toward possible victory.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDemocrats are pretty good at running a red-blue race in Oregon \u8230\'20\'26 But the dynamics of a three-way race have really kind of thrown that playbook out the window,\u8221\'20\'1D said Jake Weigler, a progressive political strategist in Oregon not involved in the race.\par \par \uc2 Betsy Johnson, who was a moderate Democrat while serving as a state senator and now is running as an independent, has been forecast to receive as much as 14% of the vote. Outside of independent voters, 17% of Democrats plan to vote for her, while only 9% of Republicans do, according to an Emerson College Polling {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://emersoncollegepolling.com/oregon-2022-republican-christine-drazan-with-two-point-lead-over-democrat-tina-kotek-for-governorship-sen-wyden-holds-19-point-lead-in-re-election-bid/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 survey released}}}\uc2  earlier this month.\par \par \uc2 Rebecca Tweed, a Republican strategist in Oregon with no connection to the governor\u8217\'20\'19s race, said it will be this subset of voters to watch come election day.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ll have to see if any of those voters that got pulled towards Betsy end up going back into their corners of the Democratic and Republican parties,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 But it could also come down to what independent voters decide to do next month.\par \par \uc2 Ariya Ahrary, who has lived in Oregon since 2007, said she was initially very happy to see the independent candidate on the ballot. But after taking a closer look at each candidate\u8217\'20\'19s policies, she said she now will probably vote for Kotek in hopes that she will help change the direction of the state.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe do want actual real change instead of just all talk. Hopefully that happens, that it\u8217\'20\'19s not just all talk, that it\u8217\'20\'19s actual action,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 By far Johnson\u8217\'20\'19s largest single financial contribution has come from \uc2 Phil Knight\uc2 , co-founder of \uc2 Nike\uc2 . Altogether, he has sent $3.75m to Johnson\u8217\'20\'19s campaign since January, and then earlier this month sent $1.5m to Drazan. In an interview with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/10/15/us/politics/kotek-drazan-oregon-governor.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the New York Times}}}\uc2  earlier this month, he said he would do anything to keep Kotek out of the governor\u8217\'20\'19s seat.\par \par \uc2 The gubernatorial race projections in a state where \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  won by 16 points just two years ago have been a shock to many across the nation. They have prompted national political figures to visit the Pacific north-west hoping to drum up support for their candidates.\par \par \uc2 On Saturday, Biden spoke at an event in Portland, where he highlighted the increasingly important role governors play in policy implementation, while praising Kotek\u8217\'20\'19s leadership and bravery.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19re a progressive state. You\u8217\'20\'19re a state that\u8217\'20\'19s always been ahead of the curve. Stay ahead of the curve, and elect Tina,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Virginia\u8217\'20\'19s governor, Glenn Youngkin, a rising Republican star, spoke at a rally for Drazan on Tuesday, while Senator Elizabeth Warren, a Democrat from Massachusetts, attended an event for Kotek this weekend.\par \par \uc2 Kotek, Drazan and Johnson recently came together for the race\u8217\'20\'19s final televised debate. The largely mild-mannered occasion was punctuated by sharp criticisms hurled between Drazan, Johnson and their Democratic rival, including over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Following the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s overturning of Roe v Wade earlier this year, Oregon has positioned itself as a safe haven for abortions. Johnson, a former Planned Parenthood board member, described herself as pro-choice. Kotek, who was endorsed by Planned Parenthood Pac of Oregon and helped with the legislative effort to codify \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access into state law in 2017, said she is a strong supporter of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, including potentially using taxpayer money to support that type of care. She accused Drazan of posing a threat to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in the state.\par \par \uc2 Drazan rebutted by saying while she wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t use taxpayer funds to support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the practice would remain legal. \u8220\'20\'1CIt gets more and more startling to me the extent to which \uc2 Tina Kotek\uc2  will lie to voters,\u8221\'20\'1D she said\par \par \uc2 Another key issue the candidates responded to during the debate was the state\u8217\'20\'19s response to the pandemic when it came to closing schools. Drazan accused both Governor Brown and Kotek of throwing \u8220\'20\'1Cour kids under the bus\u8221\'20\'1D, while Johnson said: \u8220\'20\'1CThe single worst thing we did during Covid was to shut kids out of the classroom.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Kotek, who agreed that students were kept out of the classroom too long, said it was in fact her Republican opponent who did the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.oregon.gov/ode/studentsuccess/Pages/default.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 throwing by voting against }}}\uc2  a multibillion-dollar education bill in 2019.\par \par \uc2 But it was a question from a resident of Wilsonville, a city about 17 miles south of Portland, that spotlighted an issue at the center of this race: \u8220\'20\'1CSince you\u8217\'20\'19ve been a lifelong Democrat, how do you square yourself with knowing that your current efforts will probably cost Democrats the governorship for the state?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Johnson told the audience that she joined the race because she sees herself as the best candidate to lead a state that has \u8220\'20\'1Cgone off the rails\u8221\'20\'1D, and that she has no plan to drop out.\par \par \uc2 She said: \u8220\'20\'1CI believe sports oddsmakers don\u8217\'20\'19t win games. Polls don\u8217\'20\'19t predict elections. I\u8217\'20\'19ve seen enough fourth-quarter finishes to know that it\u8217\'20\'19s not over until it\u8217\'20\'19s over. And I\u8217\'20\'19m in this race until the absolute end.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020221109eib900337\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
