\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  vote: here are the US states voting on a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to choose\b0\par\par\uc2 Poppy Noor \par \uc2 817 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 November 2022\par 11:52 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Voters in five states will dramatically shape \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies for millions of womenUS midterm election results 2022: liveMidterm elections 2022 \u8211\'20\'13 latest live news and updatesWhen will we know who won US midterm races \u8212\'20\'14 and what to expect\par \par \uc2 When the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturned {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/06/abortion-clinics-us-roe-v-wade-study"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2  in June, it put the matter of regulating \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  entirely in the hands of the states. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/11/us-midterms-congress-senate-house-races-to-watch"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 This November}}}\uc2 , voters will weigh in on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/06/us-midterm-elections-explainer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ballot initiatives}}}\uc2  that will decide the future of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/sep/23/arizona-abortion-ban-clinics-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  in five of those states: California, Kentucky, Michigan, Montana and Vermont.\par \par \uc2 Reproductive rights proponents are hoping to replicate their historic win in Kansas, where a reliably conservative state successfully defeated an anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ballot initiative in August.\par \par \uc2 Taken together, this is the highest number of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related referendums up for consideration in a single year, and the most powerful bellwether of the national fallout from the supreme court decision.\par \par \uc2 Michigan\par \par \uc2 In Michigan, a battle for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights has centered around whether a 1931 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, currently blocked, can be enforced. The ballot initiative this November asks voters to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the state constitution; if it fails, the 1931 ban could go into effect.\par \par \uc2 Michiganders are largely in support of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. Analysis suggests 55% of voters believe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be mostly legal, compared with 39% who believe it should be mostly illegal. Other polling suggests 64% of Michiganders {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.freep.com/restricted/?return=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.freep.com%2Fstory%2Fnews%2Fpolitics%2Felections%2F2022%2F09%2F22%2Fmichigan-abortion-proposal-has-strong-support-poll-shows%2F69507400007%2F"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 support}}}\uc2  adding a constitutional protection for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  through the ballot initiative.\par \par \uc2 Kentucky\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is already banned in Kentucky through a \u8220\'20\'1Ctrigger ban\u8221\'20\'1D from 2019 that came into effect immediately after Roe fell. But with legal challenges seeking to overturn the ban, opponents want to tighten their grip.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 ACLU\uc2  will argue in court on 15 November, after the midterms are over, that Kentucky\u8217\'20\'19s constitution protects \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  advocates are hoping to get ahead of that case with the ballot measure asking Kentucky voters to vote yes on language reading, \u8220\'20\'1Cnothing in this constitution shall be construed to secure or protect a right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  or require the funding of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 While Kentucky is a squarely red state, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://itunes.apple.com/gb/app/the-guardian/id409128287?mt=8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 p}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.prochoiceamerica.org/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/PPP-Kentucky-polling-memo-10.23.19.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 olling}}}\uc2  from 2019 by a group associated with progressive causes shows that 59% of Kentucky voters believe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be legal, including 71% of Democrats, 62% of independents and 45% of Republicans. However, the picture is mixed: a \uc2 Pew Research\uc2  poll from 2014 showed 57% of adults in Kentucky believe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be illegal in most cases.\par \par \uc2 California\par \par \uc2 The California initiative, brought by \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights groups, would expand \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and other reproductive healthcare access if it passes. It would write \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections into the state constitution, along with a right to contraception \u8211\'20\'13 something reproductive rights advocates worry could be a future target for conservatives. The wording in the ballot doesn\u8217\'20\'19t prohibit \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after fetal viability, while current state law does \u8211\'20\'13 meaning, if it passes, pregnant people would have expanded options if needed later in pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Considering the political makeup of California \u8211\'20\'13 where Democrats outnumber Republicans three to one in the state assembly and the senate \u8211\'20\'13 most people are expecting a win for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights come November. That\u8217\'20\'19s backed up by a recent poll showing a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nymag.com/intelligencer/2022/08/focus-on-abortion-rights-can-help-blue-state-democrats-too.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 71-18 margin}}}\uc2  for those in favor of the amendment among registered voters in California, including 35% of Republicans.\par \par \uc2 Vermont\par \par \uc2 In Vermont, pro-choice advocates are looking to shore up existing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections with a ballot initiative that, if it passes, would add a line to the state\u8217\'20\'19s constitution, reading:\par \par \uc2 [A]n individual\u8217\'20\'19s right to personal reproductive autonomy is central to the liberty and dignity to determine one\u8217\'20\'19s own life course and shall not be denied or infringed unless justified by a compelling state interest achieved by the least restrictive means\par \par \uc2 Similar to California\u8217\'20\'19s bill, a win would make anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws difficult to pass in the state. Voters have historically rejected anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ballot initiatives brought in the state.\par \par \uc2 Experts expect the initiative {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewtrusts.org/en/research-and-analysis/blogs/stateline/2022/08/11/abortion-ballot-measures-seen-as-critical-but-tricky-strategy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will pass}}}\uc2 , in a state so pro-choice that even the Republican governor supports the amendment. But some campaigners still urge caution, in part because voters will be navigating a new, unfamiliar vote-by-mail system.\par \par \uc2 Montana\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in Montana are currently protected under the constitution. Republicans have brought a confusingly worded ballot measure that would bring harsh penalties on doctors in the cases of \u8220\'20\'1Cborn alive infants\u8221\'20\'1D, including criminal penalties and $50,000 (\u163\'00\'A345,032) fines.\par \par \uc2 Supporters of the referendum say the proposed Born Alive Infant Protection Act is meant to prevent the killing of infants outside the womb after failed abortions. That is already illegal.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights proponents worry that passage would have a chilling affect on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care. Experts say odds of passage are low, pointing towards analysis showing Montanans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/05/04/upshot/polling-abortion-states.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 favor \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  being mostly legal}}}\uc2  by a 10% margin.\par \par \uc2 Associated Press contributed reporting\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020221110eiba0038q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
