\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Biden hails \u8216\'20\'18good day for democracy\u8217\'20\'19 as Democrats defy midterm expectations\b0\par\par\uc2 Joan E Greve and David Smith in Washington, and Sam Levin in Los Angeles \par \uc2 1,401 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 November 2022\par 14:32 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 1\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 President says \u8216\'20\'18giant red wave didn\u8217\'20\'19t happen\u8217\'20\'19 as Senate still in balance and race for House control much closer than predictedUS midterm election results 2022: live\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  hailed \u8220\'20\'1Ca good day\u8221\'20\'1D for democracy after Democrats defied history and outperformed expectations in America\u8217\'20\'19s midterm elections, leaving control of Congress on a knife-edge.\par \par \uc2 With ballots still being counted, Democrats were hopeful about holding the Senate, though the outcome of the tight races in Arizona and Nevada was still uncertain on Wednesday evening and another key race in Georgia was headed to a runoff. Democrats need to win two of those seats to maintain Senate control.\par \par \uc2 Republicans, meanwhile, felt they were on course to win the House \u8211\'20\'13 but by a much narrower margin than widely predicted.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe had an election yesterday \u8211\'20\'13 it was a good day, I think, for democracy,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden told reporters at the White House. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd I think it was a good day for America.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The president added: \u8220\'20\'1CWhile the press and the pundits are predicting a giant red wave, it didn\u8217\'20\'19t happen \u8230\'20\'26 Democrats had a strong night.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden looked poised for the best midterm performance by an incumbent president\u8217\'20\'19s party since \uc2 George W Bush\uc2  in 2002. Perhaps {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/09/trump-desantis-election-2024-florida"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the biggest loser}}}\uc2  of the night was his predecessor, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , as many of his handpicked candidates slumped to defeat, throwing fresh doubt over his political future.\par \par \uc2 The party that controls the White House typically loses seats in midterm elections and opinion polls had shown broad dissatisfaction with Biden and the economy. The conditions appeared ripe for a so-called Republican \u8220\'20\'1Cred wave\u8221\'20\'1D that could have drowned the president\u8217\'20\'19s legislative agenda.\par \par \uc2 But it {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/08/republicans-midterm-election-poor-preformance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 did not turn out that way}}}\uc2  and a day that had been expected to dawn with Democratic soul-searching was instead filled with Republican finger-pointing and recriminations.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Republican party needs to do a really deep introspection look in the mirror right now because this is an absolute disaster,\u8221\'20\'1D Marc Thiessen, a former chief speechwriter for Bush, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1590233789137289218?s=20&t=c3kPHw8lIzyjx3S7v-e-lw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told Fox News}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The results of the most hotly contested Senate races were giving many Republicans heartburn. Biden campaigned hard in Pennsylvania, the state of his birth, and was rewarded when \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2 , the lieutenant governor who suffered a stroke during the campaign, defeated Mehmet Oz, a celebrity doctor endorsed by Trump.\par \par \uc2 Senator Mark Kelly maintained a lead over the Republican Blake Masters in Arizona, though Kelly\u8217\'20\'19s colleague from Nevada, \uc2 Catherine Cortez Masto\uc2 , had fallen behind. But hundreds of thousands of ballots remain uncounted in those races, and election officials have warned it could take days to determine the winners.\par \par \uc2 In Georgia, Senator \uc2 Raphael Warnock\uc2 , a pastor, and Republican challenger \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2 , a former American football star, are headed to a 6 December runoff, a race that could determine control of the chamber. The Alaska Senate race was also still too close to call, but the top two candidates are both Republicans.\par \par \uc2 Republicans had been heavily favoured to take the House and did claim a major prize, winning the New York seat of \uc2 Sean Patrick Maloney\uc2 , the head of the Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 campaign arm.\par \par \uc2 But the widespread gains many forecasters predicted failed to materialise. Vulnerable Democrats such as \uc2 Abigail Spanberger\uc2  of Virginia and \uc2 Elissa Slotkin\uc2  of Michigan held on, keeping the party\u8217\'20\'19s hopes of House control alive hours after polls closed.\par \par \uc2 It may be days before the House results are clear, with roughly 30 critical races {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2022/nov/08/midterm-election-results-live-2022-map-us-midterms-latest-winners-seats-congress"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 still pending}}}\uc2 , including several key battles in California; although the state is overall Democratic, there are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/nov/09/midterm-elections-2022-results-senate-house-us-democrats-republicans-live-updates-latest-news?page=with:block-636c33ba8f08f8fb6d4d644a#block-636c33ba8f08f8fb6d4d644a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 five competitive races}}}\uc2  where votes are still being counted and where party affiliation could flip.\par \par \uc2 The House speaker, \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 , expressed optimism in the early hours of Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhile many races remain too close to call, it is clear that House Democratic members and candidates are strongly outperforming expectations across the country,\u8221\'20\'1D Pelosi said. \u8220\'20\'1CAs states continue to tabulate the final results, every vote must be counted as cast.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Kevin McCarthy, the Republican minority leader, appeared at 1.59am, much later than expected, at an event in Washington. He {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.foxnews.com/video/6315206949112"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 declared}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CIt is clear we are going to take the House back.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 McCarthy later announced his bid to become speaker if Republicans do win the House. But with a wafer-thin majority, he could face political headaches as pro-Trump extremists seek to dominate the agenda.\par \par \uc2 Biden said he would speak to McCarthy later in the day. He told reporters: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m prepared to work with my Republican colleagues. The American people have made clear, I think, that they expect the Republicans to be prepared to work with me as well.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The results also brought {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/nov/09/vermont-abortion-vote-first-us-state-constitution"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 welcome news}}}\uc2  for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights supporters devastated by the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s reversal of Roe v Wade in June. California, Vermont and Michigan voted to strengthen \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights into their constitutions, while conservative states Kentucky and Montana rejected measures to restrict access to the procedure.\par \par \uc2 Early exit polls suggested \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights had been a motivating factor for many voters, despite predictions the issue would be overshadowed by economic concerns. One exit poll {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/election/2022/exit-polls/national-results/house"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 conducted by Edison Research}}}\uc2  found that 27% of voters named \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as their top priority, compared to 31% who said the same of inflation.\par \par \uc2 Threats to democracy also appeared to be weighing heavily on voters\u8217\'20\'19 minds. According to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/2022-midterm-elections-abortion-biden-inflation-cf4dffe87a7c2fd1bdd58df0346e15dc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 AP VoteCast}}}\uc2 , 44% said the future of democracy was their primary consideration, making it the second-most common response behind inflation.\par \par \uc2 Overall, the night shaped up poorly for election deniers and candidates endorsed by Trump. Although {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/interactive/2022/election-deniers-midterms/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dozens of incumbents}}}\uc2  who challenged the 2020 presidential result did win, election deniers in key gubernatorial and secretary of state races were on track for defeat.\par \par \uc2 Democrats won governors\u8217\'20\'19 races in Michigan, Wisconsin and Pennsylvania, crucial battlegrounds in recent presidential elections likely to be pivotal again in 2024. Many saw it as yet another rebuke of Trump and his \u8220\'20\'1CMake America great again\u8221\'20\'1D (Maga) movement following losses in 2018 and 2020.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.indivisible.org/ezra-levin-0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ezra Levin}}}\uc2 , co-founder and co-executive director of Indivisible, said: \u8220\'20\'1CThis was supposed to be Maga\u8217\'20\'19s triumphant night. It turned into a massive embarrassment. While we\u8217\'20\'19re still awaiting final results, the overall picture is clear: Democrats massively performed the midterm fundamentals. Voters don\u8217\'20\'19t like anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  zealots. Voters don\u8217\'20\'19t like election deniers. Voters don\u8217\'20\'19t like Trump. And voters don\u8217\'20\'19t like Maga.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 As Trump-endorsed candidates fell, others downplayed their connection to the former president. JD Vance, who won the Ohio Republican Senate primary largely thanks to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s endorsement, did not mention his name while delivering a victory speech on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Today's cover: \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  shows he\u8217\'20\'19s future of the GOP {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Ja9rO579r4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/Ja9rO579r4}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/9Px1KBH1MP"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/9Px1KBH1MP}}}\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 New York Post (@nypost) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/nypost/status/1590329298942103552?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 The results reportedly infuriated Trump, who is expected to announce another presidential campaign as early as next week. Even more worrisome for him, the Florida governor, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , frequently named as a potential presidential candidate, easily cruised to re-election.\par \par \uc2 DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s 19-point victory in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s home state \u8211\'20\'13 notably carrying largely Latino counties such as Miami-Dade and Osceola \u8211\'20\'13 only intensified chatter about 2024.\par \par \uc2 In a potential sign of trouble for Trump, the New York Post, which the former president has been known to read avidly, put a photo of DeSantis on its cover. \u8220\'20\'1CDeFuture\u8221\'20\'1D, the cover\u8217\'20\'19s headline read. \u8220\'20\'1CYoung GOP star DeSantis romps to victory in Florida.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The glowing coverage is sure to irritate Trump, who is famous for lashing out against fellow Republicans who steal the spotlight and who last week branded the governor \u8220\'20\'1CRon DeSanctimonious\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In a preview of a potentially bloody primary, Trump told Fox News: \u8220\'20\'1CI think if he runs, he could hurt himself very badly. I really believe he could hurt himself badly. I would tell you things about him that won\u8217\'20\'19t be very flattering \u8211\'20\'13 I know more about him than anybody \u8211\'20\'13 other than, perhaps, his wife.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden, meanwhile, suggested that he is likely to make a final decision on running early next year with input from his wife, Jill Biden.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur intention is to run again,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, in the White House state dining room. \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s been our intention, regardless of what the outcome of this election was.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020221109eib9002e8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
