\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Future of Congress hangs in balance as many races still too close to call\b0\par\par\uc2 Joan E Greve, Lauren Gambino in Washington, Lois Beckett in Los Angeles; Chris McGreal in Columbus, Ohio and Miranda Bryant \par \uc2 1,555 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 November 2022\par 13:08 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 18\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Democrats have reason for cautious optimism, but Republicans still have narrow advantage in battle for HouseUS midterm election results 2022: liveUS midterm elections 2022 \u8211\'20\'13 latest live news updates\par \par \uc2 Republicans were leading the race for the House of Representatives on Wednesday, but Democrats had some cause for optimism after a midterms \u8220\'20\'1Cred wave\u8221\'20\'1D failed to materialise and the battle for the Senate, centered on Nevada and Georgia, remained neck and neck.\par \par \uc2 Americans went to the polls on Tuesday to determine control of the \uc2 US Congress\uc2  for the next two years, and election forecasts had favored Republicans in the final days of campaigning. The president\u8217\'20\'19s party typically loses seats in the midterms, and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s low approval rating, combined with concerns about the state of the US economy, had lowered Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 expectations.\par \par \uc2 But some key races were tilting toward Democrats in the final hours of Tuesday night, and the party took one of the biggest prizes of the night, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/09/john-fetterman-wins-pennsylvania-senate-race"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ferociously contested Senate race in Pennsylvania}}}\uc2  between Mehmet Oz, a \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 -backed Republican, and the Democrat \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Fetterman, who had been battling to assure voters he was fit for office after having a stroke, flipped the Republican seat in Pennsylvania into Democratic control. \u8220\'20\'1CWe held the line,\u8221\'20\'1D a teary Fetterman said, declaring victory in a speech to supporters on Wednesday morning.\par \par \uc2 In an early sign that the party was poised to stave off staggering losses in the House, Democrats won two of three House races in Virginia and tempered Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 boasts of an election day blowout. \uc2 Jennifer Wexton\uc2  and \uc2 Abigail Spanberger\uc2  fended off Republican challengers, though \uc2 Elaine Luria\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 a member of the House select committee investigating the January 6 insurrection \u8211\'20\'13 conceded to her opponent, the Republican Jen Kiggans.\par \par \uc2 With many races still too close to call, control of Congress \u8211\'20\'13 and the future of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s agenda \u8211\'20\'13 hung in the balance. Outcomes of some closely contested elections are not expected for several days, or even weeks. But the early results already returned one certainty: the election was not unfolding as Republicans had hoped.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDefinitely not a Republican wave, that\u8217\'20\'19s for darn sure,\u8221\'20\'1D Senator \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2 , a Republican from South Carolina, told MSNBC as results filtered in on Tuesday night.\par \par \uc2 In a statement, the House speaker, \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 , said it was \u8220\'20\'1Cclear that House Democratic members and candidates are strongly outperforming expectations across the country\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Republicans were still favored to regain control of the House, in part thanks to a favorable redistricting season after the 2020 census. The party has flipped at least three seats in Florida, where state legislators redrew the congressional map to give Republicans a significant advantage. And in usually blue New York, the congressman \uc2 Sean Patrick Maloney\uc2 , the chair of the Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 House campaign arm, charged with protecting the party\u8217\'20\'19s narrow majority this cycle, appeared unlikely to win re-election in his newly drawn district.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is clear that we are gonna take the House back,\u8221\'20\'1D Kevin McCarthy, the Republican House leader who hopes to replace Pelosi as speaker if his party wins control of the chamber, told supporters in Washington.\par \par \uc2 The fight for the Senate, currently split 50-50, was extremely tight, with several races too close to call in the early hours of Wednesday. The Georgia senator \uc2 Raphael Warnock\uc2  was running neck and neck with the Republican \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2 , elevating the possibility of a runoff next month if neither candidate can capture 50% of the vote. In the west, \uc2 Catherine Cortez Masto\uc2  of Nevada and her Republican opponent \uc2 Adam Laxalt\uc2 , who in the early hours of the morning was more than two points ahead, both said they did not expect results in their tightly contested race until later in the week. In Arizona, the Democratic incumbent Mark Kelly led the Republican Blake Masters.\par \par \uc2 JD Vance, the Trump-backed author of the bestselling book Hillbilly Elegy, defeated the Democratic congressman \uc2 Tim Ryan\uc2  in an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/08/jd-vance-wins-ohio-senate-race-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unexpectedly close contest for Ohio\u8217\'20\'19s open Senate seat}}}\uc2 , while the Republican \uc2 Ted Budd\uc2  beat back a spirited challenge from the Democrat Cheri Beasley for an open Senate seat in North Carolina.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/09/donald-trump-mar-a-lago-midterms-2022"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump spent election day}}}\uc2  sharing unfounded claims about ballots on Truth Social and calling on followers to \u8220\'20\'1Cprotest\u8221\'20\'1D, while the former president was accused by some of being responsible for the apparent lack of a red wave.\par \par \uc2 Fox News, traditionally a Trump ally, published a story claiming he was \u8220\'20\'1Cblasted across [the] media spectrum\u8221\'20\'1D, and claims that he was the night\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cbiggest loser\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The successes of the Democratic senators Michael Bennet of Colorado and \uc2 Maggie Hassan\uc2 , who were considered endangered in the event of a Republican blowout, gave the party hopes of maintaining control of the upper chamber.\par \par \uc2 The final results, which will determine control of Congress for the remainder of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s first term as president and could further constrain his legislative agenda, may take weeks in some closely fought Senate races. Delayed results are likely to fuel legal challenges and conspiracy theories about vote-rigging, particularly if the remaining seats determine control of the Senate.\par \par \uc2 There were hiccups at some battleground states at polling places on Tuesday, escalating fears that election deniers would use the isolated incidents to raise baseless doubts about the legitimacy of the results. Thirty-five Senate seats and all 435 House of Representatives seats were on the ballot, giving Republicans an opportunity to drastically change the makeup of Congress. Opinion polls had suggested that support for Democrats had fallen in recent weeks amid growing voter concern about high inflation and crime, two issues on which Republicans are seen as stronger.\par \par \uc2 According to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/2022-midterm-elections-abortion-biden-inflation-cf4dffe87a7c2fd1bdd58df0346e15dc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 AP VoteCast}}}\uc2 , half of voters say inflation factored significantly in their midterm decisions, a potentially ominous sign for Democratic prospects. But in more encouraging news for Democrats, a similarly large share of voters \u8211\'20\'13 44% \u8211\'20\'13 said their primary concern was the future of democracy, a theme that Biden and his party members emphasized in their final days of campaigning.\par \par \uc2 The president said American democracy was on the line in the midterms in the face of numerous challenges, from gerrymandering and voter suppression to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s false claims about vote-rigging.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur lifetimes are going to be shaped by what happens the next year to three years,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said at a final campaign rally in Maryland on Monday. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s going to shape what the next couple decades look like.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Many Democratic candidates have also focused strongly on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/nov/09/vermont-abortion-vote-first-us-state-constitution"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 protecting \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights}}}\uc2  in the wake of the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s reversal of Roe v Wade earlier this year.\par \par \uc2 The outcome of state elections for governors and judges was expected to have important implications for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in several states.\par \par \uc2 In Michigan, Governor \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2  declared victory over her Republican challenger, Tudor Dixon, an anti-choice Trump loyalist, in a race that centered on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile in Florida, the Republican governor, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , cruised to victory, amid mounting speculation about his 2024 presidential ambitions. His landslide victory included a vote from the former president, a resident of Florida who has sharpened his criticism against DeSantis as he prepares to launch another White House bid.\par \par \uc2 In Georgia, \uc2 Stacey Abrams\uc2 , a Democratic star, conceded to Governor \uc2 Brian Kemp\uc2 , concluding a bitter rematch of their 2018 showdown. Another Democratic hopeful, \uc2 Beto O\u8217\'20\'19Rourke\uc2 , fell short in his effort to unseat Texas\u8217\'20\'19s governor, Greg Abbott, who soundly won a third term.\par \par \uc2 Two gubernatorial races provided reason for optimism among Democrats. The party flipped seats in Massachusetts and Maryland, Democratic strongholds with a history of electing Republicans statewide. Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 candidates in those states will make history, as Wes Moore will become Maryland\u8217\'20\'19s first Black governor and \uc2 Maura Healey\uc2  will be the first openly lesbian governor in American history.\par \par \uc2 In New York, Governor \uc2 Kathy Hochul\uc2  easily defeated a challenge from the Republican congressman \uc2 Lee Zeldin\uc2 , who hoped to pull off an upset in the liberal state by tapping into voters\u8217\'20\'19 concern over crime. Hochul, who ascended to the role after the resignation of \uc2 Andrew Cuomo\uc2 , became the first woman elected governor in New York\u8217\'20\'19s history.\par \par \uc2 In Vermont, the Democrat Becca Balint became the first woman and first openly gay person to represent the state in Congress, while the Republican \uc2 Sarah Huckabee Sanders\uc2 , Trump\u8217\'20\'19s second press secretary and daughter of the former Arkansas governor \uc2 Mike Huckabee\uc2 , was elected as the first female governor of Arkansas. And in Florida, the 25-year-old Democrat Max Frost became the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/08/midterm-elections-more-diverse-congress"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 first Gen-Zer elected to Congress}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Anger at the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  appeared to drive many people to the polls who might not normally vote in the midterms, particularly women.\par \par \uc2 In Michigan, voters appeared on track to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, while voters in Vermont and California elected to guarantee the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in their constitution. Meanwhile in Maryland, voters overwhelmingly approved legalizing cannabis.\par \par \uc2 If the Republicans take control of the House, they have threatened to launch a series of investigations into Biden and his administration in an attempt to embarrass him in the run-up to the next presidential election.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  senior reporter Sam Levine contributed to this report\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020221108eib8003mm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
