\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 First Thing: \u8216\'20\'18Red wave\u8217\'20\'19 fails to materialise as Democrats beat expectations in the midterms\b0\par\par\uc2 Nicola Slawson \par \uc2 1,596 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 November 2022\par 11:53 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Fetterman clinches crucial Senate seat for Democrats in Pennsylvania while a slew of election-denying Republican candidates failed to win \u8211\'20\'13 although Republicans may still take the House. Plus, the drug that is Hollywood\u8217\'20\'19s worst-kept secretDon\u8217\'20\'19t already get First Thing in your inbox? Sign up here\par \par \uc2 Good morning.\par \par \uc2 Democrats have reason for cautious optimism this morning, as some of their endangered candidates appear likely to emerge victorious in the midterm elections, but Republicans still enjoy a narrow advantage in the battle for control of the House of Representatives. The Senate is too close to call, with the race in Nevada coming down to the wire and Georgia likely to go to a runoff in December.\par \par \uc2 Americans headed to the polls yesterday to determine control of the \uc2 US Congress\uc2  for the next two years, and election forecasts had favored Republicans in the final days of campaigning. The president\u8217\'20\'19s party typically loses seats in the midterms, and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s low approval rating, combined with concerns about the state of the US economy, had lowered Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 expectations.\par \par \uc2 But some key races were tilting toward Democrats, including one of the biggest prizes of the night: a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/09/john-fetterman-wins-pennsylvania-senate-race"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ferociously contested Senate race in Pennsylvania}}}\uc2  between Mehmet Oz, a Republican backed by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , and the Democrat \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2 , who has been battling to assure voters he is fit for office after having had a stroke.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe held the line,\u8221\'20\'1D a teary Fetterman said, declaring victory in a speech to supporters early this morning.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Who will win control of Congress? With many races still too close to call, control of Congress \u8211\'20\'13 and the future of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s agenda \u8211\'20\'13 still hangs in the balance. Outcomes of some closely contested elections are not expected for several days, or even weeks. But the early results already returned one certainty: the election is not unfolding as Republicans had hoped.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Where can we see the results? A definitive run-down of victories and losses is yet to come, but keep a close eye on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/nov/08/midterm-elections-2022-polls-results-senate-house-us-midterm-voting-republicans-democrats-live-updates-latest-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Guardian live blog for the latest updates}}}\uc2 . And check {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2022/nov/08/midterm-election-results-live-2022-map-us-midterms-latest-winners-seats-congress"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 our live election results page}}}\uc2  for full results of the congressional midterms, seat by seat. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-midterm-elections-2022"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Full coverage of the midterms here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Vermont and Michigan vote to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in constitutions\par \par \uc2 Voters in multiple states passed measures to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/nov/09/vermont-abortion-vote-first-us-state-constitution"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 enshrine the right to an \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  during yesterday\u8217\'20\'19s midterm elections, in a rebuke to the crackdown on reproductive freedoms taking place across the US.\par \par \uc2 In Michigan, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights campaigners declared victory on a ballot initiative looking to secure a constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , meaning the state will now escape the imposition of a 1931 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban that was on the books.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CToday, the people of Michigan voted to restore the reproductive rights they\u8217\'20\'19ve had for 50 years,\u8221\'20\'1D said Darci McConnell, a spokesperson for Reproductive Freedom for All, which put forth the ballot measure.\par \par \uc2 The news broke as other US states also saw victories for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights initiatives.\par \par \uc2 Vermont became the first state in America to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in its state constitution just before Michigan, calling its result on Tuesday after its voters backed a ballot initiative by a huge margin.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What does this mean for anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Republicans? These wins are more blows for Republicans who are increasingly finding that, when put to a vote, Americans frequently do not agree with a sweeping agenda to dismantle \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. So far, the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement has relied on judges, state houses and Republican lawmakers to curtail reproductive rights.\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  landslide victory brings Trump and 2024 into focus\par \par \uc2 It was expected to be a moment of triumph for Trump but it did not quite turn out that way. The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/09/donald-trump-mar-a-lago-midterms-2022"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 former US president appeared uneasy}}}\uc2  about the underwhelming Republican performance in the midterms at an election watch party he hosted at his plush Mar-a-Lago resort last night, after it was clear there would be no \u8220\'20\'1Cred wave\u8221\'20\'1D that he had implored his supporters to produce.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, at Ron {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/09/ron-desantis-trump-2024-florida-midterms"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s election victory party}}}\uc2  in Tampa last night, supporters of the rightwing Florida governor chanted: \u8220\'20\'1CTwo more years!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Governors serve four-year terms, but DeSantis is widely seen as a possible challenger to Trump for the Republican presidential nomination in 2024. DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s strong performance in Florida yesterday \u8211\'20\'13 as other Republicans across the US faltered \u8211\'20\'13 has greatly strengthened that position.\par \par \uc2 Trump had been reported to be planning a 2024 announcement next week, seeking to capitalise on Republican success in the midterm elections. But on the night when the Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 hoped-for \u8220\'20\'1Cred wave\u8221\'20\'1D seemed unlikely \u8211\'20\'13 though control of the House and the Senate remained in the balance \u8211\'20\'13 the atmosphere at Mar-a-Lago, was reported to be anxious.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What has Trump said about DeSantis? Trump has warned his party rival not to run for president in 2024 and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/08/donald-trump-ron-desantis-2024-president-campaign"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 threatened to reveal information about him if he does}}}\uc2 . The former US president said he would tell reporters \u8220\'20\'1Cthings\u8221\'20\'1D about the Florida governor \u8220\'20\'1Cthat won\u8217\'20\'19t be very flattering\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Why else did Trump have a bad night? He received a blow when \uc2 Doug Mastriano\uc2 , a far-right Republican candidate, lost to Josh Shapiro in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/09/josh-shapiro-wins-election-pennsylvania-governor-democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pennsylvania governor race}}}\uc2 . Trump had endorsed and heavily promoted Mastriano.\par \par \uc2 In other news \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 An\par \par \uc2 American woman has been detained in Saudi Arabia after she posted on \uc2 Twitter\uc2  that she and her young daughter had been lured to the kingdom and trapped there since 2019. US {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/nov/09/american-us-woman-carly-morris-detained-saudi-arabia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 officials confirmed the detention of Carly Morris}}}\uc2 , 34, a native of California.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The US basketball star\par \par \uc2 Brittney Griner\par \par \uc2 was transferred last week from a detention center outside the Russian capital and is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/09/brittney-griner-us-basketball-star-transferred-to-penal-colony"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on her way to a penal colony}}}\uc2 , her legal team said today. The White House has called the two-time Olympic gold medalist detention\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cwrongful\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Another {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/08/us-soldier-timothy-griffin-dies-ukraine-russia-international-legion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 American volunteer has died in combat in Ukraine}}}\uc2 , a spokesperson for the country\u8217\'20\'19s International Legion confirmed, bringing the number of US fighters killed in the war against Russia to at least six. Timothy Griffin, from New York state, had been fighting alongside Ukrainians on the eastern front.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Tesla\par \par \uc2 chief executive, \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 , has sold 19.5\par \par \uc2 m of his shares in the electric car company, according to filings published by the \uc2 US Securities and Exchange Commission\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2022/nov/09/elon-musk-sells-tesla-shares-worth-4bn"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in a transaction worth $3.95bn}}}\uc2 . The move comes after his purchase of \uc2 Twitter\uc2  for $44bn.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Meta\par \par \uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s chief, \uc2 Mark Zuckerberg\uc2 , confirmed to executives that the company\par \par \uc2 would begin laying off employees this morning, the Wall Street Journal reported\par \par \uc2 yesterday. Zuckerberg addressed hundreds of executives at the company on Tuesday morning, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2022/nov/08/meta-layoffs-facebook-mark-zuckerberg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 foreshadowing large cuts}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Stat of the day: First Gen Z member elected as midterms could usher in a more diverse Congress\par \par \uc2 Voters have elected {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/08/midterm-elections-more-diverse-congress"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the first-ever Gen Z member of Congress}}}\uc2  in the midterm elections on Tuesday, where a number of candidates are making history with their victories. Maxwell Frost, a 25-year-old Democrat, defeated a Republican in his Florida congressional race, the Associated Press reported on Tuesday evening. The Afro-Cuban progressive has organized with the \uc2 ACLU\uc2  and March for Our Lives, the gun reform group, and called for universal healthcare on the campaign trail. The departure of 46 members from the House of Representatives has created an opening for a new class of young and diverse candidates to seek federal office.\par \par \uc2 Don\u8217\'20\'19t miss this: The truth behind the weight loss drug that makes food repulsive\par \par \uc2 In Beverly Hills\u8217\'20\'19 doctors offices, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/food/2022/nov/09/i-miss-eating-weight-loss-drug-ozempic-food-repulsive"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 celebrities are clamoring for Ozempic prescriptions}}}\uc2 . It has become popular in the last two years because it makes people lose weight fast. It is controversial because it works by triggering a chemical repugnance to food itself. After being injected with Ozempic, a user could try to imagine a moist slab of black forest gateau, or a calorically-dense, half-pound Baconator bacon cheeseburger from Wendy\u8217\'20\'19s, and their body physically revolts, with spasms of nausea and waves of ill feeling. But what are the costs of the supposed wonder drug?\par \par \uc2 Climate check: Oil and gas greenhouse emissions \u8216\'20\'18three times higher\u8217\'20\'19 than producers claim\par \par \uc2 Greenhouse gas emissions from oil and gas facilities around the world are about {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2022/nov/09/oil-and-gas-greenhouse-emissions-three-times-higher-than-producers-claim"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 three times higher than their producers claim}}}\uc2 , data has shown. Climate Trace, a project to measure at source the true levels of carbon dioxide and other global heating gases, published a report today showing that half of the 50 largest sources of greenhouse gases in the world were oil and gas fields and production facilities. Many are underreporting their emissions, and there are few means of calling them to account.\par \par \uc2 Last\par \par \uc2 thing: Oldest known\par \par \uc2 sentence written in first alphabet\par \par \uc2 discovered \u8211\'20\'13 on a head-lice comb\par \par \uc2 It is a simple sentence that captures the hopes and fears of modern-day parents as much as the bronze age Canaanite who owned the doubled-edged ivory comb on which the words appear. Believed to be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/science/2022/nov/09/oldest-known-written-sentence-discovered-on-a-head-lice-comb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the oldest known sentence}}}\uc2  written in the earliest alphabet, the inscription on the luxury item reads: \u8220\'20\'1CMay this tusk root out the lice of the hair and the beard.\u8221\'20\'1D Analysis of the markings on the comb, which measures 3.5cm by 2.5cm, confirmed the writing to be Canaanite script, the earliest alphabet, which was invented about 3,800 years ago.\par \par \uc2 Sign up\par \par \uc2 First Thing is delivered to thousands of inboxes every weekday. If you\u8217\'20\'19re not already signed up, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/info/2018/sep/17/guardian-us-morning-briefing-sign-up-to-stay-informed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 subscribe now}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Get in touch\par \par \uc2 If you have any questions or comments about any of our newsletters please email {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:newsletters@theguardian.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 newsletters@theguardian.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020221109eib9001p9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
