\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Wednesday briefing: Democrats hold on, but Republicans surge\b0\par\par\uc2 Nimo Omer \par \uc2 2,178 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 November 2022\par 07:21 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 In today\u8217\'20\'19s newsletter: With full results on whether Democrats or Republicans will control the Senate and Congress yet to emerge, we check in with reporters in Florida, Michigan and elsewhere for the mood on the groundSign up here for our daily newsletter, First Edition\par \par \uc2 Good morning.\par \par \uc2 Polls across the US closed just nine hours ago and results have been pouring in. Democrats have been bracing for losses in the House but hoping for a narrow victory in the Senate. But the Senate is still a toss-up: for the past two years, control has been split exactly 50-50, so the Republicans needed to overturn just one seat to gain control of the upper house. But the first significant flip of the night actually went to the Democrats, with \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2  beating his Republican opponent in Pennsylvania. Going into these midterms, the Democrats had 222 seats in the House of Representatives to the Republicans 213 \u8211\'20\'13 so whoever takes the House will need to win 218 seats to gain a majority \u8211\'20\'13 though the House appears to be leaning Republican.\par \par \uc2 What is clear so far is that no \u8220\'20\'1Cred wave\u8221\'20\'1D came crashing in. While the Republicans have managed to retain some important seats, like Ohio, the democrats have won key Pennsylvania races, taking both the governors and the senate seats and defeating Trump endorsed nominees \uc2 Doug Mastriano\uc2  and Dr Mehmet Oz.\par \par \uc2 Predictably, the picture is still murky as results roll in. A definitive run-down of victories and losses is yet to come, but keep a close eye on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/nov/08/midterm-elections-2022-polls-results-senate-house-us-midterm-voting-republicans-democrats-live-updates-latest-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Guardian live blog for the latest updates}}}\uc2 . And check out {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2022/nov/08/midterm-election-results-live-2022-map-us-midterms-latest-winners-seats-congress"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 our live election results page}}}\uc2  to see full results of the Congressional midterms, seat by seat.\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19ve been receiving voice notes from \uc2 Guardian\uc2  journalists reporting on the ground in the US and speaking with voters across the country to get a better idea of what is going on. That\u8217\'20\'19s right after the headlines.\par \par \uc2 Five big stories\par \par \uc2 Politics\par \par \uc2 | {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2022/nov/08/pressure-grows-on-unethical-and-immoral-gavin-williamson"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gavin Williamson has quit Rishi Sunak\u8217\'20\'19s cabinet}}}\uc2  after allegations of bullying were levelled at him by a senior civil servant and former deputy chief whip, Wendy Morton. In a resignation letter, Williamson conceded that his conduct had become a distraction but vowed to clear his name.\par \par \uc2 Strikes |\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2022/nov/09/london-underground-strike-will-halt-nearly-all-tube-services-on-thursday"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 RMT\u8217\'20\'19s 24 hour walkout}}}\uc2  in the capital will halt virtually all tube services and slow much of London down. Buses are expected to be extremely busy and roads congested, in the ongoing dispute over jobs and pensions.\par \par \uc2 Environment |\par \par \uc2 The world\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2022/nov/08/greenhouse-gas-uk-windfarm-seagreen-project-scotland"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 most potent greenhouse gas}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D, sulphur hexafluoride, escaped during construction work on Scotland\u8217\'20\'19s largest windfarm. More than 80 workers were evacuated.\par \par \uc2 World Cup 2022\par \par \uc2 | Khalid Salman, a former Qatar international footballer and ambassador for the World Cup, has been criticised after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/football/2022/nov/08/qatar-world-cup-ambassador-homosexuality"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 saying that homosexuality is illegal}}}\uc2  in his country \u8216\'20\'18\u8220\'20\'1Cbecause it is damage in the mind\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Film\par \par \uc2 | Veteran actor {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/2022/nov/08/leslie-phillips-obituary?CMP=Share_iOSApp_Other"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Leslie Phillips has died}}}\uc2  at the age of 98. Phillips was known for his roles in the Carry On films and voicing the Sorting Hat in Harry Potter.\par \par \uc2 In depth: Oz is done, but DeSantis triumphs\par \par \uc2 It took two weeks to call every seat in the 2020 US presidential elections. So what\u8217\'20\'19s the point of writing a newsletter when a full picture may not emerge for at least a few days? Well, back in 2020, some Republicans capitalised on early gains to fuel conspiracies that the election was stolen from them \u8211\'20\'13 so it\u8217\'20\'19s important to know what is happening and when. Today\u8217\'20\'19s update will give you a run down of what we know so far about this year\u8217\'20\'19s midterms.\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 1 \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  referendums\par \par \uc2 When Poppy Noor, deputy features editor of Guardian US, went to Lansing, Michigan yesterday to report on the congressional race, she immediately saw a sign that said: \u8220\'20\'1CVote no on Prop 3, no to child mutilation, drain the swamp.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/31/michigan-abortion-proposal-3-campaign"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Proposal 3 is the move in Michigan}}}\uc2  to enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the state constitution.\par \par \uc2 Despite an embittered campaign, spirits are high. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a bit of a party vibe at the watch party for the campaign to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the states constitution,\u8221\'20\'1D she called in. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s so loud in here that I can\u8217\'20\'19t hear any of the results on TV,\u8221\'20\'1D she says with a laugh. Less than an hour ago, it was announced that the \u8220\'20\'1Cyes\u8221\'20\'1D campaign won, meaning that voters in Michigan chose to enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the state\u8217\'20\'19s constitution \u8211\'20\'13 a huge win for the pro-choice campaigners as it is a battleground state.\par \par \uc2 Vermont became the first state to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in its state constitution: while it was a fairly predictable result, it\u8217\'20\'19s still important: \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a strong message to Republican lawmakers who have relied on state houses and judges and other forms of minority rule in order to bring \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions across the country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 And Kentucky looks as if it will also vote against restricting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, which would be huge, Poppy says: \u8220\'20\'1CIt would show that even in a deep red state people do not want to restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 2 Florida\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/09/ron-desantis-trump-2024-florida-midterms"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 breezily won re-election as governor of Florida}}}\uc2  against Democrat \uc2 Charlie Crist\uc2 , with the Associated Press calling the race just an hour after polls closed. \u8220\'20\'1CThe victory margin was notable, with about 93% of the votes in, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  had recorded a lead of about 1.5 million,\u8221\'20\'1D says Richard Luscombe, a Guardian reporter covering the election in Miami. \u8220\'20\'1CWhen he was first elected governor four years ago, his total margin of victory was only 33,000.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 DeSantis has become a rising star in the GOP, building on his political capital from the pandemic, when he fought with local officials over his decision to lift Covid restrictions earlier than many other parts of the country. He\u8217\'20\'19s gone on to build a national platform that could lead him to be the Republican nominee in 2024.\par \par \uc2 DeSantis is seen as the most powerful potential challenger to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in the 2024 presidential elections. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/08/donald-trump-ron-desantis-2024-president-campaign"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump has warned DeSantis against running}}}\uc2  and threatened to reveal unflattering information about him if he does. His win also further crystallises Florida\u8217\'20\'19s transition from a purple state to a red one, says Richard: \u8220\'20\'1CThere was a time in the not too distant past when Florida was famous for being a swing state. In the midterm elections, that notion was thrown out of the window.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Incumbent Republican senator \uc2 Marco Rubio\uc2  crushed Val Demings by a similar margin. \u8220\'20\'1CThe margins of these Republican victories reflect a wave of red support in this state, there are no longer any elected Democrats at state level,\u8221\'20\'1D Richard says.\par \par \uc2 On a different note, the first Gen-Z member of congress was elected in Florida tonight. 25-year-old Democrat Maxwell Frost beat his Republican opponent on a platform advocating for universal healthcare and social justice.\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 3 Ohio\par \par \uc2 Trump loyalist and best selling author JD Vance won the Ohio senate race by a bigger margin than expected \u8211\'20\'13 a significant victory that could decide whether the Republicans gain control of the senate.\par \par \uc2 Guardian\uc2  reporter Chris McGreal sent me a voice note just after the polls closed in Ohio. \u8220\'20\'1CDuring the day, there were long lines to vote in some places, a reflection of what\u8217\'20\'19s at stake for many people here,\u8221\'20\'1D he says. Republicans also swept to victory in the Ohio supreme court races. \u8220\'20\'1CThese races are of huge interest to many in the state because they could decide the future of access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and democracy in the state,\u8221\'20\'1D explains Chris.\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 4 Yet to come\par \par \uc2 These were the most expensive midterms, with spending on campaigning set to hit $16.7bn, nearly doubling the cost of the 2010 races. While this may be seen as an obscene amount of money to spend on leaflets, videos and T-shirts, it is a strong indication of just how seismic these elections are.\par \par \uc2 Some of the biggest senate races, in Nevada, Georgia, Arizona and Pennsylvania, are still yet to be announced. With inevitable recounts, run-offs and delays, it might be impossible to predict where the country will be in a few months. It is already clear however that Republicans are performing a lot worse than they hoped, and the Democrats have good reason to be cautiously optimistic.\par \par \uc2 What else we\u8217\'20\'19ve been reading\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 As Elon Musk continues to trash \uc2 Twitter\uc2  and drive thousands of users off the platform, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2022/nov/08/how-to-quit-twitter-and-where-to-go-instead"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 this week\u8217\'20\'19s TechScape}}}\uc2  has a handy guide to other social media platforms that could fill the \uc2 Twitter\uc2  void in your life. To receive the newsletter in your inbox every Tuesday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/info/2022/sep/20/sign-up-for-the-techscape-newsletter-our-free-technology-email"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sign up here}}}\uc2 . Nimo\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Writer and Everyday Sexism Project founder Laura Bates is always excellent on feminism, equality and gender, never less so than {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2022/nov/08/feminists-war-on-men-misogyny-boys-gender-stereotypes-masculinity"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in this assessment of new research}}}\uc2  revealing \u8211\'20\'13 shocker! \u8211\'20\'13 that \u8220\'20\'1C challenging gender stereotypes \u8230\'20\'26 helps boys, too\u8221\'20\'1D. She notes: \u8220\'20\'1COur boys deserve better than to be used as a shield for anti-feminist provocateurs.\u8221\'20\'1D Craille Maguire Gillies, production editor, newsletters\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 As someone who likes to scare themselves silly before bed, I can very much relate to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vulture.com/2022/11/the-horror-podcasts-to-listen-to-in-order-to-fall-asleep.html#"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 this Vulture (\u163\'00\'A3) piece}}}\uc2  on the unexpectedly relaxing qualities of horror podcasts. Hannah J Davies, deputy editor, newsletters\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The government of Fiji faces a huge challenge that many other nations will also need to tackle in coming decades: how to relocate a country due to the climate crisis. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2022/nov/08/how-to-move-a-country-fiji-radical-plan-escape-rising-seas-climate-crisis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 This sweeping long read by Kate Lyons}}}\uc2  explores the challenges, successes and people who are being impacted. (And a logroll: why not {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global/2022/sep/20/sign-up-for-the-long-read-newsletter-our-free-in-depth-features-email"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sign up for the Long read newsletter}}}\uc2 , a free weekly dispatch full of in-depth features like this one?) Craille\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/2022/nov/08/stop-swiping-start-talking-the-rise-and-rise-of-the-blind-dating-app"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Leah Harper chronicles}}}\uc2  the rise of the blind-dating app. After a decade of Tinder, Hinge and \uc2 Bumble\uc2 , people are experiencing dating fatigue and getting frustrated with what they view as a superficial experience. Is digital dating without profile pictures the way forward? Nimo\par \par \uc2 Sport\par \par \uc2 Football\par \par \uc2 | {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/football/2022/nov/08/beth-mead-arsenal-england-interview-love-tour-not-hate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Beth Mead tells Donald McRae}}}\uc2  about the \u8220\'20\'1Chate\u8221\'20\'1D that drove her success last season, when she won the Euros with England, and the trials of sharing a pitch with her girlfriend and \uc2 Arsenal\uc2  teammate, Vivianne Miedema.\par \par \uc2 Cricket\par \par \uc2 | Sri Lanka Cricket is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2022/nov/08/sri-lanka-cricket-investigating-various-alleged-incidents-t20-world-cup"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 investigating \u8220\'20\'1Cvarious alleged incidents\u8221\'20\'1D at the T20 World Cup}}}\uc2  after Danushka Gunathilaka was accused of sexually assaulting a woman in Sydney last week.\par \par \uc2 World Cup |\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/football/2022/nov/08/sepp-blatter-qatar-hosting-world-cup-mistake"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Former Fifa president Sepp Blatter}}}\uc2  has said it was a mistake to hand the World Cup to Qatar, reiterating claims that the decision was down to political pressure.\par \par \uc2 The front pages\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\u8216\'20\'18Unethical, immoral\u8217\'20\'19 Williamson quits over claims he bullied staff\u8221\'20\'1D. The Guardian print edition leads this morning with the demise of a Cabinet Office minister. \u8220\'20\'1CWilliamson quits amid new claims of bullying\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 that\u8217\'20\'19s the Times while the Telegraph says \u8220\'20\'1CWilliamson quits over bullying allegations\u8221\'20\'1D. The Daily Mail reminds us what was allegedly said: \u8220\'20\'1CWilliamson forced out in \u8216\'20\'18cut your throat\u8217\'20\'19 bully row\u8221\'20\'1D. The i has \u8220\'20\'1CWilliamson resigns amid bullying and new security risk claims\u8221\'20\'1D. The Metro lines up I\u8217\'20\'19m A Celeb-bound Matt Hancock and Williamson on opposite sides of its front page, with the headline \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s in! And he\u8217\'20\'19s out\u8221\'20\'1D. A banner across the top adds a flourish: \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a jungle out there\u8221\'20\'1D. \u8220\'20\'1CRumble in the jungle\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 the Mirror says other celebs will tackle Hancock about the Covid crisis (sounds like riveting viewing \u8230\'20\'26). \u8220\'20\'1CYour 300,000 voices have been heard!\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 the Express says the pensions triple lock \u8220\'20\'1Clooks likely to be honoured\u8221\'20\'1D, crediting its reader campaign. The Financial Times\u8217\'20\'19 headline might take some decoding if you\u8217\'20\'19re not blockchain\u8211\'20\'13adjacent: \u8220\'20\'1CCrypto exchange FTX on the brink as liquidity crisis sparks call for help\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Today in Focus\par \par \uc2 What the scandal at Manston asylum centre reveals about our migration system\par \par \uc2 For the last six weeks conditions at a centre housing people who made perilous journeys across the Channel on small boats have been making the headlines. The home secretary, \uc2 Suella Braverman\uc2 , has pointed the finger at a \u8216\'20\'18broken\u8217\'20\'19 system. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/news/audio/2022/nov/09/what-scandal-manston-asylum-centre-says-about-migration-system-podcast"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 But why is the Home Office so often at the centre of a crisis?}}}\par \par \uc2 Cartoon of the day | Martin Rowson\par \par \uc2 The Upside\par \par \uc2 A bit of good news to remind you that the world\u8217\'20\'19s not all bad\par \par \uc2 Want to pull a disappearing act? Steve and Nick Tidball\u8217\'20\'19s thermal camouflage jacket has brought the fantastical idea of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2022/nov/08/what-does-a-100000-invisibility-cloak-look-like-funny-you-should-ask-"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an invisibility cloak}}}\uc2  to life, working with the University of Manchester\u8217\'20\'19s National Graphene Institute to create a garment containing 100 layers of the material. Their thermal camouflage jacket allows the wearer to blend into their surroundings under infrared light. It\u8217\'20\'19s cost \u163\'00\'A3100,000 to get this far, so don\u8217\'20\'19t expect to snap one up any time soon \u8211\'20\'13 although the brothers believe they could be on the market in the next five to 10 years.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2018/feb/12/the-upside-sign-up-for-our-weekly-email"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sign up here}}}\uc2  for a weekly roundup of The Upside, sent to you every Sunday\par \par \uc2 Bored at work?\par \par \uc2 And finally, the \uc2 Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s crosswords to keep you entertained throughout the day \u8211\'20\'13 with plenty more on the \uc2 Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Puzzles app for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apps.apple.com/app/id1487780661?mt=8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 iOS}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=uk.co.guardian.puzzles&hl=en_GB&gl=US"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Android}}}\uc2 . Until tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/crosswords/quick/16383"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Quick crossword}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/crosswords/cryptic/28910"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cryptic crossword}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020221109eib90010d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
