\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Planned Parenthood forced to turn patients away due to overwhelming demand post-Roe\b0\par\par\uc2 Richard Luscombe in Miami and agencies \par \uc2 833 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 November 2022\par 10:46 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Provider struggles to keep up as patients cross state lines to access legal abortions after supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s Dobbs decision\par \par \uc2 The supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s reversal of Roe v Wade has \u8220\'20\'1Cbroken\u8221\'20\'1D the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ecosystem in the US, according to executives of a Kansas clinic that opened just days after the landmark ruling in June.\par \par \uc2 The warning comes four days ahead of the pivotal midterm elections, in which Democrats have sought to make \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights a central issue.\par \par \uc2 It coincides with developments in Indiana, where a doctor who performed a legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  on a 10-year-old girl is suing the state\u8217\'20\'19s attorney general for a \u8220\'20\'1Cbaseless\u8221\'20\'1D investigation of her, and Michigan, where the ex-wife of a judge who voted to block an initiative protecting access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  claims he paid for her to have the procedure.\par \par \uc2 In Kansas, the Planned Parenthood center has turned away about 85% of women seeking abortions, officials say, after they have been inundated with demand from patients from states where the procedure was outlawed when federal protections were removed.\par \par \uc2 The clinic opened in a working-class area of Kansas City just four days after the supreme court ruling, originally intended as a local facility to negate the need for women to travel longer distances to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe ecosystem, it\u8217\'20\'19s not even fragile. It\u8217\'20\'19s broken,\u8221\'20\'1D said Emily Wales, president and chief executive of Planned Parenthood Great Plains.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think there\u8217\'20\'19s a perception that if you are seeking care, you can find it somewhere. And that\u8217\'20\'19s not true.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Wales said several of her group\u8217\'20\'19s clinics had extended opening hours and flown in doctors to try to keep up with demand from patients from states as distant as Texas and Louisiana, and those closer, including Arkansas, Missouri and Oklahoma.\par \par \uc2 But only about 10%-15% of women have been able to receive an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the clinics in Kansas, one of the few remaining states in the region where the procedure remains legal.\par \par \uc2 According to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://societyfp.org/wecount/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #WeCount national tracking effort}}}\uc2  by the Society of Family Planning, thousands of patients have been unable to get an appointment.\par \par \uc2 The group\u8217\'20\'19s report, released last month, found 6% fewer abortions were administered nationwide in August, when many of the more restrictive state bans on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  had already taken effect, than in April.\par \par \uc2 Some states with bans saw the number of abortions drop significantly, from 2,770 in April to below 10 in August in one, while those that still permit the procedure saw numbers increase, the survey found.\par \par \uc2 In Kansas, Colorado, Montana, Nebraska and North Carolina, there were 30% more abortions in August than in April, and in Illinois the figure was 28% greater.\par \par \uc2 Overall, the group says, the lives of 10,600 women have been \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SocietyFP/status/1587105070893903872"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 turned upside down}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D, reaching its conclusion by comparing total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  numbers before and after the Roe v Wade ruling.\par \par \uc2 Democrats have pushed to make the loss of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights a key message of the midterms, with \uc2 Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JoeBiden/status/1588305048626495489"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 promising}}}\uc2  that if his party retained control of the House, and expanded its Senate majority, it would codify Roe v Wade protections by January.\par \par \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 , the Democratic former presidential nominee, reinforced the message on Thursday at a rally for the New York governor, \uc2 Kathy Hochul\uc2 , saying that \u8220\'20\'1Ceverything is on the line\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 She attacked the Republican party, which has floated {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/13/republican-national-abortion-ban-lindsey-graham"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a nationwide \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban}}}\uc2  if it takes control of Congress.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey want to turn back the clock on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 they spent 50 years trying to make that happen,\u8221\'20\'1D said Clinton, speaking of the reversal of the 1973 Roe v Wade ruling.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut they want to turn back the clock on women\u8217\'20\'19s rights in general \u8211\'20\'13 on civil rights, on voting rights, on gay rights. They are determined to exercise control over who we are, how we feel and believe and act, in ways that I thought we had long left behind.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In Indiana, meanwhile, gynecologist Caitlin Bernard has filed a lawsuit against the state attorney general, Todd Rokita, who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/27/indiana-investigates-abortion-doctor-10-year-old-rape-victim"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 launched an investigation into her}}}\uc2  after she performed a legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  on a 10-year-old rape victim from Ohio.\par \par \uc2 Dr Bernard claims Rokita\u8217\'20\'19s scrutiny has been \u8220\'20\'1Coverbroad\u8221\'20\'1D for attempting to subpoena her patient\u8217\'20\'19s private medical records, and that his investigation was based on \u8220\'20\'1Cfrivolous\u8221\'20\'1D consumer complaints against her.\par \par \uc2 Despite Bernard reporting the procedure according to state laws, Rokita has accused her of being \u8220\'20\'1Can \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activist acting as a doctor\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In Michigan, the state supreme court judge Brian Zahra has been accused of hypocrisy by his former wife, Alyssa Jones, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/politics-news/michigan-judge-tried-block-abortion-rights-measure-ex-wife-says-helped-rcna54998"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NBC reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Zahra voted in September to block a ballot initiative that would have given voters the right to enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the state constitution. Almost four decades earlier, he arranged and paid for a procedure for Jones, his college girlfriend whom he later married, she claims.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020221107eib7002xm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
