\par\par \uc2 Art and design\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18A gut-felt, heartbreaking decision\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 Tracey Emin on her \u8216\'20\'18A-Z of  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 blanket\b0\par\par\uc2 Katy Hessel \par \uc2 875 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 November 2022\par 08:00 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 9\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The artist made The Last of the Gold to help women considering a termination. With the issue dominating tomorrow\u8217\'20\'19s US midterms, the work seems more potent than ever\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI felt pretty vulnerable. I was so broke, homeless, in debt \u8230\'20\'26 I had worked so hard at my education and coming from my background \u8230\'20\'26 I knew I wanted to be an artist and I knew that if I had a baby on my own, I felt that I had zero chance of that happening. It seemed ironic that now after all my education and fighting \u8230\'20\'26 that I was going to end up being a single mother \u8230\'20\'26 And I just thought, I can\u8217\'20\'19t bring a baby into the world with all this \u8230\'20\'26\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 These are the words of Tracey Emin reflecting on her two abortions from the early 1990s. They highlight the reality endured by so many women around the world. Emin has been making highly political work for decades. Through painting, textiles, films and more, she unveils the rawness and truths of life. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is an issue she has constantly explored, yet its importance in her work has too often been dismissed.\par \par \uc2 In 1996, for her film How It Feels, shot outside the clinic where she underwent the procedure, she speaks frankly about her experience with a male doctor who performed one of her abortions: \u8220\'20\'1CHe told me it was too late.\u8221\'20\'1D She continues: \u8220\'20\'1CHe showed me a picture of his child \u8230\'20\'26 and he told me what a wonderful mother I would make.\u8221\'20\'1D He then \u8220\'20\'1Crefused to sign the papers for me to have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The doctor should not have had beliefs for me\par \par \uc2 This doctor saw Emin solely as a child-bearing woman, with no other aspirations than to be a mother. By doing so, and by delaying the procedure, she was forced to live with her foetus for six weeks longer than she should have. This underlines how dangerous it is to have such people in positions of power, people who have not had any experience themselves, offering up advice or inflicting their own ideology on those in vulnerable positions \u8211\'20\'13 especially when they do not understand the emotional and physical implications. As Emin recounts in the film: \u8220\'20\'1CHe shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t have had beliefs for me.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 To help those facing a similar situation, in 2002 Emin constructed The Last of the Gold, a quilted blanket emblazoned with the \u8220\'20\'1CA to Z of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D. This is something, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://podcasts.apple.com/gb/podcast/the-great-women-artists/id1480259187?i=1000581608661"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the artist told me recently}}}\uc2 , she would have \u8220\'20\'1C100%\u8221\'20\'1D wanted when she was younger. \u8220\'20\'1CI am sure it\u8217\'20\'19s very much out of date now,\u8221\'20\'1D she added, \u8220\'20\'1Cbut the fundamental principle is that there is very little information or advice to give women in that situation. So at the time I thought, \u8216\'20\'18Why not put it across the gallery wall?\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Some suggestions are practical: \u8220\'20\'1CInsist on having an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as soon as possible \u8211\'20\'13 if you have the money (300 pounds) you can be treated within 24 hours \u8211\'20\'13 if you go through the \uc2 NHS\uc2  you may have to wait up to six weeks depending on availability, but then they may say no.\u8221\'20\'1D Others are emotional: \u8220\'20\'1CYou may feel in a state of euphoria from the relief, be careful as depression may follow.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Although made 20 years ago, The Last of the Gold is, sadly, still relevant, especially now that the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  has overturned Roe v Wade, leaving it up to individual state leaders to decide whether or not \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws should come into effect. Currently, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is banned in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2022/us/abortion-laws-roe-v-wade.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 13 states}}}\uc2 . In Georgia, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is banned after six weeks, a point when most women do not even realise they are pregnant.\par \par \uc2 In tomorrow\u8217\'20\'19s midterm elections, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be, for many, a deciding factor. In the swing state of Michigan \u8211\'20\'13 where Democrat \uc2 Elissa Slotkin\uc2  is hoping to be re-elected over the \u8220\'20\'1C100% pro-life, no exceptions\u8221\'20\'1D Republican candidate Tom Barrett \u8211\'20\'13 the issue is on a par with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/01/michigan-abortion-congressional-race-elissa-slotkin"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 inflation}}}\uc2 . For a while, Barrett and Slotkin were neck and neck. However, since September, the votes have risen in her favour, in part due to Republican-voting women in Michigan fearing the overturning of Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve never seen anything like it,\u8221\'20\'1D Slotkin recently told the Guardian. \u8220\'20\'1CEverywhere I go, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats}}}\uc2 , Independents and Republicans are talking about this issue. They\u8217\'20\'19re talking about how scared they are of a 1931 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban coming back in Michigan. They don\u8217\'20\'19t want it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Emin\u8217\'20\'19s raw accounts expose, on a human level, the precariousness of women\u8217\'20\'19s situation. \u8220\'20\'1CI lived it,\u8221\'20\'1D Emin told me. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd I know what it was like to make that choice. When I make work about that subject, it\u8217\'20\'19s not a fake idea or a fake notion or just a political statement. It\u8217\'20\'19s a heartfelt, gut-felt, heartbreaking decision that I had to make.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Her blanket concludes with this advice: \u8220\'20\'1CAnd most important, if you do decide you want to have the baby, don\u8217\'20\'19t listen to anyone, just listen to your heart.\u8221\'20\'1D Depending on how the elections pan out this week, many women in America may need Emin\u8217\'20\'19s work more than ever.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020221107eib70010b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
