\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Biden urges voters to \u8216\'20\'18preserve Democracy\u8217\'20\'19 and stand up against political violence - live\b0\par\par\uc2 Maanvi Singh (now) and Chris Stein (earlier) \par \uc2 8,263 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 November 2022\par 01:04 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The president sent a message to election deniers saying, \u8216\'20\'18You can\u8217\'20\'19t love your country only when you win\u8217\'20\'19Sign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.04am GMT\par \par \uc2 Recap\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s six days until the midterm elections. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  delivered a primetime address about threats to democracy, days after an intruder badly injured House speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s husband in an attack at their home in San Francisco. Meanwhile, further details about attempts by Trump allies to overturn the 2020 election have been revealed today, including an attempt to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/nov/02/midterm-elections-republicans-democrats-pelosi-biden-politics-latest?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-63627d458f08cc7814d3fb80#block-63627d458f08cc7814d3fb80"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 get a lawsuit specifically before}}}\uc2  conservative supreme court justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has happened today so far:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/nov/02/midterm-elections-republicans-democrats-pelosi-biden-politics-latest?page=with:block-636285e48f08bc16f7a70685#block-636285e48f08bc16f7a70685"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 may announce}}}\uc2  his 2024 campaign for president after next week\u8217\'20\'19s midterm elections, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Nevada\u8217\'20\'19s GOP party chair had his phone seized by federal investigators, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/nov/02/midterm-elections-republicans-democrats-pelosi-biden-politics-latest?page=with:block-636299d98f08013706b94d07#block-636299d98f08013706b94d07"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NBC News confirms.}}}\uc2  He also spoke to the January 6 committee after they sent him a subpoena.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Republican nominee for governor in Wisconsin {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/nov/02/midterm-elections-republicans-democrats-pelosi-biden-politics-latest?page=with:block-6362616a8f08bc16f7a70488#block-6362616a8f08bc16f7a70488"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 made clear}}}\uc2  his party \u8220\'20\'1Cwill never lose another election\u8221\'20\'1D if he wins, an ominous sign for voting laws and gerrymandering in a swing state crucial to both parties.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  once again {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2022/nov/02/fed-interest-rate-increase-inflation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 raised interest rates}}}\uc2  in a bid to lower the US\u8217\'20\'19 stubbornly high rate of inflation by tightening the ability of businesses and consumers to borrow money. America\u8217\'20\'19s largest trade union came out in opposition, saying working people will bear the brunt of its tighter monetary policy.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 In his speech, Biden urged voters to reject far-right election conspiracy theories and unite against political violence. \u8220\'20\'1CWe must in this moment, dig deep within ourselves and recognize that we can\u8217\'20\'19t take democracy for granted any longer,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. The president pleaded with voters to remember that \u8220\'20\'1Cdemocracy is on the ballot\u8221\'20\'1D and consider whether the candidates support will accept the election results.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Lawyers for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  working to challenge the 2020 election results wanted to appeal specifically to \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 , one of the most conservative justices on the supreme court, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/11/02/trump-lawyers-saw-justice-thomas-as-only-chance-to-stop-2020-election-certification-00064592"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to emails obtained by Politico}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 - Chris Stein, Maanvi Singh\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.48am GMT\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FBI\uc2  has arrested two alleged far-right Boogaloo Boys group members, the AP reports:\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/fbi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 FBI}}}\uc2  has arrested two alleged members of the far-right anti-government group the Boogaloo Boys, as authorities express increasing concern about the potential for violence around next week\u8217\'20\'19s US midterm elections.\par \par \uc2 Timothy Teagan was expected to appear on Wednesday in federal court in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/detroit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Detroit}}}\uc2 , where charges against him would be unsealed, an \uc2 FBI\uc2  spokesperson said.\par \par \uc2 In a criminal complaint filed on Monday, the \uc2 FBI\uc2  said there was enough evidence to charge Aron McKillips, of Sandusky, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ohio"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ohio}}}\uc2 , with illegal possession of a machine gun and the interstate communication of threats. The complaint said McKillips was a member of the Boogaloo Boys and was believed to be in a militia group called the Sons of Liberty.\par \par \uc2 McKillips\u8217\'20\'19s lawyer, Neil McElroy, said he had asked for McKillips to be released pending a 9 November detention hearing in Toledo.\par \par \uc2 Teagan\u8217\'20\'19s arrest on Tuesday came a week before election day. Election workers have been targeted by threats and harassment since the 2020 election, which \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has refused to admit he lost.\par \par \uc2 Federal authorities have charged at least five people already this year. Election officials are concerned about conspiracy theorists signing up to work as poll watchers. Some groups that have trafficked in lies about the 2020 election are recruiting and training watchers.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/02/fbi-boogaloo-boys-far-right-arrested"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 FBI arrests two alleged far-right Boogaloo Boys group members }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.33am GMT\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere in DC tonight, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s Hugo Lowell is reporting that Kash Patel, a \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  adviser and ally, will receive a limited immunity deal from federal prosecutors examining Trump\u8217\'20\'19s retention of highly-sensitive government documents at Mar-a-Lago, in exchange for his testimony in their investigation.\par \par \uc2 Lowell writes:\par \par \uc2 The immunity \u8211\'20\'13 a powerful tool that forces witnesses to testify on the promise that they will not be prosecuted for their statements or information derived from their statements \u8211\'20\'13 takes effect on 2 November and signals the importance of his testimony to the criminal investigation.\par \par \uc2 The justice department\u8217\'20\'19s interest with Patel centers on his claims that the documents found at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/mar-a-lago"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mar-a-Lago}}}\uc2  were declassified, how the documents came to end up at the property, and how Trump\u8217\'20\'19s aides and lawyers responded to requests for their return, sources said.\par \par \uc2 Read the full story:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/02/trump-advisor-kash-patel-immunity-mar-a-lago-documents"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Top Trump advisor granted immunity for testifying in Mar-a-Lago papers case}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.53am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.12am GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden: election result deniers put America on a 'path to chaos'\par \par \uc2 David Smith, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s Washington bureau chief, has highlighted some standout lines from Biden\u8217\'20\'19s speech tonight. Stay tuned for his full report.\par \par \uc2 enltrBiden: "You can't love your country only when you win."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 David Smith (@SmithInAmerica) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SmithInAmerica/status/1587947831674945543?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 2, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrBiden: "In our bones, we know democracy is at risk. We also know this: it's in our power, each and every one of us, to preserve our democracy. And I believe we will. I think I know this country. I know we will."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 David Smith (@SmithInAmerica) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SmithInAmerica/status/1587948123808301056?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 2, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrBiden: "My fellow Americans, we'll meet this moment. We just have to remember who we are. We are the United States of America."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 David Smith (@SmithInAmerica) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SmithInAmerica/status/1587948234101727233?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 2, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrBiden on January 6 insurrection: "I wish I could say the assault on our democracy had ended that day but I cannot." There are candidates who won't commit to accepting the results of the election they're in. That's the path to chaos in America.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 David Smith (@SmithInAmerica) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SmithInAmerica/status/1587947744345333762?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 2, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.16am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.45pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s speech tonight came off as a closing argument to voters, in which he ultimately asked Americans to speak \u8220\'20\'1Cwith one overwhelming, unified voice\u8221\'20\'1D against political violence.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s unlikely to be met with unity. Already, in states like Arizona, there have been multiple reports of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/20/arizona-early-voters-harassment-drop-box-monitors"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 voter intimidation}}}\uc2 . Local election officials are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/27/us-midterms-rural-california-voters-election-officials-fear-for-safety"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fearing}}}\uc2  for their safety. And disinformation is successfully {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/11/election-integrity-north-carolina-voter-suppression"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sowing distrust}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.34pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The president has concluded his speech. One of the things he did tonight was try to set expectations for how long the vote count could take.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COnce again, we\u8217\'20\'19re seeing record turnout all over the country. And that\u8217\'20\'19s good. I want Americans to vote. We want every American\u8217\'20\'19s voice to be heard,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe know that more and more ballots are cast in early voting or by mail in America. We know that many states don\u8217\'20\'19t start counting those ballots till after the polls closed on November 8.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 That means we might not get results on election night. \u8220\'20\'1CIt takes time to count all legitimate ballots and a legal and orderly manner,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, directly countering misinformation about how counting works.\par \par \uc2 In 2020, Trump and his supporters falsely characterized mail in votes that were tabulated after election day as illegitimate.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.24pm GMT\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou can\u8217\'20\'19t love your country only when you win,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said, urging unity.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s unclear how much of that this reach swing voters who might have prioritized Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 perceived strength on economic issues, or who might be voting on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , education or one of the many issues that Americans have said are weighing heavy on their minds this year.\par \par \uc2 And it\u8217\'20\'19s unlikely to convince those who have bought into the Big Lie that the 2020 election was stolen.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.25pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.18pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The speech is an appeal more than anything else \u8211\'20\'13 full of \u8220\'20\'1Cwe must\u8217\'20\'19s\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe must in this moment, dig deep within ourselves and recognize that we can\u8217\'20\'19t take democracy for granted any longer.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe must with an overwhelming voice stand against political violence and voter intimidation period. Stand up and speak against it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAll of us must remember that democracy is a covenant.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.12pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden is also directly holding \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  responsible for these threats to democracy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe has abused his power and put the loyalty to himself above loyalty to the constitution,\u8221\'20\'1D he said of the former president. \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s made the big lie an article of faith in the Maga Republican Party.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden \u8211\'20\'13 as he tends to do \u8211\'20\'13 is again avoiding saying Trump\u8217\'20\'19s name, instead referring to him as the \u8220\'20\'1Cdefeated former president.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.14pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.10pm GMT\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s a lot at stake in these midterm elections, from our economy, the safety of our streets to our personal freedoms, the future of health care, Social Security, Medicare, it\u8217\'20\'19s all important,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said, acknowledging issues that voters say are at top of mind this year. \u8220\'20\'1CBut there\u8217\'20\'19s something else at stake. democracy itself.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDemocracy is on the ballot this year,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe must vote knowing what\u8217\'20\'19s at stake and not just the policy of the moment.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.10pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.08pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Paul Pelosi\u8217\'20\'19s attacker \u8220\'20\'1Centered the home asking \u8216\'20\'18Where\u8217\'20\'19s Nancy?\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CThe same words used by the mob when they stormed the United States Capitol on Jan. 6.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Big Lie promoted by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his supporters that the 2020 election was stolen has \u8220\'20\'1Cfueled the dangerous rise in political violence and voter intimidation\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re facing a defining moment. We must, with one overwhelming, unified voice and speak as a country to say there\u8217\'20\'19s no place for voter intimidation,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.03pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden takes the stage\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has begun his primetime address on the state of democracy in the US.\par \par \uc2 He is beginning by addressing the attack on Paul Pelosi. \u8220\'20\'1CMy friend, Paul Pelosi, was home alone,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CThankfully, by the grace of God, all survived.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.30pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Guaranteed income programs are starting to catch on in the US. The policy that\u8217\'20\'19s been standard in northern Europe and Canada leads to better outcomes for children and parents.\par \par \uc2 FromJackie Mader, The Hechinger Report:\par \par \uc2 By his mid-20s, Tommy Andrade was tired of working dead-end jobs. With a young child at home, he realized he needed more than a high school diploma to support his family. When he heard about a new, advanced manufacturing program at a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/texas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas}}}\uc2  community college, Andrade was intrigued.\par \par \uc2 Some of the jobs that graduates from Austin Community College (ACC) would be trained for carried salaries well into the six figures, enough to give Andrade financial security, he figured, even in a city like Austin where the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://filterbuy.com/resources/cost-of-living-in-us/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cost of living was spiking fast}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But first Andrade would have to take a pay cut: the 14-week program required him to participate in an internship that paid $17 an hour, less than he\u8217\'20\'19d earned in his previous jobs as a salesman and bookkeeper. He worried he wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be able to afford rent, bills and after-school care for his son.\par \par \uc2 Then came some unexpected good news: ACC was launching a new guaranteed income pilot program for student parents, and program officials wanted him to join. Participants would receive $500 a month for two years with a few conditions: they must enrol in nine credits each semester and attend monthly meetings with other student parents.\par \par \uc2 Buoyed by the extra income, Andrade signed up. \u8220\'20\'1CFive hundred isn\u8217\'20\'19t anything to live off of, but it\u8217\'20\'19s enough to make a difference,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CI have some flexibility to take some risk.\u8221\'20\'1D Now, a year after enrolling in the program and on track to graduate, Andrade, 29, is living in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/seattle"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Seattle}}}\uc2  with his partner and son, having recently accepted a full-time job as a contractor at a large technology company.\par \par \uc2 Andrade\u8217\'20\'19s story points to the potential of guaranteed-income programs. These programs, which provide consistent financial support to participants over a period of time, were placed on the national radar in 2020 by former presidential candidate \uc2 Andrew Yang\uc2 , who called for a monthly income for all US residents. The idea exploded in popularity during the Covid-19 pandemic, as state and local governments, philanthropists and even some colleges sought to support people experiencing financial distress. More than 48 guaranteed income programs have been started in cities across the country since 2020. Advocates and researchers say this approach holds promise as a long-term anti-poverty strategy as well \u8211\'20\'13 especially for families with young children.\par \par \uc2 Indeed, a growing body of research shows cash transfer programs can have a particularly big impact on young kids by providing family stability during children\u8217\'20\'19s first few formative years. This is likely due, in part, to a reduction of parental stress. Studies show that when parents experience high levels of distress, it {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hechingerreport.org/the-pandemic-hit-moms-hard-and-that-stress-can-trickle-down-to-kids/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 trickles down}}}\uc2  to their kids, who exhibit higher levels of emotional distress as well. Constant stress or exposure to adverse childhood experiences like food and housing insecurity can lead to trauma and even cause changes to young children\u8217\'20\'19s brains, making them less able to cope. But that harm can be mitigated if children\u8217\'20\'19s basic needs are met and their parents have financial security.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/education/2022/nov/02/guaranteed-income-us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Guaranteed income programs starting to catch on in the US}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.36pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.49pm GMT\par \par \uc2 In his speech, Biden plans to make the case that election deniers running for office are leading a \u8220\'20\'1Cpath to chaos in America\u8221\'20\'1D, according to experts released by the DNC.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere are candidates running for every level of office in America: for governor, for Congress, for attorney general, for secretary of state who won\u8217\'20\'19t commit to accepting the results of the elections they\u8217\'20\'19re in,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden plans to say. \u8220\'20\'1CThat is the path to chaos in America. It\u8217\'20\'19s unprecedented. It\u8217\'20\'19s unlawful. And, It is un-American.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He will also make the point that this is an unusual, unprecedented election year.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is no ordinary year. So, I ask you to think long and hard about the moment we are in,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden will say. \u8220\'20\'1CIn a typical year, we are not often faced with the question of whether the vote we cast will preserve democracy or put it at risk. But we are this year.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.56pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.33pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Justice Democrats, a progressive political action committee, has urged Biden to draw a line between the right-wing threats to democracy with and the economy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf Republicans succeed in their plot against democracy, their big oil and pharma donors will be free to raise prices as high as they wish without our one tool to reign them in: government of, by, and for the people,\u8221\'20\'1D said Waleed Shahid, a spokesperson for the group.\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CPresident Biden must make a strong case for how the MAGA Republican assault on our democracy is a pocketbook issue tied to inflation." - {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/_waleedshahid?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @_WaleedShahid}}}\par \par \uc2 Our statement ahead of President Biden's major speech on democracy tonight: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Dl9ZEdEjIj"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Dl9ZEdEjIj}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Justice Democrats (@justicedems) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/justicedems/status/1587889425782083584?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 2, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 A slate of far-right candidates who have vowed to dismantle election systems are running in statewide and local races across the country, on a platform based on the conspiracy theory that the 2020 election was stolen from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But with early voting underway, economic concerns have been top of mind for many voters, polls show, possibly directing them toward Republican candidates. Progressives, including \uc2 Bernie Sanders\uc2 , have urged Democratic candidates to not to ignore voters\u8217\'20\'19 economic woes even as they center threats to democracy and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt would be political malpractice for Democrats to ignore the state of the economy and allow Republican lies and distortions to go unanswered,\u8221\'20\'1D he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/commentisfree/2022/oct/10/democrats-midterms-victory-economy-bernie-sanders"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote}}}\uc2  in a recent op-ed for the Guardian. \u8220\'20\'1CIn poll after poll, Republicans are more trusted than Democrats to handle the economy \u8211\'20\'13 the issue of most importance to people. I believe that if Democrats do not fight back on economic issues and present a strong pro-worker agenda, they could well be in the minority in both the House and the Senate next year.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.45pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.19pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Later this evening, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is set to give a speech about threats to democracy.\par \par \uc2 Biden delivered remarks on developing infrastructure jobs in the East Room of the White House earlier today. Photograph: Oliver Contreras/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 In recent weeks, he has centered in on the message that \u8220\'20\'1Cdemocracy is on the ballot\u8221\'20\'1D this election. His last primetime speech addressed threats from the \u8220\'20\'1CMaga forces\u8221\'20\'1D of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his supporters.\par \par \uc2 Tonight, the president \u8220\'20\'1Cwill be very clear tonight that he is speaking to people who don\u8217\'20\'19t agree with him on any issues, who don\u8217\'20\'19t agree on his agenda, but who really can unite behind this idea of this fundamental value of democracy\u8221\'20\'1D, White House senior adviser Anita Dunn said today during an event hosted by Axios.\par \par \uc2 He is also expected to address heightened threats against political figures, in the aftermath of a politically motivated attack on Paul Pelosi, House speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s husband.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.23pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18This is a blueprint\u8217\'20\'19: \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights ballot proposal takes off in Michigan\par \par \uc2 In the spring of this year, Julie Falbaum\u8217\'20\'19s 20-year-old son walked into a frat party filled with about 50 of his peers, holding a stack of petitions. They were for a campaign to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWho wants to be a dad?\u8221\'20\'1D he yelled. Like a park-goer throwing bread to pigeons, he chucked the forms around the room and watched as dozens of young men swarmed to sign them.\par \par \uc2 The campaign to enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the state constitution was already under way here even before Roe fell, and it has become an embittered battle in Michigan \u8211\'20\'13 to keep a 90-year-old \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban off the books. Campaigners fear that ban would criminalise doctors and pregnant people and deny essential medical care, such as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.legislature.mi.gov/documents/mcl/pdf/mcl-328-1931-III.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  miscarriage medication}}}\uc2 , now that the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  no longer exists in the US.\par \par \uc2 The battle in Michigan has brought {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.catholicnewsagency.com/news/252534/video-pro-abortion-vandals-caught-in-the-act-of-spray-painting-michigan-church"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 death threats and vandalism}}}\uc2  from pro-choice militants. On the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  side, it has involved dirty tactics from the Republican party, which tried to block a petition brought by nearly 800,000 Michiganders over {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/09/08/michigan-supreme-court-puts-abortion-on-november-ballot-00055774"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 formatting errors}}}\uc2 , and has peddled a wide campaign of misinformation.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/31/michigan-abortion-proposal-3-campaign"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18This is a blueprint\u8217\'20\'19: \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights ballot proposal takes off in Michigan}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.08pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.02pm GMT\par \par \uc2 In Arizona, the Republican candidate for governor Kari Lake turned the assault on \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s husband Paul into a punchline:\par \par \uc2 enltrArizona gubernatorial candidate Kari Lake (R) gets a big laugh from the crowd after joking about Speaker Pelosi\u8217\'20\'19s husband Paul being violently assaulted:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 , well, she\u8217\'20\'19s got protection when she\u8217\'20\'19s in D.C. \u8212\'20\'14 apparently her house doesn\u8217\'20\'19t have a lot of protection.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/8U647UTO9x"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/8U647UTO9x}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1587182585557684225?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 31, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Paul Pelosi was allegedly attacked on Friday by David DePape, who is accused of breaking into their San Francisco home and shouting \u8220\'20\'1Cwhere is Nancy?\u8221\'20\'1D DePape told investigators he wanted to take the Democratic House speaker hostage and potentially break her kneecaps, and is facing an array of state and federal charges for the assault.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s politics live blog is being handed over to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/maanvi-singh"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Maanvi Singh}}}\uc2 , who will take you through the remainder of the day, including \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s speech on threats to democracy at 7 pm eastern time.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.04pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.50pm GMT\par \par \uc2 America\u8217\'20\'19s largest trade union federation the \uc2 AFL-CIO\uc2  has come out in opposition to the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s latest rate hike, saying working people will bear the brunt of its tighter monetary policy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s decision today to raise interest rates by.75% will have a direct and harmful impact on working people and our families. The Fed\u8217\'20\'19s actions will not address the underlying causes of inflation\u8212\'20\'14the war in Ukraine, climate change\u8217\'20\'19s effect on harvests and corporate profits, and an increase in the chances that the United States enters a recession,\u8221\'20\'1D the federation\u8217\'20\'19s president \uc2 Liz Shuler{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://aflcio.org/press/releases/afl-cio-federal-reserves-interest-rate-hike-devastating-working-people"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said in a statement}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Fed seems determined to raise interest rates, though it openly admits those rates could ruin our current economy as unemployment remains low and people are able to find jobs.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 AFL-CIO\uc2  typically supports Democrats, who are increasingly opposed to the Fed\u8217\'20\'19s rate increases, despite the central bank\u8217\'20\'19s explanation that they are necessary to lower inflation in the United States.\par \par \uc2 Yesterday, a coalition of progressive lawmakers including senators \uc2 Bernie Sanders\uc2  and Elizabeth Warren {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.warren.senate.gov/oversight/letters/warren-dean-lawmakers-ask-fed-chair-powell-how-many-millions-will-be-thrown-out-of-their-jobs-from-feds-dangerous-rate-hikes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote to Fed chair}}}\uc2 Jerome Powell\uc2 , questioning the Fed\u8217\'20\'19s strategy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou continue to double down on your commitment to \u8216\'20\'18act aggressively\u8217\'20\'19 with interest rate hikes and \u8216\'20\'18keep at it until it\u8217\'20\'19s done,\u8217\'20\'19 even if \u8216\'20\'18(n)o one knows whether this process will lead to a recession or if so, how significant that recession would be,\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D the lawmakers said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese statements reflect an apparent disregard for the livelihoods of millions of working Americans, and we are deeply concerned that your interest rate hikes risk slowing the economy to a crawl while failing to slow rising prices that continue to harm families.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.26pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The governor\u8217\'20\'19s race in Wisconsin is a dead heat, Marquette Law School {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://law.marquette.edu/poll/category/poll-release/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 found in a poll released today}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Both Democratic incumbent \uc2 Tony Evers\uc2  and his Republican challenger \uc2 Tim Michels\uc2  are at 48% support among likely voters, the survey found.\par \par \uc2 In the Senate race, GOP incumbent Ron Johnson may have an edge over his Democratic challenger Mandela Barnes, but it\u8217\'20\'19s close, according to the poll. Johnson is at 50% support among likely voters, and Barnes at 48%. The race appears to have tightened up since Marquette\u8217\'20\'19s previous survey conducted from October 3-9, when Johnson polled at 52% support to Barnes\u8217\'20\'19s 46%.\par \par \uc2 Wisconsin is viewed as one of Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 best opportunities to oust a sitting Republican senator, while control of the governor\u8217\'20\'19s mansion may determine whether Wisconsin remains a swing state in future elections, or if Republicans succeeded in their campaign to use gerrymandering and election restrictions to hobble Democrats in the state.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.02pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Wisconsin\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic governor \uc2 Tony Evers\uc2  called his Republican opponent a threat to democracy after he made comments indicating he would consolidate GOP control in the state if elected, \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/martin-pengelly"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Martin Pengelly}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 The Republican candidate for governor in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/wisconsin"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Wisconsin}}}\uc2  told supporters at a campaign event that if he is elected his party \u8220\'20\'1Cwill never lose another election\u8221\'20\'1D in the state.\par \par \uc2 Tim Michels\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 opponent next Tuesday, the incumbent Democrat \uc2 Tony Evers\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Tony4WI/status/1587202557973303298?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw%7Ctwcamp%5Etweetembed%7Ctwterm%5E1587202557973303298%7Ctwgr%5E4bc00a389ff8e790f09aab76ca516eab9838e3c6%7Ctwcon%5Es1_&ref_url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Frepublicans-will-never-lose-wisconsin-tim-michels-tony-evers2022-11"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  the comment, which was released by a left-leaning group, showed the Republican was \u8220\'20\'1Ca danger to our democracy\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Michels, a construction company owner, is endorsed by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . He has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2022-08-10/election-denial-fight-spreads-to-wisconsin-with-trump-ally-s-win"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 repeated}}}\uc2  the former president\u8217\'20\'19s lie that his defeat by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in 2020 was the result of electoral fraud, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2022-08-10/election-denial-fight-spreads-to-wisconsin-with-trump-ally-s-win"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 refused}}}\uc2  to say if he would certify results in a presidential election if he was governor and a Democrat won Wisconsin.\par \par \uc2 In a debate with Evers last month, Michels {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbs58.com/news/evers-michels-portray-one-another-as-the-wrong-choice-during-gubernatorial-debate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 did not say}}}\uc2  he would accept the result of his own election. He later {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbs58.com/news/tim-michels-says-he-will-accept-nov-election-results-after-not-fully-committing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  he would.\par \par \uc2 Republican candidates in other swing states have cast doubt on whether they will accept results next week.\par \par \uc2 Fred Wertheimer, president of the non-partisan group Democracy 21, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/nov/02/midterm-elections-republicans-democrats-pelosi-biden-politics-latest"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told the Guardian}}}\uc2  this week: \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s great danger that the Trump \u8216\'20\'18big lie\u8217\'20\'19 is going to spread to states all over the country.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf election deniers lose their elections by narrow margins we can expect that they will reject the results and refuse to accept them.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/02/wisconsin-republican-gubernatorial-candidate-tim-michels"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republican says party \u8216\'20\'18will never lose another election\u8217\'20\'19 in Wisconsin if he wins}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.41pm GMT\par \par \uc2 In an attempt to preserve their fragile majorities in the House of Representatives, Democrats this year have spent money to boost far-right Republicans in certain areas, banking that these candidates would be easier for them to defeat in the midterms.\par \par \uc2 In an interview with \uc2 The Washington Post\uc2 , \uc2 Steny Hoyer\uc2 , the Democratic majority leader in the House, defends the tactic and pins the blame on Republican voters for choosing the more extreme candidate. Democratic congressman \uc2 Don Beyer\uc2 , meanwhile, signals discomfort with the strategy:\par \par \uc2 enltrNew {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PostVideo?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @PostVideo}}}\uc2  exclusive:\par \par \uc2 House Majority Leader \uc2 Steny Hoyer\uc2  (D-Md.) told The Post in a recent interview that spending by Democrats amplifying far-right Republican candidates who have questioned or denied the results of the 2020 election does not undermine U.S. democracy. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/JBGO4YGc4k"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/JBGO4YGc4k}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 JM Rieger (@RiegerReport) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RiegerReport/status/1587874056988246016?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 2, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.20pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Fed raises rates for sixth consecutive time as fight against inflation continues\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  has once again raised interest rates in a bid to lower the United States\u8217\'20\'19 stubbornly high rate of inflation by tightening the ability of businesses and consumers to borrow money.\par \par \uc2 Inflation has been a major factor in president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s low approval ratings among voters. In the run-up to the central bank\u8217\'20\'19s two-day meeting that concluded today, some Democratic senators had urged its policy setting committee to proceed cautiously or even hold off on another increase, saying rates that are higher than necessary could harm the economy.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on the Fed\u8217\'20\'19s decision from \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/dominic-rushe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dominic Rushe}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/federal-reserve"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Federal Reserve}}}\uc2  stepped up its fight against a 40-year high in US inflation on Wednesday, announcing its fourth consecutive three-quarters of a percentage point hike in interest rates.\par \par \uc2 With the cost of living crisis {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2022/sep/30/inflation-healthy-food-eating-america"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 battering consumers}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/10/arizona-midterms-crucial-senate-race"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden\u8217\'20\'19s political fortunes}}}\uc2 , Fed officials have now imposed six rate rises in a row, the sharpest increases in interest rates since the 1980s, when inflation touched 14% and rates rose to nearly 20%.\par \par \uc2 The Fed\u8217\'20\'19s latest increase brings the federal funds rate \u8211\'20\'13 which acts as a benchmark for everything including business loans, credit card and mortgage rates \u8211\'20\'13 to between 3.75% and 4% after sitting at 0% for more than a year during the coronavirus pandemic.\par \par \uc2 The central bank does not expect inflation or interest rates to reach the levels seen in the 80s. Chair \uc2 Jerome Powell\uc2  has indicated that the Fed expects rates will reach 4.4% by the end of the year and start coming down until 2024. Fed officials had expected inflation to decline this year.\par \par \uc2 But inflation \u8211\'20\'13 which the Fed initially dismissed as \u8220\'20\'1Ctransitory\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 remains stubbornly high. In September, the costs of goods and services were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2022/oct/13/us-inflation-rate-september-midterm-elections"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 8.2% higher }}}\uc2  compared to a year ago, well above the Fed\u8217\'20\'19s target inflation rate of 2%.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2022/nov/02/fed-interest-rate-increase-inflation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fed announces sixth consecutive hike in US interest rates to fight inflation}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.04pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Some of the most closely watched races this year are being held in Arizona, where Democrats are fighting to keep hold of a Senate seat, while Republicans have elevated candidates for governor and secretary of state who have promoted baseless conspiracy theories about the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 For a better understanding of how \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has transformed the politics of the southwestern state, take a look at this report \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/laughland-oliver"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Oliver Laughland}}}\uc2  in Phoenix:\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.29pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Newsom slams Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 \u8220\'20\'1Cmessaging\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Just to continue the theme of bad news for Democrats, California governor \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  (a future presidential candidate?) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CBSEveningNews/status/1587583395596476418"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has slammed}}}\uc2  his own side\u8217\'20\'19s messaging in the midterms campaign.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re getting crushed on narrative. We\u8217\'20\'19re going to have to do better in terms of getting on the offense and stop being on the damn defense,\u8221\'20\'1D Newsom told CBS News chief Washington correspondent Major Garrett in an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CBSEveningNews/status/1587583395596476418"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 interview airing Wednesday}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The comments come as some progressives in the party \u8211\'20\'13 most notably \uc2 Bernie Sanders\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 want more of a focus placed on economic issues, which polls suggest are often foremost in voters\u8217\'20\'19 minds.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.16pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Republicans target deep blue Democrat seats\par \par \uc2 In a sign of the times \u8211\'20\'13 i.e. that the Democrats now seem firmly on the back foot when it comes to defending the House \u8211\'20\'13 the Republicans are ploughing money into a couple of deep blue seats.\par \par \uc2 Politico {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/11/02/gop-ad-spending-illinois-new-york-00064509"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports }}}\uc2  that several million dollars of ad spending is now targeting a pair of seats in Illinois and Long Island in New York where both districts that went heavily for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/11/02/gop-ad-spending-illinois-new-york-00064509"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 details}}}\uc2  below:\par \par \uc2 House Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 top congressional super PAC is betting that a last minute cash infusion can flip two deep-blue districts on the edges of the House battlefield.\par \par \uc2 The Congressional Leadership Fund is going on air with seven-figure buys targeting Democratic Rep. Sean Casten in suburban Chicago and the Long Island seat held by retiring Democratic Rep. Kathleen Rice. The super PAC is investing $1.8 million and $1.5 million, respectively, on broadcast buys in the expensive Chicago and New York City media markets.\par \par \uc2 Neither district has seen much outside spending before the final days of the midterms, and President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  carried both of them by double-digits in 2020. But the late ad buys suggest Republicans see opportunities in both places as the country grapples with high cost of living and the possibility of an economic recession looming.\par \par \uc2 House Majority PAC, CLF\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic counterpart, also recently invested in both districts \u8212\'20\'14 a sign that both parties believe the seats are at risk of flipping.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.04pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Fetterman may have survived debate in Pennsylvania\par \par \uc2 Many Democrats {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/26/fetterman-oz-debate-democrats-pennsylvania-senate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 worried}}}\uc2  about \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s debate performance against Mehmet Oz in the crucial Pennsylvania senate race. Fetterman, who recently suffered a stroke, struggled at times and made several gaffes.\par \par \uc2 His performance was jumped on by many Republicans eager to boost Oz, who is seen as a weak Trumpist candidate. It also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/26/fetterman-oz-debate-democrats-pennsylvania-senate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unnerved many other}}}\uc2  observers. But a Monmouth poll seems to show that Fetterman has kept his narrow lead.\par \par \uc2 Monmouth says:\par \par \uc2 Nearly half of the electorate will either definitely (39%) or probably (9%) vote for Fetterman, which is similar to his support levels in prior Monmouth polls (48% total compared with 48% in early October and 49% in September). Oz, on the other hand, continues to make small but steady gains in support, with 32% definitely supporting him and 12% probably supporting.\par \par \uc2 More details {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.monmouth.edu/polling-institute/reports/monmouthpoll_pa_110222/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.50pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s six days until the midterm elections and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/nov/02/midterm-elections-republicans-democrats-pelosi-biden-politics-latest?page=with:block-636275d68f08bc16f7a7058e#block-636275d68f08bc16f7a7058e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 this evening at 7 pm eastern time speak}}}\uc2  about threats to democracy. The address comes days after an intruder badly injured House speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s husband in an attack at their home in San Francisco. Meanwhile, further details about attempts by Trump allies to overturn the 2020 election have been revealed today, including an attempt to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/nov/02/midterm-elections-republicans-democrats-pelosi-biden-politics-latest?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-63627d458f08cc7814d3fb80#block-63627d458f08cc7814d3fb80"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 get a lawsuit specifically before}}}\uc2  conservative supreme court justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has happened today so far:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/nov/02/midterm-elections-republicans-democrats-pelosi-biden-politics-latest?page=with:block-636285e48f08bc16f7a70685#block-636285e48f08bc16f7a70685"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 may announce}}}\uc2  his 2024 campaign for president after next week\u8217\'20\'19s midterm elections, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Nevada\u8217\'20\'19s GOP party chair had his phone seized by federal investigators, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/nov/02/midterm-elections-republicans-democrats-pelosi-biden-politics-latest?page=with:block-636299d98f08013706b94d07#block-636299d98f08013706b94d07"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NBC News confirms.}}}\uc2  He also spoke to the January 6 committee after they sent him a subpoena.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Republican nominee for governor in Wisconsin {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/nov/02/midterm-elections-republicans-democrats-pelosi-biden-politics-latest?page=with:block-6362616a8f08bc16f7a70488#block-6362616a8f08bc16f7a70488"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 made clear}}}\uc2  his party \u8220\'20\'1Cwill never lose another election\u8221\'20\'1D if he wins, an ominous sign for voting laws and gerrymandering in a swing state crucial to both parties.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.32pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The chair of Nevada\u8217\'20\'19s Republican party said he testified before the January 6 committee and had his phone seized by federal investigators, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/congress/nevada-gop-chair-says-was-interviewed-jan-6-committee-rcna55141"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NBC News reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The congressional panel investigating the attack on the Capitol issued a subpoena for documents and testimony from Michael McDonald in January, saying it was interested in finding out more about the \u8220\'20\'1Cfake elector\u8221\'20\'1D scheme, in which GOP officials signed false declarations that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  had won states that had actually been carried by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYes, I was called before them. I answered the subpoena,\u8221\'20\'1D McDonald told NBC News, declining to elaborate on what he said to the committee or if he had invoked his constitutional rights not to answer lawmakers\u8217\'20\'19 questions. McDonald was among a group of Nevada Republicans who signed a document falsely saying Trump won the state. In fact, Biden won the state by more than 33,000 votes.\par \par \uc2 McDonald\uc2  also acknowledged federal agents took his phone, which may be related to the justice department\u8217\'20\'19s investigation of attempts to overturn the 2020 vote.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.11pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The congressional investigation into the January 6 attack is just one of several \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is embroiled in. \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/hugo-lowell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hugo Lowell}}}\uc2  reports that prosecutors are zeroing-in on testimony from a top adviser to the ex-president as part of its inquiry into classified documents found at Mar-a-Lago:\par \par \uc2 The justice department is weighing whether to grant immunity to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump}}}\uc2  adviser Kash Patel and force his testimony about claims that highly sensitive government documents the \uc2 FBI\uc2  seized from the former president\u8217\'20\'19s Mar-a-Lago resort were declassified, according to sources familiar with the matter.\par \par \uc2 The status of the documents has emerged as relevant to the criminal investigation surrounding Trump\u8217\'20\'19s mishandling of national security materials since it could strengthen a potential case that the former president was in violation of state secrecy laws.\par \par \uc2 Trump and advisers such as Patel have claimed repeatedly since the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/fbi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 FBI}}}\uc2  search in August that the documents bearing classification markings found at the property had in fact been declassified before the former president departed the White House.\par \par \uc2 The claims that the documents were declassified have not been supported by evidence, however, and Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/18/trump-mar-a-lago-documents-seized-fbi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have not repeated the assertions}}}\uc2  in a related legal dispute before a judge or in court filings where they could face penalties for lying.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/02/kash-patel-immunity-deal-trump-documents-doj"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DoJ mulls immunity deal for Trump ally to secure testimony in Mar-a-Lago case}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.55pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s lawyers tailored their petition specifically to supreme court justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  for reasons both practical and symbolic, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/11/02/trump-lawyers-saw-justice-thomas-as-only-chance-to-stop-2020-election-certification-00064592"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Thomas is well known for his conservative jurisprudence, but Politico notes he is also the justice responsible for handling emergency filings out of Georgia \u8211\'20\'13 which means he would get the Trump legal team\u8217\'20\'19s petition about its election conduct, Politico says.\par \par \uc2 But the goal of the filing wasn\u8217\'20\'19t necessarily to get the supreme court to act on the Trump team\u8217\'20\'19s goal of overturning the election. Instead, Politico says his attorneys hoped the supreme court would issue a temporary stay in the case, which would give them credibility with the state\u8217\'20\'19s lawmakers as they pursued a baseless claim of fraud in Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 The suit was ultimately unsuccessful.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.31pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The reckoning over January 6 continues in Washington, where members of the Oath Keepers militia group are standing trial on charges of seditious conspiracy for their actions in the assault on the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 NBC News reports a government witness has recounted a message the Oath Keepers\u8217\'20\'19s leader Stewart Rhodes wanted to be sent to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  days after the failed attempt to stop the certification of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s election win:\par \par \uc2 enltrNew: Stewart Rhodes typed a message to send to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on Jan. 10 through Jason Alpers, who is testifying on behalf of the government.\par \par \uc2 "President Trump, you can save the Republic by doing your duty as Commander in Chief... You must use the insurrection act..."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ryan J. Reilly (@ryanjreilly) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ryanjreilly/status/1587822738596630529?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 2, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltr"If you don't then Biden/Kamala will turn all that power on you, your family, and all of us. You and your family wil be imprisoned and killed...You and your children will die in prison."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ryan J. Reilly (@ryanjreilly) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ryanjreilly/status/1587822959137259520?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 2, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltr"You must do as Lincoln did. He arrested congressmen, state legislators, and issued a warrant for SCOTUS Chief Justice Taney. Take command like Washington would... Go down in history as the savior of the Republic, not a man who surrendered it..."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ryan J. Reilly (@ryanjreilly) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ryanjreilly/status/1587823269553618946?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 2, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CI am here for you and so are all my men. We will come help you if you need us. Military and police. And so will your millions of supporters.\u8221\'20\'1D -- Stewart Rhodes, in a written message to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , after the Jan. 6 attack\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ryan J. Reilly (@ryanjreilly) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ryanjreilly/status/1587823630821605377?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 2, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/08/oath-keepers-trial-evidence-civil-war"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18We must defeat them\u8217\'20\'19: new evidence details Oath Keepers\u8217\'20\'19 \u8216\'20\'18civil war\u8217\'20\'19 timeline}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.11pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump considering post-midterm announcement of new presidential campaign\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  could announce a new campaign for the White House in the days after Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s midterm election, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/2022-midterm-elections-donald-trump-41b12f18f536017920d2f74803980899"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Associated Press reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The former president has been widely expected to again run for president in 2024, despite being embroiled in a number of investigations into various scandals from his time in office, such as the campaign to overturn the 2020 election and the January 6 assault on the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 According to the AP, Trump could announce a new campaign following next week\u8217\'20\'19s vote, where Republicans are expected to retake the House from Democrats, and potentially the Senate.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m like 95% he\u8217\'20\'19s going to run,\u8221\'20\'1D his former chief of staff Reince Priebus told the AP, noting that the bigger question is if any other Republicans would bother to challenge him.\par \par \uc2 Polls indicate Trump is still the most popular of the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s potential presidential aspirants, overcoming rivals like Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Over the summer, Republicans worried Trump would announce a run before the 8 November election, giving Democrats an opportunity to shift voters\u8217\'20\'19 attention away from issues like crime and the economy and towards the possibility of a return to office by the deeply divisive chief executive.\par \par \uc2 However, the AP notes that \u8220\'20\'1Ceven as discussions are underway about potential venues and dates for a formal announcement, Trump continues to tease the possibility of declaring his intentions at one of the rallies he\u8217\'20\'19s planned for the election\u8217\'20\'19s homestretch.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.48pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The supreme court is in the midst of hearing arguments in cases it has taken up this term, but CNN reports today\u8217\'20\'19s session began with a protest in the courtroom:\par \par \uc2 enltrDISRUPTION INSIDE THE SUPREME COURT: at start of arguments at 10am, 3 women rose separately at back of the courtroom to protest overturning Roe v Wade. \u8220\'20\'1CThe right to choose will not be taken away,\u8221\'20\'1D said one. All 3 were taken out of the courtroom; none of the Justices responded.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jessica Schneider (@SchneiderCNN) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SchneiderCNN/status/1587811116931063811?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 2, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.52pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.32pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump lawyers tailored election challenge to conservative justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\par \par \uc2 As they attempted to stop \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  from assuming the presidency despite his victory in the 2020 election, lawyers for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  wanted to appeal specifically to \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 , one of the most conservative justices on the supreme court, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/11/02/trump-lawyers-saw-justice-thomas-as-only-chance-to-stop-2020-election-certification-00064592"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to emails obtained by Politico}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe want to frame things so that Thomas could be the one to issue some sort of stay or other circuit justice opinion saying Georgia is in legitimate doubt,\u8221\'20\'1D attorney Kenneth Chesebro wrote in an email to the then-president\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers on the last day of 2020.\par \par \uc2 He called a ruling from Thomas \u8220\'20\'1Cour only chance to get a favorable judicial opinion by Jan. 6, which might hold up the Georgia count in Congress.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In the weeks after he lost the 3 November 2020 election, Trump and his allies tried to convince lawmakers and officials in swing states that voted for Biden, such as Georgia, to disrupt the certification of their results and potentially delay the Democrat from taking office. They also mounted a legal campaign with the same goal.\par \par \uc2 Politico obtained the emails from \uc2 John Eastman\uc2 , another lawyer for the president who is seen as a key architect of the campaign. The emails were among a batch Eastman unsuccessfully attempted to stop the January 6 committee from obtaining, according to Politico.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.36pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.15pm GMT\par \par \uc2 In his speech this evening, PBS NewsHour reports \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will address the attack on Paul Pelosi, husband of Democratic House speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 , who was assaulted by an intruder in their San Francisco home last week:\par \par \uc2 enltrBiden will also address attack on Pelosi\u8217\'20\'19s husband and increase in political violence, per source familiar. But it will be one part of much larger speech on threats to democracy\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Laura Barr\u243\'00\'F3n-L\u243\'00\'F3pez (@lbarronlopez) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/lbarronlopez/status/1587809512567758848?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 2, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.59pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden plans primetime speech on threats to democracy\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will this evening make a speech on threats to democracy, days after an attack on the residence of the speaker of the House and as Americans prepare to cast ballots in next week\u8217\'20\'19s midterms.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/2022-midterm-elections-biden-democracy-anita-dunn-government-and-politics-16c8a7f93e6d1718bd794671d186bed3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Associated Press reports}}}\uc2  the president will speak at 7 pm eastern time at a venue near the Capitol, which was stormed by rioters incited by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  during the January 6 insurrection.\par \par \uc2 Biden \u8220\'20\'1Cwill be very clear tonight that he is speaking to people who don\u8217\'20\'19t agree with him on any issues, who don\u8217\'20\'19t agree on his agenda, but who really can unite behind this idea of this fundamental value of democracy,\u8221\'20\'1D White House senior adviser Anita Dunn said today during an event hosted by Axios.\par \par \uc2 She added that the speech is \u8220\'20\'1Cfrom Capitol Hill, because that is where there was an attempt to subvert our democracy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Democrats are in a tough battle to hold on their majorities in the House and Senate in Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s midterm elections. The Republican party, which is fielding several candidates who have refused to say if they will accept the election result and others who took part in the January 6 riot, is seen as likely to retake the House and potentially also the Senate.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.42pm GMT\par \par \uc2 While the Wisconsin GOP is hoping to use gerrymandering and legislative control to achieve their goals, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/edpilkington"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ed Pilkington}}}\uc2  reports that Republican candidates nationwide are refusing to say if they\u8217\'20\'19ll concede their races \u8211\'20\'13 even if they lose:\par \par \uc2 Last month Kari Lake, a former local TV anchor on the Fox network, joined a rightwing podcast {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.iheart.com/podcast/960-conservative-circus-w-jame-28823469/episode/the-conservative-circus-w-james-t-101625064/?cmp=web_share&embed=true"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Conservative Circus}}}\uc2  to discuss her bid to become Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s next governor.\par \par \uc2 Lake, who has been endorsed by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , began by complaining that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  had just {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/speeches-remarks/2022/09/01/remarks-by-president-bidenon-the-continued-battle-for-the-soul-of-the-nation/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 made a speech}}}\uc2  about the threat to democracy posed by election deniers like herself who claim, without evidence, that the 2020 presidential election was stolen. The US president called them \u8220\'20\'1Cextremists\u8221\'20\'1D and warned that they were preparing to repeat their subversion efforts in November\u8217\'20\'19s midterm elections.\par \par \uc2 Moments later, when Lake was asked by the podcast host a direct question about whether she would concede were she to lose her own governor\u8217\'20\'19s race against the Democrat \uc2 Katie Hobbs\uc2 , she was evasive.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/02/trump-playbook-us-midterms-republicans-election-denial"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18The Trump playbook\u8217\'20\'19: Republicans hint they will deny election results}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.26pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Earlier this week, Wisconsin\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic party chair laid out what would happen if the GOP manages to obtain supermajorities in the state legislature, wins the governor\u8217\'20\'19s office, or both.\par \par \uc2 Wisconsin is considered a swing state, pivotal to each party\u8217\'20\'19s path to the White House. Ben Wikler warns that with uncontested control of the legislature or a Republican governor, the GOP could turn the Great Lakes state into a bastion of hard-right conservatism:\par \par \uc2 enltrIn this moment, a tiny change in votes in Wisconsin could start a domino effect that could shape the future of American history. For worse, or better.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ben Wikler (@benwikler) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/benwikler/status/1587104420449460225?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 31, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrFirst, the nightmare scenario: Mandela Barnes and \uc2 Tony Evers\uc2  could lose, and Ron Johnson and \uc2 Tim Michels\uc2  could win. Republicans could get a veto-proof supermajority in our state legislature. What would happen?\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ben Wikler (@benwikler) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/benwikler/status/1587104689660764161?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 31, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrWisconsin\u8217\'20\'19s been the tipping point state in the last two presidential elections. Both of those elections came down to less than a percentage point. If democracy breaks even further in Wisconsin, the Electoral College math gets grim\u8212\'20\'14fast. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/IahUX86yxl"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/IahUX86yxl}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ben Wikler (@benwikler) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/benwikler/status/1587104748473389061?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 31, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrTim Michels, running for governor of Wisconsin, has explicitly said that his first priority will be to \u8220\'20\'1Cfix\u8221\'20\'1D the election system by signing all of the voter suppression and election subversion laws that Governor Evers, our Democratic incumbent, has vetoed. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/a0vgjS18fi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/a0vgjS18fi}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ben Wikler (@benwikler) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/benwikler/status/1587104832736960513?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 31, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrIf \uc2 Tim Michels\uc2  rigs our elections, he will likely do it before the April 4, 2023 state Supreme Court election, which will determine the balance of power on Wisconsin\u8217\'20\'19s highest court. The state court could uphold the rigging before the 2024 presidential. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/txmqPCowSn"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/txmqPCowSn}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ben Wikler (@benwikler) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/benwikler/status/1587105097078693888?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 31, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrGov Evers, on the other hand, supports fair elections and has been a brick wall to save our democracy\u8212\'20\'14refusing to concede to Republican attacks and allowing the bipartisan Wisconsin Election Commission to do its job.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ben Wikler (@benwikler) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/benwikler/status/1587105168444768258?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 31, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrIf \uc2 Tim Michels\uc2  can scrap the bipartisan Wisconsin Election Commission and install radical Republicans\u8212\'20\'14as he has promised\u8212\'20\'14every rule governing how elections function could be shaped to advance the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s partisan agenda. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/9DcK3c3CUa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/9DcK3c3CUa}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ben Wikler (@benwikler) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/benwikler/status/1587105296580763649?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 31, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrBut if that\u8217\'20\'19s not enough to give Trump a victory, and Trump still loses 2024, Michels could refuse to certify the election.\par \par \uc2 In fact, when asked about it directly, he *only* committed to certifying the election *if* he can fix the election system first. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/3mo5xWkYWj"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/3mo5xWkYWj}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ben Wikler (@benwikler) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/benwikler/status/1587105492022730760?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 31, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrTo win the electoral college majority in 2024, we\u8217\'20\'19ll need Wisconsin.\par \par \uc2 And if we lose the governor\u8217\'20\'19s race now, the path to having a free, fair, and secure presidential election becomes stunningly bleak.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ben Wikler (@benwikler) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/benwikler/status/1587105571865612292?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 31, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrIf \uc2 Tim Michels\uc2  wins, he\u8217\'20\'19s likely to sign whatever bills the Republican-dominated legislature sends him.\par \par \uc2 But the GOP has another path to control: gaining supermajorities in both chambers of our state legislature. I talked about this with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/chrislhayes?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @ChrisLHayes}}}\uc2  : {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/PIpDUeasuO"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/PIpDUeasuO}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ben Wikler (@benwikler) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/benwikler/status/1587106258586312714?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 31, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrWhile other states got better maps after redistricting, Wisconsin's GOP-controlled state Supreme Court chose the most extreme gerrymander possible\u8212\'20\'14a map literally drawn by Republicans in our state legislature to maximize their control. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/JCBry1CJjR"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/JCBry1CJjR}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ben Wikler (@benwikler) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/benwikler/status/1587106349997080576?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 31, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrThe Wisconsin GOP is incredibly close to supermajorities in the state legislature. Under these new maps, all they have to do is pick up a handful of additional legislative districts. Supermajorities are now \u8220\'20\'1Cwithin reach.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/0Fy4EziTvz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/0Fy4EziTvz}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ben Wikler (@benwikler) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/benwikler/status/1587106454380716032?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 31, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrIf the GOP gets supermajorities in the state legislature here, the governorship, or both, they can change election laws or subvert the results, and potentially move Wisconsin\u8217\'20\'19s 10 Electoral College votes into the GOP column. We cannot let that happen.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ben Wikler (@benwikler) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/benwikler/status/1587106612032012294?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 31, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.59pm GMT\par \par \uc2 GOP candidate for governor makes plain party's real goal: permanent Republican rule\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. Yesterday in Wisconsin, \uc2 Tim Michels\uc2 , who is standing as the Republican candidate for governor in Wisconsin, said the quiet part out loud when he declared: \u8220\'20\'1CRepublicans will never lose another election in Wisconsin after I\u8217\'20\'19m elected governor.\u8221\'20\'1D Wisconsin is a swing state that Democrats have relied on to win the White House, and the Republican\u8217\'20\'19s comment underscores the reality that many in the party aren\u8217\'20\'19t simply looking to win office this year \u8211\'20\'13 they\u8217\'20\'19re aiming to find ways to make their control of government permanent. And while Wisconsin is one state, there are plenty of other examples nationwide.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is happening today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  will conclude its latest meeting and almost certainly announce another interest rate increase at 2 pm eastern time. The central bank has signaled it is committed to fighting inflation, but economists warn that if borrowing costs get too high, the economy could slow further, or even enter a recession.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s infrastructure day for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , who will stump for his legislative accomplishments including the Chips act to boost American technological prowess and last year\u8217\'20\'19s $1tn overhaul to the nation\u8217\'20\'19s public works.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Six days to go until the 8 November midterm elections!\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020221102eib2001xn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
