\par\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 The attack on Paul Pelosi should be a moment of national reckoning\b0\par\par\uc2 Jill Filipovic \par \uc2 1,640 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 November 2022\par 13:32 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 All political violence is a problem, but in terms of sheer numbers, rightwing extremism is a much more significant problem than leftwing radicalism\par \par \uc2 Much of American life has gotten coarser, uglier and crueler in the years since \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  won the presidency in 2016. Even with Trump out of office, his legacy persists, and it erodes American life every day.\par \par \uc2 On Friday, in a grisly act of political violence, a man broke into the home of the speaker of the House, \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 , one of the US right\u8217\'20\'19s most vilified political figures, and attacked her husband with a hammer, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.speaker.gov/newsroom/102822-1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fracturing}}}\uc2  his skull and leaving him with serious injuries. The attacker, 42-year-old David DePape, was reportedly carrying zip ties and duct tape and yelling: \u8220\'20\'1CWhere\u8217\'20\'19s Nancy?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Paul Pelosi is lucky he wasn\u8217\'20\'19t killed \u8211\'20\'13 a hammer to the skull can certainly do the job, especially when the victim is an elderly man. And while I imagine that \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  is feeling enormous grief and guilt over the fact that her husband was nearly murdered in an attack that seemed aimed at her, she\u8217\'20\'19s also lucky she wasn\u8217\'20\'19t home at the time of the assault.\par \par \uc2 Such an extreme act should shock the conscience of the nation. Instead, it has shown just how immune to human decency and empathy the Trumpist right has become. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s son Donald Jr tweeted an image of a pair of men\u8217\'20\'19s underwear and a hammer with the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/10/31/politics/donald-trump-jr-paul-pelosi-reaction/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 caption}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1CGot my Paul Pelosi Halloween costume ready\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 His father has thus far remained silent, as have many Republican elected officials. Conservatives in the media, meanwhile, are working overtime to deny that the right holds any responsibility here, chalking this up to a random act of violence and arguing that sometimes leftists are violent, too.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s not totally wrong: a mentally disturbed man was arrested outside supreme court justice \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s house with a gun this past summer, and another {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2021/04/21/2017-baseball-field-shooting-fbi-conculsion-483993"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shot}}}\uc2  at a bunch of Republican congressmen at baseball practice in 2017, nearly killing Representative Steve Scalise.\par \par \uc2 But there are a few major differences, not least among them the fact that rightwing political violence is much more common than leftwing political violence, and that rightwing violence is much more likely to be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ccjs.umd.edu/feature/umd-led-study-shows-disparities-violence-among-extremist-groups"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fatal}}}\uc2  than leftwing violence. In the US, rightwing extremists aren\u8217\'20\'19t just more dangerous than leftwing ones, but are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.csis.org/analysis/escalating-terrorism-problem-united-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more dangerous}}}\uc2  than Islamic radicals and those inspired by the \uc2 Islamic State\uc2  and al-Qaida. Since 1994, a majority of terrorist plots within the US were hatched by rightwing radicals.\par \par \uc2 All political violence is a problem. But in terms of sheer numbers, rightwing violence is a much more significant problem than leftwing violence.\par \par \uc2 That may be, in part, because of the right wing\u8217\'20\'19s broad permission structure when it comes to unchecked misogyny, threatening and menacing political opponents, and refusing to forcefully condemn violent acts. When Scalise was shot and Kavanaugh was threatened, prominent Democrats didn\u8217\'20\'19t sit in silence. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2017/06/14/us/steve-scalise-congress-shot-alexandria-virginia.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bernie Sanders}}}\uc2 , who was reportedly the favored candidate of the man who shot Scalise, immediately came out after the shooting to say, \u8220\'20\'1CI am sickened by this despicable act,\u8221\'20\'1D and emphasized that \u8220\'20\'1Creal change can only come about through nonviolent action.\u8221\'20\'1D When the man menacing Kavanaugh was arrested, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.foxnews.com/politics/biden-condemns-actions-armed-man-arrested-near-kavanaughs-home-supports-increased-security-justices"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden}}}\uc2  condemned the man\u8217\'20\'19s actions in no uncertain terms, and supported expanded security measures for supreme court justices.\par \par \uc2 And prominent liberals with national platforms and connections to Democratic administrations didn\u8217\'20\'19t suggest dressing up as a bloody Steve Scalise or a dead \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2  on Halloween. The only prominent liberal to make such a tasteless joke - which had nothing to do with an actual assassination attempt \u8211\'20\'13 was the famously vulgar comedian {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newsweek.com/kathy-griffin-compares-consequences-beheaded-trump-photo-paul-gosars-violent-video-1647761"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kathy Griffin}}}\uc2 , who posted a gory photo of herself holding the fake severed head of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 ; for that, she lost most of her professional work and was booted from her television gigs, investigated by the Secret Service and, according to her, threatened with a charge of conspiracy to assassinate the president of the United States.\par \par \uc2 By contrast, threatening and menacing Democrats has become a staple not just of conservative big mouths on \uc2 YouTube\uc2  and talk radio, but of Republicans seeking office. Trump, notoriously, used his rallies to encourage supporters to chant \u8220\'20\'1Clock her up\u8221\'20\'1D about \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 . Republican representative \uc2 Paul Gosar{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newsweek.com/kathy-griffin-compares-consequences-beheaded-trump-photo-paul-gosars-violent-video-1647761"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tweeted}}}\uc2  a bizarre cartoon video of him killing the Democrat representative \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2  and threatening President Biden; he refused to apologize for it, and his actions were not broadly condemned on the right.\par \par \uc2 The Republican {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vox.com/policy-and-politics/2022/10/29/23430340/nancy-pelosi-paul-pelosi-political-violence-republican-attacks"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 representative from Georgia Marjorie Taylor Greene}}}\uc2  has said that Pelosi has committed treason, a crime \u8220\'20\'1Cpunishable by death\u8221\'20\'1D. The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newsweek.com/republican-confronted-over-shooting-video-tweet-fire-pelosi-hashtag-1755661"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Minnesota Republican representative Tom Emmer}}}\uc2  tweeted a video of himself shooting a gun, along with the words \u8220\'20\'1CExercising my Second Amendment rights\u8221\'20\'1D and the hashtag #FirePelosi. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/08/03/opinion/blake-masters-arizona-senate.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Blake Masters}}}\uc2 , a Republican who is running for a Senate seat in Arizona, has published campaign ads in which he is holding guns (in one of the ads, he specifies: \u8220\'20\'1CIt wasn\u8217\'20\'19t designed for hunting \u8211\'20\'13 this is designed to kill people\u8221\'20\'1D) and has said that when it comes to what he believes is a war between left and right, \u8220\'20\'1CYou can recite an eloquent poem about pacifism right before they line you up against the wall and shoot you.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Republican \uc2 Eric Greitens\uc2  ran for Senate with an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theatlantic.com/ideas/archive/2022/10/pelosi-republicans-partisan-political-violence/671934/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ad}}}\uc2  featuring him armed and breaking down a door, saying: \u8220\'20\'1CGet a Rino-hunting permit. There\u8217\'20\'19s no bagging limit, no tagging limit, and it doesn\u8217\'20\'19t expire until we save our country.\u8221\'20\'1D (Rino stands for \u8220\'20\'1CRepublican in name only\u8221\'20\'1D, slang for moderate members of the GOP.)\par \par \uc2 There is also the fact of rightwing violence against women, which seems less and less like a political liability. Republicans do not have a total lock on misogynist violence, but the number of GOP candidates {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/04/15/us/politics/republicans-accusations-women.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 accused of abuse and assault}}}\uc2  is truly stunning \u8211\'20\'13 and so too is the party\u8217\'20\'19s general shrug in response. This seems to be another outcome of the presidency of a man who bragged on video about sexually assaulting women: abusing women and girls is simply not a disqualifier for those on the Republican ticket.\par \par \uc2 And finally, there is the rightwing conspiracy-mongering that predictably draws in those who are untethered to reality, and the related rhetoric that makes fixing the invented problem a kind of life-and-death battle of good versus evil. The anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement truly pioneered this strategy, claiming \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is murder and likening \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics to Hitler\u8217\'20\'19s extermination factories during the Holocaust.\par \par \uc2 The outcome of telling people that millions of babies were being literally murdered in this clinic down the street was a predictable one: clinics attacked, women menaced and harassed, doctors and other workers murdered. And instead of losing, the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  terrorists won: the Republican party agreed with their political aims and Republican presidents appointed anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  supreme court justices, and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is no longer a protected constitutional right.\par \par \uc2 The US right has gotten even more unhinged in recent years, with many Trump supporters embracing the QAnon conspiracy theories, believing Democrats are trafficking children through pizza restaurants and in Wayfair furniture, and even mainstream Republicans are joining in on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1CStop the Steal\u8221\'20\'1D refrain that the 2020 election was stolen (it wasn\u8217\'20\'19t).\par \par \uc2 When you promulgate totally baseless, crazy ideas and convince your followers that the mainstream media are lying to them and that political opponents aren\u8217\'20\'19t just ideologically different but are literally a threat to your life, and then you insist on living in a country where people can be armed to the teeth, it\u8217\'20\'19s tough to act surprised when your followers are crazy and violent.\par \par \uc2 There is a pattern here that you just don\u8217\'20\'19t see on the left: the fetishization of deadly weapons; violence against women that goes unpunished by the party and its supporters; the kind of troubling conspiracy theories that are catnip for crazies and that demand extreme action in response; and the fantasizing about murdering one\u8217\'20\'19s political opponents, all tossed into the cauldron together.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s not a coincidence, given the hyper-masculine misogyny element to all of this, that much of the violent rightwing fantasizing is directed at women, \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  and \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2  chief among them. This isn\u8217\'20\'19t the first time \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  was targeted by violent rightwing men. During the January 6 insurrection in 2021, she was a target of the rioters who broke into the Capitol building and wandered the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FrbodynAI9E"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 halls calling her name}}}\uc2  in the kind of singsong voices usually reserved for horror movies: \u8220\'20\'1CNancy, oh Nancy! Where are you, Nancy?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Republicans have largely refused to reckon with what happened on January 6. And even now, they are treating the Pelosi attack like a sideshow instead of the real warning it is. Just hours after Pelosi\u8217\'20\'19s husband took a hammer to the head and as he was undergoing surgery to repair his cracked skull, Virginia\u8217\'20\'19s Republican governor, Glenn Youngkin, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/dc-md-va/2022/10/28/youngkin-pelosi-attack-comment-outrage/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told}}}\uc2  an audience of rally-goers: \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s no room for violence anywhere, but we\u8217\'20\'19re going to send [Pelosi] back to be with him in California.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The attack on Paul Pelosi should be a moment of reckoning. For the past several years, it has felt like the wheels on this bus are getting progressively looser, and the risks of conflict, both political and interpersonal, rising higher. Depending on how Republicans react to this moment, it could simply be a footnote \u8211\'20\'13 a bad and tragic act, but one without lasting national effects \u8211\'20\'13 or one of those historical inflection points we look back on as indicative of the dangerous turn the nation was about to make.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Jill Filipovic is the author of OK Boomer, Let\u8217\'20\'19s Talk\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020221102eib20020c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
