\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18This is a blueprint\u8217\'20\'19:  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights ballot proposal takes off in Michigan\b0\par\par\uc2 Poppy Noor in Ann Arbor \par \uc2 1,328 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 November 2022\par 20:21 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Campaigners feel groundswell of support for proposal to stop a 1931 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban from going into effect\par \par \uc2 In the spring of this year, Julie Falbaum\u8217\'20\'19s 20-year-old son walked into a frat party filled with about 50 of his peers, holding a stack of petitions. They were for a campaign to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWho wants to be a dad?\u8221\'20\'1D he yelled. Like a park-goer throwing bread to pigeons, he chucked the forms around the room and watched as dozens of young men swarmed to sign them.\par \par \uc2 The campaign to enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the state constitution was already under way here even before Roe fell, and it has become an embittered battle in Michigan \u8211\'20\'13 to keep a 90-year-old \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban off the books. Campaigners fear that ban would criminalise doctors and pregnant people and deny essential medical care, such as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.legislature.mi.gov/documents/mcl/pdf/mcl-328-1931-III.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  miscarriage medication}}}\uc2 , now that the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  no longer exists in the US.\par \par \uc2 The battle in Michigan has brought death {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.catholicnewsagency.com/news/252534/video-pro-abortion-vandals-caught-in-the-act-of-spray-painting-michigan-church"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 threats and vandalism}}}\uc2  from pro-choice militants. On the anti-choice side, it has involved dirty tactics from the Republican party, which tried to block a petition brought by nearly 800,000 Michiganders over {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/09/08/michigan-supreme-court-puts-abortion-on-november-ballot-00055774"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 formatting errors}}}\uc2 , and has peddled a wide campaign of misinformation.\par \par \uc2 Julie Falbaum, a campaigner for the yes campaign on Proposal 3, which would establish reproductive rights, believes her son\u8217\'20\'19s story \u8211\'20\'13 that he managed to collect so many signatures at a frat party without a campaign plan - is reflective of a broad coalition of support for \u8220\'20\'1CProp 3\u8221\'20\'1D, which is supported by men and women, young people and older people, Republicans and Democrats.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI see Michigan as pivotal to the future of democracy in the United States,\u8221\'20\'1D says Deirdre Roney, 60, who travelled from Los Angeles to campaign for the ballot in Detroit, where she grew up. Explaining that Detroit is the biggest voting bloc in Michigan, and that Michigan is one of the swingiest states in the country, she adds: \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a blueprint. If this passes in Michigan, other states can use it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Indeed, Michigan\u8217\'20\'19s elections are at the center of a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  debate that has spiraled to extremes. Since the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell on 24 June, almost half of US states have banned it, or tried to.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be surprised if there are more votes for [Proposal] 3 than for the governor\u8217\'20\'19s race,\u8221\'20\'1D says Jeff Timmer, a senior adviser for the Lincoln Project, a coalition of Republicans and former Republicans who campaign to keep Trump out of office.\par \par \uc2 Timmer, who was a Republican party strategist for more than 30 years, says statewide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans are turning people off the party.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Republicans have used \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  for decades as a means to motivate their pro-life religious base. And for most everybody who was engaged in that rhetoric, it was always theoretical. They never really had to worry about real-life consequences \u8211\'20\'13 and now they do,\u8221\'20\'1D Timmer says.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a simple question of: how long should my daughter, my sister, my wife, my granddaughter go to prison? Should my doctor go to prison? Quite honestly, that\u8217\'20\'19s crazy. Most rational people would say no to that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Alisha Mcneeli, 44, a lifelong Republican who lives in Grand Rapids, Michigan, will be voting for the proposal, which also enshrines contraception rights and IVF.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI have always been a pro-choice Republican,\u8221\'20\'1D says Mcneeli, 44, a community outreach director for the Michigan child protection registry.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSince I\u8217\'20\'19ve become a mother, I\u8217\'20\'19m more pro-choice than ever. Being a parent is the hardest thing \u8211\'20\'13 physically, emotionally and financially - that I\u8217\'20\'19ve ever done in my life. I wholeheartedly believe that if a woman is not ready, she should not be forced to.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A 2016 Trump voter, Mcneeli will also vote Democratic for her national representatives in the midterms. She says \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2  touting a national 15-week ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 a proposal that didn\u8217\'20\'19t pass in the Senate \u8211\'20\'13 could be enough to turn her away from the party for ever.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI feel like I\u8217\'20\'19m slowly already doing that. He promised this was not going to even be talked about at the federal level. He completely lied. That makes me sick \u8211\'20\'13 I\u8217\'20\'19m so angry about it,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Falbaum says the biggest change in attitude she has seen since she started working on the petition earlier this year is the gender split.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn the past, it was a woman\u8217\'20\'19s issue. It was: \u8216\'20\'18Talk to my wife, my girlfriend, I don\u8217\'20\'19t know about those things.\u8217\'20\'19 And now I hear men not only understanding that it\u8217\'20\'19s not a woman\u8217\'20\'19s issue, but actively supporting it,\u8221\'20\'1D says Falbaum.\par \par \uc2 Jeff Bolanger, 69, is one of them. He lives in downtown Ann Arbor, a small and relatively liberal city near Detroit that is home to the \uc2 University of Michigan\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t really think it\u8217\'20\'19s appropriate to control people\u8217\'20\'19s choices about that,\u8221\'20\'1D Bolanger said.\par \par \uc2 Joaquin Gabaldon, 30, also says he\u8217\'20\'19s voting yes when Falbaum and Roney knock his door.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI mean, it\u8217\'20\'19s healthcare, it\u8217\'20\'19s rather straightforward,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 In Wayne county\u8217\'20\'19s Grosse Pointe Park, a wealthy, mostly white, mostly Democratic area that has recently seen more {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bridgemi.com/michigan-government/changing-grosse-pointes-subtle-racism-gives-way-political-extremism"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 election deniers and Trump supporters}}}\uc2 , several people on the doorstep said they hadn\u8217\'20\'19t heard of Proposal 3, but would support it in theory. In suburban Sterling Heights, in the divided Macomb county, Ed Bristow, 60, who works in human resources, opposes Proposal 3: \u8220\'20\'1CIt just cuts into the sovereignty of the family unit.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Democrats in Michigan joke that the signage of the no campaign \u8211\'20\'13 \u8220\'20\'1CVote no. Too confusing. Too extreme\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 makes them look silly: absent a real critique of the ballot initiative, instead they focus on making voters feel they can\u8217\'20\'19t understand for themselves. But a lot of emotive misinformation is circulating, including materials from the Catholic church that suggest a number of policies could arise from voting yes, including {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.micatholic.org/assets/files/advocacy/defeat-proposal-3/proposal-3-explanation.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 child sterilisation and \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  without parental consent}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 none of which has been proposed.\par \par \uc2 Darci McConnell, the communications director for the yes campaign, cites recent polling showing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.freep.com/restricted/?return=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.freep.com%2Fstory%2Fnews%2Fpolitics%2Felections%2F2022%2F09%2F22%2Fmichigan-abortion-proposal-has-strong-support-poll-shows%2F69507400007%2F"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 64% of Michiganders support Proposal 3.}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re very invested in misinformation, because they know people don\u8217\'20\'19t want to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 that a 1931 law has no support,\u8221\'20\'1D she says of the no campaign.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s been a lot of misinformation,\u8221\'20\'1D says Pastor John Duckworth of Wayne county. \u8220\'20\'1CPeople have been saying you don\u8217\'20\'19t have to be a doctor to perform an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  [under Proposal] 3. They\u8217\'20\'19re talking about gender reassignment surgery. None of that is true.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Referring to African Americans, he said: \u8220\'20\'1CThere weren\u8217\'20\'19t many laws from 1931 that benefited my community.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNow of course, [black voters] are not a monolith,\u8221\'20\'1D he added. \u8220\'20\'1CBut alongside Roe came protections for gay marriage, for interracial marriage, for contraception \u8230\'20\'26 This is about civil rights. For people who have had their bodies controlled for hundreds of years, this is very scary.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Falbaum described a middle-aged man she saw on the day the supreme court decision leaked. She went out to set up her petition stand to get \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the ballot at a farmer\u8217\'20\'19s market in downtown Ann Arbor \u8211\'20\'13 only someone had gotten there before her.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI said, \u8216\'20\'18You\u8217\'20\'19re first in line for the concert tickets!\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D jokes Falbaum. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd he tells me his mom died in a back alley \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , protecting him and his siblings before Roe was passed \u8211\'20\'13 because she knew she could not support another child. To honour her memory, he wanted to be first to sign the petition.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 How will she feel if Michigan votes yes on 8 November, as the polls suggest?\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt feels like a culmination of my life\u8217\'20\'19s work,\u8221\'20\'1D says Falbaum, tearing up. \u8220\'20\'1CIt just makes me feel safe.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020221031eiav0010a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
