\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Paul Pelosi attack: suspect federally charged with assault and attempted kidnapping \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Gabrielle Canon in Oakland (now) and Chris Stein in Washington \par \uc2 6,985 \uc2 words\par \uc2 31 October 2022\par 21:45 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 David DePape charged by prosecutors over Friday attackSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.39pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what happened today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The supreme court{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/31/supreme-court-affirmative-action-pelosi-attack-biden-trump-politics-latest?page=with:block-635fc6eb8f083d89e8f0d349#block-635fc6eb8f083d89e8f0d349"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 began hearing arguments}}}\uc2  in two cases that its conservative majority could use to end affirmative action. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/voting-rights-ketanji-brown-jackson-us-supreme-court-college-admissions-affirmative-action-196ab930c799bcdc8b2a4a220641dd48?utm_source=homepage&utm_medium=TopNews&utm_campaign=position_03"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The AP reported}}}\uc2  that several members of the conservative bloc, who are known foes of the policy, showed no indication of changing their minds about it during ongoing oral arguments.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.justice.gov/opa/pr/man-charged-assault-and-attempted-kidnapping-following-breaking-and-entering-pelosi-residence"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The justice department announced}}}\uc2  charges against David DePape, who allegedly broke in \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s San Francisco residence and assaulted her husband, Paul Pelosi. The charges include assault and attempted kidnapping. More charges are expected form the San Francisco\u8217\'20\'19s district attorney.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/31/supreme-court-affirmative-action-pelosi-attack-biden-trump-politics-latest?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-636014458f085d2d591b274c#block-636014458f085d2d591b274c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly}}}\uc2  asked the supreme court to stop House lawmakers from getting his tax returns.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden will reunite with \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  in Philadelphia {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/31/supreme-court-affirmative-action-pelosi-attack-biden-trump-politics-latest?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-635fe5618f08fadea4d617f7#block-635fe5618f08fadea4d617f7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on Saturday}}}\uc2  to campaign for the state\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic nominees for Senate and governor.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Democratshave a slight advantage in three crucial Senate races, and are in a dead heat for a fourth, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/31/supreme-court-affirmative-action-pelosi-attack-biden-trump-politics-latest?page=with:block-635fca078f083d89e8f0d368#block-635fca078f083d89e8f0d368"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a New York Times poll}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 - Chris Stein and Gabrielle Canon\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.16pm GMT\par \par \uc2 In the midst of midterms fervor, some Republicans have also used the attack as a chance to tout their \u8220\'20\'1Ctough on crime\u8221\'20\'1D agendas.\par \par \uc2 Texas Congressman Lance Gooden tried to blame Democrats for the attack, responding defensively to evidence that DePape may have been spurred to violence by far-right rhetoric. Others include Representative \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2 , Republican candidate Kari Lake, and former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.forbes.com/sites/saradorn/2022/10/31/trump-calls-paul-pelosi-attack-terrible-and-joins-gop-in-linking-assault-to-crime-trends/?utm_campaign=forbes&utm_source=twitter&utm_medium=social&utm_term=Gordie&sh=56b6752187bd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 who all blamed Democrats for not doing more}}}\uc2  to crack down on violent crime.\par \par \uc2 enltr. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KariLake?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @KariLake}}}\uc2  @ her event today:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 , well, she\u8217\'20\'19s got protection when she\u8217\'20\'19s in DC -- apparently her house doesn\u8217\'20\'19t have a lot of protection.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The crowd burst into laughter and the moderator was laughing so hard he covered his face with his notes. From {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KateSullivanDC?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @KateSullivanDC}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyung Lah (@KyungLahCNN) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KyungLahCNN/status/1587188182847660032?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 31, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 From Forbes:\par \par \uc2 Americans\u8217\'20\'19 concerns about crime have increased over the past year, particularly among Republicans, leading GOP candidates to make the issue a central focus of their midterm campaigns. Nearly 80% of respondents in a recent Gallup poll said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.forbes.com/sites/nicholasreimann/2022/10/28/americans-more-worried-about-violent-crime-as-republicans-make-it-a-top-midterm-issue/?sh=56329845555d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 they believe crime is rising}}}\uc2  nationally, while 56% think crime is rising where they live.\par \par \uc2 While there\u8217\'20\'19s an increasing perception of worsening crime, there\u8217\'20\'19s isn\u8217\'20\'19t strong data to support it. \uc2 Forbes\uc2  also highlighted how murder rates dropped 2.4% in the largest US cities this year, according to Major Cities Chiefs Association and violent crimes dipped 1% per \uc2 FBI\uc2  statistics.\par \par \uc2 But political divisiveness and aggressive rhetoric is fueling new concerns about the increase in attacks against public officials from both parties.\par \par \uc2 enltrLet\u8217\'20\'19s keep pretending that we don\u8217\'20\'19t know the motivation for the attack on Paul Pelosi {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/3ySXnsD3FD"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/3ySXnsD3FD}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Judd Legum (@JuddLegum) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JuddLegum/status/1587188230507610115?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 31, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 The New York Times{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/10/01/us/politics/violent-threats-lawmakers.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2  that there\u8217\'20\'19s been a tenfold increase in threats of political violence since Trump\u8217\'20\'19s election and representatives are increasingly worried about their safety.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be surprised if a senator or House member were killed,\u8221\'20\'1D Senator \uc2 Susan Collins{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/10/01/us/politics/violent-threats-lawmakers.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told the New York Times}}}\uc2  . \u8220\'20\'1CWhat started with abusive phone calls is now translating into active threats of violence and real violence.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.22pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.47pm GMT\par \par \uc2 In the aftermath of the attack, conservatives and divisive online personalities have floated conspiracy theories questioning the attack against Paul Pelosi and have helped fuel new rounds of misinformation.\par \par \uc2 From \uc2 Rolling Stone\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 Because DePape had a history of blogging about {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.rollingstone.com/politics/politics-news/david-depape-alleged-paul-pelosi-attacker-shared-qanon-beliefs-1234620507/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 far-right ideas}}}\uc2  and even dabbled in QAnon conspiracy theories, the GOP has scrambled to deny that this was an attempted assassination of a leading Democrat. Some have gone as far as peddling a conspiracy theory of their own. An \u8220\'20\'1Copinion\u8221\'20\'1D piece in the fake news publication the Santa Monica Observer falsely claimed that DePape was a sex worker hired by Pelosi and the two had gotten into a physical dispute. The piece was amplified by, among others, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.rollingstone.com/politics/politics-news/paul-pelosi-conspiracy-theory-trends-elon-musk-1234621217/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Elon Musk}}}\uc2 , who later deleted his tweeted link without explanation or apology.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 San Francisco District Attorney Brooke Jenkins told reporters Sunday t hat there is no evidence of a connection between the two men and details released by \uc2 FBI\uc2  officials Monday also counter the conspiratorial claims.\par \par \uc2 Musk, the new owner of \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , has come under criticism for spreading the misinformation, sparking concerns that he will do little to curb conspiracies amplified on the social media site.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2022/oct/31/elon-musk-paul-pelosi-tweet-twitter"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Elon Musk\u8217\'20\'19s Paul Pelosi tweet proves he has no business running Twitter | Robert Reich}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf Musk\u8217\'20\'19s tweet doesn\u8217\'20\'19t raise bright red warning signs all over the world about his judgment and character, just days after he took over one of the planet\u8217\'20\'19s largest and most influential media machines, I don\u8217\'20\'19t know what will,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Robert Reich\uc2 , the former US secretary of labor {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2022/oct/31/elon-musk-paul-pelosi-tweet-twitter?utm_term=Autofeed&CMP=twt_gu&utm_medium&utm_source=Twitter#Echobox=1667225653"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote}}}\uc2  in an editorial for the Guardian. \u8220\'20\'1CThat Musk would choose this tragedy to demonstrate the disgusting extremes such hateful lies can reach is another indictment of his character and judgment.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.28pm GMT\par \par \uc2 During the terrifying ordeal, Paul Pelosi was able to dial 9-1-1 from a bathroom, court documents show, and officials have highlighted how the quick actions of the dispatcher may have saved his life.\par \par \uc2 With the line open after placing the emergency call, the dispatcher could hear the conversation between assailant David DePape and Pelosi. Two minutes later, the police arrived.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI truly believe, based on what I know, that it was lifesaving,\u8221\'20\'1D San Francisco District Attorney Brook Jenkins {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abc7news.com/paul-pelosi-suspect-charges-attack-david-depape-prosecutor/12401427/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told}}}\uc2  ABC News. Jenkins is expected to file additional charges on Monday afternoon.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.56pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  is far from the only Washington politician facing threats. Earlier today, Democratic congressman \uc2 Eric Swalwell\uc2  detailed just how menacing the atmosphere has become:\par \par \uc2 enltr. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepSwalwell?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @RepSwalwell}}}\uc2  (D-CA) says his chief of staff spends 10 hours per week dealing with threats to him and his staff:\par \par \uc2 "We have spent hundreds of thousands of dollars in security for myself and my staff. It almost rewards people who want to make threats." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/kvfA1GENb1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/kvfA1GENb1}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1587152782779305985?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 31, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.39pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The San Francisco Chronicle has more details about David DePape, who is now facing federal charges over Friday\u8217\'20\'19s attack on Paul Pelosi.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe has been homeless. This person really does suffer from mental illness and that is probably why he was there at 2am,\u8221\'20\'1D DePape\u8217\'20\'19s longtime partner Oxane \u8220\'20\'1CGypsy\u8221\'20\'1D Taub {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sfchronicle.com/bayarea/article/Ex-girlfriend-of-suspect-in-Paul-Pelosi-attack-17545968.php"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told the Chronicle in an interview}}}\uc2 . She said DePape used drugs and struggled with mental illness, to the point that he thought \u8220\'20\'1Che was Jesus for a year.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The story paints a picture of DePape\u8217\'20\'19s erratic life and bouts of homelessness that led to him being consumed by conspiracy theories, culminating in his attack on the Democratic House speaker\u8217\'20\'19s husband.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from the Chronicle:\par \par \uc2 Taub remembered DePape, 42, as a \u8220\'20\'1Cshy and sweet\u8221\'20\'1D person who once supported her well-documented fight against San Francisco\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sfchronicle.com/bayarea/article/S-F-couple-pulls-off-their-nude-wedding-5079692.php"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 public nudity laws}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CDavid never appeared nude in any of my events even though he was encouraged to,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CHe was uncomfortable.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 When the pair met in Hawaii in 2000, she said, DePape \u8220\'20\'1Cdidn\u8217\'20\'19t know anything about politics,\u8221\'20\'1D but came to share her fervor for many progressive causes \u8212\'20\'14 though Taub also espoused conspiracy theories about the September 2001 terrorist attacks in New York and Washington, D.C.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t think he became a Trump supporter,\u8221\'20\'1D Taub said Sunday. \u8220\'20\'1CHe was against the government, but if anything he was opposed to the shadow government, against the people who really run the government and use politicians as puppets. Like Trump was a puppet. David and I were against the shadow government.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Authorities say DePape, who most recently lived in Richmond, broke into the Pelosi home in San Francisco early Friday morning looking for the House speaker but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sfchronicle.com/crime/article/Suspect-in-Paul-Pelosi-attack-was-looking-for-17545493.php"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 found her husband alone}}}\uc2 . It\u8217\'20\'19s not clear whether the intruder drove to the home or traveled there another way.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.49pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.18pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The justice department\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.justice.gov/opa/press-release/file/1548106/download?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 complaint}}}\uc2  for its charges against David DePape contains harrowing details of the assault on Paul Pelosi.\par \par \uc2 Here is what San Francisco police officers found when they responded to a 911 call at the Pelosi residence:\par \par \uc2 At 2:31 a.m., San Francisco Police Department (\u8220\'20\'1CSFPD\u8221\'20\'1D) Officer Colby Wilmes responded to the Pelosi residence, California and knocked on the front door. When the door was opened, Pelosi and DePape were both holding a hammer with one hand and DePape had his other hand holding onto Pelosi\u8217\'20\'19s forearm. Pelosi greeted the officers. The officers asked them what was going on. DePape responded that everything was good. Officers then asked Pelosi and DePape to drop the hammer. DePape pulled the hammer from Pelosi\u8217\'20\'19s hand and swung the hammer, striking Pelosi in the head. Officers immediately went inside and were able to restrain DePape.\par \par \uc2 Police found zip ties in the Pelosi residence that they said belonged to DePape, as well as retrieved from his backpack \u8220\'20\'1Ca roll of tape, white rope, one hammer, one pair of rubber and cloth gloves, and a journal.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what Paul Pelosi told a police officer as he was going to the hospital:\par \par \uc2 Pelosi stated he had never seen DePape before. Pelosi was asleep when DePape came into Pelosi\u8217\'20\'19s bedroom and stated he wanted to talk to \u8220\'20\'1CNancy.\u8221\'20\'1D When Pelosi told him that Nancy was not there, DePape stated that he would sit and wait. Pelosi stated that his wife would not be home for several days and then DePape reiterated that he would wait. Pelosi was able to go into the bathroom which is when he was able to call 9- 1-1. Pelosi stated that when the officers arrived, that was when DePape struck him with the hammer.\par \par \uc2 Here is what DePape told San Francisco police in an interview following his arrest:\par \par \uc2 DePape stated that he was going to hold Nancy hostage and talk to her. If Nancy were to tell DePape the \u8220\'20\'1Ctruth,\u8221\'20\'1D he would let her go, and if she \u8220\'20\'1Clied,\u8221\'20\'1D he was going to break \u8220\'20\'1Cher kneecaps.\u8221\'20\'1D DePape was certain that Nancy would not have told the \u8220\'20\'1Ctruth.\u8221\'20\'1D In the course of the interview, DePape articulated he viewed Nancy as the \u8220\'20\'1Cleader of the pack\u8221\'20\'1D of lies told by the Democratic Party. DePape also later explained that by breaking Nancy\u8217\'20\'19s kneecaps, she would then have to be wheeled into Congress, which would show other Members of Congress there were consequences to actions.\par \par \uc2 The complaints adds that DePape \u8220\'20\'1Cexplained that he did not leave after Pelosi\u8217\'20\'19s call to 9-1-1 because, much like the American founding fathers with the British, he was fighting against tyranny without the option of surrender. DePape reiterated this sentiment elsewhere in the interview.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.57pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Pelosi assault suspect facing federal assault, attempted kidnapping charges\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.justice.gov/opa/pr/man-charged-assault-and-attempted-kidnapping-following-breaking-and-entering-pelosi-residence"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The justice department has announced}}}\uc2  charges against David DePape, who was arrested on Friday for allegedly breaking in to House speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s San Francisco residence and assaulting her husband, Paul Pelosi.\par \par \uc2 DePape will face a charge of assault on a family member of a US official in retaliation for their work, which carries a maximum sentence of 30 years in prison, the justice department said. He will also face a charge of attempting to kidnap a US official over their work, for which he could face a maximum of 20 years in prison.\par \par \uc2 Paul Pelosi, who was injured in the attack. Photograph: Mike Theiler/Reuters\par \par \uc2 Following DePape\u8217\'20\'19s early Friday morning arrest for the attack, which left Paul Pelosi needing surgery for a skull fracture along with other injuries, San Francisco\u8217\'20\'19s police chief announced DePape was being held on suspicion of several charges, including attempted murder. The city\u8217\'20\'19s district attorney is expected to formally level charges against him today, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sfchronicle.com/crime/article/Paul-Pelosi-attack-Suspect-David-DePape-expected-17547161.php"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the San Francisco Chronicle reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.03pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.37pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump asks supreme court to stop House lawmakers from getting tax returns\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has filed an emergency petition to the supreme court, asking it to halt the release of six years of his tax returns to the House ways and means committee, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.bloomberglaw.com/us-law-week/trump-asks-supreme-court-to-block-disclosure-of-his-tax-returns"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bloomberg Law reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Internal Revenue Service\uc2  was on 3 November expected to turn over the documents to the Democratic-led committee, after the former president lost repeated lower court decisions to stop Congress from seeing the returns.\par \par \uc2 Trump defied political norms and refused to turn over his tax filings during his first run for the presidency in 2016, saying they were being audited. He maintained that stance throughout his presidency and afterwards.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on the petition, from Bloomberg Law:\par \par \uc2 The case presents \u8220\'20\'1Cimportant questions about the separation of powers that will affect every future President,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers argued. Allowing the House Ways and Means Committee to obtain a president\u8217\'20\'19s tax returns would \u8220\'20\'1Crender the office of the Presidency vulnerable to invasive information demands from political opponents in the legislative branch,\u8221\'20\'1D they added.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers also questioned the committee\u8217\'20\'19s reasons for why it wanted his financial records, claiming the true purpose was to release Trump\u8217\'20\'19s tax documents \u8220\'20\'1Cto the public for the sake of exposure.\u8221\'20\'1D They argued that the judges who initially heard the case showed too much deference to the committee and ran afoul of a balancing test laid out earlier by the Supreme Court in a fight over Congress\u8217\'20\'19 access to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s financial records, Trump v Mazars.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s request to stop the committee from immediately getting the documents will go to Chief Justice \uc2 John Roberts\uc2 . Roberts, who handles emergency matters out of the US Court of Appeals for the DC Circuit, could act on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s request by himself or circulate it to the other justices for a vote.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.52pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.21pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Supreme court conservatives indicate opposition to affirmative action\par \par \uc2 The six-justice conservative majority on the supreme court has shown skepticism towards universities\u8217\'20\'19 race-based admissions policies during oral arguments today, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 The court is hearing two cases concerning the University of North Carolina and \uc2 Harvard University\uc2 , in which the court\u8217\'20\'19s six conservative justices could potentially ban the use of race as a factor in college admissions, a practice known as affirmative action.\par \par \uc2 Such a decision would be the latest example of the court overturning longstanding precedent, after five of its nine justices earlier this year struck down Roe v Wade and allowed states to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/voting-rights-ketanji-brown-jackson-us-supreme-court-college-admissions-affirmative-action-196ab930c799bcdc8b2a4a220641dd48?utm_source=homepage&utm_medium=TopNews&utm_campaign=position_03"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The AP reports}}}\uc2  that several members of the conservative bloc are known foes of the policy, and showed no indication of changing their minds about it during ongoing oral arguments in the two cases.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from the AP\u8217\'20\'19s story:\par \par \uc2 During arguments in the first of two cases, the court sounded split along ideological lines on the issue of affirmative action.\par \par \uc2 Justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 , the court\u8217\'20\'19s second Black justice who has a long record of opposition to affirmative action programs, noted he didn\u8217\'20\'19t go to racially diverse schools. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve heard the word \u8216\'20\'18diversity\u8217\'20\'19 quite a few times and I don\u8217\'20\'19t have a clue what it means,\u8221\'20\'1D the conservative justice said at one point. At another point he said: \u8220\'20\'1CTell me what the educational benefits are?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Justice \uc2 Amy Coney Barrett\uc2 , another conservative, pointed to one of the court\u8217\'20\'19s previous affirmative action cases and said it anticipated an end to the use of affirmative action, saying it was \u8220\'20\'1Cdangerous, and it has to have an end point.\u8221\'20\'1D When, she asked, is that end point?\par \par \uc2 Justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  likened affirmative action to a race in which a minority applicant gets to \u8220\'20\'1Cstart five yards closer to the finish line.\u8221\'20\'1D But liberal Justice \uc2 Sonia Sotomayor\uc2 , the court\u8217\'20\'19s first Hispanic justice, rejected that comparison saying what universities are doing is looking at students as a whole.\par \par \uc2 Justice \uc2 Ketanji Brown Jackson\uc2 , the court\u8217\'20\'19s newest justice and its first Black female, also said that race was being used at the University of North Carolina as part of a broad review of applicants along 40 different factors.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re looking at the full person with all of these characteristics,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Justice \uc2 Elena Kagan\uc2  called universities the \u8220\'20\'1Cpipelines to leadership in our society\u8221\'20\'1D and suggested that without affirmative action minority enrollment will drop.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI thought part of what it meant to be an American and to believe in American pluralism is that actually our institutions, you know, are reflective of who we are as a people in all our variety,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 The Supreme Court has twice upheld race-conscious college admissions programs in the past 19 years, including just six years ago.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.58pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Republican and Democratic political leaders condemned Friday\u8217\'20\'19s attack on Paul Pelosi, husband to speaker of the House \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 . But one of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s sons used it as an opportunity for insults, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/martin-pengelly"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Martin Pengelly}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 In the aftermath of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/30/paul-pelosi-attack-called-911-from-bathroom"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 attack on Paul Pelosi}}}\uc2 , amid rising concern over rightwing figures stoking violence against political opponents, \uc2 Donald Trump Jr\uc2  posted online a crude meme featuring a hammer, the weapon used to attack the husband of the House speaker, \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 , on Friday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COMG,\u8221\'20\'1D the former president\u8217\'20\'19s son wrote next to the picture, which also had the caption \u8220\'20\'1CGot my Paul Pelosi Halloween costume ready\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The internet backlash was swift but Trump Jr, a full-time provocateur and surrogate for his father, doubled down equally swiftly \u8211\'20\'13 posting another, this time clearly homophobic, meme which appears to reference a baseless conspiracy theory about the assault.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/31/donald-trump-jr-misinformation-memes-paul-pelosi-hammer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump Jr posts crude memes making light of attack on Paul Pelosi}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.23pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Ohio congressman Brad Wenstrup is grieving after his niece died among more than 150 people killed in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/oct/31/how-did-the-seoul-itaewon-halloween-crowd-crush-happen-unfolded-a-visual-guide"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a crowd crush}}}\uc2  during Halloween celebrations in South Korea.\par \par \uc2 Wenstrup was the uncle of 20-year-old \uc2 University of Kentucky\uc2  nursing student Anne Marie Gieske, who was killed as a crowd of mostly young people flooded Itaewon\u8217\'20\'19s narrow, sloping streets on Saturday. In a statement from his office, the Republican member of the \uc2 US House of Representatives\uc2  said he and his wife, Monica, were mourning their niece, whom he described as \u8220\'20\'1Ca gift from God to our family\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 File photo of Republican US congressman Brad Wenstrup of Ohio. Photograph: Erin Scott/Reuters\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe loved her so much,\u8221\'20\'1D Wenstrup said.\par \par \uc2 Gieske\u8217\'20\'19s parents, Dan and Madonna Gieske, added: \u8220\'20\'1CWe are completely devastated and heartbroken over the loss of Anne Marie. She was a bright light loved by all.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnne\u8217\'20\'19s final gift to us was dying in the state of sanctifying grace. We know we will one day be reunited with her in God\u8217\'20\'19s kingdom.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Anne Marie Gieske was one of at least {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KasulisK/status/1587026120062693377/photo/1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 two young Americans}}}\uc2  to die in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/oct/31/grief-over-loved-ones-lost-in-seoul-deadly-halloween-crowd-crush-itaewon"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 South Korea\u8217\'20\'19s worst-ever crowd crush}}}\uc2 . The other was Steven Blesi, also 20 and a foreign exchange student from Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Kennesaw State University\uc2  who was out celebrating having finished some academic exams.\par \par \uc2 Blesi\u8217\'20\'19s father, Steve, told the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  that learning of his son\u8217\'20\'19s death was like being stabbed \u8220\'20\'1Ca hundred million times simultaneously\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Wenstrup has represented Ohio in the US House since 2013. He is running for re-election against Democratic challenger Samantha Meadows during the 8 November midterms.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.05pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Voters won\u8217\'20\'19t just elect lawmakers and governors in the 8 November elections. In Michigan, they\u8217\'20\'19ll choose whether or not to allow a 90-year-old \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban to go into effect. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/poppy-noor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Poppy Noor}}}\uc2  reports from Ann Arbor:\par \par \uc2 In the spring of this year, Julie Falbaum\u8217\'20\'19s 20-year-old son walked into a frat party filled with about 50 of his peers, holding a stack of petitions. They were for a campaign to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWho wants to be a dad?\u8221\'20\'1D he yelled. Like a park-goer throwing bread to pigeons, he chucked the forms around the room and watched as dozens of young men swarmed to sign them.\par \par \uc2 The campaign to enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the state constitution was already under way here even before Roe fell, and it has become an embittered battle in Michigan \u8211\'20\'13 to keep a 90-year-old \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban off the books. Campaigners fear that ban would criminalise doctors and pregnant people and deny essential medical care, such as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.legislature.mi.gov/documents/mcl/pdf/mcl-328-1931-III.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  miscarriage medication}}}\uc2 , now that the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  no longer exists in the US.\par \par \uc2 The battle in Michigan has brought death {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.catholicnewsagency.com/news/252534/video-pro-abortion-vandals-caught-in-the-act-of-spray-painting-michigan-church"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 threats and vandalism}}}\uc2  from pro-choice militants. On the anti-choice side, it has involved dirty tactics from the Republican party, which tried to block a petition brought by nearly 800,000 Michiganders over {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/09/08/michigan-supreme-court-puts-abortion-on-november-ballot-00055774"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 formatting errors}}}\uc2 , and has peddled a wide campaign of misinformation.\par \par \uc2 Julie Falbaum, a campaigner for the yes campaign on Proposal 3, which would establish reproductive rights, believes her son\u8217\'20\'19s story \u8211\'20\'13 that he managed to collect so many signatures at a frat party without a campaign plan - is reflective of a broad coalition of support for \u8220\'20\'1CProp 3\u8221\'20\'1D, which is supported by men and women, young people and older people, Republicans and Democrats.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI see {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/michigan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Michigan}}}\uc2  as pivotal to the future of democracy in the United States,\u8221\'20\'1D says Deirdre Roney, 60, who travelled from Los Angeles to campaign for the ballot in Detroit, where she grew up. Explaining that Detroit is the biggest voting bloc in Michigan, and that Michigan is one of the swingiest states in the country, she adds: \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a blueprint. If this passes in Michigan, other states can use it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/31/michigan-abortion-proposal-3-campaign"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18This is a blueprint\u8217\'20\'19: \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights ballot proposal takes off in Michigan}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.48pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will this afternoon {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/31/supreme-court-affirmative-action-pelosi-attack-biden-trump-politics-latest?page=with:block-635ff6cd8f08fadea4d618dc#block-635ff6cd8f08fadea4d618dc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 mull levying a tax on energy companies}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19 profits in a speech planned for 4:30 pm. The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/31/supreme-court-affirmative-action-pelosi-attack-biden-trump-politics-latest?page=with:block-635fdfe88f08497943234e13#block-635fdfe88f08497943234e13"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 last-minute address}}}\uc2  comes as Democrats look to reclaim credibility with voters on their handling of the economy ahead of next week\u8217\'20\'19s midterm elections, which will decide the balance of power in Congress for the coming two years.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else happened today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden will reunite with \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  in Philadelphia {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/31/supreme-court-affirmative-action-pelosi-attack-biden-trump-politics-latest?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-635fe5618f08fadea4d617f7#block-635fe5618f08fadea4d617f7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on Saturday}}}\uc2  to campaign for the state\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic nominees for Senate and governor.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Democratshave a slight advantage in three crucial Senate races, and are in a dead heat for a fourth, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/31/supreme-court-affirmative-action-pelosi-attack-biden-trump-politics-latest?page=with:block-635fca078f083d89e8f0d368#block-635fca078f083d89e8f0d368"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a New York Times poll}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The supreme court{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/31/supreme-court-affirmative-action-pelosi-attack-biden-trump-politics-latest?page=with:block-635fc6eb8f083d89e8f0d349#block-635fc6eb8f083d89e8f0d349"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is hearing arguments}}}\uc2  in two cases that its conservative majority could use to end affirmative action.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.31pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden to threaten windfall tax on oil companies as profits surge\par \par \uc2 In his speech this afternoon on oil companies\u8217\'20\'19 record profits, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will discuss whether to impose a windfall tax on energy firms, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/biden-business-prices-government-and-politics-ba71f46a47c2be5a2ffd58a258796260"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Associated Press reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Citing a person familiar with the matter, Biden will raise the possibility of a tax aimed specifically at energy companies\u8217\'20\'19 profits as a way to encourage them to lower prices at the pump.\par \par \uc2 The president is set to speak at 4:30 pm eastern time to \u8220\'20\'1Crespond to reports over recent days of major oil companies making record-setting profits even as they refuse to help lower prices at the pump for the American people,\u8221\'20\'1D the White House announced earlier today. Rising gas prices have been a major drag on Biden and his Democratic allies\u8217\'20\'19 public support ahead of the 8 November midterms, where polls indicate the state of the economy is voters\u8217\'20\'19 top issue.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.11pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Wisconsin isn\u8217\'20\'19t just the site of one of the Democratic party\u8217\'20\'19s few chances to add to their majority in the Senate \u8211\'20\'13 it\u8217\'20\'19s also pivotal to the future of American democracy, the state\u8217\'20\'19s party chair says.\par \par \uc2 In a lengthy \uc2 Twitter\uc2  thread, Ben Wikler lays out what\u8217\'20\'19s at stake in the governorship and statehouse races in the perennial swing state:\par \par \uc2 enltrIn this moment, a tiny change in votes in Wisconsin could start a domino effect that could shape the future of American history. For worse, or better.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ben Wikler (@benwikler) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/benwikler/status/1587104420449460225?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 31, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrWisconsin is a policy laboratory. If the GOP makes their control voter-proof here, they\u8217\'20\'19ll take those policies nationwide. Read this important story for details. But recognize, too, that this week could open the door to dismantling their control. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/wjh4jG6iq6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/wjh4jG6iq6}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ben Wikler (@benwikler) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/benwikler/status/1587104628927234049?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 31, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrFirst, the nightmare scenario: Mandela Barnes and \uc2 Tony Evers\uc2  could lose, and Ron Johnson and \uc2 Tim Michels\uc2  could win. Republicans could get a veto-proof supermajority in our state legislature. What would happen?\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ben Wikler (@benwikler) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/benwikler/status/1587104689660764161?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 31, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrWisconsin\u8217\'20\'19s been the tipping point state in the last two presidential elections. Both of those elections came down to less than a percentage point. If democracy breaks even further in Wisconsin, the Electoral College math gets grim\u8212\'20\'14fast. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/IahUX86yxl"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/IahUX86yxl}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ben Wikler (@benwikler) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/benwikler/status/1587104748473389061?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 31, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrTim Michels, running for governor of Wisconsin, has explicitly said that his first priority will be to \u8220\'20\'1Cfix\u8221\'20\'1D the election system by signing all of the voter suppression and election subversion laws that Governor Evers, our Democratic incumbent, has vetoed. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/a0vgjS18fi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/a0vgjS18fi}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ben Wikler (@benwikler) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/benwikler/status/1587104832736960513?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 31, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrIf \uc2 Tim Michels\uc2  rigs our elections, he will likely do it before the April 4, 2023 state Supreme Court election, which will determine the balance of power on Wisconsin\u8217\'20\'19s highest court. The state court could uphold the rigging before the 2024 presidential. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/txmqPCowSn"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/txmqPCowSn}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ben Wikler (@benwikler) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/benwikler/status/1587105097078693888?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 31, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrGov Evers, on the other hand, supports fair elections and has been a brick wall to save our democracy\u8212\'20\'14refusing to concede to Republican attacks and allowing the bipartisan Wisconsin Election Commission to do its job.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ben Wikler (@benwikler) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/benwikler/status/1587105168444768258?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 31, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrIf \uc2 Tim Michels\uc2  can scrap the bipartisan Wisconsin Election Commission and install radical Republicans\u8212\'20\'14as he has promised\u8212\'20\'14every rule governing how elections function could be shaped to advance the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s partisan agenda. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/9DcK3c3CUa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/9DcK3c3CUa}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ben Wikler (@benwikler) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/benwikler/status/1587105296580763649?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 31, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrBut if that\u8217\'20\'19s not enough to give Trump a victory, and Trump still loses 2024, Michels could refuse to certify the election.\par \par \uc2 In fact, when asked about it directly, he *only* committed to certifying the election *if* he can fix the election system first. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/3mo5xWkYWj"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/3mo5xWkYWj}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ben Wikler (@benwikler) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/benwikler/status/1587105492022730760?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 31, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrTo win the electoral college majority in 2024, we\u8217\'20\'19ll need Wisconsin.\par \par \uc2 And if we lose the governor\u8217\'20\'19s race now, the path to having a free, fair, and secure presidential election becomes stunningly bleak.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ben Wikler (@benwikler) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/benwikler/status/1587105571865612292?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 31, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.51pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Bernie Sanders\uc2  is heading to Wisconsin to drum up support for Democratic candidates, the Associated Press reports:\par \par \uc2 enltr. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BernieSanders?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @BernieSanders}}}\uc2  announces four stops in Wisconsin this week to support Democratic candidates and drive turnout\par \par \uc2 Sanders plans to be in Eau Claire, La Crosse and Madison on Friday and in \uc2 Oshkosh\uc2  on Saturday\par \par \uc2 His visit comes after former President {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BarackObama?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @BarackObama}}}\uc2  was in Milwaukee\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Scott Bauer (@sbauerAP) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/sbauerAP/status/1587090612930609156?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 31, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 The state is home to one of Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 other Senate pickup opportunities this year, with lieutenant governor Mandela Barnes trying to unseat incumbent Republican Ron Johnson. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/2022-election-forecast/senate/wisconsin/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Polls have generally shown}}}\uc2  Johnson with the advantage here.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s also home to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/2022-election-forecast/governor/wisconsin/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a very tight governors race}}}\uc2 , where Democratic incumbent \uc2 Tony Evers\uc2  is up for a second term against GOP challenger \uc2 Tim Michels\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.33pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden is making a brief trip to New York City to attend a memorial service before returning to the White House later today.\par \par \uc2 His administration has not previously announced who the memorial was in memory of, but the Associated Press reports it is secretary of state \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s father:\par \par \uc2 enltrBiden and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/FLOTUS?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @FLOTUS}}}\uc2  are in New York, attending a private memorial service for Ambassador Donald Blinken, father of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SecBlinken?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @SecBlinken}}}\uc2 , per WH.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 darlene superville (@dsupervilleap) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/dsupervilleap/status/1587101096719384577?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 31, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Donald Blinken died late last month.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.17pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden to reunite with Obama for Pennsylvania Democratic rally\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will on Saturday again join forces with \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 , under whom he served as vice-president, to rally for Pennsylvania\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic senate candidate \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2  and gubernatorial nominee \uc2 Josh Shapiro\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The rally organized by the \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  in Philadelphia comes as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/31/supreme-court-affirmative-action-pelosi-attack-biden-trump-politics-latest?page=with:block-635fca078f083d89e8f0d368#block-635fca078f083d89e8f0d368"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 polls show}}}\uc2  Fetterman with only a slight advantage over his Republican challenger Mehmet Oz. Pennsylvania\u8217\'20\'19s Senate seat is being vacated by a Republican, and represents one of Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 best opportunities to add to their tiny majority in Congress\u8217\'20\'19s upper chamber.\par \par \uc2 Shapiro {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/polls/governor/2022/pennsylvania/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is believed to be in a much better position}}}\uc2  in his race against Republican \uc2 Doug Mastriano\uc2 , a 2020 election denier who backs banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after six weeks of pregnancy and charging women who violate the prohibition with murder.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/24/doug-mastriano-pennsylvania-republicans-trump-governor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Doug Mastriano: is the Trump-backed election denier too extreme to win?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.56pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden to address oil companies 'record-setting profits' despite high pump prices\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will today make a speech about oil companies\u8217\'20\'19 \u8220\'20\'1Crecord-setting profits\u8221\'20\'1D even as prices for gasoline remain elevated across the United States.\par \par \uc2 The address was announced just minutes ago by the White House, which typically sets out the president\u8217\'20\'19s schedule a day in advance, with rare changes.\par \par \uc2 At 4:30 pm eastern time, \u8220\'20\'1Cthe president will respond to reports over recent days of major oil companies making record-setting profits even as they refuse to help lower prices at the pump for the American people,\u8221\'20\'1D according to the president\u8217\'20\'19s updated schedule. The speech will take place at the White House. Biden is currently in New York City, attending a \u8220\'20\'1Cprivate memorial service\u8221\'20\'1D for a party whose name has not been disclosed.\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s presidency thus far has been defined by inflation that has risen at rates not seen since the 1980s, sinking his approval rating and boosting Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 chances of taking control of Congress in next week\u8217\'20\'19s midterm elections. Americans are particularly sensitive to pump prices, and the nation\u8217\'20\'19s average gas price hit an all-time high over the summer, before declining.\par \par \uc2 Much of the increase has been caused by trends and disruptions in global oil markets brought about by the pandemic and Russia\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Ukraine, though the GOP has sought to place the blame squarely on the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s energy policies. The president and his Democratic allies have, in turn, argued that oil majors were engaged in price gouging, and pointed to their healthy financials as evidence. Expect to hear more about that in Biden\u8217\'20\'19s speech this afternoon.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.34pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Will Republican bastion Utah see a surprise in its Senate race? MacKenzie Ryan takes a look at the candidacy of independent Evan McMullin, who is presenting an unusually tough challenge to Republican incumbent \uc2 Mike Lee\uc2  at the polls this year:\par \par \uc2 Utah is usually reliably Republican turf but in this year\u8217\'20\'19s midterm elections a Senate race in the Mormon-dominated state could see a remarkable upset \u8211\'20\'13 and one that could damage the Republican party\u8217\'20\'19s ambitions to capture the Senate.\par \par \uc2 Independent challenger Evan McMullin, a former CIA agent who unsuccessfully ran for president against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in 2016, is seeing his race tighten against \uc2 Mike Lee\uc2 , a two-time Republican incumbent who initially supported Trump\u8217\'20\'19s legal challenge to the election but later voted to certify it.\par \par \uc2 An October poll, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.deseret.com/utah/2022/10/10/23396679/evan-mcmullin-mike-lee-locked-utah-senate-race-poll-attack-ads"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 commissioned by the Deseret News and the Hinckley Institute of Politics}}}\uc2 , shows Lee with a four-point lead with 12% of voters still undecided.\par \par \uc2 Jason Perry, director of the Hinckley Institute of Politics, calls this Senate race the tightest Utah has seen in decades. The race is also unique in Utah\u8217\'20\'19s history because it\u8217\'20\'19s not a traditional Republican versus Democrat challenge.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMcMullin\u8217\'20\'19s candidacy is an experiment and will be the ultimate test to see if a third-party challenger can really take down a well-known Republican in what has been a reliably red state,\u8221\'20\'1D Perry said.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/31/utah-evan-mcmullin-mike-lee-independent"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Utah: can an ex-CIA independent oust an incumbent Republican senator?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.17pm GMT\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was front and center during the debate between Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s Republican governor \uc2 Brian Kemp\uc2  and his Democratic challenger \uc2 Stacey Abrams\uc2  last night, \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/edwin-rios"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Edwin Rios}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 In the final televised debate with Democratic challenger {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/stacey-abrams"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Stacey Abrams}}}\uc2  before their November election, Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s governor, \uc2 Brian Kemp\uc2 , refused to say whether he would support harsher \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions if re-elected to a second term and if fellow Republicans dominating the state legislature sent them to his desk.\par \par \uc2 At WSB-TV\u8217\'20\'19s Channel 2 Action debate Sunday, Kemp, a Republican, said it was not his \u8220\'20\'1Cdesire to go move the needle any further\u8221\'20\'1D on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/state-of-georgia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Georgia}}}\uc2 , adding that he would look into additional restrictions passed by state lawmakers \u8220\'20\'1Cwhen the time comes\u8221\'20\'1D. Kemp at a previous debate had said he \u8220\'20\'1Cwould not\u8221\'20\'1D support new \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  limits.\par \par \uc2 The Sunday night debate heightened an already contentious rematch over the governorship. Kemp narrowly defeated Abrams in 2018, and polling shows he holds a lead over Abrams more than a week before the election. Abrams sought to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ajc.com/politics/in-final-debate-kemp-wont-say-whether-hed-sign-new-abortion-limits/NXSM4P35DNDOFFQO7KXSOSK73Y/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 draw a stark contrast}}}\uc2  with Kemp over the issues of guns, the economy, crime and voting restrictions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUnder \uc2 Brian Kemp\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s four years as governor, crime has gone up, hospitals have closed and communities are in turmoil,\u8221\'20\'1D Abrams said in her closing arguments.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/31/georgia-abrams-kemp-debate-governor-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Georgia governor debate: Kemp silent on question over harsher \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  restrictions}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.02pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Polls have shown his approval rating underwater with voters for months, and as the midterms approach, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/lauren-gambino"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lauren Gambino}}}\uc2  reports \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has adopted a low-key campaign style \u8211\'20\'13 for better or worse:\par \par \uc2 Music, chants and applause filled the gymnasium of a community college in an upstate New York battleground district, where \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  delivered Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 closing economic argument of the midterm election season.\par \par \uc2 The president acknowledged Americans\u8217\'20\'19 struggle to cope with painfully high inflation, while touting the progress his administration had made toward a post-pandemic recovery. He closed his remarks with a stark warning: if {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans}}}\uc2  win control of Congress, they would create \u8220\'20\'1Cchaos\u8221\'20\'1D in the economy. Then he waded into the crowd to shake hands and snap selfies.\par \par \uc2 While the visit had some of the trappings of a traditional campaign rally, it was, like much of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s recent travels, an official event \u8211\'20\'13 an understated finish to a campaign season the president has described as the \u8220\'20\'1Cmost consequential\u8221\'20\'1D of his political life.\par \par \uc2 In the final days before the 8 November election, Biden will ramp up his campaign trail appearances, with plans to visit Pennsylvania, Florida, New Mexico and Maryland to stump for Democratic candidates.\par \par \uc2 But his relatively low profile is part of a concerted strategy designed for an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/biden-approval-rating/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unpopular president}}}\uc2  in a challenging election year.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTo the extent he\u8217\'20\'19s less visible, and maybe even invisible, it\u8217\'20\'19s a plus for Democrats because it lets the candidates run their own campaigns on their own issues,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Larry Sabato\uc2 , director of the Center for Politics at the \uc2 University of Virginia\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1COut of sight, out of mind.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/31/joe-biden-midterms-campaign-low-profile"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats insist Joe Biden\u8217\'20\'19s low midterms profile is smart strategy}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.48pm GMT\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.gallup.com/poll/404243/economy-top-election-issue-abortion-crime-next.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gallup has released a new poll}}}\uc2  that confirms previous surveys finding the economy is voters\u8217\'20\'19 top concern, a worrying indicator for embattled Democrats asking Americans to give them another two years to make things right.\par \par \uc2 However, there was some good news for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s party in the survey, including that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is voters\u8217\'20\'19 number-two concern \u8211\'20\'13 and Democrats are particularly fired up about it.\par \par \uc2 Gallup found 49% of registered voters consider the economy \u8220\'20\'1Cextremely important\u8221\'20\'1D, including 64% of Republicans and 47% of independents. It\u8217\'20\'19s a lower 33% among Democrats, but with other polls finding Biden scores low marks on his handling of the economy, the figure bolsters the case for his party to lose seats in the House and Senate in the 8 November midterms as voters retaliate for months of high inflation.\par \par \uc2 But there was better news for Democrats in voters\u8217\'20\'19 rankings of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It came in second place among issues, with 42% considering it \u8220\'20\'1Cextremely important\u8221\'20\'1D, including 51% of Democrats and 38% of independents. That\u8217\'20\'19s a positive for the party in power, because Democrats have hoped the GOP will suffer its own backlash for the conservative-dominated supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision earlier this year to overturn Roe v Wade and allow states to completely ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  outrage cuts both ways. A significant 37% of Republicans see it as their top issue, potentially because they intend to vote for candidates who will further crack down on the procedure.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.23pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Democrats have slight advantage in key Senate races: poll\par \par \uc2 Democrats have a small lead over their Republican challengers in the crucial Arizona, Georgia and Pennsylvania Senate races, while Nevada is a dead heat, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/10/31/us/politics/democrats-republicans-senate-election-polls.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a New York Times poll released today}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 enltrControl of the Senate rests on a knife\u8217\'20\'19s edge, according to new polls by \uc2 The New York Times\uc2  and Siena College. The contests are close in Arizona, Georgia, Nevada and Pennsylvania. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/vwdSUIPigd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/vwdSUIPigd}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The \uc2 New York Times\uc2  (@nytimes) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/nytimes/status/1587036676412637184?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 31, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Assuming no Democratic incumbents lose elsewhere, winning those three states alone would ensure \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s allies continue to control Congress\u8217\'20\'19s upper chamber for another two years, even if Nevada senator \uc2 Catherine Cortez Masto\uc2  loses re-election to Republican \uc2 Adam Laxalt\uc2 . Polls are, however, uncertain, and there\u8217\'20\'19s still enough time before the 8 November vote for the situation to change.\par \par \uc2 The Senate is perhaps the more important of the two chambers for Democrats to control because it is responsible for considering executive appointees \u8211\'20\'13 such as supreme court justices. Years of GOP control during which Republicans presidents had their jurors confirmed created the court\u8217\'20\'19s six-member conservative majority, which earlier this year overturned Roe v Wade and seems poised to strike down affirmative action policies at universities nationwide.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.06pm GMT\par \par \uc2 What would it mean if affirmative action went away? \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/edwin-rios"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Edwin Rios}}}\uc2  spoke to students who say race-conscious admissions policies had a decisive impact on their academic opportunities, and fear its end would undo progress for future generations:\par \par \uc2 When Andrew Brennen thinks about the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  deliberations over race-conscious admissions, he reflects on his parents, both attorneys, and his brother. In 2009, his father, David, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nkaa.uky.edu/nkaa/items/show/2133#:~:text=In%202009%2C%20David%20A.,desegregation%20of%20Kentucky%20higher%20education."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 became}}}\uc2  the first Black dean of the \uc2 University of Kentucky\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s law school since the state desegregated its colleges and universities.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHad they not had access to higher education that they received, who knows what they would\u8217\'20\'19ve been doing,\u8221\'20\'1D Brennen, who graduated from the \uc2 University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill\uc2  in 2019, says. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m thinking a lot about how different my life, my brother\u8217\'20\'19s life, would be if affirmative action hadn\u8217\'20\'19t been in place.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 On Monday, as the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  hears oral arguments in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/02/supreme-court-affirmative-action-harvard"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cases against the University of North Carolina and Harvard University}}}\uc2 , the fate of race-conscious admissions is under threat. Civil rights attorneys and experts alike worry, following the high court\u8217\'20\'19s decision to overturn Roe v Wade, that the court\u8217\'20\'19s rightward tilt could spell their end.\par \par \uc2 For decades, the supreme court has consistently upheld that colleges and universities can take limited consideration of a student\u8217\'20\'19s race and ethnicity as a factor when they assess which students to accept. In the 1960s, after John F Kennedy first {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.americanbar.org/groups/crsj/publications/human_rights_magazine_home/black-to-the-future-part-ii/affirmative-action-in-higher-education--relevance-for-today-s-ra/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ordered}}}\uc2  government contractors to \u8220\'20\'1Ctake affirmative action\u8221\'20\'1D to combat racial discrimination, colleges and universities developed policies to further diversify who enrolled.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/30/affirmative-action-race-conscious-admissions-students"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US students on why affirmative action is crucial: \u8216\'20\'18They need our voices\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.50pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Affirmative action's days are likely numbered as conservative-dominated supreme court hears key cases\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. Months after they handed down a decision that ended nearly five decades of nationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s conservative majority will today hear two cases that are predicted to bring about the end of affirmative action. The court\u8217\'20\'19s six-justice conservative majority is known to be hostile to race-conscious admissions policies such as those at \uc2 Harvard University\uc2  and the University of North Carolina, and is widely expected to use the cases as an opportunity to throw out another longstanding decision in favor of modern rightwing orthodoxy.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is happening today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Bidens are heading to New York, where \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will attend a private memorial service, and first lady Jill Biden will campaign for Democrats including gubernatorial candidate \uc2 Kathy Hochul\uc2  and congressman \uc2 Sean Patrick Maloney\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The man who attackedPaul Pelosi on Friday is likely to be formally charged today. He made clear during the attack on their San Francisco home that he was looking for his wife, Democratic House speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Reminder: the 8 November midterms are only eight days away! Voters will decide whether Democrats will control the Senate and House of Representatives for another two years, as well cast ballots for gubernatorial and statehouse candidates.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020221031eiav00237\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
