\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Georgia governor debate: Kemp silent on question over harsher  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  restrictions\b0\par\par\uc2 Edwin Rios \par \uc2 485 \uc2 words\par \uc2 31 October 2022\par 14:10 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Republican \uc2 Brian Kemp\uc2  and Democratic challenger \uc2 Stacey Abrams\uc2  spar in final gubernatorial debate before midterms\par \par \uc2 In the final televised debate with Democratic challenger \uc2 Stacey Abrams\uc2  before their November election, Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s governor, \uc2 Brian Kemp\uc2 , refused to say whether he would support harsher \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions if re-elected to a second term and if fellow Republicans dominating the state legislature sent them to his desk.\par \par \uc2 At WSB-TV\u8217\'20\'19s Channel 2 Action debate Sunday, Kemp, a Republican, said it was not his \u8220\'20\'1Cdesire to go move the needle any further\u8221\'20\'1D on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions in Georgia, adding that he would look into additional restrictions passed by state lawmakers \u8220\'20\'1Cwhen the time comes\u8221\'20\'1D. Kemp at a previous debate had said he \u8220\'20\'1Cwould not\u8221\'20\'1D support new \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  limits.\par \par \uc2 The Sunday night debate heightened an already contentious rematch over the governorship. Kemp narrowly defeated Abrams in 2018, and polling shows he holds a lead over Abrams more than a week before the election. Abrams sought to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ajc.com/politics/in-final-debate-kemp-wont-say-whether-hed-sign-new-abortion-limits/NXSM4P35DNDOFFQO7KXSOSK73Y/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 draw a stark contrast}}}\uc2  with Kemp over the issues of guns, the economy, crime and voting restrictions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUnder \uc2 Brian Kemp\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s four years as governor, crime has gone up, hospitals have closed and communities are in turmoil,\u8221\'20\'1D Abrams said in her closing arguments.\par \par \uc2 The state already effectively bars most abortions after Kemp signed an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law in 2019 that prohibits the procedure six weeks into a pregnancy. The law went into effect after the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  in June {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturned}}}\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights nationwide, established nearly 50 years earlier by Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 A trial {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pbs.org/newshour/health/trial-over-georgia-law-restricting-abortion-to-six-weeks-to-begin#:~:text=Georgia%27s%20law%20bans%20most%20abortions,six%20weeks%20into%20a%20pregnancy."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has recently begun}}}\uc2  over whether the state\u8217\'20\'19s imposition of the 2019 law is constitutional.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLet\u8217\'20\'19s be clear, he did not say he wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t,\u8221\'20\'1D Abrams said in response to Kemp\u8217\'20\'19s remarks Sunday. She tied Kemp to Georgia US Senate candidate \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2 , who is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/26/herschel-walker-georgia-senate-abortion-clinic"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 accused}}}\uc2  by two women of pressuring them to have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , even though Walker has stated he is staunchly opposed to the termination of pregnancies. Walker denies the allegations.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe refuses to protect us. He refuses to defend us,\u8221\'20\'1D Abrams {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ajc.com/politics/in-final-debate-kemp-wont-say-whether-hed-sign-new-abortion-limits/NXSM4P35DNDOFFQO7KXSOSK73Y/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  of Kemp. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd yet he defended \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2 , saying that he didn\u8217\'20\'19t want to be involved in the personal life of his running mate.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 By contrast, Abrams supported legal abortions before the point of \u8220\'20\'1Cviability\u8221\'20\'1D, noting that the decision should be made \u8220\'20\'1Cbetween a doctor and a woman \u8211\'20\'13 as a medical choice.\u8221\'20\'1D Kemp contended that Abrams\u8217\'20\'19 stance shifted on whether she would support new restrictions brought to her.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is willful ignorance or misleading lies that change what I\u8217\'20\'19ve said,\u8221\'20\'1D Abrams said. \u8220\'20\'1CBut what I\u8217\'20\'19ve also always said is that there should not be arbitrary timelines set by men who do not understand biology.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 This article was amended on 31 October 2022. An earlier version said Abrams supported \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the point of viability.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020221031eiav0028m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
