\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Democrats on the defensive as economy becomes primary concern over  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 Joan E Greve in Washington \par \uc2 880 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 October 2022\par 14:15 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 47\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Polls indicate tide shifting toward Republicans with high inflation rates and gas prices working in their favor\par \par \uc2 With less than two weeks to go until election day, Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 hopes of defying political history and keeping their narrow majorities in the House and Senate appear to be fading, as many of the party\u8217\'20\'19s candidates go on the defensive in the final days of campaigning.\par \par \uc2 Over the summer, many election forecasters wondered if Democrats could avoid the widespread losses typically seen by the president\u8217\'20\'19s party in the midterms. With voters expressing outrage over the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision to end federal protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access and gas prices falling, Democrats had been hopeful that their endangered incumbents could win re-election.\par \par \uc2 In August, Democrats took the lead on the generic congressional ballot, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/polls/generic-ballot/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to FiveThirtyEight}}}\uc2 . They held on to that lead for two and a half months \u8211\'20\'13 until last week.\par \par \uc2 The national political environment now seems to have moved in Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 favor, and Democrats are running out of time to turn the tide. Gas prices started to rise again this month, although they have since {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://gasprices.aaa.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 started to moderate}}}\uc2 . With inflation at near record levels, the share of voters who name the economy as their top priority has increased since the summer.\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/10/17/us/politics/republicans-economy-nyt-siena-poll.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York Times/Siena College poll}}}\uc2  taken this month found that 44% of likely voters say economic concerns are the most important problem facing the country, compared with 36% who said the same in July. Just 5% of likely voters identified \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the most important issue right now. Voters\u8217\'20\'19 renewed focus on inflation and gas prices could hurt Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 chances in some key congressional races, given that Republicans consistently score better on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/US/gop-opens-edge-economy-crime-ahead-midterms-poll/story?id=91919888"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 surveys}}}\uc2  asking which party is better equipped to manage the economy.\par \par \uc2 The shifting winds have prompted some Democrats to question whether they made a tactical error by focusing heavily on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in their campaign messaging. Just last week, \uc2 Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/18/biden-roe-v-wade-codify-democrats-win-midterm-elections"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 promised}}}\uc2  to send a bill codifying Roe v Wade to Congress if Democrats fortify their majorities in the midterms.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI want to remind us all how we felt that day when 50 years of constitutional precedent was overturned,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said last Tuesday. \u8220\'20\'1CIf you care about the right to choose, then you got to vote.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 With surveys indicating \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights are not top of mind for most voters, some progressive lawmakers are urging their colleagues to instead emphasize economic proposals like raising the minimum wage and creating a federal paid family leave program as they campaign for re-election.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn my view, while the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  issue must remain on the front burner, it would be political malpractice for Democrats to ignore the state of the economy and allow Republican lies and distortions to go unanswered,\u8221\'20\'1D the progressive senator Bernie Sanders wrote in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/commentisfree/2022/oct/10/democrats-midterms-victory-economy-bernie-sanders"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a Guardian op-ed}}}\uc2  earlier this month.\par \par \uc2 Sanders added: \u8220\'20\'1CNow is the time for Democrats to take the fight to the reactionary Republican party and expose their anti-worker views on the most important issues facing ordinary Americans. That is both the right thing to do from a policy perspective and good politics.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Democrats worry that the strategy pivot may be coming too late for some candidates, as alarm bells go off in battleground states across the country.\par \par \uc2 In Florida, a state that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  won by just three points in 2020, the Republican governor, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , appears likely to defeat his Democratic challenger, \uc2 Charlie Crist\uc2 , by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/polls/governor/2022/florida/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 double digits}}}\uc2 . DeSantis, a Trump-like figure who is widely expected to run for president in 2024, has already raised {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.opensecrets.org/news/2022/09/florida-gov-ron-desantis-breaks-gubernatorial-fundraising-record/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 at least $177m}}}\uc2  this election cycle, setting a record for a gubernatorial campaign. DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s fundraising haul and Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 bleak polling numbers have led many of the party\u8217\'20\'19s national organizations and donors to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/10/27/florida-democrats-facing-brutal-midterms-00063666"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 abandon Florida candidates}}}\uc2 , in effect declaring a pre-emptive defeat.\par \par \uc2 In the battle for the House, Republicans are poised to recapture the majority, as districts that Biden easily won less than two years ago now appear to be up for grabs. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/10/27/maloney-dems-new-york-midterms-00063645"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 According to Politico}}}\uc2 , a recent internal poll conducted by the campaign of Julia Brownley, whose California district went for Biden by 20 points in 2020, showed the Democratic incumbent leading her Republican opponent by just one point.\par \par \uc2 Sean Patrick Maloney\uc2 , the chair of the Democratic Congressional Campaign Committee who is overseeing the party\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to maintain control of the House, now faces the risk of being ousted himself. Earlier this week, the Cook Political Report {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cookpolitical.com/analysis/house/new-york-house/ny-17-rating-change-dccc-chair-maloney-moves-lean-democrat-toss"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 changed the rating}}}\uc2  of Maloney\u8217\'20\'19s race from \u8220\'20\'1Clean Democrat\u8221\'20\'1D to \u8220\'20\'1Ctoss-up\u8221\'20\'1D. If Maloney cannot hold his seat, the defeat would mark the first time since 1992 that a sitting House campaign committee chair lost re-election. Republicans are gleeful at the prospect of toppling the DCCC chair, dumping several million dollars into Maloney\u8217\'20\'19s district.\par \par \uc2 Maloney has remained optimistic about his chances, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CBSNews/status/1585387733572354057"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 telling CBS News}}}\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m going to win this election, and when I do, they\u8217\'20\'19re going to wish they had that $9m back.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But if the national environment is as dire as it appears for Democrats, a Republican wave could soon sweep Maloney and many of his colleagues out of office.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020221028eias001e6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
