\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Anonymous woman claims \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  pressured her to have  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  and drove her to clinic \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein \par \uc2 6,108 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 October 2022\par 20:16 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Gloria Allred: Walker \u8216\'20\'18clearly wanted her to have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19Sign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 We are less than two weeks away from the 8 November midterms, and here\u8217\'20\'19s where things stand: \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/26/fetterman-oz-debate-midterms-biden-politics-latest?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-635942478f08b1b21f138dcc#block-635942478f08b1b21f138dcc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 growing more unpopular}}}\uc2 . Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 chances of keeping control of the House of Representatives are slim, while {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/26/fetterman-oz-debate-midterms-biden-politics-latest?page=with:block-6359483d8f083ccb8b581222#block-6359483d8f083ccb8b581222"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 predictions for the new Republican majority are expanding}}}\uc2 . And Senate control is coming down to a handful of races, including Pennsylvania, where the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/26/fetterman-oz-debate-midterms-biden-politics-latest?page=with:block-63592e938f080759184ffbfa#block-63592e938f080759184ffbfa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democratic candidate struggled}}}\uc2  in last night\u8217\'20\'19s debate. In Georgia, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/26/fetterman-oz-debate-midterms-biden-politics-latest?page=with:block-63595bb98f08b1b21f138f51#block-63595bb98f08b1b21f138f51"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a new poll showed}}}\uc2  Republican \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  trailing in voter support, while {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/26/fetterman-oz-debate-midterms-biden-politics-latest?page=with:block-635982608f08ef5c1742cf54#block-635982608f08ef5c1742cf54"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 his campaign is contending}}}\uc2  with a new allegation that the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  foe paid for another woman to undergo the procedure.\par \par \uc2 Elections were not the only sources of news today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2 , \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s former chief of staff, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/26/fetterman-oz-debate-midterms-biden-politics-latest?page=with:block-635950848f08b1b21f138e8d#block-635950848f08b1b21f138e8d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was ordered to appear}}}\uc2  before a special grand jury investigating election meddling in Georgia. Meadows\u8217\'20\'19 lawyer says he plans to appeal.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s legal team{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/26/fetterman-oz-debate-midterms-biden-politics-latest?page=with:block-63598aa98f08ef5c1742cfa3#block-63598aa98f08ef5c1742cfa3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 received a subpoena}}}\uc2  compelling the ex-president\u8217\'20\'19s testimony before the January 6 committee, but he may still challenge it in court.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A Michigan jury{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/26/fetterman-oz-debate-midterms-biden-politics-latest?page=with:block-635956ef8f083ccb8b581303#block-635956ef8f083ccb8b581303"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 convicted three men}}}\uc2  of charges related to plotting to kidnap the state\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic governor \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Twelve GOP candidates to oversee voting in states nationwide deny the outcome of the 2020 election, presenting a threat to democracy. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/26/fetterman-oz-debate-midterms-biden-politics-latest?page=with:block-63594d3e8f08b1b21f138e58#block-63594d3e8f08b1b21f138e58"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Arizona is home}}}\uc2  to one of the most high stakes of these races.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Speaking of people in legal trouble in Washington, reports have emerged the Democratic senator \uc2 Robert Menendez\uc2  is under federal investigation \u8211\'20\'13 again.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSenator Menendez is aware of an investigation that was reported on today, however he does not know the scope of the investigation,\u8221\'20\'1D an advisor to the New Jersey lawmaker {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.semafor.com/article/10/25/2022/senator-robert-menendez-under-investigation-again"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told Semafor}}}\uc2 , which first reported on the inquiry. \u8220\'20\'1CAs always, should any official inquiries be made, the Senator is available to provide any assistance that is requested of him or his office.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The investigation is being handled by prosecutors in New York, who have issued one subpoena in the case and contacted people connected to the senator, according to Semafor.\par \par \uc2 Menendez represents a reliably Democratic state, and is not up for re-election until 2024. Federal prosecutors brought corruption charges against him in 2015 over accusations Menendez accepted gifts and campaign funds from a Florida eye doctor in exchange for using his clout in Washington on the doctor\u8217\'20\'19s behalf. The case collapsed three years later after a jury deadlocked on the charges, and prosecutors decided not to retry Menendez.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2018/feb/01/bob-menendez-federal-prosecutors-dismiss-corruption-charges"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Federal prosecutors dismiss corruption charges against Senator Bob Menendez}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump's legal team accepts subpoena from the January 6 committee\par \par \uc2 Lawyers for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  have accepted a subpoena compelling him to sit for a deposition before the January 6 committee next month, but he may still choose to challenge the summons, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/10/26/trump-receives-subpoena-jan-6-committee-00063628"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 At what was likely its final public hearing earlier this month, the bipartisan House panel voted unanimously to subpoena the former president, saying he can resolve unanswered questions about the deadly insurrection at the Capitol. Their summons requires him to provide documents they requested by 4 November, and sit for a deposition by 14 November.\par \par \uc2 Reports have indicated the former president is open to speaking to the lawmakers. But Politico notes that Harmeet Dhillon of the The Dhillon Law Group, which is representing Trump in his dealings with the January 6 committee, has retweeted posts attacking the lawmakers\u8217\'20\'19 work on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  responded to the unnamed woman\u8217\'20\'19s claim this afternoon that he paid for her to have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  by saying, \u8220\'20\'1Cit\u8217\'20\'19s a lie\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s the same answer he gave last week when pressed on reports he paid for another woman to undergo the procedure.\par \par \uc2 ABC News has video:\par \par \uc2 enltrHerschel Walker addresses reporters as a new woman comes forward alleging Walker drove her to a clinic to have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m done with this foolishness. I\u8217\'20\'19ve already told people this is a lie and I\u8217\'20\'19m not going to entertain,\u8221\'20\'1D Walker said.\par \par \uc2 He didn\u8217\'20\'19t answer any Q\u8217\'20\'19s. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/gapol?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #gapol}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/hdthWIlZgR"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/hdthWIlZgR}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lalee Ibssa (@LaleeIbssa) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/LaleeIbssa/status/1585348130593439744?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 26, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/17/georgia-herschel-walker-admits-paying-700-check-denies-abortion-raphael-warnock"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Herschel Walker admits to writing $700 check but denies it was for \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 Attorney Gloria Allred has publicly presented some of the evidence her unnamed client has to substantiate the account of her relationship with Walker.\par \par \uc2 These include greeting cards from Walker to the woman, and a photo of Walker in bed in the woman\u8217\'20\'19s hotel room:\par \par \uc2 enltrJane Doe's attorney, Gloria Allred, presents what is alleged to be a photo of \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  (R) in the bed in Doe's hotel room.\par \par \uc2 Doe alleges Walker pressured her into having an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/PKHVXQVuQP"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/PKHVXQVuQP}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1585346787111337985?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 26, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 Woman 'devastated' by Walker 'pressure' to have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 Using the pseudonym Jane Doe, the woman accusing Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s Republican senate candidate \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  of paying for her to have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  recounted in an emotional statement how he \u8220\'20\'1Cpressured\u8221\'20\'1D her to go through with it.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI was confused, uncertain, and scared,\u8221\'20\'1D the woman, who declined to reveal her name and face, said at a press conference.\par \par \uc2 Walker, who was married at the time but had told Doe he was going to seek a divorce, gave her money to pay for the procedure. Doe said she was \u8220\'20\'1Cconfused, uncertain, and scared,\u8221\'20\'1D and when she want to a clinic, \u8220\'20\'1CI simply couldn\u8217\'20\'19t go through with it. I left the clinic in tears.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Doe then recounted how Walker drove her again to the clinic and waited for her until the procedure was finished.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI was devastated because I felt that I had been pressured into having an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Doe said. She described herself as \u8220\'20\'1Cnaive,\u8221\'20\'1D and said Walker \u8220\'20\'1Ctook advantage of me.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMost significantly, and the reason I am here today, is because he has publicly taken the position that he is \u8216\'20\'18about life\u8217\'20\'19 and against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  under any circumstances, when, in fact, he pressured me to have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and personally ensured that it occurred by driving me to the clinic and paid for it,\u8221\'20\'1D the woman said.\par \par \uc2 She noted she was an independent and voted for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  twice.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI do not believe that Herschel is morally fit to be a US senator,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd that is the reason why I am speaking up and providing proof.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Jane Doe found out she was pregnant in 1993, her attorney Gloria Allred said.\par \par \uc2 When she told \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2 , he \u8220\'20\'1Cclearly wanted her to have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and convinced her to do so. Our client alleges that Mr. Walker gave her cash to pay for the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Allred said.\par \par \uc2 Doe went to a clinic in Dallas, Texas to have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but could not go through with it. When Walker found out, Allred said he was upset.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe pressured her to go back to the clinic within the next day to go through with the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D her attorney said. \u8220\'20\'1CThe following day, Mr. Walker drove her to the clinic and waited in the parking lot for hours until the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was completed\u8230\'20\'26 Then he drove her to the pharmacy to pick up medications and supplies\u8230\'20\'26 And then he drove her home.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn the days following the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Mr. Walker began to distance himself from our client. She was very distraught because she felt that Mr. Walker had pressured her into having an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . She left Dallas and she did not return for more than 15 years because she was so traumatized,\u8221\'20\'1D Allred said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMr. Walker professes to be against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , even though he paid for and pressured our client to have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Allred said, noting that Walker was married at the time he saw Doe, but said he was going to seek a divorce.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur client feels that Mr. Walker is a complete hypocrite and does not deserve to be a United States senator from the state of Georgia,\u8221\'20\'1D Allred concluded.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Attorney Gloria Allred has started the press conference where she\u8217\'20\'19s introducing a woman using the pseudonym Jane Doe, who says Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s Republican senate candidate \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  paid for her to have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CToday my client, also known as Jane Doe, will come forward for the first time to share her truth about \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2 , a man with whom he had a romantic and intimate relationship for a number of years,\u8221\'20\'1D Allred began.\par \par \uc2 The woman began dating Walker in 1987, said Allred, and saw him for a number of years. The attorney said she had a receipt from a hotel stay from when Doe went to visit Walker in Minnesota. She also played a voicemail from Walker to the woman, in which he tells her he loves her.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 Is \uc2 Mike Lee\uc2 , the Republican senator representing deep-red Utah, in trouble? His conservative colleague Ted Cruz thinks so.\par \par \uc2 Lee is not facing a Democrat this year, but rather an independent: Evan McMullin, who has surprising momentum in a state that hasn\u8217\'20\'19t sent anyone but a Republican to the Senate in more than four decades.\par \par \uc2 Texas\u8217\'20\'19s Republican senator Cruz thinks that Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 tactic of staying out of the race in favor of McMullin might actually work:\par \par \uc2 enltrSen. Ted Cruz (R-TX) thinks Sen. \uc2 Mike Lee\uc2  (R-UT) is in \u8220\'20\'1Cjeopardy\u8221\'20\'1D of losing to Evan McMullin (I):\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDemocrats have done something really devious and dishonest \u8230\'20\'26 decided not to run a candidate.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/mvIlyM8QY8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/mvIlyM8QY8}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1585333023930826788?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 26, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 McMullin was last heard from in 2016, when he stood as an independent against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and managed to syphon the support of a few Republicans who abhorred their party\u8217\'20\'19s nominee. This year, Utah\u8217\'20\'19s other Republican senator, \uc2 Mitt Romney\uc2 , declined to endorse either McMullin or Lee, saying he considered both friends. Lee {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2FRcggr3vtc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recently went on Fox News}}}\uc2  to press Romney for his backing.\par \par \uc2 Nonetheless, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/2022-election-forecast/senate/utah/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 most polls show}}}\uc2  Lee ahead in the state, though a couple have McMullin leading.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re a few minutes away from a press conference where attorney Gloria Allred says she will introduce a woman whom Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s Republican senate candidate \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  paid to have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The woman would be the second to come forward and say that Walker, who supports a national ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  without exceptions, helped her afford the procedure. The woman\u8217\'20\'19s identity and face won\u8217\'20\'19t be revealed publicly, Allred said.\par \par \uc2 Walker is in a close race for Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s senate seat, which is currently occupied by Democrat \uc2 Raphael Warnock\uc2 . Polls have lately showed Warnock with an advantage, though an internal survey for the Walker campaign just released puts the Republican ahead:\par \par \uc2 enltrWe\u8217\'20\'19re just out of the field with a new poll for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TeamHerschel?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @TeamHerschel}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Walker: 46%\par \par \uc2 Warnock: 42%\par \par \uc2 Oliver: 3%\par \par \uc2 N=800 live calls\par \par \uc2 MoE +\\-3%\par \par \uc2 October 22-25\par \par \uc2 Moore Information Group\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Erik Iverson (@erikjiverson) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/erikjiverson/status/1585330213034287105?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 26, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/26/herschel-walker-georgia-senate-abortion-clinic"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New woman to say Herschel Walker took her to clinic for \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/world/us/exclusive-two-five-us-voters-worry-about-intimidation-polls-reutersipsos-2022-10-26/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new Reuters/Ipsos poll}}}\uc2  finds two in five US voters fear violence or intimidation at polling stations during the midterm elections. Two thirds of voters responding to the poll feared violence from rightwing extremists after the elections, if the results do not go their way.\par \par \uc2 A Republican party fueled by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  -supporting election deniers seems poised to retake the US House and maybe the Senate, and to win key state races including posts which involve the overseeing of elections.\par \par \uc2 Kathy Boockvar\uc2 , a former top election official in Pennsylvania who now advocates for secure elections, told Reuters: \u8220\'20\'1COur country is based on democracy. We should be excited about election day.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Reuters/\uc2 Ipsos\uc2  poll also found that \u8220\'20\'1Camong the registered voters \u8230\'20\'26 43% were concerned about threats of violence or voter intimidation while voting in person, [a fear] more pronounced among Democratic voters, 51% of whom said they worried about violence, although a still-significant share of Republicans \u8211\'20\'13 38% \u8211\'20\'13 harbored such concerns.\par \par \uc2 Reuters added: \u8220\'20\'1CAbout a fifth of voters \u8211\'20\'13 including one in 10 Democrats and one in four Republicans \u8211\'20\'13 said they were not confident their ballots would be accurately counted.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Some further reading: Ed Pilkington\u8217\'20\'19s interview with \uc2 Adrian Fontes\uc2 , running for secretary of state in Arizona against a rightwing election-denying opponent, Mark Finchem \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/26/arizona-midterm-election-secretary-of-state-adrian-fontes-mark-finchem"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Democracy on the ballot\u8217\'20\'19: the man fighting to keep Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s election out of an extremist\u8217\'20\'19s hands}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 Ed Pilkington, our chief reporter, has filed his report on the fallout from Tuesday night\u8217\'20\'19s potentially momentous \uc2 US Senate\uc2  debate in Pennsylvania\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 As the dust settled over Tuesday night\u8217\'20\'19s sole {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/26/pennsylvania-senate-debate-mehmet-oz-john-fetterman"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 televised debate}}}\uc2  in the crucial \uc2 US Senate\uc2  race in Pennsylvania, pundits were starkly divided over the impact of the Democrat \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s struggles with speech in his recovery from a stroke.\par \par \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2 . Photograph: Greg Nash/\uc2 EPA\par \par \uc2 The Pennsylvania lieutenant governor raised the issue of his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.inquirer.com/politics/election/john-fetterman-2022-pennsylvania-senate-stroke-medical-report-20221019.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 auditory processing disorder}}}\uc2 , which makes it difficult for him to understand certain spoken words, in his opening remarks in the debate with his Republican rival, the former TV doctor Mehmet Oz.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLet\u8217\'20\'19s also talk about the elephant in the room \u8211\'20\'13 I had a stroke,\u8221\'20\'1D Fetterman said.\par \par \uc2 Fetterman used closed captioning to help deal with his speech difficulties. Questions and answers were transcribed in real time and beamed through large screens in front of both candidates.\par \par \uc2 Reporters present in Harrisburg, Pennsylvania, noted that Fetterman occasionally struggled to articulate his views in the hour-long debate. The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.inquirer.com/politics/election/john-fetterman-mehmet-oz-pa-senate-debate-2022-20221025.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Philadelphia Inquirer}}}\uc2  said that he \u8220\'20\'1Cspoke haltingly and at times mixed up his words\u8221\'20\'1D, remarking that \u8220\'20\'1Chis speaking has been much smoother in stump speeches on the campaign trail and in a recent interview with the Inquirer than during the back-and-forth\u8221\'20\'1D of the debate with Oz.\par \par \uc2 Rightwing news outlets and commentators were much harsher, with several calling for Fetterman to drop out of the race. John Podhoretz, a conservative columnist with the New York Post, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nypost.com/2022/10/25/john-fetterman-debate-was-painful-and-shameful-he-is-physically-incapable-of-being-a-senator/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 described the Democratic candidate as \u8220\'20\'1Cimpaired\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  and said \u8220\'20\'1Cit is an act of personal, political, and ideological malpractice that Fetterman is still contesting for the Senate\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Full story:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/26/fetterman-oz-debate-democrats-pennsylvania-senate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pundits divided over Fetterman\u8217\'20\'19s performance in key Senate debate}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden targets bank 'junk fees'\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  spoke at the White House earlier, announcing an effort to remove \u8220\'20\'1Cjunk fees\u8221\'20\'1D, charges made by banks for services including overdrafts, or when a cheque turns out not to be valid.\par \par \uc2 Before the coronavirus pandemic, US banks charged customers around $15bn in junk fees every year.\par \par \uc2 Appearing with Biden, \uc2 Rohit Chopra\uc2 , director of the \uc2 Consumer Financial Protection Bureau\uc2 , said: \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re making progress. Banks across the country are cutting and even eliminating fees, saving families billions. This morning, the \uc2 CFPB\uc2  announced more actions to combat illegal and unexpected junk fees. One on surprise overdraft fees, and another on surprise depositor fees.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re putting companies on notice about their obligations under law. We\u8217\'20\'19re taking enforcement actions like one against a large bank for charging illegal overdraft fees. And customers will see hundreds of millions of dollars in refunds. We also sued a payments company for cramming $300m in extra fees on families who were just trying to sign up their kids for YMCA camps, or were just registering for a charity walkathon in their community.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd we\u8217\'20\'19re going to continue by finding ways to reduce burdens of other fees like the billions and penalties charged by banks and credit card companies through new rules and guidance. This is real money back in the pockets of American families is good for them. And it\u8217\'20\'19s good for businesses that follow the law.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden said his administration would \u8220\'20\'1Clower the cost of everyday living for American families, to put more money in the pockets of middle-income and working-class Americans, to hold big corporations accountable\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 There are, of course, less than two weeks to go before midterms election day, 8 November. Biden\u8217\'20\'19s approval rating is falling and Democrats fear a battering at the ballot box, with Republicans poised to take back the House and maybe the Senate.\par \par \uc2 Saying \u8220\'20\'1Cone of the things that I think frustrates the American people is the world\u8217\'20\'19s in a bit of disarray\u8221\'20\'1D, Biden told reporters: \u8220\'20\'1CA lot of you come from backgrounds like I came from, we\u8217\'20\'19re not poor, just regular folks. But that matters. It matters in your life \u8230\'20\'26 So anyway, I\u8217\'20\'19m optimistic, it\u8217\'20\'19s gonna take some time. And I appreciate the frustration in American people.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 Less than two weeks to go before the 8 November midterms and here\u8217\'20\'19s where things stand: \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/26/fetterman-oz-debate-midterms-biden-politics-latest?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-635942478f08b1b21f138dcc#block-635942478f08b1b21f138dcc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 growing more unpopular}}}\uc2 . Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 chances of keeping control of the House of Representatives are slim, while {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/26/fetterman-oz-debate-midterms-biden-politics-latest?page=with:block-6359483d8f083ccb8b581222#block-6359483d8f083ccb8b581222"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 predictions for the new Republican majority are expanding}}}\uc2 . And Senate control is coming down to a handful of races, including Pennsylvania, where the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/26/fetterman-oz-debate-midterms-biden-politics-latest?page=with:block-63592e938f080759184ffbfa#block-63592e938f080759184ffbfa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democratic candidate struggled}}}\uc2  in last night\u8217\'20\'19s debate, and Georgia, where {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/26/fetterman-oz-debate-midterms-biden-politics-latest?page=with:block-63595bb98f08b1b21f138f51#block-63595bb98f08b1b21f138f51"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 voters appear disinclined}}}\uc2  to support the Republican.\par \par \uc2 Elections haven\u8217\'20\'19t been the only source of news today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2 , \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s former chief of staff, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/26/fetterman-oz-debate-midterms-biden-politics-latest?page=with:block-635950848f08b1b21f138e8d#block-635950848f08b1b21f138e8d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was ordered to appear}}}\uc2  before a special grand jury investigating election meddling in Georgia. Meadows\u8217\'20\'19 lawyer says he plans to appeal.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A Michigan jury{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/26/fetterman-oz-debate-midterms-biden-politics-latest?page=with:block-635956ef8f083ccb8b581303#block-635956ef8f083ccb8b581303"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 convicted three men}}}\uc2  of charges related to plotting to kidnap the state\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic governor \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Twelve GOP candidates to oversee voting in states nationwide deny the outcome of the 2020 election, presenting a threat to democracy. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/26/fetterman-oz-debate-midterms-biden-politics-latest?page=with:block-63594d3e8f08b1b21f138e58#block-63594d3e8f08b1b21f138e58"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Arizona is home}}}\uc2  to one of the most high stakes of these races.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 New polling in Georgia from \uc2 Monmouth University\uc2  shows \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  trailing his Democratic opponent, senator \uc2 Raphael Warnock\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The state\u8217\'20\'19s race is considered one of the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s best chances to oust a sitting Democratic senator, but Monmouth finds Warnock has the edge, with 39% of those surveyed saying they will \u8220\'20\'1Cdefinitely\u8221\'20\'1D vote for him and 10% saying they will \u8220\'20\'1Cprobably\u8221\'20\'1D do so. There\u8217\'20\'19s slightly less enthusiasm for Walker with \u8220\'20\'1Cdefinitely\u8221\'20\'1D at 33% among voters and \u8220\'20\'1Cprobably\u8221\'20\'1D at 11%.\par \par \uc2 enltrGEORGIA VOTER POLL: \uc2 US Senate\uc2  race \u8211\'20\'13 Definite backers of \uc2 Raphael Warnock\uc2  (D) and \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  (R) are each up 7 pts. from Sept.\par \par \uc2 More say they will definitely *not* vote for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/HerschelWalker?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @HerschelWalker}}}\uc2  (46%) than {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ReverendWarnock?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @ReverendWarnock}}}\uc2  (40%). {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/tRZ1ESjiSx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/tRZ1ESjiSx}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/WGoU5RL1c3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/WGoU5RL1c3}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 MonmouthPoll (@MonmouthPoll) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MonmouthPoll/status/1585285598201483265?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 26, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Warnock has a clear advantage in favorability, coming in at 51% among voters as opposed to Walker\u8217\'20\'19s 43%. Monmouth notes that those figures have changed little over the past month, the time period when Walker was accused of paying for a woman\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , even though he says he supports a national ban on the procedure, without exceptions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWalker\u8217\'20\'19s path to victory is narrow, but it\u8217\'20\'19s still there. He needs to get enough voters to overlook their misgivings about him to come over to his support or benefit from a turnout disparity among the two parties\u8217\'20\'19 base voters. At this point, the latter option looks like his better bet,\u8221\'20\'1D director of the independent Monmouth University Polling Institute Patrick Murray said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s Republican senate candidate \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  backs a national ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  without exceptions, but has been accused of hypocrisy after reports emerged he paid for a woman to end her pregnancy. His credibility problem may worsen later today, after a lawyer announced plans to introduce another woman who will say Walker paid for her \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/martin-pengelly"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Martin Pengelly}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 The lawyer Gloria Allred was due on Wednesday to introduce to reporters a woman who alleges \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2 , the Republican candidate for Senate in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/state-of-georgia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Georgia}}}\uc2 , took her to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic to have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Walker has voiced strict anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies but has already been accused of paying for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  for another woman.\par \par \uc2 Allred said the woman now stepping forward, named as Jane Doe, would speak on Wednesday afternoon in Los Angeles.\par \par \uc2 The woman, Allred said, would \u8220\'20\'1Callege that she had a romantic, intimate relationship with \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  and that he drove her to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic to have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after she became pregnant as a result of her relationship with him\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Allred also promised to reveal \u8220\'20\'1Csome of Jane Doe\u8217\'20\'19s evidence in support of her romance with Mr Walker\u8221\'20\'1D, and said her client would read a statement to reporters but would not reveal her name or her face.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/26/herschel-walker-georgia-senate-abortion-clinic"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New woman to say Herschel Walker took her to clinic for \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 Jury convicts three men in plot to kidnap Michigan governor\par \par \uc2 A jury in Michigan has convicted three men on charges related to a plot to kidnap Michigan\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic governor \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/michigan-gretchen-whitmer-jackson-adam-fox-kidnap-plot-trial-0a5a930cf86e74f8a1365040b783de0d?utm_source=homepage&utm_medium=TopNews&utm_campaign=position_04"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Associated Press reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The unsuccessful scheme was attempted by anti-government extremists and came after two other defendants were found guilty of similar charges in August.\par \par \uc2 Whitmer is standing for re-election in the 8 November polls against Republican Tudor Dixon.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on today\u8217\'20\'19s verdict from the AP:\par \par \uc2 Joe Morrison, his father-in-law Pete Musico, and Paul Bellar were found guilty of providing \u8220\'20\'1Cmaterial support\u8221\'20\'1D for a terrorist act as members of a paramilitary group, the Wolverine Watchmen.\par \par \uc2 They held gun drills in rural Jackson County with a leader of the scheme, Adam Fox, who was disgusted with Gov. \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2  and other officials in 2020 and said he wanted to kidnap her.\par \par \uc2 Jurors read and heard violent, anti-government screeds as well as support for the \u8220\'20\'1Cboogaloo,\u8221\'20\'1D a civil war that might be triggered by a shocking abduction. Prosecutors said COVID-19 restrictions ordered by Whitmer turned out to be fruit to recruit more people to the Watchmen.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe facts drip out slowly,\u8221\'20\'1D state Assistant Attorney General Bill Rollstin told jurors in Jackson, Michigan, \u8220\'20\'1Cand you begin to see \u8212\'20\'14 wow \u8212\'20\'14 there were things that happened that people knew about.... When you see how close Adam Fox got to the governor, you can see how a very bad event was thwarted.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/23/gretchen-whitmer-kidnap-plot-two-men-guilty"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Duo found guilty over plot to kidnap Michigan governor Gretchen Whitmer}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 Ex-Trump chief of staff ordered to testify in Georgia election meddling investigation\par \par \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2 , who served as White House chief of staff near the end of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s administration, has been ordered by a judge to appear before a Georgia special grand jury investigating efforts to meddle with the state\u8217\'20\'19s 2020 election results, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/10/26/us/meadows-testify-georgia-election-trump.html?smid=nytcore-ios-share&referringSource=articleShare"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The New York Times reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Meadows had sued in South Carolina, where he lives, to challenge a subpoena compelling his appearance before jurors empaneled in Fulton county that is looking into attempts by Trump\u8217\'20\'19s allies to overturn Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s vote for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  two years ago.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/10/26/us/meadows-testify-georgia-election-trump.html?smid=nytcore-ios-share&referringSource=articleShare"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 According to the Times}}}\uc2 , Meadows\u8217\'20\'19 lawyer James Bannister plans to appeal the ruling. He had unsuccessfully attempted to convince judge Edward W. Miller that the Georgia jury was not criminal in nature, and thus could not force Meadows to testify.\par \par \uc2 The former chief of staff is not the only Trump White House official summoned by the grand jurors, nor the only one to resist. Trump lawyer \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  appeared before the panel, and has been told he was a target of its investigation. GOP senator \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2  was also summoned, but has challenged his subpoena all the way to the supreme court, which has temporarily blocked it as the justices consider his petition.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s not just control of Congress that\u8217\'20\'19s on the ballot this year. Republicans who deny the validity of the 2020 election are running to overseeing voting in 12 states this year \u8211\'20\'13 including Arizona. \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/edpilkington"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ed Pilkington}}}\uc2  reports on the danger posed by secretary of state candidate Mark Finchem:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBELIEVE\u8221\'20\'1D. The word is written in large blue letters above the door of \uc2 Adrian Fontes\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s campaign office in Scottsdale, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/arizona"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Arizona}}}\uc2 , a replica of Ted Lasso\u8217\'20\'19s motivational sign from the hit TV show featuring an American football coach thrown into the bear pit of the English Premier League.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt speaks to me,\u8221\'20\'1D Fontes explained. \u8220\'20\'1CIt says that \u8216\'20\'18You can do it\u8217\'20\'19 is a question of faith.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Then there\u8217\'20\'19s the sign on the other side of the door. Pinned discreetly to the back, where few visitors get to see it, is a printed notice that says: \u8220\'20\'1CAdrian, don\u8217\'20\'19t fuck it up!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 If the \u8220\'20\'1CBELIEVE\u8221\'20\'1D sign speaks to Fontes, then the F-sign \u8211\'20\'13 created by his campaign chair \u8211\'20\'13 should speak to millions of other Americans. They may not know it yet, but their future as citizens of one of the world\u8217\'20\'19s oldest democracies could depend on it.\par \par \uc2 At least that\u8217\'20\'19s how Fontes sees the upcoming midterm election in which he is standing for statewide office. Asked what is at stake on 8 November, what hangs upon him not F-ing it up, he replied: \u8220\'20\'1CLiterally the fate of the republic, and the free world too if you accept that America is still its leader. We are potentially looking at the democracy that upholds the United States of America no longer functioning.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/26/arizona-midterm-election-secretary-of-state-adrian-fontes-mark-finchem"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Democracy on the ballot\u8217\'20\'19: the man fighting to keep Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s election out of an extremist\u8217\'20\'19s hands}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 Two prominent American poll watchers have increased their forecasts for how many seats Republicans will win in House of Representatives \u8211\'20\'13 the chamber they have the best chance of retaking in the upcoming elections.\par \par \uc2 Cook Political Report now has the GOP winning 12 to 25 House seats, much more than the five necessary to gain control of the chamber:\par \par \uc2 enltrNEW {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CookPolitical?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @CookPolitical}}}\uc2  House ratings: 211 seats at least Lean R, 191 seats at least Lean D, 33 Toss Ups. Our new outlook is a GOP gain of 12-25 seats. Full analysis: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/fSRaeBY2JM"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/fSRaeBY2JM}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/RsyN70KZl0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/RsyN70KZl0}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Dave Wasserman (@Redistrict) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Redistrict/status/1585280573601292289?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 26, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 University of Virginia\uc2  poll doyen \uc2 Larry Sabato\uc2  also predicts Republicans have the advantage in House seats:\par \par \uc2 enltr. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/LarrySabato?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @LarrySabato}}}\uc2  's Crystal Ball now rates 218 House seats \u8212\'20\'14 the magic number for winning a majority \u8212\'20\'14 as at least Leans Republican in our House ratings. New analysis by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kkondik?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @kkondik}}}\uc2  : {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/DujzgtMqUb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/DujzgtMqUb}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/LL0XFEzsRj"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/LL0XFEzsRj}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Center for Politics at UVA (@Center4Politics) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Center4Politics/status/1585253900680335365?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 26, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden's approval rating falls ahead of midterms\par \par \uc2 Americans are feeling even more sour about president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  ahead of the 8 November midterms, according to polling firm Gallup.\par \par \uc2 They report that his approval rating is now at 40%, retreating from the modest recovery it saw in August but above his low point of 38% the month prior:\par \par \uc2 enltrPresident \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s latest job approval rating is 40%, similar to his 42% September rating but down from 44% in August. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/78BFFakqJX"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/78BFFakqJX}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 GallupNews (@GallupNews) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GallupNews/status/1584972540170145795?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 25, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 The data confirms that the Democratic leader\u8217\'20\'19s popularity appears to have peaked over the summer amid a series of legislative wins and declining gas prices. Biden has been unpopular with voters for more than a year now, as Americans soured on high inflation and objected to his handling of the withdrawal from Afghanistan.\par \par \uc2 The trend is a negative one for Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 chances of holding their majorities in Congress in the 8 November midterms, though many of the party\u8217\'20\'19s candidates are polling more strongly than Biden, indicating voters may be divorcing their opinions of the president from their preference for control of Congress.\par \par \uc2 Biden will in a few minutes speak about his administration\u8217\'20\'19s actions to help families deal with rising costs. This blog will cover the speech as it happens, and you can watch it below:\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 That \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is planning another run for the presidency in 2024 is well known, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/martin-pengelly"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Martin Pengelly}}}\uc2  reports he\u8217\'20\'19s considering hiring a Republican operative who played a key role in taking down Democrat \uc2 John Kerry\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s presidential campaign in 2004:\par \par \uc2 As he prepares a possible new presidential campaign, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is seeking to recruit an operative who was behind a group which famously questioned the Vietnam war record of the 2004 Democratic nominee, \uc2 John Kerry\uc2 , the \uc2 Washington Post{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/nation/2022/10/25/trump-campaign-lacivita/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The operative who ran Swift Boat Veterans for Truth, Chris LaCivita, worked for one {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/aug/31/trump-super-pac-chris-lacivita-swiftboat-joe-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump-aligned}}}\uc2  political action committee during the 2020 election and now runs another. He is also a consultant for Ron Johnson, a Trump-supporting Wisconsin senator fighting for re-election.\par \par \uc2 The Post cited four anonymous sources. It also reported LaCivita\u8217\'20\'19s response: \u8220\'20\'1CThank you for the opportunity but I don\u8217\'20\'19t comment on rumours!!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/26/swift-boat-attack-john-kerry-trump-2024-campaign"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump 2024 campaign seeks to recruit man who smeared John Kerry \u8211\'20\'13 reports}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is the oldest president ever inaugurated, and will turn 80 this year \u8211\'20\'13 but still plans to run for re-election, according to a reporter who recently interviewed the president, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/martin-pengelly"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Martin Pengelly}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is \u8220\'20\'1Ctotally running\u8221\'20\'1D for a second term, the MSNBC host \uc2 Jonathan Capehart\uc2  has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/opinions/2022/10/25/biden-run-president-again-2024/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2 , just days after interviewing the US president.\par \par \uc2 The oldest president ever inaugurated, Biden will turn 80 on 20 November.\par \par \uc2 He {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/opinions/2022/10/25/biden-run-president-again-2024/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told}}}\uc2  Capehart: \u8220\'20\'1CI can\u8217\'20\'19t even say the age I\u8217\'20\'19m going to be. I can\u8217\'20\'19t even get it out of my mouth. You think I\u8217\'20\'19m joking. I\u8217\'20\'19m not joking.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Speculation about Biden\u8217\'20\'19s age and ambition has become a constant in US politics. Some Democrats have avoided saying he should run again or committing to supporting him if he does. Republicans \u8211\'20\'13 members of a party dominated by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2 , a decidedly erratic 76 \u8211\'20\'13 regularly claim Biden is too old.\par \par \uc2 Regular Biden gaffes, this week including calling \uc2 Rishi Sunak\uc2 , the new British prime minister, \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/video/2022/oct/25/rashi-sanook-joe-biden-rishi-sunak-name-video"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Rashi Sanook}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D, have reinforced such impressions in some quarters.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/26/biden-second-term-president-msnbc-tv-interview"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden \u8216\'20\'18totally running\u8217\'20\'19 for second term as president, MSNBC interviewer says}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 Conservative justice Supreme Court \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  last night spoke before a prominent Washington rightwing group, and claimed the leak of the court\u8217\'20\'19s opinion overturning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights nationwide put the justices in danger, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/edpilkington"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ed Pilkington}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 The leak of the draft supreme court opinion abolishing the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  put members of the conservative majority at risk of assassination, \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2 , the author of the draft, has said.\par \par \uc2 Speaking in Washington at a rightwing thinktank, \uc2 the Heritage Foundation\uc2 , Alito called the leak a month before the final ruling was released \u8220\'20\'1Ca grave betrayal of trust by somebody\u8221\'20\'1D that put several justices in danger.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe leak also made those of us who were thought to be in the majority in support of overruling Roe and Casey targets for assassination because it gave people a rational reason to think they could prevent that from happening by killing one of us.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2022/oct/26/samuel-alito-supreme-court-assassination-abortion-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Alito says leak of draft \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ruling put justices at risk of assassination}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a full rundown of last night\u8217\'20\'19s Pennsylvania Senate debate between Democrat \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2  and Republican Mehmet Oz, from \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/adam-gabbatt"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Adam Gabbatt}}}\uc2  :\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights took centre stage during the debate for Pennsylvania\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 US Senate\uc2  seat on Tuesday night, as Mehmet Oz, a celebrity doctor and the Republican candidate, said decisions over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be left to \u8220\'20\'1Cwomen, doctors, local political leaders\u8221\'20\'1D, while \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2 , the Democrat candidate, criticised the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s hardline stance.\par \par \uc2 The debate in Harrisburg started with Oz, a former surgeon and long-time host of the Dr Oz television show, discussing his desire to make \u8220\'20\'1CWashington civil again\u8221\'20\'1D. The Trump-backed Republican said he wanted to \u8220\'20\'1Cunify, not divide\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 But Oz was soon reverting to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/23/republicans-midterm-elections-agenda-kevin-mccarthy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2022 Republican playbook}}}\uc2  that has been characterised by pugnacity in races across the US, as he referred to Fetterman, Pennsylvania\u8217\'20\'19s lieutenant governor, as a \u8220\'20\'1Cleft-wing extremist\u8221\'20\'1D who had \u8220\'20\'1Cradical positions\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/26/pennsylvania-senate-debate-mehmet-oz-john-fetterman"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights take centre stage as Oz and Fetterman clash in Pennsylvania Senate debate}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 Take a look at some of the highlights of the Pennsylvania Senate debate, courtesy of \uc2 The Washington Post\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 It was plain that \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2 , the state\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic lieutenant governor, was still recovering from his stroke. He attempted to lean into it, saying \u8220\'20\'1Cit knocked me down, and I\u8217\'20\'19m going to keep coming back up.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 His Republican opponent Mehmet Oz didn\u8217\'20\'19t have that problem, but made a gaffe when he said \u8220\'20\'1Cwomen, doctors, local political leaders\u8221\'20\'1D should decide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access. That\u8217\'20\'19s exactly the type of comment Democrats were looking for to remind voters of the threat to reproductive rights posed by the GOP.\par \par \uc2 It was still a rough night for Fetterman, and an online poll from a Pittsburgh television station confirms that viewers noticed:\par \par \uc2 enltrNEW: WPXI Online Poll\par \par \uc2 Who won the PA Senate Debate?\par \par \uc2 (R) Mehmet Oz \u8212\'20\'14 82%\par \par \uc2 (D) \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 18% {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/IBfFJGetal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/IBfFJGetal}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/qsp265y8EJ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/qsp265y8EJ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 InteractivePolls (@IAPolls2022) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/IAPolls2022/status/1585091444041478145?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 26, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s how the state\u8217\'20\'19s departing Republican senator \uc2 Pat Toomey\uc2  put it:\par \par \uc2 enltrAnyone watching today could tell there was only one person on that stage who can represent Pennsylvania in the \uc2 U.S. Senate\uc2 : {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DrOz?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @droz}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s sad to see \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2  struggling so much. He should take more time to allow himself to fully recover. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/pasenatedebate?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #pasenatedebate}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/abc27?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @abc27}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Pat Toomey\uc2  (@PatToomey) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PatToomey/status/1585073109992099841?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 26, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Bob Casey Jr\uc2 , Pennsylvania\u8217\'20\'19s sitting Democratic senator, tied Fetterman\u8217\'20\'19s debate performance, where he was assisted by a closed caption system, to the larger issue of rights for people with disabilities:\par \par \uc2 enltrMy office adds closed captions and alt text to our social media because we know that inclusivity and accessibility bring folks closer to our democracy and the governing process. Accessibility makes our democracy stronger. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/PASenateDebate?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #PASenateDebate}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Bob Casey Jr\uc2 . (@Bob_Casey) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Bob_Casey/status/1585062164687380480?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 26, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, an independent running as a write-in candidate on the ballot last night withdrew his candidacy, telling his supporters to vote for Fetterman:\par \par \uc2 enltrU.S. Senate Announcement: I am polling around 3% which places Democracy at risk. In the interest of protecting the United States I am dropping out of the U.S Senate Race in PA. I fully endorse \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2 . The Democrats must win. PA must be Blue. It has been an honor running.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Everett Stern (@EverettStern1) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/EverettStern1/status/1584976258693492736?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 25, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 Brave or misguided? Fetterman's halting debate performance in crucial Senate race splits Democrats\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. The candidates in Pennsylvania\u8217\'20\'19s high-stakes Senate race faced off last night, where the effects of a recent stroke on Democrat \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2  became clear. He struggled to get his words out against Republican Mehmet Oz in the sort of performance that \u8211\'20\'13 rightly or wrongly \u8211\'20\'13 has sunk candidates in the past. Pennsylvania\u8217\'20\'19s Senate seat is considered crucial for determining which party controls the chamber overall, and Democrats are now split over whether Fetterman did the right thing by showing up for the debate despite his recovery, or whether he should have skipped it. Expect to hear more about this today.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is going on:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is doing a flurry of campaign events for Democrats with less than two weeks before the 8 November midterm elections, appearing virtually today at receptions for Pennsylvania congressman \uc2 Matt Cartwright\uc2 , Iowa congresswoman Cynthia Axne and Nevada\u8217\'20\'19s congressional delegation.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 More debates are planned for today, including the New Hampshire governors race at 6pm eastern time and the South Carolina governors race at 7pm eastern time. Both states are currently led by Republicans.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is in Washington state, where she\u8217\'20\'19ll appear with Democratic senator \uc2 Patty Murray\uc2  amid fears her re-election could be in jeopardy despite the state\u8217\'20\'19s longstanding blue tilt.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020221026eiaq001us\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
