\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  rights take centre stage as Oz and Fetterman clash in Pennsylvania Senate debate\b0\par\par\uc2 Adam Gabbatt \par \uc2 1,336 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 October 2022\par 16:49 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 29\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The two candidates for the competitive Senate seat argued over the economy, crime and the tone of Republican attacks on the Democrat\u8217\'20\'19s healthUS midterms 2022: the key races\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights took centre stage during the debate for Pennsylvania\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 US Senate\uc2  seat on Tuesday night, as Mehmet Oz, a celebrity doctor and the Republican candidate, said decisions over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be left to \u8220\'20\'1Cwomen, doctors, local political leaders\u8221\'20\'1D, while \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2 , the Democratic candidate, criticised the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s hardline stance.\par \par \uc2 The debate in Harrisburg started with Oz, a former surgeon and long-time host of the Dr Oz television show, discussing his desire to make \u8220\'20\'1CWashington civil again\u8221\'20\'1D. The Trump-backed Republican said he wanted to \u8220\'20\'1Cunify, not divide\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 But Oz was soon reverting to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/23/republicans-midterm-elections-agenda-kevin-mccarthy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2022 Republican playbook}}}\uc2  that has been characterised by pugnacity in races across the US, as he referred to Fetterman, Pennsylvania\u8217\'20\'19s lieutenant governor, as a \u8220\'20\'1Cleft-wing extremist\u8221\'20\'1D who had \u8220\'20\'1Cradical positions\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 It set the tone for a contentious evening as the pair clashed over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Pennsylvania\u8217\'20\'19s minimum wage \u8211\'20\'13 which at $7.25 is lower than each of its six bordering states \u8211\'20\'13 and the economy, in what has become one of the closest-watched elections in the US.\par \par \uc2 Fetterman and Oz are vying to replace \uc2 Pat Toomey\uc2 , a retiring Republican, and with the Senate evenly divided between the two parties, both are desperate to win in a state that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  picked up by 80,000 votes in 2020.\par \par \uc2 This was Fetterman\u8217\'20\'19s highest-profile appearance of the campaign, since he suffered a stroke in mid-May, which has left him with auditory processing issues, where the brain struggles to understand the spoken word.\par \par \uc2 To accommodate Fetterman\u8217\'20\'19s condition, which he said is improving daily, two 70-inch monitors were placed above the heads of the moderators, which showed the transcribed text of their questions, and the text of Oz\u8217\'20\'19s responses.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLet\u8217\'20\'19s also talk about the elephant in the room,\u8221\'20\'1D Fetterman said in his opening remarks. \u8220\'20\'1CI had a stroke. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/31/john-fetterman-dr-oz-health-stroke"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 He [Oz] never let me forget that}}}\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Democrat was referring to the Republican\u8217\'20\'19s campaign which has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/23/dr-oz-aide-john-fetterman-stroke-pennsylvania"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 launched unsavory attacks}}}\uc2  against Fetterman, with one Oz aide, Rachel Tripp, claiming Fetterman might not have had a stroke if he \u8220\'20\'1Chad ever eaten a vegetable in his life\u8221\'20\'1D. In August Oz\u8217\'20\'19s campaign {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/henryjgomez/status/1564720328798097412"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 released}}}\uc2  what it said were \u8220\'20\'1Cconcessions\u8221\'20\'1D it was prepared to make during a debate with Fetterman, which included a promise to \u8220\'20\'1Cpay for any additional medical personnel he might need to have on standby\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Oz has since tried to distance himself from the tone of his campaign, but said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.foxbusiness.com/shows/mornings-with-maria"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on Fox Business}}}\uc2  recently: \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t think there\u8217\'20\'19s closed captioning on the floor of the Senate.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Fetterman, 53, released a report from his doctor last week that said he \u8220\'20\'1Chas no work restrictions and can work full duty in public office\u8221\'20\'1D, but the doctor noted that Fetterman has difficulty processing some words.\par \par \uc2 In a TV interview in early October, Fetterman said he will sometimes miss words, or \u8220\'20\'1Cmush\u8221\'20\'1D words together when speaking, and there were times when his issues with speech were noticeable during the debate. The Democrat appeared to struggle to find certain words and took longer than Oz to reply to questions as he read captioning on screen.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt knocked me down but I\u8217\'20\'19m going to keep coming back up,\u8221\'20\'1D Fetterman said of the stroke on Tuesday. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd this campaign is all about, to me is about fighting for everyone in Pennsylvania that ever got knocked down that needs to get back up.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The pair were asked about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  early in the debate. Nationally, Democrats have drawn attention to Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 role in the landmark Roe v Wade decision being overturned in June this year. Republicans, particularly in politically moderate states like Pennsylvania, have sought to avoid the issue.\par \par \uc2 Oz was asked: \u8220\'20\'1CShould \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  be banned in America\u8221\'20\'1D, but declined to answer directly, suggesting instead that \u8220\'20\'1Cthere should not be involvement from the federal government\u8221\'20\'1D, and that states should be able to decide their own \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI want women, doctors, local political leaders, letting the democracy that\u8217\'20\'19s always allowed our nation to thrive, to put the best ideas forward so states can decide for themselves,\u8221\'20\'1D Oz said, in remarks that were immediately derided online.\par \par \uc2 Fetterman said he would \u8220\'20\'1Cfight to re-establish\u8221\'20\'1D Roe v Wade, which he said \u8220\'20\'1Cshould be the law\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf you believe that the choice of your reproductive freedom belongs with Dr Oz, then you have a choice. But if you believe that the choice for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  belongs with you and your doctor, that\u8217\'20\'19s what I fight for,\u8221\'20\'1D the Democrat said.\par \par \uc2 Fetterman, who spent 13 years as mayor of Braddock, a small borough outside Pittsburgh, rose to national fame in the aftermath of the 2020 election, when as Pennsylvania\u8217\'20\'19s lieutenant governor he vigorously rebuffed Trump\u8217\'20\'19s claims of voter fraud, at one point referring to the then president as \u8220\'20\'1Cno different than any other random internet troll\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He has also attracted attention for his atypical \u8211\'20\'13 for a politician \u8211\'20\'13 appearance. At 6ft 8in tall, Fetterman is usually seen wearing hoodies at campaign events, and has tattoos on his forearms, including {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://john-fetterman.medium.com/the-truth-about-my-tattoos-cc4b2940ceb6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 nine on his right arm}}}\uc2  which mark the dates that people were killed \u8220\'20\'1Cthrough violence\u8221\'20\'1D in Braddock while he was mayor.\par \par \uc2 Oz is best known for hosting the Dr Oz Show, a daytime TV program about medical issues which, he said on Tuesday, \u8220\'20\'1Cruffled a lot of feathers\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The show also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.businessinsider.com/dr-oz-false-misleading-baseless-medical-claims-coronavirus-2020-4#oz-pushed-hydroxychloroquine-to-fight-the-coronavirus-even-though-its-effects-were-still-unproven-1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 promoted}}}\uc2  fad treatments and ineffective products and Oz has been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thedailybeast.com/dr-oz-worlds-best-snake-oil-salesman"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 repeatedly dubbed}}}\uc2  a \u8220\'20\'1Csnake oil salesman\u8221\'20\'1D. In 2014 he was asked to appear before a Senate committee, where he was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/news/the-fix/wp/2016/09/15/that-time-congress-railed-on-dr-oz-for-his-miracle-diet-pills/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 berated by senators}}}\uc2  over his promotion of \u8220\'20\'1Cmiracle\u8221\'20\'1D diet pills that the medical community agreed do not work.\par \par \uc2 The Fetterman campaign had tried to temper expectations ahead of the debate, and released a memo on Monday saying that debate \u8220\'20\'1Cisn\u8217\'20\'19t John\u8217\'20\'19s format\u8221\'20\'1D, pointing out that some had been underwhelmed by Fetterman\u8217\'20\'19s performance in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.c-span.org/video/?519182-1/pennsylvania-democratic-us-senate-debate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 debates}}}\uc2  during the Democratic primary this spring.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CJohn is five months post-stroke and Oz has spent the last two decades literally in a TV studio; if there\u8217\'20\'19s a home-field advantage, it\u8217\'20\'19s definitely his,\u8217\'20\'19\u8217\'20\'19 Rebecca Katz, Fetterman\u8217\'20\'19s communications adviser, told the \uc2 New York Times\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 At times Fetterman\u8217\'20\'19s speaking did hold him back, but he rebutted Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 suggestions \u8211\'20\'13 repeated through countless TV ads in the state \u8211\'20\'13 that he was \u8220\'20\'1Csoft on crime\u8221\'20\'1D, pointing to successes in bringing down gun crime in Braddock.\par \par \uc2 Oz, Fetterman said, \u8220\'20\'1Chas never made any attempt to try to address crime during his entire career except showing up for photo ops here in Philadelphia.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 On the minimum wage, Oz said \u8220\'20\'1Cmarket forces\u8221\'20\'1D would raise Pennsylvania\u8217\'20\'19s minimum wage of $7.25 \u8211\'20\'13 the lowest amount allowed under federal law and an amount, when adjusted for inflation, which is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.businessinsider.com/current-federal-minimum-wage-is-13-years-old-inflation-impact-2022-7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the lowest minimum wage in decades}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Fetterman said he \u8220\'20\'1Cabsolutely\u8221\'20\'1D supports the proposal to raise the minimum wage to $15 an hour, adding: \u8220\'20\'1CI think it\u8217\'20\'19s a disgrace at $7.25 an hour.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 As the debate drew to a close, both candidates were asked about their parties\u8217\'20\'19 potential candidates for the 2024 presidential election. Fetterman said he would support Biden if the president ran again.\par \par \uc2 In a tacit acknowledgement of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s divisiveness and deep unpopularity in parts of the country, Oz was initially less equivocal, saying only that he would \u8220\'20\'1Csupport whoever the Republican party puts up\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 A moderator reminded viewers that Trump had endorsed Oz \u8211\'20\'13 an action Trump rarely bestows on those likely to disappoint him \u8211\'20\'13 and asked Oz why he wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t return that support.\par \par \uc2 That prompted Oz, perhaps mindful of the notoriously emotional and combustible nature of his backer, to clarify his position.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COh I do,\u8221\'20\'1D Oz said. \u8220\'20\'1CI would support \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  if he decided to run for president.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020221026eiaq000jh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
