\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  assured Ted Kennedy in 2005 of respect for Roe, diary reveals\b0\par\par\uc2 Martin Pengelly in New York \par \uc2 707 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 October 2022\par 05:06 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Excerpts reported by biographer show Alito, who wrote June ruling that outlawed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said he was \u8216\'20\'18big believer in precedents\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 In a private meeting in 2005, \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2 , who would become the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  justice who wrote the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.supremecourt.gov/opinions/21pdf/19-1392_6j37.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ruling}}}\uc2  removing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the federal right}}}\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , assured Ted Kennedy of his respect for Roe v Wade, the landmark 1973 court decision which made the procedure legal in the US.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am a believer in precedents,\u8221\'20\'1D Alito said, according to diary excerpts {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/10/24/us/politics/alito-kennedy-abortion.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  by the Massachusetts senator\u8217\'20\'19s biographer, John A Farrell, on Monday. \u8220\'20\'1CPeople would find I adhere to that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Alito and Kennedy met regarding Alito\u8217\'20\'19s nomination by George W Bush. The nominee also said: \u8220\'20\'1CI recognise there is a right to privacy. I think it\u8217\'20\'19s settled.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Seventeen years later, in his ruling removing the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , via the Mississippi {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/nov/30/explainer-mississippi-abortion-rights-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 case Dobbs v Jackson}}}\uc2 , Alito {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.supremecourt.gov/opinions/21pdf/19-1392_6j37.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  the entitlement had wrongly been held to be protected as part of the right to privacy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRoe was egregiously wrong from the start,\u8221\'20\'1D he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.supremecourt.gov/opinions/21pdf/19-1392_6j37.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote this June}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The late Kennedy, a younger brother of US president John F Kennedy, who spent 47 years in the Senate, also questioned Alito about a memo he wrote as a justice department clerk in 1985, outlining his opposition to Roe. Alito told Kennedy he had been trying to impress his bosses.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI was a younger person,\u8221\'20\'1D Alito said. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve matured a lot.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 According to Farrell, Alito told Kennedy his views on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  were \u8220\'20\'1Cpersonal\u8221\'20\'1D but said: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve got constitutional responsibilities and those are going to be the determining views\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Alito was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/series/4982475/alito-s-supreme-court-nomination-confirmed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 confirmed}}}\uc2  to the supreme court by the senate, 58 votes to 42. Kennedy voted no.\par \par \uc2 Farrell reported the excerpts from Kennedy\u8217\'20\'19s diary {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/10/24/us/politics/alito-kennedy-abortion.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in the New York Times}}}\uc2 . A spokesperson for Alito \u8220\'20\'1Csaid he had no comment on the conversation\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Kennedy {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2009/aug/26/us-senator-ted-kennedy-dies"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 died in 2009, aged 77}}}\uc2 . His Senate seat was filled by a Republican, \uc2 Scott Brown\uc2 , who was subsequently defeated by Elizabeth Warren, who quickly emerged as a leading progressive. In June, after Alito\u8217\'20\'19s ruling removed the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Warren was a leading voice of liberal anger.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAfter decades of scheming,\u8221\'20\'1D she {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.warren.senate.gov/newsroom/press-releases/senator-warren-statement-on-dobbs-v-jackson-womens-health-organization"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1CRepublican politicians have finally forced their unpopular agenda on the rest of America.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Susan Collins\uc2 , a Maine Republican but a supporter of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, said she had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/25/gorsuch-kavanaugh-misled-senators-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 been misled}}}\uc2  in a meeting similar to that between Kennedy and Alito.\par \par \uc2 Collins said that in the 2018 meeting, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2018/sep/09/abortion-rights-coat-hangers-collins-kavanaugh-supreme-court-roe-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 when asked about Roe}}}\uc2 , \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2  told her to \u8220\'20\'1Cstart with my record, my respect for precedent, my belief that it is rooted in the constitution and my commitment to the rule of law\u8221\'20\'1D and added: \u8220\'20\'1CI understand precedent and I understand the importance of overturning it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In 2022, Kavanaugh sided with Alito and three other conservatives in removing the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Collins {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/06/24/us/roe-kavanaugh-collins-notes.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CI feel misled.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Discussing Alito\u8217\'20\'19s meeting with Kennedy, Stephen Gillers, a \uc2 New York University\uc2  law professor and legal ethics specialist, told the Times: \u8220\'20\'1CNo serious court watcher can doubt that what Alito said in Dobbs he deeply believed in 2005. And long before then.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Farrell\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.jafarrell.com/thebooks.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 previous books}}}\uc2  include a biography of Richard Nixon. On Monday, reviewing Ted Kennedy: A Life, the Associated Press {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.latimes.com/entertainment-arts/books/story/2022-10-24/ted-kennedy-a-life-biography-book-review"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CTeddy lived long enough for his flaws to be fully exposed. All are laid bare in this book \u8211\'20\'13 the drinking, the infidelity, the selfishness, the casual cruelty, the emotional isolation.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe central riddle of Kennedy is how these weaknesses existed alongside the benevolence, loyalty, perseverance and wisdom that made him one of the most influential senators in modern American history.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The AP review noted Kennedy\u8217\'20\'19s silence during another supreme court nomination, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/10/clarence-thomas-supreme-court-justice"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 that of Clarence Thomas in 1991}}}\uc2 , writing: \u8220\'20\'1CWhen \uc2 Anita Hill\uc2  accused Thomas of sexual harassment, Kennedy was in no position to help lead the fight against him. He passed his time at the confirmation hearings by doodling sailboats, and Thomas was confirmed.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In June this year, Thomas joined with Alito to overturn Roe v Wade. In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.supremecourt.gov/opinions/21pdf/19-1392_6j37.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 concurring opinion}}}\uc2 , he suggested other privacy based rights could be next, including the rights to contraception and same-sex marriage.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020221025eiap000mh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
