\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Two Chinese spies charged with trying to obstruct US \uc2 Huawei\uc2  investigation, Garland says \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein in Washington \par \uc2 6,105 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 October 2022\par 20:16 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Duo accused of trying to disrupt criminal prosecutionSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/24/trump-interviews-woodward-biden-rally-midterms-desantis-debate-politics-latest?page=with:block-6356d1438f0885fc0bbd4092#block-6356d1438f0885fc0bbd4092"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 justice department announced}}}\uc2  charges in three cases alleging Chinese intelligence officers attempted to steal technology, pressured a naturalized US citizen to return to the country and interfered with the prosecution of telecommunications giant \uc2 Huawei\uc2 , while warning Beijing against continued wrongdoing in the United States. Meanwhile, a prominent journalist who interviewed Trump 20 times {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/24/trump-interviews-woodward-biden-rally-midterms-desantis-debate-politics-latest?page=with:block-635683c18f08ff8bc54cfbed#block-635683c18f08ff8bc54cfbed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 warned}}}\uc2  he wasn\u8217\'20\'19t only dangerous for democracy, he was also incompetent.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else happened today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Polls show tight races for Senate in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/24/trump-interviews-woodward-biden-rally-midterms-desantis-debate-politics-latest?page=with:block-6356a51f8f08ff8bc54cfdb9#block-6356a51f8f08ff8bc54cfdb9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ohio}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/24/trump-interviews-woodward-biden-rally-midterms-desantis-debate-politics-latest?page=with:block-6356bb9f8f08855c22ca63d4#block-6356bb9f8f08855c22ca63d4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Wisconsin}}}\uc2 , and a Democrat in the lead in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/24/trump-interviews-woodward-biden-rally-midterms-desantis-debate-politics-latest?page=with:block-6356bb9f8f08855c22ca63d4#block-6356bb9f8f08855c22ca63d4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pennsylvania}}}\uc2  as the party hopes to maintain its majority in Congress\u8217\'20\'19 upper chamber.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Supreme court justice Samuel Alito{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/24/trump-interviews-woodward-biden-rally-midterms-desantis-debate-politics-latest?page=with:block-6356ea7a8f0885fc0bbd4173#block-6356ea7a8f0885fc0bbd4173"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told a top Democratic senator}}}\uc2  he considered Roe v Wade settled law during his confirmation hearing in 2005 \u8211\'20\'13 then voted to overturn it 17 years later.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Areas represented in Congress by 2020 election deniers tend to have seen their white population share decline, and be less well off and well educated than elsewhere, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/24/trump-interviews-woodward-biden-rally-midterms-desantis-debate-politics-latest?page=with:block-6356b7728f0885fc0bbd3f70#block-6356b7728f0885fc0bbd3f70"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a New York Times analysis found}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Republican senator \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s subpoena compelling his appearance before a special grand jury investigating the campaign to meddle with Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s election results two years ago {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/24/trump-interviews-woodward-biden-rally-midterms-desantis-debate-politics-latest?page=with:block-6356bf088f0885fc0bbd3fd7#block-6356bf088f0885fc0bbd3fd7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is on hold}}}\uc2  thanks to conservative supreme court justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Almost 17 years before he wrote the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s opinion overturning Roe v Wade, \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  told a prominent Democratic senator he considered the case guaranteeing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access nationwide settled law, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/10/24/us/politics/alito-kennedy-abortion.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The New York Times}}}\uc2  reports.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am a believer in precedents\u8221\'20\'1D, Alito, then a federal judge, told \uc2 Edward Kennedy\uc2 . In a reference to one of the core justifications for the original Roe decision, he told Kennedy, \u8220\'20\'1CI recognize there is a right to privacy,\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1CI think it\u8217\'20\'19s settled.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The new details were taken from Kennedy\u8217\'20\'19s private diary, portions of which will be published in the book \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Ted Kennedy\uc2 : A Life\u8221\'20\'1D set for release Tuesday, and reported by the Times.\par \par \uc2 The senator was skeptical of Alito\u8217\'20\'19s repeated statements indicating he wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t try to overturn Roe, and also didn\u8217\'20\'19t buy Alito\u8217\'20\'19s explanation that he had written a memo outlining his opposition to Roe because he was seeking a promotion while working as a lawyer in the administration of Republican president \uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2 . Kennedy voted against confirming Alito to the supreme court, and died in 2009. Last June, Alito helmed the five-justice majority that overturned Roe, and allowed states to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  completely \u8211\'20\'13 in an apparent contradiction of what he told Kennedy.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 The state department has responded to the letter from progressive lawmakers urging the Biden administration to redouble efforts to find a negotiated solution to the war in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 According to CNN, the department\u8217\'20\'19s spokesman \uc2 Ned Price\uc2  said Ukraine would be willing to engage in dialogue with Russia, but Moscow appears unwilling. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from his briefing:\par \par \uc2 enltrState Dept spokesperson \uc2 Ned Price\uc2 's response to this today: \u8220\'20\'1CIn order for diplomacy to take place, there have to be parties ready and willing to engage in diplomacy. Right now, we have heard from our Ukrainian partners repeatedly that this war will only end through diplomacy... {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/jRkkGqtRcd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/jRkkGqtRcd}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Natasha Bertrand (@NatashaBertrand) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NatashaBertrand/status/1584628016046821376?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 24, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltr...and dialogue. We have not heard any reciprocal statement or refrain from Moscow that they are ready in good faith to engage in that diplomacy and dialogue."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Natasha Bertrand (@NatashaBertrand) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NatashaBertrand/status/1584628018013556736?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 24, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 Hugo Lowell was at \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s press conference in Washington earlier and is filing updates to his Guardian report, which you can find {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/oct/24/huawei-chinese-spies-us-prosecutors-department-of-justice"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 . Hugo\u8217\'20\'19s report begins\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 Two Chinese intelligence officers tried to bribe a US law enforcement official as part of an effort to obtain inside information about a criminal case against the Chinese telecommunications company {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/huawei"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Huawei}}}\uc2 , federal prosecutors alleged in an indictment unsealed on Monday.\par \par \uc2 The move to unmask the espionage operation \u8211\'20\'13 and charge the two agents with obstruction of justice \u8211\'20\'13 amounts to an escalation by the US justice department after it accused \uc2 Huawei\uc2  in February 2020 of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2020/feb/13/huawei-new-us-indictment-decades-long-steal-technology"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 conducting racketeering and conspiracy}}}\uc2  to steal trade secrets.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis was an egregious attempt by PRC intelligence officers to shield a PRC-based company from accountability and to undermine the integrity of our judicial system,\u8221\'20\'1D the attorney general \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  said at a news conference unveiling the indictment.\par \par \uc2 The report in full:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/oct/24/huawei-chinese-spies-us-prosecutors-department-of-justice"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US accuses Chinese spies of plot to steal secrets in Huawei investigation}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 Issue One Action, a \u8220\'20\'1Cnonpartisan advocacy organization dedicated to uniting Republicans, Democrats and independents in the fight to fix our broken political system\u8221\'20\'1D, has released {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.issueoneaction.org/election-deniers-exposed-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a report}}}\uc2  in which it names \u8220\'20\'1Cthe nine most dangerous anti-democracy candidates running to administer US elections\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Included are Jim Marchant of Nevada, running for secretary of state; Mark Finchem of Arizona, running for secretary of state; and \uc2 Doug Mastriano\uc2  of Pennsylvania, running for governor.\par \par \uc2 For a story published by Guardian US today, Adam Gabbatt went to Pennsylvania to look at Mastriano\u8217\'20\'19s campaign. He writes:\par \par \uc2 Mastriano is, by most measures, an extremist.\par \par \uc2 As a state senator in Pennsylvania, he said women who violated a proposed six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.witf.org/2019/11/14/heart-beat-bill-under/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 should be charged}}}\uc2  with murder. Mastriano frequently attacks trans people, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://soundcloud.com/newstalk1037fm/news-talk-1037fm-welcomes-col-doug-mastriano-12-feb-18?utm_source=clipboard&utm_medium=text&utm_campaign=social_sharing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has said}}}\uc2  gay marriage should be illegal, and that same-sex couples should not be allowed to adopt children.\par \par \uc2 At {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.yorkdispatch.com/story/news/local/pennsylvania/2022/05/05/mastriano-embodies-christian-nationalist-movement-he-runs-governor-we-have-power-god/9661306002/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an event this summer}}}\uc2 , organized by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://poppm.org/about/bio/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a pair}}}\uc2  of self-described prophets, Mastriano told his supporters: \u8220\'20\'1CWe have the power of God with us.\u8221\'20\'1D He added that Jesus Christ is \u8220\'20\'1Cguiding and directing our steps\u8221\'20\'1D. While working at the Army War College, an academy for military members, Mastriano posed for a faculty photo {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/world/us/exclusive-pennsylvania-candidate-mastriano-posed-confederate-uniform-army-war-2022-08-26/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wearing a Confederate uniform}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 And as a key schemer in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s bid to overturn the presidential election, Mastriano {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://whyy.org/articles/mastriano-campaign-spent-thousands-on-buses-ahead-of-d-c-insurrection/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 spent thousands of dollars}}}\uc2  chartering buses to Washington DC on January 6, where images showed him {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.paspotlight.org/2021/seditionhunters-use-pa-spotlight-reporting-to-further-track-mastrianos-insurrection-movements-photos/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 close to the violence}}}\uc2  as Trump supporters stormed the US Capitol.\par \par \uc2 None of this stopped Mastriano, who was endorsed by Trump, from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pbs.org/newshour/politics/trump-pick-doug-mastriano-wins-pennsylvania-gop-primary"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 winning}}}\uc2  the Republican nomination for governor in May.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s Adam\u8217\'20\'19s full piece:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/24/doug-mastriano-pennsylvania-republicans-trump-governor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Doug Mastriano: is the Trump-backed election denier too extreme to win?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 Switching focus for a moment from China to Ukraine, 30 liberal Democrats in Congress have signed a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://progressives.house.gov/_cache/files/5/5/5523c5cc-4028-4c46-8ee1-b56c7101c764/B7B3674EFB12D933EA4A2B97C7405DD4.10-24-22-cpc-letter-for-diplomacy-on-russia-ukraine-conflict.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 letter}}}\uc2  to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , in which they call for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to change course on the matter of the Russian invasion, to couple current economic and military support for Kyiv with a \u8220\'20\'1Cproactive diplomatic push, redoubling efforts to seek a realistic framework for a ceasefire\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The lawmakers continue:\par \par \uc2 This is consistent with your recognition that \u8216\'20\'18there\u8217\'20\'19s going to have to be a negotiated settlement here\u8217\'20\'19, and your concern that \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  \u8216\'20\'18doesn\u8217\'20\'19t have a way out right now, and I\u8217\'20\'19m trying to figure out what we do about that.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 We are under no illusions regarding the difficulties involved in engaging Russia given its outrageous and illegal invasion of Ukraine and its decision to make additional illegal annexations of Ukrainian territory. However, if there is a way to end the war while preserving a free and independent Ukraine, it is America\u8217\'20\'19s responsibility to pursue every diplomatic avenue to support such a solution that is acceptable to the people of Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 The signatories are led by \uc2 Pramila Jayapal\uc2 , the chair of the Congressional Progressive Caucus, and prominent progressives including \uc2 Cori Bush\uc2 , \uc2 Ro Khanna\uc2 , \uc2 Ilhan Omar\uc2 , \uc2 Ayanna Pressley\uc2 , \uc2 Rashida Tlaib\uc2 , \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2  and \uc2 Jamie Raskin\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 As the \uc2 Washington Post{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2022/10/24/biden-ukraine-liberals/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 points out}}}\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1Cthe appeal for a shift in strategy comes amid some of the most significant US-Russian diplomatic engagement in some time, as Defense Secretary \uc2 Lloyd Austin\uc2  recently talked with his Russian counterpart, \uc2 Sergei Shoigu\uc2 , for the first time in months. The two spoke by phone Friday and again on Sunday at Shoigu\u8217\'20\'19s request, Austin wrote on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Austin said he \u8220\'20\'1Crejected any pretext for Russian escalation & reaffirmed the value of continued communication amid Russia\u8217\'20\'19s unlawful & unjustified war against Ukraine\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Chinese government\u8217\'20\'19s alleged misdeeds go beyond attempts to counter the prosecution of \uc2 Huawei\uc2 . Garland announced charges in two other cases \u8211\'20\'13 one involving technology theft and intimidation, and the other involving a pressure campaign to get a naturalized US citizen to return to China against his will.\par \par \uc2 In the first, federal prosecutors in New Jersey indicted four people, including three Chinese intelligence officers, with using \u8220\'20\'1Cthe cover of a purported Chinese academic institute to target, co-opt and direct individuals in the United States to further the PRC intelligence mission\u8221\'20\'1D over 10 years from 2008, Garland said.\par \par \uc2 They also attempted \u8220\'20\'1Cto procure technology and equipment from the United States and to have it shipped to China,\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cstop protected First Amendment activities, protests here in the United States, which would have been embarrassing for the Chinese government,\u8221\'20\'1D Garland said.\par \par \uc2 The second case involves seven people charged with undertaking \u8220\'20\'1Ca multi-year campaign of threats and harassment to force a US resident to return to China,\u8221\'20\'1D Garland said. Two of the individuals indicted in the eastern district of New York were arrested yesterday, he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDefendants threatened the victim saying that, \u8216\'20\'18coming back and turning herself in is the only way out,\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D Garland said. \u8220\'20\'1CThey showed up at the home of the victim\u8217\'20\'19s son in New York. They filed frivolous lawsuits against the victim and his son and said it would be \u8216\'20\'18endless misery for the defendant and son to defend themselves.\u8217\'20\'19 And they made clear that their harassment would not stop until the victim returned to China.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese cases demonstrate the government of China sought to interfere with the rights and freedoms of individuals in the United States and to undermine our judicial system that protects those rights,\u8221\'20\'1D Garland said. \u8220\'20\'1CThe Justice Department will not tolerate attempts by any foreign power to undermine the rule of law upon which our democracy is based.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 Justice department accuses China of attempting to disrupt prosecution of \uc2 Huawei\par \par \uc2 Two Chinese intelligence agents have been charged with attempting to disrupt the prosecution of a Chinese telecommunications firm, US attorney general \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  has announced.\par \par \uc2 While he did not name the company, the Associated Press reports it is likely \uc2 Huawei\uc2 , the giant Chinese manufacturer of cellphones, routers and other communications devices.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COver the past week, the justice department has taken several actions to disrupt criminal activity by individuals working on behalf of the government of the People\u8217\'20\'19s Republic of China,\u8221\'20\'1D Garland said in a speech.\par \par \uc2 He announced charges against \u8220\'20\'1Ctwo PRC intelligence officers with attempting to obstruct influence and impede a criminal prosecution of a PRC-based telecommunications company.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on the case {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/government-and-politics-criminal-investigations-363641d3d0e79a440214c688580ba416"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 from the AP}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 The two men, Guochun He and Zheng Wang, are accused of trying to direct a person with the \uc2 U.S. government\uc2  whom they believed was a cooperator to provide confidential information about the Justice Department\u8217\'20\'19s investigation, including about witnesses, trial evidence and potential new charges. One of the defendants paid about $61,000 for the information, the Justice Department said.\par \par \uc2 The person the men reached out to began working as a double agent for the U.S government, and his contact with the defendants was overseen by the \uc2 FBI\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The company is not named in the charging documents, though the references make clear that it\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Huawei\uc2 , which was charged in 2019 with bank fraud and again the following year with new charges of racketeering conspiracy and a plot to steal trade secrets.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is right now speaking at \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  headquarters in Washington, where he\u8217\'20\'19s warning about the consequences of a Republican takeover of Congress.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s the latest from Politico\u8217\'20\'19s reporter on the scene:\par \par \uc2 enltrFifteen days before the midterms, President Biden visits DNC headquarters in Washington and acknowledges that his party is running \u8220\'20\'1Cagainst the tide\u8221\'20\'1D and casts doubt on the polls - but predicts a final surge for the Democrats {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/cMr6efUqi4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/cMr6efUqi4}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jonathan Lemire (@JonLemire) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JonLemire/status/1584599119846379524?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 24, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrMore Biden at DNC, about Republicans:\par \par \uc2 "They'll shut down the government, they say, and send the nation into default, which raises the price for everyone if we do not cut social security and Medicare.\par \par \uc2 *dramatically whispers*\par \par \uc2 "I ain't going to do it."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jonathan Lemire (@JonLemire) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JonLemire/status/1584600696283836416?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 24, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s a reason why Biden and the Democrats are quick to mention Social Security and Medicare. The two programs are relied by older Americans, who tend to be reliable voters, and any changes to them are considered politically perilous.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 Six years ago, liberal documentary filmmaker Michael Moore correctly predicted \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s election win. Today, he\u8217\'20\'19s calling the upcoming midterms for the Democrats, and explains why in an interview with \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/edwardhelmore"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Edward Helmore}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 For the past month, Academy Award-winning documentary maker Michael Moore has been emailing out a daily missive {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.michaelmoore.com/s/mikes-midterm-tsunami-of-truth?utm_source=substack&utm_medium=menu"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMike\u8217\'20\'19s Midterm Tsunami of Truth\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  on why he believes Democrats will win big in America\u8217\'20\'19s midterm elections next month.\par \par \uc2 Moore calls it \u8220\'20\'1Ca brief honest daily dose of the truth \u8211\'20\'13 and the real optimism these truths offer us\u8221\'20\'1D. It also \u8211\'20\'13 at this moment in time \u8211\'20\'13 flies in the face of most political punditry, which sees a Republican win on the cards.\par \par \uc2 Making predictions is a risky undertaking in any election cycle, but especially in this round with Democrats banking they can hitch Republican candidates to an unpopular supreme court decision to overturn federal guarantees of a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans}}}\uc2 , meanwhile, are laser-focused on high inflation rates, economic troubles and fears over crime rates.\par \par \uc2 But political forecasting has become Moore\u8217\'20\'19s business since he correctly called that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  would win the national elections in 2016 against common judgment of the media and pollsters businesses.\par \par \uc2 The thrust of his reasoning that this will be \u8220\'20\'1CRoe-vember\u8221\'20\'1D is amplified daily in the emails. In missive {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.michaelmoore.com/p/midterm-tsunami-truth-21"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  #21}}}\uc2  (Don\u8217\'20\'19t Believe It) on Tuesday, he addressed the issue of political fatalism, specifically the media narrative that the party in power necessarily does poorly in midterm elections.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe effect of this kind of reporting can be jarring \u8211\'20\'13 it can get inside the average American\u8217\'20\'19s head and scramble it,\u8221\'20\'1D Moore wrote. \u8220\'20\'1CYou can start to feel deflated. You want to quit. You start believing that we liberals are a bunch of losers. And by thinking of ourselves this way, if you\u8217\'20\'19re not careful, you begin to manifest the old narrative into existence.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/23/michael-moore-democratic-party-win-midterm-interview"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18I\u8217\'20\'19m deadly serious\u8217\'20\'19: why film-maker Michael Moore is confident of a Democratic midterm win}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re awaiting an announcement from attorney general \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  about a \u8220\'20\'1Csignificant national security matter\u8221\'20\'1D that could involve another country. He\u8217\'20\'19s set to speak alongside \uc2 FBI\uc2  director \uc2 Christopher Wray\uc2  at a press conference beginning at 1:30 pm eastern time.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has happened today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Polls show tight races for Senate in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/24/trump-interviews-woodward-biden-rally-midterms-desantis-debate-politics-latest?page=with:block-6356a51f8f08ff8bc54cfdb9#block-6356a51f8f08ff8bc54cfdb9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ohio}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/24/trump-interviews-woodward-biden-rally-midterms-desantis-debate-politics-latest?page=with:block-6356bb9f8f08855c22ca63d4#block-6356bb9f8f08855c22ca63d4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Wisconsin}}}\uc2 , and a Democrat in the lead in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/24/trump-interviews-woodward-biden-rally-midterms-desantis-debate-politics-latest?page=with:block-6356bb9f8f08855c22ca63d4#block-6356bb9f8f08855c22ca63d4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pennsylvania}}}\uc2  as the party hopes to maintain its majority in Congress\u8217\'20\'19 upper chamber.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Areas represented in Congress by 2020 election deniers tend to have seen their white population decline, and be less well-off and well educated than elsewhere, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/24/trump-interviews-woodward-biden-rally-midterms-desantis-debate-politics-latest?page=with:block-6356b7728f0885fc0bbd3f70#block-6356b7728f0885fc0bbd3f70"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a New York Times analysis found}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Republican senator \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s subpoena compelling his appearance before a special grand jury investigating the campaign to meddle with Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s election results two years ago {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/24/trump-interviews-woodward-biden-rally-midterms-desantis-debate-politics-latest?page=with:block-6356bf088f0885fc0bbd3fd7#block-6356bf088f0885fc0bbd3fd7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is on hold}}}\uc2  thanks to conservative supreme court justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 Conservative supreme court justice blocks grand jury subpoena for \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2  testimony\par \par \uc2 Rightwing supreme court justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  has placed a temporary hold on a Georgia grand jury\u8217\'20\'19s subpoena compelling the testimony of Republican senator \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2  as part of its investigation into efforts by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s allies to meddle in the state\u8217\'20\'19s election results:\par \par \uc2 enltrBREAKING: Justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 , acting unilaterally, issues a "shadow docket" ruling for Sen. \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2 , agreeing to temporarily halt Graham from testifying in probe of pro-Trump election interference in Georgia\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 John Kruzel (@johnkruzel) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/johnkruzel/status/1584579810776739840?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 24, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Thomas is one of the court\u8217\'20\'19s most conservative justices, but the move is not unusual, according to CNN supreme court analyst Steve Vladeck :\par \par \uc2 enltrTo be clear, Justice Thomas issued an \u8220\'20\'1Cadministrative stay,\u8221\'20\'1D which blocks the Eleventh Circuit ruling only temporarily while the full Court decides whether to block it pending appeal.\par \par \uc2 Such a ruling is *not* predictive of how the full Court (or even Thomas) will vote on the stay. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/CSrBaDg9JP"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/CSrBaDg9JP}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Steve Vladeck (@steve_vladeck) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/steve_vladeck/status/1584581011622350853?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 24, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrIndeed, there are lots of recent examples of the Circuit Justice issuing such a temporary ruling and then the full Court *declining* to make it permanent.\par \par \uc2 Folks will surely overreact anyway, but this isn\u8217\'20\'19t a big deal \u8212\'20\'14 yet.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Steve Vladeck (@steve_vladeck) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/steve_vladeck/status/1584581278112051200?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 24, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/21/lindsey-graham-atlanta-grand-jury-2020-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Appeals court pauses order for Graham to testify before Atlanta grand jury}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 two best hopes for stemming their losses in the Senate or even expanding their majority are in Pennsylvania and Wisconsin, and CNN has just released a poll indicating tight races in both.\par \par \uc2 The states are home to the perhaps two best pick up opportunities for Democrats this year, with Republican senator Ron Johnson defending his seat in Wisconsin, while Pennsylvania\u8217\'20\'19s is vacant after GOP senator \uc2 Pat Toomey\uc2  opted to retire.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/10/24/politics/cnn-poll-senate-races-wisconsin-pennsylvania/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN\u8217\'20\'19s new poll}}}\uc2  indicates Johnson has a slight edge over Democrat Mandela Barnes in Wisconsin, where 50% of voters back his candidacy against 49% for his challenger.\par \par \uc2 In Pennsylvania, Democratic lieutenant governor \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2  is at 51% support against Republican Mehmet Oz, who was polling at 45%.\par \par \uc2 The poll otherwise confirmed dynamics that have become well-known this election cycle. The economy is far and away voters\u8217\'20\'19 top issue, with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  a distant second. President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is also unpopular with voters in both states, the survey finds.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 Districts whose congressional representatives have embraced conspiracy theories about the 2020 election tend to be poorer, less educated and have experienced declines in their white population, according to an analysis {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/10/23/us/politics/republican-election-objectors-demographics.html?smid=nytcore-ios-share&referringSource=articleShare"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 published by The New York Times}}}\uc2  today.\par \par \uc2 The report suggests that racial anxiety is a major factor in voters\u8217\'20\'19 willingness to embrace \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s baseless claims of fraud in \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s election win, in addition to economic stagnation and social maladies like the opioid epidemic. The report is a sprawling look at corners of the country that have grown so alienated they\u8217\'20\'19re willing to support lawmakers who object to the certification of the 2020 election, despite fears the campaign poses a mortal threat to American democracy.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from the Times:\par \par \uc2 When Representative Troy Nehls of Texas voted last year to reject \uc2 Donald J. Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s electoral defeat, many of his constituents back home in Fort Bend County were thrilled.\par \par \uc2 Like the former president, they have been unhappy with the changes unfolding around them. Crime and sprawl from Houston, the big city next door, have been spilling over into their once bucolic towns. (\u8220\'20\'1CBuild a wall,\u8221\'20\'1D Mr. Nehls likes to say, and make Houston pay.) The county in recent years has become one of the nation\u8217\'20\'19s most diverse, where the former white majority has fallen to just 30 percent of the population.\par \par \uc2 Don Demel, a 61-year-old salesman who turned out last month to pick up a signed copy of a book by Mr. Nehls about the supposedly stolen election, said his parents had raised him \u8220\'20\'1Ccolorblind.\u8221\'20\'1D But the reason for the discontent was clear: Other white people in Fort Bend \u8220\'20\'1Cdid not like certain people coming here,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s race. They are old-school.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A shrinking white share of the population is a hallmark of the congressional districts held by the House Republicans who voted to challenge Mr. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s defeat, a \uc2 New York Times\uc2  analysis found \u8212\'20\'14 a pattern {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.gmu.edu/profiles/ajardina"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 political scientists}}}\uc2  say shows how {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cambridge.org/core/journals/american-political-science-review/article/abs/activating-animus-the-uniquely-social-roots-of-trump-support/D96C71C353D065F62A3F19B504FA7577"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 white fear}}}\uc2  of losing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pnas.org/doi/10.1073/pnas.1718155115"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 status}}}\uc2  shaped the movement to keep him in power.\par \par \uc2 The portion of white residents dropped about 35 percent more over the last three decades in those districts than in territory represented by other Republicans, the analysis found, and constituents also lagged behind in income and education. Rates of so-called {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/17/books/review/deaths-of-despair-and-the-future-of-capitalism-anne-case-angus-deaton.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 deaths of despair}}}\uc2 , such as suicide, drug overdose and alcohol-related liver failure, were notably higher as well.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 The January 6 committee is likely finished with its public hearings into the deadly attack on the Capitol, and \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/tom-ambrose"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tom Ambrose}}}\uc2  surveyed readers about whether the committee\u8217\'20\'19s work changed their mind about what happened that day, and Trump\u8217\'20\'19s role in it. Here\u8217\'20\'19s what one had to say:\par \par \uc2 I think that hearings solidified what most people thought already: that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  and his allies coordinated to assault the foundations of democracy on January 6 because they were unhappy with the result of the 2020 election. The juxtaposing of previously aired and unaired video clips helped provide clearer and fuller picture of the chaos that unfolded that day.\par \par \uc2 I believe that anyone who tuned into the hearings with an open mind saw January 6 for what it was: a disgraceful attack on American democracy that amounts to treason. I believe the committee was convincing in their effort to show premeditation by the president and his followers.\par \par \uc2 I am worried that those who believe January 6 was justified will use this committee as an example as of how \u8220\'20\'1Cthe Democrats/liberals\u8221\'20\'1D are out to get the president and his followers. They demonstrate this belief daily as they continue to call for violence against elected officials and refuse to believe the truth that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  won the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 It feels like that their position is: either we won, or we were cheated. I fear that the upcoming elections in November will only be a taste of what kinds of vitriol await during the 2024 election. Patrick, 29, public school teacher from Chicago\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/24/guardian-readers-capitol-attack-hearings"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Trump should be held accountable\u8217\'20\'19: Guardian readers on the Capitol attack hearings}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republican senator Ted Cruz was a vociferous objector to the 2020 election, but ended up hiding in a supply closet when insurrectionists stormed the Capitol on January 6, as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/ramon-antonio-vargas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ramon Antonio Vargas}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 As a mob of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  supporters stormed the US Capitol during the January 6 attack in a desperate attempt to keep him in the Oval Office, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ted-cruz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ted Cruz}}}\uc2  hid in a closet next to a stack of chairs, but he never thought twice about continuing to sow doubt about the former president\u8217\'20\'19s electoral defeat, the Republican senator from Texas has revealed.\par \par \uc2 Cruz revealed his whereabouts on the day of the deadly Capitol attack \u8211\'20\'13 which unsuccessfully aimed to disrupt the certification of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s victory over Trump in the 2020 presidential election \u8211\'20\'13 in a new book. The news was first reported by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newsweek.com/ted-cruz-hid-supply-closet-during-jan-6-new-book-reveals-1754076"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Newsweek}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The book \u8211\'20\'13 titled Justice Corrupted \u8211\'20\'13 recounts how Cruz was listening to his colleague \uc2 James Lankford\uc2  of Oklahoma speak in the Senate chamber when a terrible commotion erupted outside. \uc2 Capitol police\uc2  rushed in to escort Trump\u8217\'20\'19s vice-president, \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , whom the mob wanted to hang, off the dais, and the session was paused.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn the fog of the confusion, it was difficult to tell exactly what was happening,\u8221\'20\'1D Cruz wrote. \u8220\'20\'1CWe were informed that a riot had broken out and that rioters were attempting to breach the building.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/24/ted-cruz-supply-closet-january-6-riot-book"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ted Cruz took refuge in supply closet during January 6 riot, book reveals}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 What would Republicans do with a majority in the House? Demand concessions in exchange for raising the debt limit, which will likely be necessary at some point next year, Politico reports.\par \par \uc2 GOP lawmakers could demand that the tax cuts passed during the Trump administration are made permanent, or that Social Security and Medicare, the two massive federal benefit programs for older Americans that have long been in Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 crosshairs, are overhauled. But the strategy is a risky one, because without an agreement to lift its legal ability to borrow, Washington could default on its debt \u8211\'20\'13 with potentially calamitous implications for the global economy. And even if Republicans took both the House and the Senate, expect tortuous negotiations with Biden to find an agreement.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/10/24/house-gop-2023-forecast-00062919"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 from Politico}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Tight Senate margins and a Democratic president would make it impossible for GOP leaders to deliver on the party\u8217\'20\'19s most hardline fiscal wishes, at least with President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  still in office. The disappointment would surely prompt blowback from right-leaning Republicans already known as the sharpest thorns in the party\u8217\'20\'19s side.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSpare me if you\u8217\'20\'19re a Republican who puts on your frigging campaign website, \u8216\'20\'18Trust me, I will vote for a balanced budget amendment, and I believe we should balance the budget like every family in America.\u8217\'20\'19 No shit,\u8221\'20\'1D Rep. Chip Roy (R-Texas), a member of the pro-Trump Freedom Caucus, said in an interview.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou have two simple leverage points: when government funding comes up and when the debt ceiling is debated,\u8221\'20\'1D Roy reminded his fellow Republicans. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd the only question that matters is, will leadership use that leverage?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 There was also new polling today for Ohio, which seems to align with broader national trends for the 8 November midterms.\par \par \uc2 Once considered a swing state, Ohio has become more solidly Republican in recent elections. But that doesn\u8217\'20\'19t mean JD Vance, the GOP candidate for Senate, is running away with the race. Today\u8217\'20\'19s Spectrum News / Siena poll shows him tied with Democrat \uc2 Tim Ryan\uc2 , underscoring that for all the momentum Republicans seem to have, retaking the Senate is not a sure bet.\par \par \uc2 enltrSpectrum News / Siena Poll: Ohio Likely Voters\par \par \uc2 DeWine Continues to Hold Very Large Lead over Whaley, 58-34%\par \par \uc2 Vance vs. Ryan Even, 46-46%, Two Weeks to Go\par \par \uc2 Voters Prefer Republicans over Democrats to Control Congress, 40-33% {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/nenKiR8q6o"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/nenKiR8q6o}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/K1MaXlksmQ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/K1MaXlksmQ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 SienaResearch (@SienaResearch) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SienaResearch/status/1584500188567441413?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 24, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 However, notice the strong bias among Ohio voters towards Republicans on the generic congressional ballot. That matches recent nationwide polling suggesting the GOP has overtaken Democrats as the party preferred to control Congress \u8211\'20\'13 an outcome that may well come to pass when the midterm dust settles.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 There was some dire news for Democrats this morning from The Cook Political Report, which is known for its comprehensive rankings of congressional races across the country.\par \par \uc2 The subject was congressman \uc2 Sean Patrick Maloney\uc2 , who is chair of the Democratic Congressional Campaign Committee tasked with winning elections in the House of Representatives. Cook changed their rating for his suburban New York City district to toss-up from lean Democrat:\par \par \uc2 enltrHouse rating change: Rep. \uc2 Sean Patrick Maloney\uc2  (D) moves from Lean D to Toss Up at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CookPolitical?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @CookPolitical}}}\uc2  as Dems admit the DCCC chair is now in serious danger in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/NY17?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #NY17}}}\uc2 . Full analysis: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/89bvezbNuw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/89bvezbNuw}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ncljBkSfZw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ncljBkSfZw}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Dave Wasserman (@Redistrict) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Redistrict/status/1584523113215102980?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 24, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Polls indicate that Democrats are likely to lose their majority in the House in the 8 November midterms, and a loss by Maloney would make an embarrassment of their efforts to stem what appears to be a rising tide of Republican sentiment among voters.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re 15 days away from the 8 November midterms, but early voting data from across the country indicates a surge in voter enthusiasm, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/adam-gabbatt"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Adam Gabbatt}}}\uc2  reports \u8211\'20\'13 though it\u8217\'20\'19s not yet clear which party is set to benefit:\par \par \uc2 Early voting in the midterm elections is on track to match records set in 2018, according to researchers, as voters take advantage of both in-person and mail-in voting in states across the country.\par \par \uc2 More than 5.8 million people had already cast their vote by Friday evening, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/10/21/politics/pre-election-voting-six-million/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN reported}}}\uc2 , a similar total to this stage in the 2018 elections, which had the highest turnout of any midterm vote in a generation.\par \par \uc2 States with closely watched elections, including Georgia, Florida and Ohio, are among those seeing high volumes, with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats}}}\uc2  so far casting early votes in greater numbers.\par \par \uc2 Republicans, including \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , have encouraged their supporters {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/2022-midterm-elections-health-government-and-politics-election-2020-55f4744b484919cd20d4d5e8d72e444e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to vote in person}}}\uc2 , citing a mishmash of debunked conspiracy theories about election security.\par \par \uc2 The New York Times{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/10/22/us/politics/midterm-early-voting.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  that in-person turnout is up 70% in Georgia, where the incumbent Republican governor is facing a tough challenge {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ballotpedia.org/Georgia_gubernatorial_election,_2022"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 from Democrat Stacey Abrams}}}\uc2  and \uc2 Raphael Warnock\uc2 , the Democratic US senator, is competing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.businessinsider.com/raphael-warnock-herschel-walker-georgia-senate-election-2022"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 with Herschel Walker}}}\uc2 . As of Friday about 520,000 people had already cast their ballots during in-person early voting, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fox5atlanta.com/news/georgia-sees-record-early-voting-turn-out-ahead-of-midterm-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to}}}\uc2  Fox5 Atlanta.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/23/us-midterm-elections-early-voting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US midterm elections: early voting on track to match 2018 record}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 Justice department to hold press conference on 'significant national security matter'\par \par \uc2 Attorney general \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  will this afternoon hold a press conference on a \u8220\'20\'1Csignificant national security matter,\u8221\'20\'1D the justice department has announced.\par \par \uc2 The 1:30pm eastern time speech will \u8220\'20\'1Cdiscuss significant national security cases addressing malign influence schemes and alleged criminal activity by a nation-state actor in the United States,\u8221\'20\'1D and feature Garland along with \uc2 FBI\uc2  director \uc2 Christopher Wray\uc2 , along with other top justice department officials.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  will cover the press conference on this blog as it happens.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 From Las Vegas, \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/edwin-rios"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Edwin Rios}}}\uc2  reports on the cost-of-living concerns that are influencing voters in the swing state crucial to the upcoming midterm elections:\par \par \uc2 Claudia Lopez, 39, is worried for her children.\par \par \uc2 As her curly haired seven-year-old daughter bounced around a play area inside El Mercado, a shopping center within the Boulevard Mall in Las Vegas where the smell of arepas and tacos hovers over the shops, Lopez soaked in her day off from knocking on doors and talking to residents about the upcoming election.\par \par \uc2 For much of her life, Lopez, whose parents emigrated from Mexico to California, where she was born, didn\u8217\'20\'19t care for politics. This year, that changed: since Lopez moved to Las Vegas seven years ago, rents have rocketed. In the first quarter of 2022, the Nevada State Apartment Association {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://lasvegassun.com/news/2022/apr/20/las-vegas-tenants-facing-sticker-shock-as-rents-sk/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 found}}}\uc2  that rent had soared, on average, more than 20% compared to the same period last year. That growth has since {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reviewjournal.com/business/housing/las-vegas-once-soaring-rents-now-growing-much-slower-2647409/#:~:text=The%20typical%20rent%20in%20the,hike%20in%20August%20of%202021."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 slowed}}}\uc2 , but the self-employed house cleaner worries about her children\u8217\'20\'19s future: their safety, their schools, their shelter.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t care about Democrats or {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans}}}\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Lopez says. \u8220\'20\'1CI care about change. I just want change for the better. Everything\u8217\'20\'19s getting worse. You see little kids like, \u8216\'20\'18Are they going to live to my age?\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/nevada"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nevada}}}\uc2 , the political stakes of this election are high. Latino voters are projected to account for one for every five potential voters in November, turning the state into a microcosm of the national influence voters of color will have on the election. While Nevada voted Democrat in the last election, its contests were won by slim margins. And as a voting bloc, Latinos are not monolithic: what they care about ranges from immigration to the economy and depends on where throughout the country they live.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/22/nevada-latinos-cost-of-living-midterm-elections"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18I just care about change\u8217\'20\'19: Nevada\u8217\'20\'19s Latinos on their cost-of-living fears}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump isn\u8217\'20\'19t alone in presenting a danger to democracy. As {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/adam-gabbatt"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Adam Gabbatt}}}\uc2  reports, \uc2 Doug Mastriano\uc2  is copying many of the former president\u8217\'20\'19s tactics in his campaign for governor of Pennsylvania, from his perpetual lying to his belief in conspiracy theories about the 2020 election:\par \par \uc2 As Pennsylvanians prepare to vote for their next governor, it is no exaggeration to say the future of American democracy is at stake.\par \par \uc2 Doug Mastriano\uc2 , a retired army colonel who has enthusiastically indulged \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s fantasy that the 2020 presidential election was stolen, is the Republican candidate. If he wins, he plans to deregister every single one of Pennsylvania\u8217\'20\'19s 8.7 million voters. In future elections, Mastriano would choose who certifies \u8211\'20\'13 or doesn\u8217\'20\'19t \u8211\'20\'13 the state\u8217\'20\'19s election results.\par \par \uc2 With Pennsylvania one of the few swing states in presidential elections, Mastriano could effectively have the power to decide the next president. But in a midterm election season defined by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans}}}\uc2  who seem to oppose democracy, there is some evidence that Mastriano, a retired army colonel, could be too fringe even for the Republican party.\par \par \uc2 Mastriano is, by most measures, an extremist.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/24/doug-mastriano-pennsylvania-republicans-trump-governor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Doug Mastriano: is the Trump-backed election denier too extreme to win?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 Bob Woodward\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/opinions/interactive/2022/trump-tapes-bob-woodward-interviews-audiobook/?itid=hp_opinions_p001_f007"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recorded excerpts}}}\uc2  of his conversations with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  take listeners back to 2020, and make clear just how much of the White House\u8217\'20\'19s fumbling response to Covid-19 came from the president himself.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI feel good. I think we\u8217\'20\'19re doing a great job. I think we\u8217\'20\'19ll never get credit from the fake news media no matter how good a job we do. No matter how good a job I do, I will never get credit from the media, and I\u8217\'20\'19ll never get credit from Democrats who want to beat me desperately in seven months,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump told Woodward in an early April interview, days after the economy had shut down to unsuccessfully stop the spread of a virus that would kill hundreds of thousands of Americans that year alone.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s denialism continued into July: \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s flaring up all over the world, Bob. By the way, all over the world. That was one thing I noticed last week. You know they talk about this country. All over the world, it\u8217\'20\'19s flaring up. But we have it under control.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Later that month, he insisted that he would soon release a plan to fight the virus, but appeared to tie its timing to how it would affect his election chances. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve got 106 days. That\u8217\'20\'19s a long time. You know, if I put out a plan now, people won\u8217\'20\'19t even remember it in a hundred \u8212\'20\'14 I won the last election in the last week.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 While Woodward agrees with many other observers of the former president that his attempts to overturn the 2020 election make him a danger to democracy, he also makes the case to listeners that Trump didn\u8217\'20\'19t even fully understand how to do his job \u8211\'20\'13 and the nation paid the price.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTrump reminds how easy it is to break things you do not understand \u8212\'20\'14 democracy and the presidency,\u8221\'20\'1D Woodward concludes.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 'Trump is an unparalleled danger' reporter warns after hours of interviews with ex-president\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  reporter Bob Woodward {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/opinions/interactive/2022/trump-tapes-bob-woodward-interviews-audiobook/?itid=hp_opinions_p001_f007"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has released}}}\uc2  more excerpts from his interviews with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in 2020, and closes with this warning: \u8220\'20\'1CTrump is an unparalleled danger.\u8221\'20\'1D Describing him as \u8220\'20\'1Coverwhelmed by the job\u8221\'20\'1D while in office as Covid-19 spread across the United States, Woodward warns that Trump continues to pursue \u8220\'20\'1Ca seditious conspiracy\u8221\'20\'1D to overturn the 2020 election \u8211\'20\'13 and end democracy itself. While Woodward is far from the first person to say that, the journalist\u8217\'20\'19s opinion is uniquely informed, given that the two men spoke 20 times during the last year of his presidency.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a look at what\u8217\'20\'19s happening today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Florida\u8217\'20\'19s Republican governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  will face his Democratic challenger \uc2 Charlie Crist\uc2  for the only debate of the election at 7pm ET.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will hold a rally today at the headquarters of the \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  at 1pm.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Poll tracker FiveThirtyEight {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/2022-election-forecast/senate/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 downgraded Democrats\u8217\'20\'19}}}\uc2  chances of keeping control of the Senate over the weekend, lowering it to 55% amid a wave of polls that signal several of its candidates may be in trouble.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020221024eiao001s7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
