\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 What a pregnancy actually looks like before 10 weeks \u8211\'20\'13 in pictures\b0\par\par\uc2 Poppy Noor \par \uc2 975 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 October 2022\par 09:35 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 In 13 US states, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is banned even in the earliest stages of pregnancy. But we rarely see what such tissue really looks like\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is now banned or severely restricted in 14 states in the US, the outcome of a decades-long campaign by anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  advocates. In many states, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is no longer seen as a health procedure, but a morality issue. Pennsylvania\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Doug Mastriano\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 once a state senator, now running for governor \u8211\'20\'13 is one of a number of Republican politicians who has called for murder {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/27/republican-pennsylvania-doug-mastriano-abortion-murder"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 charges for people who defy \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  bans.}}}\par \par \uc2 In 13 of those 14 states, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is banned even in the earliest stages of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 These images, supplied to us by the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://myanetwork.org/the-issue-of-tissue/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 MYA Network}}}\uc2 , a network of clinicians and activists who came together earlier in the pandemic when some states tried to classify \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as \u8220\'20\'1Cnon-essential\u8221\'20\'1D medical care, show what tissue in the first nine weeks of pregnancy actually looks like.\par \par \uc2 Above is early pregnancy tissue, at four weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Dr Joan Fleischman, part of the MYA Network, uses a gentle handheld device that removes the tissue. This more delicate type of extraction keeps it intact.\par \par \uc2 Above is pregnancy tissue extracted at five weeks.\par \par \uc2 Sometimes, patients want to see the tissue after an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CThey are stunned by what it actually looks like,\u8221\'20\'1D says Fleischman. \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s when I realized how much the imagery on the internet and on placards \u8211\'20\'13 showing human-like qualities at this early stage of development \u8211\'20\'13 has really permeated the culture. People almost don\u8217\'20\'19t believe this is what comes out.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Above is tissue removed at six weeks, when misleadingly named \u8220\'20\'1Cfetal heartbeat\u8221\'20\'1D bills outlaw \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CClinicians date pregnancy from the first day of your last period, to help predict the due date. But you\u8217\'20\'19re not pregnant for those first two weeks , \u8221\'20\'1D says Fleischman. So someone with a six-week pregnancy may have very little time after a missed period to get \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care in states with a six-week limit.\par \par \uc2 Many images on the internet and in textbooks show development to be quite far along at this stage.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA lot of early pregnancy images are driven by people who are against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and feel that life begins at conception, or by prenatal enthusiasts who want women to be excited about their pregnancy. What about people who aren\u8217\'20\'19t?\u8221\'20\'1D she asks.\par \par \uc2 Above is pregnancy tissue at seven weeks. There is still no visible embryo. The gestational sac is not yet half an inch. \u8220\'20\'1CI have been in the training field, and medical students and clinicians who see it are also shocked. That is how pervasive this misinformation is,\u8221\'20\'1D Fleischman says.\par \par \uc2 Patients may come in for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  fearful at this stage, having read through forums or looked at images online. \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re expecting to see a little fetus with hands \u8211\'20\'13 a developed, miniature baby.\u8221\'20\'1D Often, she says, \u8220\'20\'1Cthey feel they\u8217\'20\'19ve been deceived.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 This image shows decidua (tissue to support the pregnancy) and the gestational sac (which would eventually become the amniotic sac, which supports the fetus). If we looked closer, under a microscope, would we see more human qualities?\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf you zoom in on anything, including sperm and an egg getting fertilized, it\u8217\'20\'19s just an incredible thing to watch. But that\u8217\'20\'19s very different from the everyday ways we see life. That perspective to me is the most relevant \u8211\'20\'13 but it is somehow absent from our consciousness,\u8221\'20\'1D says Fleischman.\par \par \uc2 Above is a gestational sac removed at eight weeks of pregnancy. While these images relate to early pregnancy, the network does not differentiate between a \u8220\'20\'1Cgood time\u8221\'20\'1D and a \u8220\'20\'1Cbad time\u8221\'20\'1D to have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , nor does it dismiss how emotionally fraught losing a pregnancy at any stage, including early pregnancy, can be. But they want people to know what is actually being removed in early pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is medical care. Every single person who makes this decision is complex. But this information, showing tissue in the first 10 weeks, is literally absent from our common understanding of what is going on, and people deserve accurate information.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 This image shows the gestational sac of a nine-week pregnancy. This is everything that would be removed during an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and includes the nascent embryo, which is not easily discernible to the naked eye. Showing this tissue can be a relief to patients. \u8220\'20\'1COften people don\u8217\'20\'19t speak to anyone about getting an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . They make a very quiet, private decision because they\u8217\'20\'19re afraid to see people\u8217\'20\'19s reactions. And then I do this simple procedure that\u8217\'20\'19s a few minutes longer than a Pap test. For those who choose to look at the tissue, you can literally feel the tension come down. People have been on this emotional roller coaster. And they\u8217\'20\'19re like, \u8216\'20\'18You\u8217\'20\'19re kidding. This is all that was?\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D says Fleischman.\par \par \uc2 Finally, above is a number of gestational sacs on one petri dish, showing the progression in growth from five weeks of pregnancy to nine weeks. The sac grows 1mm a day.\par \par \uc2 Talking about why we don\u8217\'20\'19t see these images more often, Dr Michele Gomez, who is part of the MYA Network, says: \u8220\'20\'1CI do think there are some clinicians who are concerned about patient\u8217\'20\'19s reactions. But it\u8217\'20\'19s not really our right or our responsibility to decide how people will respond to this. We\u8217\'20\'19re just putting out the information and the facts to counter the misinformation. To say: this is not something that\u8217\'20\'19s scary, or dangerous, or violent. It\u8217\'20\'19s just a picture of something that\u8217\'20\'19s in your body.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 This article was amended on 19 October 2022 to include the detail that at nine weeks the nascent embryo is not easily discernible to the naked eye.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020221019eiaj000ia\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
