\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Biden vows to codify Roe if Democrats win midterms: \u8216\'20\'18You gotta vote\u8217\'20\'19\b0\par\par\uc2 Lauren Gambino \par \uc2 920 \uc2 words\par \uc2 21 October 2022\par 16:44 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 US president cast election as choice between Republicans who seek to impose nationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban and Democrats defending right to choose\par \par \uc2 With Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 congressional majorities at risk this November, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  vowed on Tuesday that the first bill he sent to Capitol Hill next year would codify Roe v Wade \u8211\'20\'13 if Americans return his party to power with wide enough margins to pass \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s a major lift for Democrats, who face a challenging political environment marked by a rocky economy and decades-high inflation. But the loss of abortions rights has sparked a political backlash, motivating Democratic voters and women more broadly who have registered to vote in significant numbers since the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision to overturn Roe in Dobbs v Jackson.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m asking the American people to remember how you felt that day the extreme Dobbs decision came down and Roe was overturned after 50 years,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said during remarks at an event hosted by the \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  at the Howard Theater in Washington. \u8220\'20\'1CThe anger, the worry, the disbelief.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf you care about the right to choose,\u8221\'20\'1D he added, \u8220\'20\'1Cthen you gotta vote\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Standing in front of a banner that read \u8220\'20\'1CRestore Roe\u8221\'20\'1D, the president cast the election as a choice between Republicans who would seek to impose a nationwide ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Democrats who have vowed to protect reproductive rights.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf Republicans get their way with a national ban it won\u8217\'20\'19t matter where you live in America,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said, vowing to veto such a bill if it reached his desk.\par \par \uc2 All or most abortions are banned {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2022/jun/28/tracking-where-abortion-laws-stand-in-every-state"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  in at least 14 US states}}}\uc2 , with several more engaged in legal battles to restrict access. The White House estimates that 26.5 million women of reproductive age live in states with bans or severe restrictions.\par \par \uc2 With weeks left before the midterm elections, the White House and Democrats have increasingly focused their campaign message on protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , an issue they hope will galvanize women and independent voters.\par \par \uc2 Clear majorities of Americans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/fact-tank/2022/06/13/about-six-in-ten-americans-say-abortion-should-be-legal-in-all-or-most-cases-2/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 believe}}}\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should remian legal and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/politics/2022/07/06/majority-of-public-disapproves-of-supreme-courts-decision-to-overturn-roe-v-wade/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dissapprove}}}\uc2  of the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision. Yet polling {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2022/10/17/upshot/times-siena-poll-likely-voters-crosstabs.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 consistently shows}}}\uc2  that voters\u8217\'20\'19 top priority this election is the economy and inflation, issues that play to Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 strengths. Biden\u8217\'20\'19s approval rating remains low, which is a drag on vulnerable Democratic candidates.\par \par \uc2 But Biden predicted that women would punish Republicans for enacting abortions bans and restrictions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Dobbs decision \u8230\'20\'26 practically dares women to go ahead, lead and be heard,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, pointing to Kansas, where voters in the conservative state decisively defeated a Republican-led effort to strip away \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. \u8220\'20\'1CCome this November we\u8217\'20\'19re going to see what happens all over America.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden said the only way to \u8220\'20\'1Cstop these extremist laws that are putting in jeopardy women\u8217\'20\'19s health\u8221\'20\'1D is for Congress to codify \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights at the federal level. But he conceded that presently \u8220\'20\'1Cwe\u8217\'20\'19re short a handful of votes\u8221\'20\'1D to do so and urged Americans to elect more Democrats next month.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf we do that, here\u8217\'20\'19s the promise I make to you and the American people: the first bill that I will send to the Congress will be to codify Roe v Wade,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd when Congress passes it, I\u8217\'20\'19ll sign it in January, 50 years after Roe was first decided the law of the land.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Even if Democrats were able to overcome historical and political headwinds to keep both majorities in Congress, it may not be enough to enshrine the 1973 supreme court ruling into law. The Senate would need to abolish the filibuster, or create an exception to the rule requiring 60 votes to advance most legislation in the chamber. Two moderate Democrats have already voiced their opposition to amending the filibuster.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this summer, Biden, an institutionalist long resistant to changing parliamentary procedures, announced his support for ending the filibuster to guarantee a women\u8217\'20\'19s right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  under pressure from Democrats demanding a stronger response from their party\u8217\'20\'19s leader. The administration has also taken additional steps to protect access to the procedure.\par \par \uc2 Biden stressed that the new legal landscape was already causing chaos and harm for patients and providers. Victims of rape and incest were being forced to travel out-of-state to receive an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , he said, while doctors fear the repercussions of intervening in instances with life-threatening pregnancies.\par \par \uc2 Patients having miscarriages have reported delayed or denied care as a result of the new laws and other patients say they have been denied medication for certain conditions because the drugs could also be used to terminate a pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 He also said that the Dobbs decision \u8220\'20\'1Crisks the border right to privacy for everyone,\u8221\'20\'1D threatening same-sex marriage other fundamental rights.\par \par \uc2 He also appealed directly to young people who tend to vote at lower rates than their older counterparts. Praising their turnout in 2020, he reminded them of his decisions to forgive billions of dollars in student-loan debt and to issue pardons for thousands of people convicted of marijuana possession \u8211\'20\'13actions that were popular among young people.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYour generation will not be ignored, will not be shunned and will not be silent,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said, adding: \u8220\'20\'1CIn 2020 you voted to deliver the change you wanted to see in the world. In 2022 you need to exercise your power to vote again for the future of our nation and the future of your generation.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020221019eiaj000h7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
