\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Biden pledges to codify  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights if Democrats win midterms: \u8216\'20\'18I\u8217\'20\'19ll sign it in January\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Gloria Oladipo in New York \par \uc2 3,245 \uc2 words\par \uc2 18 October 2022\par 20:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 President says his first move will be to codify Roe v WadeSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 Summary\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s it for the US live politics blog today!\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a summary of what we covered today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden promised to codify Roe v wade in his first post-midterms legislation if Democrats keep control of Congress, saying \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ll sign it in January\u8221\'20\'1D during a speech at a DNC event in Washington DC.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden also promised to veto any federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban that comes across his desk, as Republicans push for a federal ban following the overturn of Roe v wade in June.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden pledged to ban assault weapons during the DNC speech. Biden said, \u8220\'20\'1CI did it once, I\u8217\'20\'19ll do it again\u8221\'20\'1D, in reference to a ban he helped negotiate as a senator.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Candidates across key races in Utah, Georgia, and Ohio had heated debates yesterday, with November midterms less than a month away.\par \par \uc2 Thank you for reading; see you tomorrow!\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 Could \uc2 Kathy Hochul\uc2  be in trouble in New York\par \par \uc2 New York is not a state that too many Democrats have been worried about in recent years. But a couple of recent polls have shown governor \uc2 Kathy Hochul\uc2  with only a relatively narrow lead over her Republican opponent.\par \par \uc2 Politico has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/10/18/poll-hochul-leads-zeldin-4-points-00062302"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the details}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Two polls Tuesday showed the race for New York governor getting closer than perhaps many had initially expected in the deep-blue state.\par \par \uc2 A Siena College Research Institute poll early Tuesday found Democratic Gov. \uc2 Kathy Hochul\uc2  held an 11-percentage-point edge over Republican Rep. \uc2 Lee Zeldin\uc2  in a state where Democrats have won every statewide race over the past two decades. That was down from a 17-point lead a month ago.\par \par \uc2 Then an even closer poll came out in the afternoon: A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://poll.qu.edu/poll-release?releaseid=3859"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Quinnipiac University survey found}}}\uc2  Hochul with a razor-thin 50 percent to 46 percent lead over Zeldin \u8212\'20\'14 putting Zeldin within striking distance of a potentially major upset.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn the blue state of New York, the race for governor is competitive,\u8221\'20\'1D Quinnipiac polling analyst Mary Snow said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  journalist Bob Woodward announced today that he will be releasing a new audiobook entitled \u8220\'20\'1CThe Trump Tapes,\u8221\'20\'1D which features eight hours of raw interviews with former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more background on the book {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://edition.cnn.com/2022/10/18/politics/bob-woodward-trump-tapes-audiobook-recorded-interviews/index.html?bt_ee=pZt9dxRby0j4GT4QCCbmElJnkplHPS310Ca4PFVr0YPkQxGACbTzZ4LXimq%2Bvzmx&bt_ts=1666103659526"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 from CNN}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 The interviews offer unvarnished insights into the former president\u8217\'20\'19s worldview and are the most extensive recordings of Trump speaking about his presidency \u8212\'20\'14 including explaining his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/interactive/2018/06/politics/trump-kim-summit-cnnphotos/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rationale for meeting Kim}}}\uc2 , his relationship with Russian President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 , and Trump\u8217\'20\'19s detailed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2020/09/10/politics/trump-disclosures-anxiety/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 views of the US nuclear arsenal}}}\uc2 . The audio also shows how Trump decided to share with Woodward the letters Kim wrote to him \u8211\'20\'13 the letters that helped spark the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/09/21/politics/appeals-court-mar-a-lago-criminal-classified-documents"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOJ investigation into classified documents}}}\uc2  Trump took to Mar-a-Lago\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 Woodward said in the book\u8217\'20\'19s introduction that he is releasing the recordings in part because \u8220\'20\'1Chearing Trump speak is a completely different experience to reading the transcripts or listening to snatches of interviews on television or the internet.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He describes Trump as \u8220\'20\'1Craw, profane, divisive and deceptive. His language is often retaliatory.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYet, you will also hear him engaging and entertaining, laughing, ever the host. He is trying to win me over, sell his presidency to me. The full-time salesman,\u8221\'20\'1D Woodward said. \u8220\'20\'1CI wanted to put as much of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s voice, his own words, out there for the historical record and so people could hear and judge and make their own assessments.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 Jean-Pierre also mentioned student loan forgiveness applications that opened on Monday, as lawsuits are still being waged against Biden\u8217\'20\'19s proposal.\par \par \uc2 enltrJean-Pierre on student debt relief: The president wanted to keep a campaign promise. We\u8217\'20\'19re talking about 40 million borrowers who are going to benefit from this policy.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 David Smith (@SmithInAmerica) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SmithInAmerica/status/1582444490748751872?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 18, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 Jean-Pierre has been asked several questions about the economy, specifically about gas prices and inflation.\par \par \uc2 One question centered on the strength of the economy, as \uc2 Bloomberg\uc2  economists {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&rct=j&q=&esrc=s&source=web&cd=&cad=rja&uact=8&ved=2ahUKEwiohprhter6AhXnlYkEHdUkC64QvOMEKAB6BAgKEAE&url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bloomberg.com%2Fnews%2Farticles%2F2022-10-17%2Fforecast-for-us-recession-within-year-hits-100-in-blow-to-biden&usg=AOvVaw3SdJ6TRSOSkLTsacVdZKns"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 predict a \u8220\'20\'1C100% chance\u8221\'20\'1D of a recession}}}\uc2 , but Jean-Pierre contended that the economy is resilient given economic policies put forth by Biden.\par \par \uc2 enltrJean-Pierre: \u8220\'20\'1CLet\u8217\'20\'19s not forget what the president has done the past 19 months. He has made the economy his top priority.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 David Smith (@SmithInAmerica) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SmithInAmerica/status/1582439457633947649?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 18, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 On oil, Jean-Pierre said that the oil production under Biden has increased, a seeming conflict given Biden\u8217\'20\'19s past comments about transitioning towards cleaner energy options.\par \par \uc2 enltrJean-Pierre: \u8220\'20\'1CThere is no shortage of opportunity or incentive for oil companies to ramp up production\u8230\'20\'26 The United States has produced more oil in President Biden\u8217\'20\'19s first year than under President Trump\u8217\'20\'19s first year.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 David Smith (@SmithInAmerica) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SmithInAmerica/status/1582440291037958144?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 18, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 A reporter asked a question about Brittney Griner, who turned 32 years old today.\par \par \uc2 Jean-Pierre has said that it is a priority of Biden to get Griner home, as well as Paul Whelan, a former US marine who has been incarcerated in Russia since 2018.\par \par \uc2 enltrJean-Pierre on Brittney Griner: \u8220\'20\'1CGetting Brittney home, getting Paul Whelan home is a priority for this administration\u8230\'20\'26 We\u8217\'20\'19re going to continue working through our channels that we have with Russia.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 David Smith (@SmithInAmerica) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SmithInAmerica/status/1582438923036688384?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 18, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Jean-Pierre would not provide information on Griner\u8217\'20\'19s condition, what access to the \uc2 WNBA\uc2  star looks like, or other questions.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 Jean-Pierre was just asked what Biden\u8217\'20\'19s plan is if Democrats do not keep control in the midterm elections come November.\par \par \uc2 Jean-Pierre responded with: \u8220\'20\'1CThe way that we make Roe into law is to make sure we have legislation and we codify it. That is the best way to protect women\u8217\'20\'19s rights.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrJean-Pierre: \u8220\'20\'1CThe way that we make Roe into law is to make sure we have legislation and we codify it. That is the best way to protect women\u8217\'20\'19s rights.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 David Smith (@SmithInAmerica) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SmithInAmerica/status/1582436746268053505?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 18, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Jean-Pierre added that the president believes that it\u8217\'20\'19s important for people to \u8220\'20\'1Cmake their voices heard\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrJean-Pierre: \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s always said that what people need to do is make their voices heard.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 David Smith (@SmithInAmerica) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SmithInAmerica/status/1582436899284996096?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 18, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Jean-Pierre also refused to give a specific number of how many more votes would be enough for Biden to codify Roe.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 Press briefing is now underway.\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  opened up the conference about the overturning of Roe v wade.\par \par \uc2 Jean-Pierre confirmed again that Biden plans on making Roe v wade the \u8220\'20\'1Claw of the land\u8221\'20\'1D around the 50th anniversary of the Roe v wade\u8217\'20\'19s decision next year.\par \par \uc2 enltrAt White House briefing. Press Secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2 : \u8220\'20\'1CPresident Biden is continuing to fight to restore reproductive rights for millions of American women\u8230\'20\'26 President Biden believes that Roe was rightly decided nearly 50 years ago.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/fRXJeH6XnU"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/fRXJeH6XnU}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 David Smith (@SmithInAmerica) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SmithInAmerica/status/1582433881227423746?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 18, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 The White house press briefing should be happening shortly, scheduled for 1:45 pm eastern time.\par \par \uc2 Stay tuned!\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden will be speaking on gas prices tomorrow, said White house chief of staff on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In a response to comments from Hill reporter Hanna Trudo about Biden\u8217\'20\'19s speech on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \uc2 Ronald Klain\uc2  responded that Biden will be speaking about gas prices tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 enltrAbortion as a closing pitch was always going to be a really risky proposition. But up against the economy? It makes it look almost fringe. Of course many people will disagree with this, but the cost of gas is *extremely* important to nearly everyone, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is simply not\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Hanna Trudo (@HCTrudo) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/HCTrudo/status/1582419412925050900?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 18, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrNot an either / or. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @POTUS}}}\uc2  spoke about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  today, will speak about gas prices tomorrow. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/pPg6TLGdUX"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/pPg6TLGdUX}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Ronald Klain\uc2  (@WHCOS) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/WHCOS/status/1582421092760580098?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 18, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden also pledged to veto any federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, warning that Republicans have made efforts to push such legislation.\par \par \uc2 enltrBiden claims Minority Leader Kevin McCarthy would push a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban if the GOP wins the House:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf Republicans get their way with a national ban, it won\u8217\'20\'19t matter where you live \u8230\'20\'26 If such a bill were to pass in the next several years, *whispers* I'll veto it." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/n3dd1FXsNz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/n3dd1FXsNz}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1582416458809753609?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 18, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden also touched on gun control, promising that if Democrats kept control of Congress in January, he would sign a ban on assault weapons.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd by the way if you give me a Democratic congress we\u8217\'20\'19re going to ban assault weapons again\u8221\'20\'1D, said Biden.\par \par \uc2 Biden added: \u8220\'20\'1CI did it once, I\u8217\'20\'19ll do it again\u8221\'20\'1D, referring to a 10-year ban {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2022/06/04/biden-assault-weapons-ban/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he negotiated as a senator in 1994}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 'I'll sign it in January': Biden pledges to codify Roe v Wade if Democrats win midterms\par \par \uc2 There it is. Biden has officially announced that if Democrats gain control of Congress, his first move will be to send a bill codifying Roe v Wade and sign such legislation ahead of the 50th anniversary of the 1973 decision.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI believe Congress should codify Roe, once and for all,\u8221\'20\'1D said Biden as the crowd cheered.\par \par \uc2 Biden added: \u8220\'20\'1CThe first bill that I will send to the Congress will be to codify Roe v Wade \u8230\'20\'26 and if Congress passes it, I\u8217\'20\'19ll sign it in January.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTogether, we\u8217\'20\'19ll restore the right to choose to every woman, in every state in America,\u8221\'20\'1D said Biden, emphasizing that the crowd needed to vote to ensure such protections.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden is currently speaking at a DNC event at Howard Theatre.\par \par \uc2 So far, Biden has mentioned that 16 states have passed bans on abortions since the overturning of Roe v Wade in June.\par \par \uc2 enltr. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @POTUS}}}\uc2  says 16 states have enacted \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans since Dobbs. \u8220\'20\'1CThere is so much confusion and uncertainty\u8221\'20\'1D for doctors and nurses who just want to do their jobs {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/QuCL1Gkmwo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/QuCL1Gkmwo}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Mike Memoli (@mikememoli) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mikememoli/status/1582413270442733568?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 18, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Biden also warned about the decision having consequences on other issues, calling out justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 opinion that same-sex marriage, contraception, and other issues should be re-examined.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 The DNC event has started, with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights remaining in the spotlight.\par \par \uc2 From journalist Kellie Meyer:\par \par \uc2 enltrBiden's backdrop at the DC event today. Keeping \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the spotlight ahead of the midterms.\par \par \uc2 The issue energized the base, esp. women voters, after \uc2 SCOTUS\uc2  overturned Roe v. Wade in June. New polling showing that energy faded in the fall.\par \par \uc2 We discuss tonight on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NewsNation?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @NewsNation}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/VsdAtF7fKr"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/VsdAtF7fKr}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kellie Meyer (@KellieMeyerNews) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KellieMeyerNews/status/1582411867829305354?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 18, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re currently waiting on Biden to begin his speech about midterm elections at the Howard Theatre in Washington DC, scheduled for 12:15 pm eastern time.\par \par \uc2 Stay tuned!\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden promises to codify Roe v Wade as first piece of post-midterm legislation\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will announce today that the first bill he will send to Capitol Hill will be one that codifies federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections, if Democrats can secure enough seats in Congress, reported Reuters.\par \par \uc2 This announcement is the first time Biden has prioritized \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, with the November midterm elections less than a month away.\par \par \uc2 Republicans are projected to win during the November election, likely taking control of at least the House. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has remained a salient issue, one that could help Democrats win more support.\par \par \uc2 Biden will expand more on the promise today during planned remarks at a Democratic National Convention (DNC) event.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 In case you missed it: former president \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  chimed in on Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 messaging ahead of midterms. More from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s Sam Levine:\par \par \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  acknowledged Democrats can be \u8220\'20\'1Ca buzzkill\u8221\'20\'1D with their abstract campaign messaging and could better connect with voters by emphasizing what constituents feel in their day to day lives.\par \par \uc2 During an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://crooked.com/podcast/obamas-advice-for-democrats/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 interview on Pod Save America,}}}\uc2  released Friday, Obama acknowledged that he \u8220\'20\'1Cused to get into trouble\u8221\'20\'1D when he appeared too professorial, including by standing behind a lectern and talking about policy in theoretical ways that didn\u8217\'20\'19t directly connect with voters.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s not how people think about these issues,\u8221\'20\'1D Obama said, less than a month before his party tries to hang on to control of both congressional chambers during the 8 November midterms. \u8220\'20\'1CThey think about them in terms of, you know, the life I\u8217\'20\'19m leading day to day. How does politics \u8230\'20\'26 how is it even relevant to the things that I care most deeply about?\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy family, my kids, work that gives me satisfaction, having fun, not being a buzzkill, right?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Read the full article {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/18/barack-obama-democrats-buzzkill-midterms"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/18/barack-obama-democrats-buzzkill-midterms"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Obama admits Democrats can be a \u8216\'20\'18buzzkill\u8217\'20\'19 and urges better messaging}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 Challenging Scalise is Democrat Katie Darling, a business executive.\par \par \uc2 Darling has centered her campaign around climate change concerns, the state\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, and Louisiana\u8217\'20\'19s underperforming schools, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2022/10/03/louisiana-female-candidate-birth/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports the Washington Post}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a now-viral campaign video from Darling, which depicts a fictionalized scenario of her giving birth.\par \par \uc2 enltrLouisiana ranks 50th in crime, 48th in education, and 46th in health care. I\u8217\'20\'19m running for Congress to stop this race to the bottom because our children deserve better. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/OfFQHuPTzU"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/OfFQHuPTzU}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Katie Darling for Louisiana (@katie4louisiana) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/katie4louisiana/status/1576980407849046017?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 3, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Read the full article on the video {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2022/10/03/louisiana-female-candidate-birth/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Louisiana representative Steve Scalise is under fire for new video footage from January 6, showing the second ranking Republican standing next to House speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  as she called for military assistance.\par \par \uc2 From {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nola.com/news/politics/article_c841637e-4e59-11ed-9299-abaa8be3d4ab.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  the New Orleans Advocate}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Last Thursday, a House investigatory panel released a video showing that on the day of the riot, Scalise was standing an arm\u8217\'20\'19s length away from Pelosi listening to her demand for the National Guard. Critics have denounced Scalise for attacking Pelosi for not calling for help even though he can be seen on the videotape near her while she did.\par \par \uc2 Scalise had questioned if Democratic leadership failed to quickly get help during the Capitol riots, when Trump supporters stormed the Capitol building.\par \par \uc2 Scalise chanted \u8220\'20\'1Chear, hear\u8221\'20\'1D during a June news conference when Republican members asked about Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 actions, reported the Advocate.\par \par \uc2 Read the full article {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nola.com/news/politics/article_c841637e-4e59-11ed-9299-abaa8be3d4ab.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 As for Lee, Utah senator \uc2 Mitt Romney\uc2  still hasn\u8217\'20\'19t endorsed him, highlighting a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/elections/2022/10/14/utah-senate-mcmullin-lee-romney/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 potent divide in the Utah GOP}}}\uc2  between Trump loyalists and his critics.\par \par \uc2 enltrMitt Romney still hasn't endorsed his fellow Republican senator from Utah, \uc2 Mike Lee\uc2 , in his re-election bid.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Griffin (@kylegriffin1) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kylegriffin1/status/1582340721146748930?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 18, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump was also a key discussion topic in Utah\u8217\'20\'19s senate debate.\par \par \uc2 Independent candidate Evan McMullin accused Republican \uc2 Mike Lee\uc2 , the senate incumbent, of being loyal to Trump.\par \par \uc2 Utah Republican Sen. \uc2 Mike Lee\uc2 , right, and his independent challenger Evan McMullin pose for photographs before their televised debate, Monday, Oct. 17, 2022, in Orem, Utah, three weeks before Election Day. Photograph: Rick Bowmer/AP\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not going to Washington, if we prevail, to be a bootlicker for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  or \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . And that\u8217\'20\'19s a commitment I\u8217\'20\'19ve made to putting Utah first\u8221\'20\'1D, said McMullin of Lee.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Lee argued that Democrats were McMullin\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cadopted party\u8221\'20\'1D, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/10/18/mondays-debates-attacks-midterms-ohio-utah-georgia-00062251"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported Politico}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Lee added: \u8220\'20\'1CParties are an important proxy. They\u8217\'20\'19re an important proxy for ideas. You\u8217\'20\'19re asking the people to put faith, blind trust in you\u8230\'20\'26That\u8217\'20\'19s not how we lead to a good policy outcome.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump and Pelosi were also a contention point in last night\u8217\'20\'19s Ohio debate.\par \par \uc2 Ryan pressed Vance on his association with Trump, calling Vance out for criticizing Trump at times but asking for the former president\u8217\'20\'19s support on other occasions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou have to have the courage to take on your leaders. These leaders in DC will eat you up like a chew toy,\u8221\'20\'1D said Ryan, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/10/17/politics/ohio-senate-debate-takeaways-tim-ryan-jd-vance/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported CNN}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou were calling Trump America\u8217\'20\'19s Hitler, then you kiss his ass, and then you kissed his ass, and he endorsed you and you said he is the greatest president of all time.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump also made a comment at a recent rally, saying Vance was \u8220\'20\'1Ckissing my ass\u8221\'20\'1D to get Trump to campaign for him.\par \par \uc2 In response, Vance said: \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  told a joke\u8230\'20\'26and Tim Ryan has decided to run his entire campaign on it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 Last night, Ryan and Vance had a highly personal and heated final debate, with the two attempting to persuade voters as midterms loom.\par \par \uc2 In one moment, Ryan accused Vance of \u8220\'20\'1Crunning around\u8221\'20\'1D people that support the \u8216\'20\'18great replacement theory\u8217\'20\'19, the belief that white people are being replaced by immigrants and other ethnic minorities, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/10/17/politics/ohio-senate-debate-takeaways-tim-ryan-jd-vance/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported CNN}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere is no big grand conspiracy \u8211\'20\'13 this is a country who has been enriched by immigrants,\u8221\'20\'1D said Ryan.\par \par \uc2 Vance was angry at Ryan\u8217\'20\'19s remarks, noting that his wife Usha is the \u8220\'20\'1Cdaughter of South Asian immigrants.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Vance also blamed Ryan\u8217\'20\'19s accusations on his biracial children \u8220\'20\'1Cget attacked by scumbags online and in person because you are so desperate for political power, that you will accuse me, the father of three beautiful biracial babies, of engaging in racism. We are sick of it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrMODERATOR: "What is your opinion of the "Great Replacement Theory?'"\par \par \uc2 Tim Ryan accuses J.D. Vance of believing in the ideas that inspired the Buffalo shooting. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/zRHe2OeCVT"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/zRHe2OeCVT}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Townhall.com (@townhallcom) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/townhallcom/status/1582158736919236609?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 17, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 Heated debates as US midterms approach\par \par \uc2 Good morning. Candidates vying for various positions had tense debates on Monday, with midterm elections less than a month away.\par \par \uc2 In Ohio, Democratic representative Tim Ryan and Republican candidate JD Vance had their last debate as \uc2 US Senate\uc2  candidates, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://link.axios.com/click/29405850.467746/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuYXhpb3MuY29tLzIwMjIvMTAvMTgvamQtdmFuY2UtdGltLXJ5YW4tb2hpby1zZW5hdGUtZGViYXRlLXJhY2lzbT91dG1fc291cmNlPW5ld3NsZXR0ZXImdXRtX21lZGl1bT1lbWFpbCZ1dG1fY2FtcGFpZ249bmV3c2xldHRlcl9heGlvc2FtJnN0cmVhbT10b3A/616518bf2a2eb77cae4f1c1bBa9b2baf2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported Axios}}}\uc2 . The heated debate touched on a number of topics, including accusations of racism that Ryan accused Vance of. In response, Vance called Ryan \u8220\'20\'1Cdesperate\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cdisgraceful\u8221\'20\'1D, blaming the Democrat for abuse facing his biracial children.\par \par \uc2 Down south, candidates in Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s gubernatorial race also had a debate, Axios further reported. Democrat \uc2 Stacey Abrams\uc2  and incumbent Brian Kemp clashed about gun policy, as Abrams blamed Kemp\u8217\'20\'19s lax approach to gun control on increased violence in the Peach state.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020221018eiai00107\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
