\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 White House calls Trump\u8217\'20\'19s remarks on American Jews \u8216\'20\'18antisemitic and insulting\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Lauren Gambino in Washington \par \uc2 4,127 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 October 2022\par 20:33 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Ex-president criticizes US Jews for not backing Israel enoughSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 Good afternoon. We\u8217\'20\'19re closing the liveblog for the day. Here\u8217\'20\'19s a look back at what\u8217\'20\'19s happened so far today.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Georgia Republican senate candidate Herschel Walker{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/17/georgia-herschel-walker-admits-paying-700-check-denies-abortion-raphael-warnock"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 admitted to writing $700 check }}}\uc2  to his ex-girlfriend but denies it was for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Walker, who is running in one of the most competitive Senate races in the country, has spent weeks dogged by reports that he sent the unnamed woman money to end her pregnancy. Running as a staunch conservative with Trump\u8217\'20\'19s backing, Walker has publicly argued that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be illegal nationwide without exceptions.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The US {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/secret-service"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Secret Service}}}\uc2  was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/17/secret-service-trump-hotels-congressional-committee"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 made to pay as much as $1,185 a night}}}\uc2  to stay at properties belonging to former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , a congressional committee said on Monday as it released documents that appeared to show the former president profiting from his protection details in and out of office.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Steve Bannon{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://storage.courtlistener.com/recap/gov.uscourts.dcd.237438/gov.uscourts.dcd.237438.152.0_3.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 should be sentenced}}}\uc2  to six months in prison and a $200,000 fine for \u8220\'20\'1Chis sustained, bad-faith contempt of Congress\u8221\'20\'1D, the justice department said in a legal filing on Monday. Bannon was found guilty on two counts of criminal contempt of Congress in July for ignoring a subpoena from the US House committee investigating the January 6 attack.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  condemned remarks by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  about American Jews as \u8220\'20\'1Cantisemitic\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cinsulting\u8221\'20\'1D to both Jewish people and Israelis. She also announced that Biden will host president \uc2 Isaac Herzog\uc2  of Israel at the White House on 26 October.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 The White House formally unveiled its website for student loan forgiveness applications.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a game-changer for millions of Americans,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said in remarks at the White House. He added that \u8220\'20\'1Cit took an incredible amount of effort to get this website done in such a short time.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrJUST IN: Pres. Biden unveils website for federal student loan debt relief application.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt takes less than five minutes\u8230\'20\'26This is a game-changer for millions of Americans.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/1SlS2LJ69i"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/1SlS2LJ69i}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/zWAe1RUCjT"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/zWAe1RUCjT}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 ABC News Politics (@ABCPolitics) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ABCPolitics/status/1582090564853727232?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 17, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 A beta version of the website, studentaid.gov, launched on Friday. Biden said 8 million Americans used the website over the weekend to apply for student-loan forgiveness.\par \par \uc2 This summer, under immense pressure from progressives, Biden announced that he would cancel up to $10,000 in student loan debt for individuals making less than $125,000 a year or more for Pell grant recipients.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 Asked if Biden regretted his comment that British Prime Minister \uc2 Liz Truss\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19 tax -cut plan was a mistake, Jean-Pierre responded simply: \u8220\'20\'1CNo.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Commenting on another world leader\u8217\'20\'19s domestic policies, especially those of a close ally, is usually seen as taboo. Biden, an institutionalist who usually adheres to the norms and codes of foreign relations, is also prone to blunt admissions that often send his aides scrambling to clarify.\par \par \uc2 Pressed further about the remark \u8211\'20\'13 Biden said he wasn\u8217\'20\'19t the only one who thought her economic policies were a mistake \u8211\'20\'13 Jean-Pierre said she had no further comment on who the president might have been referring to. The reporter said he was curious if Biden was referring to discussions with world leaders or if it was a reference to a staff member who viewed the move as a \u8220\'20\'1Cmistake\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/live/2022/oct/17/jeremy-hunt-mini-budget-liz-truss-conservatives-labour-tax-uk-politics-live"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Liz Truss admits \u8216\'20\'18mistakes have been made\u8217\'20\'19 as Jeremy Hunt says \u8216\'20\'18eye-watering\u8217\'20\'19 decisions on tax and spending need to be made \u8211\'20\'13 live}}}\par \par \uc2 The plan, which sent financial markets into a tailspin and caused a sharp drop in the value of the pound, was widely criticized by economists and experts.\par \par \uc2 Jean-Pierre also wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t weigh in on the UK\u8217\'20\'19s new finance minister, \uc2 Jeremy Hunt\uc2  nor his plans to drop much of Truss\u8217\'20\'19 tax plan.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe UK is a close ally \u8230\'20\'26 and we work with them on a range of issues, including on strengthening the global economy,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global/2022/oct/16/joe-biden-liz-truss-tax-cuts-a-mistake-and-i-wasnt-the-only-one-who-thought-so"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden calls Liz Truss tax cuts a \u8216\'20\'18mistake\u8217\'20\'19 as political fallout continues}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 On Russia\u8217\'20\'19s attacks on Ukraine, Jean-Pierre said: \u8220\'20\'1CThe United States strongly condemns Russia\u8217\'20\'19s missile strikes today which continues to demonstrate Russia\u8217\'20\'19s brutality.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She said the administration is in touch with Ukraine across the administration and noted that Biden spoke to Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s president {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/volodymyr-zelenskiy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy}}}\uc2  last week when he addressed the leaders of the Group of 7 nations.\par \par \uc2 Russia attacked Kyiv with nearly 30 \u8220\'20\'1Ckamikaze\u8221\'20\'1D drones on Monday morning, killing at least four people, including a pregnant woman and her partner, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/oct/17/kyiv-hit-by-a-series-of-explosions-from-drone-attack"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Guardian is reporting}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are going to continue to work with our allies and partners, continue to impose costs on Russia to hold them accountable for their war crimes,\u8221\'20\'1D Jean-Pierre said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 Jean-Pierre has fielded a few questions on the midterms and Biden\u8217\'20\'19s travel schedule in the final weeks of the election cycle, particularly why he isn\u8217\'20\'19t appearing at more campaign events.\par \par \uc2 Jean-Pierre, caveating her response by saying she is prohibited from talking about politics from the podium, pushed back. She argued that he has been \u8220\'20\'1Ctraveling nonstop,\u8221\'20\'1D noting his recent swing through Colorado, Oregon and California. This week he\u8217\'20\'19ll travel to the battleground states of Pennsylvania and Florida.\par \par \uc2 Reporters kept pressing. The subtext of their questions is that Biden is unpopular and his presence in some states could do more harm than good for Democrats in contested races. Biden has long joked that he would campaign for or against a Democrat \u8211\'20\'13 whatever would help them more.\par \par \uc2 She would not say whether Democrats in states like Arizona and Georgia are asking the White House for help, saying only: \u8220\'20\'1CHe is going to go where he is needed the most.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In Pennsylvania, Biden will appear alongside the Democratic candidate for Senate, \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2 , whose health has been under scrutiny since he suffered a stroke earlier this summer. Asked whether Biden has any concerns about Fetterman\u8217\'20\'19s health, Jean-Pierre said: \u8220\'20\'1CThe president has found him to be an impressive individual who is just as capable as always.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 Jean Pierre: Trump's comments on American Jews 'antisemitic and insulting'\par \par \uc2 The White House press briefing is underway, and press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  began with a question about \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s attack on American Jews.\par \par \uc2 She called the former president\u8217\'20\'19s comments \u8220\'20\'1Cantisemitic, as you all know, and insulting both to Jews and to our Israeli allies.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut let\u8217\'20\'19s be clear, for years, for years now, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has aligned with extremists and antisemitic figures and it should be called out,\u8221\'20\'1D she added. \u8220\'20\'1CWe need to root out antisemitism everywhere it rears its ugly head. \u8230\'20\'26 With respect to Israel, our relationship is iron clad and it\u8217\'20\'19s rooted in shared values and interests. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  clearly doesn\u8217\'20\'19t understand that either.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She also condemned Ye\u8217\'20\'19s antisemitic posts, but said she was not able to comment on the announcement this morning that he intends to purchase the far-right social media site, Parler.\par \par \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  at the White House. Photograph: Susan Walsh/AP\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 During \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s presidency, hotels and properties owned by the former president charged the Secret Service \u8220\'20\'1Cexorbitant\u8221\'20\'1D rates \u8211\'20\'13 as much as $1,185 per night at the Trump International Hotel in DC \u8211\'20\'13 according to new documents released on Monday by the House Committee on Oversight and Reform.\par \par \uc2 The secret service was tasked with protecting the safety of Trump and his family during his presidency, and therefore followed them on their travels.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe exorbitant rates charged to the Secret Service and agents\u8217\'20\'19 frequent stays at Trump-owned properties raise significant concerns about the former president\u8217\'20\'19s self-dealing and may have resulted in a taxpayer-funded windfall for former president Trump\u8217\'20\'19s struggling businesses,\u8221\'20\'1D the committee chair, the New York representative \uc2 Carolyn Maloney\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://oversight.house.gov/news/press-releases/chairwoman-maloney-releases-new-information-showing-trump-owned-properties"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  in a statement.\par \par \uc2 According to the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2 , which first reported on the payments, the new documents reveal, based on the committee\u8217\'20\'19s review, that US taxpayers paid the president\u8217\'20\'19s company at least $1.4m for Secret Service agents\u8217\'20\'19 stays at Trump properties for his and his family\u8217\'20\'19s protection.\par \par \uc2 The analysis shows that the Secret Service received more than 40 waivers from the Secret Service to let the agency spend more than the recommended rates.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 In a new interview, \uc2 Fiona Hill\uc2  says Putin is adapting, not giving up and is using messengers like Elon Musk to propose an end to the conflict on his terms.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPutin plays the egos of big men, gives them a sense that they can play a role. But in reality, they\u8217\'20\'19re just direct transmitters of messages from \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Hill {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/magazine/2022/10/17/fiona-hill-putin-war-00061894"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told}}}\uc2  Politico.\par \par \uc2 Hill, one of the nation\u8217\'20\'19s foremost experts on Russia and Putin, argues that the west has been slow to realize that Putin is waging a world war, what she describes as a \u8220\'20\'1Cgreat power conflict over territory which overturns the existing international order and where other states find themselves on different sides of the conflict.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a great power conflict, the third great power conflict in the European space in a little over a century,\u8221\'20\'1D Hill said . \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s the end of the existing world order. Our world is not going to be the same as it was before.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Read the full interview {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/magazine/2022/10/17/fiona-hill-putin-war-00061894"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  attacked US Jews on his social media platform last night, saying that they should \u8220\'20\'1Cget their act together\u8221\'20\'1D and show more appreciation to Israel \u8220\'20\'1Cbefore it\u8217\'20\'19s too late.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNo President has done more for Israel than I have. Somewhat surprisingly, however, our wonderful Evangelicals are far more appreciative of this than the people of the Jewish faith, especially those living in the U.S.,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump wrote on Truth Social.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThose living in Israel, though, are a different story \u8212\'20\'14 Highest approval rating in the World, could easily be P.M.!\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 It is not the first time Trump has flirted with the antisemitic trope that Jews hold \u8220\'20\'1Cdual loyalty\u8221\'20\'1D or are more loyal to Israel than the US. As in this post, he suggested that American Jews, who traditionally favor Democrats, should be more supportive of him because of his policies toward Israel.\par \par \uc2 enltrFormer US president warns US Jews to get their \u8220\'20\'1Cact together,\u8221\'20\'1D be more like Israelis, and appreciate him more {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/taRYa53d74"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/taRYa53d74}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Maggie Haberman (@maggieNYT) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/maggieNYT/status/1581638552538185728?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 16, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 Dr \uc2 Anthony Fauci\uc2 : long Covid is an \u8216\'20\'18insidious\u8217\'20\'19 public health emergency Photograph: Stefani Reynolds/AFP/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 In an exclusive interview with the Guardian, Dr \uc2 Anthony Fauci\uc2  warned about the dangers of long Covid, which he called an \u8220\'20\'1Cinsidious\u8221\'20\'1D if hard-to-diagnose public health emergency for millions of people.\par \par \uc2 Speaking to the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s David Smith, the nation\u8217\'20\'19s top infectious disease expert explained that the rates of long Covid are worrying, even if they receive far less attention than death and hospitalization rates.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C It isn\u8217\'20\'19t that you have people who are hospitalized or dying, but their function is being considerably impaired,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 One of the major challenges to diagnosing and treating long Covid is that relatively little is known about it. There is no test for long Covid, Smith writes, and its precise causes remain mysterious. Fauci said long Covid is likely more prominent among those with existing psychological issues, but he adds: \u8220\'20\'1CThe one thing you don\u8217\'20\'19t want to fall into the trap of saying is well, it\u8217\'20\'19s all psychological, because it\u8217\'20\'19s not, it\u8217\'20\'19s real.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Fauci urged Congress to continue investing in efforts to combat the virus and long Covid.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve hit a wall when it comes to further resources for Covid, including long Covid. There doesn\u8217\'20\'19t appear to be a lot of resources that are waiting for us right now,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CI hope that changes. If you declare victory, you\u8217\'20\'19re declaring an imaginary victory because we haven\u8217\'20\'19t won the battle yet.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Read the full interview here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2022/oct/17/fauci-interview-long-covid-risk-emergency-response-coronavirus"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dr Anthony Fauci: long Covid is an \u8216\'20\'18insidious\u8217\'20\'19 public health emergency }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 Major retailers will begin selling hearing aids over the counter without a prescription and at a much lower cost, as part of a new Biden administration rule that take effect today.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CStarting today, hearings aids are now on store shelves across the country \u8212\'20\'14 for thousands of dollars less than they previously cost,\u8221\'20\'1D the White House said in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2022/10/17/fact-sheet-cheaper-hearing-aids-now-in-stores-thanks-to-biden-harris-administration-competition-agenda/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fact sheet on Monday}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The move comes as Democrats tout their efforts to lower the cost of prescription drugs and ease the economic burden of high inflation and rising cost of living ahead of the midterms.\par \par \uc2 According to the White House, several major retailers, \uc2 Walgreens\uc2 , CVS and \uc2 Walmart\uc2  among them, will begin selling the devices today. It estimates that the rule could lower average costs by as much as $3,000 per pair of hearing aids. Nearly 30 million Americans have hearing loss, according to the fact sheet, including nearly 10 million adults under age 60.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 Today the Guardian launched a four-part series on Latino voters \u8211\'20\'13 a fast-growing, incredibly diverse voting bloc with the collective power to sway the 2022 midterm elections.\par \par \uc2 Though Latino voters have historically favored Democrats \u8211\'20\'13 and recent polling suggests that they still do \u8211\'20\'13 the party\u8217\'20\'19s grip on these voters is slipping as economic forces provide an opening for Republicans. This year, due in part to population growth and redistricting, Latino voters make up a significant slice of the electorate in several of the most competitive House and Senate races. The stakes for both parties could not be higher.\par \par \uc2 In the first installment, yours truly provides a very broad overview of the well-financed fight to engage and mobilize Latino voters this cycle. But look out for the rest of the series, with reports from Florida, Texas and the mountain west.\par \par \uc2 enltrOther pieces coming through Thursday look at why hopes that the south FL Latino vote would eventually turn aren't materializing, what drives Latino voter turnout and changing patterns in south TX, and a profile of a Mtn. West community where Latino voters are unexpectedly mighty. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/F3Sf2VasDN"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/F3Sf2VasDN}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ramon Antonio Vargas (@RVargasAdvocate) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RVargasAdvocate/status/1581975223502790657?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 17, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/17/democrats-republicans-campaign-latinos-hispanics-midterms"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats and Republicans fight to make inroads with Latinos ahead of midterms}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 My colleague Joan Greve recently published this report from Maine, where she assessed the state of Paul LePage\u8217\'20\'19s political comeback.\par \par \uc2 The state\u8217\'20\'19s famously belligerent former governor \u8211\'20\'13 Trump before Trump, as he once claimed \u8211\'20\'13 announced his retirement from politics in 2018 and decamped to Florida. But now he\u8217\'20\'19s back, challenging the state\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic governor, Janet Mills.\par \par \uc2 Now, in his campaign to return to the governor\u8217\'20\'19s mansion, LePage is distancing himself from the former president. He believes Biden won the 2020 election, a fact few Republicans are willing to accept publicly. But has he really changed?\par \par \uc2 Read the full report here.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/16/paul-lepage-maine-trump-governor-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Paul LePage: is Maine ready to welcome back the \u8216\'20\'18Trump before Trump\u8217\'20\'19?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kevin McCarthy expects to be the next speaker of the \uc2 US House of Representatives\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 That is the takeaway from a frenetic two days on the campaign trail with the Republican leader, according to a new report in Punchbowl news. Along the way, McCarthy spoke candidly about his path to the speakership, how difficult it is for Republicans to keep the job and offered his view of why he thinks his party is on track to wrest the majority from Democrats.\par \par \uc2 McCarthy tells donors and supporters that Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 chances are improving by the day. He is blunt that August was a bad month for Republicans, but says the tide is turning and the election is increasingly being fought on issues that advantage Republicans, such as the economy, immigration and crime.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat happened was all the issues came back on the front page. The cost of living continued to rise. Kids are going back to school and you\u8217\'20\'19re concerned about what type of education you\u8217\'20\'19re getting. And if you question your school board, somehow you\u8217\'20\'19re a terrorist. The price of gas was up seven cents last week with no hope of America being energy independent. We watch crime rise every single day,\u8221\'20\'1D McCarthy said at a fundraising event in Chicago.\par \par \uc2 Interestingly, McCarthy believes the tide began to turn sharply against Democrats {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/01/biden-speech-philadelphia-extremist-republicans-threaten-democracy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 after Biden\u8217\'20\'19s Philadelphia speech}}}\uc2 , in which the president warned that Trumpism posed an acute threat to American democracy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt all stops Sept. 1, the night that President Biden gave a speech in Philadelphia \u8211\'20\'13 an angry speech,\u8221\'20\'1D McCarthy added.\par \par \uc2 He also believes he\u8217\'20\'19ll be speaker no matter how big \u8211\'20\'13 or small \u8211\'20\'13 Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 winning majority is, meaning he thinks he can unite his fractious party behind him.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf I\u8217\'20\'19m even up for speaker, that means we won seats. I\u8217\'20\'19ve been [the top House Republican for] two cycles. I\u8217\'20\'19ve never lost seats, I\u8217\'20\'19ve only won,\u8221\'20\'1D he tells Punchbowl.\par \par \uc2 enltrI was shocked by McCarthy's candor about just how hard it is for Republicans to stay speaker. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/4c1PLjtqnT"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/4c1PLjtqnT}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jake Sherman (@JakeSherman) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JakeSherman/status/1581989070460575746?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 17, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 McCarthy is also open about how hard it is for a Republican to keep the job, noting that his most recent predecessors left after only a few years. By contrast, House Speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  has led her party for decades.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 First lady Jill Biden sat down for an interview this weekend with \uc2 Newsmax\uc2 , the far-right news network that cast doubt on her husband\u8217\'20\'19s election victory in 2020.\par \par \uc2 According to a press release touting the 20-minute interview, Biden discussed her efforts to combat cancer and her meeting with Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s first lady.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere are things Americans disagree with, but fighting cancer is one thing that unites Americans; and we\u8217\'20\'19re honored to have Dr. Biden talk of her efforts and President Biden\u8217\'20\'19s to combat this deadly condition,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Newsmax Media\uc2  CEO \uc2 Christopher Ruddy\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Newsmax\uc2  host, Nancy Brinker, is the founder of the \uc2 Susan G Komen Breast Cancer Foundation\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newsmax.com/newsfront/jill-biden-cancer-ukraine/2022/10/16/id/1092103/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 interview}}}\uc2  airs at 9pm.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 A new NYT/Siena poll looks glum for Democrats. After their fortunes appeared to reverse this summer, Republicans have regained their edge with voters just weeks left before election day.\par \par \uc2 enltrNEW: NYT/Siena poll shows Republicans opening up a 49-45 lead in race for Congress as the economy becomes dominant concern of 2022.\par \par \uc2 The swing toward the GOP among women voters who identified as independent in the last month is striking. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/JPRgHo55iZ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/JPRgHo55iZ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Shane Goldmacher (@ShaneGoldmacher) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ShaneGoldmacher/status/1581990016636841985?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 17, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 According to the poll, Republicans hold a 49-45 lead in the race for Congress, with the economy being a top priority for voters in 2022. The shift was driven by women who identified as independent voters.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn September, they favored Democrats by 14 points. Now, independent women backed Republicans by 18 points.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The poll found the share of voters who ranked the economy or inflation as a top issue climbed nearly 10%. Republicans have long held an advantage on the economy, a trend that is even more pronounced with inflation at a 40-year-high and Democrats in control in Washington. A far smaller share of voters prioritize issues that favor Democrats, such as \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and guns.\par \par \uc2 Moreover, voters are extremely dissatisfied with the president, a factor that further hurts Democrats.\par \par \uc2 Read more {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/10/17/us/politics/republicans-economy-nyt-siena-poll.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2  and play with the crosstabs {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2022/10/17/upshot/times-siena-poll-likely-voters-crosstabs.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 Justice department urges prison time for \uc2 Steve Bannon\par \par \uc2 Steve Bannon{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://storage.courtlistener.com/recap/gov.uscourts.dcd.237438/gov.uscourts.dcd.237438.152.0_3.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 should be sentenced}}}\uc2  to six months in prison and a $200,000 fine for \u8220\'20\'1Chis sustained, bad-faith contempt of Congress,\u8221\'20\'1D the justice department said in a legal filing on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Bannon, the former Donald Trump White House strategist, was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/22/steve-bannon-trial-trump-contempt-congress-charges"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 found guilty}}}\uc2  on two counts of criminal contempt of Congress in July for ignoring a subpoena from the committee investigating the January 6 attack.\par \par \uc2 The department submitted its recommendation for his punishment on Monday ahead of his scheduled sentencing on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/17/steve-bannon-contempt-case-jan-6-justice-dept"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Steve Bannon: justice department urges six-month prison term in contempt case}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 Ye to buy right-wing social media network Parler\par \par \uc2 Some early-breaking news: Ye, formerly Kanye West, is buying the rightwing social media network Parler for an undisclosed sum, the platform announced on Monday.\par \par \uc2 The deal is expected to close in the fourth quarter of this year, the \uc2 Guardian\uc2  reports. News of the purchase comes {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/music/2022/oct/09/kanye-west-ye-instagram-twitter-accounts-locked-antisemitic-posts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  a week after Twitter and Instagram locked }}}\uc2  the rapper\u8217\'20\'19s accounts over antisemitic posts.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn a world where conservative opinions are considered to be controversial we have to make sure we have the right to freely express ourselves,\u8221\'20\'1D Ye said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 Last year, Parler was effectively forced offline for allowing violent videos of the January 6 Capitol attack to circulate on its platform.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2022/oct/17/kanye-west-to-buy-right-wing-social-network-parler"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kanye West to buy rightwing social network Parler }}}\par \par \uc2 This is only the latest in a series of controversial moves by the artist. Over the weekend, Ye claimed in a podcast appearance that George Floyd died from a drug overdose. Minneapolis police officer Derek Chauvin was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jun/25/derek-chauvin-george-floyd-murder-sentencing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 convicted of Floyd\u8217\'20\'19s murder}}}\uc2  in May 2020. Floyd\u8217\'20\'19s family is considering taking legal action.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/music/2022/oct/17/family-of-george-floyd-considers-legal-action-over-kanye-west-comments"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Family of George Floyd considers legal action over Kanye West comments}}}\par \par \uc2 And that was after Ye appeared wearing a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/music/2022/oct/04/kanye-west-white-lives-matter-t-shirt-paris-fashion-week"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhite Lives Matter\u8221\'20\'1D shirt}}}\uc2  at Paris Fashion Week.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republican \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  a no-show for key debate\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. I hope everyone had a nice weekend. We\u8217\'20\'19re in the heat of election season, with just a handful of weeks left before Americans go to the polls.\par \par \uc2 Hours ago, Russia attacked the Ukrainian capital of Kyiv with \u8220\'20\'1Ckamikaze\u8221\'20\'1D drones, killing at least three people. For the latest, we encourage you to follow our {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/oct/17/russia-ukraine-war-live-explosions-heard-in-kyiv-conflict-has-pushed-four-million-children-into-poverty-says-un"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ukraine live blog}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a look at what else is happening today in US politics:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Last night, Georgia Senate GOP candidate \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  was a no-show for his second and final debate with Democratic senator \uc2 Raphael Warnock\uc2 , hosted by the Atlanta Press Club debate on Sunday. The race is among the most competitive in the country and polling suggests the candidates are effectively tied.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re also watching an NBC interview with Walker set to air tonight. In a preview, Walker admits giving his ex-girlfriend a $700 check, but denies it was for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after being \u8220\'20\'1Cconfronted with a receipt from an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic and a check dated days later and bearing his name\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltr'That's my check': Walker acknowledges giving $700 to his ex, but denies her claim he knew it was for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/uS1svxsGQI"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/uS1svxsGQI}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kristen Welker (@kwelkernbc) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kwelkernbc/status/1581969553671979008?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 17, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 This evening, candidates in battleground states will square off in a series of crucial debates. In Georgia, Republican Governor \uc2 Brian Kemp\uc2  will debate Democratic challenger \uc2 Stacey Abrams\uc2 . In Utah, Republican senator \uc2 Mike Lee\uc2  debates his independent challenger, Evan McMullin. The candidates for Ohio\u8217\'20\'19s open senate seat \u8211\'20\'13 Democratic congressman \uc2 Tim Ryan\uc2  and Republican JD Vance \u8211\'20\'13 will hold their second debate this evening. While in Iowa, Republican governor \uc2 Kim Reynolds\uc2  faces her Democratic challenger, Deidre DeJear, in a debate.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is returning to the White House after spending the weekend in his home state of Delaware. Press Secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  will brief reporters at 1.30pm.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The January 6 committee is expected to formally subpoena \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  this week, in an attempt to compel the former president to answer questions about his role in the deadly insurrection at the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020221017eiah000xw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
