\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  admits to writing $700 check but denies it was for  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein \par \uc2 707 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 October 2022\par 17:44 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The Georgia Republican candidate for the Senate claims he has \u8216\'20\'18no idea\u8217\'20\'19 what the money was used for\par \par \uc2 Confronted on Sunday with receipts that appear to prove he paid for the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  of a woman he once dated, staunch anti-abortionist \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s Republican candidate for the \uc2 US Senate\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 had a ready response: \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a lie.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Walker is competing for a Senate seat considered pivotal to determining which party controls the chamber in the 8 November midterms, but his campaign has spent weeks under fire after reports emerged earlier this month that Walker \u8211\'20\'13 who has publicly argued that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be illegal nationwide without exceptions \u8211\'20\'13 sent the unnamed woman money to end her pregnancy.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/meet-the-press/video/full-herschel-walker-interview-yes-that-s-my-check-150803013785"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 In an interview with NBC News}}}\uc2 , Walker was presented with an image of a check for $700 written in 2009, to which he responded, \u8220\'20\'1CYes, that\u8217\'20\'19s my check.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 However, he disputed that its purpose was to pay for the termination of the woman\u8217\'20\'19s pregnancy. He maintained his denial even after NBC showed him a receipt from the clinic where the woman \u8211\'20\'13 whose name was not revealed by the network but who has said she is also the mother of one of Walker\u8217\'20\'19s children \u8211\'20\'13 underwent the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a lie,\u8221\'20\'1D Walker said, saying that it\u8217\'20\'19s not unusual he would send money to someone with whom he had a child. \u8220\'20\'1CI know that\u8217\'20\'19s what the people want to know \u8211\'20\'13 it\u8217\'20\'19s a lie.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Walker also said he has helped the woman \u8220\'20\'1Cforever\u8221\'20\'1D and had \u8220\'20\'1Cno idea\u8221\'20\'1D what the $700 might have been for.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSo when they show me a check and I never said anything about an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , I never said anything about anything and they say this, that\u8217\'20\'19s just people talking,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 A former college football and \uc2 NFL\uc2  star who is endorsed by former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , Walker is trying to unseat Democratic incumbent \uc2 Raphael Warnock\uc2 , who won a Senate seat just last year in a special election and is now vying for a full six-year term. Georgia, where early voting began on Monday, is among a handful of states including Pennsylvania, Wisconsin and Arizona which are expected to determine whether Democrats maintain control of Congress\u8217\'20\'19s upper chamber or lose power to the GOP.\par \par \uc2 The senior pastor of Atlanta\u8217\'20\'19s Ebenezer Baptist church where \uc2 Martin Luther King Jr\uc2  once preached, Warnock has held off on attacking Walker over the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  revelations, but voters appear to have taken note.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/2022-election-forecast/senate/georgia/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Poll aggregator FiveThirtyEight registered}}}\uc2  a significant jump in Warnock\u8217\'20\'19s chances and a decline in Walker\u8217\'20\'19s prospects in early October, when the Daily Beast broke the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  story.\par \par \uc2 At their lone debate encounter on Friday, Walker attacked Warnock for being soft on crime and for supporting Democratic policies he claimed drove inflation higher. But the Republican also denied ever supporting a hardline \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban and created an unusual scene by pulling out a badge to prove his support for law enforcement \u8211\'20\'13 even though he was never known to have served as a police officer.\par \par \uc2 Asked to clarify the moment by NBC, Walker again displayed the badge, describing it as both \u8220\'20\'1Ca real badge\u8221\'20\'1D and an \u8220\'20\'1Chonorary badge\u8221\'20\'1D that he always carries with him.\par \par \uc2 He said it was given to him by the sheriff of Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s Johnson county, where his home town is located. The former running back for the University of Georgia Bulldogs added: \u8220\'20\'1CIf anything happens in this county, I have the right to work with the police in getting things done.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 NBC reported that the sheriff of Johnson county, a rural area about 150 miles south-east of Atlanta, confirmed that he had given Walker the badge and could call upon him if there were a crisis.\par \par \uc2 The 8 November midterms are 22 days away, but Walker and Warnock\u8217\'20\'19s Friday debate appearance will be their only encounter of this campaign.\par \par \uc2 While Warnock has committed to three debate appearances, Walker would only participate in the one. Warnock appeared at a Sunday debate against libertarian Senate candidate Chase Oliver hosted by the Atlanta Press Club, where Walker\u8217\'20\'19s absence was noted with an empty lectern.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020221017eiah001mf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
