\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Indiana supreme court blocks state from enforcing  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ban\b0\par\par\uc2 Maya Yang \par \uc2 616 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 October 2022\par 21:00 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Court order keeps ban on hold while judges consider whether Republican-backed effort violates state constitution\par \par \uc2 The Indiana supreme court issued an order Wednesday that prevents the state from enforcing a Republican-backed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban while it considers whether it violates the state constitution.\par \par \uc2 The supreme court took over the case after a county judge blocked the ban last month, spurring the attorney general to appeal the decision. The court denied a request from the state attorney general\u8217\'20\'19s office to set aside the preliminary injunction, setting a hearing on the lawsuit filed by \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic operators for 12 January.\par \par \uc2 Owen county judge Kelsey Hanlon blocked the law from being enforced, writing that \u8220\'20\'1Cthere is reasonable likelihood that this significant restriction of personal autonomy offends the liberty guarantees of the Indiana constitution\u8221\'20\'1D and that the clinics will prevail in the lawsuit.\par \par \uc2 The ban was approved by the state\u8217\'20\'19s Republican-dominated legislature on 5 August and signed by Republican governor \uc2 Eric Holcomb\uc2 . That made Indiana the first state to enact tighter \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions after the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  eliminated federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections by overturning Roe v Wade in June.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFollowing the overturning of Roe, I stated clearly that I would be willing to support legislation that made progress in protecting life,\u8221\'20\'1D Holcomb {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.indystar.com/story/news/politics/2022/08/05/indiana-abortion-law-passed-final-vote-to-come/65391000007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  in August when he approved the ban.\par \par \uc2 The five-member supreme court, all of whom were appointed by Republican governors, did not explain their decision.\par \par \uc2 The American Civil Liberties Union of Indiana, which is representing the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics, filed the lawsuit on August 31. It argued that the ban would \u8220\'20\'1Cprohibit the overwhelming majority of abortions in Indiana and, as such, will have a devastating and irreparable impact on the plaintiffs and, more importantly, their patients and clients\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 A joint statement by \uc2 ACLU\uc2 , Planned Parenthood and other women\u8217\'20\'19s health centers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.aclu-in.org/en/press-releases/court-temporarily-blocks-indiana-abortion-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  said}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CThere are 1.5 million people of reproductive age in the state of Indiana, and every single one of them deserve the right to make their own decisions about their bodies, families, and futures\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Ken Falk, the ACLU of Indiana\u8217\'20\'19s legal director, pointed to the state constitution\u8217\'20\'19s declaration of rights, including \u8220\'20\'1Clife, liberty and the pursuit of happiness\u8221\'20\'1D in arguing before the county judge that it included a right to privacy and to make decisions on whether to have children.\par \par \uc2 The state attorney general\u8217\'20\'19s office said the court should uphold the ban, saying arguments against it are based on a \u8220\'20\'1Cnovel, unwritten, historically unsupported right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D in the state constitution.\par \par \uc2 The attorney general\u8217\'20\'19s office had asked the supreme court to take over the case, bypassing the typical intermediate step of it being considered by the state appeals court.\par \par \uc2 Neither the \uc2 ACLU\uc2  nor the state attorney general\u8217\'20\'19s office immediately commented on the court\u8217\'20\'19s action.\par \par \uc2 The Indiana ban aimed to replace state laws that generally prohibited abortions after the 20th week of pregnancy and tightly restricted them after the 13th week. The ban includes exceptions allowing abortions in cases of rape and incest, before 10 weeks post-fertilization; to protect the life and physical health of the mother; and if a fetus is diagnosed with a lethal anomaly.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis bill says, we are only going to give full constitutional rights to women if their very life is threatened, or they are a victim of rape. Then those women and girls have just 10 weeks to come to terms with the assault, being pregnant by their assaulter, and sorting through that trauma,\u8221\'20\'1D Indiana state senator Shelli Yoder {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/15/indiana-abortion-ban-trigger-law"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told}}}\uc2  the Guardian last month.\par \par \uc2 The question of whether the Indiana constitution protects \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights is undecided.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020221012eiac003mm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
