\par\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 The new state of healthcare in America: one for men and a worse one for women\b0\par\par\uc2 Moira Donegan \par \uc2 1,238 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 October 2022\par 14:05 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 After Roe v Wade, women in anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  states can\u8217\'20\'19t access life-saving medication for everything from chronic pain to lupus to ulcers\par \par \uc2 Maybe the pharmacist at the Tucson, Arizona, \uc2 Walgreens\uc2  was acting out of religious conviction. Maybe they were afraid that they could get arrested. We may never know. What we do know is that on 26 September, two days after Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban went into effect, Emma Thompson, a 14-year-old girl with rheumatoid arthritis and osteoporosis, was denied her prescription for methotrexate.\par \par \uc2 Thompson had been on methotrexate for some time; this was a longstanding prescription that she was getting refilled. The drug, a potent anti-inflammatory drug, is used to treat a wide array of issues, from autoimmune disorders, like Thompson\u8217\'20\'19s, to arthritis and cancer. It\u8217\'20\'19s estimated that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/health/2022/08/08/abortion-bans-methotrexate-mifepristone-rheumatoid-arthritis/?utm_source=substack&utm_medium=email"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 60%}}}\uc2  of all rheumatoid arthritis patients are prescribed the drug, and for Thompson, it was working well. After a childhood spent in and out of hospitals, enduring years of debilitating pain, her doctors had finally found a medication and a dosage that seemed to be working for her. Her symptoms abated enough that she was able to attend school. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s her first year and she\u8217\'20\'19s in high school and it feels like a dream,\u8221\'20\'1D said Thompson\u8217\'20\'19s mother, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kold.com/2022/10/01/teen-girl-denied-medication-refill-under-azs-new-abortion-law/?utm_source=substack&utm_medium=email"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kaitlin Preble}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CShe\u8217\'20\'19s not in a wheelchair, she has a social life and friends for the first time, and a life all young people should have.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 There are now two standards of medical care: the one that men are entitled to, and the lesser one that women have to make do with\par \par \uc2 But in high doses, methotrexate can also terminate a pregnancy. The drug is not used in most abortions \u8211\'20\'13 when methotrexate is used as an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drug, it is often administered as an injection to treat an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://uihc.org/educational-resources/methotrexate-ectopic-pregnancy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ectopic pregnancy}}}\uc2 , the kind of nonviable pregnancy that occurs when a fertilized egg implants outside the uterus, which can never result in a baby and frequently has fatal implications for pregnant women. It\u8217\'20\'19s for this reason that several state \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans mention methotrexate by name. When the pharmacy wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t fill Thompson\u8217\'20\'19s prescription, this was why: they refused to give the drug to any female patient of \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/nation/2022/10/05/abortion-arizona-arthritis-prescription-refill/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 childbearing age}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Thompson is not alone. Facing politically motivated refusals from rightwing or religious healthcare providers \u8211\'20\'13 and caution and confusion from others, who may refuse to prescribe or dispense necessary drugs for fear of being prosecuted or sued under \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans \u8211\'20\'13 American women living in anti-choice states have suddenly found themselves unable to access a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/health/2022/08/08/abortion-bans-methotrexate-mifepristone-rheumatoid-arthritis/?utm_source=substack&utm_medium=email"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wide array of medications}}}\uc2 . Drugs which can be used in abortions, or which can possibly cause fetal abnormalities, are used to treat everything from chronic pain to lupus to ulcers to acne. These were medications that these patients were prescribed, and medications that they could get with relative ease before Dobbs. They are medications that they could still get, if they were men.\par \par \uc2 In response, these women have had to change the course of their medical treatment, or gone through onerous procedures to find new prescribers, pharmacists or medicines. Many women and trans people have long had to take pregnancy tests before they are allowed to access certain medications, proving that there is no fetus to be harmed or risked before they are allowed the medicine that they need to get well. Others are now finding that scared or anti-choice doctors are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/health/2022/08/08/abortion-bans-methotrexate-mifepristone-rheumatoid-arthritis/?utm_source=substack&utm_medium=email"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 demanding that they have themselves sterilized}}}\uc2  before they can continue the treatments that allow them to live normal, productive and relatively pain-free lives.\par \par \uc2 This is the new state of healthcare in America, where misogynist laws banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  have ushered in an era of sex-segregated medical care for all sorts of ailments and conditions. In states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is banned, there are now de facto two standards of medical care: the one that men are entitled to, and the lesser one that women have to make do with.\par \par \uc2 Thompson was relatively lucky. She had a doctor and a mother who both advocated for her, and were alert to the injustice of her plight. Deborah Power, Thompson\u8217\'20\'19s rheumatologist who prescribed the methotrexate, was so outraged when she heard that the prescription had been refused that she expressed her frustration on \uc2 Twitter\uc2  at what was being done to her patient.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWelcome to AZ,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/bonespower/status/1574598975788789761"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dr Power wrote}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CToday a pharmacist denied the MTX refill for my adolescent patient \u8230\'20\'26 MTX denied purely because she\u8217\'20\'19s female, barely a teenager.\u8221\'20\'1D The post went viral. Meanwhile, Thompson\u8217\'20\'19s mother, Preble, drove to the pharmacy \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/nation/2022/10/05/abortion-arizona-arthritis-prescription-refill/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 and made a big deal inside}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D. She eventually learned that the pharmacists who denied her daughter\u8217\'20\'19s prescription had looked up the patient\u8217\'20\'19s age and sex, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/nation/2022/10/05/abortion-arizona-arthritis-prescription-refill/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 but not her medical history}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy entire life, I was in and out of the hospital,\u8221\'20\'1D Thompson told a local news station. \u8220\'20\'1CI was never able to stay in school until this past year, I was never able to ride a bike or get on the monkey bars like other kids could.\u8221\'20\'1D She continued: \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s not right. They\u8217\'20\'19re trying to make any girl who\u8217\'20\'19s on this medication drop a pregnancy test when they get their medicine and I feel like it\u8217\'20\'19s really unfair.\u8221\'20\'1D Eventually, Thompson was able to get her medication, and hopefully, she will be able to keep getting it \u8211\'20\'13 to keep her pain manageable, to stay in school, and to live the full life that she deserves.\par \par \uc2 Other patients haven\u8217\'20\'19t been so lucky, and other doctors have not been such good advocates for their patients. In Tennessee, Becky Hubbard, a 46-year-old whose rheumatoid arthritis became so debilitating that she had to quit her job as a nurse, was told by her own longtime rheumatologist that she would either have to go on birth control or get sterilized if she wanted to continue taking her medication. If she refused, she wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t get the prescription. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s frustrating as hell,\u8221\'20\'1D Hubbard {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/health/2022/08/08/abortion-bans-methotrexate-mifepristone-rheumatoid-arthritis/?utm_source=substack&utm_medium=email"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told the Washington Post}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CIf you can\u8217\'20\'19t get the medicine that gets you out of the flares, you just have to live with the pain.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The logic of misogyny often dictates that women sacrifice their own needs and wellbeing for the comfort of others. Be it as doting wives, as ever-available mothers, as self-effacing workhorses or as ornamental sex objects, sexist culture frequently demands that women\u8217\'20\'19s own ambitions, comforts, desires and, yes, health, be put aside to make them better suited to serve and support those around them. The anti-choice movement has always relied on this logic, extending women\u8217\'20\'19s obligation to sacrifice themselves for other people into an obligation to sacrifice themselves for potential other people, or future other people, the embryo or the fetus whose interests seem to supplant any claims the pregnant person may have over her own future, ambitions or body. To deny women medication that could damage a pregnancy, even when there is no pregnancy, just takes this same logic even further. The nominal benefit to others is erased; there is not even a pretext of another person whose interests can justify the mandate to make women suffer. The only principle that remains is make women suffer. If Thompson\u8217\'20\'19s case is any indication, that mandate also extends to girls.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020221012eiac001jl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
