\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Kevin McCarthy claimed Trump had no idea his supporters carried out Capitol attack \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein in Washington \par \uc2 4,323 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 October 2022\par 20:05 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Top Republican House made claim in meeting with police officers despite ex-president having urged supporters to \u8216\'20\'18fight like hell\u8217\'20\'19Sign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 If the GOP wins the House in the upcoming midterms, they will {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/10/midterm-election-jan-6-mccarthy-republicans-democrats-biden-latest?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-634430f98f083d981ab0ddcf#block-634430f98f083d981ab0ddcf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 investigate Hunter Biden}}}\uc2  and attempt to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/10/midterm-election-jan-6-mccarthy-republicans-democrats-biden-latest?page=with:block-634418008f0825d5ecc79080#block-634418008f0825d5ecc79080"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 turn a blind eye}}}\uc2  towards the January 6 insurrection, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/10/midterm-election-jan-6-mccarthy-republicans-democrats-biden-latest?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-634430f98f083d981ab0ddcf#block-634430f98f083d981ab0ddcf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an interview with a top lawmaker}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/10/midterm-election-jan-6-mccarthy-republicans-democrats-biden-latest?page=with:block-63440eb18f08fe8d3bd4a09d#block-63440eb18f08fe8d3bd4a09d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the memoir of a police officer wounded in the insurrection}}}\uc2 . But that hasn\u8217\'20\'19t happened yet, and today brought news that a key witness before the January 6 committee {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/10/midterm-election-jan-6-mccarthy-republicans-democrats-biden-latest?page=with:block-634470f98f0870981cb4f3eb#block-634470f98f0870981cb4f3eb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is cooperating with a probe into election meddling in Georgia}}}\uc2 , while a lawmaker on the panel {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/10/midterm-election-jan-6-mccarthy-republicans-democrats-biden-latest?page=with:block-634465018f0870981cb4f36f#block-634465018f0870981cb4f36f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signaled its Thursday hearing}}}\uc2  may include more details of the Secret Service\u8217\'20\'19s actions around the attack.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else happened today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/10/midterm-election-jan-6-mccarthy-republicans-democrats-biden-latest?page=with:block-6344446b8f0870981cb4f1f4#block-6344446b8f0870981cb4f1f4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 condemned Russia\u8217\'20\'19s missile strikes}}}\uc2  across a swath of Ukraine, including the capital Kyiv, and said the country has Washington\u8217\'20\'19s support. Later, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/10/midterm-election-jan-6-mccarthy-republicans-democrats-biden-latest?page=with:block-634477f88f0870981cb4f42f#block-634477f88f0870981cb4f42f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he spoke with}}}\uc2  the country\u8217\'20\'19s leader \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2  about Kyiv\u8217\'20\'19s need for more air defenses.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Republican senator Tommy Tuberville{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/10/midterm-election-jan-6-mccarthy-republicans-democrats-biden-latest?page=with:block-63443ae98f0870981cb4f16e#block-63443ae98f0870981cb4f16e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 resorted to racism}}}\uc2  at a rally for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 In a column for the Guardian, Senator Bernie Sanders{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/10/midterm-election-jan-6-mccarthy-republicans-democrats-biden-latest?page=with:block-6344295f8f0834e330f6357f#block-6344295f8f0834e330f6357f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 warned Democrats of the perils}}}\uc2  of campaigning on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights alone.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 The White House has now released its version of president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s phone call with Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The readout largely matches Zelenskiy\u8217\'20\'19s tweet from earlier this afternoon:\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Joseph R. Biden\uc2 , Jr., spoke today with President \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskyy\uc2  of Ukraine. He expressed his condemnation of Russia\u8217\'20\'19s missile strikes across Ukraine, including in Kyiv, and conveyed his condolences to the loved ones of those killed and injured in these senseless attacks. President Biden pledged to continue providing Ukraine with the support needed to defend itself, including advanced air defense systems. He also underscored his ongoing engagement with allies and partners to continue imposing costs on Russia, holding Russia accountable for its war crimes and atrocities, and providing Ukraine with security, economic, and humanitarian assistance.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 Last week, Nebraska\u8217\'20\'19s Republican senator \uc2 Ben Sasse\uc2  announced he would leave Congress to take over as president of the \uc2 University of Florida\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 As documented by The Tampa Bay Times, he did not get a particularly warm reception from some students today {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wowt.com/2022/10/10/sen-ben-sasse-visits-university-florida/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 during his visit}}}\uc2  to the campus in Gainesville:\par \par \uc2 enltrOutside Sen. \uc2 Ben Sasse\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s moderated forum to meet with students, hundreds have gathered protesting Sasse as the sole finalist in UF\u8217\'20\'19s presidential search, citing his previous public statements on same-sex marriage and the search sealed from the public among reasons. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Uay2bQIbEf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Uay2bQIbEf}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Divya Kumar (@divyadivyadivya) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/divyadivyadivya/status/1579551060859183106?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 10, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrIn a previous session with faculty, Sasse\u8217\'20\'19s first question was regarding how he would ensure LGBTQ+ members felt protected. Sasse said he believed in the \u8220\'20\'1Cimmeasurable worth and universal dignity of every single person.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Divya Kumar (@divyadivyadivya) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/divyadivyadivya/status/1579551070535421952?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 10, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrProtesters are now in the room Sasse\u8217\'20\'19s forum with students was held and a forum with staff is scheduled for 3:30. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/NFh998ZrHP"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/NFh998ZrHP}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Divya Kumar (@divyadivyadivya) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/divyadivyadivya/status/1579553490468483072?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 10, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/07/senate-republican-ben-sasse-depart-washington-university-florida"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ben Sasse, Republican who voted to convict Trump, to depart Congress}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 Some of the biggest revelations from the January 6 committee\u8217\'20\'19s public hearings came from the testimony of Cassidy Hutchinson, a White House aide who witnessed and overheard {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/28/january-6-committee-session-new-evidence"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shocking behavior}}}\uc2  by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and others in his administration.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/10/10/politics/cassidy-hutchinson-cooperation-trump-investigation/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN reports}}}\uc2  she is now cooperating with the special grand jury empaneled by a county prosecutor in Georgia to investigate the effort by Trump\u8217\'20\'19s allies to interfere with the state\u8217\'20\'19s backing of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from CNN:\par \par \uc2 The former top aide to then-White House chief of staff \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2  could offer Georgia prosecutors insights about what she witnessed in the West Wing, as well as steps her former boss took specifically when it came to Georgia.\par \par \uc2 Prosecutors have called {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/08/25/politics/mark-meadows-fani-willis-georgia-trump-investigation/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 for Meadows to testify }}}\uc2  before the special grand jury, but they are still working to secure his testimony. A hearing on the matter is scheduled for late October.\par \par \uc2 Meadows was among the participants on the January 2021 call between Trump and Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s secretary of state \uc2 Brad Raffensperger\uc2 , and Meadows also made a surprise visit to a Cobb County location in December 2020, where officials were conducting an absentee ballot signature audit.\par \par \uc2 Hutchinson has also been cooperating with the Justice Department, which also faces a pre-election quiet period, in its criminal investigation into efforts to subvert the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 An attorney for Hutchinson did not respond to CNN\u8217\'20\'19s requests for comment.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian president \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2  says he has spoken with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  after the Russian missile attacks on his country.\par \par \uc2 The topics of conversation included Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s need for air defenses and today\u8217\'20\'19s United Nations general assembly vote on a resolution condemning Russia\u8217\'20\'19s annexation of four Ukrainian regions:\par \par \uc2 enltrProductive conversation with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @POTUS}}}\uc2 . Air defense is currently the number 1 priority in our defense cooperation.\par \par \uc2 We also need US leadership with the \uc2 G7\uc2 's tough stance and with support for our UN GA resolution.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 ????????? ?????????? (@ZelenskyyUa) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ZelenskyyUa/status/1579547763255443456?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 10, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 The White House hasn\u8217\'20\'19t yet provided their own readout of the call.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 The same day that Moscow barraged Ukraine with missiles, Russian-speaking hackers have taken down the websites of several US airports, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/gloria-oladipo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gloria Oladipo}}}\uc2  reports, but flight operations do not appear to have been impacted:\par \par \uc2 Websites for more than a dozen US airports were temporarily brought offline by cyberattacks on Monday morning, with Russian-speaking hackers claiming responsibility for the disruption.\par \par \uc2 About 14 public-facing websites for a number of sizable airports, including LaGuardia airport in New York City, were targeted and inaccessible to the public. Most have since been brought back online.\par \par \uc2 A senior official told {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/Technology/cyberattacks-reported-us-airports/story?id=91287965"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ABC News}}}\uc2  that the attacks did not affect air traffic control, internal airport communication or other key operations. But the official said that the interruption caused an \u8220\'20\'1Cinconvenience\u8221\'20\'1D for travelers attempting to access information.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/10/cyberattacks-disrupt-us-airport-websites"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cyberattacks force over a dozen US airport websites offline }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 The January 6 committee\u8217\'20\'19s hearing on Thursday will probably center on evidence collected over the summer, including the Secret Service\u8217\'20\'19s actions around the insurrection, a lawmaker on the panel said over the weekend.\par \par \uc2 In a Sunday interview with MSNBC, \uc2 Zoe Lofgren\uc2 , a California Democrat serving on the committee, also downplayed the importance of its interview with Ginni Thomas, the wife of conservative supreme court justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  who has lobbied state lawmakers nationwide to support efforts to overturn the 2020 election. \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t think she was a major player in this personally,\u8221\'20\'1D Lofgren said.\par \par \uc2 The committee hasn\u8217\'20\'19t held a public hearing since late July, and Lofgren said the upcoming session will likely focus on evidence collected by investigators during the break. \u8220\'20\'1CI think it will shed some light on the events of the day and the events leading up to it, the connections between the extremists and the Republicans,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 You can watch the interview {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.msnbc.com/yasmin-vossoughian-reports/watch/rep-zoe-lofgren-d-ca-says-ginni-thomas-may-be-featured-in-upcoming-jan-6-committee-hearing-150257221714"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 . The January 6 committee will hold its next hearing beginning at 1pm eastern time on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/hugo-lowell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hugo Lowell}}}\uc2  about what Christina Bobb, a lawyer for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  involved in the Mar-a-Lago secrets case, told the justice department:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s lawyer Christina Bobb was instructed to certify to the justice department that all sensitive government documents stored at his Mar-a-Lago resort subpoenaed by a grand jury had been returned, though she had not herself conducted the search for the records.\par \par \uc2 The certification of subpoena compliance appears to be at the center of a criminal investigation into obstruction of justice surrounding the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 former US president}}}\uc2  after the assurance was proved to be untrue when the \uc2 FBI\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s search of the property turned up more than 100 more documents marked classified.\par \par \uc2 The saga around the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/mar-a-lago"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mar-a-Lago}}}\uc2  documents has become increasingly mired in the courts as Trump has repeatedly claimed the \uc2 FBI\uc2  search and resultant investigation is politically motivated. Meanwhile, the justice department and Democrats have portrayed the taking of the documents as a potentially serious national security breach.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/10/trump-lawyer-christina-bobb-mar-a-lago-certify-documents"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump lawyer told to certify Mar-a-Lago document search she did not conduct}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump lawyer spoke to justice department in Mar-a-Lago document investigation\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Hugo Lowell reports that Christina Bobb, a lawyer for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , spoke to the justice department as it investigates the government secrets discovered at the former president\u8217\'20\'19s Mar-a-Lago resort in August.\par \par \uc2 enltrConfirming NBC that Trump lawyer Christina Bobb spoke to the Justice Dept on Friday \u8212\'20\'14 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GuardianUS?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @GuardianUS}}}\uc2  story with a different take coming shortly\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Hugo Lowell (@hugolowell) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hugolowell/status/1579530248990863360?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 10, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Bobb was one of two attorneys who are considered as potential witnesses or targets in the case, after the justice department alleged the Bobb and Evan Corcoran had lied about complying with a grand jury subpoena.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  will soon have more on this developing story.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/31/donald-trump-lawyers-christina-bobb-evan-corcoran"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Two Trump lawyers could be witnesses or targets in FBI investigation}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 Top White House adviser Jake Sullivan is set to talk about the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s national security strategy in a speech Wednesday at \uc2 Georgetown University\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 enltrNEW: Top Biden advisor {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JakeSullivan46?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @JakeSullivan46}}}\uc2  will discuss the administration's first National Security Strategy in a speech this Wed at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/georgetownsfs?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @georgetownsfs}}}\uc2 , followed by a moderated conversation w/ {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/OSullivanMeghan?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @OSullivanMeghan}}}\uc2 . Follow us and co-host {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CNASdc?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @CNASdc}}}\uc2  for live coverage! {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/YnOWyP64wL"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/YnOWyP64wL}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Georgetown SFS (@georgetownsfs) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/georgetownsfs/status/1579487652264710149?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 10, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 American presidents periodically release the document spelling out their security concerns and how they intend to deal with them. Biden {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/wp-content/uploads/2021/03/NSC-1v2.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 released an interim strategy last year}}}\uc2 , but was late getting the full report out because of Russia\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Ukraine, \uc2 The New York Times\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 enltrBiden\u8217\'20\'19s National Security Strategy is overdue. WH officials decided to rewrite a draft after Russia invaded Ukraine. They brought in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/thomaswright08?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @thomaswright08}}}\uc2  to oversee that. A main idea will be bolstering \u8220\'20\'1Cdemocratic resilience\u8221\'20\'1D in the US & abroad. Earlier story: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/6szm9K5cPh"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/6szm9K5cPh}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Lhm7C2Vu6U"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/Lhm7C2Vu6U}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Edward Wong (@ewong) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ewong/status/1579509381288587264?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 10, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 The GOP lawmakers poised to take over the House of Representatives in the upcoming midterm elections {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/10/midterm-election-jan-6-mccarthy-republicans-democrats-biden-latest?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-634430f98f083d981ab0ddcf#block-634430f98f083d981ab0ddcf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will investigate }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/10/midterm-election-jan-6-mccarthy-republicans-democrats-biden-latest?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-634430f98f083d981ab0ddcf#block-634430f98f083d981ab0ddcf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hunter Biden}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/10/midterm-election-jan-6-mccarthy-republicans-democrats-biden-latest?page=with:block-634418008f0825d5ecc79080#block-634418008f0825d5ecc79080"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 downplay January 6}}}\uc2 , according to recent interviews and the memoir of a police officer wounded in the insurrection. While it\u8217\'20\'19s a quiet day in Washington \u8211\'20\'13 where federal offices are shut for Columbus Day \u8211\'20\'13 candidates nationwide are scrambling to make their pitch to voters {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/10/midterm-election-jan-6-mccarthy-republicans-democrats-biden-latest?page=with:block-63441d1b8f0825d5ecc790c0#block-63441d1b8f0825d5ecc790c0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 before the 8 November polls}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what has happened today so far:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 In a column for the Guardian, Senator Bernie Sanders{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/10/midterm-election-jan-6-mccarthy-republicans-democrats-biden-latest?page=with:block-6344295f8f0834e330f6357f#block-6344295f8f0834e330f6357f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 warned Democrats of the perils}}}\uc2  of campaigning on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights alone.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/10/midterm-election-jan-6-mccarthy-republicans-democrats-biden-latest?page=with:block-6344446b8f0870981cb4f1f4#block-6344446b8f0870981cb4f1f4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 condemned Russia\u8217\'20\'19s missile strikes}}}\uc2  across a swath of Ukraine, including the capital Kyiv, and said the country has Washington\u8217\'20\'19s support.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Republican senator Tommy Tuberville{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/10/midterm-election-jan-6-mccarthy-republicans-democrats-biden-latest?page=with:block-63443ae98f0870981cb4f16e#block-63443ae98f0870981cb4f16e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 resorted to racism}}}\uc2  at a rally for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden condemns Russian strikes on Ukraine, says will support Kyiv 'for as long as it takes'\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has condemned Russia\u8217\'20\'19s missile strikes on a number of Ukrainian cities today, including the capital Kyiv, and said they reinforce America\u8217\'20\'19s commitment to help the country fend off Moscow\u8217\'20\'19s invasion.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s the full statement from the White House:\par \par \uc2 The United States strongly condemns Russia\u8217\'20\'19s missile strikes today across Ukraine, including in Kyiv. These attacks killed and injured civilians and destroyed targets with no military purpose. They once again demonstrate the utter brutality of Mr. Putin\u8217\'20\'19s illegal war on the Ukrainian people.\par \par \uc2 We offer our condolences to the families and loved ones of those who were senselessly killed today, as well as our best wishes for the recovery of those who were wounded. These attacks only further reinforce our commitment to stand with the people of Ukraine for as long as it takes. Alongside our allies and partners, we will continue to impose costs on Russia for its aggression, hold Putin and Russia accountable for its atrocities and war crimes, and provide the support necessary for Ukrainian forces to defend their country and their freedom. We again call on Russia to end this unprovoked aggression immediately and remove its troops from Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  has a separate live blog with the latest on the global reaction to today\u8217\'20\'19s attacks:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/oct/10/russia-ukraine-war-live-news-putin-russian-security-council-zaporizhzhia-nuclear-power-plant-hit-again-latest-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Russia-Ukraine war live: UN chief condemns \u8216\'20\'18unacceptable escalation\u8217\'20\'19 by Russia after deadly wave of missile strikes across Ukraine}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Another of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s allies is on trial in New York over charges he acted as an unregistered foreign agent for the United Arab Emirates in order to access its vast investment pool, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/j-oliver-conroy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 J Oliver Conroy}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTrump is the man,\u8221\'20\'1D Thomas \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Tom\u8221\'20\'1D Barrack\uc2 , a wealthy investor friend of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s, wrote to someone in a foreign government, in 2016, as Trump\u8217\'20\'19s likelihood of being named the Republican nominee for president began to become a certainty. Barrack added, cryptically, that someone called \u8220\'20\'1CHH\u8221\'20\'1D should be ready to travel.\par \par \uc2 The meaning of those words, and the intent behind them, are at the center of the latest court case to roil Trump\u8217\'20\'19s circle. Prosecutors have said that the \u8220\'20\'1CHH\u8221\'20\'1D in Barrack\u8217\'20\'19s email referred to His Highness Mohammed bin Zayed Al Nahyan, the current leader of the United Arab Emirates, and that Barrack was trying to secretly and illegally trade his access to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s ear for the graces of the Emirati government and its vast pool of investment money.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/10/trump-ally-tom-barrack-trial"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Trump is the man\u8217\'20\'19: trial paints a White House plagued by foreign influence}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republicans looking to win in the upcoming midterms have campaigned on high inflation and rising crime. But over the weekend, Alabama\u8217\'20\'19s Republican senator Tommy Tuberville resorted to another tactic: racism.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey want crime. They want crime because they want to take over what you got. They want to control what you have. They want reparations because they think the people that do the crime are owed that. Bullshit!\u8221\'20\'1D Tuberville declared in a speech on Saturday.\par \par \uc2 The word reparation is the give away here. In the context of American politics, it typically refers to the idea of financial compensation to African Americans for slavery and racial discrimination. Thus, Tuberville appears to say that Black Americans are \u8220\'20\'1Cthe people that do the crime.\u8221\'20\'1D CNN breaks it down here:\par \par \uc2 Tuberville is not standing for re-election this year, and won\u8217\'20\'19t face voters again until 2026. Instead, he was speaking at a rally for a politician who may well be on ballots across the country in two years time: \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jan/09/california-reparations-slavery-african-americans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18If not us, then who?\u8217\'20\'19: inside the landmark push for reparations for Black Californians}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 The contenders in one of November\u8217\'20\'19s most-watched Senate races will square off tonight in Ohio.\par \par \uc2 JD Vance, the Republican nominee for Senate, will face his Democratic opponent \uc2 Tim Ryan{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://fox8.com/news/the-stage-is-set-ryan-vance-to-debate-at-fox-8-tonight/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in a debate hosted by Fox 8 News}}}\uc2  and beginning at 7pm eastern time. Ohio has trended Republican in recent years, and the Trump-endorsed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/2022-election-forecast/senate/ohio/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Vance appears to have the edge in recent polls}}}\uc2 , though has struggled to establish a clear lead over Ryan.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/25/jd-vance-ohio-senate-race-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 JD Vance playing defense in unexpectedly close Ohio Senate race }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 GOP planning investigation of 'Biden family influence peddling' if they take House\par \par \uc2 If they win a majority in the House in the 8 November midterms, Republicans intend to make an investigation of \u8220\'20\'1CBiden family influence peddling\u8221\'20\'1D a priority next year, a top GOP lawmaker said today.\par \par \uc2 Kentucky lawmaker James Comer is the top Republican on the House oversight and reform committee, and in a Republican-led Congress would assume chairmanship of the panel that conducts investigations. In an interview on Fox Business. he made clear that an investigation into \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s son \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  would be announced very soon after the new legislative session begins in the new year:\par \par \uc2 enltrHunter Biden and the Biden Family have peddled influence across the globe to enrich themselves at the expense of American interests.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s clear that Joe was involved. The question is: to what extent?\par \par \uc2 We will get that answer for the American people. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MorningsMaria?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @MorningsMaria}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/HNgIwRQiZ9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/HNgIwRQiZ9}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rep. James Comer (@RepJamesComer) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepJamesComer/status/1579468458642837513?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 10, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  has been under federal investigation since 2018, and the GOP has long seized on his business dealings to try to paint his father as corrupt. Multiple media outlets reported last week that prosecutors believe they have evidence to charge \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  with crimes related to lying on a gun-purchase background check, and with not declaring all his foreign income.\par \par \uc2 The US attorney for Delaware, who was appointed by former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , will decide whether to proceed with a prosecution.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/07/hunter-biden-reports-say-fbi-has-enough-evidence-for-prosecution"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hunter Biden: reports say FBI has enough evidence for prosecution}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 Sanders is on to something. The state of the economy has been a determining factor in many elections, but as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/dominic-rushe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dominic Rushe}}}\uc2  reports from Phoenix, high inflation and rock-bottom unemployment have put the world\u8217\'20\'19s largest market in an unusually strange place right now:\par \par \uc2 In her back pocket, Ana Diaz carries a smooth grey pebble she calls her \u8220\'20\'1Cknock-knocker\u8221\'20\'1D. She uses it to get a loud rap on the front doors of the South Phoenix neighborhood where she is canvassing for the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats}}}\uc2  ahead of November\u8217\'20\'19s crucial midterm elections.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s 110F (43C) in the early afternoon sun, and Diaz is aiming to knock on 80 doors in this largely Latino neighborhood and speak to at least 20 people, encouraging them to vote. Diaz, a Los Angeles-based bartender and \uc2 Unite Here\uc2  union member, is a familiar face to many in this working-class area. In her T-shirt that reads \u8220\'20\'1CWorker power\u8221\'20\'1D she has been knocking on these doors since 2018.\par \par \uc2 Voters are all talking about the economy. Diaz, too, worries about inflation: her grocery bill is so high she thinks she may have to stop buying beef. But for her, the Democrats and good union jobs are the answer. \u8220\'20\'1CWhen we get together, we can make them change,\u8221\'20\'1D she says.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/10/arizona-midterms-crucial-senate-race"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 America\u8217\'20\'19s \u8216\'20\'18weird\u8217\'20\'19 economy isn\u8217\'20\'19t working \u8211\'20\'13 can Democrats convince voters they can fix it? }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senator Bernie Sanders has written a column for \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 , warning Democrats against campaigning exclusively on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the midterms, and arguing that Republicans have plenty of vulnerabilities to seize on when it comes to their view of the economy:\par \par \uc2 As someone who has a lifetime 100% pro-choice voting record, and is outraged by the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s horrific decision to overturn Roe v Wade, there is no question but that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats}}}\uc2  must continue to focus on the right of women to control their own bodies. This is a fight that most Americans want us to wage and, given the Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 extremist position on the issue, makes them genuinely vulnerable.\par \par \uc2 But, as we enter the final weeks of the 2022 midterm elections, I am alarmed to hear the advice that many Democratic candidates are getting from establishment consultants and directors of well-funded Super Pacs that the closing argument of Democrats should focus only on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Cut the 30-second \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ads and coast to victory.\par \par \uc2 I disagree. In my view, while the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  issue must remain on the front burner, it would be political malpractice for Democrats to ignore the state of the economy and allow Republican lies and distortions to go unanswered.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/commentisfree/2022/oct/10/democrats-midterms-victory-economy-bernie-sanders"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t focus only on \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  in the midterms. That\u8217\'20\'19s a mistake | Bernie Sanders}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 The details of Kevin McCarthy\u8217\'20\'19s recollection of January 6 come from Hold the Line: The Insurrection and One Cop\u8217\'20\'19s Battle for America\u8217\'20\'19s Soul, by \uc2 Michael Fanone\uc2 , a Washington DC police officer who responded to the Capitol as it was being attacked.\par \par \uc2 He\u8217\'20\'19s since left the city police force and become outspoken about the events of that day, and spoke to CBS News about his book set for release on Tuesday:\par \par \uc2 McCarthy isn\u8217\'20\'19t the only Republican the book cast in an unfavorable light. Fanone also recounts a bizarre remark senator \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2  made when they met:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2022/oct/07/trump-lindsey-graham-michael-fanone-capitol-rioters-shot-head-book"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump ally Lindsey Graham told ex-cop Capitol rioters should be shot in head}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 Spare a thought today for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/matthew-cantor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Matthew Cantor,}}}\uc2  who went on what must have been a tiring journey into the neediest corner of the Republican and Democratic parties:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIs your phone off, Patriot?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAre you still a Republican?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is getting SAD!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHOW MANY TIMES ARE WE GOING TO HAVE TO ASK?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The midterm elections are approaching, and political messaging teams are hard at work overwhelming inboxes across America. And while {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans}}}\uc2  and Democrats rely heavily on guilt trips to squeeze money out of voters, the language they employ is markedly different \u8211\'20\'13 and says a lot about what\u8217\'20\'19s wrong with each of them.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/09/republican-democrat-political-fundraising-emails"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18We\u8217\'20\'19re positively BEGGING you\u8217\'20\'19: how Republicans and Democrats demand money differently}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 But what are the midterms? \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/davidsmith"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 David Smith}}}\uc2  has all the answers you need about the 8 November elections that will decide control the House and Senate for the next two years:\par \par \uc2 American elections are like Olympics. Presidential votes happen every four years in step with the summer Games: 2020, 2016, 2012, 2008, 2004 and so on.\par \par \uc2 Midterms, meanwhile, happen every four years in line with the winter Games: 2022, 2018, 2014, 2010, 2006, 2002 and so on.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMidterms\u8221\'20\'1D is therefore an apt name because they take place halfway through a president\u8217\'20\'19s term of office. They are often regarded by pundits {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2022/08/27/midterms-trump-choice-sundaytake/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 as a referendum}}}\uc2  on the incumbent president.\par \par \uc2 Indeed, this year\u8217\'20\'19s midterms on 8 November will be voters\u8217\'20\'19 the first opportunity to render a national verdict on the presidency of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . But his name will not be on the ballot and other factors can come into play such as specific candidates, local dynamics or national issues.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/06/us-midterm-elections-explainer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 What are the US midterm elections and who\u8217\'20\'19s running?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 In the days after the January 6 insurrection, top House Republican Kevin McCarthy was ready to dump \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve had it with this guy,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, and pondered whether to ask him to resign, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/04/21/us/politics/trump-mitch-mcconnell-kevin-mccarthy.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the New York Times reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 It didn\u8217\'20\'19t take long for McCarthy\u8217\'20\'19s anger to subside. By the end of the month, he was with Trump at his Mar-a-Lago resort in Florida, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2021/01/28/politics/donald-trump-kevin-mccarthy-meeting/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 taking a picture together}}}\uc2  that made clear the now-former president was back on good terms with his party. While some Republicans never lost sight of the serious threat the January 6 insurrection posed to American democracy, many have since taken to downplaying the deadly attack on the Capitol, as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/10/10/politics/michael-fanone-kevin-mccarthy-january-6/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 today\u8217\'20\'19s CNN report}}}\uc2  about McCarthy\u8217\'20\'19s meeting with officers who fought the rioters makes clear.\par \par \uc2 Perhaps it was worth it for McCarthy and his party. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/2022-election-forecast/house/?cid=rrpromo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 They are favored}}}\uc2  to pick up the few seats necessary in the upcoming midterms to win a majority in Congress\u8217\'20\'19s lower chamber, putting McCarthy on track to be elected speaker.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 Poised to lead House, new book shows McCarthy denying reality of January 6\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. The United States has witnessed a bizarre spectacle over the past year and a half, as Republicans who were themselves in the Capitol when it was stormed by insurrectionists on January 6 try to downplay the severity of the attack. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/10/10/politics/michael-fanone-kevin-mccarthy-january-6/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN reports}}}\uc2  that Kevin McCarthy, the GOP leader in the House of Representatives who stands a good chance of becoming its speaker next year, told officers who fought with the mob that then-president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  had no idea it was his supporters causing the violence \u8211\'20\'13 even though he addressed them just prior to the attack. McCarthy has been an ardent supporter of the former president and his statement isn\u8217\'20\'19t much of a surprise, but the detail underscores the mental gymnastics Republicans are doing to avoid acknowledging what their embrace of Trump means for America.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is happening today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Not a ton! Why? Because it\u8217\'20\'19s Columbus Day, or Indigenous Peoples\u8217\'20\'19 Day, depending on which state you are in. It\u8217\'20\'19s a federal holiday, so many government offices are closed.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 United Nations General Assembly\uc2  will discuss Russia\u8217\'20\'19s annexation of four regions in Ukraine beginning at 3 pm eastern time, and vote on a resolution to condemn the move.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is coming back to the White House after spending the weekend in Delaware.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020221010eiaa001xm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
