\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Sanders warns Democrats not to focus solely on  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ahead of midterms\b0\par\par\uc2 Gloria Oladipo \par \uc2 553 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 October 2022\par 15:32 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Senator urges party to center campaign on economy, warning: \u8216\'20\'18You can\u8217\'20\'19t win elections unless you have support of working class\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 The Vermont senator Bernie Sanders warns that Democrats should not only focus on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights ahead of the midterm elections in November.\par \par \uc2 In an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/commentisfree/2022/oct/10/democrats-midterms-victory-economy-bernie-sanders"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 opinion column for the Guardian published on Monday}}}\uc2 , Sanders warned that Democrats need to embrace an agenda that addresses the economic woes facing America and supports the working class, not just one solely focused on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt would be political malpractice for Democrats to ignore the state of the economy and allow Republican lies and distortions to go unanswered,\u8221\'20\'1D said Sanders, adding that he \u8220\'20\'1Chas a lifetime 100% pro-choice voting record\u8221\'20\'1D and disapproves of the US {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision}}}\uc2  in June to eliminate federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections.\par \par \uc2 Sanders said that Democrats are recruiting \u8220\'20\'1Cconsultants and directors of well-funded Super Pacs\u8221\'20\'1D who urged their party to exclusively focus on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCut the 30-second \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ads and coast to victory,\u8221\'20\'1D wrote Sanders, who is an independent but votes with the Democrats.\par \par \uc2 But Sanders argued that Democrats also need to focus on countering \u8220\'20\'1Canti-worker\u8221\'20\'1D views from Republicans and ways that their policies could hurt the working class.\par \par \uc2 Sanders wrote: \u8220\'20\'1CNow is the time for Democrats to take the fight to the reactionary Republican party and expose their anti-worker views on the most important issues facing ordinary Americans.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Sanders highlighted stark economic inequality in the US. He noted that 60% of Americans live paycheck to paycheck and questioned if Republicans will legitimately address such issues by ending tax breaks, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/commentisfree/2021/feb/17/federal-minimum-wage-increase-moral-issue"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 raising the federal minimum wage}}}\uc2  or providing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2018/dec/11/universal-healthcare-could-save-america-trillions-whats-holding-us-back"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 universal healthcare}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIs there one Republican prepared to raise taxes on billionaires, or do they want to make a bad situation worse by extending Trump\u8217\'20\'19s tax breaks for the rich and repealing the estate tax?\u8221\'20\'1D Sanders wrote.\par \par \uc2 He added: \u8220\'20\'1CIs there one Republican in Congress who is prepared to raise the federal minimum wage to at least $15 an hour \u8230\'20\'26 Is there one Republican who believes that healthcare is a human right and supports universal coverage?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Sanders noted the importance of gaining the \u8220\'20\'1Csupport of working-class people\u8221\'20\'1D ahead of the November midterm elections, especially through actions like extending the child tax credit, increasing social security benefits and expanding Medicare coverage.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou can\u8217\'20\'19t win elections unless you have the support of the working class of this country,\u8221\'20\'1D Sanders wrote. \u8220\'20\'1CBut you\u8217\'20\'19re not going to have that support unless you make it clear that you\u8217\'20\'19re prepared to take on powerful special interests \u8211\'20\'13 and fight for the millions of Americans who are struggling economically.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Sanders concluded by promoting a multi-pronged agenda for the Democratic party to implement, one that includes addressing economic inequality and securing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf we close this critical midterm campaign with a clear, unified vision to meet the needs of working families, to take on corporate greed, and protect a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to choose, we will begin to rebuild the trust between Democrats in Washington and the working families of this country,\u8221\'20\'1D Sanders said. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd we\u8217\'20\'19ll win the election.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Democrats hope to preserve \u8211\'20\'13 or even widen \u8211\'20\'13 thin advantages in both congressional chambers these midterms.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020221010eiaa002e8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
