\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Ohio court blocks six-week  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ban indefinitely\b0\par\par\uc2 Maya Yang \par \uc2 461 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 October 2022\par 12:51 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 As litigation continues, abortions up to 22 weeks of pregnancy remain legal in state\par \par \uc2 The American Civil Liberties Union\uc2  and other \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights groups have won a ruling from a lower court in Ohio that has indefinitely blocked the state\u8217\'20\'19s ban on terminating pregnancies after six weeks.\par \par \uc2 In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.acluohio.org/en/press-releases/ohio-lower-court-grant-preliminary-injunction-six-week-abortion-ban-will-remain"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2  released on Friday, the \uc2 ACLU\uc2  announced that Judge Christian Jenkins of the Hamilton county court of common pleas said that it would grant \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers\u8217\'20\'19 and advocates\u8217\'20\'19 request for a preliminary injunction against Ohio\u8217\'20\'19s senate bill 23 (SB 23), a law that prohibits abortions starting at roughly a month and a half of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 The law has three {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ohioattorneygeneral.gov/Files/Briefing-Room/News-Releases/Heartbeat-Law-Explainer.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 exceptions}}}\uc2  : to prevent the death of the mother; when there is serious risk of \u8220\'20\'1Csubstantial and irreversible impairment of a major bodily function of the pregnant mother\u8221\'20\'1D; and in cases of ectopic pregnancies.\par \par \uc2 In the meantime, as litigation over the ban continues, abortions up to 22 weeks of pregnancy remain legal in Ohio.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights groups and women\u8217\'20\'19s health centers, including Planned Parenthood and Preterm-Cleveland, hailed the court\u8217\'20\'19s decision, calling it a \u8220\'20\'1Cmajor victory\u8221\'20\'1D. The injunction comes after a temporary restraining order that had blocked the state\u8217\'20\'19s ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after six weeks but could have been removed at the time of Friday\u8217\'20\'19s ruling.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are thrilled \u8230\'20\'26 and relieved that patients in Ohio can continue to access \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as we work to fight this unjust and dangerous ban in court,\u8221\'20\'1D the groups said in a joint statement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe preliminary injunction will be in place for the duration of our case, which means abortions will be legal in Ohio for a period much, much longer than the temporary restraining order granted. This court ruling will provide significant relief to Ohio patients and clinics.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The groups said that they were focused on securing a permanent injunction from the court.\par \par \uc2 Last month, Jenkins wrote in the temporary restraining order that the law would result in \u8220\'20\'1Cirreparable harm\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe record is replete with evidence of women who have suffered and whose health has been placed in jeopardy as a result of SB 23,\u8221\'20\'1D he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fox19.com/2022/09/14/hamilton-county-judge-grants-restraining-order-against-ohios-abortion-ban/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said.}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSB 23 clearly discriminates against pregnant women and places an enormous burden on them to secure safe and effective healthcare such that it violates Ohio\u8217\'20\'19s Equal Protection and Benefit Clause and is therefore unconstitutional.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s conservative majority voted in June to eliminate the federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights the landmark case Roe v Wade established in 1973. That left each state to decide whether to prohibit \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in their jurisdictions.\par \par \uc2 Since then, more than 26 states have prohibited or severely limited access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , or were expected to do so.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020221007eia7003bh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
