\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18We won\u8217\'20\'19t be intimidated by Putin\u8217\'20\'19s rhetoric,\u8217\'20\'19 says White House after Biden\u8217\'20\'19s \u8216\'20\'18Armageddon\u8217\'20\'19 warning \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein \par \uc2 5,226 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 October 2022\par 20:12 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18We have not seen any reason to adjust our own nuclear posture,\u8217\'20\'19 says press secretary Sign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/07/biden-putin-russia-nuclear-weapons-ukraine-midterm-elections-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-634023448f085c150750f8f5#block-634023448f085c150750f8f5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 issued a dire warning}}}\uc2  about \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s willingness to use nuclear weapons in Ukraine, and warned that if such weapons are deployed, \u8220\'20\'1Carmageddon\u8221\'20\'1D would follow. The White House said the president\u8217\'20\'19s comments weren\u8217\'20\'19t based on any new intelligence or signs that such an attack might happen soon, but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/07/biden-putin-russia-nuclear-weapons-ukraine-midterm-elections-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-63404fae8f085c150750fbf7#block-63404fae8f085c150750fbf7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rather an indication of how seriously the administration takes such threats}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else happened today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 September was another decent month of job growth, though there were signs of weakness in the US labor market, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/07/biden-putin-russia-nuclear-weapons-ukraine-midterm-elections-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-63402e7b8f088272fbb9d771#block-63402e7b8f088272fbb9d771"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to new government data}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The White House press secretary{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/07/biden-putin-russia-nuclear-weapons-ukraine-midterm-elections-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-634058948f085c150750fc81#block-634058948f085c150750fc81"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 declined to comment}}}\uc2  on reports that prosecutors believe they have enough evidence to charge the president\u8217\'20\'19s son \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  with crimes related to lying on a firearm purchase background check and not reporting all his income.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s student debt relief plan survived {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/07/biden-putin-russia-nuclear-weapons-ukraine-midterm-elections-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-634031d18f088272fbb9d7bf#block-634031d18f088272fbb9d7bf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 another court challenge}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2 , the Republican Senate candidate in Georgia, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/07/biden-putin-russia-nuclear-weapons-ukraine-midterm-elections-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-634077108f08e561623cb514#block-634077108f08e561623cb514"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fired a top staffer}}}\uc2  amid revelations Walker paid for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  despite his hardline stance against the procedure.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has issued a statement of congratulations to the winners of this year\u8217\'20\'19s Nobel Peace prize, which went to rights activists in Russia, Ukraine and Belarus.\par \par \uc2 The decision was seen as a repudiation of Russian president \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 . Here\u8217\'20\'19s what Biden\u8217\'20\'19s had to say:\par \par \uc2 This year\u8217\'20\'19s Nobel Peace Prize winners remind us that, even in dark days of war, in the face of intimidation and oppression, the common human desire for rights and dignity cannot be extinguished. On behalf of the American people, I congratulate Ales Bialiatski of Belarus, Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s Center for Civil Liberties, and the Russian organization Memorial on this deserved honor.\par \par \uc2 For years, they have tirelessly fought for human rights and fundamental freedoms\u8212\'20\'14including the right to speak freely and criticize openly. They have pursued their mission with passion and persistence. Throughout its history, Memorial has revealed the truth about the abuse of Soviet and Russian citizens, despite intense intimidation. Ales Bialiatski has never backed down from demanding the democratic freedoms the Belarusian people deserve, even while imprisoned. And, in the midst of Russia\u8217\'20\'19s brutal and unprovoked war against Ukraine, the Center for Civil Liberties is documenting in real time the war crimes and atrocities Russia is inflicting on the Ukrainian people. Above all, the brave souls who do this work have pursued the truth and documented for the world the political repression of their fellow citizens\u8212\'20\'14speaking out, standing up, and staying the course while being threatened by those who seek their silence. In doing so, they have made our world stronger. Ales Bialiatski, the Center for Civil Liberties, and Memorial deserve to be recognized for the work they have done, the example they have set, and the hope they inspire for a better future through their unwavering dedication to fundamental freedoms.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/oct/07/nobel-peace-prize-given-to-human-rights-activists-in-belarus-russia-and-ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nobel peace prize given to human rights activists in Belarus, Russia and Ukraine}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 In other Senate news, \uc2 Marco Rubio\uc2 , a Republican representing Florida who is up for re-election this year, has found himself in a feud with a drag queen, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/coral-murphy-marcos"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coral Murphy Marcos}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 A drag queen called the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/florida"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Florida}}}\uc2  senator \uc2 Marco Rubio\uc2  a bigot, after the Republican included her in a campaign ad in which he attacked \u8220\'20\'1Cthe radical left\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Lil Miss Hot Mess, who performs in Los Angeles, responded to Rubio in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://fb.watch/f-Q-cePfbZ/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 video}}}\uc2  after he used footage of her reading to children during {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/culture/2022/sep/28/drag-queen-story-hour-book-store-montana"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Drag Queen Story Hour}}}\uc2 , a children\u8217\'20\'19s program that started in 2015.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI have one question for \uc2 Marco Rubio\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Lil Miss Hot Mess said in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/glaad/status/1577687240242782210?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw%7Ctwcamp%5Etweetembed%7Ctwterm%5E1577687240242782210%7Ctwgr%5E8512eb2e77c25f98bf8875d9c4ed02b4690f8bae%7Ctwcon%5Es1_&ref_url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.advocate.com%2Fpolitics%2F2022%2F10%2F05%2Fdrag-queen-asks-why-marco-rubio-obsessed-her"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 video}}}\uc2  released by Glaad, an LGBTQ+ advocacy group.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhy are you so obsessed with me and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/culture/drag"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Drag}}}\uc2  Story Hour? We\u8217\'20\'19re simply out here reading books to children, encouraging them to use their imagination to envision a more just and fabulous world.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/07/marco-rubio-drag-queen-little-miss-hot-mess-ad"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Drag queen featured in Marco Rubio campaign ad calls him a bigot}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republican Georgia senate candidate fires top staffer amid \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  uproar\par \par \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2 , the Republican senate candidate in Georgia, has fired his campaign\u8217\'20\'19s political director, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/10/07/politics/herschel-walker-taylor-crowe-georgia-senate/index.html?utm_content=2022-10-07T16%3A14%3A07&utm_term=link&utm_source=twCNNp&utm_medium=social"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to CNN}}}\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 The decision came after The Daily Beast reported Walker, who backs banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide without exceptions, paid for the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  of a woman who he later had another child with. The Georgia senate race in which Walker is trying to unseat Democrat \uc2 Raphael Warnock\uc2  is seen as crucial to controlling Congress\u8217\'20\'19s upper chamber, but many high-profile Republicans continue to support Walker, despite the revelations.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from CNN:\par \par \uc2 The departure of Taylor Crowe, who previously held the same role on ex-GOP Sen. \uc2 David Perdue\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s failed bid for Georgia governor this year, comes just weeks before Election Day in the crucial Senate contest against Democratic incumbent \uc2 Raphael Warnock\uc2 . With an evenly split Senate, Republicans are hoping to flip the Georgia seat as they look to take control of the chamber.\par \par \uc2 Two people familiar with the matter said Crowe was fired after suspected leaking to members of the media. It is unclear if there were any other factors at play.\par \par \uc2 Walker campaign manager Scott Paradise declined to comment when reached by CNN on Friday. Crowe himself did not respond to multiple requests for comment.\par \par \uc2 CNN has not been able to independently verify the allegation against Walker, who has repeatedly denied that he ever paid for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/07/herschel-walker-republicans-abortion-denial"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans throw support behind Herschel Walker after \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  denial}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 The White House has hit out at a bill {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.lankford.senate.gov/news/press-releases/lankford-wants-to-roll-back-government-price-controls-on-prescription-drugs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 proposed by Republican senators }}}\uc2  to roll back provisions of an August spending measure that are projected to reduce both the US budget deficit and prescription drug prices for people who receive health insurance through the government.\par \par \uc2 The ability for the Medicare and Medicaid programs to negotiate drug prices was a change long sought by Democrats, and included in the Inflation Reduction Act spending bill \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  signed in August. Yesterday, Republican senators \uc2 James Lankford\uc2  and \uc2 Mike Lee\uc2  introduced a bill to repeal that ability, arguing it \u8220\'20\'1Ccreates even more barriers to effectively bringing down the cost of prescriptions, particularly for senior adults on Medicare.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  had to say about that:\par \par \uc2 Today, MAGA Congressional Republicans introduced legislation that puts special interests before working families. Their new bill is a giveaway to big pharma at the expense of seniors by ending Medicare\u8217\'20\'19s new ability to negotiate lower drug prices. Their vision for the country is extreme and out of touch with working families across the country.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 What could a Russian tactical strike look like and how would the US respond?\par \par \uc2 Julian Borger, our world affairs editor, writes from Washington\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 The past week has seen a rapid escalation in nuclear rhetoric, beginning with \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s threat to use \u8220\'20\'1Call forces and means\u8221\'20\'1D to defend newly seized territory in Ukraine and ending with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s warning of \u8220\'20\'1CArmageddon\u8221\'20\'1D if Russia crosses the nuclear Rubicon.\par \par \uc2 However, the realities underlying the menacing vocabulary are a far greyer area than the bluster suggests. It is far from certain that Putin would be prepared to be the first leader to use nuclear weapons in wartime since 1945, over his territorial ambitions in Ukraine. If his primary goal is to stay in power, that could be exactly the wrong way of going about it.\par \par \uc2 Even if he did issue the launch order, he has no guarantee it would be carried out. Nor can he be absolutely sure that the weapons and their delivery systems would work.\par \par \uc2 On the US side, despite \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s apocalyptic language at a private fundraiser on Thursday night, it is not at all inevitable that Washington would respond to Putin\u8217\'20\'19s nuclear use with nuclear retaliation. Past wargaming suggests there would be vigorous debate within the administration to say the least.\par \par \uc2 Full story:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/oct/07/biden-putin-nuclear-threats-tactical-strike-us-response-analysis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Are Putin\u8217\'20\'19s nuclear threats really likely to lead to Armageddon?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 NBC News reports that the Republican Nebraska senator \uc2 Ben Sasse\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s imminent departure from Congress to be president of the University of the Florida, first reported on Thursday, is the result of high-level Republican rivalries.\par \par \uc2 Ben Sasse\uc2 . Photograph: Michael Reynolds/\uc2 EPA\par \par \uc2 Quoting \u8220\'20\'1Ca top Republican insider\u8221\'20\'1D, NBC says the Florida governor, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , was behind the move, which was meant as one in the eye for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Marc Caputo, an NBC reporter, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MarcACaputo/status/1578130487968759812"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 writes}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CIn May, Trump said he regretted supporting \uc2 Ben Sasse\uc2 . Now, DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s man at UF has engineered Sasse\u8217\'20\'19s hiring. \u8216\'20\'18Everyone knows what this is about: Ron and Don,\u8217\'20\'19 a top Republican insider tells me, echoing others.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 As the only Republican who polls even close to Trump, DeSantis is widely thought to be planning a presidential run of his own.\par \par \uc2 There could be another angle to Sasse\u8217\'20\'19s move.\par \par \uc2 Pete Ricketts\uc2 , the Republican Nebraska governor, will appoint a replacement for Sasse, should he join UF as expected and resign before January, when a new governor will be in place.\par \par \uc2 On Friday, in messages viewed by the Guardian, a Trump insider said the Sasse move was \u8220\'20\'1Cabout Ricketts money to DeSantis. This is what Pete wanted so he can appoint himself to the Senate.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for Ricketts did not immediately respond to a request for comment.\par \par \uc2 Full story:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/07/senate-republican-ben-sasse-depart-washington-university-florida"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ben Sasse, Republican who voted to convict Trump, to depart Congress}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 In Hagerstown, Maryland, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has delivered a long attack on Republican policies on taxation, spending, healthcare, drugs prices and benefits including social security and Medicare. The midterm elections are just a month away, after all.\par \par \uc2 He singles out \uc2 Paul Gosar\uc2 , a far-right Arizona Republican who has slammed Biden\u8217\'20\'19s agenda as \u8220\'20\'1Csocialist\u8221\'20\'1D but, Biden says, has asked for federal spending in his district. Biden asks, who\u8217\'20\'19s the socialist there?\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI was surprised to see so many socialists in the Republican caucus,\u8221\'20\'1D he adds.\par \par \uc2 Biden says: \u8220\'20\'1CWhen it comes to the next Congress, it\u8217\'20\'19s not a referendum. It\u8217\'20\'19s a choice, a choice between two very different ways of looking at the economy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He repeatedly decries \u8220\'20\'1Ctrickle-down economics\u8221\'20\'1D, the notion that tax cuts for the rich will benefit everyone else, so central to the current \uc2 British government\uc2  under \uc2 Liz Truss\uc2 , of course.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  speaks in Hagerstown, Maryland. Photograph: Elizabeth Frantz/Reuters\par \par \uc2 Biden also decries Republican election denial, among those who claim he stole the 2020 election from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , but says he has \u8220\'20\'1Cnever been more optimistic about America\u8217\'20\'19s prospects\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Raising his voice, he insists there is \u8220\'20\'1Cnothing, nothing we\u8217\'20\'19ve ever set our mind to that we have not been able to do\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Music, applause \u8230\'20\'26 and scene.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden speaks on jobs, the economy and more\par \par \uc2 In Hagerstown, Maryland, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has hailed this morning\u8217\'20\'19s jobs numbers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re proving that our best days are ahead of us, not behind us. Just look at today\u8217\'20\'19s jobs report. Our economy created 263,000 jobs last month \u8211\'20\'13 that\u8217\'20\'19s 10 million jobs since I\u8217\'20\'19ve come into office. That\u8217\'20\'19s the fastest job growth at any point of any president in American history. Historic progress.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe unemployment rate remains at historic lows: 3.5% unemployment. That includes the lowest unemployment among Hispanic Americans ever in the history of this country, the second-lowest employment among Black teenagers.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The president does adds a nod to expectations of a slowdown in jobs numbers soon: \u8220\'20\'1COur jobs recovery will cool while still powering our recovery.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Our business editor, Dominic Rushe, has more on such concerns:\par \par \uc2 According to career services firm {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.challengergray.com/blog/job-cuts-surge-46-in-september-2022-up-68-from-same-month-last-year-september-hiring-intentions-fall-to-lowest-level-since-2011/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Challenger, Gray & Christmas}}}\uc2 , it was the fifth month this year that job cuts were higher than the corresponding month in 2021. \uc2 Challenger\uc2  also reported a sharp slowdown in hiring intentions, with employers announcing in September that they planned to take on 380,014 workers, the lowest September total since 2011.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSome cracks are beginning to appear in the labor market. Hiring is slowing and downsizing events are beginning to occur,\u8221\'20\'1D senior vice-president Andrew Challenger said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe cooling housing market and Fed\u8217\'20\'19s rate hikes are leading to job cuts among mortgage staff at banks and lenders. The recession concerns are leading to increased uncertainty, and companies across sectors are beginning to reassess staffing needs.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2022/oct/07/us-jobs-report-september-unemployment-rate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US employers added 263,000 new jobs in September as \u8216\'20\'18cracks\u8217\'20\'19 appear in labor market}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is now speaking in Hagerstown, Maryland, where he is visiting Volvo Group Powertrain Operations to talk about unions, jobs and other pressing pre-midterms priorities. Of course, a lot of minds are on what he said yesterday in New York, about Russia, the threat of nuclear war and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/07/biden-warns-world-would-face-armageddon-if-putin-uses-a-tactical-nuclear-weapon-in-ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the possibility of \u8220\'20\'1CArmageddon\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m a union guy,\u8221\'20\'1D he says in Hagerstown, also branding himself the most \u8220\'20\'1Cpro-union president American history\u8221\'20\'1D, dedicated to the \u8220\'20\'1Csingle best workers in the world\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll keep listening, of course.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/07/biden-putin-russia-nuclear-weapons-ukraine-midterm-elections-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-634023448f085c150750f8f5#block-634023448f085c150750f8f5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 issued a dire warning}}}\uc2  about \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s willingness to use nuclear weapons in Ukraine, and warned that if such weapons are deployed, \u8220\'20\'1Carmageddon\u8221\'20\'1D would follow. The White House said the president\u8217\'20\'19s comments weren\u8217\'20\'19t based on any new intelligence or signs that such an attack might happen soon, but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/07/biden-putin-russia-nuclear-weapons-ukraine-midterm-elections-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-63404fae8f085c150750fbf7#block-63404fae8f085c150750fbf7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rather an indication of how seriously the administration takes such threats}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is going on today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 September was another decent month of job growth, though there were signs of weakness in the US labor market, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/07/biden-putin-russia-nuclear-weapons-ukraine-midterm-elections-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-63402e7b8f088272fbb9d771#block-63402e7b8f088272fbb9d771"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to new government data}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The White House press secretary{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/07/biden-putin-russia-nuclear-weapons-ukraine-midterm-elections-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-634058948f085c150750fc81#block-634058948f085c150750fc81"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 declined to comment}}}\uc2  on reports that prosecutors believe they have enough evidence to charge the president\u8217\'20\'19s son \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  with crimes related to lying on a firearm purchase background check and not reporting all his income.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s student debt relief plan survived {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/07/biden-putin-russia-nuclear-weapons-ukraine-midterm-elections-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-634031d18f088272fbb9d7bf#block-634031d18f088272fbb9d7bf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 another court challenge}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 The White House press secretary had less to say about the reports published yesterday and today revealing that federal investigators believe they have enough evidence to bring charges against \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s son, \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is an ongoing investigation being handled independently by the department of justice so I would refer you to the department of justice,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  replied when asked about the reports.\par \par \uc2 Republicans have long tried to use the allegations of wrongdoing by \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  to paint the president as corrupt. During his administration, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  pressured Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s president \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2  to investigate both Joe and \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s business dealings in the country to hurt the former\u8217\'20\'19s presidential prospects, leading Democrats to impeach Trump in 2020.\par \par \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  has been under investigation since 2018, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/national-security/2022/10/06/hunter-biden-tax-gun-charges/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Washington Post}}}\uc2  along with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/10/06/politics/hunter-biden-investigation-federal-prosecutors-weighing-charges/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/hunter-biden-case-decision-paused-amid-discussions-between-defense-lawyers-and-prosecutors-11665094544?mod=Searchresults_pos1&page=1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Wall Street Journal}}}\uc2  say that prosectors believe they have the evidence to charge \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  with crimes related to lying on a background check for purchasing a firearm, and for not reporting all of his foreign income. A Trump-appointed US attorney in Delaware will ultimately make a decision on whether or not to bring a case against the president\u8217\'20\'19s son.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s remarks last night weren\u8217\'20\'19t based on any new intelligence, but rather a reinforcement of what Washington officials have been saying publicly in response to Putin\u8217\'20\'19s threats using nuclear weapons, White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe president\u8230\'20\'26 has been a very consistent. He was reinforcing what we have been saying, which is how seriously\u8230\'20\'26 we take these threats about nuclear weapons as we have done when the Russians have made these threats throughout the conflict,\u8221\'20\'1D Jean-Pierre said aboard Air Force One. \u8220\'20\'1CSo the kind of irresponsible rhetoric we have seen is no way for the leader of a nuclear-armed state to speak, and that\u8217\'20\'19s what the President was making very clear.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 As Biden did in remarks to Democratic donors last night, Jean-Pierre also brought up the Cuban Missile Crisis, when the Soviet Union and the United States came perilously close to nuclear conflict in 1962. \u8220\'20\'1CIf the Cuban missile crisis has taught us anything, it is the value of reducing nuclear risk and not brandishing it,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 'We won't be intimidated by Putin's rhetoric': White House\par \par \uc2 Russia\u8217\'20\'19s use of a nuclear weapon in Ukraine would cause \u8220\'20\'1Cunintended consequences\u8221\'20\'1D for Moscow, the White House press secretary said, while noting there\u8217\'20\'19s no evidence yet that president \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  intends to use his atomic arsenal.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRussia\u8217\'20\'19s talk of using nuclear weapons is irresponsible, and there\u8217\'20\'19s no way to use to use them without unintended consequences. It cannot happen\u8230\'20\'26 We won\u8217\'20\'19t be intimidated by Putin\u8217\'20\'19s rhetoric,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  told reporters aboard Air Force One during president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s short flight to Hagerstown, Maryland, where he is to speak about the economy.\par \par \uc2 She downplayed the possibility that the first use of a nuclear weapon in war since 1945 was imminent.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have not seen any reason to adjust our own nuclear posture, nor do we have indications they are preparing to use them, but Putin can de-escalate this at any time and there is no reason to escalate.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She did not comment directly on Biden\u8217\'20\'19s prediction last night that Russia\u8217\'20\'19s use of a nuclear weapon would cause \u8220\'20\'1CArmageddon\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden isn\u8217\'20\'19t the only leader whose comments about Russia are grabbing headlines today.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s Finland\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister \uc2 Sanna Marin\uc2  wasting no words on how the war in Ukraine should end:\par \par \uc2 enltrFinnish prime minister \uc2 Sanna Marin\uc2  was asked about a potential off-ramp for Russia to end the war in Ukraine. Her reply: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/VblWxkMuFc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/VblWxkMuFc}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rikhard Husu (@RikhardHusu) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RikhardHusu/status/1578308226709590017?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 7, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 As he set off from the White House on yet another lengthy day of travel, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  gave the press no opportunity to ask about his \u8220\'20\'1Carmageddon\u8221\'20\'1D comment.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s from \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/davidsmith"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 David Smith}}}\uc2 , who\u8217\'20\'19s covering the president\u8217\'20\'19s departure. Biden is en route now to Hagerstown, Maryland, where he\u8217\'20\'19ll speak about the economy, before flying to Philadelphia and finally Wilmington, Delaware, where he is to spend the weekend.\par \par \uc2 Press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  will take questions from reporters on Air Force One during the flight to Hagerstown, so we may find out more about the White House\u8217\'20\'19s view of Russia\u8217\'20\'19s intentions.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden 'armageddon' remark not driven by new intelligence: White House\par \par \uc2 US president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s remark last night that Russian president \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  was serious about using nuclear weapons in Ukraine and that doing so would risk \u8220\'20\'1Carmageddon\u8221\'20\'1D was not based on any new intelligence, Semafor reports.\par \par \uc2 The president\u8217\'20\'19s dire assessment of the risk of nuclear war \u8211\'20\'13 which he said was at its highest level since the Cuban Missile Crisis 60 years ago - was instead a reflection of Washington\u8217\'20\'19s seriousness when it comes to Putin\u8217\'20\'19s increasingly strident rhetoric, a White House official said:\par \par \uc2 enltrA WH official says of Biden comments on Putin at DNC reception last night: "The President\u8217\'20\'19s comments reinforce how seriously we take these threats about nuclear weapons \u8211\'20\'13 as we have done when the Russians have made these threats throughout the conflict."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Morgan Chalfant (@mchalfant16) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mchalfant16/status/1578402605105119232?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 7, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltr"The kind of irresponsible rhetoric we have seen is no way for the leader of a nuclear armed state to speak," official says.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Morgan Chalfant (@mchalfant16) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mchalfant16/status/1578402644225400832?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 7, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrI'm told no new assessment drove his comments.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Morgan Chalfant (@mchalfant16) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mchalfant16/status/1578402925373685761?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 7, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 Democrats are sounding the alarm about their fundraising numbers ahead of the 8 November midterms, \uc2 The Washington Post\uc2  reports.\par \par \uc2 While candidates have spent hundreds of millions of dollars in their bid to retain their majority in the House of Representatives, Republicans are outspending them in areas where Democrats are vulnerable, and have shown more flexibility in getting dollars to pay for television advertisements and other campaign tactics in races that need them most.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2022/10/07/house-democrats-fundraising/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 from the Post}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Top Democratic strategists have concluded that they lack the funds needed to fully contest all of their potentially winnable House races this cycle, people familiar with the situation said, forcing tough decisions about where to spend on television ads as Republican outside groups flood the airwaves.\par \par \uc2 The relative shortfall in outside spending is likely to leave some Democratic incumbents in contested races at sharp advertising disadvantages, while restricting the party\u8217\'20\'19s ability to compete in open seats or to unseat Republican incumbents, these people said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere are places that I don\u8217\'20\'19t know if we are going to be able to get to,\u8221\'20\'1D said Tim Persico, the executive director of the Democratic Congressional Campaign Committee. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s just money. They have billionaires and corporations stepping up with big checks and we just don\u8217\'20\'19t have the same type of support. We are just getting outspent everywhere, so it is just a question of how much can we withstand.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Democrats pointed to a TV ad spending advantage by Republican outside groups, which have the flexibility to move money around the House landscape strategically in the final weeks. That edge has become more alarming as a recent shift in the national mood has put more seats in contention for Democrats, who find themselves hamstrung by the Republican advantage in donors on the GOP side.\par \par \uc2 Another House Democratic strategist said the inability to fully fund key races could prove to be the difference between winning and losing control of Congress, or between keeping Republicans to a five-seat majority and a 15-seat majority. \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t think it is hyperbole to say at this point that money is going to make the difference,\u8221\'20\'1D said this person, who like others spoke on the condition of anonymity to talk more freely about strategy.\par \par \uc2 Democrats are not favored by nonpartisan analysts to hold the House this cycle, because of the narrow majority they now enjoy and the historical head winds that the president\u8217\'20\'19s party typically faces in his first midterm elections. But some Democrats feel their chances of winning have risen in recent months, given a summer spike in Democratic enthusiasm after the Supreme Court\u8217\'20\'19s decision to overturn the ruling establishing a constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and a recent uptick in President Biden\u8217\'20\'19s approval rating.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 Either explicitly or implicitly, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be on the ballots many Americans receive in the 8 November midterms. Will advocates of the procedure see a repeat of the success they had in Kansas, where they successfully kept \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  legal in a deeply red state? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/poppy-noor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Poppy Noor}}}\uc2  digs into the issue:\par \par \uc2 When Kansans voted overwhelmingly to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  this summer, the 59-41 referendum margin in the deep-red state sent shockwaves through the country, inspiring pro-choice advocates and sending anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  campaigners scrambling for an unexpected political dogfight as five similar ballot initiatives approach in November.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  referendums \u8211\'20\'13 in Kentucky, Montana, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/california"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 California}}}\uc2 , Vermont and Michigan \u8211\'20\'13 have seen both sides organize extensive campaigns.\par \par \uc2 In Kentucky and Montana, red like {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kansas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kansas}}}\uc2 , it was Republicans and anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  advocates who brought the initiatives with the aim of removing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections from state constitutions.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/07/abortion-votes-america-kansas-kentucky-california-michigan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 More \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  votes across US \u8211\'20\'13 can Kansas inspire another pro-choice win?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 As he often does with a healthy jobs report, Biden cheered the latest data as a sign that the economy is performing well under his watch:\par \par \uc2 enltrToday's jobs numbers are an encouraging sign that we are transitioning to stable, steady growth. And more Americans are working than ever before.\par \par \uc2 There's more to do to grow our economy from the bottom up and middle out, but we're making progress.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 President Biden (@POTUS) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS/status/1578389938697113600?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 7, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 If you read between the lines, the \u8220\'20\'1Cstable, steady growth\u8221\'20\'1D Biden is referring to is more aspiration than reality at the moment. Inflation remains high in the United States, though is believed to be poised to decline in the months ahead. Meanwhile, government data showed negative growth in the previous two quarters, raising fears of a recession. But that dynamic may also reverse in the final quarters of the year \u8211\'20\'13 creating the type of economic conditions Biden hopes revive his sagging popularity among American voters.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s plan to cancel some student debt has survived in court \u8211\'20\'13 again.\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press reports that a federal judge in Wisconsin has dismissed a lawsuit from a taxpayer group trying to stop the measure that would cancel as much as $20,000 in student loans for millions of borrowers.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from the AP:\par \par \uc2 The Brown County Taxpayers Association argued that Biden\u8217\'20\'19s order unlawfully circumvented Congress\u8217\'20\'19 power over spending. They also argued the plan was discriminatory by seeking to give particular help to borrowers of color.\par \par \uc2 U.S. District Judge William Griesbach, an appointee of President \uc2 George W. Bush\uc2 , tossed the case Thursday, writing that the group does not have standing to challenge the plan simply because they are taxpayers.\par \par \uc2 Biden enacted the debt relief plan under the HEROES Act, which was passed after the Sept. 11 attacks sparked an American-led military campaign aimed at terrorism. The act gave the executive branch authority to forgive student loan debt in association with military operations or national emergencies.\par \par \uc2 The president cited COVID-19 as reason to invoke the act. The lawsuit, filed by the conservative Wisconsin Institute for Law and \uc2 Liberty\uc2  on behalf of the taxpayers group, had argued it was an overextension of executive power that improperly sidestepped Congress.\par \par \uc2 A libertarian group last month sued over the plan in Indiana, but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/biden-health-lawsuits-covid-missouri-862d783188de45b698c54b00820d3616"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the AP reports a judge declined to block the White House proposal}}}\uc2  and told the plaintiffs to resubmit their argument.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/24/joe-biden-us-student-loan-debt-cancellation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden unveils plan to cancel $10,000 in student loan debt for millions}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 Government data released this morning confirmed that the US labor market remains strong \u8211\'20\'13 but perhaps not that strong. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/dominic-rushe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dominic Rushe}}}\uc2  dove into the numbers and tells us what he found:\par \par \uc2 US employers added 263,000 new jobs in September as the unemployment rate dipped to 3.5%, the \uc2 Bureau of Labor Statistics\uc2  announced on Friday.\par \par \uc2 The jobs market has shown signs of slowing recently after regaining all the jobs that were lost during the pandemic. September\u8217\'20\'19s gain was down from the 315,000 jobs added in August and far lower than the 420,000 average monthly gain thus far in 2022. But growth has remained robust despite rising interest rates and growing fears of a recession.\par \par \uc2 How long the job market can maintain its current trajectory is unknown. The \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  blames the current cost of living crisis in part on a tight labor market and rising wages and has signaled it would like to see hiring fall, and unemployment rise, as it seeks to tamp down inflation.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2022/oct/07/us-jobs-report-september-unemployment-rate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US employers added 263,000 new jobs in September as \u8216\'20\'18cracks\u8217\'20\'19 appear in labor market}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 Even after the \uc2 FBI\uc2  searched his Mar-a-Lago resort in August, \uc2 The New York Times\uc2  reports that investigators are skeptical that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has turned over all the government documents in his possession. Here\u8217\'20\'19s the latest on the saga from \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/martin-pengelly"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Martin Pengelly}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US Department of Justice\uc2  has told lawyers for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  it thinks he has not handed back all the documents he took from the White House, the \uc2 New York Times{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/10/06/us/politics/trump-white-house-documents-lawyers.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The paper said Jay Bratt, the DoJ head of counterintelligence operations, communicated with lawyers for Trump \u8220\'20\'1Cin recent weeks\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The news, the Times said, is \u8220\'20\'1Cthe most concrete indication yet that investigators remain skeptical that Mr Trump has been fully cooperative in their efforts to recover documents \u8230\'20\'26 supposed to have [been] turned over to the National Archives at the end of his term\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Laurence Tribe, a Harvard law professor, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/tribelaw/status/1578170827593420801"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  the news \u8220\'20\'1Clooks like a major step toward an indictment of Trump by DoJ for obstruction of justice\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/07/us-justice-department-says-trump-didnt-turn-over-all-documents-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US justice department says Trump didn\u8217\'20\'19t turn over all documents \u8211\'20\'13 report}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 What\u8217\'20\'19s shocking about Biden\u8217\'20\'19s remark isn\u8217\'20\'19t that \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  is considering using nuclear weapons.\par \par \uc2 The Russian president {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/sep/21/putin-announces-partial-mobilisation-in-russia-in-escalation-of-ukraine-war"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has personally threatened to do so}}}\uc2  as his military faces setbacks in its bloody invasion of Ukraine. But when the US president \u8211\'20\'13 who has access to information from America\u8217\'20\'19s spy agencies that few others do \u8211\'20\'13 warns that Putin is indeed serious, and compares the current moment to the 1962 Cuban Missile Crisis, then it\u8217\'20\'19s something else. The question is: what?\par \par \uc2 One possibility is that the utterance was part of the public rhetoric campaign the White House has been waging to warn it against using a nuclear weapon. Last month, national security adviser Jake Sullivan warned doing so would bring {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/25/us-russia-ukraine-war-nuclear-weapons-jake-sullivan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Ccatastrophic consequences\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Speaking at a Democratic fundraiser last night, Biden acknowledged a level of uncertainty about Russia\u8217\'20\'19s goals, and how far Putin was willing to go to achieve them. \u8220\'20\'1CWe are trying to figure out what is Putin\u8217\'20\'19s off-ramp? Where does he find a way out? Where does he find himself where he does not only lose face but significant power?\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/07/biden-warns-world-would-face-armageddon-if-putin-uses-a-tactical-nuclear-weapon-in-ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden warns world would face \u8216\'20\'18Armageddon\u8217\'20\'19 if Putin uses a tactical nuclear weapon in Ukraine}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Shock as Biden suggests Putin's nuclear threats could mean 'Armageddon'\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. The job of an American president often involves reassuring or comforting the nation during uncertain times. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  instead gave Americans a blunt assessment of reality last night, when he suggested that the Russian president, \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 , was not kidding with his threats to to use nuclear weapons in Ukraine, and warned the world was the closest it has been to \u8220\'20\'1CArmageddon\u8221\'20\'1D in six decades. Chilling stuff.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is going on today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The president is back on the road with a trip that will take him to Hagerstown, Maryland, Philadelphia and finally Wilmington, Delaware, for the weekend.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Wisconsin Republican senator Ron Johnson debates his Democratic challenger Mandela Barnes at 8pm.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 New data{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bls.gov/news.release/empsit.nr0.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shows}}}\uc2  the US labor market remained strong in September, adding 263,000 positions and sending the unemployment rate down to 3.5%.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020221007eia7001s5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
