\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Biden pardons all federal offenses of simple marijuana possession \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Maya Yang (now); Chris Stein (earlier) \par \uc2 6,285 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 October 2022\par 20:09 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 President urges governors to do the same with state offenses: \u8216\'20\'18No one should be in a local jail or state prison for that reason\u8217\'20\'19Sign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 Summary\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s nearly 4pm in Washington DC. Here\u8217\'20\'19s where things stand:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Oath Keepers founder Stewart Rhodes told a member of the extremist group before the 2020 election that he had a contact in the Secret Service, a witness testified Thursday in Rhodes\u8217\'20\'19 Capitol riot trial. John Zimmerman, who was part of the North Carolina chapter, said Rhodes told him that Rhodes had a Secret Service agent\u8217\'20\'19s telephone number.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/joebiden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden}}}\uc2  has announced a pardon of all prior federal offenses of simple possession of marijuana. \u8220\'20\'1CThere are thousands of people who have prior Federal convictions for marijuana possession, who may be denied employment, housing, or educational opportunities as a result. My action will help relieve the collateral consequences arising from these convictions,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said in a statement released on Thursday afternoon.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/joebiden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden}}}\uc2  addressed workers at the \uc2 IBM\uc2  manufacturing plant in Poughkeepsie, New York on Thursday afternoon where he spoke of the Chips and Science Act that includes over $52bn in federal subsidies. The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/climate-2022-midterm-elections-biden-technology-business-7aa66d84e150a4c1d54831677075cee9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $280bn package}}}\uc2  seeks to boost the US\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/technology-business-congress-asia-economy-2868a5c494e99a2050a3f9495ba2b544"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 semiconductor industry}}}\uc2  and scientific research in attempts to create more high-tech jobs across the country while also help it compete better with international rivals such as China.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The federal government on Thursday expressed support for New York City\u8217\'20\'19s lawsuit seeking to halt the spread of \u8220\'20\'1Cghost guns\u8221\'20\'1D as city and state officials try to hold sellers of the largely untraceable firearms accountable. In a \u8220\'20\'1Cstatement of interest\u8221\'20\'1D filed in Manhattan federal court, the Department of Justice expressed \u8220\'20\'1Cserious concerns\u8221\'20\'1D about the proliferation of ghost guns, and said kits containing the weapons\u8217\'20\'19 components are classified as firearms under federal gun control law.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A federal judge has temporarily blocked parts of New York state\u8217\'20\'19s new gun law, in order to allow the Gun Owners of America, an advocacy group, to pursue a lawsuit challenging the legislation. The law came into effect on 1 September, creating new requirements for obtaining a license, including submitting social media accounts for review, and creating a list of public and private places where having a gun became a felony crime, even for license holders.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  has issued a health {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://emergency.cdc.gov/han/2022/han00477.asp"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 advisory}}}\uc2 , regarding an outbreak of Ebola in Uganda. The alert summarises \u8220\'20\'1Crecommendations for public health departments and clinicians, case identification and testing, and clinical laboratory biosafety considerations.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Oath Keepers founder Stewart Rhodes told a member of the extremist group before the 2020 election that he had a contact in the Secret Service, a witness testified Thursday in Rhodes\u8217\'20\'19 Capitol riot trial.\par \par \uc2 Associated Press reports:\par \par \uc2 John Zimmerman, who was part of the North Carolina chapter, said Rhodes told him that Rhodes had a Secret Service agent\u8217\'20\'19s telephone number. Zimmerman said he believed Rhodes spoke on the phone with the agent about the logistics of a September 2020 rally that then-President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  held in Fayetteville, North Carolina.\par \par \uc2 The claim came on the third day of testimony in the case against Rhodes and four others charged with seditious conspiracy for what authorities have described as a detailed, drawn-out plot to use force to stop the transfer of presidential power from Trump to Democrat \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , who won the election.\par \par \uc2 Prosecutor Kathryn Rakoczy had asked Zimmerman whether Rhodes ever told him about having any kind of connection to Trump.\par \par \uc2 Zimmerman could not say for sure that Rhodes was speaking to someone with the Secret Service \u8212\'20\'14 only that Rhodes told him he was \u8212\'20\'14 and it was not clear what they were discussing. Zimmerman said Rhodes wanted to find out the \u8220\'20\'1Cparameters\u8221\'20\'1D that the Oath Keepers could operate under during the election-year rally.\par \par \uc2 The significance of the detail in the government\u8217\'20\'19s case is unclear. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s potential ties to extremist groups have been a focus of the House committee investigating the riot at the Capitol on Jan. 6, 2021.\par \par \uc2 Another Oath Keeper expected to testify against Rhodes has claimed that after the riot, Rhodes phoned someone seemingly close to Trump and made a request: tell Trump to call on militia groups to fight to keep him in power. Authorities have not identified that person; Rhodes\u8217\'20\'19 lawyer says the call never happened.\par \par \uc2 Secret Service spokesman Anthony Guglielmi said it is not uncommon for \u8220\'20\'1Cprotest groups\u8221\'20\'1D to contact the agency with logistical questions about rallies. He noted that firearms are always prohibited within restricted areas being secured by the agency.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Oath Keepers are certainly a known demonstration group.\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Guglielmi said he is not aware of any contact between Rhodes and an agency representative but would not be surprised if Rhodes said he had contacted the secret Service before the North Carolina event.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t have any way to track that down without some more information,\u8221\'20\'1D the spokesman said.\par \par \uc2 Rhodes, from Granbury Texas, and four associates are being tried on a Civil War-era charge.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden to pardon all federal offenses of simple marijuana possession\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has announced a pardon of all prior federal offenses of simple possession of marijuana.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere are thousands of people who have prior Federal convictions for marijuana possession, who may be denied employment, housing, or educational opportunities as a result. My action will help relieve the collateral consequences arising from these convictions,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said in a statement released on Thursday afternoon.\par \par \uc2 He went on to urge all governors to do the same with regards to state offenses, saying, \u8220\'20\'1CJust as no one should be in a Federal prison solely due to the possession of marijuana, no one should be in a local jail or state prison for that reason, either.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The president also called on the Secretary of Health and Human Services and the Attorney General to begin the administrative process to review how marijuana is scheduled under federal law.\par \par \uc2 Marijuana is currently classified in Schedule 1 of the Controlled Substances Act under federal law. This classification puts marijuana in the same schedule as for heroin and LSD and even higher than the classification of fentanyl and methamphetamine, two drugs that are fueling the ongoing overdose epidemic across the country.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  addressed workers at the \uc2 IBM\uc2  manufacturing plant in Poughkeepsie, New York on Thursday afternoon where he spoke of the CHIPS and Science Act that includes over $52 billion in federal subsidies.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSince we\u8217\'20\'19ve been elected, we\u8217\'20\'19ve created 678,000 new manufacturing jobs where, And we\u8217\'20\'19re just getting started. Where is it written that we can\u8217\'20\'19t lead manufacturing in the world? I don\u8217\'20\'19t know where that\u8217\'20\'19s written. And that\u8217\'20\'19s one of the things that CHIPS Act is going to change \u8211\'20\'13 the law that\u8217\'20\'19s going build the future in a proud, proud legacy, not only for \uc2 IBM\uc2  but for the country,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/climate-2022-midterm-elections-biden-technology-business-7aa66d84e150a4c1d54831677075cee9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $280 billion package}}}\uc2  seeks to boost the US\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/technology-business-congress-asia-economy-2868a5c494e99a2050a3f9495ba2b544"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 semiconductor industry}}}\uc2  and scientific research in attempts to create more high-tech jobs across the country while also help it compete better with international rivals such as China.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAmerican manufacturing - the backbone of our economy got hollowed out because companies began to move jobs and production overseas. And as a result, today, we\u8217\'20\'19re down to barely 10% of the world\u8217\'20\'19s chips, despite leading in chip research and design,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe need [these chips] in conductors, not only to make Javelin missiles, but also the weapon systems, the future that is going to rely even more on advanced chips, Unfortunately we produce 0% of these advanced chips today\u8230\'20\'26China is trying to move ahead of us in manufacturing them,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe United States has to lead the world in producing these advanced chips,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said, adding that \u8220\'20\'1Csome of our friends\u8221\'20\'1D on the Republican side bought into China\u8217\'20\'19s lobbying in Congress against the act.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe CHIPS and Science Act is not handing out blank checks to companies\u8230\'20\'26 I\u8217\'20\'19ve directed my administration\u8230\'20\'26 to be laser focused on the guard rails that\u8217\'20\'19s gonna protect taxpayers dollars.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ll make sure the companies partner with unions, community colleges, technical schools, and offer training and apprenticeships. We\u8217\'20\'19re going to make sure\u8230\'20\'26small and minority owned businesses get to participate. We\u8217\'20\'19re gonna make sure the companies do not take these taxpayers dollars, do not turn around and make investments in China, investments that undermine our supply chains and natural security. That\u8217\'20\'19s a guarantee.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 US president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  looks at a quantum computer as he tours the \uc2 IBM\uc2  facility in Poughkeepsie, New York, on October 6, 2022. Photograph: Mandel Ngan/AFP/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s about economic security\u8230\'20\'26it\u8217\'20\'19s about national security\u8230\'20\'26and that\u8217\'20\'19s what we\u8217\'20\'19re going to see in this factory, in the Hudson Valley,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden added.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have the best and most productive workers in the world. We have the best research universities in the world\u8230\'20\'26 We wrote and passed the Bipartisan Infrastructure Law\u8230\'20\'26and we finally decided that we\u8217\'20\'19re going to move up from number 13 in the world on infrastructure to number one,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Chips and Science Act is not handing out blank checks to\u8230\'20\'26companies\u8230\'20\'26we\u8217\'20\'19re going to make sure that small and minority-owned businesses get to participate,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn this law, I have the power to take back federal funding if companies are not meeting the requirements,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe future of the chips industry is going to be made in America\u8230\'20\'26and many of these good paying jobs don\u8217\'20\'19t require a set of college degrees,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe largest American investment of its kind,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said in his address as he celebrates this summer\u8217\'20\'19s passage of a $ {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/biden-science-technology-united-states-economy-2fa651c540c9869890dfe670bcdcb7ea"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 280 billion legislative package}}}\uc2  intended to boost the US semiconductor industry and scientific research.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is set to deliver remarks at around 2pm ET at the \uc2 IBM\uc2  site in Poughkeepsie, New York.\par \par \uc2 Biden is expected to speak on creating jobs in the Hudson Valley and lowering costs, among other topics.\par \par \uc2 We will bring you the latest updates on his address so do stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration announced that the US will start screening travelers from Uganda for Ebola as an additional precaution aimed at trying to prevent an outbreak in the African country from spreading, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 The federal government on Thursday expressed support for New York City\u8217\'20\'19s lawsuit seeking to halt the spread of \u8220\'20\'1Cghost guns,\u8221\'20\'1D as city and state officials try to hold sellers of the largely untraceable firearms accountable.\par \par \uc2 In a \u8220\'20\'1Cstatement of interest\u8221\'20\'1D filed in Manhattan federal court, the Department of Justice expressed \u8220\'20\'1Cserious concerns\u8221\'20\'1D about the proliferation of ghost guns, and said kits containing the weapons\u8217\'20\'19 components are classified as firearms under federal gun control law.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CGhost guns are a major contributor to the ongoing plague of gun violence,\u8221\'20\'1D US Attorney Breon Peace in Brooklyn said in a statement accompanying the filing, which US Attorney \uc2 Damian Williams\uc2  in Manhattan also signed.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe United States will continue to employ every means available, including civil tools, to keep ghost guns and other illegal firearms out of the hands of criminals and reduce the risk of gun violence. The United States filed a Statement of Interest in this important litigation to ensure that the Court is informed of the federal government\u8217\'20\'19s views of pertinent firearms statutes and regulations,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 New York City and state Attorney General Letitia James on June 29 filed two lawsuits accusing 10 out-of-state distributors of creating a public nuisance by selling unfinished frames and receivers to buyers within the state.\par \par \uc2 Ghost guns do not have serial numbers and can be acquired without background checks, potentially letting people otherwise ineligible to buy firearms to construct finished guns.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are not going to let gun companies turn New York into a city of mail-order murder,\u8221\'20\'1D New York City Mayor Eric Adams said when announcing the city\u8217\'20\'19s lawsuit.\par \par \uc2 Both lawsuits were filed six days after the supreme court struck down a century-old New York law that strictly limited the carrying of guns outside the home.\par \par \uc2 Federal law largely shields gun makers from lawsuits over shootings. There is an exception for when sellers knowingly violate statutes governing firearms sales and marketing.\par \par \uc2 Three of the five defendants in the city\u8217\'20\'19s lawsuit have settled, and agreed to stop sales to city residents.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 Steven Donziger, ahuman rights lawyer, environmental justice advocate and Guardian US columnist, writes today about a \u8216\'20\'18terrifying case\u8217\'20\'19 about to be heard by the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 It is well-known that intense competition between democracy, authoritarianism, and fascism is playing out across the globe in a variety of ways \u8211\'20\'13 including in the United States. This year\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/us-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 supreme court}}}\uc2  term, which started this week, is a vivid illustration of how the situation is actually worse than most people understand.\par \par \uc2 A supermajority of six unelected ultraconservatives justices \u8211\'20\'13 five put on the bench by presidents who did not win the popular vote \u8211\'20\'13 haveaggressively grabbed yet another batch of cases that will allow them to move American law to the extreme right and threaten US democracy. The leading example of this disturbing shift is a little-known case called Moore v Harper, which could lock in rightwing control of the United States for generations.\par \par \uc2 The heart of the Moore case is a formerly fringe legal notion called the Independent State Legislature (ISL) theory. This theory posits that an obscure provision in the US constitution allowing state legislatures to set \u8220\'20\'1Ctime, place, and manner\u8221\'20\'1D rules for federal elections should not be subject to judicial oversight. In other words, state legislatures should have the absolute power to determine how federal elections are run without court interference.\par \par \uc2 Think about this theory in the context of the last US election. After \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  defeated \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  resoundingly in both the popular vote and in the electoral college, Trump tried to organize a massive intimidation campaign to steal the election which played out in the storming of the Capitol building on 6 January. But behind the scenes, the legal core of this attempt was to convince the many Republican-controlled state legislatures (30 out of 50 states) to send slates of fake Trump electors from states like Arizona, Georgia and Michigan where Trump lost the popular vote.\par \par \uc2 If Trump had succeeded, he would have \u8220\'20\'1Cwon\u8221\'20\'1D the election via the electoral college (itself an anti-democratic relic) and been able to stay in office. If the supreme court buys the theory in the Moore case, this could easily happen in 2024 and beyond. In fact, it is possible Republicans will never lose another election again if this theory is adopted as law. Or put another way, whether Republicans win or lose elections via the popular vote will not matter because they will be able to maintain power regardless.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s not democracy.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2022/oct/06/the-most-terrifying-case-of-all-is-about-to-be-heard-by-the-us-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The most terrifying case of all is about to be heard by the US supreme court | Steven Donziger}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Judge blocks New York gun law\par \par \uc2 A federal judge has temporarily blocked parts of New York state\u8217\'20\'19s new gun law, in order to allow the Gun Owners of America, an advocacy group, to pursue a lawsuit challenging the legislation.\par \par \uc2 Reuters has the report:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe law came into effect on 1 September, creating new requirements for obtaining a license, including submitting social media accounts for review, and creating a list of public and private places where having a gun became a felony crime, even for license holders.\par \par \uc2 Lawmakers in New York\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic-controlled legislature passed the law during an emergency session in July after the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  found the state\u8217\'20\'19s licensing regime for firearms to be unconstitutional following a challenge by the New York affiliate of the \uc2 National Rifle Association\uc2 , a powerful gun-owners\u8217\'20\'19 rights group.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, Glenn Suddaby, chief judge of the US district court in Syracuse, agreed to issue the order at the request of six New York- resident members of Gun Owners of America, which competes with the \uc2 National Rifle Association\uc2  in political influence. Suddaby said his order would not take effect for three days, to allow the New York government to appeal.\par \par \uc2 Suddaby {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/01/new-york-to-enact-new-gun-restrictions-in-response-to-supreme-court-decision"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 last month ruled}}}\uc2  that much of the new law was unconstitutional in dismissing an earlier lawsuit by Gun Owners of America in which he found neither the group nor an individual member of it had standing to sue before the law came into effect.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Background:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/01/new-york-to-enact-new-gun-restrictions-in-response-to-supreme-court-decision"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York enacts new gun restrictions in response to supreme court decision}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Florida mayor to whom \uc2 Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/video/2022/oct/05/joe-biden-caught-swearing-on-hot-mic-video"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 uttered a profanity}}}\uc2  captured by a live microphone, sparking a minor viral fuss, said the presidential f-bomb did not bother him in the slightest.\par \par \uc2 The two men met on Wednesday, as Biden {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/05/biden-hurricane-ian-florida-ron-desantis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 visited areas of Florida}}}\uc2  hit by Hurricane Ian. The president was heard to say: \u8220\'20\'1CNobody fucks with a Biden.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The incident set off a minor media storm. The White House did not comment.\par \par \uc2 Ray Murphy, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fortmyersbeachfl.gov/Directory.aspx?EID=116"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 mayor of Fort Myers Beach}}}\uc2 , told {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/joe-biden/florida-mayor-laughs-bidens-hot-mic-f-bomb-rcna50953?fbclid=IwAR3F8eMZQVvGeTnc_nWrlxRNrmvzVunddI1BjuhY4wAIYipLpyNO_DGBpm8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NBC}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CIt was not directed at anybody. It was just two guys talking. It didn\u8217\'20\'19t faze me one bit. That\u8217\'20\'19s just the way two guys talk to each other from our respective backgrounds.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 We have video of the moment:\par \par \uc2 Murphy told NBC he and the president quickly discovered they had a lot in common.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re both Irish Catholics,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re both devout Catholics. But every once [in] a while a little salty language comes out.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden has had brushes with hot mics and salty language before. Most famously, in 2010 he enlivened the signing ceremony for the Affordable Care Act by telling his then boss, \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/richard-adams-blog/2010/mar/23/joe-biden-obama-big-fucking-deal-overheard"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 This is a big fucking deal}}}\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden later told {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.npr.org/2016/10/17/498292076/biden-shares-views-on-the-state-of-american-politics"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NPR}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CThank God my mother wasn\u8217\'20\'19t around to hear.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In January this year, Biden appeared to think his microphone was off when he called a Fox News reporter, Peter Doocy, \u8220\'20\'1Ca stupid son of a bitch\u8221\'20\'1D for asking a question about inflation. The president {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=w36iYu6XH9E"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said sorry}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/06/florida-mayor-not-offended-joe-biden-salty-language-live-microphone"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Florida mayor not offended by Biden\u8217\'20\'19s \u8216\'20\'18salty language\u8217\'20\'19 on live microphone}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  has issued a health {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://emergency.cdc.gov/han/2022/han00477.asp"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 advisory}}}\uc2 , regarding an outbreak of Ebola in Uganda.\par \par \uc2 The alert summarises \u8220\'20\'1Crecommendations for public health departments and clinicians, case identification and testing, and clinical laboratory biosafety considerations\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The federal agency emphasises that the alert is a precaution, as \u8220\'20\'1Cno suspected, probable, or confirmed EVD cases related to this outbreak have yet been reported in the United States\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Its aim, it says, is to raise awareness among clinicians.\par \par \uc2 Reuters, meanwhile, reports that the Biden administration \u8220\'20\'1Cwill begin redirecting US-bound travelers who have been to Uganda within the previous 21 days to five major American airports to be screened for Ebola\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The change is expected to take effect within the coming week or so, a source said. The travelers will need to arrive at New York-JFK, Newark, Atlanta, Chicago O\u8217\'20\'19Hare or Washington Dulles. There is no vaccine for the Sudan strain of the disease behind the latest Uganda infections.\par \par \uc2 The Biden White House does contain experience in dealing with Ebola. \uc2 Ron Klain\uc2 , the president\u8217\'20\'19s chief of staff, was \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Ebola tsar during an outbreak in 2014.\par \par \uc2 In 2020, during the darkest days of the Covid pandemic, Klain wrote for the Guardian: \u8220\'20\'1COf the many hard days I spent coordinating the US fight against {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/ebola"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ebola}}}\uc2  in 2014-15, none was more painful than 29 November 2014, when I spoke at the funeral of Martin Salia, a doctor who left Maryland to return to his native Sierra Leone to help cope with the devastating death toll among healthcare workers during that epidemic.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDr Salia contracted Ebola while performing surgery; by the time he was airlifted back to the US for treatment, he was too ill to be saved. At his funeral, I noted that while history is filled with all sorts of accidental heroes and unwilling heroes, \u8216\'20\'18the greatest heroes are people who choose to face danger, who voluntarily put themselves at risk to help others.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s Klain\u8217\'20\'19s full piece:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2020/aug/13/obama-ebola-ronald-klain-healthcare-workers-coronavirus"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 I was Obama\u8217\'20\'19s Ebola tsar. US healthcare workers are dying at a shameful rate | Ronald A Klain}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 Democrats {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/06/biden-democrats-gas-prices-oil-opec-saudi-midterms-latest?page=with:block-633ed3f68f085c245067ad87#block-633ed3f68f085c245067ad87"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  are seething}}}\uc2  over Saudi Arabia\u8217\'20\'19s push for Opec+ to cut oil production, potentially driving up US gas prices just as voters head to the midterm elections. Meanwhile, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/06/biden-democrats-gas-prices-oil-opec-saudi-midterms-latest?page=with:block-633eef378f088272fbb9cb48#block-633eef378f088272fbb9cb48"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 embarked on a long day of travel}}}\uc2  that will see him tout the Chips bill to boost semiconductor production, and also attend two Democratic fundraisers as the party prepares to defend its slim holds on both the House and Senate.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has happened today so far:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2 , the Republican candidate for Senate in Georgia, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/06/biden-democrats-gas-prices-oil-opec-saudi-midterms-latest?page=with:block-633ee2ac8f085c150750ed2f#block-633ee2ac8f085c150750ed2f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said he knew \u8220\'20\'1Cnothing about\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  a woman\u8217\'20\'19s claim he paid for her to have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 and then had a child with him.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Republicans{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/06/biden-democrats-gas-prices-oil-opec-saudi-midterms-latest?page=with:block-633ee66d8f088272fbb9caad#block-633ee66d8f088272fbb9caad"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 may decide to impeach}}}\uc2  homeland security secretary Alejandro Mayorkas if they win a majority in the House.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Election deniers{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/06/biden-democrats-gas-prices-oil-opec-saudi-midterms-latest?page=with:block-633eddae8f08cb77d5166b17#block-633eddae8f08cb77d5166b17"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appear poised to win}}}\uc2  many races in the upcoming midterms, no matter what happens, \uc2 The Washington Post\uc2  found.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 A Democratic senator has joined in on the calls to punish Saudi Arabia for backing the Opec+ cut to global oil production:\par \par \uc2 enltrFrom unanswered questions about 9/11 & the murder of Jamal Khashoggi, to conspiring w/ Putin to punish the US w/ higher oil prices, the royal Saudi family has never been a trustworthy ally of our nation. It\u8217\'20\'19s time for our foreign policy to imagine a world without their alliance.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Senator Dick Durbin (@SenatorDurbin) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenatorDurbin/status/1578024093118787585?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 6, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrThere\u8217\'20\'19re also unjust arrests:\par \par \uc2 Raif Badawi, finally released after 10 years in jail, but unable to leave SA to reunite w/ family in Canada.\par \par \uc2 Waleed Abu al-Khair, human rights lawyer still in jail.\par \par \uc2 Salma al-Shehab, women\u8217\'20\'19s rights activist facing outrageous 34 year prison sentence.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Senator Dick Durbin (@SenatorDurbin) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenatorDurbin/status/1578024094708428802?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 6, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, John Kennedy, the Republican senator who two years ago proposed a similar measure to retaliate against Saudi Arabia for not cutting production even as global demand was crashing \u8211\'20\'13 thereby driving prices below the cost of production for American oil firms \u8211\'20\'13 today blames Biden for the Opec+ cut:\par \par \uc2 enltrOPEC is taking advantage of Pres. Biden\u8217\'20\'19s reliance on foreign oil and slashing supply, which will drive up prices that Louisianians pay.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s as simple and sad as that.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 John Kennedy (@SenJohnKennedy) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenJohnKennedy/status/1577666861847793666?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 5, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 While his Democratic allies have blamed Saudi Arabia for the Opec+ production cut, the decision also has the potential to put Biden on the defensive.\par \par \uc2 In July, he traveled to Saudi Arabia in a trip widely seen as an attempt to convince its defacto leader, crown prince \uc2 Mohammed bin Salman\uc2 , to produce more oil. It was a hard pill to swallow for Biden, who had pledged while running for office to turn the country into a \u8220\'20\'1Cglobal pariah\u8221\'20\'1D for killing journalist Jamal Khashoggi. Critics of the visit seized on his fist-bump greeting with the crown prince as evidence of the president\u8217\'20\'19s flip-flopping:\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s greeting to Saudi Crown Prince Mohammed bin Salman was not well received by the US president\u8217\'20\'19s allies. Photograph: Bandar Algaloud/Reuters\par \par \uc2 As he left the White House today, Biden was asked if he regrets the trip to Riyadh. \u8220\'20\'1CThe trip was not essentially for oil. The trip was about the Middle East and about Israel and rationalization of positions. But it is a disappointment and says that there are problems,\u8221\'20\'1D he replied.\par \par \uc2 Indeed, Biden did also visit Israel on the trip, and the White House has repeatedly said seeking peace in the Middle East was a major goal.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is keenly aware of the consequences a midterm rout for Democrats would have on his presidency, and is starting a lengthy day of travel aimed a preventing that from happening.\par \par \uc2 He\u8217\'20\'19s heading to Poughkeepsie, New York for a tour of an \uc2 IBM\uc2  facility and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://newsroom.ibm.com/2022-10-06-IBM-and-CEO-Arvind-Krishna-Welcome-President-Biden-to-Poughkeepsie-Site,-Company-Plans-to-Invest-20-billion-in-the-Hudson-Valley-Region-Over-10-Years"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the announcement}}}\uc2  of the tech firm\u8217\'20\'19s plans to spend $20 billion over 10 years in the Hudson Valley region. Biden will use that news to highlight the success of the Chips act Congress approved over the summer to boost semiconductor production.\par \par \uc2 Then he flies to Red Bank, New Jersey, for a Democratic fundraiser, and then to New York City for another fundraiser, this one focused on the party\u8217\'20\'19s campaign to keep control of the Senate. Biden is then expected back at the White House late this evening.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 What\u8217\'20\'19s worse, attacking the US capitol, or spending more money than you should on gasoline?\par \par \uc2 To Republican senator Tom Cotton, the answer is clearly the latter. Here\u8217\'20\'19s his comment on \uc2 Hugh Hewitt\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s show this morning that quite succinctly sums up the pitch each party is making to voters ahead of the 8 November midterms:\par \par \uc2 enltrSen. Tom Cotton (R-AR): \u8220\'20\'1CThe Democrats are always saying, \u8216\'20\'18Never forget January 6th.\u8217\'20\'19 Yeah, remember that on January 6th gas was at $2.40 a gallon.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/dK1KMxHO2h"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/dK1KMxHO2h}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1578031370152341504?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 6, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Indeed, Democrats do not want voters to forget that supporters of Republican president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , animated by his baseless conspiracy theories, carried out a history-making insurrection at the US Capitol that day. Meanwhile, the GOP hopes Americans will overlook the attack in favor of their promise to somehow bring gas prices nearer to where they were when the economy was reeling from Covid-19. We\u8217\'20\'19ll find out how voters feel in a few weeks.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 While taking the Senate is a steeper hill to climb, Republicans have a much better shot of winning a majority in the House of Representatives, where they would have the power to launch impeachment proceedings.\par \par \uc2 The bigger question is: who would they impeach? And what for?\par \par \uc2 While some Democrats believe they\u8217\'20\'19ll go straight for Biden himself, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/10/06/politics/kevin-mccarthy-alejandro-mayorkas-republican-impeachment-effort/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN reports}}}\uc2  that a campaign has emerged to impeach homeland security secretary Alejandro Mayorkas, whom the GOP complains is at fault for not stopping {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/03/alejandro-mayorkas-us-mexico-border-migrants-warning"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the flow of migrants and asylum seekers across the southern border with Mexico}}}\uc2 . Indeed, Republican lawmakers have been campaigning on the border issue in the upcoming midterms, and impeaching Mayorkas could give them the ability to say they\u8217\'20\'19ve made good on that promise, though launching the procedure against a cabinet secretary has only been done once before in American history.\par \par \uc2 However, the strategy is not without risks, and it\u8217\'20\'19s unclear if enough Republican House lawmakers would back it, or if their leader Kevin McCarthy is on board. Here\u8217\'20\'19s what CNN has to say:\par \par \uc2 GOP Rep. \uc2 Steve Womack\uc2  of Arkansas said Republicans \u8220\'20\'1Cshould focus on policy\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cleave some of the other more emotional topics for another day.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe risk is if people lose faith in the ability of Congress to even do its basic function,\u8221\'20\'1D Womack said of voter blowback for impeaching Mayorkas. \u8220\'20\'1CThe people that I talk to from all stripes tell me they want a Congress that works \u8211\'20\'13 not a Congress that is preoccupied with kind of revenge-type agendas. Because then a lot of other things (that) need to happen don\u8217\'20\'19t get to happen. And then that hurts the country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 So far, McCarthy has carefully sidestepped impeachment questions, insisting Republicans are not going to pre-determine the outcome but are willing to go wherever the facts and the law lead them.\par \par \uc2 Yet McCarthy has not shut the door on the idea either, particularly when it comes to Mayorkas. And when pressed by CNN on whether Mayorkas is vulnerable to impeachment in a GOP-led House, he replied: \u8220\'20\'1CWhat happens at the border is above everything else.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 Back to \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2 , the Republican candidate for Senate in Georgia was on conservative radio host \uc2 Hugh Hewitt\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s show today, and responded to reports he paid for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  for a woman he also had a child with.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what he had to say:\par \par \uc2 enltrNew: \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2 , who has pushed for a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, says of paid-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  allegation on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hughhewitt?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @hughhewitt}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CIf that had happened, I would have said there's nothing to be ashamed of there. People have done that \u8212\'20\'14 but I know nothing about it.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Tqx48i3rGK"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Tqx48i3rGK}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Shane Goldmacher (@ShaneGoldmacher) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ShaneGoldmacher/status/1578010653872328706?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 6, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 The story is particularly worrying for Walker, since he said he would support a national ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  without exceptions, if elected.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  has a report out today quantifying the massive number of 2020 election deniers standing as Republicans for state and federal offices nationwide, and concluding that many will win their races in November.\par \par \uc2 The report finds 299 GOP politicians standing for House, Senate or statewide office who baselessly believe \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  did not win the 2020 election. Of these, 174 are running in seats considers safe for Republicans, while 51 are in close races.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/nation/2022/10/06/elections-deniers-midterm-elections-2022/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from the Post}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 The implications will be lasting: If Republicans take control of the House, as many political forecasters predict, election deniers would hold enormous sway over the choice of the nation\u8217\'20\'19s next speaker, who in turn could preside over the House in a future contested presidential election. The winners of all the races examined by The Post \u8212\'20\'14 those for governor, lieutenant governor, secretary of state, attorney general, Senate and House \u8212\'20\'14 will hold some measure of power overseeing American elections.\par \par \uc2 Many of these candidates echo the false claims of former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 claims that have been thoroughly investigated and dismissed by myriad officials and courts. Experts said the insistence on such claims, despite the lack of evidence, reflects a willingness among election-denying candidates to undermine democratic institutions when it benefits their side.\par \par \uc2 The Post\u8217\'20\'19s count \u8212\'20\'14 assembled from public statements, social media posts, and actions taken by the candidates to deny the legitimacy of the last presidential vote \u8212\'20\'14 shows how the movement arising from Trump\u8217\'20\'19s thwarted plot to overturn the 2020 election is, in many respects, even stronger two years later. Far from repudiating candidates who embrace Trump\u8217\'20\'19s false fraud claims, GOP primary voters have empowered them.\par \par \uc2 The issue has dominated in key battlegrounds. In Warren, Mich., on Saturday, Trump campaigned for three statewide candidates, all of them deniers: Tudor Dixon for governor, Matthew DePerno for attorney general and Kristina Karamo for secretary of state.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t believe we\u8217\'20\'19ll ever have a fair election again,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump told the crowd. \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t believe it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Post\u8217\'20\'19s report characterizes election denying as essentially a form of corruption and a political tactic used to win races. Larry Jacobs, a professor studying legislative politics at the \uc2 University of Minnesota\uc2 , warns the proliferation of election deniers in Congress could cause chaos, both for this year\u8217\'20\'19s election and the 2024 presidential race.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is no longer about \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . This is about the entire electoral system and what constitutes legitimate elections. All of that is now up in the air,\u8221\'20\'1D Jacobs said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 When it comes to the midterms, one of the most important races is taking place in Georgia, where Democratic senator \uc2 Raphael Warnock\uc2  is fighting to keep his seat in a state that only narrowly elected him last year. \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  is his Republican opponent, but as the Associated Press reports, he\u8217\'20\'19s been engulfed in a scandal over how his personal life has clashed with his stance on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 A woman who said \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  paid for her \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2009 is the mother of one of his children, according to a new report, undercutting the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/state-of-georgia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Georgia}}}\uc2  Republican Senate candidate\u8217\'20\'19s claims he didn\u8217\'20\'19t know who she was.\par \par \uc2 The Daily Beast, which first reported the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said it had agreed not to reveal details of the woman\u8217\'20\'19s identity.\par \par \uc2 Walker, who has expressed support for a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban without exceptions, called the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  allegation a \u8220\'20\'1Cflat-out lie\u8221\'20\'1D, threatened a lawsuit against the outlet and said he had no idea who the woman might be.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday night, the Beast revealed that the woman \u8211\'20\'13 who was not named \u8211\'20\'13 was so well known to Walker that, according to her, they conceived another child years after the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . She decided to continue with the pregnancy, though she noted that Walker, as during the earlier pregnancy, expressed that it wasn\u8217\'20\'19t a convenient time for him, the outlet reported.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/06/herschel-walker-abortion-mother-children"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Woman who said Herschel Walker paid for \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  also has child with him \u8211\'20\'13 report}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 Why are three House Democrats {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://malinowski.house.gov/media/press-releases/representatives-malinowski-casten-and-wild-introduce-bill-remove-us-troops"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 proposing the United States remove its troops}}}\uc2  and weapons systems from Saudi Arabia and the United Arab Emirates? Because those countries are on the side of Russia, they argue.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSaudi Arabia and the UAE\u8217\'20\'19s drastic cut in oil production, despite President Biden\u8217\'20\'19s overtures to both countries in recent months, is a hostile act against the United States and a clear signal that they have chosen to side with Russia in its war against Ukraine,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Tom Malinowski\uc2 , Sean Casten and Susan Wild wrote. \u8220\'20\'1CBoth countries have long relied on an American military presence in the Gulf to protect their security and oil fields. We see no reason why American troops and contractors should continue to provide this service to countries that are actively working against us. If Saudi Arabia and the UAE want to help Putin, they should look to him for their defense.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Their rhetoric lines up with what White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  said yesterday when she declared that the two million barrel per-day cut in oil production makes it \u8220\'20\'1Cclear that OPEC+ is aligning with Russia.\u8221\'20\'1D While she didn\u8217\'20\'19t call for a withdrawal in military aid, she did say that the cut would drive energy prices higher right as many poor countries were struggling with inflation caused by Russia\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Ukraine. The broader political worry for the White House is that it will cause gas prices to spike again at home, an Americans will react by voting against Democrats in the 8 November midterms.\par \par \uc2 As for the bill\u8217\'20\'19s prospects, consider {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cassidy.senate.gov/newsroom/press-releases/in-response-to-saudi-aggression-cassidy-to-introduce-bill-to-withdraw-american-troops-impose-oil-tariffs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a similar effort}}}\uc2  from Republican senator \uc2 Bill Cassidy\uc2  introduced shortly after Covid-19 forced the shutdown of the US economy in early 2020. He proposed tariffs on Saudi oil imports and the removal of US troops from the country if Riyadh didn\u8217\'20\'19t back efforts for a deep slash in Opec+ production as global demand collapsed and prices plummeted. While the bill went nowhere, the three Democrats argue it worked in getting the oil cartel to agree to a bigger cut \u8211\'20\'13 though then-president \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/article/us-global-oil-trump-saudi-specialreport/special-report-trump-told-saudi-cut-oil-supply-or-lose-u-s-military-support-sources-idUSKBN22C1V4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 also reportedly played a role in convincing the Saudis}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 Democrats seek revenge after Saudi-led Opec+ slashes oil production ahead of midterms\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics readers. Vengeance is on the mind of some Democrats after Opec+, the bloc of oil-producing countries in which Saudi Arabia plays a leading role, decided to slash its crude output yesterday. The move will have ripple effects globally, and could drive up prices at gas pumps in the United States just as voters are casting ballots in the midterms. The White House condemned the move yesterday, but later in the day, three lawmakers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://malinowski.house.gov/media/press-releases/representatives-malinowski-casten-and-wild-introduce-bill-remove-us-troops"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 came out with a bill}}}\uc2  that essentially declares Saudi Arabia is no longer an ally of Washington, and would mandate American troops leave that country and the United Arab Emirates. There\u8217\'20\'19s no telling yet if Congress has the will, or the time, to consider it before the end of the year.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is happening today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is heading to New York and New Jersey, where he\u8217\'20\'19ll visit an \uc2 IBM\uc2  facility and cheer {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://newsroom.ibm.com/2022-10-06-IBM-and-CEO-Arvind-Krishna-Welcome-President-Biden-to-Poughkeepsie-Site,-Company-Plans-to-Invest-20-billion-in-the-Hudson-Valley-Region-Over-10-Years"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the announcement of $20bn in new investments}}}\uc2  from the company. He then attends two fundraisers for Democrats.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Two senatorial candidate debates are scheduled today: Arizona Democrat Mark Kelly will spar with two challengers, including Republican \uc2 Blake Masters\uc2 , at 9 m. Iowa Republican \uc2 Chuck Grassley\uc2  faces his Democratic opponent, Mike Franken, at 8pm.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Labor department data{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dol.gov/ui/data.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shows}}}\uc2  an uptick in new unemployment assistance claims nationwide, but they remain at very low levels in a sign of the job market\u8217\'20\'19s strength.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020221006eia60028q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
