\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Over 60 clinics in 15 US states have stopped offering abortions, study finds\b0\par\par\uc2 Coral Murphy Marcos \par \uc2 782 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 October 2022\par 19:40 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s overruling of Roe v Wade prompted bans of most abortions in more than a dozen states\par \par \uc2 More than 60 clinics across 15 US states have stopped offering abortions since the supreme court overruled Roe v Wade, the ruling which guaranteed the right, a new study found.\par \par \uc2 The court\u8217\'20\'19s decision this summer, in Dobbs v Jackson, Mississippi, has prompted bans of most abortions in more than a dozen states. Other states are fighting over access to the procedure by suing to block enforcement of laws restricting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The new {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/2022/10/100-days-post-roe-least-66-clinics-across-15-us-states-have-stopped-offering-abortion-care?utm_source=Guttmacher+Email+Alerts&utm_campaign=af571cd1b8-100dayspostroeguttupdate&utm_medium=email&utm_term=0_9ac83dc920-af571cd1b8-260727353"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 study}}}\uc2  by the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2 , a non-profit which works on reproductive rights advocacy and research, found that in 15 states with a previous total of 79 clinics that offered \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , that number had dropped to 13 as of Sunday.\par \par \uc2 All the 13 clinics are in Georgia, where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is banned at about six weeks, when many women are unaware they are pregnant. In 14 states, no provider currently offers abortions, the study said.\par \par \uc2 Among the 66 clinics that no longer offer \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , 40 still offer services that may include prescribing birth control or helping patients find \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services in other states. But 26 have shut down completely.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen clinics close down or stop offering \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care, it represents a lost source of healthcare for their community,\u8221\'20\'1D the study said.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden issued an executive order as a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2022/08/03/fact-sheet-president-biden-issues-executive-order-at-the-first-meeting-of-the-task-force-on-reproductive-healthcare-access-2/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 response}}}\uc2  to the Dobbs decision, including mandates to protect patient privacy, defend the right to travel for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care and protect the procedure in the case of emergency care.\par \par \uc2 Several obstetrician-gynecologists spoke this week at a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.c-span.org/video/?523406-1/president-biden-addresses-task-force-reproductive-healthcare-access"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 meeting}}}\uc2  of the Reproductive Health Care Access taskforce, about the difficulties imposed by bans in their states.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI have had teenagers with chronic medical conditions that make their pregnancy very high risk and women with highly desired pregnancies who receive a terrible diagnosis of a fetal anomaly cry when they learn that they can\u8217\'20\'19t receive their \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in our state and beg me to help them,\u8221\'20\'1D said Dr Nisha Verma, an obstetrician-gynecologist from Atlanta, Georgia.\par \par \uc2 The Guttmacher study found that in the 14 states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is now unavailable, 125,780 abortions were performed in 2020. Patients seeking \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care in such states must now travel.\par \par \uc2 Companies including \uc2 Bank of America\uc2  and \uc2 Kroger\uc2  have expanded job benefits to cover the cost for employees to travel to other states to access \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care.\par \par \uc2 In Georgia, 41,620 abortions were obtained in 2020. The Guttmacher study mentions that the stringent timeframe to schedule and receive an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Georgia leaves people with the same options as people in states with a total ban. More than 29% of US women of reproductive age live in states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is banned or severely restricted.\par \par \uc2 The bans are overwhelming clinics in states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is still legal.\par \par \uc2 Arizona is the latest state to make almost all abortions illegal, after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/sep/23/arizona-abortion-ban-clinics-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a judge lifted a nearly 50-year-old injunction }}}\uc2  that blocked a near-total ban. Immediately after the ruling, several Arizona clinics {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/24/arizona-abortion-ban-law"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stopped offering the procedure}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 For Americans seeking other types of care, the supreme court decision has had second-hand effects. In some states, patients {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/sep/26/us-abortion-bans-restrict-access-essential-medications"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 face delays and refusals}}}\uc2  in getting medications that can be used for abortions as well as the primary reason for being prescribed.\par \par \uc2 Some states require pharmacists to have a doctor\u8217\'20\'19s permission before filling a prescription for medication that can also be used to stop pregnancies, such as methotrexate, which is also used to treat arthritis, even if such prescriptions have been refilled in the past.\par \par \uc2 Bans on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at any point are in place in 12 Republican-led states. Florida and Utah have bans that go into effect after 15 and 18 weeks gestation, respectively. Clinics in Wisconsin have stopped providing abortions, amid litigation over whether a ban passed in 1849 is in place.\par \par \uc2 Indiana, Ohio and South Carolina saw total or six-week bans go into effect briefly before they were temporarily blocked. The Guttmacher researchers said 26 states were likely to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  within a year of Roe v Wade being overturned.\par \par \uc2 In Texas, 12 clinics have closed entirely while 11 are open without offering abortions. All three clinics that offered \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Louisiana have closed.\par \par \uc2 Reproductive rights are at issue across the US the 2022 midterm elections approach. Women and young people are expected to vote in bigger numbers than usual, given the appeal of the issue.\par \par \uc2 In Kansas, new-registered voters helped {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/03/kansas-abortion-rights-referendum-reaction"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reject a constitutional amendment}}}\uc2  that would have said there was no right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the state.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020221006eia6003bk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
