\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Texas attorney general who tried to flee  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  subpoena ordered to testify\b0\par\par\uc2 Coral Murphy Marcos in New York \par \uc2 599 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 October 2022\par 16:13 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Republican \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2  allegedly escaped home and jumped into truck driven by his wife to avoid being served by subpoena\par \par \uc2 The Texas attorney general, \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2 , must testify in court in an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  lawsuit after a federal judge reversed his decision to quash a subpoena filed by pro-choice interests.\par \par \uc2 Reproductive rights groups filed a class-action lawsuit against Paxton\u8217\'20\'19s office in August in an attempt to stop possible prosecution of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds that help women seek the procedure outside Texas, which has banned almost all \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 US district judge \uc2 Robert Pitman\uc2  granted a motion from lawyers representing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights non-profits, which asked the judge to require Paxton to testify.\par \par \uc2 Pitman had previously ruled to quash the subpoena upon Paxton\u8217\'20\'19s request on the basis that he could not be compelled to testify in a hearing as a high-ranking government official.\par \par \uc2 Emails from the lawyers for the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds show they tried repeatedly to serve Paxton through his attorneys before the hearing.\par \par \uc2 A process server then tried to serve Paxton with the subpoena at his residence. When he arrived at Paxton\u8217\'20\'19s home, according to an affidavit, the server knocked on the door and said he was there to deliver legal documents. Paxton later fled in a truck driven by his wife, state senator and Republican, Angela Paxton.\par \par \uc2 Paxton said in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KenPaxtonTX/status/1574608678854205440?s=20&t=Bv1rlLPSr3CXwbT3JoxJXA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tweet}}}\uc2  that he was trying to avoid \u8220\'20\'1Ca stranger lingering outside\u8221\'20\'1D his home when he fled in his truck.\par \par \uc2 Pitman\u8217\'20\'19s reversal on Tuesday came after he learned Paxton failed to disclose repeated emails from the plaintiffs.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe court will not sanction a scheme where Paxton repeatedly labels his threats of prosecution as real for the purposes of deterrence and as hypothetical for the purposes of judicial review,\u8221\'20\'1D Pitman wrote.\par \par \uc2 The plaintiffs in the lawsuit filed in Austin are Fund Texas Choice, the North Texas Equal Access Fund, the Lilith Fund for Reproductive Equity, Frontera Fund, The Afiya Center, West Fund, Jane\u8217\'20\'19s Due Process, Clinic Access Support Network and Dr Ghazaleh Moayedi.\par \par \uc2 Besides Paxton, a Republican, the suit names county and district attorneys who could enforce the state\u8217\'20\'19s near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. The law, known as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://capitol.texas.gov/billlookup/History.aspx?LegSess=87R&Bill=HB1280"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 House Bill 1280,}}}\uc2  was triggered into effect after the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  in June overturned Roe v Wade, ending the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 At least 14 states have banned most abortions. In September, a judge in Arizona ruled that a near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban must be enforced. The law, which dates back to 1864, orders a prison sentence of up to five years for anyone who helps a woman obtain an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling has also made patients face delays and refusals in getting medications that can be used for abortions as well as the primary reason given for being prescribed.\par \par \uc2 A 14-year-old girl in Arizona was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/nation/2022/10/05/abortion-arizona-arthritis-prescription-refill/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 denied a refill for a medication}}}\uc2  to treat her arthritis after the state\u8217\'20\'19s new \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law had taken effect. Emma Thompson had been taking methotrexate, a medication that is also used to end ectopic pregnancies, to treat her rheumatoid arthritis and osteoporosis.\par \par \uc2 Walgreens notified the family last month that they would need a doctor\u8217\'20\'19s permission before a pharmacist could fill the prescription despite having been refilled in the past.\par \par \uc2 In July, the \uc2 American College of Rheumatology\uc2  released a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.rheumatology.org/Portals/0/Files/Methotrexate-Guidance-Policymakers.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement recommending pharmacists}}}\uc2  to fulfill methotrexate prescriptions \u8220\'20\'1Cwithout delay and with the assumption that they are not being used to terminate a pregnancy\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020221005eia5002e7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
