\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Republican \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  pledges to sue over report he paid for  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Joanna Walters \par \uc2 6,263 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 October 2022\par 20:30 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Senate candidate in Georgia reportedly paid for the procedure for a former girlfriend in 2009Sign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 US politics live blog readers, it\u8217\'20\'19s been a vigorous day of news. There will be more from us tomorrow, following events as they happen. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is going to Florida to review the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/04/hurricane-ian-death-toll-florida-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 aftermath of Hurricane Ian}}}\uc2 . He\u8217\'20\'19ll meet with the state\u8217\'20\'19s Republican governor, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , during the visit.\par \par \uc2 For now, we\u8217\'20\'19re closing this blog. There is a great selection of news and other stories on our {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 front page}}}\uc2  and our blog of the war in Ukraine is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/oct/04/russia-ukraine-war-live-updates-ukrainians-break-through-russian-defences-in-south-advance-rapidly-in-east"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s how the day went:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Lawyers for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump}}}\uc2  have asked the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  today {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/04/herschel-walker-abortion-senate-biden-roe-wade-trump-latest-updates?page=with:block-633c91be8f0865e1775f43f1#block-633c91be8f0865e1775f43f1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to step into}}}\uc2  the legal fight over the classified documents seized during an \uc2 FBI\uc2  search of his Florida estate.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/04/herschel-walker-abortion-senate-biden-roe-wade-trump-latest-updates?page=with:block-633c8c488f08cd9030799f52#block-633c8c488f08cd9030799f52"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 condemned}}}\uc2  the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June decision}}}\uc2  by the rightdominated \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  to overturn Roe v Wade, as part of the pivotal Mississippi case Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization, and tear up half a century of constitutional \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the US. \u8220\'20\'1CThe Dobbs decision created a healthcare crisis in America,\u8221\'20\'1D she said at a White House event 100 days after the ruling.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 National Republican Senatorial Committee chairmanRick Scott and other prominent Republicans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/04/herschel-walker-abortion-senate-biden-roe-wade-trump-latest-updates?page=with:block-633c87608f08cd9030799f1f#block-633c87608f08cd9030799f1f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 are still behind}}}\uc2  Georgia Senate candidate \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  amid the scandal that\u8217\'20\'19s blown his already-rocky midterm election campaign sideways.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  told the Ukrainian president,\uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2 , earlier today that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/04/herschel-walker-abortion-senate-biden-roe-wade-trump-latest-updates?page=with:block-633c65278f0865e1775f422b#block-633c65278f0865e1775f422b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Washington will provide}}}\uc2  Kyiv with $625m in new security assistance, including High Mobility Artillery Rocket System (HIMARS) launchers, the White House said.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Giant tents for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/04/herschel-walker-abortion-senate-biden-roe-wade-trump-latest-updates?page=with:block-633c63ae8f08cd9030799d62#block-633c63ae8f08cd9030799d62"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 temporarily housing}}}\uc2  asylum seekers arriving in New York City after crossing the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-mexico-border"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US-Mexico border}}}\uc2  are being moved to an island off Manhattan from a remote corner of the Bronx, after storms raised concerns over flooding at the original site.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 There is no sign {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/04/herschel-walker-abortion-senate-biden-roe-wade-trump-latest-updates?page=with:block-633c5cfc8f0865e1775f41ae#block-633c5cfc8f0865e1775f41ae"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 of a lawsuit}}}\uc2  (yet) from Georgia Republican Senate candidate \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  against the Daily Beast following the latest chapter of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/22/herschel-walker-senate-republican-primary-georgia-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Walker}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s tumultuous campaign for the Senate {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/04/christian-walker-son-herschel-abortion-hypocrite"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unfolded last night}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 US climate envoy John Kerry{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/04/herschel-walker-abortion-senate-biden-roe-wade-trump-latest-updates?page=with:block-633c589d8f0865e1775f416b#block-633c589d8f0865e1775f416b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said today}}}\uc2  some western government ministers avoided a so-called \u8220\'20\'1Cfamily photo\u8221\'20\'1D of participants at climate talks in Kinshasa because they were uncomfortable with the presence of Russia\u8217\'20\'19s representative.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump asks supreme court to intervene in Mar-a-Lago dispute\par \par \uc2 Lawyers for former president {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump}}}\uc2  asked the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  today to step into the legal fight over the classified documents seized during an \uc2 FBI\uc2  search of his Florida estate.\par \par \uc2 The Trump team asked the court to overturn a lower court ruling and permit an independent arbiter, or special master, to review the roughly 100 documents with classified markings that were taken in the 8 August search at his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/mar-a-lago"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mar-a-Lago}}}\uc2  private club, resort and residence in Palm Beach, Florida, The Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 A three-judge panel last month limited the special master\u8217\'20\'19s review to the much larger tranche of non-classified {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/29/trump-mar-a-lago-special-master-judge-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 documents}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris: supreme court overturning of Roe v Wade 'created a healthcare crisis'\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  are convening the second meeting at the White House of the administration\u8217\'20\'19s Task Force on Reproductive Healthcare Access.\par \par \uc2 The vice-president condemned the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June decision}}}\uc2  by the right-dominated \uc2 US Supreme Court\uc2  to overturn Roe v Wade, as part of the pivotal Mississippi case Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization and tear up half a century of constitutional \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights across the US.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Dobbs decision created a healthcare crisis in America,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said.\par \par \uc2 She added: \u8220\'20\'1CA woman should have the freedom to make decisions about her own body. The government should not be making these decisions for the women of America.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Harris noted that if the \uc2 US Congress\uc2  could codify the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  previously afforded under Roe, rightwing leaders \u8220\'20\'1Ccould not ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and they could not criminalize providers, so it\u8217\'20\'19s important for everyone to know what\u8217\'20\'19s at stake. To stop these attacks on women, we need to pass this law,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 The vice-president also reminded people that ultra-conservative supreme court justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 , at the time of the June ruling, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/clarence-thomas-roe-gay-marriage-contraception-lgbtq"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appeared to offer a preview}}}\uc2  of the court\u8217\'20\'19s potential future rulings, and that they may return to the issues of curtailing contraception access and marriage equality, threatening LGBTQ+ rights, on the basis of constitutional privacy rights such as those just ripped up in the overturning of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 At the same event, the president said that he created the task force in the aftermath of the \uc2 Scotus\uc2  decision \u8220\'20\'1Cwhich most people would acknowledge is a pretty extreme decision,\u8221\'20\'1D in order to take a \u8220\'20\'1Cwhole of government approach\u8221\'20\'1D to addressing \u8220\'20\'1Cthe damage\u8221\'20\'1D of that ruling.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe court got Roe right nerarly 50 years ago. Congress should codify the protections of Roe and do it once and for all. But right now we are short a handful of votes, so the only way it\u8217\'20\'19s going to happen is if the American people make it happen.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMeanwhile, congressional Republicans are doubling down on their extreme position with the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/13/republican-national-abortion-ban-lindsey-graham"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 proposal for a national ban}}}\uc2 . Let me be clear what that means. It means that even if you live in a state where extremist Republican officials aren\u8217\'20\'19t running the show, your right to choose will still be at risk.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  address a meeting of the reproductive healthcare access taskforce. Photograph: Elizabeth Frantz/Reuters\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republican leaders stick with \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  despite crisis in his Senate campaign\par \par \uc2 National Republican Senatorial Committee chairman \uc2 Rick Scott\uc2  is still behind Georgia Senate candidate \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  amid the scandal that\u8217\'20\'19s blown a new hole in his midterm election campaign.\par \par \uc2 enltrNRSC Chairman \uc2 Rick Scott\uc2  sticks by \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 "When the Democrats are losing, as they are right now, they lie and cheat and smear their opponents. That\u8217\'20\'19s what\u8217\'20\'19s happening right now." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/fC59lVFzen"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/fC59lVFzen}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Julie Tsirkin (@JulieNBCNews) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JulieNBCNews/status/1577324959445180417?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 4, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Missouri Senator \uc2 Josh Hawley\uc2 , last noticed by national and international audiences when the House January 6 committee showed the tape of him {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/24/josh-hawley-republican-senator-ran-running-capitol-attack-kansas-city-star"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fleeing the Trumpist}}}\uc2  insurrectionists that he had previously publicly egged on, is also still walking the Walker walk.\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CYou have done enough, have you no sense of decency?\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/HawleyMO?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @HawleyMO}}}\par \par \uc2 Hawley affirms support for \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  after report Georgia Republican paid for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/zu8zWKvO0v"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/zu8zWKvO0v}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/9V2WJd6oVM"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/9V2WJd6oVM}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jewel Kelly For Missouri (@JewelCommittee) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JewelCommittee/status/1577370140877864960?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 4, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 The mother of the late congresswoman \uc2 Jackie Walorski\uc2  told {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/joebiden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden}}}\uc2  that her daughter was in \u8220\'20\'1Cheaven with Jesus\u8221\'20\'1D after the president apologized for mistakenly calling for Walorski during public remarks last week, despite her death in August.\par \par \uc2 During a private meeting in the Oval Office with the Walorski family on Friday, Biden apologized, the New York Post first reported, for a gaffe he made during a summit on food insecurity on 28 September, when he called into the audience to see if Walorski was in attendance, as the Republican representative from Indiana had served as co-chairperson of the House Hunger Caucus.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CJackie, are you here? Where\u8217\'20\'19s Jackie? She must not be here,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said, seeming to forget, or be unaware, that Walorski had died. The congresswoman was killed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/03/jackie-walorski-dead-indiana-congress-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in an August car accident}}}\uc2  in Indiana.\par \par \uc2 When asked about Biden\u8217\'20\'19s confusion, the White House press secretary, \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/28/biden-hunger-food-conference-congress-shutdown-machin-politics-latest?page=with:block-63348eae8f086841b84c3f2a#block-63348eae8f086841b84c3f2a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 downplayed the president\u8217\'20\'19s mistake}}}\uc2 , calling his comments \u8220\'20\'1Cnot all that unusual\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Jean-Pierre added that Biden was acknowledging the congresswoman\u8217\'20\'19s work and keeping her \u8220\'20\'1Ctop of mind\u8221\'20\'1D because he would be meeting with her family later that week.\par \par \uc2 While speaking to the president, the late congresswoman\u8217\'20\'19s mother, Martha \u8220\'20\'1CMert\u8221\'20\'1D Walorski, told Biden that her daughter was in heaven when he asked for her.\par \par \uc2 Jackie\u8217\'20\'19s father Keith Walorski said Biden and his staff were \u8220\'20\'1Cvery, very good\u8221\'20\'1D to his family but they do not plan on voting for him in 2024 because they strongly disagree with his policy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMost of the Biden agenda is not what you would call a conservative Christian agenda,\u8221\'20\'1D Keith Walorski said. \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s who we are.\u8221\'20\'1D The rest of that article is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/04/joe-biden-apologizes-mistake-dead-congresswoman-jackie-walorski"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 At an Oval Office meeting in July 2020, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  asked aides if {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ghislaine-maxwell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ghislaine Maxwell}}}\uc2 , the former girlfriend of the financier and sex offender \uc2 Jeffrey Epstein\uc2  who had been arrested on sex trafficking charges, had named him among influential contacts she might count upon to protect her.\par \par \uc2 According to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2022/oct/02/confidence-man-review-maggie-haberman-donald-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new book}}}\uc2  by Maggie Haberman of the \uc2 New York Times\uc2 , Trump asked \u8220\'20\'1Ccampaign advisers \u8230\'20\'26 \u8216\'20\'18You see that article in the [New York] Post today that mentioned me?\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe kept going, to silence. \u8216\'20\'18She say anything about me?\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Epstein was convicted and sentenced in Florida in 2008, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2008/07/01/business/01epstein.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on state prostitution charges}}}\uc2 . He was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2019/07/06/nyregion/jeffrey-epstein-arrested-sex-trafficking.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 arrested}}}\uc2  again in July 2019, on sex-trafficking charges. He {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2019/aug/10/jeffrey-epstein-dead-prison-report-latest"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 killed himself}}}\uc2  in prison in New York a month later.\par \par \uc2 Links between Epstein, Maxwell and prominent associates including Trump and Prince Andrew have stoked press speculation ever since.\par \par \uc2 Maxwell, the daughter of the British press baron Robert Maxwell, was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/jul/02/ghislaine-maxwell-arrest-jeffrey-epstein-charges-latest-fbi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 arrested}}}\uc2  in New Hampshire on 2 July 2020.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://pagesix.com/2020/07/04/ghislaine-maxwell-prepared-to-snitch-on-big-names-to-save-herself/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 story}}}\uc2  which seemed to worry Trump, according to Haberman, appeared in the celebrity-focused Page Six section of the New York tabloid on 4 July 2020.\par \par \uc2 It quoted Steve Hoffenberg, an Epstein associate, as saying: \u8220\'20\'1CGhislaine thought she was untouchable \u8211\'20\'13 that she\u8217\'20\'19d be protected by the intelligence communities she and Jeffrey helped with information: the Israeli intelligence services, and Les Wexner, who has given millions to Israel; by Prince Andrew, President Clinton and even by President Trump, who was well-known to be an acquaintance of her and Epstein\u8217\'20\'19s.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Maxwell was ultimately {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/dec/29/ghislaine-maxwell-sex-trafficking-trial-verdict"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 convicted}}}\uc2  in New York in December 2021, on five of six charges relating to the sex-trafficking of minors. In July 2022, she was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/28/ghislaine-maxwell-sentencing-sex-trafficking-epstein"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sentenced}}}\uc2  to 20 years in prison.\par \par \uc2 Haberman\u8217\'20\'19s eagerly awaited book, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2022/oct/02/confidence-man-review-maggie-haberman-donald-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Confidence Man: The Making of Donald Trump and the Breaking of America}}}\uc2 , is published in the US on Tuesday. Check out the whole report {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2022/oct/04/trump-ghislaine-maxwell-epstein-maggie-haberman-book-confidence-man"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 From left, American real estate developer \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his girlfriend (and future wife), former model Melania Knauss, financier (and future convicted sex offender) \uc2 Jeffrey Epstein\uc2 , and British socialite Ghislaine Maxwell pose together at the Mar-a-Lago club, Palm Beach, Florida, February 12, 2000. Photograph: Davidoff Studios Photography/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 In February this year, Prince Andrew {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2022/feb/15/prince-andrew-and-virginia-giuffre-reach-settlement-in-principle"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 settled}}}\uc2  a civil case brought by an Epstein victim who alleged she was forced to have sex with the royal. Andrew vehemently denies wrongdoing but has suffered {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/15/jeffrey-epstein-prince-andrew-queen-death"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a collapse of his standing}}}\uc2  in public and private.\par \par \uc2 Then US president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , right, and then-first lady Melania Trump, left, accompanied by Britain's Prince Andrew, leave after a tour of Westminster Abbey in London, June 3, 2019. Photograph: Matt Dunham/AP\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  is emphasizing how much \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  want the \uc2 US Congress\uc2  to enshrine the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the US into national legislation.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s 100 days today since the now firmly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2022/oct/02/us-supreme-court-cases-monumental-impact-democracy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 right-leaning US Supreme Court}}}\uc2  in late June {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturned Roe v Wade}}}\uc2  and ripped up half a century of a constitutional, federal {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rights to seek an \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  in the US.\par \par \uc2 Jean-Pierre said the court \u8220\'20\'1Ctook away nearly 50 years of protections and we have seen women respond and Americans respond\u8230\'20\'26they have made their voices loud and clear and I expect we will continue to see that type of reaction.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She added, of services such as \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and contraception: \u8220\'20\'1CThese are difficult decisions that women should be making for themselves with their health care provider, no-one else should be making that decision for them, not Republican officials\u8230\'20\'26\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Reuters adds {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.usnews.com/news/top-news/articles/2022-10-04/factbox-u-s-abortion-restrictions-mount-after-overturn-of-roe-v-wade#:~:text=Oct.%204%2C%202022%2C%20at%201%3A26%20p.m.&text=(Reuters)%20%2D%20Thirteen%20states%20have,years%20of%20federal%20abortion%20protections."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in this report}}}\uc2  that 13 US states have begun enforcing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans since the court decision, a swift and dramatic change after nearly 50 years of federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  has begun today\u8217\'20\'19s media briefing and is reminding everyone that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and first lady Jill Biden are going to Fort Myers, Florida, tomorrow, in the aftermath of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/04/hurricane-ian-death-toll-florida-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 devastating }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/04/hurricane-ian-death-toll-florida-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hurricane Ian}}}\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 Yesterday, the US president and first lady were in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/puerto-rico"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Puerto Rico}}}\uc2  to announce funding in the wake of Hurricane Fiona that smashed into the island territory last month just before Ian howled in from the Atlantic.\par \par \uc2 Biden {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/oct/03/puerto-rico-biden-hurricane-fiona-aid"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 admitted that aid}}}\uc2  and assistance to Puerto Rico in the five years since Hurricane Maria hit there and now Hurricane Fiona has not been timely or sufficient.\par \par \uc2 Jean-Pierre says Biden will meet {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/30/ron-desantis-hurricane-ian-florida-sandy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Florida\u8217\'20\'19s Republican}}}\uc2  governor {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/01/desantis-hurricane-ian-aid-disaster-relief-florida"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ron DeSantis}}}\uc2  while he\u8217\'20\'19s in the state tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s our colleague Martin Pengelly on the governor last week:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/30/ron-desantis-hurricane-ian-florida-sandy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ron DeSantis changes with the wind as Hurricane Ian prompts flip-flop on aid}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 It has been called a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ProfNickStephan/status/1485837489952759808"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 textbook example}}}\uc2  of discrimination against Black voters in the US. And a ruling on it from the supreme court is expected any day.\par \par \uc2 It isn\u8217\'20\'19t the kind of explicit voting discrimination, like poll taxes and literacy tests, that kept voters from the polls in the south during the Jim Crow era. Instead, it is more subtle.\par \par \uc2 Let us walk you through the case with our visual explainer.\par \par \uc2 The case focuses on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/alabama"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Alabama}}}\uc2 , where the Republican-controlled legislature, like states across the US, recently completed the once-a-decade process of redrawing the boundaries of congressional maps. If partisan politicians exert too much control over the redistricting process, they can effectively engineer their own victories, or blunt the advantages of the other side, by allocating voters of particular political persuasions and backgrounds to particular districts.\par \par \uc2 Under the new districts, Black people make up 25% of the Alabama\u8217\'20\'19s population, but comprise a majority in just one of the state\u8217\'20\'19s seven districts.\par \par \uc2 In late January, a panel of three federal judges issued a 225-page opinion explaining how the state {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jan/25/alabama-electoral-maps-discriminate-black-voters-federal-court-rules"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was discriminating}}}\uc2  against Black voters.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBlack voters have less opportunity than other Alabamians to elect candidates of their choice to Congress,\u8221\'20\'1D the panel wrote. The judges gave Alabama 14 days to come up with a new plan and said the state had to draw two districts where Black voters comprise a majority.\par \par \uc2 Check out the whole terrific {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2022/feb/04/alabama-gerrymandering-republicans-black-voters-map"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 interactive here}}}\uc2 , from Guardian US colleagues Sam Levine and Andrew Witherspoon.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  today has been hearing a hugely important case that could ultimately gut one of the most powerful remaining provisions of the Voting Rights Act, the 1965 law that is one of America\u8217\'20\'19s most powerful anti-discrimination measures.\par \par \uc2 The case deals with the seven new congressional districts that Alabama adopted last year. Six of those districts are represented by a Republican in Congress and one is represented by a Democrat. That Democratic district is 55% Black, the only Black majority district in the state.\par \par \uc2 The plaintiffs in the case argue that Alabama Republicans who control the state legislature packed as many Black voters as possible into the one Democratic district to weaken the influence of Black voters overall in the state. Black people make up about a quarter of Alabama\u8217\'20\'19s population, but only are a majority in one district.\par \par \uc2 The central question in the case is how much mapmakers are required to take race into account when drawing districts. The plaintiffs argue that the Voting Rights Act requires Alabama to draw a second district where Black people make up a majority.\par \par \uc2 But Alabama argues that doing so would require the state to sort voters based on race, which is unconstitutional.\par \par \uc2 If the court, which has been extremely hostile to voting rights and the Voting Rights Act in particular, were to embrace that latter view, it would make it enormously difficult to challenge districts in the future.\par \par \uc2 A three judge panel agreed with the plaintiffs and ordered the state to redraw the map. But the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  stepped in earlier this year and halted that order.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 Interim summary\par \par \uc2 Hello US politics live blog readers, it\u8217\'20\'19s a lively day for news and there\u8217\'20\'19s much more to come in the next few hours, but here\u8217\'20\'19s where things stand right now:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  told Ukrainian presidentVolodymyr Zelenskiy earlier today that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/04/herschel-walker-abortion-senate-biden-roe-wade-trump-latest-updates?page=with:block-633c65278f0865e1775f422b#block-633c65278f0865e1775f422b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Washington will provide}}}\uc2  Kyiv with $625 million in new security assistance, including High Mobility Artillery Rocket System (HIMARS) launchers, the White House said.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Giant tents for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/04/herschel-walker-abortion-senate-biden-roe-wade-trump-latest-updates?page=with:block-633c63ae8f08cd9030799d62#block-633c63ae8f08cd9030799d62"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 temporarily housing}}}\uc2  asylum seekers arriving in New York City after crossing the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-mexico-border"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US-Mexico border}}}\uc2  are being moved to an island off Manhattan from a remote corner of the Bronx, after storms raised concerns over flooding at the original site.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 There is no sign {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/04/herschel-walker-abortion-senate-biden-roe-wade-trump-latest-updates?page=with:block-633c5cfc8f0865e1775f41ae#block-633c5cfc8f0865e1775f41ae"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 of a lawsuit}}}\uc2  (yet) from Georgia Republican Senate candidate \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  against the Daily Beast following the latest chapter of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/22/herschel-walker-senate-republican-primary-georgia-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Walker}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s tumultuous campaign for the Senate {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/04/christian-walker-son-herschel-abortion-hypocrite"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unfolded last night}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 US climate envoy John Kerry{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/04/herschel-walker-abortion-senate-biden-roe-wade-trump-latest-updates?page=with:block-633c589d8f0865e1775f416b#block-633c589d8f0865e1775f416b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said today}}}\uc2  some western government ministers avoided a so-called \u8220\'20\'1Cfamily photo\u8221\'20\'1D of participants at climate talks in Kinshasa because they were uncomfortable with the presence of Russia\u8217\'20\'19s representative.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Herschel Walker \u8217\'20\'19s Senate campaign {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/04/herschel-walker-abortion-senate-biden-roe-wade-trump-latest-updates?page=with:block-633c305a8f0865e1775f3fab#block-633c305a8f0865e1775f3fab"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is in crisis}}}\uc2  in Georgia after the latest twist in the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  row became very personal and turns the heat up further in the furious midterms battle for control of the \uc2 US Senate\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 US to give Ukraine more rocket launchers, Biden tells Zelenskiy\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  told Ukrainian president \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2  earlier today that Washington will provide Kyiv with $625 million in new security assistance, including High Mobility Artillery Rocket System (HIMARS) launchers, the White House said.\par \par \uc2 The US president was joined in the call by vice president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , the White House said in a statement, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 The president underscored that Washington will never recognize Russian annexation of Ukrainian territory, it added.\par \par \uc2 Biden:\par \par \uc2 pledged to continue supporting Ukraine as it defends itself from Russian aggression for as long as it takes,\u8221\'20\'1D the statement said.\par \par \uc2 Check out all the \uc2 Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s detailed reporting on Russia\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Ukraine {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 , and you can follow our global live blog on the war {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/oct/04/russia-ukraine-war-live-updates-ukrainians-break-through-russian-defences-in-south-advance-rapidly-in-east"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Giant tents for temporarily housing asylum seekers arriving in New York City after crossing the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-mexico-border"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US-Mexico border}}}\uc2  are being moved to an island off Manhattan from a remote corner of the Bronx, after storms raised concerns over flooding at the original site.\par \par \uc2 Mayor Eric Adams announced Monday that the city\u8217\'20\'19s humanitarian relief center will now be on Randall\u8217\'20\'19s Island, which sits in the waters between Manhattan, Queens and the Bronx. It\u8217\'20\'19s connected by five bridges to the three boroughs, and people can take buses or walk off the island to reach the city\u8217\'20\'19s subway system, \uc2 The Associated Press\uc2  reports.\par \par \uc2 The center\u8217\'20\'19s tents had been put up in a parking lot at Orchard Beach, in the northeast part of the Bronx on Long Island Sound, where access to public transportation is limited. Images online showed water ponding at the site following rainfall over the weekend.\par \par \uc2 In a statement announcing the change, Adams said while the city could have made the original location work, moving the center \u8220\'20\'1Cis the most efficient and effective path forward.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 An aerial photo taken with a drone shows emergency tents being assembled to house asylum seekers bussed to New York City from Texas and Arizona by Republican governors there, without any warning to or liaison with the city. The tents were in the process of being raised last week in the parking lot of Orchard Beach, in the Bronx borough. Photograph: Justin Lane/\uc2 EPA\par \par \uc2 The city\u8217\'20\'19s plan for Orchard Beach had been met with concern by immigration advocates, who cited its inaccessibility among other reasons, and that concern extended to the new location.\par \par \uc2 The city must look to other solutions instead of tent cities, where our clients will be isolated, vulnerable to extreme weather, and far from public transportation and other critical services,\u8221\'20\'1D the \uc2 Legal Aid Society\uc2  and the \uc2 Coalition for the Homeless\uc2  said in a statement today.\par \par \uc2 Here is the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/27/there-had-to-be-somewhere-better-new-york-criticized-for-building-migrant-tents-in-flood-prone-lot"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s report}}}\uc2  on the tent camp when it was first set up in the Bronx.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/27/there-had-to-be-somewhere-better-new-york-criticized-for-building-migrant-tents-in-flood-prone-lot"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18There had to be somewhere better\u8217\'20\'19: New York criticized for building migrant tents in flood-prone lot}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 No sign of lawsuit from Georgia Republican Senate candidate \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  against Daily Beast\par \par \uc2 When the latest chapter of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/22/herschel-walker-senate-republican-primary-georgia-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Herschel Walker}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s tumultuous campaign for the Senate {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/04/christian-walker-son-herschel-abortion-hypocrite"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unfolded last night}}}\uc2 , the former \uc2 NFL\uc2  player noted that he was going to sue the Daily Beast the following morning.\par \par \uc2 It looks like the ex-running back is now running back on that. Is morning AM or just, before lunch? No sign yet of a suit from the GOP candidate in his Senate race against incumbent and Democrat, \uc2 Raphael Warnock\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Was it a bluff? There\u8217\'20\'19s also been mention that maybe it\u8217\'20\'19s coming {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/10/03/politics/herschel-walker-abortion/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tomorrow morning}}}\uc2 . It remains to be seen how voters will respond to all this. The Daily Beast reported last night that despite being an anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  fundamentalist in his campaigning in these mid-terms, in the past {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/04/herschel-walker-anti-abortion-senate-nominee-denies-media-report-he-paid-for-abortion-in-2009"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Walker paid}}}\uc2  for an ex to have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . He\u8217\'20\'19s called that story a flat-out lie, though, with close scrutiny, his denials are not as watertight as he\u8217\'20\'19d like them to sound.\par \par \uc2 Critics are salivating about what might surface in discovery if Walker plowed ahead with a lawsuit, to say nothing of success being very much against the odds for him even if he had a flawless reputation in such a suit in the US, anyway.\par \par \uc2 enltrWho wants to bet Hershel will NEVER file suit? The Discovery will destroy his case.\par \par \uc2 Now- every woman who was paid by a congressman in office now to have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should come forward before the elections to expose the hypocrisy.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Carmela (@denise_yak) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/denise_yak/status/1577097391836082176?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 4, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Now there is light pouring through the cracks and there may be no lawsuit at all.\par \par \uc2 enltrNEW: Walker\u8217\'20\'19s lawyer tells me \u8220\'20\'1CWe are currently considering our options but no final decision has been made on the future handling of this matter.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Pq482nRRAC"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/Pq482nRRAC}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Elizabeth Campbell (@ECampbell360) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ECampbell360/status/1577295326926569474?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 4, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 Russia's war in Ukraine further complicates global efforts on climate crisis\par \par \uc2 US climate envoy \uc2 John Kerry\uc2  said today some western government ministers avoided a so-called \u8220\'20\'1Cfamily photo\u8221\'20\'1D of participants at climate talks in Kinshasa because they were uncomfortable with the presence of Russia\u8217\'20\'19s representative.\par \par \uc2 Russia\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/oct/04/russia-ukraine-war-latest-what-we-know-on-day-223-of-the-invasion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 invasion of Ukraine}}}\uc2  has shattered relations with the west, complicating international efforts to cooperate on global crises like the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/climate-crisis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 climate crisis}}}\uc2 , Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 All top-level participants were meant to pose for the picture on Monday after the start of the three-day event in the Congolese capital \u8211\'20\'13 the last chance for countries to discuss strategies before the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/cop27"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cop27}}}\uc2  climate summit in Egypt in November.\par \par \uc2 Some European delegates were notably absent from the flag-decked stage. Of those who attended, dozens of dignitaries, including the Egyptian foreign minister, \uc2 Sameh Shoukry\uc2 , and the United Nations Deputy Secretary General \uc2 Amina Mohammed\uc2 , waited for over 10 minutes before the photo was taken without the absentees.\par \par \uc2 They didn\u8217\'20\'19t want to show up for the picture,\u8221\'20\'1D Kerry said when asked about the apparent no-shows.\par \par \uc2 He is in Kinshasa for the talks but also did not join the photo.\par \par \uc2 It was not clear exactly how many delegates chose to skip the shoot, but an official with the British delegation confirmed envoy {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2022/jun/08/alok-sharma-in-running-to-be-uns-global-climate-chief"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Alok Sharma}}}\uc2  was among them.\par \par \uc2 An \uc2 EU\uc2  official also confirmed its envoy had not joined the photo and would do the same at similar photo opportunities at Cop27.\par \par \uc2 I don\u8217\'20\'19t know if a big decision was made. I do know that all the ministers of these countries were very troubled by the presence of the Russian. Russia is not a country that is treated exactly like others at the moment,\u8221\'20\'1D Kerry told reporters.\par \par \uc2 Kerry said delegates\u8217\'20\'19 sudden camera-shyness would not affect negotiations:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe photo is the photo, but the work at Cop, it continues.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Russian climate envoy Ruslan Edelgeriyev, who stood at the far end of the back row for the picture, told Reuters he had not noticed anyone refusing to join the shoot due to his presence.\par \par \uc2 He said that discussing \u8220\'20\'1Cmatters irrelevant to climate change will get us nowhere\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The US special presidential envoy for climate, \uc2 John Kerry\uc2 , and the deputy secretary general of the United Nations, \uc2 Amina Mohammed\uc2 , meet in Kinshasa, Democratic Republic of Congo. Photograph: Justin Makangara/Reuters\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  has extensive coverage of the war in Ukraine, which began in February with Russia\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of its neighbor. You can follow news developments via our global war live blog, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/oct/04/russia-ukraine-war-live-updates-ukrainians-break-through-russian-defences-in-south-advance-rapidly-in-east"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Pennsylvania\u8217\'20\'19s open race to succeed retiring Republican US Senator \uc2 Pat Toomey\uc2 , meanwhile, is one of those on a razor\u8217\'20\'19s edge.\par \par \uc2 Axios calls the battle between {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/12/john-fetterman-pennsylvania-rally-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrat John Fetterman}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/03/pennsylvania-republican-primary-mehmet-oz-wins-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republican Mehmet Oz}}}\uc2  , who\u8217\'20\'19s backed by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1Cthe majority-making race\u8221\'20\'1D in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-midterm-elections-2022"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 midterm elections}}}\uc2  next month.\par \par \uc2 Various outlets have Oz {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://elections-daily.com/2022/10/04/ratings-update-republicans-and-democrats-gain-in-under-the-radar-races/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gaining ground}}}\uc2  against Fetterman in their nasty, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/23/dr-oz-aide-john-fetterman-stroke-pennsylvania"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 personal campaign}}}\uc2 , who was placed six points ahead of his rival in a recent USA Today {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/politics/2022/10/04/fetterman-leads-oz-pennsylvania-senate-race/8161323001/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 but also showing the Republican for governor of Pennsylvania, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/27/republican-pennsylvania-doug-mastriano-abortion-murder"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Doug Mastriano}}}\uc2 , tumbling {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://elections-daily.com/2022/10/04/ratings-update-republicans-and-democrats-gain-in-under-the-radar-races/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 badly}}}\uc2  in his race against Democratic candidate and state attorney general {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/22/pennsylvania-josh-shapiro-democrat-republican-rival-doug-mastriano"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Josh Shapiro}}}\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2  campaigning in Philadelphia. Photograph: Cory Clark/NurPhoto/REX/\uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 Axios notes in its morning news letter that Pennsylvania is the tightest Senate race in the country, and adds that: \u8220\'20\'1CBesides Pennsylvania, the other {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://link.axios.com/click/29258065.58865/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuY29va3BvbGl0aWNhbC5jb20vcmF0aW5ncy9zZW5hdGUtcmFjZS1yYXRpbmdzP3V0bV9zb3VyY2U9bmV3c2xldHRlciZ1dG1fbWVkaXVtPWVtYWlsJnV0bV9jYW1wYWlnbj1uZXdzbGV0dGVyX2F4aW9zYW0mc3RyZWFtPXRvcA/5b74658adabb342d565838ffC7d1f8285"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tossup}}}\uc2  Senate races are in Nevada, Georgia and Wisconsin.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, yet another report sharply criticizes medic Oz\u8217\'20\'19s track record in experimenting on animals.\par \par \uc2 Jezebel {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://jezebel.com/dr-oz-s-scientific-experiments-killed-over-300-dogs-e-1849609272"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports that}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 A review of 75 studies published by Mehmet Oz between 1989 and 2010 reveals the Republican Senate candidate\u8217\'20\'19s research killed over 300 dogs and inflicted significant suffering on them and the other animals used in experiments.\par \par \uc2 Oz, the New Jersey resident who\u8217\'20\'19s currently running for \uc2 U.S. Senate\uc2  from Pennsylvania, was a \u8220\'20\'1Cprincipal investigator\u8221\'20\'1D at the Columbia University Institute of Comparative Medicine labs for years and assumed \u8220\'20\'1Cfull scientific, administrative, and fiscal responsibility for the conduct\u8221\'20\'1D of his studies.\par \par \uc2 Over the course of 75 studies published in academic journals reviewed by Jezebel, Oz\u8217\'20\'19s team conducted experiments on at least 1,027 live animal subjects that included dogs, pigs, calves, rabbits, and small rodents.\par \par \uc2 Thirty-four of these experiments resulted in the deaths of at least 329 dogs, while two of his experiments killed 31 pigs, and 38 experiments killed 661 rabbits and rodents.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a further quick summary of some of the controversial background about \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2 , the Republican candidate for Senate in Georgia who\u8217\'20\'19s challenging Democratic incumbent \uc2 Raphael Warnock\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 This one comes {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2022/10/04/1126692026/herschel-walker-rejects-abortion-report-georgia-republican"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 from NPR}}}\uc2  with a bit of help from \uc2 The Associated Press\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The allegation against Walker is the latest in a series of stories about the football legend\u8217\'20\'19s past that has rocked the first-time candidate\u8217\'20\'19s campaign in one of the most competitive Senate races in the country. Earlier this year, Walker acknowledged reports that he had three children he had not previously talked about publicly.\par \par \uc2 Walker has often boasted of his work helping service members and veterans struggling with mental health. Yet The Associated Press reported in May that various records showed he overstated his role in a for-profit program that is alleged to have preyed upon veterans and service members while defrauding the government.\par \par \uc2 The AP also has reported that a review of public records detailed accusations that Walker repeatedly threatened his ex-wife\u8217\'20\'19s life, exaggerated claims of financial success and alarmed business associates with unpredictable behavior. Walker himself has at times discussed his long struggle with mental illness.\par \par \uc2 As a Senate hopeful, Walker has supported a national ban on abortions with no exceptions for cases involving rape, incest or a woman\u8217\'20\'19s health being at risk \u8212\'20\'14 particularly notable at a time when Roe v. Wade has been overturned by the Supreme Court and Democrats in Congress have been discussing codifying \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights into federal law.\par \par \uc2 Also noting that Walker calls reasons for having an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  because you\u8217\'20\'19ve been raped, perhaps even by a relative, or because your health or even your life are at risk \u8220\'20\'1Cexcuses.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 A reminder that even before this {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/04/christian-walker-son-herschel-abortion-hypocrite"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 latest scandal}}}\uc2 , \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  was becoming notorious for saying weird nonsense on the campaign trail.\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CHow can global warming be real if it\u8217\'20\'19s cold outside? A lot of money it\u8217\'20\'19s going to trees. Don\u8217\'20\'19t we have enough trees?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur good air floats over to China\u8217\'20\'19s bad air. China\u8217\'20\'19s bad air moves over to our good air space, which would force us to clean that back up.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 ~\uc2 Herschel Walker{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/4DrmL8frL8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/4DrmL8frL8}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Debbie Downer stands with Ukraine???????? (@JohnstonSharon) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JohnstonSharon/status/1577311833291362305?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 4, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Getting nastier:\par \par \uc2 enltrYes, Christian Walker is a spoiled brat, an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Influencer?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Influencer}}}\uc2  who was more than happy to go along with Herschel's campaign and yes, Christian has a lying, shitty deadbeat dad with secret kids everywhere. Both things can be true at once. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/GwwRYOrMq2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/GwwRYOrMq2}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Elizabeth #WomensRightsAreHumanRights (@TheHopsbride) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TheHopsbride/status/1577311782066130944?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 4, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Georgia conservative pundit:\par \par \uc2 enltrI'd largely thought Walker could pull this off despite his baggage. I'll see what sort of response he mounts, but given text messages tonight, Georgia GOP'ers are praying for Dr. Oz to win. Walker hasn't mounted a good response to any attack, and this is brutal, probably a KO.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Erick Erickson (@EWErickson) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/EWErickson/status/1577108284514844672?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 4, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 No live cage fight after all?\par \par \uc2 enltrThe \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  and \uc2 Raphael Warnock\uc2  debate scheduled for October 14 has been canceled. \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  did not want to debate \uc2 Raphael Warnock\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Adam Parkhomenko (@AdamParkhomenko) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AdamParkhomenko/status/1577160623523516416?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 4, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 If the battle for control of the \uc2 US Senate\uc2  overall is on a knife edge in these midterm elections, certain states\u8217\'20\'19 races are on a razor\u8217\'20\'19s edge.\par \par \uc2 The congressional upper chamber has been split 50-50 since the 2020 presidential election, with Democrats only maintaining the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/06/jon-ossoff-wins-georgia-runoff-election-democrats-senate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 upper hand}}}\uc2  because they have the White House and therefore the vice president, who also serves as president of the senate, has the deciding vote. Even then, when most legislation needs 60 votes to pass the senate and, in cases when 51 votes will do losing just one democratic senator {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/31/joe-manchin-hails-deal-inflation-reduction-act"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sinks a bill}}}\uc2 , progress for the Democrats on 2020 election promises {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jan/11/joe-biden-voting-rights-filibuster-congress-georgia-us-politics-latest-covid?page=with:block-61ddf42c8f0841d0f6ca6e3e#block-61ddf42c8f0841d0f6ca6e3e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has been difficult}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But struggles notwithstanding, of course the Democrats are desperate to keep control of the senate while the Republicans are desperate to flip it.\par \par \uc2 And Georgia is crucial. It\u8217\'20\'19s also incredibly evocative because in early 2021, Democrats \uc2 Raphael Warnock\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/06/jon-ossoff-wins-georgia-runoff-election-democrats-senate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 John Ossoff}}}\uc2  both won their run-offs to capture seats and become first-time senators and in the process {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/06/jon-ossoff-wins-georgia-runoff-election-democrats-senate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hand control}}}\uc2  of the senate to the Democrats.\par \par \uc2 Ossoff unseated Republican senator \uc2 David Perdue\uc2  in that race, who tried to make a comeback in these midterms by challenging current state governor \uc2 Brian Kemp\uc2  in the GOP gubernatorial primary, but lost despite (because of??) being endorsed by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 And when Warnock also unseated a Republican to win his run-off, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/06/raphael-warnock-first-black-senator-from-georgia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pastor became}}}\uc2  the first every Black US Senator from Georgia. Now, less than two years into his term, he\u8217\'20\'19s being challenged for his seat {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/22/herschel-walker-senate-republican-primary-georgia-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 by a rarity}}}\uc2 , a Black man running as a Republican who counts white conservatives as his base \u8211\'20\'13 and has no experience in politics, one \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Prior to the latest scandal for Walker, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/campaign/3666657-warnock-leading-walker-by-5-points-in-georgia-senate-race-poll/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Warnock was slightly ahead}}}\uc2  in the polls.\par \par \uc2 Guardian US is running a series of special news features this week on Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s role in the midterm elections, here\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/03/stacey-abrams-democrats-georgia-governor-brian-kemp"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 part one}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/04/georgia-immigrant-vote-midterms"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 part two}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Walker campaign crisis in Georgia over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  row turns heat up further in furious midterms battle for Senate\par \par \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2 , the controversial Republican candidate in Georgia for a vital \uc2 US Senate\uc2  seat, is attempting to weather the latest tempest that has tossed his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-midterm-elections-2022"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 midterm election}}}\uc2  campaign from turbulent into full-blown crisis.\par \par \uc2 The news broke last night that the former \uc2 NFL\uc2  football {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/22/herschel-walker-senate-republican-primary-georgia-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 player turned political candidate}}}\uc2 , who is campaigning on a hard anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  line, had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/04/herschel-walker-anti-abortion-senate-nominee-denies-media-report-he-paid-for-abortion-in-2009"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 paid for an \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  for a former girlfriend in 2009, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thedailybeast.com/pro-life-herschel-walker-paid-for-girlfriends-abortion-georgia-senate?ref=home"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a report}}}\uc2  by the Daily Beast.\par \par \uc2 As the Beast puts it in the strap below the headline to its report: \u8220\'20\'1CThe woman has receipts \u8211\'20\'13 and a \u8216\'20\'18get well\u8217\'20\'19 card she says the football star, now a Senate candidate, sent her.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Walker blasted out a top-line denial via \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , calling the story overall a flat-out lie, also calling it a \u8220\'20\'1CDemocrat attack\u8221\'20\'1D, while the Beast insists its article is backed up to the hilt. Walker says he\u8217\'20\'19ll sue the Beast today.\par \par \uc2 enltrRegarding the latest Democrat attack: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/OjrDcGak95"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/OjrDcGak95}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  (@HerschelWalker) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/HerschelWalker/status/1577075271470964737?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 3, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 He also appeared on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/fox-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fox News}}}\uc2  to blame politics, saying: \u8220\'20\'1CNow everyone knows how important this seat is and they [Democrats] will do anything to win this seat. They wanted to make it about anything except inflation, crime and the border being wide open.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But Walker\u8217\'20\'19s son, 23-year-old Christian Walker, then responded on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 . Yikes.\par \par \uc2 enltrI know my mom and I would really appreciate if my father \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  stopped lying and making a mockery of us.\par \par \uc2 You\u8217\'20\'19re not a \u8220\'20\'1Cfamily man\u8221\'20\'1D when you left us to bang a bunch of women, threatened to kill us, and had us move over 6 times in 6 months running from your violence.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Christian Walker (@ChristianWalk1r) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ChristianWalk1r/status/1577104266543497216?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 4, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 And:\par \par \uc2 enltrI don\u8217\'20\'19t care about someone who has a bad past and takes accountability. But how DARE YOU LIE and act as though you\u8217\'20\'19re some \u8220\'20\'1Cmoral, Christian, upright man.\u8221\'20\'1D You\u8217\'20\'19ve lived a life of DESTROYING other peoples lives. How dare you.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Christian Walker (@ChristianWalk1r) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ChristianWalk1r/status/1577105221775679488?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 4, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 The sitting Senator from Georgia whom \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  is challenging, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/05/georgia-runoff-elections-ossoff-warnock-perdue-loeffler"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrat Raphael Warnock}}}\uc2  , is striving to stay above the fray \u8211\'20\'13 maybe hoping the former running back will be hoisted by his own petard?\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 Georgia Republican Senate candidate \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2 's campaign in crisis over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  story\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers, it\u8217\'20\'19s a lively start to the day as midterm election candidates for the \uc2 US Senate\uc2  are making news, so is \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , the CDC on Covid and pro-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  politicians on the rights of women 100 days after the \uc2 US Supreme Court\uc2  ripped up Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what\u8217\'20\'19s already cooking in Washington and midterm campaigns:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2 , the Republican challenging Democratic sitting Senator \uc2 Raphael Warnock\uc2  in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/24/us-midterm-primaries-key-races-watch"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 crucial state}}}\uc2  of Georgia this election, has pledged to sue the Daily Beast today over a story last night that, despite campaigning as an anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  hardliner, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/04/herschel-walker-anti-abortion-senate-nominee-denies-media-report-he-paid-for-abortion-in-2009"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he paid for an \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  for a former girlfriend in 2009. Walker says the story\u8217\'20\'19s a lie. His son then called his father a liar; this thing is boiling over and scalding his Senate chances \u8211\'20\'13 fatally?\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has apologized to the family of the late Indiana Republican \uc2 Jackie Walorski\uc2 , admitting to a gaffe last week when he spoke at an event and was looking around for her, calling publicly \u8220\'20\'1Cwhere\u8217\'20\'19s Jackie?\u8221\'20\'1D, when the congresswoman had been killed in a horrific car crash in August. The US president invited her parents to the Oval Office to talk late last week, the New York Post {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nypost.com/2022/10/03/wheres-jackie-walorskis-mom-tells-biden-in-heaven-as-he-says-sorry-for-gaffe/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden and the vice-president,\uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , this afternoon will speak at the second meeting of the administration\u8217\'20\'19s special task force on reproductive healthcare access, at the White House. Cabinet members will attend, including the health secretary, \uc2 Xavier Becerra\uc2 , and the education secretary, \uc2 Miguel Cardona\uc2 . That\u8217\'20\'19s expected at 3.30pm ET, and the White House press secretary, \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2 , is scheduled to hold the daily press briefing at 1pm.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  (CDC) last night announced the CDC it will discontinue a country-by-country list of advisories that inform travelers of risk and restrictions in each relating to Covid-19. The federal agency will post a notice if there is a concerning variant emerging in a country or a significant change in travel recommendations.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020221004eia4001xo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
