\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Abbott and O\u8217\'20\'19Rourke clash on  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  and immigration in Texas debate\b0\par\par\uc2 Valerie Gonzalez in Edinburg, Texas \par \uc2 775 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 October 2022\par 14:45 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Democratic challenger aiming to wrest governorship away from rightwing Abbott in November election\par \par \uc2 Immigration, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and border security all came up in Friday\u8217\'20\'19s contentious, rapid-paced gubernatorial debate in Texas, where \uc2 Beto O\u8217\'20\'19Rourke\uc2  is trying to help the Democrats wrest back the far-right leaning state from Greg Abbott and the Republicans.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/01/uvalde-school-shooting-beto-o-rourke-texas-greg-abbott"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Abbott and his challenger O\u8217\'20\'19Rourke}}}\uc2  kept their sole debate fierce and lively in spite of an almost completely empty venue on the \uc2 University of Texas Rio Grande Valley\uc2  campus in Edinburg. The lack of a meaningful audience was one of several conditions imposed by the governor, according to O\u8217\'20\'19Rourke\u8217\'20\'19s camp, who described the offer to debate as a \u8220\'20\'1Ctake it or leave it\u8221\'20\'1D type of deal.\par \par \uc2 Even though the election will fall during a midterm, non-presidential election year, voters are expected to be more motivated to go to the polls than before in large part because of the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s elimination of the federal {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  rights established by Roe v Wade in 1973.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m governing from principles,\u8221\'20\'1D Abbott said when asked if he had moved too far to the right. After the supreme court reversed Roe v Wade in June, Texas enacted a ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  without no exceptions, even in cases of rape or incest.\par \par \uc2 Abbott said he and his wife are Catholics who have been against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  their whole lives, and he described wanting to share the joys of adoption, which the couple experienced when they adopted their daughter.\par \par \uc2 The governor touted healthcare options and resources available to women after they give birth, but he said an emergency contraception pill \u8211\'20\'13 like Plan B \u8211\'20\'13 could be used to stop a pregnancy before it happens.\par \par \uc2 O\u8217\'20\'19Rourke countered: \u8220\'20\'1CThis election is about reproductive freedom, but I\u8217\'20\'19ve got to respond to this, this silliness on Plan B \u8211\'20\'13 this comment he made about eliminating rape in the state of Texas. This is an attack on women.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Abbott has said in the past months he would \u8220\'20\'1Celiminate rape\u8221\'20\'1D when pressed about the exclusion of exceptions to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  for victims of rape.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s arguable that rapists enjoy more rights under Greg Abbott than their victims do because they can sue the families of their victims if [the families] help [the rapists\u8217\'20\'19] victims get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D O\u8217\'20\'19Rourke said, referring to a Texas law that allows private citizens to sue those who help someone receive an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The debate was held in south Texas, a much-visited area by Abbott, who has increased law enforcement\u8217\'20\'19s presence at the border with Mexico ostensibly to deter human and drug smuggling largely through a program called Operation Lone Star.\par \par \uc2 Abbott\u8217\'20\'19s administration has poured over $4bn in taxpayer money into the program. And, as the moderator and O\u8217\'20\'19Rourke pointed out, the arrival of immigrants on the Texas border has reached record levels.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CZero dollars should be going to Operation Lone Star and that\u8217\'20\'19s what it would be if we had a president enforcing the immigration laws of the United States of America,\u8221\'20\'1D Abbott said, echoing his frequent criticism about the Joe Biden White House\u8217\'20\'19s approach to the border.\par \par \uc2 Under Operation Lone Star, members of Texas\u8217\'20\'19s national guard and troopers from the state\u8217\'20\'19s public safety department have been forcibly deployed to the border. Both agencies have since had members die amid the mission.\par \par \uc2 O\u8217\'20\'19Rourke has previously expressed opposition to the presence of national guard troops at the border. But Friday, he said he favored partnering local sheriffs\u8217\'20\'19 deputies and state troopers with national guard troops who volunteer for the mission.\par \par \uc2 It isn\u8217\'20\'19t the first time O\u8217\'20\'19Rourke has modified political positions. He supported a complete ban on high-powered rifles when he unsuccessfully ran for president in 2019, but in gun-friendly Texas, he\u8217\'20\'19s pushed for requiring people to be at least 21 years old rather than just 18 before they can legally buy such weapons.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Abbott at one point found himself defending his taxpayer-funded bussing of migrants and asylum seekers from Texas to Democratic-controlled cities as a way to reduce stress on border communities. But O\u8217\'20\'19Rourke dismissed those trips as mere \u8220\'20\'1Cpolitical stunts\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Before the debate started, 40% of the crowd of 15 allowed into the session leaned toward voting for Abbott, 27% for O\u8217\'20\'19Rourke and 33% were undecided. They were polled again afterward. The results indicated Abbott moved up slightly to 43% \u8211\'20\'13 but O\u8217\'20\'19Rourke swayed more undecided voters and nearly doubled his gains to 50%.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020221001eia1001p5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
