\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Biden takes aim at food insecurity with first hunger conference in 50 years \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein \par \uc2 5,627 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 September 2022\par 20:10 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Biden releases national hunger and nutrition strategy, which includes a slate of goals to help end food insecuritySign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/28/biden-hunger-food-conference-congress-shutdown-machin-politics-latest?page=with:block-633459128f08ef7e8107bf94#block-633459128f08ef7e8107bf94"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rolled out his plan}}}\uc2  to fight hunger in the United States, with an eye towards ending it by 2030. Meanwhile, Hurricane Ian {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/28/hurricane-ian-florida-tracker-path-latest-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 made landfall in Florida}}}\uc2  amid fears it could do grievous damage to its west coast.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else happened today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The supreme court{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/28/biden-hunger-food-conference-congress-shutdown-machin-politics-latest?page=with:block-63344a0b8f086841b84c3b48#block-63344a0b8f086841b84c3b48"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is getting ready for its next term}}}\uc2 , and is expected to receive an update regarding the investigation into the leak of its draft decision overturning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/28/biden-hunger-food-conference-congress-shutdown-machin-politics-latest?page=with:block-633453508f084e56bac575b0#block-633453508f084e56bac575b0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called for negotiating }}}\uc2  with Russia to end the war in Ukraine and mulled himself, of course, as leading the delegation. Meanwhile, a new book {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/28/biden-hunger-food-conference-congress-shutdown-machin-politics-latest?page=with:block-63344ed48f086841b84c3b89#block-63344ed48f086841b84c3b89"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 revealed}}}\uc2  further disquieting details of his presidency.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Jury selection{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/28/biden-hunger-food-conference-congress-shutdown-machin-politics-latest?page=with:block-633475ce8f08ef7e8107c14c#block-633475ce8f08ef7e8107c14c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 continued}}}\uc2  in the trial of five Oath Keepers accused of seditious conspiracy for their actions related to the January 6 insurrection.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The White House denied a report that Treasury secretary Janet Yellen{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/28/biden-hunger-food-conference-congress-shutdown-machin-politics-latest?page=with:block-633497bd8f084e56bac57957#block-633497bd8f084e56bac57957"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 could depart the administration next year}}}\uc2  as it looks to reframe its fight against inflation.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 As she sometimes does, singer-songwriter and trained flautist Lizzo played a flute during her performance in Washington on Tuesday. But it wasn\u8217\'20\'19t just any instrument. Lizzo played notes through a more than 200-year-old crystal flute made for President James Madison and on loan from the \uc2 Library of Congress\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The largest library in the world also has the largest collection of flutes in the world, and when its librarian Carla Hayden heard that Lizzo was coming to town, she asked if she was interested in playing Madison\u8217\'20\'19s instrument at her show.\par \par \uc2 The library has written {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://blogs.loc.gov/loc/2022/09/its-about-danged-time-lizzo-at-the-library/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an amusing blog about what happened next}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 When Library curator Carol Lynn Ward-Bamford walked the instrument onstage and handed it to Lizzo to a roar of applause, it was just the last, most visible step of our security package. This work by a team of backstage professionals enabled an enraptured audience to learn about the Library\u8217\'20\'19s treasures in an exciting way.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs some of y\u8217\'20\'19all may know I got invited to the \uc2 Library of Congress\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Lizzo said, after placing her own flute (named Sasha Flute) down on its sparkling pedestal, which had emerged minutes earlier from the center of the stage. Following the aforementioned, highly popular \uc2 Twitter\uc2  exchange between Lizzo the Librarian of Congress, the crowd knew what was coming.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI want everybody to make some noise for James Madison\u8217\'20\'19s crystal flute, y\u8217\'20\'19all!\u8221\'20\'1D They made more noise than the instrument, having been at the Library for 81 years, has been exposed to in quite some time. Maybe ever.\par \par \uc2 She took it gingerly from Ward-Bamford\u8217\'20\'19s hands, walked over to the mic and admitted: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m scared.\u8221\'20\'1D She also urged the crowd to be patient. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s crystal, it\u8217\'20\'19s like playing out of a wine glass!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 NBC4 Washington has footage of the moment she played it at the show:\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 Last April, at least nine people were bitten by a rabid red fox that stalked Capitol Hill, sparing neither lawmaker nor reporter alike.\par \par \uc2 The animal was caught and euthanized by the DC health department, while those bitten were given many shots to stop rabies or any other infections. But the story, surprisingly, does not end there.\par \par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal reports that one of those bit, Democratic representative \uc2 Ami Bera\uc2  of California, introduced legislation to cover the cost of rabies vaccines for the uninsured:\par \par \uc2 enltrThe rabid fox that terrorized the Capitol grounds has led to legislation.\par \par \uc2 Rep. \uc2 Ami Bera\uc2  (D., Calif.), one of the victims, introduced legislation to reduce the cost of the rabies vaccine for uninsured Americans\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Natalie Andrews (@nataliewsj) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/nataliewsj/status/1575175579850010625?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 28, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrFrom Bera's office: The Affordable Rabies Treatment for Uninsured Act would establish a program to reimburse health care providers for furnishing post-exposure prophylaxis (PEP) to uninsured individuals.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Natalie Andrews (@nataliewsj) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/nataliewsj/status/1575183334048956416?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 28, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrThe CDC estimates that 60,000 Americans receive PEP each year after possible exposure to rabies. Although rabies is a vaccine-preventable disease, costs for patients can be high, with treatment ranging from $1,200 to $6,500.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Natalie Andrews (@nataliewsj) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/nataliewsj/status/1575183335940231168?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 28, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2022/apr/07/rabid-red-fox-capitol-hill-caught-euthanized"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Rabid red fox that bit nine on Capitol Hill caught and euthanized}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 A man whose actions likely changed the course of American history is petitioning for his freedom after decades behind bars, the Associated Press reports:\par \par \uc2 Sirhan Sirhan, who assassinated presidential candidate \uc2 Robert F Kennedy\uc2  in 1968, is asking a judge to free him from prison by reversing a decision by the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/california"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 California}}}\uc2  governor to deny him parole.\par \par \uc2 Sirhan shot Kennedy in 1968 at the Ambassador hotel in Los Angeles, moments after the US senator from New York claimed victory in California\u8217\'20\'19s pivotal Democratic presidential primary. He wounded five others during the shooting.\par \par \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 , the California governor, in January overruled two parole commissioners who had found that Sirhan no longer was a risk. The governor argued Sirhan remains a threat to the public and has not taken responsibility for a crime that changed American history.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/28/sirhan-sirhan-robert-f-kennedy-california"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sirhan Sirhan, man who assassinated Robert Kennedy, asks judge to free him}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 One of the biggest problems the Biden administration is facing is the state of the economy.\par \par \uc2 It was supposed to be one of the bright spots. Unemployment has ticked down steadily since \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  took office in January 2021 with Americans still reeling from the mass layoffs that occurred as Covid-19 broke out less than a year prior. But the rise in inflation that sent prices for gasoline, food and housing spiking throughout 2021 and into the next year did a number on his approval ratings, and there are signs in the administration that heads may roll, at least figuratively.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2022/09/28/janet-yellen-treasury-midterms-shuffle"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Axios reported yesterday}}}\uc2  that the White House is preparing for the exit of Treasury secretary \uc2 Janet Yellen\uc2 , as well as \uc2 Brian Deese\uc2 , the director of the National Economic Council. Chair of the Council of Economic Advisers \uc2 Cecilia Rouse\uc2  is also expected to return to teaching next year.\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s myriad reasons why inflation has climbed during the Biden era at rates not seen since the 1980s, including the actions of the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 , the independent central bank where the Democratic president has appointed many of the top officials. However, a shake-up of the White House economic staff could give Biden the opportunity to reframe his approach to controlling price growth in the world\u8217\'20\'19s largest economy. As the report notes, much of what happens will depend on the outcome of the midterms, particularly if Republicans take the Senate, which would confirm any new Treasury secretary or other cabinet-level position. It\u8217\'20\'19s also worth noting that White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  today denied that Yellen or Deese were going anywhere, the Associated Press reports:\par \par \uc2 enltr. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PressSec?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @PressSec}}}\uc2  says neither Treasury Sec. \uc2 Janet Yellen\uc2  or NEC director \uc2 Brian Deese\uc2  are part of plans for turnover post midterm elections.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Fatima Hussein (@fatimathefatima) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/fatimathefatima/status/1575194183706771456?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 28, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 Oregon is the site of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/polls/governor/2022/oregon/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a close race}}}\uc2  to replace Democratic governor \uc2 Kate Brown\uc2 , who has reached her term limits. As she prepares to exit the governor\u8217\'20\'19s mansion, Amanda Waldroupe spoke to Brown about her surprising tactic for reforming the criminal justice system:\par \par \uc2 Last October, \uc2 Kate Brown\uc2 , the governor of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/oregon"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Oregon}}}\uc2 , signed an executive order granting clemency to 73 people who had committed crimes as juveniles, clearing a path for them to apply for parole.\par \par \uc2 The move marked the high point in a remarkable arc: as Brown approaches the end of her second term in January, she has granted commutations or pardons to 1,147 people \u8211\'20\'13 more than all of Oregon\u8217\'20\'19s governors from the last 50 years combined.\par \par \uc2 The story of clemency in Oregon is one of major societal developments colliding: the pressure the Covid-19 pandemic put on the prison system and growing momentum for criminal justice reform.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s also a story of a governor\u8217\'20\'19s personal convictions and how she came to embrace clemency as a tool for criminal justice reform and as an act of grace, exercising the belief that compassionate mercy and ensuring public safety are not mutually exclusive.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf you are confident that you can keep people safe, you\u8217\'20\'19ve given victims the opportunity to have their voices heard and made sure their concerns are addressed, and individuals have gone through an extensive amount of rehabilitation and shown accountability, what is the point of continuing to incarcerate someone, other than retribution?\u8221\'20\'1D Brown said in a June interview.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/28/oregon-governor-kate-brown-clemency"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The story of one US governor\u8217\'20\'19s historic use of clemency: \u8216\'20\'18We are a nation of second chances\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  responded to questions on why \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  referred to Indiana representative \uc2 Jackie Walorski\uc2  during his speech on hunger today, when the congresswoman died last month in a car accident.\par \par \uc2 During today\u8217\'20\'19s press briefing, Jean-Pierre said that Biden\u8217\'20\'19s remarks were \u8220\'20\'1Cnot all that unusual\u8221\'20\'1D and that he was acknowledging Walorski\u8217\'20\'19s previous work as co-chair of the House Hunger Caucus.\par \par \uc2 Jean-Pierre added that the congresswoman was \u8220\'20\'1Ctop of mind\u8221\'20\'1D, as Biden meets with her family this week.\par \par \uc2 enltrBiden was \u8220\'20\'1Cacknowledging her incredible work,\u8221\'20\'1D White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  said when asked about the incident later, adding that Biden had already planned to welcome her family to the White House for a bill signing on Friday. \u8220\'20\'1CShe was on top of mind,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jarrett Renshaw (@JarrettRenshaw) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JarrettRenshaw/status/1575186494079520769?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 28, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 In other news, a California man who pleaded guilty to plotting to bomb the state\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic party headquarters following the defeat of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will be sentenced today, reported the Associated Press.\par \par \uc2 Ian Benjamin Rogers, a Napa, California resident, pleaded guilty in May to conspiring to destroy the headquarters building and other properties in Sacramento by fire or explosives.\par \par \uc2 Rogers also pleaded guilty to possessing an explosive device and possessing a machine gun as part of a plea agreement that could get him seven to nine years in federal prison.\par \par \uc2 Rogers and Jarrod Copeland had been charged by prosecutors in San Francisco for planning to attack buildings they associated with Democrats following Trump\u8217\'20\'19s defeat in the 2020 US presidential election.\par \par \uc2 Rogers\u8217\'20\'19 attorney, Colin Cooper, spoke about his client before today\u8217\'20\'19s sentencing, emphasizing how remorseful Rogers is: \u8220\'20\'1CMr Rogers feels awful for letting anybody down. He\u8217\'20\'19s been in custody for a year and a half. He\u8217\'20\'19s never been in trouble before. Every single day he expresses regret and remorse for any involvement he\u8217\'20\'19s had in anything and all he\u8217\'20\'19s asking for now is for people to give him a chance to prove that he has redemptive qualities.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden also warned oil and gas companies not to raise prices on the hundreds of thousands of Florida residents preparing for Hurricane Ian, reports the Associated Press.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDo not, let me repeat, do not use this as an excuse to raise gasoline prices or gouge the American people,\u8221\'20\'1D said Biden today while speaking about his plan to fight hunger in the US.\par \par \uc2 Biden added that the natural disaster \u8220\'20\'1Cprovides no excuse for price increases at the pump\u8221\'20\'1D and that he will ask federal officials to determine if price gouging is going on.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/28/hurricane-ian-florida-tracker-path-latest-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hurricane Ian nears landfall in south-western Florida as officials warn of \u8216\'20\'18catastrophic impact\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 live }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/28/biden-hunger-food-conference-congress-shutdown-machin-politics-latest?page=with:block-633459128f08ef7e8107bf94#block-633459128f08ef7e8107bf94"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rolled out his plan}}}\uc2  to fight hunger in the United States, with an eye towards ending it by 2030. Meanwhile, Hurricane Ian {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/28/biden-hunger-food-conference-congress-shutdown-machin-politics-latest?page=with:block-63345dd98f086841b84c3c4c#block-63345dd98f086841b84c3c4c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is churning towards}}}\uc2  Florida and threatening to do the state grievous damage.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has happened today so far:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The supreme court{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/28/biden-hunger-food-conference-congress-shutdown-machin-politics-latest?page=with:block-63344a0b8f086841b84c3b48#block-63344a0b8f086841b84c3b48"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is getting ready for its next term}}}\uc2 , and is expected to receive an update regarding the investigation into the leak of its draft decision overturning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/28/biden-hunger-food-conference-congress-shutdown-machin-politics-latest?page=with:block-633453508f084e56bac575b0#block-633453508f084e56bac575b0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called for negotiating }}}\uc2  with Russia to end the war in Ukraine and mulled himself, of course, as leading the delegation. Meanwhile, a new book {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/28/biden-hunger-food-conference-congress-shutdown-machin-politics-latest?page=with:block-63344ed48f086841b84c3b89#block-63344ed48f086841b84c3b89"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 revealed}}}\uc2  further disquieting details of his presidency.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Jury selection{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/28/biden-hunger-food-conference-congress-shutdown-machin-politics-latest?page=with:block-633475ce8f08ef7e8107c14c#block-633475ce8f08ef7e8107c14c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 continued}}}\uc2  in the trial of five Oath Keepers accused of seditious conspiracy for their actions related to the January 6 insurrection.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 US condemns Iranian attacks in Iraqi Kurdistan\par \par \uc2 The White House has decried recent Iranian drone and missile strikes in Iraqi Kurdistan, as Tehran faces protests over the death of a Kurdish woman in the custody of its morality police.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s the statement from national security adviser Jake Sullivan:\par \par \uc2 The United States strongly condemns the drone and missile attack launched against Iraq\u8217\'20\'19s Kurdistan region earlier today. We stand with Iraq\u8217\'20\'19s leaders in the Kurdistan region and Baghdad in condemning these attacks as an assault on the sovereignty of Iraq and its people. Iranian leaders continue to demonstrate flagrant disregard not only for the lives of their own people, but also for their neighbors and the core principles of sovereignty and territorial integrity enshrined in the UN Charter. Iran cannot deflect blame from its internal problems and the legitimate grievances of its population with attacks across its borders. Its flagrant use of missiles and drones against its neighbors, as well as its providing of drones to Russia for its war of aggression in Ukraine and to proxies throughout the Middle East region, should be universally condemned. The United States will continue to pursue sanctions and other means to disrupt Iran\u8217\'20\'19s destabilizing activities across the Middle East region.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/sep/27/how-death-kurdish-woman-galvanised-women-iran-mahsa-amini"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 How the death of a Kurdish woman galvanised women all over Iran}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Earlier today, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://centerforpolitics.org/crystalball/articles/notes-on-the-state-of-politics-sept-28-2022/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sabato\u8217\'20\'19s Crystal Ball}}}\uc2 , written by politics gurus at the \uc2 University of Virginia\uc2 , moved their prediction for the Pennsylvania governor\u8217\'20\'19s race from \u8220\'20\'1Cleans Democratic\u8221\'20\'1D to \u8220\'20\'1Clikely Democratic\u8221\'20\'1D. The news below was cited as one of the reasons why, because it shows that the Republican nominee in the race holds beliefs about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  that appear to be beyond what the state\u8217\'20\'19s voters will support. Here\u8217\'20\'19s the latest from \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/martin-pengelly"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Martin Pengelly}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Asked in 2019 if he was saying women should be charged with murder for violating an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban he proposed, \uc2 Doug Mastriano\uc2 , now the Republican nominee for governor of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/pennsylvania"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pennsylvania}}}\uc2 , said: \u8220\'20\'1CYes, I am.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Mastriano was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.witf.org/2019/11/14/heart-beat-bill-under/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 talking to WITF}}}\uc2 , a radio station, about a bill he sponsored as a state senator.\par \par \uc2 The bill would have barred most abortions when a fetal heartbeat could be detected, which is usually about six weeks into pregnancy, before many women know they are pregnant.\par \par \uc2 Mastriano was asked: \u8220\'20\'1CYou can give me a yes or no on this. Would that woman who decided to have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  which would be considered an illegal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  be charged with murder?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Mastriano said: \u8220\'20\'1COK, let\u8217\'20\'19s go back to the basic question there. Is [a fetus] a human being? Is that a little boy or girl? If it is, it deserves equal protection under the law.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He was asked: \u8220\'20\'1CSo you\u8217\'20\'19re saying yes?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Mastriano {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SawyerHackett/status/1574820825835999244"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CYes, I am. If it\u8217\'20\'19s a human being, if it\u8217\'20\'19s an American citizen there, a little baby, I don\u8217\'20\'19t care what nationality it is, it deserves equal rights before the law.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 NBC News reported the remark on Tuesday. Mastriano did not immediately comment.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/27/republican-pennsylvania-doug-mastriano-abortion-murder"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Top Republican urged murder charges for women who defied \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere in Washington, jury selection is ongoing in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/27/oath-keepers-stewart-rhodes-trial-january-6-joe-biden-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-6332f2488f08ef7e8107b294#block-6332f2488f08ef7e8107b294"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the trial of five Oath Keepers members}}}\uc2  on seditious conspiracy charges related to their role in the January 6 insurrection at the US Capitol, including founder Stewart Rhodes.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s far from determinative of how the trial will go, but Politico has some details of the jurors that have been selected to serve thus far:\par \par \uc2 enltrUPDATE from the Oath Keepers trial:\par \par \uc2 -Four of five prospective jurors questioned today have made the initial cut, bringing two day total to 14 potential jurors.\par \par \uc2 -The four: A defense lobbyist, \uc2 Northrop Grumman\uc2  defense contractor, DOD civilian employee and patent office employee.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Cheney (@kyledcheney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kyledcheney/status/1575153705493856258?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 28, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrThe one juror stricken was a lawyer at a big firm who handles international dispute resolution. He had RTed or liked tweets calling Rs nihilists and comparing Trump supporters to fascists. He said he could be a fair juror and would set aside views but admitted it\u8217\'20\'19d be a struggle.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Cheney (@kyledcheney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kyledcheney/status/1575155024463798273?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 28, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrThe defense objected to two of the jurors that Mehta ultimately qualified. One of them, the DOD employee, said he viewed Oath Keepers as anti-democracy and willing to overturn election by force but would be willing to have his views contradicted by evidence.\par \par \uc2 Among the reasons\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Cheney (@kyledcheney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kyledcheney/status/1575156282428108800?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 28, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrHe said he\u8217\'20\'19d served on a jury before and found a murder suspect not guilty, and he repeatedly said he would fairly assess evidence in the case, even if it contradicted views informed by media he consumes.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Cheney (@kyledcheney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kyledcheney/status/1575156821655953408?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 28, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden closes up with some remarks on the Covid pandemic, describing the grassroots efforts to get food to struggling families as \u8220\'20\'1Cpeople doing God\u8217\'20\'19s work\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Then he makes a claim that\u8217\'20\'19s worth fact checking. Biden said that the high level of food insecurity caused by the pandemic has come down thanks to the American Rescue Plan and the economy rebounding. One in 10 families struggled to feed their families in 2021 \u8211\'20\'13 which is back around pre-pandemic levels, but the numbers are rising quickly this year since key economic policies like the child tax credit, expanded food stamps eligibility and universal free school meals were not renewed by Congress.\par \par \uc2 Biden knows, and the new strategy suggests, that tackling economic and racial inequalities through things like a living wage, closing the Medicaid coverage gap, and affordable childcare and housing are the only ways to really eradicate food poverty.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s why the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/28/joe-biden-hunger-nutrition-donation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $8bn pledged }}}\uc2  by private corporations, universities, foundations and nonprofits may help a bit, but will not tackle the structural and systemic issues that cause poverty and racial inequalities, which is what\u8217\'20\'19s needed in order to end hunger and cut the burden of diet-related diseases in the richest country in the world.\par \par \uc2 Still, Biden ended with a rallying call: \u8220\'20\'1CIn America, no child should go to bed hungry. No parent should die of a preventable disease\u8230\'20\'26 this is the United States of America, nothing is beyond our capacity.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/28/joe-biden-hunger-nutrition-donation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 More than $8bn pledged to Joe Biden\u8217\'20\'19s goal of ending hunger}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 With universal free lunches a long long way off, one of the new food strategy\u8217\'20\'19s more interesting commitments is about supporting schools in making meals from scratch and buying produce from local farmers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis will lead to healthier meals and strengthen rural economies,\u8221\'20\'1D said Biden. This is a welcome nod to the urgent need to redesign our globalised food system, which is dominated by a handful of transnational monopolies like \uc2 Tyson Foods\uc2 . Today, \uc2 Tyson\uc2  pledged to give more free chicken to schools \u8211\'20\'13 rather ironic, some might argue, given the company\u8217\'20\'19s track record on worker conditions, unhealthy processed foods and animal welfare.\par \par \uc2 Biden also rightly emphasises the \u8220\'20\'1Cwe are what we eat\u8221\'20\'1D mantra, given that diets high in processed fatty, sugary, salty foods have led to at least 35% of adults being obese in 19 states, and one in 10 Americans having diabetes.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CScience changes things. People are realising that certain diseases are affected by what they eat. The more we can spread the word and educate people, the more we\u8217\'20\'19ll see changes,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 Not quite so sure about him suggesting that the link between our diets and disease is new information \u8211\'20\'13 the evidence has been overwhelming for decades now, but powerful business interests like the sugar, fast food and meat packing industries have often stymied government regulations to improve food labelling and reduce the toxicity of processed foods. Still, a commitment to piloting food prescriptions for people on Medicaid and Medicare is a definite thumbs up.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden made an unfortunate gaffe in his remarks, referencing someone named Jackie and asking if she was in attendance. He may have been referring to \uc2 Jackie Walorski\uc2 , a Republican representative from Indiana who died in an August car accident.\par \par \uc2 Walorski was co-chair of the House Hunger Caucus dedicated to fighting food insecurity in the United States. The chair of the caucus, Democrat \uc2 Jim McGovern\uc2  of Massachusetts, was in attendance at the event. Here\u8217\'20\'19s video of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s comment:\par \par \uc2 enltrPresident Biden seems to forget that Rep. \uc2 Jackie Walorski\uc2  (R-IN) died in a car crash in August, seeking her out in the audience:\par \par \uc2 "Jackie, are you here? Where's Jackie? She must not be here." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/inzKDHrPK7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/inzKDHrPK7}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1575145859133706251?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 28, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/03/jackie-walorski-dead-indiana-congress-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Indiana congresswoman Jackie Walorski dies in car crash}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden is going into the main pillars of the national hunger and nutrition strategy released on Tuesday, which includes a slew of goals to help end food insecurity, give people more information and options to eat more healthily, and help folks take up regular physical activity.\par \par \uc2 Unfortunately, the goals are more a call to action, as Congress has ended Covid-era policies like the universal free school meals program and the expanded child tax credits which had massively reduced food insecurity and child poverty in the US.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m calling on Congress to make the expanded child tax credit permanent. We\u8217\'20\'19ve tried, and didn\u8217\'20\'19t get it done the first time, but we\u8217\'20\'19ll get it done next time,\u8221\'20\'1D said Biden rather optimistically, given the extremely unlikely scenario that the Democrats win convincing majorities in the midterms.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 Turning to the issue of hunger, Biden begins with reference to the transformational changes inspired by Nixon\u8217\'20\'19s 1969 conference, and that he believes the advances in nutrition and technology since then can make \u8220\'20\'1CAmerica healthier and stronger as a nation.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He references the reduction in child poverty from one in four kids 30 years ago, to one in 20 today as evidence that his \u8220\'20\'1Cbold goal to end hunger by 2030 and lower the toll of diet related diseases\u8221\'20\'1D can become a reality.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden has kicked off his remarks by warning of the destructive power of Hurricane Ian as it approaches the Florida coast, and pledging that his administration will help affected states recover.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI made it clear to the governor and the mayors that the federal government is ready to help in every single way possible\u8230\'20\'26 We\u8217\'20\'19ll be there every step of the way,\u8221\'20\'1D the president said.\par \par \uc2 After knocking out power to Cuba when it struck the island, emergency planners fear Ian could cause grievous damage to Florida. Follow \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s live blog for the latest on the storm:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/28/hurricane-ian-florida-tracker-path-latest-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hurricane Ian barrels towards Florida as officials warn of looming catastrophe \u8211\'20\'13 live}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 More than 500 people are attending today\u8217\'20\'19s White House conference on hunger, nutrition and health - the first since former president \uc2 Richard Nixon\uc2  hosted one in 1969.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has just begun giving his remarks, and he will be appearing alongside cabinet members Tom Vilsack, secretary of agriculture, and \uc2 Xavier Becerra\uc2 , secretary of health and human services, as well as a crew of legislators with a special interest in hunger and nutrition including \uc2 Debbie Stabenow\uc2 , \uc2 Cory Booker\uc2 , and \uc2 Jim McGovern\uc2 . Also, there is ambassador Susan Rice, the White House domestic policy advisor and Spanish chef Jos\u233\'00\'E9 Ram\u243\'00\'F3n Andr\u233\'00\'E9s Puerta, founder of \uc2 World Central Kitchen\uc2 , a non-profit providing meals in the wake of natural disasters and in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Biden has frequently commented on the long lines of cars at food banks during the first years of the pandemic, when government shutdowns and widespread layoffs and furloughs led to millions of families relying on food aid for the first time ever. Still, it\u8217\'20\'19s not a new phenomena; while the introduction of means-tested food stamps, free school lunches and other nutrition benefits has led to a decline in food insecurity since Nixon\u8217\'20\'19s conference, it\u8217\'20\'19s barely budged in the past two decades, with major spikes during the Great Recession and first year of Covid.\par \par \uc2 Nixon will forever be President Watergate, but it\u8217\'20\'19s worth remembering some landmark progressive laws approved with bipartisan support during his time in the White House, a feat that seems almost impossible today given the deep political polarisation. Major environmental justice policy wins included food stamps, the National Environmental Protection Act, the Clean Water Act, and the creation of the \uc2 Environmental Protection Agency\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re awaiting president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s address at the White House Conference on Hunger, Nutrition, and Health, where he\u8217\'20\'19s expected to outline how his administration will reach its goal of ending hunger in the United States by 2030.\par \par \uc2 You can watch his live remarks delivered in Washington below:\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Democratic House speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  has endorsed the White House\u8217\'20\'19s push, saying in a statement, \u8220\'20\'1CPresident Kennedy once told the World Food Congress: \u8216\'20\'18We have the capacity to eliminate hunger from the face of the earth in our lifetime. We need only the will.\u8217\'20\'19 Inspired by the tireless efforts of advocates across the country, House Democrats will never relent in our fight to build a future free from hunger, food insecurity and diet-related disease.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 For those whom a book about Trump isn\u8217\'20\'19t enough, here\u8217\'20\'19s the former president calling for negotiating with Russia to end the war in Ukraine, and mulling himself as head of the group.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what he said, from Politico:\par \par \uc2 enltrSeems unlikely that Trump will be taken up on his offer to negotiate an end to the Russia-Ukraine war {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/oJEsMlEN9n"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/oJEsMlEN9n}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jonathan Lemire (@JonLemire) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JonLemire/status/1575119990436626435?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 28, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 In 2016, New Jersey\u8217\'20\'19s Republican former governor \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2  asked \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to more forcefully condemn white supremacists. The then-presidential candidate took his time in doing so, saying, \u8220\'20\'1CA lot of these people vote.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s one of the many anecdotes about Trump revealed in \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.amazon.com/Confidence-Man-Making-Breaking-America/dp/0593297342/ref=tmm_hrd_swatch_0?_encoding=UTF8&qid=1664372677&sr=8-1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Confidence Man: The Making of Donald Trump and the Breaking of America}}}\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D a new book about his presidency from \uc2 New York Times\uc2  reporter Maggie Haberman, which {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2022/09/28/trump-book-white-house-bomb-mexico/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Washington Post obtained}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The review also finds Trump openly pondering when liberal supreme court justice \uc2 Ruth Bader Ginsburg\uc2  might pass away from her cancer, and asking whether it would be possible to bomb drug labs in Mexico after a top health department official showed up in uniform to advise him of the approach.\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s a lot more to the book, which comes out next Tuesday. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more of what the Post found:\par \par \uc2 Throughout the book, Trump is portrayed as transactional and narcissistic \u8212\'20\'14 at times charming, at other times cruel \u8212\'20\'14 but always attuned to his own political fortunes, no matter the issue. During his meeting in the Oval Office with \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  in 2016, he eschewed policy and asked Obama how he kept his approval ratings high, according to the book. He told advisers that he needs people such as Pennsylvania Senate nominee Mehmet Oz (R) in office in case the election is challenged in 2024 or they try to impeach him again.\par \par \uc2 When Trump first met British Prime Minister Theresa May, he soon turned the conversation to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CSome people are pro-life, some people are pro-choice. Imagine if some animals with tattoos raped your daughter and she got pregnant?\u8221\'20\'1D he said, according to the book. Pointing to then-Vice President \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , he described him as the \u8220\'20\'1Ctough one\u8221\'20\'1D on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . He soon moved the topic away from Northern Ireland to an offshore wind project he wanted to block near his property, the book says.\par \par \uc2 Trump was often crass and profane about world leaders and others in his orbit. He referred to German Prime Minister \uc2 Angela Merkel\uc2  as \u8220\'20\'1Cthat b----,\u8221\'20\'1D according to the book. When \uc2 Ruth Bader Ginsburg\uc2  was dying in 2020, the book says, Trump would sarcastically raise his hands to the sky in prayer and say: \u8220\'20\'1CPlease God. Please watch over her. Every life is precious,\u8221\'20\'1D before asking an aide: \u8220\'20\'1CHow much longer do you think she has?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 Months after the end of a term in which the rightwing majority made history by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturning \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/23/us-supreme-court-new-york-law-gun-control"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expanding the ability to carry a concealed weapon}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/30/us-supreme-court-ruling-restricts-federal-power-greenhouse-gas-emissions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 limited the Environmental Protection Agency\u8217\'20\'19s ability to regulate power plant emissions}}}\uc2 , the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s justice\u8217\'20\'19s are gathering again today, SCOTUSblog reports.\par \par \uc2 While the private meeting is a normal part of preparing for the upcoming term, justices are expected to get an update on the investigation into the unusual May leak of the draft decision in Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization, the case that reversed Roe v Wade and ended nearly a half-century of nationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access:\par \par \uc2 enltrToday at \uc2 SCOTUS\uc2 : The justices meet privately for their annual "long conference" to review cert petitions that have rolled in over the summer. They'll also likely discuss the status of the Dobbs leak investigation and whether to continue live audio of oral arguments this term.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 SCOTUSblog (@SCOTUSblog) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SCOTUSblog/status/1575106527559843840?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 28, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 Why is the White House convening a summit on food insecurity for the first time in half a century? As The Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/nina-lakhani"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nina Lakhani}}}\uc2  reports, a combination of high inflation and the end of pandemic support programs has squeezed vulnerable households, prompting the Biden administration to step in with a pledge to end hunger by 2030. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from her report:\par \par \uc2 When was the last food conference?\par \par \uc2 The last food conference, hosted by \uc2 Richard Nixon\uc2  in 1969, was a pivotal moment in American food policy that led to the expansion of food stamps and gave rise to the Women, Infants and Children program that today provides parenting advice, breastfeeding support and food assistance to the mothers of half the babies born each year.\par \par \uc2 How bad is hunger in the US now?\par \par \uc2 One in 10 households {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/07/us-food-insecure-families-poverty-study"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 struggled to feed their families}}}\uc2  in 2021 due to poverty \u8211\'20\'13 an extraordinary level of food insecurity in the richest country in the world. The rate has barely budged in the past two decades amid deepening economic inequalities and welfare cuts.\par \par \uc2 Food insecurity remains stubbornly high in the US, with only a slight downward trend from 2021 \u8211\'20\'13 but significantly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2021/apr/14/americas-year-of-hunger-how-children-and-people-of-color-suffered-most"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  lower than 2020 when the Covid shutdown and }}}\uc2  widespread layoffs led to record numbers of Americans relying on food banks and food stamps to get by.\par \par \uc2 The conference comes as the cost of food is soaring due to double-digit inflation, and amid fears of recession. The cost of groceries in July was up 13.1% compared with last year, with the price of cereal, bread and dairy products rising even higher, according to the Consumer Price Index.\par \par \uc2 Households are under more pressure as states roll back pandemic-linked financial support such as free school meals for every child and child tax credits. Many states are stopping expanded food stamp benefits.\par \par \uc2 Real-time data from the US Census survey \u8220\'20\'1Csuggest that food hardship has been steadily rising in families with children this year\u8221\'20\'1D, Diane Whitmore Schanzenbach, director of the Institute for Policy Research at \uc2 Northwestern University\uc2 , recently told the Guardian.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/28/white-house-hunger-food-nutrition-health-conference-explained"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Why is the White House having its first hunger conference in 50 years?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden takes aim at food insecurity in the wealthy but hungry United States\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. The United States may be the world\u8217\'20\'19s biggest economy and one of the wealthiest nations on the planet but everyday, many Americans struggle to provide enough food for their family. The Biden administration will today convene the first summit in 50 years aimed at turning around this trend, with the goal of ending hunger by 2030 and reducing diseases related to nutrition. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will speak at the event at 10am ET.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is happening today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Hurricane Ian{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/27/hurricane-ian-florida-tampa-cuba"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 continues churning towards Florida\u8217\'20\'19s west coast}}}\uc2 , after hitting Cuba and knocking out its entire electrical grid. It\u8217\'20\'19s expected to make landfall today amid fears of a devastating storm surge.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Sanctions chiefs from the state and treasury departments {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.foreign.senate.gov/hearings/keeping-the-pressure-on-russia-and-its-enablers-examining-the-reach-of-and-next-steps-for-us-sanctions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will testify before the Senate foreign relations committee}}}\uc2  about whether the campaign to punish Russia for invading Ukraine is working, at 10 am eastern time.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Senate will continue negotiating a short-term government funding measure to prevent a shutdown on 1 October, after conservative Democrat Joe Manchin{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/27/government-shutdown-senate-vote-funding-bill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dropped a controversial energy permitting provision}}}\uc2  that threatened to hold up the bill.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220928ei9s001xj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
