\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 January 6 committee postpones Wednesday hearing over hurricane \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein \par \uc2 5,817 \uc2 words\par \uc2 27 September 2022\par 20:05 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Panel cites threat of Hurricane Ian bearing down on parts of Florida, and says the \u8216\'20\'18investigation goes forward\u8217\'20\'19Sign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 The January 6 insurrection continued to reverberate through Washington, as the trial of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/27/oath-keepers-stewart-rhodes-trial-january-6-joe-biden-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-6332f2488f08ef7e8107b294#block-6332f2488f08ef7e8107b294"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 five Oath Keepers, including founder of the militant group }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/27/oath-keepers-stewart-rhodes-trial-january-6-joe-biden-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-6332f2488f08ef7e8107b294#block-6332f2488f08ef7e8107b294"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Stewart Rhodes}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/27/oath-keepers-stewart-rhodes-trial-january-6-joe-biden-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-6332f2488f08ef7e8107b294#block-6332f2488f08ef7e8107b294"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 , began}}}\uc2 , while another rioter {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kyledcheney/status/1574838978754351115"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was sentenced}}}\uc2  to more than seven years in prison after pleading guilty to assaulting a police officer. Meanwhile, the congressional committee investigating the attack {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/27/oath-keepers-stewart-rhodes-trial-january-6-joe-biden-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-63334a248f084e56bac56d70#block-63334a248f084e56bac56d70"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 postponed its hearing}}}\uc2  planned for Wednesday, citing Hurricane Ian\u8217\'20\'19s approach towards Florida.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else happened today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The top Senate Republican said he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/27/oath-keepers-stewart-rhodes-trial-january-6-joe-biden-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-63334e9b8f084e56bac56d9b#block-63334e9b8f084e56bac56d9b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 would support a bill}}}\uc2  tweaking America\u8217\'20\'19s election laws to prevent the types of legal plots that were attempted on January 6, greatly raising its chances of passage.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/27/oath-keepers-stewart-rhodes-trial-january-6-joe-biden-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-633344848f08ef7e8107b75e#block-633344848f08ef7e8107b75e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 condemned}}}\uc2  Idaho\u8217\'20\'19s anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws after a university said its staff should only offer condoms for preventing STIs, not as birth control.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Texas\u8217\'20\'19s attorney general fled a process server {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/27/oath-keepers-stewart-rhodes-trial-january-6-joe-biden-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-633305c78f084e56bac569b0#block-633305c78f084e56bac569b0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 delivering him a subpoena}}}\uc2  related to a lawsuit filed by \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  advocates against the state\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to stop them from helping women seek care in other states.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The White House has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/27/oath-keepers-stewart-rhodes-trial-january-6-joe-biden-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-63331cac8f086841b84c3149#block-63331cac8f086841b84c3149"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unveiled a major anti-hunger plan}}}\uc2  to address the United States\u8217\'20\'19 troublingly high rates of food insecurity.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 Top Senate Republican endorses changes to election law intended to stop another January 6\par \par \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 , the Senate Republican leader, has endorsed a measure to change the procedures for counting electoral votes to prevent the types of legal strategies allies of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  attempted on January 6.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI look forward to supporting the legislation, as introduced in committee,\u8221\'20\'1D McConnell said in a speech on the Senate floor Tuesday afternoon.\par \par \uc2 While it was already thought to have the votes to pass, McConnell\u8217\'20\'19s endorsement greatly increases the bill\u8217\'20\'19s chances of passing the Democratic-controlled chamber, where most legislation requires the support of at least 10 Republicans in addition to all Democrats.\par \par \uc2 The bill, called the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.collins.senate.gov/imo/media/doc/one_pager_on_electoral_count_reform_act_of_2022.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Electoral Count Reform Act of 2022}}}\uc2 , clarifies the 1887 Electoral Count Act, which Trump\u8217\'20\'19s allies cited loopholes in to try to convince vice-president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  to delay or overturn \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s election win when Congress convened on January 6, 2021.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/20/bipartisan-senate-group-electoral-count-act"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bipartisan Senate group reaches deal to reform Electoral Count Act}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 The leaders of the January 6 committee have issued a statement explaining their decision to postpone tomorrow\u8217\'20\'19s hearing, citing the threat of Hurricane Ian.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn light of Hurricane Ian bearing down on parts of Florida, we have decided to postpone tomorrow\u8217\'20\'19s proceedings. We\u8217\'20\'19re praying for the safety of all those in the storm\u8217\'20\'19s path,\u8221\'20\'1D the committee\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic chair \uc2 Bennie Thompson\uc2  and Republican vice-chair \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  said in a joint statement. \u8220\'20\'1CThe Select Committee\u8217\'20\'19s investigation goes forward and we will soon announce a date for the postponed proceedings.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 Tomorrow\u8217\'20\'19s hearing of the January 6 committee has indeed been postponed, \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Hugo Lowell confirms:\par \par \uc2 enltrNew: Confirming Wash Post that the Jan. 6 committee hearing scheduled for tomorrow has been postponed, per source familiar\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Hugo Lowell (@hugolowell) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hugolowell/status/1574838294545928256?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 27, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 January 6 committee mulling postponement due to Hurricane Ian\par \par \uc2 The January 6 committee may reschedule its hearing set for tomorrow due to Hurricane Ian, which is expected to hit Florida\u8217\'20\'19s west coast and could cause severe damage, \uc2 The Washington Post\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 enltrNews: Tmrw's {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/January6thCmte?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @January6thCmte}}}\uc2  hearing is likely to be postponed due to Hurricane Ian, me & {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/jdawsey1?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @jdawsey1}}}\uc2  are told.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jacqueline Alemany (@JaxAlemany) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JaxAlemany/status/1574834209444827136?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 27, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 The Wednesday hearing is the first since late July, and potentially the committee\u8217\'20\'19s last public session before the 8 November midterms. The bipartisan committee investigating the insurrection at the Capitol was expected to air a variety of new evidence, potentially touching on the actions of Trump ally \uc2 Roger Stone\uc2  as well as the Secret Service.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 The White House has condemned Idaho\u8217\'20\'19s anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law after a university cited it when warning staff that condoms could be provided to prevent sexually transmitted infections, but not as birth control.\par \par \uc2 Press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  said the university\u8217\'20\'19s warning is an indication that the legislation is intended to undercut rights:\par \par \uc2 enltrFor years, GOP officials have gone after contraception and family planning services. After the Supreme Court\u8217\'20\'19s decision in Dobbs, GOP officials appear more empowered to strip Americans of their basic rights. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/3VNpW0dUgd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/3VNpW0dUgd}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  (@PressSec) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PressSec/status/1574831635459182607?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 27, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrTo be clear, nothing under Idaho law justifies the university\u8217\'20\'19s decision to deny students access to contraception. But the situation in Idaho speaks to the unacceptable consequences of extreme \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  (@PressSec) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PressSec/status/1574831638575517699?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 27, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrThe overwhelming majority of Americans believe in the right to birth control, as well as the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , without government interference. These policies are extreme and backwards.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  (@PressSec) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PressSec/status/1574831641595371520?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 27, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/27/condoms-abortion-students-university-of-idaho-memo-birth-control"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 University of Idaho says staff can offer condoms for STDs \u8211\'20\'13 not birth control}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 The sentencing of Kyle Young, a January 6 rioter who pled guilty to a charge of assaulting the police, is underway in Washington.\par \par \uc2 Two of the Washington police officers he assaulted have spoken at the Iowa man\u8217\'20\'19s sentencing, including \uc2 Michael Fanone\uc2 , who was shocked by another rioter with a taser as Young restrained him. He\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/09/26/opinions/january-6-attacks-capitol-court-sentencing-young-fanone/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 asked for Young to be sentenced to at least 10 years in prison}}}\uc2 , much more than federal prosecutors are seeking.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from Politico:\par \par \uc2 enltrHAPPENING NOW: MPD Officers Moore and Fanone are addressing Judge Amy Berman Jackson as she prepares to sentence Jan. 6 defendant Kyle Young, who participated in some of the most brutal violence that day at the Capitols' Lower West Terrace Tunnel.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Cheney (@kyledcheney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kyledcheney/status/1574812685056843776?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 27, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrDOJ is recommenting 86 months for Young, who brought his minor son into the melee and handed a taser to another rioter, who used it against Fanone.\par \par \uc2 Fanone is speaking now, describing the events of the day. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/6jEktwy8WU"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/6jEktwy8WU}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/NaCK4tGTXU"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/NaCK4tGTXU}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Cheney (@kyledcheney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kyledcheney/status/1574813878202114048?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 27, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrYOUNG, addressing the court, turns to Officer Fanone, apologizes and breaks down crying.\par \par \uc2 "I am so so sorry. And if I could take it back I would."\par \par \uc2 Turning to the judge, he says, "Whatever you give me as a punishment, I accept."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Cheney (@kyledcheney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kyledcheney/status/1574825757095993344?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 27, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 Secret Service turned cellphones of agents involved in January 6 over to inspector general\par \par \uc2 The Secret Service took cellphones from 24 agents involved in its response to January 6 and turned them over to the homeland security department\u8217\'20\'19s inspector general as he investigates the deletion of text messages and other data from around the time of the insurrection, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/national-security/secret-service-took-cellphones-24-agents-involved-agencys-jan-6-riot-r-rcna49476"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NBC News reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 While it\u8217\'20\'19s not clear what Joseph Cuffari has been able to obtain from the phones, NBC says the seizure of the government-supplied devices occurred in July, after the inspector general informed the Secret Service that he would launch a criminal probe into the deletion of the records.\par \par \uc2 The missing data has become a major issue for the January 6 committee, which has taken evidence from a variety of people at the Capitol and in the Trump White House around the time of the attack. Interest in what the Secret Service knew about the insurrection was raised after Trump administration aide Cassidy Hutchinson said that agents had witnessed alarming behavior by the then-president shortly before the attack, including a physical altercation for the steering wheel of his limousine. However, the agency said data from 5 and 6 January were lost in a pre-planned upgrade of its cellphones.\par \par \uc2 Cuffari himself has also come in for criticism. Last week, staff of the homeland security watchdog called on president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to fire him, accusing him in an anonymous letter of \u8220\'20\'1Cpoor decision-making\u8221\'20\'1D, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pogo.org/investigation/2022/09/dhs-watchdog-staff-call-on-biden-to-fire-inspector-general-cuffari"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Project on Government Oversight reported}}}\uc2 . Appointed by Trump, Cuffari is a former aide to Republican Arizona governors \uc2 Doug Ducey\uc2  and \uc2 Jan Brewer\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/11/missing-secret-service-texts-congress-notified-april"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Secret Service watchdog suppressed memo on January 6 texts erasure}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 Thomas Zimmer writes\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 As the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/jan-6-hearings"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 6 hearings}}}\uc2  are about to resume, it is unlikely that our basic understanding of what happened between the 2020 presidential election and the attack on the Capitol will significantly change.\par \par \uc2 That is a testament to the crucial work the committee has already done and to which we owe much of our detailed knowledge of the weeks long, multi-level coup attempt and the evolving strategies of those involved in this deliberate campaign to nullify the election results, prevent the transfer of power and end constitutional government in America.\par \par \uc2 And yet, the committee\u8217\'20\'19 job is far from done.\par \par \uc2 It still has an important role to play in determining the meaning and role of January 6 in US history. Was the attack on the US Capitol a failed, desperate, last-ditch effort by delusional extremists? Or will it be remembered as a milestone in America\u8217\'20\'19s accelerating descent into authoritarianism \u8211\'20\'13 an assault on the system that didn\u8217\'20\'19t succeed initially but played a key role in democracy\u8217\'20\'19s demise?\par \par \uc2 The answer to these questions is not decided by facts and past events. In a very real sense, January 6 isn\u8217\'20\'19t over yet, and the success or failure of the Trumpian coup attempt will be decided by what happens next.\par \par \uc2 If that sounds counter-intuitive, it is helpful to examine how the meaning of another infamous historical event to which January 6 has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/world/2021/01/15/trump-hitler-us-capitol-beer-hall-putsch/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 often been compared}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 the Beer Hall Putsch, Adolf Hitler\u8217\'20\'19s failed coup attempt in November 1923 \u8211\'20\'13 changed significantly over time.\par \par \uc2 More:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2022/sep/27/january-6-changed-america-here-are-two-directions-the-country-could-go-now"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 6 changed America. Here are two directions the country could go now | Thomas Zimmer}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 Gloria Oladipo writes\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 The Department of Justice has pushed back on the unsubstantiated claims from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  that the agency planted evidence during its search of Mar-a-Lago in August, submitting a slightly amended list of seized materials and an affidavit that the list reflects what was taken.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FBI\uc2  submitted a first version of the inventory list several weeks ago. It only had one business day to compile that list but had more time to submit the most recent version, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://edition.cnn.com/2022/09/26/politics/justice-department-maralago-seized-materials-list-full-accurate/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN}}}\uc2  reported. The agency also said that in the updated version it filtered out potentially privileged items.\par \par \uc2 Judge Raymond Dearie, the special master appointed to review the case, requested that the \uc2 FBI\uc2  provide a \u8220\'20\'1Cfull and accurate\u8221\'20\'1D picture of what was obtained in the search.\par \par \uc2 Dearie\u8217\'20\'19s request came after Trump and several allies claimed, without evidence, that the \uc2 FBI\uc2  planted items during its search of the Florida mansion.\par \par \uc2 Dearie has given Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers until Friday to provide evidence to back up the accusation that the agency is \u8220\'20\'1Cincorrectly describing\u8221\'20\'1D any materials.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/27/doj-trump-evidence-affidavit-mar-a-lago"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DoJ pushes back on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s claims it planted evidence at Mar-a-Lago }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has a legal \u8211\'20\'13 if incremental \u8211\'20\'13 win to celebrate.\par \par \uc2 Earlier today, the 2nd circuit court of appeals ruled that a lower-court judge was wrong when he said Trump, as president, was not covered by a federal law that can shield federal employees from liability in incidents related to their work.\par \par \uc2 The case involved is the defamation suit brought by the writer E Jean Carroll, who alleges that Trump raped her in a New York department store changing room in the 1990s, which Trump vehemently denies.\par \par \uc2 As Politico {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/09/27/trump-libel-suit-e-jean-carroll-00058995"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2  today, \u8220\'20\'1CUnder Trump, the justice department belatedly invoked that law \u8211\'20\'13 known as the Westfall Act \u8211\'20\'13 in a bid to shut down the defamation case Carroll filed in 2019 stemming from statements Trump issued denying that he raped Carroll, including a declaration that \u8216\'20\'18She\u8217\'20\'19s not my type.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Last year, under President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , the justice department stirred controversy by reaffirming the department\u8217\'20\'19s earlier stance that Trump was essentially immune from suit because he was acting within the scope of his duties when fielding media questions about the alleged rape at the \uc2 Bergdorf Goodman\uc2  in 1995 or 1996.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, two of three judges on the appeals court said there was \u8220\'20\'1Cmanifest uncertainty\u8221\'20\'1D about whether Trump was covered by the Westfall Act. The third judge said the law did not apply.\par \par \uc2 As Politico reports, any resolution is likely \u8220\'20\'1Cmany more months, if not years\u8221\'20\'1D away.\par \par \uc2 Alina Habba, a lawyer for Trump, said: \u8220\'20\'1CWe are extremely pleased \u8230\'20\'26 This decision will protect the ability of all future presidents to effectively govern without hindrance. We are confident that the DC Court of Appeals \u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 the next stop for the case \u8211\'20\'13 \u8220\'20\'1Cwill find that our client was acting within the scope of his employment when properly repudiating Ms Carroll\u8217\'20\'19s allegations.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Carroll and the justice department did not immediately comment.\par \par \uc2 Carroll {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/20/e-jean-carroll-trump-lawsuit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has said}}}\uc2  she plans to directly accuse Trump of rape under a new New York law that allows civil claims over alleged sex crimes otherwise subject to a 20-year statute of limitations.\par \par \uc2 More:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/20/e-jean-carroll-trump-lawsuit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Writer E Jean Carroll to file new lawsuit after accusing Trump of rape}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 As Hurricane Ian churns towards Florida\u8217\'20\'19s west coast, \uc2 Deanne Criswell\uc2 , administrator of the \uc2 Federal Emergency Management Agency\uc2 , has joined the White House press briefing.\par \par \uc2 She\u8217\'20\'19s talking about the preparations for the latest storm, as well as Puerto Rico\u8217\'20\'19s recovery from Hurricane Fiona last week.\par \par \uc2 enltr. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/FEMA_Deanne?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @FEMA_Deanne}}}\uc2  live in the press briefing room: \u8220\'20\'1CI can tell you our biggest concern as we wait for the storm to make landfall is storm surge. It is a leading cause of hurricane-related fatalities. If people are told to evacuate by their local officials, listen to them.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/HTqa0RUxp3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/HTqa0RUxp3}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jaclyn Rothenberg (she/her) (@FEMAspox) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/FEMAspox/status/1574800298023043073?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 27, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 You can watch the briefing below:\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 The January 6 insurrection continues to reverberate through Washington today, as the trial of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/27/oath-keepers-stewart-rhodes-trial-january-6-joe-biden-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-6332f2488f08ef7e8107b294#block-6332f2488f08ef7e8107b294"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 five Oath Keepers, including founder of the militant group }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/27/oath-keepers-stewart-rhodes-trial-january-6-joe-biden-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-6332f2488f08ef7e8107b294#block-6332f2488f08ef7e8107b294"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Stewart Rhodes}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/27/oath-keepers-stewart-rhodes-trial-january-6-joe-biden-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-6332f2488f08ef7e8107b294#block-6332f2488f08ef7e8107b294"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 , begins}}}\uc2 , while another rioter is sentenced after pleading guilty to assaulting a police officer. Meanwhile, the congressional committee investigating the attack is preparing to hold its first public hearing in more than two months tomorrow, with Trump ally \uc2 Roger Stone{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/27/oath-keepers-stewart-rhodes-trial-january-6-joe-biden-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-63330ed68f08ef7e8107b42c#block-63330ed68f08ef7e8107b42c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said to feature prominently}}}\uc2 , among other evidence.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else happened so far today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Senate appears ready to pass a bill tweaking America\u8217\'20\'19s election laws to prevent the types of legal plots that were attempted on January 6, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/27/oath-keepers-stewart-rhodes-trial-january-6-joe-biden-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-63330f978f084e56bac56a37#block-63330f978f084e56bac56a37"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a Democratic lawmaker sponsoring the bill said}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Texas\u8217\'20\'19s attorney general fled a process server {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/27/oath-keepers-stewart-rhodes-trial-january-6-joe-biden-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-633305c78f084e56bac569b0#block-633305c78f084e56bac569b0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 delivering him a subpoena}}}\uc2  related to a lawsuit filed by \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  advocates against the state\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to stop them from helping women seeking care in other states.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The White House has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/27/oath-keepers-stewart-rhodes-trial-january-6-joe-biden-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-63331cac8f086841b84c3149#block-63331cac8f086841b84c3149"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unveiled a major anti-hunger plan}}}\uc2  to address the United States\u8217\'20\'19 troublingly high rates of food insecurity.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 Opponents of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s student debt relief plan have cast it as expensive and potentially illegal, and the Associated Press reports that a California law firm has taken the plan to court to see whether it will hold up.\par \par \uc2 The libertarian Pacific Legal Foundation sued over the plan in Indiana, where an employee of the firm lives and where the state government said it intends to levy taxes on any canceled debt, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/biden-education-lawsuits-executive-branch-88a53926a6583fdb7b8c311206f5357f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to the AP}}}\uc2 . The lawsuit challenges the plan on the grounds that the employee is set to get his debt erased through a federal program for civil servants, and thus he will face a tax burden under the White House program.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from the report:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCongress did not authorize the executive branch to unilaterally cancel student debt,\u8221\'20\'1D said Caleb Kruckenberg, an attorney at Pacific Legal Foundation. He said it\u8217\'20\'19s illegal for the executive branch to create the policy \u8220\'20\'1Cby press release, and without statutory authority.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The suit\u8217\'20\'19s plaintiff is Frank Garrison, described as a public interest attorney who lives in Indiana and is employed by the libertarian group.\par \par \uc2 Garrison is on track to get his student debt erased through a separate federal program for public servants. Although most borrowers will need to apply for Biden\u8217\'20\'19s plan, Garrison and many others in that program will automatically get the relief because the Education Department has their income information on file.\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s plan would automatically cancel $20,000 of Garrison\u8217\'20\'19s debt, which in turn would trigger an \u8220\'20\'1Cimmediate tax liability\u8221\'20\'1D from the state of Indiana, according to the suit. Under the debt forgiveness program he\u8217\'20\'19s enrolled in now, canceled debt cannot be taxed.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMr. Garrison and millions of others similarly situated in the six relevant states will receive no additional benefit from the cancellation \u8212\'20\'14 just a one-time additional penalty,\u8221\'20\'1D the suit argues.\par \par \uc2 Any student debt forgiven under Biden\u8217\'20\'19s plan would also be subject to state taxes in Arkansas, California, Minnesota, Mississippi, North Carolina and Wisconsin, unless lawmakers in those states change their current laws.\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s plan promises to cancel $10,000 in federal student debt for borrowers with incomes of less than $125,000 per year or households making less than $250,000. Those who received federal Pell Grants to attend college would get an additional $10,000 erased.\par \par \uc2 An application to receive the benefit is expected by early October.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/24/joe-biden-us-student-loan-debt-cancellation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden unveils plan to cancel $10,000 in student loan debt for millions}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 The United States is one of the world\u8217\'20\'19s richest countries, but many people struggle to put enough food on the table. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/nina-lakhani"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nina Lakhani}}}\uc2  reports on a new White House plan to change that:\par \par \uc2 The Biden government has launched a new strategy to end hunger in the US by 2030 through the expansion of benefits such as free school meals and food stamps.\par \par \uc2 One in 10 households struggled to feed their families in 2021 due to poverty \u8211\'20\'13 an extraordinary level of food insecurity in the richest country in the world which has barely budged in the past two decades amid deepening economic inequalities and welfare cuts.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/wp-content/uploads/2022/09/White-House-National-Strategy-on-Hunger-Nutrition-and-Health-FINAL.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The plan,}}}\uc2  published on Tuesday, also aims to cut diet-related diseases by increasing access to healthy food and exercise as new data shows that more than 35% of people in 19 states and two territories are obese \u8211\'20\'13 more the double the number of states in 2018 \u8211\'20\'13 while one in 10 Americans have diabetes. It includes proposals to reform food packaging and voluntary salt and sugar reduction targets for the food industry, as well as working to expand Medicaid and Medicare access to obesity counselling and nutrition.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/27/us-biden-effort-end-hunger-2030-expanding-benefits-diet-food-deserts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US launches effort to end hunger by 2030 by expanding benefits and access to healthy foods}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 As the January 6 committee enters what is likely to be the home stretch of its investigation, a new poll has found it hasn\u8217\'20\'19t meaningfully shifted beliefs about what happened that day.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.monmouth.edu/polling-institute/reports/monmouthpoll_us_092722/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Monmouth University finds}}}\uc2  that around four in 10 Americans hold \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  responsible for the insurrection at the Capitol, slightly less than in late June, while three in 10 believe the election was stolen from him, a figure that\u8217\'20\'19s moved little since November 2020.\par \par \uc2 People are also divided over the hearings\u8217\'20\'19 impacts on democracy, with about 25% saying it strengthens it, 34% saying it weakens the system of government and 35% saying it has no impact. However, the poll did find opinions of America\u8217\'20\'19s system of government have rebounded in recent months:\par \par \uc2 enltrNATIONAL POLL: Half believe the American system of government is basically sound. This marks a return to pre-2021 levels after hitting an all-time low of 36% in June.\par \par \uc2 BASICALLY SOUND by PARTY:\par \par \uc2 DEM \u8211\'20\'13 56% (36% in June)\par \par \uc2 REP \u8211\'20\'13 52% (39% in June) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/njGFZbHFxc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/njGFZbHFxc}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/AWdL2zrDi2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/AWdL2zrDi2}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 MonmouthPoll (@MonmouthPoll) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MonmouthPoll/status/1574776019130748931?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 27, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Director of the Monmouth University Polling Institute Patrick Murray tied the hearings\u8217\'20\'19 ebb and flow to Americans\u8217\'20\'19 perceptions of the system of government.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s certainly a correlation between the hearings kicking off and a decreased faith in the American system\u8217\'20\'19s resilience, but it is not clear what caused the rebound,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt may be that Americans feel confident in our democratic processes after withstanding the test of Jan. 6, or it could simply be they are no longer thinking about those dangers without the weekly presence of televised hearings.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 January 6 committee set to focus on \uc2 Roger Stone\uc2 's role in lead-up to attack\par \par \uc2 When it holds its next public hearing on Wednesday, the January 6 committee will likely show footage of Trump ally \uc2 Roger Stone\uc2  discussing violence against left-wing protesters, and predicting that the 2020 election would be overturned by force, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2022/09/26/jan6-committee-roger-stone-documentary/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Washington Post reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The video was obtained from Danish filmmakers who followed Stone around from 2019 through 2021, and decided to cooperate with a subpoena from a congressional panel. \u8220\'20\'1CBeing with \uc2 Roger Stone\uc2  and people around him for nearly three years, we realized what we saw after the 2020 election and Jan. 6 was not the culmination but the beginning of an antidemocratic movement in the United States,\u8221\'20\'1D Christoffer Guldbrandsen, director of the documentary titled \u8220\'20\'1CA Storm Foretold,\u8221\'20\'1D told the Post.\par \par \uc2 Footage reported earlier this year shows Stone advocating for Trump to reject the official results and use federal judges allied with him to ensure his victory. In July 2020, he predicted that Democrats would try to steal the election, and said, \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s going to be really nasty\u8230\'20\'26 If the electors show up at the electoral college, armed guards will throw them out.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\u8216\'20\'18I\u8217\'20\'19m the president. F--- you\u8230\'20\'26 You\u8217\'20\'19re not stealing Florida, you\u8217\'20\'19re not stealing Ohio. I\u8217\'20\'19m challenging all of it, and the judges we\u8217\'20\'19re going to are judges I appointed.\u8217\'20\'19 \u8221\'20\'1D Stone says, mimicking what Trump would say.\par \par \uc2 He also advocates for violence against antifascist protesters and other left-wing groups, saying \u8220\'20\'1CF--- the voting, let\u8217\'20\'19s get right to the violence. Shoot to kill, see an antifa, shoot to kill. F--- \u8217\'20\'19em. Done with this bulls---.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Stone later added a caveat: \u8220\'20\'1CI am of course only kidding. We renounce violence completely. We totally renounce violence. The left is the only ones who engage in violence.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/mar/04/roger-stone-trump-election-jared-kushner"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roger Stone raged at \u8216\'20\'18disgrace\u8217\'20\'19 Trump over failure to overturn election \u8211\'20\'13 report}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 Congress is up against an end-of-the-month deadline to pass a short-term funding measure, or risk shutting down the government \u8211\'20\'13 which neither party wants. But as the Senate convenes today, it is also considering legislation that would tweak America\u8217\'20\'19s election laws to stop the sort of plot attempted on January 6.\par \par \uc2 The legislation, a version of which has also been introduced in the House of Representatives, needs the votes of all Democrats and at least 10 Republicans to pass. Democratic senator Amy Klobuchar told MSNBC today she believes it has that support:\par \par \uc2 enltrSenate Rules Committee Chairwoman Sen. Amy Klobuchar (D-MN) says the bipartisan Electoral Count Reform Act already has "ten Republicans" and thinks it will have enough votes to pass:\par \par \uc2 "We keep adding senators to this bill, Democrats and Republicans." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/yrRaGl2J5i"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/yrRaGl2J5i}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1574773606487310337?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 27, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/19/liz-cheney-zoe-lofgren-electoral-count-act-bill-january-6-attack"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Liz Cheney and Zoe Lofgren to propose bill to stop another January 6 attack}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Oath Keepers trial is kicking off today with jury selection, as well as some last-minute moves by the group\u8217\'20\'19s attorneys to delay the proceedings, which Politico reports have not panned out.\par \par \uc2 Both sides have also given estimates of how long the trial will take:\par \par \uc2 enltrUPDATE from the Oath Keepers trial:\par \par \uc2 Judge Mehta rejected another attempt by defendants to change venue. He noted that of initial 150 jury candidates, 40% had never even heard of the Oath Keepers, and vast majority expressed no prejudgment bias.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Cheney (@kyledcheney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kyledcheney/status/1574766008417624064?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 27, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrThose numbers get even smaller, Mehta noted, after a round of jurors were struck by both parties, including one who was a \uc2 Capitol Police\uc2  officer and another who worked on the hill on Jan. 6\par \par \uc2 He also said all prospective jurors will be told not to watch Jan. 6 hearing tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Cheney (@kyledcheney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kyledcheney/status/1574766612238028800?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 27, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrA masked Stewart RHODES was seated in the courtroom as the proceedings got underway.\par \par \uc2 DOJ says it has prepped 40 potential witnesses for trial throughout August/Sept and is providing 302s of prep sessions to defense.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Cheney (@kyledcheney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kyledcheney/status/1574766958750359555?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 27, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrLatest trial timing estimates:\par \par \uc2 DOJ: 3-4 weeks\par \par \uc2 Defense: 2-3 weeks\par \par \uc2 If trial gets underway next week, we're looking at a mid- to late-November verdict\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Cheney (@kyledcheney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kyledcheney/status/1574767385436995594?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 27, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 When a process server turned up at his house with a subpoena related to a case filed by \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights groups, Texas\u8217\'20\'19s top law enforcement officer did what any reasonable person would do: fled the scene in a truck driven by his wife.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.texastribune.org/2022/09/26/texas-attorney-general-ken-paxton-subpoena-abortion-lawsuit/?utm_campaign=trib-social&utm_content=1664244917&utm_medium=social&utm_source=twitter"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Texas Tribune reports}}}\uc2  that process server Ernesto Martin Herrera had a hard time getting legal documents to the state\u8217\'20\'19s attorney general \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2 , which would have compelled his testimony today in a lawsuit from \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups aimed at blocking Texas\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to retaliate against them for facilitating access to the procedure out of state. Here\u8217\'20\'19s how the encounter played out, according to the Tribune:\par \par \uc2 When Herrera arrived at Paxton\u8217\'20\'19s home in McKinney on Monday morning, he told a woman who identified herself as Angela that he was trying to deliver legal documents to the attorney general. She told him that Paxton was on the phone and unable to come to the door. Herrera said he would wait.\par \par \uc2 Nearly an hour later, a black Chevrolet Tahoe pulled into the driveway, and 20 minutes after that, \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2  exited the house.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI walked up the driveway approaching Mr. Paxton and called him by his name. As soon as he saw me and heard me call his name out, he turned around and RAN back inside the house through the same door in the garage,\u8221\'20\'1D Herrera wrote in the sworn affidavit.\par \par \uc2 Angela Paxton then exited the house, got inside a Chevrolet truck in the driveway, started it and opened the doors.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA few minutes later I saw Mr. Paxton RAN from the door inside the garage towards the rear door behind the driver side,\u8221\'20\'1D Herrera wrote. \u8220\'20\'1CI approached the truck, and loudly called him by his name and stated that I had court documents for him. Mr. Paxton ignored me and kept heading for the truck.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Herrera eventually placed the subpoenas on the ground near the truck and told him he was serving him with a subpoena. Both cars drove away, leaving the documents on the ground.\par \par \uc2 Paxton attacked the report on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , saying he worried he was in danger:\par \par \uc2 enltrThis is a ridiculous waste of time and the media should be ashamed of themselves. All across the country, conservatives have faced threats to their safety \u8212\'20\'14 many threats that received scant coverage or condemnation from the mainstream media.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Attorney General \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2  (@KenPaxtonTX) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KenPaxtonTX/status/1574608584201056262?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 27, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrIt\u8217\'20\'19s clear that the media wants to drum up another controversy involving my work as Attorney General, so they\u8217\'20\'19re attacking me for having the audacity to avoid a stranger lingering outside my home and showing concern about the safety and well-being of my family.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Attorney General \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2  (@KenPaxtonTX) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KenPaxtonTX/status/1574608678854205440?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 27, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 Denver Riggleman\u8217\'20\'19s book about his time serving as a staffer on the January 6 committee and in Congress comes out today, and while his revelations about the investigation have made headlines, the former lawmaker has plenty to say about his former Republican colleagues, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/martin-pengelly"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Martin Pengelly}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 The Republican congressmen \uc2 Louis Gohmert\uc2  and \uc2 Paul Gosar\uc2  adopted such extreme, conspiracy-tinged positions, even before the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-capitol-breach"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US Capitol attack}}}\uc2 , that a fellow member of the rightwing Freedom Caucus thought they \u8220\'20\'1Cmay have had serious cognitive issues\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Denver Riggleman, once a US representative from Virginia, reports his impression of his former colleagues from Texas and Arizona in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/26/white-house-call-january-6-rioter-denver-riggleman-book-the-breach"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a new book}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Breach: The Untold Story of the Investigation into January 6th is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://bookshop.org/books/the-breach-the-untold-story-of-the-investigation-into-january-6th/9781250866769"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 published in the US}}}\uc2  on Tuesday. \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  obtained an early copy.\par \par \uc2 Riggleman is a former \uc2 US air force\uc2  intelligence officer who lost his seat in Congress after he officiated a same-sex marriage. In his book, he describes fallout beyond his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/jun/14/virginia-republican-officiated-gay-wedding-loses-nomination-for-congress"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 primary defeat}}}\uc2 , including someone tampering with the wheels of his truck, endangering the life of his daughter.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2022/sep/27/denver-riggleman-book-republicans-paul-gosar-louie-gohmert"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republican ex-congressman suggests colleagues \u8216\'20\'18had serious cognitive issues\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Besides the Capitol itself, \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 cellphone is turning into perhaps the most important place for understanding the events around the January 6 attack, \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/hugo-lowell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hugo Lowell}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2 , \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s former White House chief of staff, was at the center of hundreds of incoming messages about ways to aid Trump\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to overturn the 2020 election results, according to texts he turned over to the House January 6 select committee that have been published in a new book.\par \par \uc2 The texts included previously unreported messages, including a group chat with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump administration}}}\uc2  cabinet officials and plans to object to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s election certification on January 6 by Republican members of Congress and one former US attorney, as well as other Trump allies.\par \par \uc2 The book, The Breach, was obtained by the Guardian in advance of its scheduled publication on Tuesday. Written by the former Republican congressman and senior adviser to the investigation Denver Riggleman, the work has already become controversial after being condemned by the panel as \u8220\'20\'1Cunauthorized\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/26/mark-meadows-text-messages-january-6-breach-book"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Meadows was central to hundreds of texts about overturning 2020 election, book says}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 Inflation is high in America, but one accused rioter in the January 6 insurrection has a plan to cut costs: go hunting.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/nation/2022/09/27/jan-6-gun-hunting-groceries/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Washington Post}}}\uc2  reports that Jon Mott, an Arkansas man facing charges over unlawfully breaching the Capitol\u8217\'20\'19s rotunda, has been granted permission by a federal judge to uses firearms for hunting, though he can\u8217\'20\'19t keep them in his home or office. Mott was arrested in May 2021 after being identified as part of the mob that attacked the Capitol, and his conditions of release prohibited him from possessing weapons. He\u8217\'20\'19s charged with \u8220\'20\'1Centering a restricted building, disorderly conduct in a restricted building and two counts of violent entry and disorderly conduct on Capitol grounds,\u8221\'20\'1D according to the Post, and has pled not guilty.\par \par \uc2 More than 2,000 people may face charges related to January 6, but the report notes this isn\u8217\'20\'19t the first time gun possession issues have popped up. A Georgia defendant has asked for two of his firearms back so he can kill snakes on his property, while a Texas woman who had already been sentenced had her right to own a weapon restored by a judge who found she had a credible safety concern.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 Five members of the Oath Keepers including founder Stewart Rhodes are facing charges of seditious conspiracy, a dire allegation that the justice department hasn\u8217\'20\'19t pursued since 2010.\par \par \uc2 Federal investigators {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jan/14/stewart-rhodes-oath-keepers-january-6-us-capitol-attack"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have alleged}}}\uc2  that the group spent months planning the attack on the Capitol, with Rhodes spending $20,000 on weapons and equipment in the weeks leading up to the attack. The group also planned to have armed \u8220\'20\'1Cquick reaction forces\u8221\'20\'1D positioned to storm the Capitol, with Rhodes texting an encrypted group chat on January 6, \u8220\'20\'1CWe will have several well equipped QRF\u8217\'20\'19s outside DC.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A conviction on seditious conspiracy charges could attract a prison sentence of up to 20 years, but keep in mind, the last time the justice department brought the charges in 2010, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.lawfareblog.com/last-time-justice-department-prosecuted-seditious-conspiracy-case"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a judge ultimately threw them out}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere today, Kyle Young will be sentenced after pleading guilty to one charge of assaulting a police officer. Prosecutors say the Iowa resident restrained Washington, DC police officer \uc2 Michael Fanone\uc2  as another rioter shocked him with a taser Young provided. Fanone, who has since left the force but testified before the January 6 committee, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/09/26/opinions/january-6-attacks-capitol-court-sentencing-young-fanone/index.html?utm_content=2022-09-27T11%3A00%3A12&utm_source=twCNN&utm_medium=social&utm_term=link"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote for CNN}}}\uc2  of his hopes for Young\u8217\'20\'19s sentencing:\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, Young\u8217\'20\'19s attorney will ask a judge to sentence him to two years \u8211\'20\'13 a laughably short sentence. Prosecutors have asked for a seven-year term \u8211\'20\'13 not quite a joke but also not nearly long enough. By comparison, a former New York police officer with no criminal record received 10 years for attacking officers during the riot.\par \par \uc2 What do I think Young deserves? Not less than 10 years in prison. And an assigned cell in maximum security with his co-conspirator: \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 Oath Keepers leader Rhodes to stand trial on seditious conspiracy charges over January 6 insurrection\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. The trial of one of the most notorious groups involved in the January 6 insurrection begins today in Washington, as five members of the Oath Keepers, including its founder Stewart Rhodes, face the rarely used charge of seditious conspiracy for allegedly plotting to disrupt the certification of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s election win. Separately, a judge will sentence Kyle Young, who pleaded guilty to charges related to violently assaulting a police officer during the attack. More than a year and a half after the insurrection, the cases could bring justice to some of its most high-profile participants.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is happening today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Senate is getting to work on two important bills, one to prevent a government shutdown at the end of the month, and the other to reform America\u8217\'20\'19s election laws to prevent another January 6.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 As Hurricane Ian moves towards Florida, \uc2 Federal Emergency Management Agency\uc2  head \uc2 Deanne Criswell\uc2  will appear at the White House press briefing beginning at 12pm ET.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will speak about his administration\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to lower healthcare costs and preserve social security at 11.30am ET.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220927ei9r001p9\par }\par \b \uc2 Search Summary\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 atleast5(abortion)\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clb